{"run_id": "fe69ac93-1879-4592-a242-76a2a1acf90b", "timestamp": "2026-04-07T13:52:10.749958+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1897568", "question": "Counter-Strike: Leo Team vs Brute (BO3) - NODWIN Clutch Series Play-In Group A", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Winners match between Leo Team and Brute in the NODWIN Clutch Series Play-In Group A, initially scheduled for April 7 at 10:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Leo Team\" if Leo Team win the match against Brute.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Brute\" if Brute win the match against Leo Team.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-07T20:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-07T14:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.6, "volume_usd": 1079.2991410000002, "category": "counter-strike"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing provides fragmented tournament data from unrelated CS competitions (RIVALS LEAGUE, GLuck SixSeven, etc.) but contains NO information about the specific Leo Team vs Brute matchup, their rosters, recent form, or head-to-head records. MARKET PRICE AS WEAK SIGNAL: Current market prices (YES 60% / NO 40%) reflect some market consensus favoring Leo Team, but without underlying data in the briefing, this price cannot be validated or contradicted. LEO TEAM EVIDENCE: Brief mention of Leo Team's participation in other tournaments with roster names (amster, Malkiss, marat2k) suggests competitive experience, but no data on their current form, win-loss record, or performance in NODWIN specifically. BRUTE EVIDENCE: Essentially absent from briefing. No roster information, tournament history, or competitive standing provided. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: NODWIN Clutch Series Play-In Group A is C-tier with lower stakes; play-in matches typically involve similarly-ranked teams with high variance outcomes. BO3 FORMAT: Best-of-3 provides moderate sample size, reducing extreme upsets, but this stabilizing effect is minimal without team quality data. TIMING: Event is TODAY (~6 hours to resolution). At this proximity, the outcome is likely already determined or heavily influenced by team preparation/roster status that is not reflected in the briefing. RESOLUTION CRITERIA: Clear and unambiguous\u2014straightforward win condition with forfeiture/cancellation fallbacks. No ambiguity in how the match will resolve. CONFIDENCE JUSTIFICATION: Both confidence_yes and confidence_no are set LOW (28 and 25) because the briefing lacks substantive competitive data for either team. The probability_score of 58 reflects mild deference to market prices (60% YES) in the absence of contradictory data, but this is a near-coin-flip estimate with very weak conviction.", "key_factor": "Briefing document contains no substantive data on either Leo Team or Brute's recent form, head-to-head history, roster quality, or NODWIN Clutch Series Play-In Group A standings; outcome is essentially data-blind."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "YES SIDE STRENGTHS: Leo Team has documented competitive experience advancing through tournament brackets in RIVALS LEAGUE Season 1, suggesting organizational stability and player familiarity with competitive environments. The roster includes named players (amster, Malkiss, marat2k) with tournament credentials, indicating some level of established competitive pedigree. NO SIDE WEAKNESSES: The briefing provides essentially zero substantive data on Brute\u2014no roster names, no tournament results, no recent form, no head-to-head history. This information vacuum is concerning for the underdog side; if Brute were clearly dominant or well-established, market pricing and available analysis would reflect it. CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing explicitly states 'no direct match information, recent form data, or team rosters for this specific matchup' and 'Insufficient publicly available data on Leo Team's recent form or win-loss record.' This severely limits confidence on BOTH sides, not just NO. MARKET PRICING ALIGNMENT: The 60% YES price aligns with the modest information advantage favoring Leo Team (some tournament history vs. none documented). However, this is a weak signal in a low-stakes C-tier tournament where both teams are in Play-In qualification. PLAY-IN CONTEXT: Play-In matches typically involve teams of similar competitive standing with unpredictable outcomes. The briefing notes this explicitly\u2014suggesting inherent competitive parity reduces any information edge Leo Team may hold. TOURNAMENT TIER REALITY: NODWIN Clutch Series is C-tier with lower stakes. BO3 format provides only moderate sample size for variance; any team can win on map selection variance, player form variance, or tactical execution on a given day. ASYMMETRIC CONFIDENCE: confidence_yes is 35 (not higher) because Leo Team's tournament experience is documented but shallow and does not include recent form data. confidence_no is 32 (similarly low) because there is almost no public information on Brute at all\u2014the absence of data does not mean weakness, it means opacity. PROBABILITY JUSTIFICATION: 58% reflects the market's slight favor to Leo Team (documented experience over undocumented opponent) while heavily discounting the signal strength due to extreme data scarcity. A coin flip (50%) would be defensible; 60% is modestly reasonable but not strongly supported. REVERSAL RISK: Event is TODAY, resolving in ~6 hours. There is insufficient time for significant new information or major roster changes to emerge. The match will likely proceed as scheduled and resolve based on in-game performance, which is inherently unpredictable in a play-in context.", "key_factor": "Leo Team's demonstrated tournament experience and roster credentials in RIVALS LEAGUE, combined with minimal public information disadvantaging Brute's competitive standing."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "MARKET MISPRICING SIGNAL: YES is priced at 60% despite the briefing containing zero comparative data on either team's recent form, head-to-head record, or roster strength \u2014 this is classic favorite bias in the absence of real information. LEO TEAM'S APPARENT CREDENTIALS ARE HOLLOW: The briefing cites Leo Team's 'competitive experience' and names three players, but provides no recent results, win rates, or performance against comparable opponents. Tournament participation \u2260 tournament success. BRUTE IS COMPLETELY UNKNOWN: The briefing offers literally nothing about Brute's roster, recent form, or competitive tier. In a C-tier, low-stakes play-in match, an unknown team is not automatically weaker \u2014 it may simply lack press coverage. PLAY-IN MATCHES ARE INHERENTLY VOLATILE: The briefing explicitly notes that play-in group matches 'typically involve teams of similar competitive standing with unpredictable outcomes.' This directly contradicts the 60-40 pricing. NO HEAD-TO-HEAD DATA: Absence of Leo vs Brute history means no pattern recognition, no counter-strategy data, and no momentum factors. This favors the underdog (Brute) because market confidence in Leo rests on reputation, not empirical head-to-head advantage. BO3 FORMAT ADDS UNCERTAINTY: While BO3 is a moderate sample size, it's not large enough to eliminate upset potential in evenly matched play-in competitors. Brute could adapt mid-series or exploit map-selection advantages the market hasn't quantified. DATA FRESHNESS RISK: This match resolves TODAY in ~6 hours. The briefing data (2026-04-07 13:52 UTC) is extremely recent but the actual news summary admits 'fragmented tournament data' and 'no direct match information.' Market prices may reflect pre-tournament hype rather than recent form. LEO TEAM'S PARTICIPATION IN OTHER TOURNAMENTS MAY INDICATE FATIGUE: The briefing mentions Leo Team's activity in RIVALS LEAGUE Season 1 and other events in the March-April window. Overcommitment across tournaments could diminish focus on this qualifier, while Brute may have had more rest or preparation time. C-TIER TOURNAMENT UNPREDICTABILITY: NODWIN Clutch Series is explicitly noted as C-tier with 'lower stakes.' Lower-tier tournaments have higher variance, less predictable outcomes, and teams that may under-prepare. Leo Team's market favoritism may not translate to a play-in environment. ASYMMETRIC CONFIDENCE JUSTIFIED: Confidence in YES is low (35) because Leo Team's credentials are unsubstantiated; confidence in NO is also modest (42) because Brute's profile is entirely absent. The market has taken a bet on Leo's reputation without solid recent data to support it. UNDERDOG PRICING: At 40%, Brute is genuinely undervalued. In a play-in match between two teams with zero comparative data, a 60-40 split favors the team with press coverage over the team with actual competitive strength \u2014 a classic trap.", "key_factor": "Brute's true competitive standing is entirely obscured by data gaps, while Leo Team's recent tournament participation may mask deeper structural weaknesses or roster instability."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.55, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains no actionable competitive intelligence on either Leo Team or Brute \u2014 no recent match results, head-to-head history, roster current status, or map pool compatibility. TOURNAMENT TIER: C-tier NODWIN event with play-in format suggests both teams are similarly ranked, indicating near 50-50 base rate for such matchups. LEO TEAM SIGNAL (weak): Fragmented evidence shows Leo Team competed in RIVALS LEAGUE Season 1 and advanced through brackets; however, timeline and opponents are unclear. Tournament data references March-April 2026 matches but no recent form vs. Brute. BRUTE SIGNAL (absent): Zero information provided on Brute's roster, recent performance, or competitive history. Search results mention EC BANGA, Viggo, eLITenergy forfeits, but nothing about Brute specifically. MARKET PRICE ANALYSIS: 60% YES / 40% NO suggests modest market confidence in Leo Team. Without underlying data, this may reflect: (a) slightly better public perception of Leo Team, or (b) information asymmetry favoring Leo Team backers. Insufficient evidence to validate this spread. BO3 FORMAT: Best-of-3 provides moderate sample to reduce variance, but without map pool, player form, or recent H2H, this advantage is neutral. TIME-TO-RESOLUTION: Event resolves TODAY in ~6 hours. No time for new information. Market price will likely converge to ~$0.01/$0.99 once outcome becomes clear in final hours. CONFIDENCE SYMMETRICALLY LOW: Both confidence_yes and confidence_no are set to 26-28 because briefing provides zero comparative data on either team's current strength. This is a genuine information vacuum, not a coin flip with hidden edges. ANCHOR TO 50-55: Given market price of 60% YES and complete absence of validating data, probability_score nudged slightly above 50 to reflect modest market consensus, but with minimal conviction. True base rate for identical play-in teams is 50%.", "key_factor": "In C-tier Counter-Strike play-in matches with symmetric team information, ~50% win rate for either side; outcomes are highly dependent on roster strength, recent form, and map pool \u2014 factors entirely absent from briefing."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "\u2022 CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains fragmented tournament data with NO direct information about Leo Team vs Brute matchup, rosters, recent form, or head-to-head history. \u2022 Market price (60% YES) appears to reflect slight Leo Team favoritism, but this is based on minimal evidence \u2014 only that Leo Team appears in tournament brackets elsewhere, not on direct competitive comparison. \u2022 Briefing provides Leo Team roster names (amster, Malkiss, marat2k) but ZERO information about Brute's roster or competitive standing, creating severe asymmetric information. \u2022 Play-In Group A format indicates both teams are likely similar in competitive tier (C-tier tournament), suggesting closer than 60-40 split should be expected. \u2022 Market shows LOW VOLUME ($1,079 USD) and matches TODAY (6 hours to resolution) \u2014 liquidity is thin, suggesting price may not reflect informed trading but rather scattered bets with limited data. \u2022 Current 60-40 split appears to be rational apathy rather than informed conviction \u2014 market has priced in 'Leo Team has some tournament experience' but lacks depth to justify the bias. \u2022 BO3 format reduces variance vs BO1, but with zero match history or recent form data, the outcome is genuinely uncertain. \u2022 SENTIMENT: Market is APATHETIC \u2014 neither side shows conviction; price reflects weak signal (Leo Team name recognition) rather than robust analysis. This is nearly a coin flip being quoted at 60-40. \u2022 Confidence scores both depressed (35/32) because briefing provides insufficient evidence for EITHER direction \u2014 no recent performance data, no roster depth analysis, no map preferences. \u2022 Slight lean to 58 (vs 50) reflects only that Leo Team appears in multiple tournament datasets in briefing, but this is weak evidence at best and may reflect data collection bias rather than skill.", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.45, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains zero direct information about Leo Team vs Brute matchup, head-to-head history, recent form, or roster comparisons\u2014only fragmented tournament metadata from unrelated competitions. MARKET SIGNAL MISMATCH: YES price at 60% suggests meaningful confidence differential, but no supporting evidence in briefing justifies this 20-point spread; this appears to be soft-information or liquidity-driven pricing rather than data-driven. PLAY-IN STRUCTURAL CONTEXT: Group A Play-In format in C-tier tournaments (Liquipedia Tier C) typically features regional-level teams with comparable skill tiers; elimination matches in this context are fundamentally unpredictable without roster/form data. LEO TEAM PROFILE: Briefing shows Leo Team advanced to Grand Final in an unnamed C-tier event (defeating j!nX 2-1 in semis), indicating mid-tier competitive competence, but no timeframe for this result or relevance to current April 2026 form. BRUTE INFORMATION VACUUM: Zero mentions of Brute's tournament history, roster, recent performance, or even which region they represent; impossible to conduct comparative analysis. BO3 FORMAT IMPLICATION: Best-of-3 reduces variance relative to single-map play, but with equivalent team strength, each map is essentially a coin flip; without map veto data or historical win rates, format does not break symmetry. TEMPORAL CONCERN: Tournament metadata spans Feb-April 2026; Leo Team's Grand Final appearance may be recent (April 10 date listed) or historical (March dates shown)\u2014unclear if this is current form or archive data. RESOLUTION RISK: Forfeit/walkover clauses in resolution criteria (50-50 if team withdraws pre-match) add ~5-10% uncertainty to binary outcome; not negligible in low-information environment. ESPORTS SPECIALIST INSIGHT: In lower-tier CS2 tournaments, team availability, stand-in players (briefing mentions 'Viggo substitutes KralleJ'), and organizational stability are primary outcome drivers\u2014none of this information provided for either team. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in YES requires Leo roster strength proof or Brute weakness evidence; high confidence in NO requires opposite. Briefing provides neither, justifying LOW confidence on both sides.", "key_factor": "Play-In matches in C-tier tournaments typically involve evenly-matched regional teams with minimal public statistical differentiation; the 60% YES market pricing appears inflated relative to available competitive data."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.35, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing contains zero substantive information about either Leo Team's or Brute's current form, recent win-loss records, or head-to-head history. The 60% YES price appears anchored to Leo Team's name recognition across other tournaments, not this specific matchup. ROSTER VOLATILITY SIGNAL: The briefing explicitly documents multiple roster substitutions and forfeits in this tournament series (EC BANGA forfeit, Viggo substitutes KralleJ, eLITenergy forfeit). This suggests unstable roster conditions and last-minute changes are endemic to this event \u2014 a red flag for 6-hour pre-match reversals. BRUTE ANONYMITY: Brute has virtually no documented competitive history in the provided briefing. This absence is itself suspicious in a C-tier tournament context \u2014 Brute could be a rising/reformed roster, a regional qualifier team, or a late-addition entry with undocumented preparation. PLAY-IN ELIMINATION STRUCTURE: This is a play-in GROUP A match, not a main bracket fixture. Teams in play-in rounds are typically more volatile, less practiced together, and more susceptible to meta shifts or tactical surprises than established teams. MARKET MISPRICING DIRECTION: The 60/40 split suggests modest confidence in Leo Team, not overwhelming dominance. For a BO3 between two nearly-equal unknown teams in a C-tier qualifier, 60% is insufficiently extreme to rule out a 35% reversal scenario. TIMELINE PRESSURE: With only ~6 hours until match (TODAY timing), any disruption (illness, DDoS, technical forfeit, or last-minute sub) is harder to correct and more likely to swing the match to the prepared underdog. ABSENCE OF EVIDENCE ON LEO FORM: While Leo Team shows tournament appearance history, the briefing provides zero recent performance metrics, win-loss trends, or map pool data specific to this 2026 period. March/early April results shown are from other tournaments; current form is unknown. CONTRARIAN PIVOT: Council consensus likely anchors on Leo Team's historical presence; the real risk is Brute as an unknown challenger with different tactical preparation or a fresh roster that hasn't been mapped/scouted.", "key_factor": "Brute fields an unexpected roster substitution or lineup change that exploits a meta shift or tactical weakness Leo Team has not prepared for, combined with Leo Team suffering a key player illness or technical issue in the opening hours before match time."}], "final_score": 0.5088016528925621, "no_score": 0.5005084745762712, "edge": -0.0911983471074379, "no_edge": 0.10050847457627121, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 51% for YES (need \u226560%); YES-side confidence too low: 31% (need \u226570%)", "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1897568", "question": "Counter-Strike: Leo Team vs Brute (BO3) - NODWIN Clutch Series Play-In Group A", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Winners match between Leo Team and Brute in the NODWIN Clutch Series Play-In Group A, initially scheduled for April 7 at 10:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Leo Team\" if Leo Team win the match against Brute.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Brute\" if Brute win the match against Leo Team.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-07T20:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-07T14:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.6, "volume_usd": 1079.2991410000002, "category": "counter-strike"}, "key_facts": ["Best of 3 (Online) * Group B elimination match ** EC BANGA forfeit the match as they are unable to field a complete lineup.", "Best of 3 (Online) * Group B opening match ** Viggo substitutes KralleJ.", "Best of 3 (Online) * Group A opening match ** eLITenergy forfeit the match due to a scheduling conflict with another event.", "ASTRAL matchup at CCT Season 3 Europe Series 20!", "I've watched this savage kid for awhile now\u2026..", "BMZ matchup at ESL Challenger League Season 51 Asia-Pacific Cup 3!", "Complete overview of the CYBERSHOKE Prospects vs.", "eternal premium matchup at GLuck SixSeven Season 1!", "13\n\n94\n\nAncient\n\n6\n\n33\n\n11\n\n56\n\nOverpass\n\n13\n\n76\n\n13\n\n76\n\n52\n\nTeam TRUPPENTRUPPEN\n\nLEOLEO\n\nApril 10, 2026 - 17:00 CEST\n\nTRUPPEN\")\n\nvs(Bo5)\n\nLEO\")\n\nWatch here\n\nThird Place Match\n\nThird Place Match\n\n3rd Place\n\n3rd\n\nskibidibicicletaskibidi\n\n1\n\nj!nX Esportsj!nX\n\n2\n\nMarch 29, 2026 - 17:00 CEST\n\nskibidi\")\n\n1:2(Bo3)\n\nj!nX\")\n\n10\n\n82\n\nOverpass\n\n13\n\n49\n\n13\n\n49\n\nMirage\n\n11\n\n83\n\n7\n\n61\n\nAncient\n\n13\n\n67\n\n## Additional Content\n\n[edit]\n\