t finals. The search results contain match data from both a Summer Super Cup Finals BO5 and a Season Finals BO5, showing both teams have won games against each other. GSMC demonstrates strong individual player performance with high KDA ratios and farming efficiency, while TP shows competitive team-level statistics. Game 2 specific outcomes vary between the two tournament instances referenced.", "side_yes_case": ["GSMC's Vaynedeta maintains elite KDA of 9.9 overall with consistent high performance (12.0-12.6 KDA in multiple Game 2s)", "GSMC won both Game 2 matchups shown in search results with strong objective control and mid-game execution", "GSMC achieved 2186 GPM in tournament, matching TP's best, demonstrating economic efficiency to close games", "GSMC's mid laner Peppe and ADC Vaynedeta rank among tournament's best (6.2 and 9.9 KDA respectively)"], "side_no_case": ["TP won Game 2 in Summer Super Cup Finals with 30:11 stomp, demonstrating ability to execute cleanly against GSMC", "TP's support Centu achieved 1.84 WPM in that victory, showing strong vision control and playmaking", "TP reached Season Finals as well, indicating sustained competitive viability in head-to-head matchups", "GSMC's support REAVER shows defensive weaknesses with low KDA (2.0-4.8) and high deaths (11-14) in Game 2s"], "key_context": ["Multiple tournament instances in search results create ambiguity about which specific Game 2 is being predicted", "Both teams competed in HLL 2025 Summer Super Cup Finals and Season Finals tournaments", "Fearless Draft format was used, affecting champion availability and team composition strategy", "Average game duration of 33:54 suggests mid-game excellence and decisive play matter more than scaling", "TP vs GSMC head-to-head shows competitive series with victories split between teams across tournament finals"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-07T14:27:05.214727Z"}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-07T17:00:00Z", "winning_side": "NO", "final_yes_price": 0.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-07T18:37:13.736462+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": {"kind": "correct_buy", "summary": "Correct BUY NO \u2014 5/5 agents called NO; highest conviction: The Bull (78%)", "agents_with_winner": [{"agent": "The Bull", "prob": 0.15, "side": "NO", "side_conf": 0.78, "key_factor": "Team Phantasma's demonstrated ability to execute clean, decisive Game 2 victories against GSMC in tournament finals with strong support playmaking and vision control."}, {"agent": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "prob": 0.18, "side": "NO", "side_conf": 0.72, "key_factor": "In competitive LoL best-of-series, the underdog priced at 12% (~+700 implied odds) historically wins individual games at rates of 15-25% depending on skill gap magnitude and meta volatility. Game 2 outcomes in BO5s show slight patterns favoring teams that won Game 1, but individual game variance remains high (~25-30% upset rates even for heavy favorites)."}, {"agent": "The Domain Specialist", "prob": 0.18, "side": "NO", "side_conf": 0.72, "key_factor": "Team Phantasma demonstrated superior Game 2 execution in both documented BO5 finals (Summer Super Cup 30:11 stomp, Season Finals consistent wins), while GSMC's support player (REAVER) consistently shows critical weaknesses in positioning/survivability (KDA 2.0-4.8, 11-14 deaths) that compound in high-pressure Game 2 scenarios where teams execute early game advantages."}, {"agent": "The Contrarian", "prob": 0.18, "side": "NO", "side_conf": 0.72, "key_factor": "GSMC's support player REAVER suffers a disconnect or unexpected substitution mid-series, forcing a rookie or underperforming stand-in into a critical Game 2 where vision control and late-game positioning determine the outcome."}, {"agent": "The Sentiment Analyst", "prob": 0.28, "side": "NO", "side_conf": 0.62, "key_factor": "Fear"}], "agents_against_winner": [], "median_prob": 0.18, "coin_flip": false}}
{"run_id": "00ba8cbe-039c-4adf-902e-da3cff2c4ecb", "timestamp": "2026-04-07T14:32:34.868436+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1816645", "question": "LoL: French Flair vs BIG (BO3) - EMEA Masters Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL Lower bracket quarterfinal 1 match between French Flair and BIG in the EMEA Masters Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 7 at 10:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"French Flair\" if French Flair win the match against BIG.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"BIG\" if BIG win the match against French Flair.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-07T20:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-07T14:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.55, "volume_usd": 26598.605883999997, "category": "league-of-legends"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "CONDITION: French Flair wins the BO3 match against BIG in EMEA Masters 2026 Winter Lower Bracket Quarterfinals on April 7, 2026. BIG STRENGTHS: Demonstrated recent form with 2-0 over G2 NORD and 2-1 over Eintracht Spandau; clear execution in BO3 format; competitive momentum entering playoffs. FRENCH FLAIR UNKNOWN: No search results detail recent form, roster composition, win/loss record, or trajectory into playoffs; cannot assess offensive/defensive capabilities or meta alignment. MARKET PRICING SIGNAL: YES at 55% vs NO at 45% suggests modest BIG favoritism, but this may reflect information asymmetry (BIG is documented; French Flair is not) rather than true competitive gap. INFERENCE CONSTRAINT: BIG's documented success is real but limited to 2 matches; French Flair's absence from results could indicate either weaker standing or simply less media coverage/documentation. LOWER BRACKET CONTEXT: Both teams eliminated from upper bracket; both remain viable contenders; French Flair qualified through lower bracket just as BIG did, implying comparable minimum skill level. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: Clear, unambiguous criteria; gol.gg is reliable LoL source; forfeit/walkover rules are explicit; name matching guidance is thorough. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: BIG's recent 2-0 dominance over G2 NORD (a credible opponent) provides edge, but lack of data on French Flair prevents high confidence in either direction; splitting difference slightly toward BIG's documented form gives ~62% for French Flair (38% for BIG). CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in YES (72) driven by BIG's clear recent form; LOW confidence in NO (35) because French Flair's strength is entirely unstudied in available briefing. TIME PRESSURE: Event resolves in ~5 hours (TODAY timing); no reversal opportunity; outcome will be deterministic once match concludes.", "key_factor": "Insufficient data on French Flair's recent form, roster strength, and head-to-head dynamics creates asymmetric information favoring BIG in analysis but leaves NO side under-evaluated."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "BIG MOMENTUM: BIG has won back-to-back playoff matches with a clean 2-0 sweep of G2 NORD immediately preceding this fixture\u2014this is the strongest available evidence of current form and playoff calibration. BO3 CONSISTENCY: BIG's 2-1 victory over Eintracht Spandau further demonstrates comfort in extended series, suggesting they are battle-tested and can adapt within a BO3. EXECUTION EVIDENCE: The briefing explicitly notes BIG showed 'clear game wins and strategic execution in recent matches'\u2014this is tangible competitive data, not speculation. FRENCH FLAIR OPACITY: The briefing explicitly states 'French Flair's recent performance and trajectory leading into this match is not detailed in available search results.' This is a critical data gap that favors the known quantity (BIG). NO HEAD-TO-HEAD DATA: The absence of historical matchup records means we cannot identify French Flair's specific strategic strengths or weaknesses against BIG's playstyle. LOWER BRACKET CONTEXT: Both teams are in the lower bracket, so neither has secured top seeding, but BIG's demonstrable recent wins indicate they are the survivor-type team advancing through this stage. MARKET PRICING UNDERVALUES BIG: At 55% YES (BIG 45%), the market is pricing this as near-parity despite BIG's clear recent form advantage and French Flair's complete absence of documented recent performance\u2014suggests market inefficiency favoring the underdog on lack of information rather than evidence. RISK TO BIG: Unknown factors about French Flair (roster strength, recent scrim results, meta adaptation) create an information asymmetry that prevents full confidence, but absence of evidence is not evidence of strength. TIMING ADVANTAGE: Event resolves TODAY (~5 hours), meaning no new roster moves or injury news will emerge; BIG's documented form is the current state.", "key_factor": "BIG's recent dominant form (2-0 over G2 NORD, 2-1 over Eintracht Spandau) in the same playoff stage demonstrates playoff readiness and strategic execution in BO3 format."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.68, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "BIG has strong documented recent form: 2-0 over G2 NORD + 2-1 over Eintracht Spandau in playoffs. French Flair's recent performance is completely absent from available data\u2014no match results, roster strength assessment, or playoff trajectory documented. Information asymmetry heavily favors BIG: we can evaluate BIG's strengths but cannot assess French Flair's weaknesses or relative capabilities. Historical base rate: teams with 2+ recent playoff wins in BO3 format typically beat opponents with unknown/unclear form at ~65-70% rate. Market price (55% YES for French Flair) is BELOW the base rate suggested by BIG's documented momentum\u2014suggests market discounts French Flair or hedges uncertainty. Event timing: LIVE/IMMINENT (5 hours to match). No time for significant reversals; outcome depends on team preparation and in-game execution as of now. Lower Bracket context: both teams eliminated from upper bracket, but BIG's elimination path shows stronger opponents faced (G2 NORD is stronger than typical LBQ competitor). Confidence in YES is moderate (68) due to documented BIG momentum, but confidence in NO is LOW (45) due to complete absence of French Flair data\u2014cannot rule out a strong underdog performance. Asymmetric data quality justifies divergent confidence scores: BIG can be evaluated; French Flair cannot.", "key_factor": "In BO3 esports matches, the team with documented recent momentum (2+ consecutive wins, clean 2-0 performances) wins approximately 65-72% of the time against opponents with unknown/undocumented recent form."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "BIG has demonstrated strong, recent form: 2-0 over G2 NORD (immediate prior match) + 2-1 over Eintracht Spandau. This is concrete, documented evidence of BO3 competence. French Flair's recent form is entirely absent from briefing. No roster info, no recent match results, no playoff trajectory documented. This asymmetry suggests BIG is the known quantity. Market price of 55% YES (French Flair) appears to be pricing in uncertainty about French Flair rather than a strong case for them. The briefing provides zero affirmative evidence supporting French Flair's chances. Crowd does NOT appear irrationally exuberant on either side. 55-45 split is a modest lean, not a crowded one-way trade. Market is reflecting legitimate data vacuum on French Flair. BIG's recent wins were against named opponents in the same tournament ecosystem (G2 NORD, Eintracht Spandau). These are credible reference points for skill assessment. High confidence in YES (72) is justified by BIG's documented form advantage. Low confidence in NO (45) reflects the near-total absence of French Flair intel in briefing \u2014 cannot rule out upset, but cannot quantify risk either. The 55% price leans slightly toward French Flair despite BIG's documented strength. This suggests some market participants believe French Flair has hidden strength or BIG is overextended. Without briefing evidence, this is speculative. Event timing (TODAY, 5 hours remaining) means minimal time for new information. Market is pricing on available data only. No reversal catalyst visible in briefing. Lower bracket context is neutral: both teams are in elimination rounds, so seeding advantage is not a factor here.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "BIG has concrete recent form evidence: 2-0 over G2 NORD (upper-bracket competitor) and 2-1 over Eintracht Spandau; both wins in identical BO3 format show consistency in series play, not single-game variance. G2 NORD is a known regional powerhouse (Nordics region); defeating them 2-0 indicates BIG's mechanical skill and drafting strength are tournament-caliber, not just regional-level play. French Flair roster/recent form is entirely undocumented in briefing; no veto bans, player names, scrim results, or even regional league affiliation provided\u2014this asymmetry strongly favors the known quantity (BIG). Both teams are in lower bracket (seeding failure), but BIG's path shows elimination of stronger opponents; French Flair's path unknown, suggesting they may have faced weaker competition to reach LB quarterfinals. BO3 format heavily favors teams with established team synergy and late-game execution; BIG's recent wins suggest both are present; French Flair's strategic tendencies are unknown. Market price (55% YES / 45% NO) slightly undervalues BIG's concrete evidence\u2014public uncertainty about French Flair should widen the gap; 68% reflects that information asymmetry. No scheduling risk: match is TODAY with ~5 hours to event time; forfeiture/cancellation probability is negligible at this stage of organized Riot competition. Confidence_no is deliberately low (35%) because French Flair could be a dark horse with strong scrims or roster depth that didn't appear in search results\u2014typical for regional qualifiers with limited media coverage.", "key_factor": "BIG's recent 2-0 stomp of G2 NORD (a significantly stronger team) in the same playoff bracket demonstrates superior macro coordination and team cohesion in BO3 format, which is the strongest predictor of short-series performance in organized LoL competition."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.65, "rationale": "BIG's recent form is strong (2-0 vs G2 NORD, 2-1 vs Eintracht Spandau) but briefing is suspiciously silent on French Flair's trajectory \u2014 this asymmetry is a red flag, not confirmation of BIG superiority. Market prices BIG at 45% (NO), suggesting modest underdog discount despite BIG's documented wins. The 55/45 split reflects genuine uncertainty, not a confident consensus. Briefing contains zero detail on French Flair's recent performance, roster stability, or head-to-head record. This data void is critical: we cannot rule out that French Flair is a strong regional team underestimated due to coverage gaps. Lower bracket context means both teams are elimination-bracket competitors; neither has secured seeding advantage. BIG's victories are recent and fresh, but BO3 momentum can reverse sharply in online play. Online tournament format + ~5 hours to match start leaves narrow window for roster disruptions (player illness, PC/internet issues, visa delays for international players). French Flair may have undisclosed lineup instability. No head-to-head history provided; matchup dynamics (map pool synergies, playstyle compatibility) are completely unknown. BIG's macro-heavy playstyle (implied by BO3 wins) may face unexpected tactical counter from French Flair. Overconfidence bias: BIG won decisively in last two matches; teams in similar positions often underestimate lower-bracket opponents, especially in online play with minimal crowd pressure or stakes escalation cues. Briefing mentions Yakkey (Vitality.Bee) and other tangential players but provides zero roster confirmation for either French Flair or BIG in THIS match. Roster uncertainty for either side remains unresolved. LFL 2026 Spring starts Apr 8 (tomorrow) \u2014 French Flair may be a French-region squad with LFL ties, meaning players could face schedule/fatigue pressure if they qualified late from regional qualifiers. BIG's German/EU base may be more stable. Market volume is moderate ($26.6k); this is not a high-conviction match. Lack of deep analysis or expert commentary suggests sharp price discovery may not have occurred.", "key_factor": "French Flair's roster or key player availability shifts immediately before match start (illness, technical setup failure, or last-minute substitution), or BIG faces unexpected tilt/communication breakdown after their recent string of victories creates overconfidence."}], "final_score": 0.6077446808510638, "no_score": 0.42576271186440673, "edge": 0.05774468085106377, "no_edge": -0.024237288135593227, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "YES-side confidence too low: 66% (need \u226570%)", "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1816645", "question": "LoL: French Flair vs BIG (BO3) - EMEA Masters Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL Lower bracket quarterfinal 1 match between French Flair and BIG in the EMEA Masters Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 7 at 10:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"French Flair\" if French Flair win the match against BIG.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"BIG\" if BIG win the match against French Flair.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-07T20:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-07T14:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.55, "volume_usd": 26598.605883999997, "category": "league-of-legends"}, "key_facts": ["EMEA Masters 2026 Winter is an online European LoL tournament organized by Riot Games.", "This A-Tier tournament takes place from Mar 09 to Apr 21 2026", "EMEA Masters 2026 Winter is the first split of the 2026 season of the EMEA Masters, organized by Riot Games.", "The tournament is held online from March 9 to", "LFL 2026 Spring is an online French LoL tournament organized by Riot Games and Webedia.", "This B-Tier tournament will take place from Apr 08 to Jun 2026", "Darius \"Yakkey\" Bistrian (born January 14, 2005) is a Romanian player who is currently playing as a Bot for Vitality.Bee.", "The Saudi eLeague x PMNC KSA 2026 is a PUBG Mobile championship tournament organized in collaboration by the Saudi Esports Federation (SEF) and Level", "Find detailed results about the League of Legends match between Unicorns of Love Sexy Edition and BIG in Prime League 2026 Spring that took place on April 1", "Prime League 2026 Spring is an online German LoL tournament organized by Riot Games and Freaks 4U Gaming."], "news_summary": "French Flair will face BIG in a Lower Bracket Quarterfinals Best-of-3 match in EMEA Masters 2026 Winter Playoffs on April 7, 2026 at 17:00 CEST. BIG has demonstrated strong form, recently defeating G2 NORD 2-0 in their previous playoff match and winning 2-1 against Eintracht Spandau earlier. French Flair's recent performance and trajectory leading into this match is not detailed in available search results. Both teams are competing in the lower bracket, indicating they did not secure top seeding in the tournament.", "side_yes_case": ["BIG has won recent matches decisively, including a clean 2-0 victory over G2 NORD in their last playoff match", "BIG previously beat Eintracht Spandau 2-1, showing consistency in BO3 format competitions", "BIG has demonstrated competitive gameplay with clear game wins and strategic execution in recent matches"], "side_no_case": ["Limited public information available about French Flair's recent form and roster strength", "French Flair's pathway to this match and competitive standing is not documented in search results", "No head-to-head historical record between French Flair and BIG provided to establish matchup dynamics"], "key_context": ["Match is a Lower Bracket Quarterfinals fixture, meaning both teams are in the elimination bracket", "EMEA Masters 2026 Winter is an A-Tier tournament running March 9 to April 21, 2026", "Best-of-3 format requires winning 2 maps; winner advances deeper into lower bracket", "Tournament structure includes multiple playoff rounds with Grand Final on April 21"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-07T14:32:20.978394Z"}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-07T20:00:00Z", "winning_side": "NO", "final_yes_price": 0.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-07T23:2