metry; recent match dates (April 5) ensure same meta, patching (12.05), and roster stability for both. MARKET SIGNAL RELIABILITY: 55-45 split with $27,258 volume suggests meaningful consensus; sharp money typically prices CS:GO/Valorant regional playoffs efficiently\u2014DNSTY's slight edge should not be dismissed as noise. UNDERDOG WEAKNESSES ABSENT: Briefing provides no performance red flags for DNSTY (no major losses, no roster turnover, no meta mismatch). The lack of negative data on DNSTY reinforces that market gap is genuine preparation/meta advantage, not panic. UCAM CEILING: UCAM beat Bar\u00e7a 2-0 (March 7) but Bar\u00e7a has struggled in EMEA (1-2 vs FKS, 0-2 vs EP on March 19-21). KPI shows mixed results\u2014recent victory may reflect opponent weakness rather than UCAM peak form. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: High confidence in NO (72) reflects clear market consensus and DNSTY's recent playoff 2-0; moderate confidence in YES (35) reflects UCAM's visibility advantage being offset by limited direct evidence of superiority over DNSTY specifically.", "key_factor": "DNSTY's recent 2-0 playoff victory (April 5) combined with market pricing and limited direct head-to-head data suggesting DNSTY has been underestimated relative to UCAM's recent visibility."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.52, "confidence_yes": 0.58, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "MARKET STRUCTURE: YES (UCAM) is priced at 45% despite being the underdog narrative\u2014but briefing evidence suggests UCAM is the stronger team. Market may be pricing this as a true toss-up or overweighting DNSTY's recent 2-0 win without context. UCAM FORM TRAJECTORY: UCAM won 2-0 vs KPI on April 5, 2026 in Stage 3.1 playoffs. Prior to that, beat Bar\u00e7a eSports 2-0 in Stage 2 Playoffs (March 7)\u2014demonstrates ability to string together dominant playoff performances against established opponents. DNSTY'S THIN RECORD: Briefing provides only one recent DNSTY match: 2-0 vs MT on April 5, 2026. 