pecialist", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "UCAM shows consistent dominant performances: multiple consecutive 2-0 victories (vs KPI on April 5, vs Bar\u00e7a on March 7) indicate refined team coordination and meta adaptation during peak playoff timing. DNSTY's recent performance limited to single documented 2-0 win (vs MT on April 5); insufficient match history to assess consistency, map pool depth, or playoff pressure resilience. BO3 format favors teams with deeper strategic flexibility and proven map adaptability; UCAM's documented success across multiple opponents (KPI, Bar\u00e7a) suggests superior preparation. Bar\u00e7a eSports appearance in UCAM's recent wins is notable\u2014Bar\u00e7a competes in VCL EMEA tier, indicating UCAM has faced higher-tier competition than DNSTY's documented MT opponent. No direct head-to-head history between teams in briefing; market pricing (45% YES / 55% NO) reflects genuine uncertainty and data asymmetry favoring the underdog. Event timing is TODAY (~5 hours to resolution); extreme recency of April 5-7 matches means current roster and meta stability are confirmed, reducing tactical surprise factors. Playoff stage (Rising Phase 1 Playoffs vs regular season group play) typically features tighter map bans, less innovation, and higher correlation to raw team strength\u2014favors UCAM's demonstrated consistency. Confidence in YES is modest (62) due to sparse DNSTY data; confidence in NO is lower (48) because the briefing provides insufficient counter-evidence to justify overweighting DNSTY despite market pricing lean.", "key_factor": "UCAM's recent 2-0 victories in Stage 3.1 playoffs demonstrate superior current form and map control consistency, while DNSTY's single documented 2-0 win lacks sufficient recent match data to establish competitive parity in a high-pressure BO3 playoff context."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.55, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "UCAM's recent 2-0 victories (KPI, Bar\u00e7a) are against teams of unclear current standing; the briefing provides no comparative tier or recent form data for either opponent, making UCAM's 'strong form' claim unverifiable. DNSTY's single visible win (2-0 vs MT on April 5) is equally sparse in context; no information exists on MT's competitive level or meta adherence, so DNSTY's capability is assumed rather than proven. Head-to-head history is explicitly absent from the briefing\u2014zero direct UCAM vs DNSTY match records; both teams are near-peers in a B-Tier bracket with likely similar skill ceilings. BO3 format crucially favors adaptability and in-series adjustments over raw aggregate strength; a team that reads the meta faster or has superior tactical flexibility in map veto/agent selection can win 2-1 despite lower overall pedigree. Patch 12.05 is mentioned but no patch notes or agent/mechanic changes are described; if a recent patch heavily favors utility-heavy or aggressive sentinel plays (or vice versa), the team with deeper practice on that style gains a hidden edge. VCL EMEA Stage 1 results for UCAM show 0-2 losses and a 2-3 playoff loss, suggesting performance ceiling issues or fatigue; if UCAM has been grinding multiple tournaments in short span, mental fatigue or tactical staleness in playoffs is plausible. DNSTY appears to have less tournament volume in the briefing's match history, which could indicate either: (a) a newer roster that has trained intensively on a single meta, or (b) a team avoiding over-exposure and arriving fresh for playoffs. Absence of player-level data (injuries, stand-ins, role swaps, recent trades) is a critical blind spot; if UCAM's in-game leader or sentinel player is playing through an undisclosed issue, DNSTY's site execution could exploit it. Market prices (45% YES / 55% NO) reflect mild NO bias, suggesting smart money slightly favors DNSTY; this contrarian positioning is consistent with the theory that UCAM's recent wins are less impressive on closer scrutiny. Playoff intensity and pressure favor the team with sharper mental clarity; if DNSTY has genuinely lower expectations and UCAM is perceived favorite, psychological weight could shift defensive execution.", "key_factor": "DNSTY executes a meta-shift or map-pool strategy that exploits a specific weakness in UCAM's agent selection or site execution that recent stage matches did not fully expose."}], "final_score": 0.5105361930294906, "no_score": 0.4869189189189189, "edge": 0.06053619302949059, "no_edge": -0.06308108108108113, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Contrarian call: council prob 51% < 70% threshold; Contrarian call: YES-side confidence 48% < 80% threshold", "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1898498", "question": "Valorant: UCAM Esports Club vs DNSTY (BO3) - VCL Spain: Rising Phase 1 Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant Upper bracket semifinal 2 match between UCAM Esports Club and DNSTY in the VCL Spain: Rising Phase 1 Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 7 at 2:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"UCAM Esports Club\" if UCAM Esports Club win the match against DNSTY.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"DNSTY\" if DNSTY win the match against UCAM Esports Club.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-08T00:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-07T18:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.45, "volume_usd": 27258.157460999995, "category": "valorant"}, "key_facts": ["VALORANT Challengers 2026 Spain: Rising Stage 3 Phase 1 is an online Spanish VAL tournament organized by Riot Games and LVP.", "Top Valorant esports teams rankings list and tiers in Europe.", "Game 2\n\nPatch 12.05\n\n### Match History\n\nHead to Head\n\n| Date | Tier | Tournament | Opponent | Score | vs.", "Opponent |\n ---  ---  --- |\n| March 2, 2026 - 15:00 CET | B-Tier | VCL Spain: Stage 2 - Group A | UCAM EsportsUCAM | 2 : 0 | KPI GamingKPI |  |\n| February 28, 2026 - 11:00 CET | B-Tier | VCL Spain: Stage 2 - Group A | UCAM EsportsUCAM | 2 : 1 | KPI GamingKPI | Details |\n| January 13, 2026 - 19:00 CET | B-Tier | VCL Spain: Stage 1 - Round 3 | UCAM EsportsUCAM | 1 : 1 | KPI GamingKPI | Details |\n| October 10, 2025 - 18:00 CEST | Qualifier | RBHG: Spanish Qual.", "- Playoffs | UCAM EsportsUCAM | 1 : 2 | KPI GamingKPI | Details |\n| July 13, 2025 - 18:00 CEST | B-Tier | VCL Spain: Stage 3 - Group A | UCAM EsportsUCAM | 2 : 0 | KPI GamingKPI | Details |\n\nUCAM EsportsUCAM [...] KPI GamingKPI\n\n| Date | Tournament | Score | vs.", "Opponent |\n ---  --- |\n| April 5, 2026 - 17:00 CEST | VCL Spain: Stage 3.1 | 2 : 0 |  | Details |\n| March 2, 2026 - 15:00 CET | VCL Spain: Stage 2 - Group A | 0 : 2 | UCAM | Details |\n| March 1, 2026 - 13:00 CET | VCL Spain: Stage 2 - Group A | 2 : 0 |  | Details |\n| February 28, 2026 - 11:00 CET | VCL Spain: Stage 2 - Group A | 1 : 2 | UCAM | Details |\n| January 26, 2026 - 17:00 CET | VCL Spain: Stage 1 - Round 7 | 1 : 1 |  | Details |\n\nRetrieved from \"\"\n\nHidden categories:\n\n Pages with unknown player input in matches\n Matches\n Finished Matches [...] UCAM EsportsUCAM\n\n| Date | Tournament | Score | vs.", "Opponent |\n ---  --- |\n| March 28, 2026 - 17:00 CET | VCL EMEA: Stage 1 - Playoffs | 2 : 3 |  | Details |\n| March 27, 2026 - 20:00 CET | VCL EMEA: Stage 1 - Playoffs | 0 : 2 |  | Details |\n| March 26, 2026 - 17:00 CET | VCL EMEA: Stage 1 - Playoffs | 2 : 1 | MDR | Details |\n| March 23, 2026 - 19:30 CET | VCL EMEA: Stage 1 - Group C | W : FF |  | Details |\n| March 22, 2026 - 17:00 CET | VCL EMEA: Stage 1 - Group C | 2 : 0 |  | Details |\n\nKPI GamingKPI", "VCL Spain 2024: Split 2 - Round 12\n\nBar\u00e7a eSports\n\n| Date |  | Tournament | Score | | vs.", "Opponent |  |\n ---  ---  --- \n| March 21, 2026 - 19:50 CET | VCL EMEA: Stage 1 - Group B | VCL EMEA: Stage 1 - Group B |  | 1 : 2 | FKS | Details |\n| March 19, 2026 - 17:00 CET | VCL EMEA: Stage 1 - Group B | VCL EMEA: Stage 1 - Group B |  | 0 : 2 | EP | Details |\n| March 8, 2026 - 11:00 CET | VCL Spain: Stage 2 - Playoffs | VCL Spain: Stage 2 - Playoffs |  | 3 : 1 | DSY | Details |\n| March 7, 2026 - 13:50 CET | VCL Spain: Stage 2 - Playoffs | VCL Spain: Stage 2 - Playoffs |  | 2 : 0 | UCAM | Details |\n| March 1, 2026 - 13:40 CET | VCL Spain: Stage 2 - Group B | VCL Spain: Stage 2 - Group B |  | 2 : 1 | NOVO | Details |\n\nVCL EMEA: Stage 1 - Grou