{"run_id": "2ddade8b-5c9e-4aed-86b8-c934e1763670", "timestamp": "2026-04-08T09:45:11.583713+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1828734", "question": "LoL: Ninjas in Pyjamas vs Invictus Gaming (BO3) - LPL Group Ascend", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Ninjas in Pyjamas and Invictus Gaming in the LPL Group Ascend, initially scheduled for April 8 at 5:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Ninjas in Pyjamas\" if Ninjas in Pyjamas win the match against Invictus Gaming.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Invictus Gaming\" if Invictus Gaming win the match against Ninjas in Pyjamas.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-08T15:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-08T09:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.465, "volume_usd": 158772.21760599996, "category": "league-of-legends"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.46, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.27, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: Match must occur and produce a winner (NiP vs IG, best-of-3 format). Resolution criteria are clear: NiP winning = YES, IG winning = NO. Forfeit/walkover before start = 50-50. Cancellation/tie beyond 7 days = 50-50. EXECUTION RISK: Match is TODAY (5 hours until scheduled start, 5 hours until market end). Both teams confirmed in LPL 2026 Split 2. No cancellation/delay signals in briefing. High probability match executes as scheduled. COMPETITIVE ANALYSIS GAP: Briefing contains zero performance data. No recent match records, win/loss percentages, player rosters, patch synergies, head-to-head history, or form metrics provided. Search results explicitly note 'Limited direct performance data is available'. MARKET PRICING ANALYSIS: Current prices show YES at 46% / NO at 53% (near parity, slight NO lean). This ~7-point spread likely reflects modest market confidence in IG as slight favorite in LPL domestic competition, but pricing does not indicate a strong predictive signal without underlying form data. TEAM CONTEXT: NiP is traditionally an international/Western org; competing in LPL domestic league is strategically notable. IG is LPL-native powerhouse. Context suggests IG may hold structural advantage in domestic LPL play, but no concrete evidence provided. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Cannot defensibly estimate P(YES) or P(NO) from available data. Current market price (46% YES) is anchored to trading activity, not fundamental ana