ts either contrarian positioning or that IG has recent documented dominance not reflected in the briefing. ABSENCE-OF-SIGNAL: Briefing explicitly states 'Limited direct performance data is available'\u2014yet the NO side (IG) is still priced at 53%. This pricing assumes IG superiority without evidence, suggesting misprice opportunity on YES side. BLACK SWAN: NiP may have discovered a scrim-tested meta adaptation or roster chemistry edge (e.g., new jungler synergy, AP bot lane pocket pick) that doesn't show in public scrims but is live-tested in Week 2. IG, as a legacy LPL fixture, may be predictable to aggressive international scouts. WEEK 2 TIMING: Early season group stage\u2014teams are still calibrating. NiP, as a non-Chinese org, may have structural preparation advantages (bootcamp discipline, anti-meta scouting) that raw win-loss records don't capture. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes=35 (weak hand on evidence) and confidence_no=42 (slightly stronger, but still weak) reflect that BOTH sides lack data. NO side is NOT strongly supported\u2014just assumed. LIVE EVENT RISK: Resolves in ~5 hours. If match has started or is about to start, shares will rapidly trade to extreme (0.01 or 0.99) as outcome becomes clear. Current pricing at 46/53 suggests pre-match uncertainty, not settled confidence. CONTRARIAN POSITION: Council likely anchors on 'IG in LPL = domestic strong' without questioning whether NiP's international discipline or recent roster moves create a live upset vector.", "key_factor": "NiP's recent scrim performance or meta specialization (AP-heavy comps, lane-swap tactics) exploits IG's known weaknesses in a format where the briefing provides zero direct performance data on either team."}], "final_score": 0.4616129032258065, "no_score": 0.5390178571428571, "edge": -0.003387096774193521, "no_edge": 0.004017857142857184, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 54% for NO (need \u226557%); NO-side confidence too low: 32% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1828734", "question": "LoL: Ninjas in Pyjamas vs Invictus Gaming (BO3) - LPL Group Ascend", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Ninjas in Pyjamas and Invictus Gaming in the LPL Group Ascend, initially scheduled for April 8 at 5:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Ninjas in Pyjamas\" if Ninjas in Pyjamas win the match against Invictus Gaming.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Invictus Gaming\" if Invictus Gaming win the match against Ninjas in Pyjamas.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-08T15:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-08T09:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.465, "volume_usd": 158772.21760599996, "category": "league-of-legends"}, "key_facts": ["LPL 2026 Split 2 is an offline Chinese LoL tournament organized by TJ Sports.", "This S-Tier tournament takes place from Apr 04 to Jun 2026 featuring 14 teams", "The 2026 Esports World Cup is an upcoming multi-game esports tournament held in Riyadh, Saudi Arabia, hosted by the Esports World Cup Foundation (EWCF) and ESL", "LPL Split 2 2026 - Regular Season - Week 1-4.", "LPL Split 2 Week 2 continues on April 8 with Invictus Gaming vs Ninjas in Pyjamas and Team WE vs Top Esports.", "Track what Kalshi's markets predict for \"LPL 2026: Invictus Gaming vs.", "Ninjas in Pyjamas Map 2\", or trade it yourself.", "Ninjas in Pyjamas Map 1\", or trade it yourself.", "Ninjas in Pyjamas League of Legends match originally scheduled for Apr 8, 2026 at 5:00 AM EDT, then the market resolves to Yes.", "Don't miss the upcoming League of Legends match between Ninjas in Pyjamas and Invictus Gaming today, 8 April 2026."], "news_summary": "Ninjas in Pyjamas and Invictus Gaming are scheduled to face off in the LPL 2026 Split 2 regular season on April 8, 2026, as part of Group Ascend. This is an offline S-Tier tournament organized by TJ Sports running from April through June 2026 with 14 participating teams. The match was tracked on prediction markets including Kalshi with individual map winner markets available. Limited direct performance data is available in the search results to assess current form or head-to-head dynamics between these two teams.", "side_yes_case": ["Match officially scheduled and confirmed for April 8, 2026 with market verification via Sofascore", "Invictus Gaming competing in LPL's prem