dicating meaningful win probability", "Insomnia's upper semifinals appearance indicates they've beaten other lower-bracket teams", "Murash Gaming previously lost 0-2 to FENNEL and REIGNITE FOXX, showing vulnerability"], "key_context": ["Double-elimination Lower Round 2 match; loser is eliminated from playoffs contention", "Best of 3 (Bo3) format reduces variance compared to single maps", "Tournament structure: Phase 2 is continuation of VALORANT Challengers 2026: Japan Split 1", "Recent head-to-head: Murash 2-0 Insomnia on Feb 4, 2026 in earlier phase", "Match details pending player stats and map selection information"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-07T23:54:18.715998Z"}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-08T10:10:00Z", "winning_side": "NO", "final_yes_price": 0.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-08T10:46:10.514730+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": {"kind": "wrong_buy", "summary": "Wrong BUY YES \u2014 only 1/7 agents called NO (winner); loudest wrong voice: The Rules Lawyer (72%)", "agents_with_winner": [{"agent": "The Bear", "prob": 0.42, "side": "NO", "side_conf": 0.58, "key_factor": "Insomnia's recent upper-bracket semifinal run demonstrates adaptive gameplay and tournament momentum that may have closed the skill gap since the February 2-0 loss to Murash."}], "agents_against_winner": [{"agent": "The Rules Lawyer", "prob": 0.62, "side": "YES", "side_conf": 0.72, "key_factor": "Match scheduled for April 8 12:00 AM ET (~10 hours away); insufficient recent performance data on current team rosters and meta adaptation since Feb 4 head-to-head; forfeiture/walkover risk could trigger 50-50 resolution."}, {"agent": "The Bull", "prob": 0.64, "side": "YES", "side_conf": 0.72, "key_factor": "Murash Gaming's recent 2-0 momentum victory over RIDDLE ORDER combined with a decisive 2-0 head-to-head precedent against Insomnia in the same tournament."}, {"agent": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "prob": 0.62, "side": "YES", "side_conf": 0.72, "key_factor": "In competitive esports double-elimination lower bracket matches between teams with clear recent form differentials (win streak vs. recent loss), the favored team wins approximately 60-68% of the time in Bo3 formats."}, {"agent": "The Sentiment Analyst", "prob": 0.64, "side": "YES", "side_conf": 0.72, "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent": "The Domain Specialist", "prob": 0.64, "side": "YES", "side_conf": 0.72, "key_factor": "In double-elimination lower bracket matches, momentum and recent map pool adjustments often outweigh historical head-to-head records; Murash's 2-0 win streak and superior betting odds (1.54 vs 2.32) indicate current form advantage, but Insomnia's upper semifinals run (beating teams to reach that stage) suggests adaptive capability that could narrow the gap."}, {"agent": "The Contrarian", "prob": 0.64, "side": "YES", "side_conf": 0.72, "key_factor": "Insomnia deploys a radical map-pool strategy or recent patch exploit that directly counters Murash's core agent compositions, compounded by motivation asymmetry (Murash overconfident after 2-0 vs RIDDLE ORDER; Insomnia facing elimination desperation)."}], "median_prob": 0.64, "coin_flip": false}}
{"run_id": "72caa34a-3172-46b4-8072-92decea58d59", "timestamp": "2026-04-08T08:09:38.317179+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1846508", "question": "Valorant: T1 Academy vs DRX Academy (BO3) - VCL Korea: Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant Lower bracket quarterfinal 1 match between T1 Academy and DRX Academy in the VCL Korea: Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 8 at 4:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"T1 Academy\" if T1 Academy win the match against DRX Academy.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"DRX Academy\" if DRX Academy win the match against T1 Academy.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to