m 50-50. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: With event happening in ~6 hours and no performance data available, both confidence_yes and confidence_no must remain low (~27-28). Market price of 54/46 is used as baseline due to complete information asymmetry. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: VLR.gg will publish official results; secondary sources available within 2 hours. No mechanism risk identified for a completed match with clear winner.", "key_factor": "Briefing provides no substantive performance data, head-to-head records, current roster compositions, or recent form for either T1 Academy or DRX Academy, making any probability estimate speculative rather than evidence-based."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.54, "confidence_yes": 0.32, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "MARKET SIGNAL: YES is priced at 54% (slight favorite), suggesting marginal confidence in T1 Academy over DRX Academy. This narrow spread indicates genuine uncertainty. T1 ADVANTAGES: T1 is a historically elite Korean esports organization with strong infrastructure, player development systems, and competitive pedigree. Academy rosters typically benefit from parent org resources and talent pipelines. DRX COMPETITIVE STANDING: DRX is also a historically competitive Korean organization with proven academy pipelines. Both are tier-1 Korean orgs with similar structural advantages, limiting differentiation. CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing provides NO recent match statistics, head-to-head records, current roster compositions, or form data for either academy team. No VODs available. ACADEMY-LEVEL UNPREDICTABILITY: Academy matches are inherently volatile\u2014rosters may include developing talent with inconsistent performance. Without individual player form data or recent matchups, predictive power is severely limited. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS: DRX Academy has no documented disadvantages in the briefing. Both teams operate under similarly resourced parent organizations. The 8-point spread cannot be justified by organizational