s infrastructure claim but receives less weight in market pricing. DRX's academy development record is not actually scrutinized in briefing. ACADEMY-LEVEL UNPREDICTABILITY: Briefing notes 'Academy match outcomes often unpredictable without current roster and form information.' This cuts both ways but favors underdogs \u2014 upsets are MORE common in low-information environments where favorites are priced on brand rather than current performance. ROSTER COMPOSITION UNKNOWN: No player stats, roster lists, or recent performance metrics provided for either T1A or DRX A. The provided player tables appear incomplete/garbled and don't clarify which players are currently active on either academy roster. NO RECENT FORM DATA: Zero recent match results, win-loss records, or momentum indicators for either academy team in current season. Both teams are black boxes \u2014 T1's 54% pricing reflects organizational assumption, not demonstrated recent superiority. MURPHY'S LAW ON T1 FAVORITE: Market may be overweighting T1 brand recognition and parent-org pedigree. If T1A has roster instability, player rotations, or is fielding developmental talent, the infrastructure advantage evaporates. Favorites in low-information playoffs often fail due to complacency. DRX UNDERDOG UPSIDE: DRX's academy pipeline claim suggests consistent player development. If DRX A's roster has team cohesion, recent synergy, or chemistry advantages, they could exploit T1A's potentially less-integrated roster. BO3 FORMAT EFFECT: Best-of-3 introduces variance \u2014 upsets are likelier in multi-map formats where momentum swings and map-pick strategy matter. Single dominant performance sufficient to take match. TIMING PRESSURE: Event is TODAY (6 hours to match at ~2:00 AM ET / 4:00 AM KST). Market will resolve imminently. Late moves toward NO likely signal smart money recognizing DRX value or T1 concern. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Both confidence scores are low (~35-38%) because briefing data is genuinely insufficient. Cannot build strong conviction on either side from provided material. This argues for near-50 probability, but T1's 54% pricing on brand alone justifies slight DRX lean. FINAL PROBABILITY RATIONALE: Setting NO at 46% (matching market) rather than pushing lower reflects genuine uncertainty. DRX is not mispriced as egregiously undervalued as some academy upsets, but market's 54-46 split appears driven by organizational brand rather than form \u2014 slight underdog value exists for DRX.", "key_factor": "DRX's historically competitive pipeline and academy development system creates parity with T1 Academy despite market favoring T1, while severe data gaps make predictive confidence unreliable for both sides."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.5, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing provides no recent head-to-head records, current roster compositions, recent form data, or player performance metrics for either T1 Academy or DRX Academy. NO MATCH HISTORY: Search results explicitly state 'minimal direct information about recent form, head-to-head records, or team composition for either academy squad' and 'No recent match statistics...provided.' ACADEMY-LEVEL UNCERTAINTY: Academy team performance is inherently less predictable than main roster matches due to roster flux, variable preparation, and lower competition consistency. PARENT ORG SIGNAL (WEAK): T1 and DRX are both tier-1 Korean Valorant organizations with strong infrastructure, making this roughly a coin flip at organizational level. Historical T1 dominance in main roster does not reliably transfer to academy performance. EVENT TIMING CAVEAT: Match is TODAY/LIVE (resolves in ~6 hours). At this stage, near-zero time remains for market-moving information. Current 54% YES price reflects minimal additional data vs. baseline. MARKET PRICE ANALYSIS: 54/46 split (YES $0.54, NO $0.46) is very close to 50-50, consistent with genuine uncertainty. No strong mispricing signal detected. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Both confidence scores set to 25 (LOW) because briefing data is insufficient to justify confidence in EITHER side. No meaningful performance metrics, lineup info, or recent trends provided for either team. BASE RATE FOR ACADEMY MATCHUPS: Academy esports matches typically resolve near 50-50 absent specific roster/form data, particularly in tier-2 regional competitions. VERDICT: Genuine coin flip. Probability anchored to 50 due to complete data absence for both competitors.", "key_factor": "Academy-level esports matchups lack consistent historical base rates; parent org strength (T1 vs DRX) provides weak signal (~45-55% range for tier-1 org academies)"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.52, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.27, "rationale": "Market is essentially a coin flip at 54/46, reflecting profound data scarcity rather than genuine confidence in either direction. Briefing contains NO recent match statistics, head-to-head records, current rosters, or form data for either T1 Academy or DRX Academy. T1 org infrastructure heuristic is offset by DRX's equally strong academy pipeline \u2014 both are tier-1 Korean orgs with comparable development systems. Academy-level competition is inherently high-variance; roster stability and player form matter more than org pedigree, but neither is documented in briefing. The 54% YES price suggests marginal bias toward T1 (possibly brand equity or org size), but this bias is not anchored in actionable evidence. Search results mention VCL Korea tier-2 context but provide zero tactical, recent-form, or head-to-head data to justify deviation from 50/50. With ~6 hours to match start (TODAY timing), no new intel is likely to emerge; market is pricing on institutional guesses, not signal. Both confidence scores are LOW (27-28) because briefing data is critically insufficient for either side \u2014 cannot evaluate strengths/weaknesses of academy rosters. Rational apathy detected: market is not panicking or euphoric, just reflecting genuine uncertainty with a negligible brand-equity lean toward YES. No ignored signals or crowded trades visible \u2014 the crowd is correctly admitting ignorance via near-parity pricing.", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.52, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.27, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains no recent match results, head-to-head records, or current roster compositions for either T1 Academy or DRX Academy\u2014these are essential inputs for academy-level prediction. ORGANIZATIONAL PRESTIGE vs. ACADEMY PERFORMANCE: While T1 and DRX are both Tier 1 Korean orgs, academy rosters often field developing talent, not org infrastructure quality; academy results poorly correlate with main roster strength. MATCH TIMING: Event is TODAY/LIVE (resolves ~6 hours from briefing timestamp); shares will likely trade toward $0.01 or $0.99 once match begins, suggesting market may already have embedded information from live play if match has commenced. CURRENT MARKET PRICING (54% YES / 46% NO): Modest 8-point spread suggests near-even assessment by market participants; consistent with structural uncertainty when detailed team data is unavailable. ACADEMY-TIER UNPREDICTABILITY: VCL Korea academy matches exhibit high variance in outcomes due to roster volatility, player development asymmetries, and limited public scrim/practice data; predictive confidence must remain low. INSUFFICIENT COUNTER-EVIDENCE: Briefing provides no DRX Academy-specific performance metrics, recent tournament results, or head-to-head history to justify confidence in either outcome direction. RESOLUTION SOURCE (vlr.gg): Market will rely on official VCL Korea reporting; no ambiguity risk noted in resolution criteria, but lack of pre-match data prevents substantive probability calibration. EXPERT ASSESSMENT: A 20+ year esports analyst would require current roster sheets, recent scrim results, agent pool trends (meta shifts between seasons), and individual player form data\u2014NONE of which are in the briefing.", "key_factor": "Academy-tier Valorant matches lack the established meta dominance and roster stability of main rosters, making predictive power from organizational prestige (T1 vs DRX) unreliable without current player form, agent pool mastery, and recent scrim/match data."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.52, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.27, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains NO recent performance stats, head-to-head records, current roster compositions, or win/loss streaks for either T1A or DRX Academy\u2014making ANY confident probability estimate unreliable. MARKET SIGNAL MISMATCH: 54-46 split suggests weak consensus; if either team had demonstrable recent form advantage, market would be wider (62-38 or tighter at parity). This narrowness screams 'both teams equally opaque to market participants.' ACADEMY VOLATILITY: Academy rosters are inherently less stable than main teams. Injuries, roster churning, and player development trajectories create hidden form variations absent from aggregate stats. KOREAN ESPORTS CONTEXT: VCL Korea academy matches often involve players on trial or in development; motivation and familiarity with teammates can vary wildly match-to-match, creating underrated variance. ABSENCE SIGNAL\u2014RECENT VODs UNAVAILABLE: Briefing explicitly states 'VODs Unavailable,' preventing public review of recent team gameplay, coordination quality, or tactical adaptation\u2014a red flag for prediction confidence. BLACK SWAN: Last-minute roster substitution (illness, personal emergency, visa delay) is plausible in academy esports where bench depth is shallow. A stand-in joining a BO3 high-stress playoff match could cause communication breakdowns, positioning confusion, or morale collapse\u2014far more impactful than raw individual skill. TIMING PRESSURE: Match is TODAY (~6 hours). If a substitute is required, it will be chaotic and underreported until match begins. This creates a 5% scenario (substitute forced mid-event) with 50%+ swing potential. UNDERDOG HIDDEN FORM: DRX Academy may have outperformed recent tournament trends or adapted tactically since last publicized match; T1 Academy may be overrated due to org prestige rather than current squad performance. NO TIEBREAKER DATA: Briefing provides zero info on clutch-moment performance, map pool strengths, or how each team handles reverse sweeps in BO3 format under playoff pressure.", "key_factor": "A key player from either academy roster receives a last-minute illness, visa issue, or personal emergency requiring a stand-in, fundamentally altering team cohesion and communication in a high-pressure playoff BO3."}], "final_score": 0.5131372549019608, "no_score": 0.4884422110552763, "edge": -0.02686274509803921, "no_edge": 0.028442211055276334, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 51% for YES (need \u226557%); YES-side confidence too low: 29% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1846508", "question": "Valorant: T1 Academy vs DRX Academy (BO3) - VCL Korea: Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant Lower bracket quarterfinal 1 match between T1 Academy and DRX Academy in the VCL Korea: Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 8 at 4:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"T1 Academy\" if T1 Academy win the match against DRX Academy.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"DRX Academy\" if DRX Academy win the match against T1 Academy.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-08T14:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-08T08:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.54, "volume_usd": 22760.778068, "category": "valorant"}, "key_facts": ["Top Valorant esports teams rankings list and tiers in North America.", "Top Valorant esports teams rankings list and tiers in Asia-Pacific.", "Top Valorant esports teams rankings list and tiers in Japan.", "# T1 Academy\n\n## T1A\n\nwww.t1.gg   @T1\n\nSouth Korea\n\nOverview Stats Matches News Transactions\n\nMatches   Events  History\n\nStatus:\n\n Upcoming  Upcoming Completed  \n\nCore:\n\n All  None All #B223 #Q1O8  \n\nToggle Match Details\n\nVCL 26: Korea Split 1\n\nPlayoffs \u22c5 LR1\n\nT1 Academy   T1A\n\nLIVE\n\nDRX Academy   DRXA\n\nVODs\n\nUnavailable\n\n2:00 am\n\nContact\nPrivacy\n\n\u2022\n\nTerms\n\nFind us on:\n\n Twitter   Discord", "|  |  | R | ACS | K | D | A | +/\u2013 | KAST | ADR | HS% | FK | FD | +/\u2013 |\n ---  ---  ---  ---  ---  ---  --- |\n| hezacoil  REBO | astra vyse | 1.34 1.37 1.35 | 220 227 239 | 36 22 14 | /  24 13 11 / | 19 9 10 | +12 +9 +3 | 87% 96% 74% | 153 148 160 | 33% 46% 24% | 7 3 4 | 1 0 1 | +6 +3 +3 |\n| Kachoww  REBO | neon | 1.27 1.38 1.32 | 252 249 248 | 40 24 16 | /  27 16 11 / | 11 6 5 | +13 +8 +5 | 78% 85% 68% | 161 167 152 | 24% 26% 22% | 7 3 4 | 6 4 2 | +1 -1 +2 |\n| batujnax  REBO | skye fade | 1.62 0.80 1.28 | 245 300 146 | 39 30 9 | /  27 14 13 / | 12 6 6 | +12 +16 -4 | 80% 96% 58% | 154 186 110 | 23% 25% 20% | 4 4 0 | 5 2 3 | -1 +2 -3 | [...] |  |  | R | ACS | K | D | A | +/\u2013 | KAST | ADR | HS% | FK | FD | +/\u2013 |\n ---  ---  ---  ---  ---  ---  --- |\n| Kachoww  REBO | neon | 1.59 1.20 2.55 | 263 220 368 | 17 10 7 | /  8 8 0 / | 5 3 2 | +9 +2 +7 | 88% 83% 100% | 171 153 216 | 17% 26% 8% | 2 1 1 | 0 0 0 | +2 +1 +1 |\n| batujnax  REBO | skye | 1.49 1.77 0.81 | 287 354 127 | 18 16 2 | /  9 7 2 / | 4 1 3 | +9 +9 0 | 88% 100% 60% | 192 233 95 | 35% 48% 7% | 3 3 0 | 3 2 1 | 0 +1 -1 |\n| reazy  REBO | omen | 1.45 1.05 2.42 | 281 225 417 | 17 9 8 | /  10 9 1 / | 7 5 2 | +7 0 +7 | 88% 83% 100% | 171 147 229 | 29% 25% 35% | 2 1 1 | 1 1 0 | +1 0 +1 |\n| hezacoil  REBO | astra | 1.14 0.87 1.78 | 169 145 228 | 10 6 4 | /  8 7 1 / | 12 6 6 | +2 -1 +3 | 94% 92% 100% | 104 90 137 | 35% 33% 36% | 1 0 1 | 0 0 0 | +1 0 +1 | [...] |  |  | R | ACS | K | D | A | +/\u2013 | KAST | ADR | HS% | FK | FD | +/\u2013 |\n ---  ---  ---  ---  ---  ---  --- |\n| Whiteslow  FF | cypher | 1.20 2.00 0.41 | 245 382 109 | 25 20 5 | /  18 6 12 / | 3 1 2 | +7 +14 -7 | 64% 79% 50% | 162 244 80 | 34% 35% 30% | 3 3 0 | 1 1 0 | +2 +2 0 |\n| deminatiX  FF | sova | 1.13 1.10 1.15 | 282 249 315 | 26 12 14 | /  21 9 12 / | 4 1 3 | +5 +3 +2 | 79% 79% 79% | 165 140 189 | 29% 14% 46% | 4 1 3 | 4 2 2 | 0 -1 +1 |\n| ef1sS  FF | omen | 0.67 0.52 0.82 | 162 86 238 | 14 4 10 | /  21 8 13 / | 5 2 3 | -7 -4 -3 | 61% 64% 57% | 112 62 161 | 25% 16% 30% | 2 0 2 | 4 2 2 | -2 -2 0 |\n| pAwn1  FF | breach | 0.67 1.12 0.22 | 124 202 46 | 12 10 2 | /  21 8 13 / | 6 4 2 | -9 +2 -11 | 61% 79% 43% | 93 137 49 | 34% 45% 15% | 2 2 0 | 2 2 0 | 0 0 0 |", "Nice\n\nFinals weekend\n\nEven only Valve-partnered third party events are the only ones counted to the VRS and Majors system.", "EWC doesn't even affect the VCT circuit at all except bragging rights\n\nDue to the swap between ULF and Eternal Fire, please re-do your pickems.", "The official statement by Riot is that EF will retain a team in VCL Turkiye, so we'll expect some sort of academy team for the current roster\n\nThen don't believe them easily?", "Yeah but at this point DRG has international experience comparable to Tier 1 teams and have been competing in the upper echelon, while AQ is formed with pieces from all over [...] What China is going through is basically what EVERY region is going through at the start of the 23-24 season.", "The blur between T1 and T2 is catching up to the partnership teams that were hastily put."], "news_summary": "T1 Academy and DRX Academy are set to compete in a VCL Korea Playoffs Lower Round 1 (BO3) match. The search results indicate the match is scheduled or upcoming on VLR.gg but provide minimal direct information about recent form, head-to-head records, or team composition for either academy squad. No substantive performance data, roster changes, or contextual analysis specific to this matchup was found in the available search results.", "side_yes_case": ["Insufficient data in search results to establish comparative strengths", "T1 organization historically has strong infrastructure and player development systems", "Academy teams reflect parent org competitive positioning within Korean Valorant ecosystem"], "side_no_case": ["Insufficient data in search results to establish comparative weaknesses", "DRX is a historically competitive Korean organization with strong academy pipeline", "Academy match outcomes often unpredictable without current roster and form information"], "key_context": ["Match format: Best of 3 (BO3) in VCL Korea Playoffs Lower Round 1", "No recent match statistics, head-to-head records, or current roster compositions provided", "Academy-level competition adds uncertainty compared to main roster matches", "VCL Korea represents tier 2 competitive level in Korean Valorant ecosystem", "Search results lack VODs, detailed match history, and player performance metrics for either team"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-08T08:09:25.692155Z"}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-08T14:10:00Z", "winning_side": "YES", "final_yes_price": 1.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-08T20:14:07.170159+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "9bfd9dcc-7f75-4ca0-b2aa-3d798c2200df", "timestamp": "2026-04-08T09:43:03.865888+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1909431", "question": "Counter-Strike: Brute vs INFURITY Gaming (BO3) - United21 Group C", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Decider match between Brute and INFURITY Gaming in the United21 Group C, initially scheduled for April 8 at 4:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Brute\" if Brute win the match against INFURITY Gaming.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"INFURITY Gaming\" if INFURITY Gaming win the match against Brute.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-08T14:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-08T08:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.6, "volume_usd": 22596.561105000023, "category": "counter-strike"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: Market resolves YES if Brute wins the BO3 match; NO if INFURITY Gaming wins. Criteria are clear and unambiguous regarding the match outcome itself. CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing provides no recent head-to-head history, map veto records, or comparative skill assessments between these two teams in Group C context. BRUTE EVIDENCE (LIMITED): Recent wins in NODWIN Clutch Series 7 (2-0 vs Rune Eaters, 2-1 in other matches) demonstrate some competitive activity and readiness, but these are qualifier matches, not Group C seeding data. BRUTE CONTEXT: Valve ranking of 736 points suggests roster stability, but briefing explicitly notes 'may be outdated (mentioned as old roster on HLTV ranking)', undermining the reliability of this signal. INFURITY GAMING: No performance data, roster composition, recent form, regional tier, or competitive history provided in briefing. Complete information vacuum on the NO side. MARKET PRICING: Current 60/40 split (YES at $0.60, NO at $0.40) reflects marginal confidence in Brute. This aligns loosely with the limited positive signals about Brute's recent activity, but does not reflect any substantive competitive advantage evidence. TIMING RISK (SECONDARY): Match is TODAY (resolves in ~4 hours). Insufficient time for major format changes, but pre-match upsets remain plausible in BO3 Counter-Strike without deep tactical/roster intelligence. ASYMMETRIC CONFIDENCE: Brute has at least some recent match history cited (even if qualifier-level and from generic source). INFURITY Gaming has zero briefing support for either strength or weakness. This justifies lower confidence on the NO side. PROBABILITY ASSESSMENT: Market pricing of 60% YES appears slightly optimistic given the data parity. Without head-to-head records, map compatibility, or United21-specific form data, a true 50-50 would be defensible. Slight upside to Brute (58% vs 42%) reflects marginal edge from demonstrated recent competitive activity in a qualifier context, not strategic superiority. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: HLTV.org publication within 2 hours post-match, or credible consensus thereafter. No ambiguity in team naming (both names are clear and match standard CS rosters). Mechanism risk is low.", "key_factor": "Insufficient competitive intelligence on both teams' current form, head-to-head history, map pool compatibility, and meta alignment in United21 Group C specifically; briefing data is largely generic background with one outdated reference to BRUTE's 'old roster'."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.68, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "BRUTE MOMENTUM: Recent wins in NODWIN Clutch Series 7 (2-0 vs Rune Eaters, 2-1 in other matches) show active competitive engagement and demonstrable ability to string together map wins in BO3 format, directly relevant to today's BO3 task. BRUTE STRUCTURAL ADVANTAGE: Valve ranking of 736 points indicates roster stability and recognized tier status; this baseline credibility supports the 60% market pricing as reasonable. MARKET CONSENSUS ALIGNMENT: YES at 60% reflects modest but real confidence in BRUTE\u2014not an extreme overpriced position; suggests market has incorporated available data fairly. INFURITY GAMING OPACITY: No roster data, recent form, region, or head-to-head history provided in briefing. Complete absence of counter-evidence leaves the underdog case weak; market pricing INFURITY at 40% appears justified by information vacuum. DOUBLE-ELIMINATION SAFETY: While this is a Group C match in GSL format, both teams can lose once and advance; BRUTE's recent wins suggest they are more likely the stronger team fighting to stay in upper bracket, not the team scrambling from lower bracket. TIMING RISK (MINOR): Match resolves TODAY in ~4 hours with high volumes ($22.6k), indicating genuine liquidity and no obvious liquidity trap; late timing does not create unusual reversal opportunity. WEAKNESSES OF NO CASE: INFURITY Gaming's case rests entirely on 'limited data about BRUTE' and 'unspecified roster composition'\u2014these are absence-of-evidence arguments, not evidence-of-absence. Without positive data on INFURITY's recent form or head-to-head edge, the 40% price may actually be generous to the underdog. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in YES (68) because BRUTE's recent match results are concrete and recent; lower confidence in NO (35) because INFURITY Gaming has no supporting data in the briefing at all\u2014market may be underestimating BRUTE's true advantage due to information imbalance. MAP POOL & META UNKNOWNS: Briefing does not detail team-specific map strengths or Group C meta; this cuts both ways but slightly favors the team (BRUTE) with visible recent form over the team (INFURITY) with no data. PROBABILITY ASSESSMENT: 62% reflects BRUTE as legitimate favorite with recent match proof, but acknowledges meaningful uncertainty from INFURITY Gaming's complete data absence and the inherent parity in BO3 online matches at this tier.", "key_factor": "BRUTE's recent competitive momentum from NODWIN Clutch Series 7 (2-0, 2-1 wins) demonstrates match readiness and form heading into this Group C decider."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.35, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "BRUTE's recent wins (2-0, 2-1 vs Rune Eaters in NODWIN) are against unknown/lower-tier opposition \u2014 no evidence these teams represent Group C caliber competition. BRUTE's 736 Valve ranking points suggest mid-tier EU status, NOT a dominant force; this is modest for a 'favored' side priced at 60%. Briefing explicitly flags BRUTE roster as 'old' per HLTV \u2014 potential structural instability or player fatigue not captured in market pricing. INFURITY Gaming is almost completely opaque: no roster names, no recent match data, no region confirmation. Market may be overconfiding in BRUTE simply due to higher information availability. GSL double-elimination format means this is a single BO3 decider in Group C \u2014 not a sustained series. Single-match volatility in CS favors upsets more than best-of-7 would. Match timing (TODAY, ~4 hours away) means near-zero time for market correction if new information emerges about either team's current form or roster issues. BRUTE has provided no map pool evidence, meta adaptation evidence, or performance consistency data beyond two NODWIN matches. This is insufficient to justify 60% confidence in a BO3 knockout. No head-to-head history provided; no evidence BRUTE counters INFURITY Gaming's likely play style or map preferences. The briefing notes 'Limited public information is available about INFURITY Gaming's recent form' \u2014 but also limited strategic/tactical analysis of BRUTE's vulnerabilities. Market pricing (60/40) appears driven by name recognition and NODWIN recency bias, not by deep competitive analysis of Group C meta or matchup dynamics. If INFURITY Gaming possesses specialized map picks or anti-meta strategies, BRUTE's 'old roster' may struggle to adapt mid-series; BO3 format allows for map-driven upsets. INFURITY Gaming's underdog status + information asymmetry + single BO3 format + imminent timing = elevated upset probability not reflected in 60/40 split. Conservative estimate: 35% for YES reflects skepticism about BRUTE's true Group C-caliber strength and heavy overweighting of limited NODWIN sample size by the market.", "key_factor": "INFURITY Gaming's actual roster composition, recent form, and map pool remain completely unspecified in the briefing, creating asymmetric information that favors the underdog in a coin-flip scenario."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.52, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing provides no reliable head-to-head history, current roster statistics (player ratings/recent demos), or opponent scouting for either team. BRUTE's recent wins (2-0 vs Rune Eaters, 2-1 in NODWIN Clutch Series 7) are positive but come against unknown-tier opposition; no map pool, anti-strat data, or calibration against INFURITY available. INFURITY Gaming's roster, recent form, map preferences, and playstyle are entirely absent from the briefing \u2014 this asymmetry in data does not justify a confident directional bet. Market price (YES 60% / NO 40%) suggests some participants have private information or access to team rankings/recent scrims, but briefing does not corroborate this divergence from 50-50. Event timing is TODAY with ~4 hours to resolution \u2014 insufficient time for major reversal; match will almost certainly play as scheduled (low forfeit/cancellation risk in organized qualifier). Double-elimination GSL format context is provided but does not inform win probability for this specific match (relevant only for downstream advancement). Base rate for ungoverned regional CS BO3 matches between similarly-tiered teams: ~48\u201352% win likelihood depends entirely on roster synergy, recent bootcamp results, and meta familiarity \u2014 none quantified here. Confidence in YES is LOW (28) because BRUTE's limited recent credential data does not distinguish them from INFURITY, and no opponent analysis exists. Confidence in NO is equally LOW (26) because INFURITY's complete absence from briefing leaves no basis to claim upset likelihood; this is genuine uncertainty, not a weakness case. Probability score set to 52 (slight lean toward market consensus YES) reflects mild deference to market price (60% YES) while heavily discounting confidence due to data vacuum; true fair value is likely 48\u201352.", "key_factor": "In competitive Counter-Strike BO3 group-stage matches between tier-2/tier-3 regional teams with sparse recent public data, outcomes cluster near 50-50 when prior head-to-head records and current roster form are unavailable."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "Market is pricing Brute at 60% YES despite severe data asymmetry favoring neither team decisively. Briefing provides concrete evidence of Brute's recent form (2-0 vs Rune Eaters, 2-1 other matches in NODWIN), establishing baseline competitive readiness. Valve ranking of 736 points suggests Brute has roster stability, a positive but not decisive signal. Critical gap: INFURITY Gaming has zero documented recent performance data, head-to-head history, or roster info in briefing. This asymmetry could reflect market knowledge (traders know INFURITY's weakness) OR market apathy (insufficient data attention). Event is TODAY with ~4 hours to resolution \u2014 limited time for new information to surface; current price likely reflects pre-match consensus. The 60/40 split is modest, not extreme \u2014 suggests market is cautiously favoring Brute without overconfidence. Briefing explicitly flags 'old roster' concern for Brute, introducing uncertainty about recent lineup stability. GSL double-elimination format is standard; no special advantage signal for either team from structure alone. Without INFURITY recent form data, confidence in either direction is suppressed \u2014 market may be accurately reflecting genuine uncertainty rather than misprice. Low volume ($22.6k) and imminent resolution timing suggest this is a niche/regional qualifier without strong information flow.", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.55, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "BRUTE demonstrated recent competitive activity (2-0 vs Rune Eaters, 2-1 in another match) in NODWIN Clutch Series 7, suggesting the roster is actively playing, but quality of opposition is unclear and recent \u2260 necessarily strong. BRUTE holds 736 Valve ranking points, indicating some established competitive pedigree, but Valve rankings reflect historical performance\u2014not current form 2-3 days before this event. The briefing explicitly notes BRUTE's roster may be 'old' on HLTV ranking, creating uncertainty about whether the lineup that won NODWIN matches is the same roster competing today. INFURITY Gaming has zero performance data in the briefing\u2014region unknown, recent form unknown, roster composition unknown; this asymmetry creates high epistemic uncertainty on the NO side. GSL double-elimination format means this Group C match is a single qualifier round; losing does not eliminate BRUTE from playoff contention (they drop to loser's bracket), reducing the stakes and potentially affecting preparation intensity. Market price of 60% YES reflects ~10-point premium over 50%, consistent with BRUTE having marginally more evidence of recent activity; however, the scarcity of INFURITY Gaming data prevents falsification of that premium. Timing: match resolves in ~4 hours (LIVE/IMMINENT); no time remains for roster changes or major new information; reliance on briefing data as-is. No head-to-head historical record, map veto tendencies, or anti-stratting information provided for either team; both are effectively opaque on the competitive meta-level. The briefing's 'Case for NO' accurately identifies the missing data: INFURITY Gaming roster and recent form are entirely unspecified, making a confident NO call impossible despite theoretical parity.", "key_factor": "BRUTE's recent 2-0 and 2-1 results in NODWIN Clutch Series 7 provide marginal evidence of current form, but these wins against unknown opposition (Rune Eaters appears to be lower-tier) do not reliably predict BO3 performance in a structured group stage with 4 equally-seeded competitors; the 'old roster' notation raises concerns about roster stability between qualifiers and this event."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing provides almost NO concrete information about either team's current form, map pool, or head-to-head history. The 60% YES price on Brute appears driven by recent NODWIN wins and Valve ranking presence, but this is thin evidence for a same-day BO3. INFURITY Gaming is completely opaque: no roster, no recent results, no region confirmed. The briefing's silence on the NO side is deafening\u2014this is classic market underpricing of unknown-but-plausible upsets in qualifier tournaments. BRUTE's 'old roster' tag (mentioned in KEY CONTEXT) suggests potential personnel uncertainty or recent changes. If the team listed in the market is not the same roster that earned those NODWIN wins, the wins are not predictive. Early morning match timing (4:00 AM ET / likely EU afternoon) favors teams with established schedules and sleep discipline. Qualifier-stage teams often have erratic preparation; a motivated underdog with better sleep/morale on game day is a genuine edge. Double-elimination group stage pressure differs from closed qualifier matches. BRUTE's NODWIN wins came in a lower-stakes environment; Group C advancement carries real playoff seeding implications. Underperformance under pressure is a classic qualifier upset vector. Market volume is moderate ($22.6k) but not high. This suggests limited sharp money and possible casual overweight on the higher-ranked/more-familiar name (Brute). Asymmetric information strongly favors the NO side here. Resolution criterion allows 50-50 ties on forfeit/disqualification. Qualifier-stage teams have higher admin/logistical failure rates. A mid-series technical dispute or unexpected walkover is low-probability but high-impact. No map pool or veto data provided. If Infurity has a specialist map Brute is weak on and forces it in veto, the series dynamic inverts. This is completely invisible in the briefing. Confidence in YES is LOW (35) because Brute's evidence is shallow and depends on old/unclear roster data. Confidence in NO is also relatively LOW (42) because Infurity is a complete unknown. This is a high-entropy market where the true probability could easily swing 20+ points on game-day roster confirmation or tactical preparation quality\u2014neither side deserves high confidence.", "key_factor": "INFURITY Gaming fields an unexpected roster substitution or tactical pivot (likely a ringer or fresh player) that exploits Brute's preparation gap, or Brute suffers a last-minute lineup disruption before the 4:00 AM ET start."}], "final_score": 0.5218211920529802, "no_score": 0.5058781362007169, "edge": -0.07817880794701981, "no_edge": 0.10587813620071684, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 52% for YES (need \u226557%); YES-side confidence too low: 43% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1909431", "question": "Counter-Strike: Brute vs INFURITY Gaming (BO3) - United21 Group C", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Decider match between Brute and INFURITY Gaming in the United21 Group C, initially scheduled for April 8 at 4:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Brute\" if Brute win the match against INFURITY Gaming.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"INFURITY Gaming\" if INFURITY Gaming win the match against Brute.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-08T14:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-08T08:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.6, "volume_usd": 22596.561105000023, "category": "counter-strike"}, "key_facts": ["Group Stage: Four double-elimination format (GSL) groups.", "Each group has 4 teams; All matches are Bo3.", "Top two teams from each group advance to the Playoffs.", "NODWIN Clutch Series 7 Closed Qualifier.", "Best of 3 (Online) * Group A opening match.", "This ranking includes matches and secured prize money from ...", "# RECENT ACTIVITY\n\n# MINIGAME\n\n# TOP 30 TRANSFERS\n\nLucas 'nqz' Soares\npaiN\npaiN\npaiN\npaiN\nKacper 'xKacpersky' Gabara\nNinjas in Pyjamas\nNinjas in Pyjamas\nNinjas in Pyjamas\nNinjas in Pyjamas\nJeorge 'Jeorge'  Endicott\nNRG\nVoca\nVoca\nDominik 'GruBy