 zero competitive intelligence on either team \u2014 no recent form, roster status, head-to-head records, or meta alignment. Search results are entirely contaminated with unrelated college basketball/golf content, indicating a retrieval failure rather than legitimate absence of data. MARKET STRUCTURE MISMATCH: 84% NO pricing reflects extreme confidence in GIANTX, yet the briefing provides NO supporting evidence for this conviction. The confidence gap between market price and available data is a red flag. BLACK SWAN \u2014 ADMINISTRATIVE/TECHNICAL: Event is TODAY/IMMINENT (3 hours to match start). Resolution criteria explicitly allow 50-50 outcomes for forfeits, walkovers, disqualifications, or matches not completed within 7 days. With zero pre-match briefing, lineup uncertainty, or patch deployment timing unknown, risk of a disruption forcing 50-50 resolution is material and under-priced. BLACK SWAN \u2014 ROSTER VOLATILITY: VCT EMEA Group Omega context unknown; no confirmation that both rosters are finalized or that key players are available. A last-minute illness, visa issue, or substitute could fundamentally alter match dynamics \u2014 especially relevant in esports where individual skill variance is extreme. MARKET PRICING ASSUMES CONSENSUS: The 84% NO reflects a strong narrative about GIANTX superiority, but this narrative is entirely absent from the briefing. This suggests either: (a) the market is correct and the briefing failed to retrieve relevant stats, or (b) the market is pricing a consensus that may not hold under pressure. CONFIDENCE SYMMETRY: Both confidence_yes and confidence_no are deliberately LOW (22\u201324) because the briefing is essentially blank. A coin flip (50%) would be more honest than 16%, but the market has priced heavily. Accepting the market's view without data verification is irrational. META/PATCH UNKNOWN: Valorant patches and meta shifts can dramatically favor one team's playstyle over another. The briefing is silent on current patch, map pool, and which agent/composition advantage either team holds. CONTRARIAN LENS: If this market is indeed mispriced at 84% NO, the error is likely a momentum/consensus cascade, not evidence-driven. The absence of data supporting GIANTX's dominance is itself a signal that the market may be over-confident.", "key_factor": "A last-minute roster substitution, technical pause extending beyond match window, or server instability forces a 50-50 resolution despite market pricing."}], "final_score": 0.2885135135135135, "no_score": 0.6977631578947369, "edge": 0.1300135135135135, "no_edge": -0.14373684210526316, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 22% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1856140", "question": "Valorant: Pcific Esports vs GIANTX (BO3) - VCT EMEA Group Omega", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between Pcific Esports and GIANTX in the VCT EMEA Group Omega, initially scheduled for April 8 at 11:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Pcific Esports\" if Pcific Esports win the match against GIANTX.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"GIANTX\" if GIANTX win the match against Pcific Esports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus o