 are common, and map-veto advantage (unknown from briefing) can swing series; raw ranking alone does not determine BO3 outcomes. Regain roster includes fuzenko (Ukraine, Rating 1.18) and Zucar (Rating 1.18)\u2014both above-average performers by stats; InControl individual player stats unavailable for direct comparison. Event timing: match occurs TODAY with resolution ~7 hours away; no late-breaking roster changes, health issues, or technical failures are documented that would invalidate the matchup. InControl's recent Inferno result (13-7 vs F5) shows competitive play but does not establish superiority over regain\u2014opponent strength unclear. Briefing lacks: (1) regain's world ranking, (2) head-to-head history, (3) map-pool strengths for either team, (4) recent InControl playoff performance trajectory. This asymmetric data gap limits confidence in both directions. Market price (30% YES, 70% NO) suggests analytical consensus favors regain; this aligns with regain's recent win streak but may overweight recent form vs. structural ranking advantage. Lower Bracket Final context: regain entered with wins vs TSG, FlyQuest RED, Zomblers (Apr 3-6), suggesting regain earned this matchup; InControl's bracket path less documented.", "key_factor": "In Challenger League BO3 formats, map-veto dynamics and team-specific map pools matter more than raw ranking; InControl's #159 HLTV ranking is meaningful but incomplete without regain's ranking and recent head-to-head or mirror-match performance data."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "regain has logged a remarkable recent run: 2-0 vs FlyQuest RED (Apr 3), 2-0 vs TSG (Apr 4), 2-1 vs Zomblers (Apr 6), and 2-1 vs Akimbo (Apr 7), indicating a sharp upward trajectory into the playoffs. InControl's #159 world ranking is a historical data point with unknown recency; if it predates the last 2-4 weeks, it may not reflect roster changes, player form decay, or recent losses in this exact tournament structure. The briefing shows InControl as favorites (30% YES price = 70% NO price), yet provides minimal regain comparative data\u2014only roster names and partial stats. This information asymmetry is a classic market inefficiency favoring the underdog. regain's roster includes fuzenko (Ukraine, 1.18 Rating 3.0), Zucar (1.18 Rating 3.0), and dvrk (1.04 Rating 3.0) with 7 months stability\u2014competitive depth that contradicts a weak underdog narrative. Lower-bracket finals under high-intensity playoff pressure can favor momentum teams over seeded favorites, particularly in C-Tier ESL events where roster consistency is volatile. InControl's last visible ESL result is a 2-0 win vs F5 (Apr 5), but no subsequent playoff match data is provided; regain has visibly competed in parallel tournaments 2 days before this match, suggesting fresher gameplay rhythm. A BO3 format requires 2-map consistency; if InControl struggles on regain's comfort maps or if a key InControl player (KmZ, C0C0, twigs) underperforms, regain's balanced roster could exploit map-specific weaknesses. The market is pricing InControl at 30% (YES) based on ranking alone; regain's recent win streak and lack of visible weaknesses in the briefing suggest market overconfidence in the seeded favorite.", "key_factor": "regain's recent 7-game win streak (4-2 in ESL Cup #3 + dominant 2-1 performance in parallel Dust2.us series) combined with momentum-driven playoff performance could upset InControl's higher seed, especially if InControl's #159 ranking reflects older roster data and lacks recent LAN verification."}], "final_score": 0.3484251968503937, "no_score": 0.6714814814814816, "edge": 0.0434251968503937, "no_edge": -0.023518518518518494, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 54% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1918242", "question": "Counter-Strike: InControl vs regain (BO3) - ESL Challenger League North America Cup #3 Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Lower bracket final match between InControl and regain in the ESL Challenger League North America Cup #3 Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 8 at 9:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"InControl\" if InControl win the match against regain.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"regain\" if regain win the match against InControl.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot 