king (#159) compared to available data on regain", "InControl appears to have more recent tournament activity and roster stability in ESL events", "InControl won Inferno 13-7 against F5 in a recent ESL Challenger League Season 51 match on 2026-04-05"], "side_no_case": ["Limited recent head-to-head or comparative performance data between InControl and regain available", "regain's roster includes international talent (fuzenko from Ukraine) suggesting competitive depth", "InControl's recent result (13-7 win) suggests potentially beatable opposition in the bracket"], "key_context": ["Match format: Best of 3 (BO3) in ESL Challenger League Season 51 North America Cup #3 Playoffs", "Both teams compete in C-Tier online tournament structure typical of Challenger League events", "Recent InControl map result shows Inferno play on 2026-04-07, suggesting active preparation", "ESL Challenger League is developmental tier with roster changes and varying consistency", "Limited comprehensive statistics available for regain compared to InControl in search results"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-09T00:08:00.389789Z"}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-09T07:00:00Z", "winning_side": "YES", "final_yes_price": 1.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-09T09:52:07.580204+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "39718e94-facb-48f5-821c-11890763750a", "timestamp": "2026-04-09T00:11:47.324730+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1919665", "question": "Counter-Strike: MIBR vs 3DMAX (BO3) - PGL Bucharest Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Quarterfinal 1 match between MIBR and 3DMAX in the PGL Bucharest Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 9 at 3:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"MIBR\" if MIBR win the match against 3DMAX.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"3DMAX\" if 3DMAX win the match against MIBR.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-09T13:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-09T07:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.415, "volume_usd": 22391.367607000007, "category": "counter-strike"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.3, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: Market resolves YES if MIBR wins the BO3 match; NO if 3DMAX wins. Forfeit/disqualification/walkover by either team resolves to 50-50. Normal match completion with a winner resolves to that winner. EVENT TIMING: Match is TODAY (April 9, 2026, 3:00 AM ET / 7:00 UTC), resolving in ~13 hours. Once played, outcome will be clear and market will trade at extremes (~$0.01 or ~$0.99) before official HLTV resolution. MIBR CASE (YES side): Demonstrated 2-0 map victories (13-7 Mirage, 13-9 Anubis) in a recent playoff match; secured advancement through Swiss rounds; Brazilian team with potential regional familiarity. 3DMAX CASE (NO side): Also qualified for playoffs, indicating comparable competitive standing; no documented recent form or performance metrics in briefing; limited head-to-head data. CURRENT MARKET PRICING: YES at 42% suggests market moderately favors 3DMAX (58%). This pricing reflects asymmetric information and betting patterns, but the briefing provides minimal substantive competitive intelligence on either team beyond MIBR's one prior match result. DATA QUALITY ASSESSMENT: Briefing is heavily contaminated with irrelevant content (Gamers Club Liga, player rosters, formatting artifacts). Actual competitive intelligence is sparse: one MIBR map result, no 3DMAX form data, no head-to-head history, pre-tournament favorites identified but neither MIBR nor 3DMAX mentioned as favorites. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes (35) lower than baseline because MIBR's single prior match result is insufficient to establish trend or map pool strength against THIS opponent. 3DMAX data gap is equally severe, yielding confidence_no (30) \u2014 inability to evaluate the NO side's actual form/strategy creates material uncertainty. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: Market price of 42 (YES) is reasonable given data scarcity, but represents betting consensus rather than fundamental analysis. No briefing evidence supports material deviation from market price in either direction. Slight underweight to YES reflects: (1) pre-tournament favorites not including MIBR, (2) lack of 3DMAX performance data prevents confident dismissal of NO side, (3) single prior result insufficient for BO3 prediction. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: HLTV resolution within 2 hours post-match or credible consensus; no ambiguity in team identification (MIBR and 3DMAX are clear, unambiguous entries). Forfeit risk minimal given both teams advanced to quarterfinals. FINAL ASSESSMENT: Probability_score of 42 reflects market consensus with modest confidence on both sides due to severe data gaps. Neither team is analytically favored based on briefing content.", "key_factor": "Insufficient competitive data on both teams' recent form, head-to-head history, and 3DMAX's playoff performance; briefing contains mostly fragmented tournament information rather than actionable match-specific intelligence."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "NO (3DMAX) is the market favorite at 58%, indicating the market perceives near-parity with slight edge to 3DMAX in a high-uncertainty matchup. MIBR's documented strength: 2-0 playoff victory (13-7 Mirage, 13-9 Anubis) shows map closing ability and Swiss round advancement, supporting competitive credibility. Critical weakness in YES case: MIBR is NOT among pre-tournament favorites (PARIVISION and MongolZ identified as top seeds), suggesting seeds/bookmakers saw other teams as stronger. 3DMAX's qualification to playoffs alone indicates comparable competitive standing\u2014the briefing explicitly states 3DMAX 'also qualified for playoffs, suggesting comparable competitive standing.' Asymmetric data quality strongly favors NO analysis: 3DMAX's recent form, map pool, and head-to-head dynamics are entirely undocumented, creating information vacuum that market prices as neutral-to-slight-3DMAX advantage. Regional advantage claim (MIBR 'home region') is speculative\u2014tournament is PGL Bucharest (Romania), not Brazil, so geographic advantage is neutral or favors neither team. Best-of-3 format reduces variance; MIBR's 2-0 sample is small (single match), insufficient to establish dominance trajectory. Market pricing at 58/42 reflects genuine uncertainty; neither team has documented pre-tournament seeding or recent dominance trajectory in briefing. For YES to overcome NO, MIBR would need to outperform a team of equal qualification standing without documented recent underperformance by 3DMAX\u2014low catalyst support. The case for NO is not 'strong form' but 'absence of evidence of weakness'\u2014market correctly prices this as slight favorite status without inflating confidence.", "key_factor": "Market pricing reflects 3DMAX's qualification to playoffs and symmetric competitive standing with MIBR, while both teams lack dominant pre-tournament seeding."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.48, "confidence_yes": 0.32, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "MARKET STRUCTURE EXPLOIT: YES is priced at 42% despite being called the 'underdog' \u2014 but the briefing provides ONE concrete data point favoring MIBR (13-7, 13-9 wins) and ZERO concrete data about 3DMAX's recent form, recent matchups, or head-to-head record. This asymmetry artificially depresses YES pricing. INFORMATION VOID ON 3DMAX: The briefing explicitly states 'Limited specific information is available about 3DMAX's current form or head-to-head matchup dynamics' and '3DMAX's recent performance metrics are not detailed.' Yet the market has priced NO at 58% anyway \u2014 suggesting confidence without evidentiary support. BOTH TEAMS EQUALLY QUALIFIED: The briefing confirms BOTH teams 'advanced through Swiss rounds' and 'qualified for playoffs, suggesting comparable competitive standing.' There is no hierarchical evidence that MIBR is materially stronger. FAVORITE'S FRAGILITY: The single MIBR win cited (vs unnamed opponent, 13-7 / 13-9) is presented as evidence of dominance, but these scorelines are standard playoff victories \u2014 not dominant blowouts. Margins of 6 and 4 rounds in BO1 games do not guarantee BO3 success. MIBR NOT A TOP SEED: Briefing notes PARIVISION and The MongolZ are 'pre-tournament favorites,' explicitly excluding MIBR from top-tier status. This suggests MIBR and 3DMAX are more evenly matched than the 58/42 split implies. CRITICAL TIMING: This is a LIVE/IMMINENT event (resolves in ~13 hours). Reversal scenarios require major structural failures (forfeit, disqualification) \u2014 which the resolution criteria address separately at 50-50. The BO3 format itself mitigates upsets: best-of-three reduces variance compared to single-map outcomes. OVERPRICED NARRATIVE FOR NO: The market may be anchoring on MIBR's documented win while failing to account for the complete absence of counter-evidence on 3DMAX. Absence of evidence is being treated as evidence of absence \u2014 a classic fallacy. LIQUIDITY & SOFT EVIDENCE: $22.4k volume is moderate; this is not a heavily-researched market. Market-making spreads may reflect genuine uncertainty rather than informed conviction, especially given the data gaps on both sides. PROBABILITY ADJUSTMENT FOR UNCERTAINTY: With symmetric information gaps (one team's form known, the other's form hidden), the true underlying probability should approach 50-50. The current 58/42 split overweights the single MIBR data point and underweights 3DMAX's ability to qualify through the same tournament structure. CONFIDENCE CAVEAT: Both confidence scores are LOW (32 / 28) because the briefing provides insufficient granular data on either team's current roster, recent LAN form, map pool matchups, or individual player performance. This is not a market with strong predictive signals \u2014 it is a market pricing one visible data point (MIBR's win) against a void. YES at 48 reflects genuine equipoise, not conviction.", "key_factor": "Severe information asymmetry: MIBR's single documented win is overstated while 3DMAX's form remains entirely undisclosed, creating artificial underdog pricing for a match between two evenly-matched playoff teams."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "EVENT TIMING: Match resolves TODAY in ~13 hours (LIVE/IMMINENT). Share prices are likely already reflecting genuine market sentiment from bettors with real-time information. Reversal scenarios requiring major upsets have minimal time to manifest. ASYMMETRIC DATA QUALITY: Briefing provides concrete evidence for MIBR (2-0 Swiss advance, 13-7/13-9 map wins) but almost no actionable data on 3DMAX form, recent wins, map pool, or head-to-head history. This creates a critical information gap. MARKET PRICE DIVERGENCE: YES priced at 42% reflects skepticism despite MIBR's demonstrated strength. This suggests sophisticated market participants (esports bettors) have information not in the briefing\u2014likely indicating 3DMAX competitive standing or head-to-head history favors the underdog. BASE RATE LIMITATION: CS2 bo3 playoffs lack a universal historical baseline applicable here. Neither team is seeded as 'favorite' per briefing (PARIVISION/MongolZ are top seeds), meaning MIBR and 3DMAX occupy mid-tier competitive tiers where outcomes are genuinely close to 50-50. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: Both teams cleared Swiss rounds and made playoffs, suggesting rough parity. MIBR's 2-0 result is positive but single-match evidence is weak for predicting bo3 against prepared opponent. REGION/HOME ADVANTAGE: MIBR Brazilian player familiarity is noted, but PGL Bucharest is a LAN event (likely neutral venue), reducing home-region edge significance. CONFIDENCE PENALTY: With <24 hours to match start and no head-to-head data, 3DMAX's actual current form remains opaque. confidence_no must stay LOW (26) to reflect this uncertainty, even though market price suggests 3DMAX competitiveness. confidence_yes similarly modest (28) because single prior match does not override the information asymmetry and market skepticism. RESOLUTION: Align with market price (42%) as best estimate given information present. Market participants have stronger real-time data on both teams than briefing provides.", "key_factor": "Best-of-3 playoff matches in tier-1 CS2 tournaments show ~50% variance by seed/form; unseeded/mid-tier teams (MIBR/3DMAX vs favored PARIVISION/MongolZ) have historically unpredictable outcomes"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "Market price (42% YES) reflects minimal information asymmetry \u2014 briefing provides concrete evidence only for MIBR (2-0 win, 13-7/13-9 scorelines), but near-zero data on 3DMAX form or head-to-head history. MIBR case is stronger on paper (documented recent wins, home-region advantage, tournament progression), yet market prices them as slight underdog \u2014 suggests crowd may be factoring in unknown strength of 3DMAX or perceiving MIBR as tournament dark horse rather than favorite. Pre-tournament favorites are PARIVISION and MongolZ, not MIBR/3DMAX \u2014 both quarterfinal teams appear similarly seeded/ranked, which may justify near 50-50 pricing despite MIBR's documented recent form. Critical data gap: 3DMAX performance metrics entirely absent from briefing. Market cannot meaningfully price differential without this. Crowd is not panicking or euphoric; pricing reflects genuine uncertainty. Briefing noise (Steam sync prompts, tournament structure complaints, unrelated South American league tables) adds no signal \u2014 market correctly ignoring irrelevant content. Event timing is TODAY (~13 hours to resolution). If match is live or imminent by resolution time, sharp traders will have additional real-time data unavailable to briefing. Current 42/58 split may reflect early-market positioning before line movement. Volume is moderate ($22.4k) \u2014 not a crowded trade, not abandoned. Rational apathy dominates: market is pricing genuine coin flip with slight 3DMAX lean, possibly due to missing counter-narrative in briefing data. MIBR recent form (2-0 with clean scorelines) should rationally push them above 50% if that were the only signal; market at 42% suggests crowd believes 3DMAX has unshown strengths or MIBR is tournament vulnerable. This is a rational hedge given information poverty, not mispricing.", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "MIBR evidence is thin: one documented 2-0 victory (13-7 Mirage, 13-9 Anubis) against an unnamed opponent provides minimal predictive power; scorelines suggest competent execution but not dominance (both maps 13-9 or tighter range) 3DMAX form data entirely absent: no performance metrics, map strengths, recent fragging power, or anti-stratting capability documented; qualified for playoffs but zero granular match data Neither team listed as pre-tournament favorite (PARIVISION, MongolZ identified instead): suggests both MIBR and 3DMAX are mid-tier seeds, reducing confidence in any directional probability BO3 format amplifies variance: single map upsets are common in CS2; need for veto strategy, map pool depth, and clutch player performance\u2014none assessable from briefing No head-to-head history provided: historical matchup data is critical in esports; playstyle compatibility, proven counter-stratting, and recent personnel changes unknown EVENT TIMING CRITICAL: match is TODAY (13 hours to resolution); market price (42% YES) likely reflects live odds and community sentiment; late briefing data freshness (2026-04-09 00:11 UTC) suggests minimal new information post-briefing cutoff before match start Brazilian regional context (MIBR home): South American competitive scene shown in tables but no direct correlation to LAN performance at European venue; infrastructure advantage speculative Data quality asymmetry: MIBR has one documented result; 3DMAX has zero\u2014impossible to fairly weight both sides; neither confidence level should exceed 40 Briefing contamination: includes unrelated tournament tables (Gamers Club Liga, VRS South AM) and incomplete metadata (Steam login prompt, incomplete tournament overview text); signal-to-noise ratio very poor", "key_factor": "The briefing lacks current roster composition, recent online/LAN performance trajectories, map pool compatibility, and head-to-head veto history\u2014all critical inputs in CS2 match prediction where meta shifts and player chemistry heavily influence BO3 outcomes."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "BRIEFING SILENCE ON 3DMAX: The document provides detailed MIBR stats (2-0 with 13-7, 13-9 scorelines) but offers zero concrete data on 3DMAX's form, recent matches, map pool, or roster health\u2014a critical asymmetry suggesting underdog risk is underpriced at 42%. NO HEAD-TO-HEAD HISTORY: The briefing explicitly states 'Limited documentation of head-to-head historical matchup data'\u2014in BO3 formats, tactical matchup design often matters more than aggregate strength; MIBR's scorelines could reflect weak opponents rather than playoff-tier resilience. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT MISMATCH: PARIVISION and The MongolZ are identified as 'pre-tournament favorites,' implying MIBR and 3DMAX are mid-tier seeds; a mid-tier opponent (3DMAX) in a BO3 playoff has inherently higher variance than the 42% market price suggests for an underdog in a single-elimination format. MAP POOL VULNERABILITY: MIBR's demonstrated wins on Mirage and Anubis do not guarantee those maps survive a BO3 veto against a team whose map strengths are completely undocumented; if 3DMAX excels on Inferno, Vertigo, or Nuke, MIBR may be forced into unfamiliar territory. MENTAL/MORALE UNKNOWN: No data on either team's psychological state post-Swiss rounds\u2014MIBR may suffer fatigue from extended play; 3DMAX may enter with momentum from a recent upset or elevated confidence against a team they've studied. BRAZILIAN HOME REGION ADVANTAGE OVERSTATED: The briefing mentions 'home region advantage with established infrastructure,' but PGL Bucharest is in Romania, not Brazil; any regional advantage is marginal and the briefing provides no detail on 3DMAX's geographic or logistical constraints. SCORELINE INFLATION: 13-7 and 13-9 victories look dominant, but in playoff contexts these margins can reflect opponent weakness rather than MIBR excellence; without opponent identity or 3DMAX counter-data, the 42% YES price assumes MIBR's baseline strength is higher than evidence supports. PLAYOFF VOLATILITY: BO3 single-elimination matches in tier-1 CS are inherently high-variance; even a 55-45 expected matchup can flip 40-60 on any given day due to anti-strats, player form fluctuation, or tactical innovation\u2014the flat 58% NO price may not adequately reflect this variance. ROSTER/ILLNESS RISK (IMMINENT EVENT): With match ~13 hours away, a last-minute illness, visa issue, or player benching on either side becomes plausible; briefing provides no roster confirmation or health status for either team, creating unquantified tail risk. CONTRARIAN ANCHOR: Market consensus (42% YES) assumes MIBR's documented wins + seeding superiority outweigh 3DMAX's opacity; but opacity in a high-variance BO3 format is asymmetrically dangerous\u2014if 3DMAX is even-strength, the market underprices their winning chances by 6-8 percentage points.", "key_factor": "3DMAX's IGL or key anchor player executes a tactical innovation (anti-eco rounds, off-meta utility setup, or aggressive early-round executes) that exploits MIBR's map pool or defaults, forcing MIBR into uncomfortable reads and snowballing map wins despite appearing stronger in raw stats."}], "final_score": 0.44604255319148933, "no_score": 0.5406349206349207, "edge": 0.031042553191489353, "no_edge": -0.044365079365079274, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 54% for NO (need \u226557%); NO-side confidence too low: 36% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1919665", "question": "Counter-Strike: MIBR vs 3DMAX (BO3) - PGL Bucharest Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Quarterfinal 1 match between MIBR and 3DMAX in the PGL Bucharest Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 9 at 3:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"MIBR\" if MIBR win the match against 3DMAX.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"3DMAX\" if 3DMAX win the match against MIBR.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-09T13:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-09T07:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.415, "volume_usd": 22391.367607000007, "category": "counter-strike"}, "key_facts": ["The two main pre-tournament favorites, PARIVISION and The MongolZ, will face off in the quarter-finals.", "EYEBALLERS matchup at PGL Bucharest 2026!", "Weird that the playoffs start on Thursday, why not start on friday and finish on sunday?", "Please log in and sync your account with Steam to", "Complete overview of the PGL Bucharest 2026 - Semi-final #2.", "Gamers Club Liga S\u00e9rie A: March 2026 is an online South American CS2 tournament organized by Gamers Club.", "This C-Tier tournament took place from Mar 13 to", "Best of 3 (LAN) * Swiss round 2 (teams with a 0-1 record).", "2026) | |\n\n|  |  |\n --- |\n| 1 | Brazil naitte |\n| 2 | Brazil WOOD7 |\n| 3 | Brazil ksloks |\n| 4 | Brazil nardes |\n| 5 | Brazil diozera |\n| C | Brazil cx1 |\n\nBrazil\nBrazil\nBrazil\nBrazil\nBrazil\nBrazil\n\n|  |\n\n|  |\n| VRS South AM (Mar.", "2026) | |\n\n|  |  |\n --- |\n| 1 | Brazil happ |\n| 2 | Brazil zmb |\n| 3 | Brazil Leomonster |\n| 4 | Brazil Alisson |\n| 5 | Brazil divine \"Divine (Brazilian player)\") |\n| C | Brazil disturbed \"Disturbed (Brazilian player)\") |\n\nBrazil\nBrazil\nBrazil\nBrazil\nBrazil\nBrazil\n\n|  |\n\n|  |\n| VRS South AM (Mar."], "news_summary": "MIBR and 3DMAX are scheduled to face off in a Best of 3 match at PGL Bucharest 2026 playoffs. Search results confirm MIBR's participation in the tournament with a documented 2-0 victory over an unnamed opponent (13-7 on Mirage, 13-9 on Anubis). Limited specific information is available about 3DMAX's current form or head-to-head matchup dynamics. The tournament is structured as a playoff event taking place in April 2026.", "side_yes_case": ["MIBR demonstrated strong map control and closing ability with 13-7 and 13-9 victories in a previous playoff match", "MIBR secured advancement through Swiss rounds, indicating competitive performance in the tournament", "Brazilian team competing at home region advantage with established infrastructure and player familiarity"], "side_no_case": ["3DMAX's recent performance metrics and form trajectory are not detailed in available search results", "Limited documentation of head-to-head historical matchup data between MIBR and 3DMAX", "3DMAX also qualified for playoffs, suggesting comparable competitive standing"], "key_context": ["PGL Bucharest 2026 playoff format with best-of-3 matches", "PARIVISION and The MongolZ identified as pre-tournament favorites, suggesting MIBR/3DMAX are not among top seeds", "Tournament scheduled for April 2026 with playoffs starting April 7", "No recent head-to-head match history provided in search results", "Both teams demonstrated ability to advance through tournament stages"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-09T00:11:35.625555Z"}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-09T13:00:00Z", "winning_side": "NO", "final_yes_price": 0.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-09T17:03:24.037011+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
