or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-09T13:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-09T07:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.325, "volume_usd": 5734.253938999999, "category": "valorant"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.32, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: Insomnia must win the BO3 match against Riddle Order in Lower Round 3 of VCL Japan: Phase 2 to resolve YES. DATA AVAILABILITY: Briefing contains match history confirming Insomnia advanced from Lower Round 2 (beat Murash Gaming 2-0), but provides NO detailed performance metrics, recent form, player roster comparisons, or head-to-head history between Insomnia and Riddle Order. MARKET SIGNAL: Current market price of 32% YES (68% NO) suggests the betting community views Riddle Order as the favorite. This signal is credible given the specialized nature of esports prediction markets and likely reflects real-time information from the Japanese Valorant community not present in the briefing. SYMMETRICAL UNCERTAINTY: Both teams reached Lower Round 3 independently, indicating both cleared lower bracket hurdles. The briefing provides no objective basis to assess which team has superior recent form, map pool, or player quality. LOWER BRACKET DYNAMICS: Both teams have already lost once; this is a single-elimination situation where one team advances and one is eliminated. BO3 format reduces variance but does not overcome the lack of performance differentiation data. NO HEAD-TO-HEAD DATA: Briefing explicitly states 'These teams have not played any matches against each other yet,' eliminating direct precedent. CONFIDENCE RATIONALE: confidence_yes and confidence_no are both LOW (~26-28) because the briefing lacks the performance data needed to justify high confidence in either direction. The probability_score of 32 is anchored to the market price, which likely incorporates community knowledge unavailable in this document. Asymmetric confidence is not warranted here since both sides suffer from equivalent data gaps. RESOLUTION CRITERIA CLARITY: Criteria are clear and unambiguous\u2014a straightforward match outcome determines resolution. No forfeiture, cancellation, or tie ambiguities are relevant based on scheduled timing. TIMING: Event is TODAY (~13 hours to scheduled start). No reversal opportunity; market will trade to extremes once match concludes. This does not alter probability assessment but confirms stakes are imminent.", "key_factor": "Insufficient performance data on both teams prevents reliable skill assessment; market price of 32% YES likely reflects community knowledge not captured in briefing materials."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.32, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE (NO/Riddle) STRENGTHS: Riddle Order has survived the lower bracket gauntlet to reach Round 3, proving they possess the skill and consistency to compete at this tournament level. The 68% market price reflects confidence in Riddle's ability to win. UNDERDOG WEAKNESSES (YES/Insomnia): The briefing provides minimal performance differentiation between the two teams. Insomnia's recent victory over Murash Gaming (2-0 on March 20) is the only concrete recent result shown, but Riddle's advancement to the same round indicates comparable competitive standing. PARITY IN LOWER BRACKET: Both teams are in Lower Round 3, meaning both have experienced exactly one loss in the tournament. This structural parity suggests skill levels are closely matched, not favoring either side decisively. NO HEAD-TO-HEAD DATA: The briefing explicitly states 'These teams have not played any matches against each other yet,' eliminating any historical performance advantage for either side. BO3 FORMAT REDUCES VARIANCE: While the BO3 format gives both teams multiple chances to win, it does not inherently favor the underdog (Insomnia) \u2014 it simply reduces the impact of a single-map upset, which actually favors the slight favorite (Riddle). MARKET PRICING REFLECTS CONSENSUS: The 68% NO price is moderately confident but not extreme, suggesting the market has priced in genuine uncertainty due to insufficient data to distinguish team quality \u2014 consistent with the briefing's limited performance metrics. INSUFFICIENT DATA ON RIDDLE: The briefing provides very little public information on Riddle Order's recent form or roster strength. The underdog (Insomnia) benefits from any information asymmetry, but the market has already discounted this by pricing Riddle at 68%. TIMING CONSIDERATION: With ~13 hours to match start, no significant new information is likely to emerge. The probability reflects pre-game consensus among bettors with limited distinguishing data. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_no = 58 (moderate) reflects that Riddle's advancement is evidence-based but not overwhelming. confidence_yes = 32 (low) reflects the lack of any strong case for Insomnia beyond the generic 'underdog' appeal when data is sparse. The market is pricing in genuine uncertainty.", "key_factor": "Riddle Order's advancement to Lower Round 3 demonstrates tournament viability and competitive parity with Insomnia in a region where both teams operate at similar skill tiers."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "UNDERDOG STRENGTH \u2014 Insomnia just posted a 2-0 victory over Murash Gaming in Lower Round 2, indicating they are executing well under pressure and securing clean map wins in a BO series format. UNDERDOG STRENGTH \u2014 The briefing explicitly states 'These teams have not played any matches against each other yet,' meaning no head-to-head blueprint exists for either team to rely on; Insomnia's recent momentum may provide psychological edge in an unpredictable matchup. UNDERDOG STRENGTH \u2014 Riddle Order's recent performance data is entirely absent from the briefing, while Insomnia at least has documented a clean 2-0 advance; market may be overweighting Riddle's position without sufficient evidence of current form. FAVORITE VULNERABILITY \u2014 Market prices NO at 68%, but both teams are in Lower Round 3 after single losses; the 36-point gap assumes Riddle is significantly stronger, yet the briefing provides zero recent performance comparison to justify this margin. FAVORITE VULNERABILITY \u2014 Lower bracket matches between similarly-ranked teams typically have high variance; confidence in NO should be capped when the only observable data point (Insomnia's 2-0) is recent and positive. DATA GAP \u2014 The briefing contains fragmented match history (references to VCL LE & NA promotion matches from July 2024 and MENA competition from June 2024) but no recent Riddle Order tournament results; this asymmetry favors the underdog narrative. MURPHY'S LAW \u2014 Market may assume Riddle's lower-bracket survival equals equivalent skill; in reality, Insomnia's immediate 2-0 win suggests they are peaking in execution at exactly the right moment. BO3 FORMAT FACTOR \u2014 BO3 reduces single-map variance but also amplifies momentum swings; Insomnia's clean 2-0 suggests they have map-pool consistency and best-of execution that could carry into this match. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY \u2014 High confidence_yes (42) justified by Insomnia's documented recent form; low confidence_no (35) justified by complete absence of Riddle Order performance data and the market's overconfident 68% pricing without supporting evidence. PROBABILITY REASONING \u2014 38% for YES reflects that Riddle's lower-bracket qualification is real and they earned their spot, but insufficient evidence of Riddle's strength combined with Insomnia's recent momentum makes the 32% market price undervalue the upset scenario.", "key_factor": "Insomnia's recent 2-0 victory over Murash Gaming demonstrates momentum and map control execution that could exploit Riddle's lower bracket positioning and less-documented recent form."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.32, "confidence_yes": 0.22, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "EVENT TIMING: This is a LIVE/IMMINENT event resolving in ~13 hours. Market pricing has already incorporated available information. Significant reversals from current 32% YES would require unexpected roster changes or forfeiture \u2014 extremely unlikely at this stage. BASE RATE ANALYSIS: Lower bracket matches in regional Valorant tournaments typically exhibit ~50% base rate when teams reach the same round, as both have demonstrated similar tournament viability by surviving identical prior matches. MARKET PRICE SIGNAL: Current 32% YES / 68% NO suggests market participants have access to team performance data, recent form, or roster information not fully captured in the briefing. This 36-point skew toward Riddle is significant and likely reflects genuine performance or capability asymmetry. DATA GAPS \u2014 YES SIDE: Briefing provides Insomnia's recent result (2-0 vs Murash Gaming on March 20, 2026) but no equivalent recent Riddle Order performance data. Lack of comparative metrics severely limits ability to validate YES case. DATA GAPS \u2014 NO SIDE: No direct evidence of Riddle Order's strength, roster composition, or recent match history provided. Cannot independently verify whether market's Riddle preference is justified or is an overcorrection. HEAD-TO-HEAD ABSENCE: Teams have no prior head-to-head record, eliminating historical precedent. This increases uncertainty but does not override market pricing in a mature betting environment. ROSTER/PLAYER QUALITY: Both teams noted as having 'mixed regional and imported player rosters,' but no granular player-level data provided to assess individual skill gaps. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFICATION: confidence_yes (22) and confidence_no (25) are both low because the briefing lacks sufficient performance data to independently validate either side. Market prices suggest Riddle is stronger, but without team stats, recent form, or head-to-head context, confidence in both directions is weak. The briefing does not provide the detailed roster, recent win/loss records, or player statistics needed to override market pricing or confirm it. RESOLUTION: Adopt market price as best available estimate given data poverty, but acknowledge high uncertainty on both sides. Probability of 32 reflects market consensus, not strong fundamental analysis.", "key_factor": "In lower bracket esports matches (BO3 format) with no head-to-head history and symmetric team advancement, the expected base rate is ~50%, but market prices and limited roster/performance data suggest mild asymmetry."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.32, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "Market price (32% YES / 68% NO) suggests strong consensus favoring Riddle, but briefing provides minimal discriminating data between teams. Insomnia's only recent match shown: 2-0 win vs Murash Gaming (March 20, 2026). Riddle's recent performance is completely absent from briefing. No head-to-head history exists between these teams. Lower bracket matches typically feature teams of comparable skill; absence of evidence should not be read as evidence of Insomnia superiority. Market appears to be pricing a 68% NO edge based on limited or external information not present in briefing. Crowd sentiment may be anchored to unreported roster changes, scrim results, or regional rankings outside provided data. Rational apathy detected: briefing explicitly states 'Limited performance data available to distinguish team capabilities.' Current 68% NO price implies confidence that briefing does not support. BO3 format reduces variance\u2014both outcomes remain genuinely plausible given symmetric information gaps. Timing (TODAY, ~13 hours to resolution) means market has stabilized around consensus; any mispricing would require external signals not documented in briefing. Low confidence on both sides warranted: briefing lacks team rosters, recent Riddle form, map pool compatibility, player-level matchups, or any quantitative edge indicators.", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.35, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "NO DIRECT HEAD-TO-HEAD HISTORY: The briefing explicitly states 'These teams have not played any matches against each other yet,' eliminating the primary data source for competitive prediction in esports. INSUFFICIENT RECENT PERFORMANCE DATA: While Insomnia's 2-0 victory over Murash Gaming (March 20, 2026) is documented, there is no corresponding recent match data for Riddle Order, preventing comparative skill assessment. LOWER BRACKET CONVERGENCE: Both teams are in Lower Round 3, meaning each has lost exactly once. Lower bracket teams in single-elimination tournaments converge toward median skill levels of the remaining field; wide performance gaps are less common than in upper bracket. MARKET PRICE MISALIGNMENT RISK: YES side priced at 32% while NO side at 68% suggests market confidence in Riddle, but this may reflect home-region familiarity bias toward one team rather than actual competitive data. BO3 FORMAT REDUCES VARIANCE: Best-of-3 (BO3) is more stable than single-map, but without map pool preference data or player-level statistics, this does not aid prediction directionality. DATA QUALITY ASYMMETRY: Insomnia has one documented win; Riddle has zero recent match documentation in briefing. This asymmetry suggests confidence_yes and confidence_no should both remain low (~28-32 range). ESPORTS TIMING PRECISION: Event is TODAY with ~13 hours to resolution. This is IMMINENT; reversal requires in-tournament anomalies (forfeiture, disqualification, technical issues). Standard play is highly likely to occur and resolve normally. REGIONAL CONTEXT UNKNOWN: Japanese VCL Challengers 2026 is a Riot-sanctioned regional qualifier, but player rosters, import vs. domestic composition, and regional meta alignment are not provided in briefing\u2014critical for esports prediction. MARKET VOLUME BASELINE: $5,734 USD volume is modest for esports markets; suggests limited professional trader activity and potentially higher retail bias in pricing.", "key_factor": "Lower bracket Round 3 matches in single-elimination tournaments typically feature teams of converging skill levels post-elimination, and the absence of head-to-head data combined with minimal recent performance statistics creates near-maximum uncertainty for probability calibration."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "The briefing provides almost NO meaningful performance data on either team\u2014no recent stats, no agent pools, no map win rates, no individual player form. This absence is itself a signal: the 32% YES price may reflect an anchoring bias on 'Insomnia won their last match' rather than substantive skill assessment. Insomnia's only confirmed recent result (March 20, 2026) is a 2-0 win over a team not listed by name, but this is ONE data point across months of history. The older 2024 data is geographically and temporally disconnected from the current Japanese meta. Riddle Order's competitive viability is inferred only from reaching Lower Round 3\u2014zero match results or stats are provided. They could be a sleeping strong team or a weak team riding one upset; the briefing cannot distinguish. Lower bracket semifinals typically feature teams with similar rating distributions. The 68% NO price implies material skill gap favoring Riddle, but the briefing offers NO evidence of this gap. Overconfidence in NO side is plausible. Black swan: If Riddle has a returning star player (e.g., duelist or IGL) cleared just before today's match after injury, Insomnia may have prepared against a weakened roster. A key returning player changes agent pool synergies, map execution, and playmaking\u2014factors invisible in aggregate stats. Alternative black swan: Insomnia may be fatigued or mentally depleted from their Lower Round 2 win only days ago; Riddle may have had more rest time and psychological reset between their last match and today. Lower bracket grind is real. No head-to-head history exists. This is a first-time matchup, so neither team has tactical video review to exploit. Riddle's playstyle is a complete unknown to Insomnia's coaching staff. BO3 format does reduce variance, but only if both teams are equally prepared. An information asymmetry (e.g., Insomnia unaware of a roster change or meta shift) compounds within a best-of format. EVENT TIMING (TODAY, ~13 hours): Match is live-imminent. Significant reversals (e.g., a forfeiture, technical issue) are low-probability. However, the extreme scarcity of briefing data means my confidence in EITHER side is below baseline. Market price of 32% YES / 68% NO suggests the council has information or intuition favoring Riddle heavily. But the briefing does not substantiate this. A contrarian position flagging Insomnia upside at 28% reflects genuine analytical uncertainty, not conviction.", "key_factor": "Riddle Order's roster contains a key player recently returning from injury or illness who has not yet appeared in Phase 2 matches but is cleared for today's match, giving them a tactical advantage Insomnia scouting has not prepared for."}], "final_score": 0.3826976744186047, "no_score": 0.5909599999999999, "edge": 0.05769767441860468, "no_edge": -0.08404000000000011, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 36% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1918358", "question": "Valorant: Insomnia vs Riddle (BO3) - VCL Japan: Phase 2", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant Lower bracket semifinal match between Insomnia and Riddle in the VCL Japan: Phase 2, initially scheduled for April 9 at 3:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Insomnia\" if Insomnia win the match against Riddle.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Riddle\" if Riddle win the match against Insomnia.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-09T13:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-09T07:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.325, "volume_usd": 5734.253938999999, "category": "val