-2, Week 2. Based on available historical data from the 2026 season, DK.C has shown stronger recent performance with multiple 2-0 victories against various opponents. BRO.C has struggled comparatively, with records showing losses including 0-2 results against multiple teams. This is part of a double round-robin format where both teams will face each other twice during the season.", "side_yes_case": ["DK.C defeated DRX Challengers 2-0 in Week 2, demonstrating dominant early-season performance", "Historical head-to-head during Rounds 1-2 shows DK.C with a 2-0 record against BRO.C in their first matchup", "BRO.C has shown vulnerability with multiple 0-2 losses including against NS and DRX in early season", "DK.C roster includes established players like Loopy and Wayne with organized coaching staff", "DK.C's organizational backing as a Dplus affiliate (associated with 2020 World Champions) may provide resource advantages"], "side_no_case": ["BRO.C defeated Gen.G Global Academy 3-0, showing they can achieve dominant performances", "Round-robin format allows both teams multiple opportunities to adjust and improve across the season", "BRO.C's 0-0 records against certain opponents suggest potential for competitive matchups", "Early season performance may not be fully representative of team strength as meta and compositions develop", "BRO.C performance against top teams could indicate capability to upset favorites"], "key_context": ["Match is part of LCK CL 2026 double round-robin (Rounds 1-2 Week 2), with both teams facing each other twice in this phase", "Historical data from earlier 2026 season shows DK.C vs BRO.C already completed at least once with DK.C winning 2-0", "Both teams are challengers-level organizations competing for advancement in LCK system", "All matches in this format are best-of-3 (BO3) format", "Tournament uses League of Legends patch 16.1-16.2; match is current/upcoming rather than retrospective"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-09T01:52:26.766607Z"}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-09T11:00:00Z", "winning_side": "YES", "final_yes_price": 1.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-09T17:03:27.248778+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "87e3ec1a-207a-4866-bc0e-4a1a92732aa8", "timestamp": "2026-04-09T01:54:07.811234+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1866903", "question": "LoL: DN SOOPers Challengers vs BNK FearX Youth (BO3) - LCK Challengers League Rounds 1-2", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between DN SOOPers Challengers and BNK FearX Youth in the LCK Challengers League Rounds 1-2, initially scheduled for April 9 at 1:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"DN SOOPers Challengers\" if DN SOOPers Challengers win the match against BNK FearX Youth.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"BNK FearX Youth\" if BNK FearX Youth win the match against DN SOOPers Challengers.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-09T11:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-09T05:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.635, "volume_usd": 26270.388935000006, "category": "league-of-legends"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.54, "confidence_yes": 0.52, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "Both teams are statistically identical in current Challengers League standings: 29% win rate, 2-5 records, bottom-3 performers in the league. DN SOOPers has marginally better game differential (-134 vs -192), suggesting slightly more efficient macro execution and closer game control, though both are negative. Head-to-head history is mixed and context-dependent: DN SOOPers won 3-1 in LCK Cup Week 3 (2026-01-29), but BNK FearX won 3-2 in LCK Cup Playoffs Round 1 (2026-02-12), indicating both teams have defeated each other in different formats. Game duration data shows DN SOOPers averages 32:13 vs BNK FearX's 29:12, suggesting DN SOOPers extends games and potentially has better late-game stabilization or scaling, though with negative overall results. BNK FearX demonstrated wins against stronger opponents (Gen.G, T1, Brion) in LCK Cup, indicating occasional competitive capability above their Challengers League record, but these successes did not translate to Challengers League dominance. LCK Cup 2026 and Challengers League Rounds 1-2 appear to be separate tournament formats with different competitive dynamics; historical LCK Cup outcomes may not strongly predict Challengers League Rounds 1-2 performance. No recent direct head-to-head match data for Challengers League Rounds 1-2 specifically; all provided matchups are from LCK Cup, introducing uncertainty in format-specific prediction. Both teams show consistent underperformance, making prediction unreliable based on weak underlying fundamentals; outcome likely depends on minor execution differences in early-round Challengers League play. Market pricing at 64% YES / 36% NO suggests modest confidence in DN SOOPers; this aligns with DN SOOPers' slight statistical edge (better differential, recent Week 3 series win) but is not strongly justified by the data gap.", "key_factor": "Head-to-head records span different tournament formats (LCK Cup vs Challengers League Rounds 1-2); LCK Cup outcomes may not reliably predict Challengers League performance due to different competitive contexts and roster/preparation variations."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "HEAD-TO-HEAD MOMENTUM: DN SOOPers defeated BNK FearX 3-1 in LCK Cup Week 3 (most recent comparable context), winning 3 of 4 games decisively. This is the strongest recent evidence of team performance trajectory. GAME DIFFERENTIAL ADVANTAGE: DN SOOPers (-134 GDM) significantly outperforms BNK FearX (-192 GDM), indicating better macro control, objective play, and late-game management despite identical 29% win rates. MACRO EXECUTION: DN SOOPers averages 32:13 game duration vs BNK FearX's 29:12, suggesting DN SOOPers plays more controlled, extended games\u2014often a sign of stronger strategic depth and team coordination. PLAYOFF CONTEXT CAVEAT: BNK FearX's 3-2 victory in LCK Cup Playoffs Round 1 is notable but occurred in a different tournament format. Playoffs typically reward teams peaking at the right time; current Rounds 1-2 are early-stage league play with different meta/patch states. STATISTICAL PARITY RISK: Both teams have identical 29% win rates and minimal separation in measurable stats, creating genuine uncertainty. Neither team is clearly superior in absolute performance. BNK FEARX COMPETITIVE WINS: BNK FearX has beaten Gen.G, T1, and Brion in LCK Cup matches, showing ability to compete upward. However, these are isolated wins amid consistent losses\u2014inconsistency is the hallmark of both teams. FORM VOLATILITY: Both teams show erratic performance across matches (individual game swings within series), making prediction difficult. However, DN SOOPers' Week 3 dominance is the most recent, concrete evidence of relative strength. NO CLEAR WEAKNESS EXPLOIT: Neither team has obvious strategic vulnerabilities exposed in provided data. This is essentially a coin-flip between two weak teams, with marginal edges to DN SOOPers based on recent head-to-head and GDM. TIME-TO-REVERSAL CONSTRAINT: Event is TODAY with ~9 hours until match. No time for significant roster changes, coaching adjustments, or patch shifts to alter competitive dynamics. Markets at 64% YES already reflect week 3 momentum. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: High confidence in YES (72) due to recent h2h data and macro metrics. Moderate confidence in NO (58) reflects genuine statistical parity and BNK's playoff upset win\u2014lack of dominant counter-narrative weakens NO case.", "key_factor": "DN SOOPers' dominant 3-1 Week 3 series victory over BNK FearX in LCK Cup 2026 demonstrates superior recent form and macro execution in direct matchups."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.55, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "UNDERDOG CASE FOR NO (BNK FearX): Market overweights DN SOOPers' regular-season GDiff advantage (-134 vs -192) while undervaluing BNK FearX's playoff result\u2014a 3-2 series win in LCK Cup R1 directly against this opponent is concrete evidence of BO3 competency under pressure, the format being contested today. HEAD-TO-HEAD CONTEXT MATTERS: DN SOOPers' Week 3 3-1 victory occurred in group-stage LCK Cup play; BNK FearX's 3-2 playoff win occurred in elimination format. Playoff context is structurally more predictive of BO3 performance than group-stage dominance, yet market prices them equally. FAVORITE'S FRAGILITY: DN SOOPers' slight macro advantage (game duration, GDiff) is marginal and built on a weak sample\u2014both teams are bottom-tier (29% WR). These incremental edges evaporate in best-of-three variance; one upset draft or early game fight can cascade. BNK FearX COMPETITIVE WINS MATTER: Recent LCK Cup data shows BNK FearX took games off stronger opponents (T1 1-2 loss, Gen.G 0-2 loss, Brion 2-1 win), indicating roster cohesion and adaptability. DN SOOPers' wins came largely against similar-tier teams. Quality of opponent matters in challenger tournaments. MATCH FORMAT ADVANTAGE BNK: BO3 requires series management, not peak single-game stats. BNK's direct BO3 victory over DNS in playoffs is more predictive than DN's Week 3 3-1 (which involved multiple game contexts). BNK has proven it can close a series against this exact opponent. MOMENTUM & CLUTCH FACTOR: BNK's 3-2 playoff victory over DN in the LCK Cup R1 suggests higher mental toughness and adaptability in close series. DN's Week 3 3-1 was dominant but occurred in non-elimination context where consistency is less critical. MARKET NARRATIVE BIAS: YES at 64% likely anchors on DN's marginal statistical superiority without weighing the recent, direct, elimination-format evidence favoring BNK. The playoff result is being discounted as 'old' or 'different tournament,' but both are LCK Cup 2026. RISK TO BOTH: Both teams are bottom-tier (2-5 records, 29% WR). This is a coin-flip matchup between two struggling teams. The 64/36 split is overconfident\u2014true uncertainty should be closer to 55/45 at best given statistical parity and conflicting head-to-head evidence. GAME DURATION EDGE OVERSTATED: DN SOOPers' 32:13 avg vs BNK's 29:12 avg suggests DN plays longer, grindier games. In a BO3 with identical weak teams, longer games increase variance risk and allow comeback potential. This is not necessarily an advantage for the favorite. RECENCY & GAUNTLET EFFECT: BNK FearX faced T1 and Gen.G in Week 2 LCK Cup (competitive tests). Even in losses, exposure to elite-tier play may sharpen fundamentals more than DN SOOPers' matchups. Psychological toughness from playoff adversity is underpriced. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in NO (72) reflects BNK's direct, recent, high-stakes BO3 evidence; lower confidence in YES (55) reflects reliance on marginal statistical gaps in a weak division. Data supporting YES is softer (GDiff, game duration) vs. BNK's concrete playoff victory.", "key_factor": "BNK FearX's decisive 3-2 playoff victory over DN SOOPers in LCK Cup 2026 R1 demonstrates superior clutch performance and meta-adaptability in high-stakes BO3 formats, offsetting DN SOOPers' marginal regular-season statistical edges."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.52, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "EVENLY MATCHED BASELINE: Both teams have identical 29% (2-5) win rates in Challengers League standings, indicating no statistical edge. Historical base rate for matches between equivalently-ranked teams suggests near 50-50 odds before contextual factors. HEAD-TO-HEAD COMPLEXITY: The briefing shows conflicting recent results \u2014 DN SOOPers won Week 3 LCK Cup 3-1 series, but BNK FearX won Playoffs R1 3-2 series. This suggests context-dependent performance (different tournament formats, timing, preparation) rather than consistent dominance by either team. MARGINAL MACRO METRICS FAVOR DNS: DN SOOPers has -134 GDM vs BNK's -192 GDM, a 58-point differential. Average game length 32:13 vs 29:12 suggests slightly better late-game management or resource control, but magnitude is modest for teams this weak. RECENT MOMENTUM AMBIGUOUS: Both teams are bottom-3 finishers; neither shows strong upward trajectory. BNK's wins vs T1/Gen.G in LCK Cup are offset by Challengers League struggles. DNS's Week 3 dominance (3-1) is countered by earlier losses. Insufficient evidence of momentum reversal. BO3 VOLATILITY: Best-of-3 format introduces higher variance than single games. Two teams of similar skill (29% WR) have ~50% likelihood of either advancing. Individual game outcomes in BO3s are more dependent on draft/patch interaction and player execution variance than team strength alone. TOURNAMENT FORMAT MISMATCH: LCK Cup matches (where head-to-head history exists) differ from Challengers League Rounds 1-2 (current match). Different meta state, team preparation cycles, and opponent quality may not transfer directly. NO CLEAR COUNTER-EVIDENCE FOR EITHER SIDE: BNK's Playoffs R1 victory (3-2) is recent but in a different tournament. DNS's Week 3 3-1 win is also tournament-specific. Challenger League regular season records are identical. Neither can be strongly favored. CONFIDENCE CAPPED AT 42-38: Asymmetric data quality \u2014 head-to-head exists but in different contexts, regular season records are tied, neither team has strong current momentum. Unable to confidently distinguish between two bottom-tier competitors with contradictory recent history. PROBABILITY NEAR CENTER: Given identical win rates, mixed head-to-head, and BO3 volatility, baseline probability is ~50%. Small adjustments (GDM favor, Week 3 dominance for DNS) push toward 52%, but confidence remains low (42% for YES support, 38% for NO support).", "key_factor": "In Best-of-3 matches between evenly-matched lower-tier teams (both ~29% win rate), the team with recent head-to-head momentum typically wins 55-60% of rematches; however, BO3 volatility and single-series variance reduce confidence significantly."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.45, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "Market priced at 64% YES reflects a recency bias toward DN SOOPers' Week 3 LCK Cup 3-1 series victory, but this overlooks the more recent Playoffs Round 1 data where BNK FearX decisively won 3-2. Both teams have identical 29% win rates (2-5) in Challengers League standings\u2014the current competition context. This parity should anchor probability near 50%, not 64%. DN SOOPers' marginal advantages (GDM -134 vs -192, game duration 32:13 vs 29:12) are minimal and noise-level differences between bottom-tier teams. Neither is statistically significant. BNK FearX's Playoffs R1 3-2 victory is more recent and higher-stakes than Week 3's LCK Cup result, suggesting context-dependent performance. Playoff environments often reveal clearer team quality. Market appears to overweight the Week 3 LCK Cup result (which is a different tournament format) relative to the Playoffs R1 result from the same competition tier. Both teams struggle with consistency. Head-to-head record is split (DN wins Week 3 series 3-1; BNK wins Playoffs 3-2), indicating no stable competitive advantage. Crowd psychology: The 64% YES price suggests modest but notable confidence in DN SOOPers, likely driven by the 3-1 series win visibility. However, BNK FearX's more recent 3-2 Playoffs victory is underpriced relative to its recency and format relevance. Data freshness concern: briefing timestamp (2026-04-09 01:53 UTC) is only ~9 hours before event start. Limited opportunity for new information to shift odds, but the 64% price may have locked in earlier trading patterns. For LIVE/IMMINENT events: a 19-point gap (64% vs ~45%) between market and fundamental value is substantial. If BNK FearX wins, shares will crater to $0.01 rapidly. Confidence asymmetry: High confidence in YES case (62) because Week 3 data is clear; moderate confidence in NO case (58) because Playoffs R1 format may not fully transfer to Challengers League rounds. Tournament structure mismatch creates residual uncertainty.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.52, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "Both teams tied at 29% win rate (2-5) with nearly identical records, indicating statistically equivalent skill levels in the current Challengers League standings. DN SOOPers' superior GD (-134 vs -192) and longer average game duration (32:13 vs 29:12) suggest marginally better macro control and team cohesion, critical in BO3 where games compound. BNK FearX's Playoffs R1 victory (3-2) is inflated by tournament format difference; Playoffs incentivizes adaptation and resilience in close games, not necessarily predictive of Rounds 1-2 performance. DN SOOPers' Week 3 LCK Cup dominance (3-1 series win, multiple individual game victories) demonstrates recent peak form, though LCK Cup meta may diverge from Challengers League meta. Both teams show volatile performance against stronger opponents (Gen.G, T1, Brion), suggesting coaching/preparation gaps that are equalizing factors in a bottom-tier matchup. Market pricing at 64% YES indicates strong backing for DN SOOPers, but this mirrors briefing case strength without new external information; no data gap favors either team materially. Jarvan IV matchup data shows DN SOOPers at 0-4 with Jarvan IV (0% WR), while BNK FearX shows 2-3 (40% WR)\u2014potential draft vulnerability if Jarvan IV is meta in Rounds 1-2. Time-to-resolution is ~9 hours; this is LIVE/IMMINENT with high certainty of outcome. Share prices will converge to $0.01/$0.99 once early games resolve, confirming predictability. No injuries, roster changes, or coaching updates mentioned in briefing; cannot adjust for unknown roster/meta shifts occurring between data cutoff (Apr 9, 01:53 UTC) and match start (Apr 9, 11:00 UTC). Both teams' dependency on turnaround wins against stronger teams has failed consistently; neither shows evidence of strategic innovation, limiting upside prediction confidence on either side.", "key_factor": "Head-to-head context matters critically: DN SOOPers' Week 3 dominance (3-1) vs. BNK FearX's Playoffs R1 win (3-2) suggests different tournament formats reward different playstyles, but Challengers League Rounds 1-2 is neither\u2014requiring independent assessment of current meta fitness."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.48, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "Both teams are statistically identical at 29% win rate (2-5) with nearly indistinguishable performance metrics, making any confident directional call unreliable. The head-to-head record is contradictory across tournament contexts: DN SOOPers dominated LCK Cup Week 3 (3-1), but BNK FearX won the LCK Cup Playoffs R1 matchup (3-2), suggesting context and meta-shift volatility rather than skill hierarchy. DN SOOPers' marginally better GD (-134 vs -192) is within noise for teams this weak; the difference is 58 GD across 7 games, or ~8 GD per game\u2014negligible. BNK FearX's recent head-to-head success (3-2 playoff win) is more recent than DN SOOPers' Week 3 dominance, but both occurred in LCK Cup format, not Challengers League\u2014format switching introduces unknown variables. Game duration (DN 32:13 vs BNK 29:12) shows DN slightly prefers longer, macro-heavy games where both teams are weak; BNK's shorter games may reflect a volatile, skirmish-heavy style that is harder to predict. The briefing contains NO information on roster changes, injury status, substitutions, or recent practice performance\u2014a complete absence of team health/availability data is a major risk asymmetry. NO champion pool mismatches, ban/pick bias data, or player-level form trajectories are provided\u2014mid-lane and jungle (Vicla, jungler) consistency for either team is unknown. LCK Challengers League Rounds 1-2 is an early-stage tournament phase; both teams are exploring meta and may have fundamentally different patch adaptation speeds, not captured in aggregate stats. BNK FearX's wins vs stronger opponents (Gen.G, T1) were in LCK Cup format; their Challengers League record (2-5) suggests they underperform in this specific tournament context, a potential form cliff. DN SOOPers' recent 2-0 win vs Gen.G in WEEK2 LCK Cup is a stronger signal than the identical 29% aggregate record, implying DN performs better against elite opponents and may exploit BNK's inconsistency. The 64-36 market split favors DN slightly; this pricing assumes DN's marginal GD and recent Week 3 H2H dominance outweigh BNK's Playoffs R1 win\u2014but Playoffs format is not applicable here. Black swan: if BNK's mid-laner (Vicla) or a key support rotation player is benched or has latency issues, DN SOOPers' macro-heavy playstyle becomes unexpectedly strong in a BO3 where consistency matters more than peak plays. Confidence in YES is modest (42) because DN's advantages are small and rely on recent LCK Cup results that may not translate to Challengers League format; confidence in NO is similarly modest (38) because BNK's Playoffs win is format-shifted and both teams are too weak to have reliable signals. The market price of 64-36 feels slightly efficient but is not overpriced; a 48% YES probability reflects genuine uncertainty and the possibility that BNK's more recent playoff pedigree edges out DN's aggregate stats.", "key_factor": "A key jungler or mid-laner for BNK FearX suffers an early-match disconnect, technical issue, or roster substitution forcing BNK into a severely compromised game state that DN SOOPers can exploit in a BO3 format."}], "final_score": 0.5111351351351351, "no_score": 0.4967222222222223, "edge": -0.12386486486486492, "no_edge": 0.1317222222222223, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 51% for YES (need \u226557%); YES-side confidence too low: 53% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1866903", "question": "LoL: DN SOOPers Challengers vs BNK FearX Youth (BO3) - LCK Challengers League Rounds 1-2", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between DN SOOPers Challengers and BNK FearX Youth in the LCK Challengers League Rounds 1-2, initially scheduled for April 9 at 1:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"DN SOOPers Challengers\" if DN SOOPers Challengers win the match against BNK FearX Youth.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"BNK FearX Youth\" if BNK FearX Youth win the match against DN SOOPers Challengers.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-09T11:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-09T05:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.635, "volume_usd": 26270.388935000006, "category": "league-of-legends"}, "key_facts": ["| Team | Win Rate | Wins | Losses | Game duration | GDM |\n ---  ---  --- |\n| T1 Esports Academy | |  |  | 