 to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-09T17:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-09T11:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.575, "volume_usd": 8.884011000000001, "category": "overwatch"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: Market resolves to FURY if FURY wins the BO3 match against Rankers on April 9 at 7:00 AM ET. CURRENT STANDINGS SUPPORT RANKERS: Rankers holds 1-1 record vs FURY's 0-2; Rankers' map differential is -2 vs FURY's -5; Rankers demonstrated ability to win at least one match. CASE FOR FURY: FURY may have higher intrinsic team quality despite poor results; early-stage group play performance is volatile; FURY could be motivated by 0-2 deficit; single BO3 outcome unpredictable between struggling teams. CASE FOR RANKERS: Superior recent record (1-1 vs 0-2) and better map differential (-2 vs -5) suggest better current form; Rankers has proven they can secure victories in this tournament; momentum typically favors winning team. DATA GAPS & UNCERTAINTY: Briefing standings table is corrupted/incomplete (duplicate entries, formatting errors); no direct head-to-head match history provided; no recent roster, player performance, or coaching changes mentioned; no odds from professional betting sources or esports analysts included. ASYMMETRIC CONFIDENCE: Rankers' superior record in group stage provides moderate evidence for Rankers outcome. However, lack of direct comparison, corrupted data, and volatile early-season performance create substantial uncertainty. Confidence in Rankers case (confidence_no) is also low due to limited data quality for both sides. MARKET PRICING (57% YES for FURY) appears to overweight FURY despite worse record, suggesting market may be pricing in unmea