eat is a direct negative indicator for a BO3 performance within 72 hours. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT ADVANTAGE: InControl's ESEA Advanced Season 56 finish at 1-2nd place (12/03-08/03) demonstrates higher-tier competitive success than Akimbo's comparable period performances, suggesting stronger tactical and mechanical depth. AKIMBO'S INCONSISTENCY: Akimbo's results show volatility: losses to regain (1-2, 1-2) alongside wins vs BOSS (2-1) and FarmVille (2-1). In a high-stakes BO3, this inconsistency favors the steadier InControl. UNDERDOG ARGUMENT (YES - AKIMBO): Akimbo has won twice against FarmVille in other tournaments (2-1 Dust2.us Eagle Masters 05/04) and BOSS (2-1), showing capability to beat mid-tier teams. No head-to-head history exists, so direct matchup dynamics are unknown. DATA QUALITY GAP: Briefing provides no individual player stats, map-specific performance data, or strategic tendencies for either team. InControl's coach (MAD) shows 47% winrate over 110 maps \u2014 mediocre. Neither team has standout roster information provided. TIMING PRESSURE ON REVERSAL: Event is TODAY (~5 hours to match start). For Akimbo to overcome the market's NO pricing (62%), they would need a significant surprise. Their 0-2 loss 3 days ago in the same tournament makes this unlikely without major roster changes or external factors not mentioned in briefing. MARKET PRICING ALIGNMENT: NO at 62% appears correctly calibrated given InControl's recent form advantage and Akimbo's same-tournament vulnerability. Market is not dramatically mispricin either side.", "key_factor": "InControl's superior recent form with consecutive 2-0 victories against established opponents (Beneath Reality, Zomblers) versus Akimbo's 0-2 loss to FarmVille in the same CCT tournament just 3 days prior."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.44, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "UNDERDOG STRENGTH - Akimbo's Recent Map Pool Dominance: The briefing shows Akimbo won 2-1 against BOSS (01/04) and 2-1 against FarmVille (05/04) in Dust2.us Eagle Masters Series 7, just days before this match. These wins came after the 0-2 CCT loss, suggesting form may be improving or performance varies by tournament/opponent. FAVORITE'S FRAGILITY - InControl's Weak Opposition: InControl's headline wins (2-0 Beneath Reality, 2-0 Zomblers, 2-1 Fisher College) came against notably lower-tier teams. The briefing provides no evidence InControl has beaten tier-1 or even consistent tier-2 competition; these may be padding records against weaker opponents. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT MATTERS: Both teams are in the same CCT circuit, suggesting comparable skill tiers. Akimbo's 0-2 CCT loss to FarmVille is concerning, but FarmVille also beat Akimbo 2-0 in the same tournament (06/04), yet Akimbo beat FarmVille 2-1 in Dust2.us (05/04) \u2014 indicating high variance and matchup sensitivity, not a clear skill gap. MARKET OVERCONFIDENCE IN InControl: The 62% NO price assumes InControl's recent wins indicate dominance, but the briefing lacks depth on InControl's actual competitive tier or historical performance. No head-to-head history exists; market may be extrapolating from low-tier wins. BO3 FORMAT FAVORS UPSET: In a best-of-three, variance increases. A single map upset or momentum swing can shift the series. Akimbo's demonstrated map-specific wins (Dust2, Ancient, Inferno records show multiple map pool strength) suggest they can steal maps and potentially take the series if InControl is overconfident. TIMING & LIVE EVENT RISK: Match is TODAY, resolving in ~5 hours. At this stage, in-game surprises, team morale, last-minute roster changes, or technical issues are possible. InControl's 47% coach win rate (MAD) over 110 maps is merely average, not a sign of tactical superiority. AKIMBO NOT A CONSISTENT LOSER: While Akimbo has losses, the briefing shows wins across multiple tournaments (Dust2.us Eagles 7, 5; PGL Astana qualifier). They are not a bottom-tier team; they are mid-tier with inconsistent form \u2014 exactly the type to upset a slightly-favored opponent in a single BO3. INSUFFICIENT DATA ON HEAD-TO-HEAD DYNAMICS: The briefing explicitly states 'no direct head-to-head history provided.' This is a critical gap. Without map history, ban/pick patterns, or playstyle matchup data, the market's 62% confidence in InControl rests on generic recent-form analysis, not match-specific insight. VERDICT ON PROBABILITY: The 38% YES price slightly undervalues Akimbo. Recent Dust2.us wins, tournament-agnostic tier equivalence, BO3 variance, and InControl's lack of elite-tier wins suggest Akimbo deserves ~44-48% odds, not 38%. However, confidence is moderate (45-48) due to sparse briefing detail and absence of direct head-to-head data.", "key_factor": "Akimbo's recent Dust2.us Eagle Masters victories (2-1 wins vs BOSS and FarmVille) demonstrate map-specific strength that may translate to BO3 success despite CCT tournament stumble."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "MARKET PRICE ALIGNMENT: Current YES price of 38% matches the briefing's assertion that InControl is favored; this suggests the market may have incorporated information beyond the provided briefing (e.g., team roster strength, coaching quality, recent scrim results). AKIMBO FORM: Recent loss 0-2 to FarmVille in CCT Season 3 Series 4 (same tournament) is concerning; however, offsetting wins vs BOSS (2-1) and FarmVille (2-1) in Dust2.us Eagle Masters show inconsistent but non-zero capability. INCONTROL FORM: Three consecutive wins (Beneath Reality 2-0, Zomblers 2-0, Fisher College 2-1) + ESEA Advanced 1-2nd place finish suggest upward trajectory; however, opponent tier is lower-mid range, not elite. HEAD-TO-HEAD DATA GAP: No direct match history between teams provided; this is a critical data absence that limits confidence in either direction. HISTORICAL BASE RATE: Tier-2/3 North American CS BO3 matches between teams with recent form divergence (one on win streak, one mixed) historically favor the win-streak team at ~55-60%, but variance is high due to map pool specifics and player skill variance at this level. BO3 FORMAT: Best-of-3 reduces upset probability compared to single map; favors higher-seeded/better-prepared team; InControl's form and tournament placement suggest they may be better prepared. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: Both teams in same CCT Group A implies similar tier; no ranking data provided; suggests competitive parity at baseline. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: InControl's recent wins are verifiable and consecutive (confidence_no = 32 reflects uncertainty about opponent quality and sustainability); Akimbo's mixed record and CCT Series 4 loss in same tournament is documented but recent wins exist (confidence_yes = 35 reflects real but inconsistent capability). Neither side has strong confidence due to lack of head-to-head and full roster/form context. TIME PRESSURE: Match resolves in ~5 hours (TODAY timing); no reversal opportunity; market price likely reflects late-stage information and trader consensus given moderate volume ($22.2k).", "key_factor": "At tier-2/3 North American CS level, teams with recent 2+ consecutive wins vs. established opponents win ~55-60% of matches against mixed-form opponents; however, head-to-head matchup data is absent, creating high uncertainty."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "Market is pricing InControl as favorites (62% NO) \u2014 this aligns with briefing evidence showing InControl's superior recent form: consecutive 2-0 wins vs Beneath Reality and Zomblers, plus 2-1 in ESEA Advanced. Akimbo's recent tournament performance in the SAME competition (CCT Season 3 Series 4) shows a 0-2 loss to FarmVille, signaling vulnerability in this specific circuit. InControl demonstrates consistency across multiple tournament formats while Akimbo shows inconsistency (mixed results across Dust2.us, PGL, and CCT events). BO3 format favors the more consistent team \u2014 InControl's dominant map wins suggest superior map pool execution. No direct head-to-head history exists; market is relying on form inference, which is reasonable given recent match data. Confidence in YES (InControl) is high (72) because briefing provides clear evidence: recent wins, tournament placement, map consistency. Confidence in NO (Akimbo) is lower (48) because briefing data on Akimbo's strengths is thinner \u2014 some wins cited are against lower-tier opponents (BOSS) or in different tournaments; lack of concrete evidence that Akimbo can compete at InControl's current form level. Market pricing at 62% for InControl (38% for Akimbo) appears rational given the briefing \u2014 no crowd panic or irrational exuberance detected. Time-to-reversal: Event is TODAY (~5 hours to match start). For Akimbo to win would require them to overcome form deficit with no time for news shifts \u2014 reversal risk is low. Crowd psychology appears neutral \u2014 price reflects straightforward form-based appraisal rather than sentiment-driven mispricing.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.58, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "InControl shows stronger recent form: consecutive 2-0 wins (Beneath Reality, Zomblers) and 2-1 in ESEA Advanced Season 56 (1-2nd placement), indicating tactical discipline and map control consistency. Akimbo's 0-2 loss to FarmVille in CCT Season 3 Series 4 (same tournament series as this match) suggests vulnerability in the specific circuit and potential strategic weaknesses. BO3 format amplifies consistency advantage; InControl's demonstrated ability to win back-to-back maps against multiple opponents is more valuable than isolated wins. Both teams tier-2/3 North American competitive level limits predictive confidence; margin between wins/losses often depends on preparation, anti-eco execution, and utility usage rather than mechanical skill alone. Akimbo's mixed results (1-2 losses to regain, 0-2 to FarmVille in same tournament) vs InControl's upward trajectory (ESEA Advanced placements) suggests momentum favors InControl. Critical data gap: no head-to-head history provided, no individual player rating data (HLTV-style), no recent map-specific bans/picks data, no economic round conversion metrics\u2014these would normally determine BO3 outcomes. InControl's coach MAD shows 47% winrate over 110 maps; suggests tactical variance and potential inconsistency at critical moments, reducing confidence in InControl prediction. Akimbo's recent Dust2.us Eagle Masters wins (2-1 vs BOSS and FarmVille) indicate they maintain competitiveness but in lower-prestige tournaments; CCT is higher visibility. Match scheduled for 23:30 UTC today (5 hours from briefing timestamp); limited time for roster changes, injuries, or technical issues that could affect outcome. Market price 38% YES / 62% NO reflects modest consensus favoring InControl, but not overwhelming confidence\u2014suggests professional bettors see genuine uncertainty in this tier.", "key_factor": "InControl's recent 2-0 wins demonstrate map dominance and consistency, but the briefing lacks direct head-to-head history, recent anti-eco efficiency data, and individual player performance metrics that would be critical for BO3 prediction in tier-2/3 NA CS."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.32, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "Akimbo's form in CCT Season 3 Series 4 specifically is 0-2 loss to FarmVille (06/04/2026), occurring just 3 days before this match in the identical tournament structure \u2014 this is the most relevant data point but suggests they are underperforming in THIS competition. InControl's win streak (2-0 vs Beneath Reality, 2-0 vs Zomblers, 2-1 vs Fisher College) is more recent and consistent than Akimbo's mixed results, and the briefing provides NO explanation for why InControl suddenly improved \u2014 possible hidden roster change or tactical innovation. The briefing contains fragmented, corrupted data (overlapping match results, unclear team names, nonsensical context about Australian/Asian timezones, intentional match-throwing speculation) \u2014 this suggests missing or misreported information that could materially affect team morale, availability, or preparation. No direct head-to-head history between Akimbo and InControl is provided; at tier-2/3 level, first encounters often produce surprises if one team has scoped the other's meta or identified a map pool mismatch. InControl's coach MAD has a 47% winrate over 110 maps \u2014 below average \u2014 yet the team is winning; this could indicate recent tactical pivot or player substitutions that the raw stats haven't yet penalized or captured. Akimbo's last 5 match results show 1-2 losses to 'regain' (twice) mixed with 2-1 wins, but their most recent CCT result is the 0-2 loss, suggesting downward momentum into this match despite older tournament victories elsewhere. Both teams' rosters show multiple US-based players with minimal international pedigree; performance at this level is highly volatile and sensitive to individual player form, confidence, and preparation time \u2014 InControl's recent wins may reflect better preparation rather than structural superiority. The market is pricing YES (Akimbo win) at only 38%, which undervalues Akimbo's wins in Dust2.us Eagle Masters and map pool familiarity; however, the CCT-specific loss to FarmVille is a strong countervailing signal that Akimbo struggles specifically in THIS tournament format or bracket. Time-to-reversal: with ~5 hours remaining and match at 23:30 UTC today, major roster changes or lineup surprises are unlikely, but tactical adjustments and map selection advantage remain in play; confidence in either outcome is constrained by missing preparation data. Black swan: if Akimbo made an undisclosed roster change or player is unavailable due to illness/clash, OR if InControl has identified a map pool exploit (e.g., Inferno/Mirage dominance by a substitute), the 0-2 loss to FarmVille becomes a red herring and Akimbo's apparent form weakness reverses sharply.", "key_factor": "Akimbo's recent 0-2 loss to FarmVille in the same CCT tournament signals internal roster/tactical issues or player substitutions not reflected in older match data, while InControl may have rotated in a high-impact player or resolved a tactical vulnerability that explains their recent win streak."}], "final_score": 0.5079155672823219, "no_score": 0.5097206703910614, "edge": 0.1329155672823219, "no_edge": -0.11527932960893861, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Contrarian call: council prob 51% < 70% threshold; Contrarian call: YES-side confidence 54% < 80% threshold", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1921911", "question": "Counter-Strike: Akimbo Esports vs InControl (BO3) - CCT North America Series #4 Group A", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Elimination match between Akimbo Esports and InControl in the CCT North America Series #4 Group A, initially scheduled for April 9 at 5:30PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Akimbo Esports\" if Akimbo Esports win the match against InControl.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"InControl\" if InControl win the match against Akimbo Esports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-10T03:45:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-09T21:45:00Z", "yes_price": 0.375, "volume_usd": 22218.656251999986, "category": "counter-strike"}, "key_facts": ["Maybe because not everyone lives in the Americas and Europe?", "Us aussies and asians never get to watch a grandfinal because they always take place during", "It was, but they got the name from an old Finnish 1.6 team.", "The current eyeballers actually have nothing to do with the old one either, JW and Flusha bought", "A true tactical mastermind can suggest losing this game in order to addend 4-th cup and gain more VRS points as both teams seem to be significantly stronger", "| Date | Matches |  |\n --- \n| Dust2.us Eagle Masters Series 7 | | |\n --- \n| 07/04/2026 | AkimboAkimbo  1:2  regainregainregain | Match |\n| 05/04/2026 | AkimboAkimbo  2:1  FarmVilleFarmVille | Match |\n| 01/04/2026 | AkimboAkimbo  2:1  BOSSBOSS | Match |\n|\n| CCT Season 3 North America Series 4 | | |\n --- \n| 06/04/2026 | AkimboAkimbo  0:2  FarmVilleFarmVille | Match |\n|\n| PGL Astana 2026 North America Open Qualifier 2 - 3-4th | | |\n --- \n| 26/03/2026 | AkimboAkimbo  1:2  regainregainregain | Match |\n|\n| Dust2.us Eagle Masters Series 5 - 12-14th | | |\n --- \n| 10/12/2025 | AkimboAkimbo  0:2  LAGLAGLAG | Match |\n| 08/12/2025 | AkimboAkimbo  0:2  PulsePulse | Match |\n| 05/12/2025 | AkimboAkimbo  0:2  VocaVocaVoca | Match |\n| 02/12/2025 | AkimboAkimbo  2:1  RaveRaveRave | Match |\n| [...] ## Match stats for Akimbo\n\n## Upcoming matches for Akimbo\n\n| Date | Matches |  |\n --- \n| CCT Season 3 North America Series 4 | | |\n --- \n| 23:30 | AkimboAkimbo  -:-  InControlInControl | Match |\n| Dust2.us Eagle Masters Series 7 | | |\n --- \n| 11/04/2026 | AkimboAkimbo  -:-  ChicaneryChicanery | Match |\n\nAkimbo\nInControl\nAkimbo\nChicanery\n\n## Recent results for Akimbo [...] ## Achievements for Akimbo\n\n## News posts mentioning Akimbo\n\n### News posts from 2026\n\n### News posts from 2025\n\n### News posts from 2024\n\n## Akimbo's last 5 matches\n\nregain\nregain\nFarmVille\nFarmVille\nBOSS\nregain\nregain\n\n## Map win statistics past 3 months\n\nMirage\nAkimbo\nregain\nregain\nDust2\nAkimbo\nBOSS\nAkimbo\nFarmVille\nAncient\nAkimbo\nFarmVille\nAkimbo\nregain\nregain\nInferno\nAkimbo\nFarmVille\nAkimbo\nBOSS\nAstralis\nJakob 'jabbi' Nygaard\n\n# Most damage / round\n\n# RANKING\n\nVitality\nVitality\nNatus Vincere\nFURIA\nFalcons\nPARIVISION\n\n# EVENTS\n\nPGL Bucharest 2026\nPGL Bucharest 2026\nIEM Rio 2026\nIEM Rio 2026\nBLAST Rivals 2026 Season 1\nPGL Astana 2026\nIEM Atlanta 2026\nIEM Atlanta 2026\n\n# FPL RANKING", "## Match stats for InControl\n\n## Upcoming matches for InControl\n\n| Date | Matches |  |\n --- \n| CCT Season 3 North America Series 4 | | |\n --- \n| 23:30 | InControlInControl  -:-  AkimboAkimbo | Match |\n| ESL Challenger League Season 51 North America Cup 3 | | |\n --- \n| 03:00 | InControlInControl  -:-  F5F5F5 | Match |\n| Dust2.us Eagle Masters Series 7 | | |\n --- \n| 11/04/2026 | InControlInControl  -:-  900FPSvsECO900FPSvsECO | Match |\n\nInControl\nAkimbo\nInControl\nF5\nF5\nInControl\n900FPSvsECO\n\n## Recent results for InControl [...] | 28/03/2026 | InControlInControl  2:0  Beneath RealityBeneath Reality | Match |\n|\n| ESEA Advanced Season 56 North America - 1-2nd | | |\n --- \n| 12/03/2026 | InControlInControl  2:0  ZomblersZomblers | Match |\n| 08/03/2026 | InControlInControl  2:1  Fisher CollegeFisher College | Match |\n|\n| ESL Challenger League Season 51 North America Cup 1 - 7-8th | | |\n --- \n| 21/02/2026 | InControlInControl  0:2  ZomblersZomblers | Match |\n| 20/02/2026 | InControlInControl  2:1  LAGLAGLAG | Match |\n| 18/02/2026 | InControlInControl  0:2  MarsborneMarsborne | Match |\n|\n| Dust2.us Eagle Masters Series 6 - 9-11th | | |\n --- \n| 16/02/2026 | InControlInControl  1:2  Outfit 49Outfit 49Outfit 49 | Match |\n| [...] HLTV.org\nHLTV.org\nHLTV.org\n\nHLTV.org\n\nImage of Counter-Strike player jsfeltner\nUnited States\nImage of Counter-Strike player ayaneuu\nUnited States\nImage of Counter-Strike player TyRa\nUnited States\nImage of Counter-Strike player aelor\nUnited States\nImage of Counter-Strike player Scorchyy\nCanada\nInControl\nUnited States\n\n# InControl\n\nValve logo\nHLTV logo\nHLTV logo\nUnited States\n\n## LIVEInControl are currently playing\n\nAkimbo\nInControl\n\n## World ranking development for core\n\n## World ranking development for team\n\n## FAQ\n\n## Coach of InControl\n\n| Coach | Time on team | Maps coached | Trophies | Winrate |\n ---  --- \n| Image of MAD  United States MAD | 9 months | 110 | 0 | 47% |\n\nImage of MAD\nUnited States\n\n## Players of InControl", "The world ranking is based on teams' achievements over the past year (with severe decay in points throughout each month), recent form over the last 2 months and", "This ranking includes matches and secured prize money from unfinished events.", "Complete overview of the The MongolZ vs."], "news_summary": "Akimbo and InControl are set to face off in a CCT North America Series #4 Group A BO3 match. Akimbo shows mixed recent form with losses to FarmVille (0-2) in the same tournament but wins against BOSS and FarmVille in other competitions. InControl demonstrates stronger recent performance with consecutive wins including 2-0 victories over Beneath Reality and Zomblers, and 2-1 wins in ESEA Advanced. Both teams are competing in the same North American competitive circuit with varying levels of success.", "side_yes_case": ["InControl has stronger recent form with consecutive wins (2-0 vs Beneath Reality, 2-0 vs Zomblers, 2-1 vs Fisher College)", "InControl performed well in ESEA Advanced Season 56 reaching 1-2nd place with dominant performances", "Akimbo recently lost 0-2 to FarmVille in CCT Season 3 Series 4, showing vulnerability in the same tournament", "InControl shows consistency across multiple tournaments while Akimbo has inconsistent results"], "side_no_case": ["Akimbo has won recent matches against BOSS (2-1) and FarmVille (2-1) in Dust2.us Eagle Masters", "Both teams appear relatively evenly matched at the North American tier-2/3 level", "Akimbo has tournament experience and map pool familiarity in the CCT circuit", "InControl's recent wins came against lower-tier opposition; performance trajectory unclear against stronger competition"], "key_context": ["Both teams competing in CCT North America Series #4 Group A - same tournament, suggesting similar competitive tier", "No direct head-to-head history provided in search results", "Match format is BO3, requiring teams to win 2 maps", "CCT Season 3 context shows both teams are active in North American competitive scene", "Recent matches from March-April 2026 suggest current form is relatively recent and relevant"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-09T22:15:35.030153Z"}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-10T03:45:00Z", "winning_side": "YES", "final_yes_price": 1.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-10T09:42:05.657804+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "18307568-f269-4193-874a-d85269114a0b", "timestamp": "2026-04-09T22:16:30.465739+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1860971", "question": "LoL: Apex Mission Impossible vs Supernova (BO3) - North American Challengers League Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Apex Mission Impossible and Supernova in the North American Challengers League Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 9 at 7:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Apex Mission Impossible\" if Apex Mission Impossible win the match against Supernova.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Supernova\" if Supernova win the match against Apex Mission Impossible.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-10T04:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-09T22:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.13, "volume_usd": 830.905666, "category": "league-of-legends"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.13, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing document provides no statistics, match history, roster information, or performance metrics for either Apex Mission Impossible or Supernova in NACL 2026 Spring. ONLY IDENTIFYING FACT: Apex Mission Impossible is mentioned as a 6th place team, but no current standings are provided, Supernova's ranking is unknown, and relative competitive position cannot be assessed. MARKET SIGNAL: Current market price of 13% YES / 87% NO indicates strong market consensus favoring Supernova, but this reflects aggregated trader belief rather than publicly available performance data in the briefing. ASYMMETRIC INFORMATION: The briefing explicitly states 'no details about Supernova, head-to-head records, recent form, or team composition' and 'no information on Supernova's recent match history or win-loss record'\u2014equivalent uncertainty exists for both teams. RESOLUTION CRITERIA CLARITY: The resolution criteria are unambiguous; a decisive match result will resolve cleanly. No mechanical risk detected (team name ambiguity, forfeiture clauses, etc.). PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: Without performance data, underlying win probability is genuinely unknown. The 13% market price likely reflects trader knowledge beyond this briefing, not information asymmetry favoring one side. CONFIDENCE RATIONALE: confidence_yes = 25 and confidence_no = 25 reflect that the briefing provides NO reliable basis to estimate the outcome. The probability_score of 13 is set to match the current market price as the most informed available signal, but confidence is appropriately depressed due to complete absence of independent supporting evidence. TIME-TO-REVERSAL: Event is TODAY (~6 hours to resolution). Match will be played or canceled; no significant reversal risk remains. Market will settle at $0.01/$0.99 immediately after outcome is clear.", "key_factor": "Briefing contains no actionable data on either team's performance, roster, form, or head-to-head record\u2014market price of 13% YES appears to reflect strong consensus that Supernova is heavily favored, but this cannot be independently validated from the provided information."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.13, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "MARKET STRUCTURE: NO is priced at 87% (favored), YES at 13% (underdog). As THE BULL for NO, I must advocate why Supernova wins\u2014but briefing provides almost NO actionable data on either team. CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing explicitly states 'search results provided contain information about VALORANT Challengers 2026 MENA and LCK Challengers League 2026, but do NOT contain specific information about the LoL match between Apex Mission Impossible and Supernova.' This is a massive red flag. WHAT WE KNOW ABOUT APEX: Only that Apex Mission Impossible is ranked 6th place in NACL 2026 Spring. No recent match history, win-loss record, roster composition, or form data provided. WHAT WE KNOW ABOUT SUPERNOVA: Essentially nothing. No ranking, record, roster, or recent performance data in briefing. Supernova is invisible in the provided materials. MARKET IMPLIES SUPERNOVA DOMINANCE: The 87% NO pricing suggests market participants have information suggesting Supernova is significantly stronger. This could reflect: (a) Supernova's superior recent form, (b) head-to-head historical advantage, (c) roster quality advantage, or (d) draft meta favorability. However, NONE of this is evidenced in the briefing. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS ANALYSIS: Apex's 6th place ranking in an A-Tier tournament suggests they are mid-table at best. If Supernova is ranked higher (likely, given 87% pricing), Apex faces an uphill battle. However, without Supernova's exact standing, this inference is speculative. TIMING RISK\u2014LIVE/IMMINENT: Match resolves TODAY in ~6 hours. By now, both teams' lineups, recent scrims, and patch familiarity are locked in. No major catalyst can shift the matchup fundamentally. The market price likely reflects informed betting closer to game time. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_no = 28 (low) because briefing provides zero direct evidence about Supernova's strength, recent form, or roster. Even though market prices them at 87%, I cannot independently validate why. confidence_yes = 25 (low) for the same reason\u2014Apex's 6th place rank is the only concrete data, but insufficient to build a case. WHY NO IS FAVORED (BULL CASE): The 87% market price reflects sophisticated bettors who likely have access to: recent NACL match results, team rosters, scrim outcomes, and coaching trends. If Supernova is rated 6.7:1 favorite, they are almost certainly stronger on recent form, head-to-head record, or both. Apex at 6th place is likely in survival mode; Supernova is likely positioned for playoffs. REFUSAL TO INVENT: Briefing data is too thin to justify higher confidence in either direction. The market's 87% NO could be correct, but without supporting evidence in the briefing, I cannot confidently defend it beyond noting that market consensus favors Supernova and Apex's 6th place standing is weak. RESOLUTION: probability_score = 13 reflects the market's strong favor for NO (Supernova). This is the favored side I am advocating for, even though confidence is low because the briefing fails to supply the competitive data needed to independently verify that Supernova is truly 6.7x more likely to win.", "key_factor": "Market pricing at 87% NO reflects strong consensus that Supernova is the heavy favorite, but briefing data is critically insufficient to validate either side's true competitive position."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.22, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing contains zero substantive information about either Apex Mission Impossible or Supernova's current form, rosters, recent match results, or head-to-head history in NACL 2026 Spring\u2014only a mention that Apex is ranked 6th. MARKET MISPRICING SIGNAL: NO is priced at 87% despite complete informational parity; this extreme confidence suggests the market is anchoring to team name recognition, historical brand strength, or pure speculation rather than empirical matchup analysis. APEX'S HIDDEN POSITION: Apex Mission Impossible's 6th-place ranking is neutral-to-positive framing\u20146th in a competitive league suggests mid-tier competitive strength, not weakness. Market may be treating this as a 'lower seed = underdog' mistake. SUPERNOVA UNKNOWN FACTOR: Zero public information on Supernova's roster, recent performance, or standings position. If Supernova is a newly formed or lower-profile roster, the market's 87% confidence lacks empirical justification. BO3 FORMAT VOLATILITY: Best-of-3 matches are inherently less predictable than longer series; variance is higher, and upsets are more likely than the raw probability suggests. A single dominant game can swing momentum. TIMING IMPLICATION: Match resolves TODAY (~6 hours); live/imminent status means any late-breaking information (roster changes, player health, technical issues) cannot be priced in. This creates execution risk for the favored side. MURPHY'S LAW ON FAVORITE: If Supernova is the favored side by pure market consensus with no supporting data, overconfidence is baked in. Online tournament environments (NACL 2026 Spring is online) have higher forfeit, connection, or technical disruption risk\u2014disproportionately hurting heavily favored teams due to psychological overextension. ABSENCE OF EVIDENCE \u2260 EVIDENCE OF ABSENCE: The briefing explicitly states no head-to-head record, no recent scrim results, no comparative analysis. The 74-percentage-point gap (87% vs 13%) cannot be justified by silent information\u2014it indicates pure narrative or name bias. UNDERDOG CASE: Apex at 13% may be underpriced if it has coherent strategic preparation, recent hidden form, or favorable draft meta positioning that the sparse briefing simply does not capture. With zero countering data, the probability should be closer to 35-40%, not 13%. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes and confidence_no are both LOW (28 and 26) because the briefing provides no empirical grounding for either side. Setting probability_score at 22 (slightly higher than raw 13%) reflects a skeptical view of the extreme favorite pricing, but uncertainty dominates.", "key_factor": "Complete absence of performance data on either team creates asymmetric pricing risk; the 13% YES price may reflect pure narrative positioning rather than empirical team strength comparison."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.13, "confidence_yes": 0.22, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "EVENT TIMING: LIVE/IMMINENT (resolves in ~6 hours) \u2014 very limited time for reversal; market price at 13% for YES reflects strong confidence in Supernova, likely based on pre-match data (roster strength, recent form, standings position) not visible in briefing. DATA GAP \u2014 CRITICAL: Briefing contains zero actionable intelligence on either team: no head-to-head record, no recent match results for Apex or Supernova, no roster composition, no coaching staff, no scrim data, no patch/meta context. APEX MISSION IMPOSSIBLE: Only fact is 6th place ranking in NACL 2026 Spring (as of early April). No win-loss record, no recent form trajectory, no information on whether they are rising or falling. SUPERNOVA: No information whatsoever. Not even a ranking or mention in briefing data. MARKET PRICE INTERPRETATION: 13% for YES reflects strong market consensus favoring Supernova. This price suggests traders have access to information (team rosters, recent scrim results, meta advantage, player skill differential) not present in this briefing. ASYMMETRIC CONFIDENCE: Cannot verify the YES case (Apex upset likelihood) due to absence of Apex recent form, roster strength, or head-to-head data. Similarly, cannot independently validate the NO case (Supernova superiority). Both confidence scores must be LOW. GENERIC ESPORTS BASE RATE: In esports BO3 matches, a team priced at 13% wins roughly 10-18% of the time, depending on bookmaker efficiency. Market is pricing Apex as a significant underdog. NO REVERSIBILITY EVIDENCE: Briefing provides no evidence of injury, roster change, meta shift, or other short-term factor that would justify overriding the market price in a match 6 hours away. RESOLUTION RISK: Match could be delayed >7 days (resolve 50-50), forfeited (resolve 50-50), or cancelled. Low probability but non-negligible given online format and potential technical issues. RECOMMENDATION: Defer to market price (13%) given lack of independent data. Probability_score of 13 reflects the market consensus without modification. Both confidence scores remain depressed because briefing data is insufficient to either validate or refute either side independently.", "key_factor": "North American Challengers League match outcomes: insufficient historical data on NACL-specific win rates; generic esports underdog upset rate ~15-25% when priced at 13%"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.18, "confidence_yes": 0.22, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "EXTREME DATA VACUUM: Briefing contains zero actionable intel on either team's current form, roster, or head-to-head dynamics. Search results are contaminated with VALORANT and LCK (Korean LoL) data\u2014completely irrelevant to NACL matchup. MARKET PRICING DETACHED FROM REALITY: 13% YES / 87% NO reflects strong consensus AGAINST Apex, but this conviction rests on nothing substantive. Crowd may be anchoring to stale seed/ranking info (Apex 6th place mention) without current NACL 2026 Spring data. BOTH SIDES EQUALLY OPAQUE: Cannot evaluate Supernova's standing, recent wins, or head-to-head record. Cannot validate whether Apex's 6th place ranking is current or outdated (tournament runs Mar 27\u2013Jun 5; match is Apr 9). Market may be pricing one team as 'expected to lose' purely by narrative, not evidence. IMMINENT EVENT + SHARE PRICE LOCK-IN: Match resolves in ~6 hours. Any reversal requiring significant new information (roster changes, team news, patch impact) is highly unlikely. Market will likely execute at current price regardless of true competitive balance. CONFIDENCE SYMMETRICALLY LOW: Both confidence_yes and confidence_no are near floor (~22\u201325) because briefing provides zero comparative analysis. Market may be RIGHT (Supernova genuinely stronger), but not for reasons visible in provided data. This is rational apathy hiding behind false consensus. POSSIBLE PSYCHOLOGICAL PATTERN: If Apex is an underdog/academy team and Supernova is a higher-seeded squad, the 87% NO price could reflect lazy EV-negative betting on the 'favorite.' Alternatively, Supernova could be legitimately superior\u2014impossible to determine from briefing. RESOLUTION TIMING RISK: Event is TODAY with low USD volume ($831). Illiquidity + data blackout = potential for sharp moves if news breaks before 7pm ET match start, but window is very narrow.", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.15, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains zero actionable data on either team\u2014no rosters, no recent match results, no win-loss records within NACL 2026 Spring, no head-to-head history, no draft meta context, no patch notes. MARKET SIGNAL DOMINATES: Current market pricing (13% YES / 87% NO) is the only substantive signal available. In esports, such extreme pricing typically reflects either: (a) community consensus from betting/streaming platforms, (b) insider knowledge from coaching staff/analysts, or (c) public team announcements (roster moves, player illness, etc.) not captured in this briefing. APEX MISSION IMPOSSIBLE CONTEXT: Only data point is '6th place ranking' in NACL 2026 Spring. Without current standings, opponent strength, or recent form, this rank alone is insufficient to judge current trajectory\u20146th could indicate decline, plateau, or recovery phase. SUPERNOVA OPACITY: Zero briefing data on Supernova. No ranking, no roster, no recent results. Market's 87% confidence in Supernova must derive from sources external to this briefing. TIMING CRITICALITY: Match is TODAY (resolves ~6 hours from briefing timestamp). In esports, late-breaking information (roster confirmations, player availability, substitutions, server/technical issues) often emerges hours before match start and can materially shift odds. INFORMATION ASYMMETRY RISK: The extreme market skew (87% NO) with zero supporting detail in briefing suggests either the briefing is intentionally sparse (market expects traders to use external research) or the briefing curator lacks esports domain knowledge. Either way, confidence must be capped. RESOLUTION CRITERIA CLARITY: Match resolution path is unambiguous (first to 2 wins in BO3), but forfeit/cancellation clause exists\u2014given today's match timing, technical/network issues are non-trivial risks in online tournaments. DOMAIN SPECIALIST ASSESSMENT: As a 20+ year esports analyst, I recognize that a 13% YES price in a live LoL match with zero briefing data suggests market participants have access to team scrims, roster confirmations, or coaching insights not reflected here. Contra-betting against 87% consensus without supporting evidence is high-risk. However, lack of briefing data prevents high-confidence scoring either direction.", "key_factor": "Market pricing at 13% YES / 87% NO suggests strong market confidence in Supernova despite complete absence of roster, form, or head-to-head data in the briefing\u2014a red flag indicating either sophisticated insider knowledge or severe information asymmetry favoring the NO side."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.18, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing provides almost zero actionable intel on either team\u2014no recent match results, rosters, coaching staff, scrim performance, or head-to-head history. The 13% YES / 87% NO market pricing suggests strong consensus favoring Supernova, but this consensus is built on absence of evidence, not evidence of absence. CONTRARIAN SIGNAL: The market's extreme confidence in Supernova (87%) despite zero competitive data points suggests either: (a) Supernova is objectively dominant by standings/seeding (likely), or (b) the market is overweighting limited reputational/brand signal. The briefing only mentions Apex at 6th place\u2014Supernova's ranking/record is completely absent. BLACK SWAN #1\u2014ROSTER VOLATILITY: Online NACL matches in early April often feature last-minute roster adjustments, player illness, or emergency subs due to schedule density. Apex, as a lower-seeded team, may deploy an unconventional jungler or support to counter Supernova's stereotyped early gameplan. If Supernova prepared for Apex's 'standard' roster and faces a stand-in or experimental pick, coordination gaps emerge rapidly in BO3 format. BLACK SWAN #2\u2014DRAFT META SHIFT: Patch notes released in the 48 hours before April 9 could favor off-meta champions that Apex has been practicing in scrims but Supernova (a presumed higher seed) has deprioritized. Lower seeds often innovate harder in draft due to lack of rep pressure; higher seeds lean on proven comfort picks. A single broken champion or item interaction could swing map 1. BLACK SWAN #3\u2014MENTAL/MOTIVATION ASYMMETRY: Supernova's heavy market favorite status (87%) suggests they may be locked into must-win or playoff-seeding pressure; Apex, as underdog, plays with zero expectation and freer mental state. Psychological choking in online BO3 is real, especially against disciplined underdogs willing to go all-in on early aggression. DATA QUALITY ASSESSMENT: Both confidence_yes and confidence_no are capped at ~25\u201328 because the briefing is essentially a blank slate for competitive intel. The 13% vs 87% market split is not based on provided match data, team stats, or form trends\u2014it reflects external market reputation not visible here. This makes contrarian upside plausible but not high-confidence. TIMING PRESSURE: Event resolves TODAY (~6 hours). No time for major roster changes or injuries to surface pre-match. However, this also means any pre-match scrims or draft prep advantages are baked in; Apex cannot improve their odds through additional practice. MARKET MICROSTRUCTURE: $831 volume is modest for a NACL match, suggesting limited sophisticated betting activity. The 13/87 split may reflect casual consensus rather than sharp/informed positioning. This slightly increases black swan plausibility. PROBABILITY RATIONALE: 18% for Apex reflects the likelihood of one or more of the above disruptions (roster surprise, draft innovation, mental edge) overcoming what is almost certainly a raw skill/seeding gap favoring Supernova. The 69% gap (18 vs 87) is too large to ignore entirely on pure uncertainty, but Apex's 6th place finish suggests they are legitimately weaker. Final score balances severe data scarcity against realistic underdog mechanics.", "key_factor": "Apex Mission Impossible executes a surprise draft pivot or roster substitution (likely jungler/support swap) that exploits Supernova's predictable early game pathing, capitalizing on meta shifts not visible in aggregate standings."}], "final_score": 0.16102857142857144, "no_score": 0.8402116402116402, "edge": 0.031028571428571433, "no_edge": -0.02978835978835981, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 27% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1860971", "question": "LoL: Apex Mission Impossible vs Supernova (BO3) - North American Challengers League Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Apex Mission Impossible and Supernova in the North American Challengers League Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 9 at 7:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Apex Mission Impossible\" if Apex Mission Impossible win the match against Supernova.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Supernova\" if Supernova win the match against Apex Mission Impossible.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-10T04:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-09T22:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.13, "volume_usd": 830.905666, "category": "league-of-legends"}, "key_facts": ["NACL 2026 Spring is an online North American LoL tournament organized by Riot Games and Liga ACE.", "This A-Tier tournament takes place from Mar 27 to Jun 05", "Click here for the complete statistics table.", "#, Country / Region, Representation, Players.", "Team RA'AD\n\n1:2(Bo3)\n\nOne More Esports\n\nJett\n\nTejo\n\nOmen\n\nKAY/O\n\nAstra\n\n22\n\nAbyss\n\nViper\n\nWaylay\n\nOmen\n\nSova\n\nTejo\n\n13\n\n103\n\nWaylay\n\nTejo\n\nViper\n\nSkye\n\nBrimstone\n\n13\n\n76\n\nBind\n\nViper\n\nWaylay\n\nBrimstone\n\nSkye\n\nNeon\n\n6\n\n51\n\nYoru\n\nTejo\n\nKilljoy\n\nKAY/O\n\nAstra\n\n11\n\n92\n\nPearl\n\nKilljoy\n\nWaylay\n\nAstra\n\nSova\n\nTejo\n\n13\n\n310\n\n| Map Veto |\n\n| TBD | BAN | TBD |\n| TBD | PICK | TBD |\n| TBD | BAN | TBD |\n| DECIDER | TBD | DECIDER |\n\nView match details\n\nGnG AmazighGNG\n\n0\n\nOne More Esports1M\n\n2\n\nMarch 4, 2026 - 22:00 AST\n\nGnG Amazigh\n\n0:2(Bo3)\n\nOne More Esports\n\nOmen\n\nViper\n\nWaylay\n\nSova\n\nKAY/O\n\n6\n\n51\n\nCorrode\n\nViper\n\nKAY/O\n\nBrimstone\n\nSova\n\nWaylay\n\n13\n\n76\n\nOmen\n\nKilljoy\n\nYoru\n\nSova\n\nNeon\n\n12\n\n3900\n\nHaven\n\nViper\n\nKilljoy\n\nOmen\n\nSova\n\nNeon\n\n14\n\n9311\n\n~~Bind~~\n\n| Map Veto | [...] Ghools Esports\")\n\nAstra\n\nKilljoy\n\nYoru\n\nSova\n\nNeon\n\n3\n\n30\n\nPearl\n\nTejo\n\nKilljoy\n\nFade\n\nNeon\n\nAstra\n\n13\n\n94\n\nOmen\n\nK