{"run_id": "fe7c6349-ef66-48b9-a1ba-9c91f755ad81", "timestamp": "2026-04-10T11:47:29.353817+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1928473", "question": "Counter-Strike: Entropy vs ImmuNe (BO1) - Parken Challenger Championship Group A", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike match between Entropy and ImmuNe in the Parken Challenger Championship Group A, initially scheduled for April 10 at 7:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Entropy\" if Entropy win the match against ImmuNe.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"ImmuNe\" if ImmuNe win the match against Entropy.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-10T17:10:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-10T11:10:00Z", "yes_price": 0.375, "volume_usd": 2260.244854, "category": "counter-strike"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: Entropy must win a BO1 match against ImmuNe in Parken Challenger Championship Group A on April 10, 7:00 AM ET. CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains no comparative strength data, recent form, head-to-head records, or roster information for either team. The tournament table shows Entropy Gaming with a 2-1 record in the group stage, but ImmuNe does not appear in the provided standings at all. ENTROPY VISIBILITY: Entropy Gaming appears in the standings (6th place, 2-1 record, +3 RD) indicating tournament participation and demonstrated competitive play. This is the only concrete performance data available. IMMUNE DATA ABSENCE: ImmuNe has zero representation in the briefing data\u2014no standings position, no match results, no performance indicators. This creates asymmetric information favoring NO side assessment. MARKET PRICING SIGNAL: Current prices (YES 38% / NO 62%) align with Entropy's lower seeding position (6th of visible teams) relative to higher-ranked opponents. The pricing appears rational given limited data, not indicative of strong Entropy fundamentals. BO1 VOLATILITY: Best-of-1 format inherently reduces predictability and increases upset probability. This should anchor probability estimates toward 50%, not extreme values. RESOLUTION CRITERIA: Clear and straightforward\u2014match must be completed with a decisive winner. No ambiguity in team identification or resolution mechanism beyond standard online source delays. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFICATION: confidence_yes and confidence_no both set to 25 because (1) insufficient data on either team's strength prevents confident YES estimate, and (2) complete absence of ImmuNe performance data prevents confident NO estimate. The 38% probability_score reflects market consensus under information poverty, not strong analytical conviction. TIME CONSTRAINT: Event resolves in ~5 hours. Too imminent to significantly reassess without new performance data. Market pricing likely reflects all available public information at this stage.", "key_factor": "Severe data insufficiency: no performance metrics, head-to-head records, roster information, or recent form data available for either team; market pricing appears to reflect available information rather than underlying competitive reality."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE ANALYSIS (NO/ImmuNe @ 62%): The market has priced ImmuNe as the clear favorite despite zero performance data in the briefing. This pricing discrepancy suggests either: (1) ImmuNe has superior recent results not captured in search results, (2) roster/player strength favors ImmuNe, or (3) head-to-head history favors ImmuNe. In low-information environments, market consensus often reflects edge knowledge from esports analysts and bettors with deeper tournament data. UNDERDOG CASE (YES/Entropy @ 38%): Entropy Gaming demonstrated a 2-1 record in PROJECT V 2026 Split 2 Weekly #2, showing competitive form in recent weeks. However, this is the ONLY concrete performance data available for either team. Entropy's +3 round differential in the Parken standings (42-39 across 3 matches) places them 6th in the current group \u2014 a mid-table finish that does not suggest championship-level strength. CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing explicitly states 'No specific information about Entropy's or ImmuNe's recent form, head-to-head records, roster strength, or tournament performance is available.' This asymmetric information gap is the core driver of confidence reduction on BOTH sides. We are estimating market prices, not underlying truth. BO1 FORMAT RISK: Best-of-1 matches are inherently volatile and sample-size dependent. This format reduces the predictive power of form-based analysis and elevates randomness. However, this volatility affects BOTH teams equally \u2014 it does not swing the probability decisively in either direction. MARKET PRICING AS SIGNAL: A 62% NO price (vs. 38% YES) in a data-poor environment is noteworthy. Esports prediction markets on niche C-Tier tournaments are typically bet by informed community members with access to regional tournament data, scrim results, and roster knowledge. The market's 24-point spread suggests ImmuNe has demonstrable advantages that the briefing does not surface. OFFLINE TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: Parken is a Danish offline event. ImmuNe's potential home-region advantage (if Danish-based or EU-based with lower travel friction) could explain market pricing. Entropy's travel logistics are unknown but represent a potential disadvantage in an unfamiliar venue. ENTROPY'S TOURNAMENT STANDING WEAKNESS: At 6th place in Group A with a +3 round differential, Entropy is not tracking as a top-4 team in this tournament. While tournament placement mid-tournament is not fully predictive, it suggests ImmuNe (if higher-placed) has accumulated more consistent wins. NO REVERSALS VISIBLE: The briefing contains no injury reports, roster changes, disqualifications, or other catalysts that would explain a sudden ImmuNe collapse. The underdog (Entropy) would need to execute flawlessly in a single map against a favorite with hidden form advantages \u2014 a low-probability scenario. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: confidence_yes is 28 (low) because Entropy's only visible edge (a 2-1 record elsewhere) is thin and does not counter the market's 62% ImmuNe price. confidence_no is 35 (also low) because the briefing provides no actual data on ImmuNe's strengths \u2014 we are trusting market consensus in a data-void. Neither side can be assessed with high confidence, but NO's market premium suggests structural information advantages. PROBABILITY ASSIGNMENT: A 62 probability_score directly mirrors the market's NO price, reflecting the maxim that well-informed esports betting markets often price information correctly when data is sparse. The market premium for ImmuNe is treated as a credible signal absent contradicting evidence in the briefing.", "key_factor": "ImmuNe's market pricing to 62% reflects either superior recent form, roster strength, or head-to-head advantage not visible in the briefing data \u2014 a signal that institutional knowledge favors ImmuNe despite the information vacuum."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "UNDERDOG CASE FOR ENTROPY (YES): Entropy demonstrated a 2-1 record in PROJECT V 2026 Split 2 Weekly #2, showing they can compete and win matches in organized tournaments. In a BO1 format, single-map variance is high \u2014 one strong map pick or preparation can swing the result. BO1 VOLATILITY: Best-of-1 matches are inherently unpredictable compared to longer series. The briefing offers NO head-to-head data, meaning historical matchups do not constrain the outcome. A single map eliminates comeback potential and maximizes the impact of preparation, anti-strat execution, and day-to-day form. DATA ASYMMETRY & MARKET MISPRICING: The briefing explicitly states ImmuNe has NO performance data or context in search results. The market may be pricing NO at 62% on name recognition, assumption of strength, or default bias rather than on concrete evidence. Entropy at least has a documented recent win-record. FAVORITE'S HIDDEN WEAKNESS: ImmuNe's lack of data could indicate they are a newer roster, lesser-known squad, or have not competed in tracked tournaments recently. The absence of evidence is not evidence of strength. A team with no public form data is harder to assess \u2014 they could be vulnerable if underprepared for an offline event. ENTROPY'S DEMONSTRATED FORM: Entropy went 2-1 in recent tournament play, including wins against tournament-level opposition. This is the only concrete performance signal in the briefing for either team. In the absence of counter-evidence for ImmuNe, Entropy's documented competitiveness is valuable. OFFLINE TOURNAMENT LOGISTICS: The match is offline in Denmark. If ImmuNe is based outside Denmark or Europe, travel fatigue, unfamiliar LAN environment, or preparation disruption could disadvantage them. No roster location data is provided, but this remains a possible edge for a locally-based or better-prepared Entropy. MARKET PRICING AS SIGNAL, NOT PROOF: YES at 38% reflects market consensus, but with only $2,260 in volume and no expert commentary in the briefing, this price may be thin and reactive rather than informationally efficient. The 62/38 split does not prove ImmuNe is stronger \u2014 it reflects uncertainty with a slight lean. CONFIDENCE CAPS DUE TO DATA SCARCITY: Confidence on both YES and NO sides is capped below 40 because the briefing provides insufficient concrete evidence for either team \u2014 no roster info, head-to-head records, recent form for ImmuNe, or tournament seeding context. The probability score of 42 reflects a slight lean toward Entropy based on documented recent wins, but this is a weak signal in a high-variance BO1. REALISTIC UPSET NARRATIVE: Entropy, having proven they can win recent matches, faces an ImmuNe team with zero documented performance context. In a single-map format, Entropy's preparation, map pool advantage, or in-game execution could prevail. The market may have overweighted ImmuNe's name or underweighted BO1 volatility. PROBABILITY JUSTIFICATION: 42 reflects YES slightly below the market underdog baseline (38%) because the briefing does not provide strong positive evidence for Entropy beyond a single recent tournament record, nor does it provide disqualifying evidence against ImmuNe. A BO1 with no head-to-head data and limited form visibility deserves near-parity pricing; Entropy's 2-1 record nudges it marginally above 40, but not confidently so.", "key_factor": "BO1 format inherently favors upset potential, and Entropy's recent 2-1 tournament record demonstrates competitive capability against tournament opposition."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.45, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: No head-to-head history, recent form differential, roster strength comparison, or player-level metrics available for either Entropy or ImmuNe. BO1 FORMAT INHERENT UNPREDICTABILITY: Best-of-1 matches in esports exhibit high variance due to single-map dependency, minimal adaptation opportunity, and map-veto luck. Historical BO1 outcomes deviate significantly from skill-based BO3 predictions. ENTROPY MARGINAL SIGNAL: Entropy Gaming shows 2-1 record (42-39 rounds, +3 RD) in Parken Group A pool play. This is a weak positive signal (slight positive round differential) but within noise margins for C-Tier competition. No external recent form data provided. IMMUNE NO DATA: ImmuNe absent from provided tournament standings and search results. Cannot assess relative skill, recent trajectory, or roster composition. Complete informational asymmetry. CURRENT MARKET PRICE (38% YES / 62% NO) implies ImmuNe favored by ~24 percentage points. This pricing may reflect:\n  (a) Public/betting community knowledge of ImmuNe's superior current form (not in briefing),\n  (b) Roster strength differences invisible to briefing data,\n  (c) Overweighting of ImmuNe based on historical brand/tournament seeding.\n  Without access to that information, cannot validate or refute the market's confidence in ImmuNe. BASE RATE FOR LOWER-TIER BO1: When team-specific data is unavailable and format is BO1, historical outcomes approximate 50-55% for any given competitive pairing. Market price of 62% NO suggests information asymmetry favoring ImmuNe knowledge. TIME URGENCY (5 hours to resolution): Match is imminent. Substantial roster changes, lineup surprises, or systematic reversals are unlikely at this stage. Market price reflects likely informed consensus. CONFIDENCE PENALTY: Both confidence_yes and confidence_no are LOW (~26-28) because the briefing lacks the foundational data required to distinguish skill differentials. The 38/62 split appears to embed external information (likely from esports betting markets, team rankings, or roster data) not present in the document. Confidence asymmetry is minimal because we are equally blind to both teams' true strength. ASSESSMENT: Without roster, head-to-head, or recent form data, probability_score regresses toward 50. Market price of 38 YES / 62 NO suggests ImmuNe is preferred by available-but-unshown information. Modest adjustment to 45 (slightly favoring NO's market consensus) reflects low-confidence acceptance of market signal, balanced against BO1 volatility.", "key_factor": "In lower-tier CS2 BO1 matches (C-Tier, Valve Tier 2), outcomes are highly volatile. Historical base rate for favored teams in BO1 formats is ~55-60% win probability, but with minimal roster/form data, reversion to ~50% is warranted. BO1 inherent variance is ~\u00b115% around any predicted baseline."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "Market price (38% YES / 62% NO) reflects extreme information asymmetry \u2014 briefing provides Entropy's recent record (2-1, +3 RD in tournament) but ZERO data on ImmuNe's performance, roster, or history. Entropy appears in tournament standings (6th place, 2-1 record) with measurable form; ImmuNe is completely absent from briefing \u2014 market may be pricing ImmuNe's unknown status as weakness rather than genuine competitive assessment. BO1 format inherently high-variance; with no head-to-head data, map pool compatibility unknown, and no roster information for either team, the 62% confidence in ImmuNe appears overconfident rather than data-driven. Rational apathy detected: market has settled on a price but lacks the information density to justify the 24-point spread. This is crowd consensus with low conviction, not a well-informed market. Entropy's tournament presence (measurable performance vs. ImmuNe's invisibility in briefing) could justify slight YES lean, but confidence in both sides must remain very low due to critical data gaps. No recent news, no roster changes, no player-level analysis \u2014 market is pricing largely on availability bias (Entropy visible in standings) rather than true competitive strength assessment. With ~5 hours to match start and no new information likely to emerge, current price reflects static sentiment rather than informed trading. Either team could easily reverse this with a BO1 upset. Confidence scores capped at 28/25: insufficient data on either side to support strong conviction. Both confidence levels remain depressed due to missing ImmuNe context and lack of H2H intelligence.", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "Market currently prices YES (Entropy) at 38%, which is below even-money; this suggests modest sentiment favoring ImmuNe despite lack of ImmuNe performance data in briefing. Entropy Gaming appears in the provided group standings with a 2-1 record and +3 round differential (42-39), placing them 6th in a 8-team group\u2014mid-table performance, not dominant. No ImmuNe data exists in briefing; cannot assess roster quality, recent form, map pool, or head-to-head history; this asymmetry is critical in a BO1 where preparation and meta-read matter enormely. BO1 format in Counter-Strike is inherently volatile; single-map outcomes hinge on veto strategy, map comfort, and day-to-day form variation; round differential from group play (Entropy +3) is weak predictor for BO1. Offline Danish tournament context: Entropy may have logistical advantage if based in region; ImmuNe's location unknown, but travel burden could affect performance in BO1 (less time to adapt than BO3). Parken Challenger #4 is C-Tier (lowest professional tier); both teams are regional/semi-professional level; performance variance is higher and roster stability lower than tier-1 circuits. Group stage performance (2-1 record) places Entropy in knockout contention but not favorites; mid-table seed status does not indicate BO1 match advantage. Briefing explicitly notes 'limited relevant information' and 'no specific information about Entropy's or ImmuNe's recent form, head-to-head records, roster strength'; both sides of market are under-informed. Event timing is TODAY with ~5 hours to resolution; shares will likely trade toward $0.01 or $0.99 shortly before match if predictive power consolidates, but briefing data is too sparse to justify high confidence in either direction now. Confidence_yes=28 and confidence_no=26 reflect symmetric uncertainty: Entropy has marginal group-stage data (slight positive signal) but ImmuNe is a complete unknown (negative data quality, not necessarily a weak team). Probability_score=42 places Entropy as slight underdog in current market pricing; reasoning: Entropy's +3 RD is modest, BO1 favors unpredictability, and ImmuNe's absence from briefing prevents confident dismissal of their strength.", "key_factor": "BO1 format inherently inflates variance and reduces predictive power compared to BO3; Entropy's modest +3 round differential in group play suggests marginal edge but insufficient data on ImmuNe makes confidence asymmetrically weak on both sides."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "The briefing is conspicuously silent on ImmuNe's roster, recent form, and head-to-head history \u2014 a major data gap that prevents confident assessment of NO probability despite market pricing at 62%. Entropy appears in the tournament standings (2-1 record, +3 round differential), suggesting baseline competitive participation, but the table formatting is corrupted and provides no clarity on map pools, player lineups, or performance trajectory. BO1 format dramatically amplifies the variance of single-map outcomes; roster changes, tactical surprises, and map-specific expertise become disproportionately powerful \u2014 a factor often underpriced in low-information markets. This is a C-Tier Danish offline tournament with minimal mainstream coverage; roster churn, last-minute stand-ins, and logistical friction (travel, accommodation, practice time) are commonplace in regional Tier 2 CS2 and rarely reported in advance. The market prices Entropy at 38% despite it being the only team with ANY documented recent performance in the briefing (Glacial Guardians beat Entropy, but at least Entropy has a track record); ImmuNe has zero data points, yet the market assigns it 62% \u2014 possible sign of informed betting, but equally consistent with casual pricing on an underdog. Key absence: no information on whether either team has qualified for next rounds or is playing for pride/seeding; motivation asymmetry in Tier 2 tournaments can swing BO1 outcomes by 15\u201320 percentage points. Black swan scenario: ImmuNe's primary rifler or IGL is unavailable (visa delay, illness, family emergency common in regional tournaments), forcing a sub with inferior calibration to the team's usual antistrat pool \u2014 Entropy's 42 rounds in three matches suggest grindy, methodical gameplay that exploits such misalignment. Inverse risk: Entropy's 2-1 record masks a volatile form trajectory (e.g., beat weak opponents, lost to top seed); brief briefing data precludes trend analysis. Market volume ($2,260) is low for a live event in 5 hours, suggesting limited arbitrage activity and potential mispricing on either side.", "key_factor": "ImmuNe fields a substitute player or experiences a last-minute roster disruption that goes unreported until match start, offsetting Entropy's apparent competitive edge in the limited available data."}], "final_score": 0.44160000000000005, "no_score": 0.5512437810945274, "edge": 0.06660000000000005, "no_edge": -0.07375621890547257, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 55% for NO (need \u226557%); NO-side confidence too low: 29% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1928473", "question": "Counter-Strike: Entropy vs ImmuNe (BO1) - Parken Challenger Championship Group A", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike match between Entropy and ImmuNe in the Parken Challenger Championship Group A, initially scheduled for April 10 at 7:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Entropy\" if Entropy win the match against ImmuNe.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"ImmuNe\" if ImmuNe win the match against Entropy.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-10T17:10:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-10T11:10:00Z", "yes_price": 0.375, "volume_usd": 2260.244854, "category": "counter-strike"}, "key_facts": ["Parken Challenger Championship #4 is an offline Danish CS2 tournament organized by New Breed Agency and Esplay.", "This C-Tier tournament is a Valve Tier 2", "| # | Team | Matches | Rounds | RD | Round 1 | Round 2 | Round 3 |\n ---  ---  ---  --- |\n| 1.", "| Sissi State Punks Sissi State Punks | 3-0 | 26-10 | +16 | To Be Determined | ALTERNATE aTTaX EVO Split | TwoFace Gaming Lotus |\n| 2.", "| TonTaubenSchie\u00dfer TonTaubenSchie\u00dfer\") | 3-0 | 28-22 | +6 | To Be Determined | Reveal Multigaming Bind | Entropy GamingEntropy Gaming Bind |\n| 3.", "| Glacial Guardians Glacial Guardians\") | 2-1 | 40-30 | +10 | Entropy GamingEntropy Gaming Bind | Dortmund eSports Breeze | Exceptional GamingExceptional Gaming Haven |\n| 4.", "| Reveal Multigaming Reveal Multigaming | 2-1 | 35-29 | +6 | Ingenious EsportsIngenious Esports Lotus | TonTaubenSchie\u00dfer Bind | REH Gaming Haven | [...] | 4.", "| TeamOrangeGaming TeamOrangeGaming | 2-1 | 36-30 | +6 | Dortmund eSports Lotus | Entropy GamingEntropy Gaming Split | ALTERNATE aTTaX EVO Lotus |\n| 6.", "| Entropy GamingEntropy Gaming Entropy Gaming | 2-1 | 42-39 | +3 | Glacial Guardians Bind | TeamOrangeGaming Split | 