rmat means the winner needs 2 map wins; matches are offline in West Lake Gymnasium, Hangzhou", "Group Stage week 2 suggests these teams are in mid-to-late group phase with playoff implications pending", "Both teams showed inconsistency early (losses followed by dominant wins), making form trajectory analysis uncertain", "VCT 2026 China is S-Tier official tournament with significant competitive stakes for regional standings"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-10T12:02:23.214733Z"}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-10T17:45:00Z", "winning_side": "NO", "final_yes_price": 0.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-10T19:29:13.652245+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": {"kind": "missed_opportunity", "summary": "Missed opportunity \u2014 council favored NO at 68% (7/7 agents, 3 high-conv) but PASSed. Reason: NO-side confidence too low: 65% (need \u226567%)", "agents_with_winner": [{"agent": "The Bull", "prob": 0.28, "side": "NO", "side_conf": 0.72, "key_factor": "Bilibili Gaming's dominant recent form (2-0 over JDG, 2-0 over Titan) and established head-to-head counter-strategy against FunPlus Phoenix in high-stakes offline matches."}, {"agent": "The Rules Lawyer", "prob": 0.32, "side": "NO", "side_conf": 0.71, "key_factor": "Criteria are clear and unambiguous"}, {"agent": "The Sentiment Analyst", "prob": 0.32, "side": "NO", "side_conf": 0.71, "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent": "The Domain Specialist", "prob": 0.35, "side": "NO", "side_conf": 0.65, "key_factor": "BLG's recent 2-0 dominance over JDG (April 5) and Titan (April 7) represents a critical form trajectory shift into the match window, while FPX's Week 1 loss to JDG exposes a structural vulnerability that BLG has now validated it can exploit."}, {"agent": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "prob": 0.32, "side": "NO", "side_conf": 0.62, "key_factor": "In BO3 esports matches between evenly-matched regional teams with recent head-to-head splits, the underdog (28% market price) typically has 25-35% true win probability; teams showing recent dominant form (2-0 wins) maintain ~60-65% win rates in immediate follow-ups."}, {"agent": "The Bear", "prob": 0.35, "side": "NO", "side_conf": 0.58, "key_factor": "FPX's dominant 2-0 form trajectory in Week 2 (beating TYLOO 2-1 on April 7 and AG 2-0 on April 3) combined with recent head-to-head unpredictability suggests the market overweights BLG's single dominant win vs JDG while undervaluing FPX's momentum and map pool flexibility heading into a BO3."}, {"agent": "The Contrarian", "prob": 0.32, "side": "NO", "side_conf": 0.58, "key_factor": "FPX player substitution or tactical pivot triggered by internal team discord or last-minute coaching adjustment that mirrors the 'legija is such a fraud' sentiment visible in community chatter, causing map-pool vulnerability exploitation by BLG."}], "agents_against_winner": [], "median_prob": 0.32, "coin_flip": false}}
{"run_id": "561e392e-bc16-4223-88d5-70083cdfb768", "timestamp": "2026-04-10T12:03:15.315521+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1844410", "question": "LoL: JD Gaming vs Anyone's Legend (BO3) - LPL Group Ascend", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between JD Gaming and Anyone's Legend in the LPL Group Ascend, initially scheduled for April 10 at 7:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"JD Gaming\" if JD Gaming win the match against Anyone's Legend.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Anyone's Legend\" if Anyone's Legend win the match against JD Gaming.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-10T18:10:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-10T12:10:00Z", "yes_price": 0.405, "volume_usd": 164403.21920700013, "category": "league-of-legends"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "JD Gaming holds a significant standings advantage (50 points vs 20 points, 2.5x differential) after Split 1, indicating stronger overall competitive performance and roster quality. Ranking disparity (2nd vs 4th place) correlates with competitive strength in esports team hierarchies, favoring JD Gaming in a direct matchup. However, Split 1 points do not guarantee Split 2 performance \u2014 meta shifts, roster adjustments, or specific matchup dynamics could favor Anyone's Legend. Best-of-three format (BO3) reduces variance compared to single games; stronger team (JD Gaming) is favored but not guaranteed to win. No head-to-head history or recent form data provided for either team in Split 2 context \u2014 limits precision of probability estimate. Current market price of 40% YES suggests broader uncertainty; this pricing implies roughly even odds despite JD Gaming's ranking advantage. Resolution criteria are clear: first team to win BO3 series wins the match. No ambiguity regarding match completion or naming. EVENT TIMING is TODAY (resolves in ~6 hours): match is imminent. Reversal scenarios (cancellation, tie, delay >7 days) are unlikely given proximity to scheduled event. Probability 62 reflects JD Gaming's structural advantage while acknowledging split-specific volatility and BO3 upset potential. Confidence in YES (72) is moderate-to-high due to clear ranking differential; confidence in NO (48) is lower due to lack of Split 2-specific performance data for Anyone's Legend.", "key_factor": "Team name 'Anyone's Legend' lacks explicit verification against gol.gg; minor discrepancies in team naming could theoretically trigger 50-50 resolution, though the criteria's flexibility suggests this is unlikely if the real-world match is unambiguous."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.35, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE STRENGTHS (NO \u2014 Anyone's Legend): Market prices NO at 60%, reflecting skepticism of JD Gaming's ability to convert their ranking advantage into a BO3 win. Anyone's Legend qualified for LPL Split 2 alongside 13 other top teams, demonstrating they met competitive thresholds to participate in this S-Tier tournament\u2014not a free pass to anyone. Championship points (20 vs 50) reflect Split 1 performance only; meta shifts, roster adjustments, and team momentum in Split 2 (which just began Apr 4) can meaningfully diverge from prior standings. Best-of-three format inherently favors underdogs: single-elimination drama, momentum swings, and draft flexibility allow mid-tier teams to exploit weaknesses\u2014especially if JD Gaming is rusty or overconfident. JD Gaming's recent record shows 2-3 mixed form in King Pro League Spring 2026, suggesting they are NOT in dominant shape heading into this match. UNDERDOG WEAKNESSES (YES \u2014 JD Gaming): Despite ranking 2nd with 50 points, JD Gaming's 2-3 recent record is a red flag\u2014they are underperforming relative to preseason expectations. No head-to-head history provided between these teams, meaning no playable tendencies favoring either side\u2014creates uncertainty that benefits the underdog in a BO3. JD Gaming's 2.5x points advantage is meaningful but NOT insurmountable in a single BO3 match; many ranked-2nd teams lose to ranked-4th teams in playoff-style series. The 60% NO price (Anyone's Legend) appears FAIR given: mixed recent form by JD, BO3 upset potential, lack of head-to-head data, and meta volatility in a newly-started split. However, JD Gaming's superior Split 1 points, roster stability, and strategic pedigree remain genuine anchors for their candidacy\u2014the 40% YES price is not irrational. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_no (72) > confidence_yes (45) because the briefing provides direct evidence of JD Gaming's mixed recent form (2-3 record) but lacks ANY recent performance data on Anyone's Legend in Split 2, creating information imbalance favoring the NO side narrative. Lower confidence_yes reflects uncertainty about JD Gaming's current form and lack of specific matchup intelligence; higher confidence_no reflects the plausibility of upset in BO3 given the data gaps.", "key_factor": "Anyone's Legend's qualification and competitive viability in LPL Split 2 combined with BO3 upset potential suggests the 60% NO pricing may undervalue their chances despite the 2.5x points gap."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "UNDERDOG STRENGTHS: Anyone's Legend qualified for LPL Split 2 alongside 13 other top teams, demonstrating baseline competitive viability \u2014 not a relegation-tier opponent but a mid-table competitor (4th place, 20 points vs JD Gaming's 2nd place, 50 points). FAVORITE VULNERABILITY: JD Gaming's recent form is mixed \u2014 their 2-3 record in King Pro League Spring 2026 indicates inconsistency and potential tactical issues despite superior Split 1 standings, suggesting they may not be executing at peak level heading into this match. META VOLATILITY: Split 2 performance often diverges materially from Split 1 due to patch changes, meta shifts, and roster adjustments. The briefing explicitly notes 'Split 2 performance could diverge from Split 1 standings due to meta changes or roster adjustments' \u2014 this is a concrete risk factor for the favorite. RANKING GAP IS MEANINGFUL BUT NOT DISQUALIFYING: 2.5x points advantage (50 vs 20) is substantial, but both teams occupy mid-table positioning (2nd and 4th), not a dominant-vs-weak matchup. Best-of-three format amplifies upset potential \u2014 even favored teams lose BO3s at meaningful rates. MISSING HEAD-TO-HEAD DATA: No direct match history or recent performance metrics between these two teams are provided in the briefing. Without specific H2H evidence, the favorite's advantage rests solely on aggregate standings, which can be misleading in tournament play. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: Market prices YES at 40% (underdog) and NO at 60% (favorite). Given JD Gaming's 2-3 recent form, missing H2H data, potential meta shifts, and Anyone's Legend's legitimate competitive qualification, JD Gaming's win probability should be closer to 62% rather than 60%, suggesting modest underpricing of YES. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in YES estimate (72) because JD Gaming's mixed form and the briefing's explicit acknowledgment of meta-driven performance divergence provide concrete evidence for upset risk. Lower confidence in NO (45) because the briefing lacks specific recent matchup data, head-to-head records, or detailed performance metrics that would justify a strong favorite stance. TIME-TO-RESOLUTION: Event resolves TODAY (~6 hours). No time for team roster changes or major meta shifts, but match is imminent enough that pre-game conditions (form, momentum, preparation) are heavily weighted. JD Gaming's recent 2-3 form is current and concerning. CONCLUSION: JD Gaming is the reasonable favorite but not a heavy favorite. Anyone's Legend deserves 40%+ implied probability given mid-table competitive parity, JD Gaming's recent mixed results, and absent head-to-head evidence. Recommend YES at 62% \u2014 a modest uplift reflecting underdog viability.", "key_factor": "Anyone's Legend's qualification for LPL Split 2 and potential meta-driven performance divergence from Split 1 standings, combined with JD Gaming's recent mixed form (2-3 record) suggesting vulnerability despite ranking advantage."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "JD Gaming holds 2nd place (50 pts) vs Anyone's Legend 4th place (20 pts) \u2014 a 2.5x points differential strongly favors JD Gaming In LPL regional competition, championship points correlate strongly with team strength and roster quality; this gap suggests JD Gaming is the materially stronger team BO3 format increases upset potential vs BO1, but does not erase a 2.5x points gap \u2014 historical upset rates in BO3 for ranked mismatches remain ~25-35% Market prices YES at 40%, which undervalues JD Gaming's competitive advantage relative to historical win rates for top-seeded teams in this format JD Gaming's recent 2-3 record in KPL Spring 2026 introduces some form uncertainty, but does not override Split 1 championship standing advantage Anyone's Legend's 4th place standing confirms competitive entry into LPL Split 2, but no evidence of recent momentum or meta advantages that would justify 60% NO pricing Meta shifts and roster adjustments are possible explanations for NO case, but these are speculative without concrete evidence; standings remain strongest available signal Event timing (TODAY, ~6 hours to match) means limited time for new information to emerge; current market mispricing likely reflects overweighting of upset narrative vs base-rate advantage Confidence in YES is elevated (72) due to clear ranking signal; confidence in NO is suppressed (48) because briefing lacks head-to-head history, recent form, or meta context that would justify flipping the favorite", "key_factor": "In professional LoL, higher-seeded teams win ~65-70% of regular season matches against lower-seeded opponents; upset rates in BO3 format ~25-35%"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "Market is underpricing JD Gaming despite decisive ranking advantage: JD (50pts, 2nd place) vs Anyone's Legend (20pts, 4th place) \u2014 a 2.5x points gap. Current 40% YES price reflects unwarranted pessimism. JD Gaming's superior Split 1 performance is concrete evidence of stronger roster/execution. NO side (60%) appears crowded \u2014 market may be overvaluing upset potential in a single BO3 without head-to-head data or evidence of Anyone's Legend competitive parity. JD Gaming's recent 2-3 record in King Pro League is noted but does NOT override their 50-point seasonal standing. Mixed form \u2260 weakness vs a 20-point team. Anyone's Legend's qualification alone (NO case) is insufficient to justify 60% odds \u2014 qualification \u2260 competitive equivalence. No counter-evidence provided. Rational apathy detected: Market has discounted JD's ranking advantage too heavily. The briefing provides no upset signals (meta shock, roster changes favoring ALG, recent ALG wins). Imminent event timing (6 hours to resolution) means reversal odds are low; current price reflects crowd fear rather than data. Asymmetric confidence: High confidence in YES (strong ranking signal); lower confidence in NO (no substantive counter-argument beyond generic upset potential).", "key_factor": "Fear"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "JD Gaming's 50-point lead (2nd vs 4th place) reflects superior Split 1 execution across patch cycles, suggesting more stable teamfighting and macro play under current meta conditions. Anyone's Legend's 4th-place standing (20 points) indicates suboptimal performance in Split 1 but does not preclude competitive matches\u2014LPL group stages feature frequent upsets due to high team parity and fast meta evolution. BO3 format favors the higher-seeded team in close matchups; JD's ranking advantage compounds across multiple games, reducing upset probability compared to single-game scenarios. No head-to-head data or recent patch-specific performance metrics provided; blind matchup analysis relies solely on standings proxy, which historically has ~65-70% predictive accuracy in LPL regular season. Anyone's Legend's qualification into Split 2 Group Ascend and 4th-place seeding confirm baseline competitive competency; not an academy or wildcard team, so 40% market YES price may undervalue JD's ranking advantage. Missing data on roster changes, recent scrim results, and meta-specific champion pool advantages prevents higher confidence; both confidence scores reflect incomplete information on both sides. EVENT_TIMING: Match resolves in ~6 hours (TODAY, LIVE/IMMINENT); limited time for narrative reversals or strategic surprises; pricing should reflect fairly stable pre-game assessments.", "key_factor": "LPL championship points serve as a proxy for roster strength and meta adaptation, but Split 2 meta shifts and mid-season roster rotations can create significant upset conditions that raw standings do not capture."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "JD Gaming's 2-3 record in King Pro League Spring 2026 (mentioned in briefing) signals recent mixed form and potential momentum loss despite higher ranking \u2014 this disconnect between standings and current win-rate is a critical red flag. Anyone's Legend's 4th-place standing (20 pts) is only 2.5x behind JD Gaming, not a decisive gap for a BO3 \u2014 regular season volatility is high in April within the first month of Split 2. The briefing explicitly states 'Split 2 performance could diverge from Split 1 standings due to meta changes or roster adjustments' \u2014 this is silent on what those changes are, suggesting potential blind spot in JD Gaming's adaptation to evolving meta. No head-to-head history provided between these teams in the briefing \u2014 historical matchup data (bans, win conditions, individual player performance) is entirely absent, eliminating a key confidence pillar. LPL Split 2 began only 6 days ago (April 4); standings reflect only early matches. Sample size is extremely small; a 2-3 record is noise in a tournament context, not a reliable predictor. Anyone's Legend's qualification to LPL Split 2 confirms they are not a wildcard \u2014 they have demonstrated sufficient competitive viability to earn a spot, reducing the 'true underdog' framing. Offline tournament format increases susceptibility to day-of roster/personnel disruptions (illness, travel logistics, coaching adjustments) that online records do not capture \u2014 given TODAY timing, any last-minute news is unavailable. The market's 40% YES / 60% NO pricing suggests some uncertainty; if JD Gaming were a clear favorite, pricing would be more like 65-70% YES \u2014 the 40% YES price hints at latent concern about JD Gaming's form. BO3 format inherently favors the underdog more than BO1; upsets in BO3 are 30-40% more common than aggregate ranking would suggest, as teams can adapt between games.", "key_factor": "Anyone's Legend has identified a meta-favorable or map-pool advantage in Split 2 that directly counters JD Gaming's playstyle, combined with potential roster substitution or illness affecting JD Gaming's starting lineup not yet reflected in standings."}], "final_score": 0.6035849056603774, "no_score": 0.42769230769230776, "edge": 0.19858490566037734, "no_edge": -0.1673076923076922, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Contrarian call: council prob 60% < 70% threshold; Contrarian call: YES-side confidence 68% < 80% threshold", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1844410", "question": "LoL: JD Gaming vs Anyone's Legend (BO3) - LPL Group Ascend", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between JD Gaming and Anyone's Legend in the LPL Group Ascend, initially scheduled for April 10 at 7:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"JD Gaming\" if JD Gaming win the match against Anyone's Legend.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Anyone's Legend\" if Anyone's Legend win the match against JD Gaming.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-10T18:10:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-10T12:10:00Z", "yes_price": 0.405, "volume_usd": 164403.21920700013, "category": "league-of-legends"}, "key_facts": ["LPL 2026 Split 2 is an offline Chinese LoL tournament organized by TJ Sports.", "This S-Tier tournament takes place from Apr 04 to Jun 2026 featuring 14 teams", "|  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n ---  ---  --- \n| Ranking | \ud83d\udcc8\ud83d\udcc9 | Team | Total Points | Split 1 | Split 2 | Split 3 |\n| 1.", "| New | Bilibili GamingBilibili Gaming Bilibili Gaming | 80 | 80 |  |  |\n| 2.", "| New | JD GamingJD Gaming JD Gaming | 50 | 50 |  |  |\n| 3.", "| New | Weibo GamingWeibo Gaming Weibo Gaming | 40 | 40 |  |  |\n| 4.", "| New | Anyone's LegendAnyone's Legend Anyone's Legend | 20 | 20 |  |  |\n| 5.", "| New | Invictus GamingInvictus Gaming Invictus Gaming | 10 | 10 |  |  |\n| 6.", "| New | Top EsportsTop Esports Top Esports | 10 | 10 |  |  |\n| 7.", "| New | Ninjas in PyjamasNinjas in Pyjamas Ninjas in Pyjamas | 5 | 5 |  |  |\n| 8."], "news_summary": "JD Gaming and Anyone's Legend are competing in the LPL 2026 Split 2 regular season. JD Gaming currently holds 50 championship points (2nd place) after Split 1, while Anyone's Legend has accumulated 20 points (4th place). Both teams are participants in the ongoing LPL Split 2 tournament which runs from April to June 2026. The match is a best-of-three series within the Group Ascend segment of the tournament.", "side_yes_case": ["JD Gaming ranked 2nd in championship standings with 50 points vs Anyone's Legend at 4th with 20 points", "JD Gaming's superior Split 1 performance suggests stronger roster and strategic execution", "JD Gaming maintains a 2.5x points advantage in season standings", "No evidence of Anyone's Legend competing at equivalent competitive level based on available standings"], "side_no_case": ["Anyone's Legend qualified for LPL Split 2 alongside other top teams, indicating competitive viability", "Regular season match results against specific opponents not provided in search results", "Split 2 performance could diverge from Split 1 standings due to meta changes or roster adjustments", "Best-of-three format allows for upset potential despite ranking differences"], "key_context": ["LPL 2026 Split 2 runs April 4 to June 2026 with 14 teams competing", "Championship points system tracks cumulative season performance across splits", "JD Gaming's record shown as 2-3 in King Pro League Spring 2026 suggests recent mixed form", "Both teams are mid-table positioned (2nd and 4th) indicating gap may not be insurmountable", "Specific match schedule and head-to-head history between these teams not available in search results"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-10T12:03:05.686587Z"}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-10T18:25:00Z", "winning_side": "YES", "final_yes_price": 1.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-10T19:29:14.460205+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "20fec2dd-60f1-4d6d-9b0e-a3dcbebeacb4", "timestamp": "2026-04-10T12:04:07.004544+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1931503", "question": "Dota 2: L1ga Team vs GamerLegion (BO3) - PREMIER SERIES Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Dota 2 Lower bracket quarterfinal 1 match between L1ga Team and GamerLegion in the PREMIER SERIES Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 10 at 7:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"L1ga Team\" if L1ga Team win the match against GamerLegion.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"GamerLegion\" if GamerLegion win the match against L1ga Team.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://www.dotabuff.com. However, if https://www.dotabuff.com has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-10T18:15:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-10T12:15:00Z", "yes_price": 0.395, "volume_usd": 30121.467896000002, "category": "dota-2"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing provides fragmented tournament tables and match histories but contains almost no specific information about GamerLegion's recent performance, roster, or competitive standing. GamerLegion is mentioned only in the resolution criteria, not in any actual match results or tournament data. L1GA FORM ANALYSIS: Available data shows L1GA competing in PREMIER SERIES in early April 2026 with mixed results\u2014wins against Pips (2:1), VP (2:1), Power Rangers (2:0), but a 0:2 loss to NGX on April 7. This inconsistency does not establish clear dominance. HISTORICAL CONTEXT: L1GA appears in EPL Season 33 playoffs where Yellow Submarine defeated them 0:2 (December 2025). This shows L1GA can lose decisively to competent opponents, but does not predict outcomes against GamerLegion. MARKET PRICING MISALIGNMENT: Current market prices (40% YES / 60% NO) suggest traders believe GamerLegion is slightly favored, but the briefing provides no data to support this belief\u2014GamerLegion's recent results, tournament seeding, roster quality, or head-to-head record are entirely absent. BO3 FORMAT: A best-of-three requires two map wins. Without form data, map pool compatibility analysis, or recent H2H records, probability cannot be anchored to concrete competitive indicators. TIMING CONSTRAINT: Event is TODAY with ~6 hours to resolution. No meaningful reversal of match outcome is possible once play begins. Low confidence reflects insufficient data to different