CALITY: Market resolves in ~5 hours (TODAY event timing, end date 2026-04-11 00:30 UTC). If the match has NOT yet started or begun moments ago, the 76% probability reflects either: (a) early match result (if live), (b) pre-match sentiment lock-in, or (c) information asymmetry among traders. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes=42 because the market signal is strong and unambiguous (76% is decisive), but grounded entirely in unknown late-day price movement and a single Gentle Mates player strength mention, not team-level performance data. confidence_no=28 because there is virtually NO data to assess whether Karmine Corp can compete; the case for Karmine Corp is pure silence, making it impossible to evaluate defensive arguments or upset potential. RESOLUTION CRITERIA CLARITY: Criteria are unambiguous \u2014 YES resolves if Gentle Mates win; NO if Karmine Corp win. 50-50 applies only if match is canceled, delayed >7 days, ends in tie, or forfeits/DQ before start. Standard win conditions result in clean YES/NO resolution. MECHANISM RISK (SECONDARY): VLR.gg is the primary source; 2-hour fallback to credible reporting exists. This is a major esports tracking site and unlikely to have publication delays. Team name ambiguity risk is low (Gentle Mates and Karmine Corp are distinct, recognizable team names). Risk of mechanism failure \u2248 2-5%; does not materially alter core probability. PROBABILITY INFERENCE: Given the 76% market price on match day, with modest recent volatility and a known strong individual player signal for Gentle Mates (marteen Yoru), but no data on Karmine Corp or broader team form, the market appears to be pricing Gentle Mates as slight-to-moderate favorite. Absent contradictory briefing data, the 76% market price is the strongest available signal. Setting probability_score at 76 (matching market) reflects deference to price discovery in a two-sided market with real money exposure.", "key_factor": "Briefing document contains no meaningful performance data for either Gentle Mates or Karmine Corp; probability estimate relies entirely on market price signal rather than team strength assessment."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.68, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "MARKET MOMENTUM: YES side has surged +24.5pp over 7 days with a sharp +13.0pp spike 2 hours before match time (Apr 10 19:42 UTC), indicating informed traders or real-time intelligence favoring Gentle Mates. This recent acceleration is the strongest signal available. VOLUME & CONVICTION: $93,127 in trading volume with 148 data points for YES vs 44 for NO shows 3.4x more trading activity backing Gentle Mates\u2014typical of markets with clearer favorites or better-informed players. ROSTER STRENGTH HINT: Brief mentions Gentle Mates as 'boasting the world's best Yoru player in marteen'\u2014a notable competitive credential suggesting the team has at least one elite-tier player, which elevates their overall competitive tier. TECHNICAL PRICING: 76% YES vs 24% NO reflects substantial market consensus. Such a 3:1 spread typically reflects genuine competitive disparity rather than blind speculation in esports betting. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS: NO side (Karmine Corp) has NO positive signals in the briefing\u2014no player credentials mentioned, no tactical innovations noted, no recent momentum. Absence of evidence is weakness in esports prediction. TIMING ASYMMETRY: With match resolving in ~5 hours, the +13.0pp YES move 2 hours ago likely reflects late-stage intel (team readiness, scrim results, roster updates, or technical advantages scouted). Limited time for reversal. DATA GAP ACKNOWLEDGMENT: Briefing lacks head-to-head history, recent series records, or detailed performance metrics for either team\u2014this creates uncertainty but does not shift probability away from market consensus which prices YES at 76%. NO REVERSAL CATALYSTS: For Karmine Corp to win from 24%, they would need to overcome demonstrated market conviction, late-stage momentum, and a named-elite player advantage at Gentle Mates. No briefing signals support such a reversal. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in YES estimate (68) reflects clear market signal and roster credential. Lower confidence in NO estimate (35) reflects complete absence of supporting data for Karmine Corp\u2014they may be strong, but no evidence exists in briefing.", "key_factor": "Strong market conviction and recent momentum surge (+13.0pp on Apr 10 19:42 UTC) reflecting YES-side dominance in betting activity despite sparse team-specific performance data."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing provides no concrete performance metrics, recent match results, or roster strength analysis for either Gentle Mates or Karmine Corp. The player statistics shown are from FNATIC vs Team Vitality\u2014completely unrelated to this matchup. MARKET PRICING DISCONNECT: YES priced at 76% represents strong conviction, yet this high confidence exists despite the briefing explicitly stating 'limited specific information about Gentle Mates or Karmine Corp's current form.' This is a red flag for underinformed pricing. GENTLE MATES' UNDERRATED ASSET: Only concrete team data provided is that Gentle Mates 'arguably boasts the world's best Yoru player in marteen' and runs a double-Duelist composition with bipo (Neon) and marteen (Phoenix/Waylay). This is a genuine competitive strength\u2014specialized agent mastery can decisively win maps in BO3 formats. UNDERDOG POSITIONING: At 24%, NO (Karmine Corp) is genuinely underdog-priced. With zero performance data on Karmine Corp in the briefing, the market is betting against an unknown opponent. Unknown \u2260 weak, but it creates asymmetric pricing risk. VOLATILE MARKET BEHAVIOR: Sharp 22pp drop on Apr 06, then +13.5pp recovery Apr 07, followed by -14pp swing Apr 10 shows high uncertainty. This volatility pattern (especially the recent -14pp plunge on NO) suggests reactive trading rather than fundamental analysis\u2014likely driven by external chatter or incomplete information. BO3 FORMAT AMPLIFIES VARIANCE: Best-of-Three matches are inherently volatile. A team with a specialized map pool (like Gentle Mates' Yoru/Duelist focus) can lose map 1, adapt, and take maps 2-3. 76% YES pricing suggests low probability of Karmine Corp stealing even one map\u2014this underestimates BO3 upset potential. TIME-TO-REVERSAL PRESSURE: Event timing is TODAY (resolves in ~5 hours). Market shares will cascade toward $0.01 or $0.99 once match begins and early rounds show form. Current 76/24 split may not survive 10 minutes of live gameplay if Karmine Corp takes opening map. MARKET ASSUMPTION: The 76% YES price implicitly assumes Gentle Mates is the stronger team, but briefing provides zero comparative analysis. This could reflect accurate insider information (coach/player networks, scrim results), or it could reflect herd bias on a team name traders recognize. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes set to 25 (low) because the YES case relies entirely on absence of negative data about Gentle Mates\u2014not positive evidence. confidence_no set to 28 (low) because Karmine Corp is even more opaque; neither side has adequate evidence. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: 28% for NO reflects that 76% YES is likely reflecting *some* underlying truth (Gentle Mates probably is favored), but the lack of supporting evidence in the briefing means the true edge is likely narrower. 76% \u2192 72% confidence reduction is conservative and appropriate given data void.", "key_factor": "Severe data vacuum prevents confident assessment of either team's recent form, roster strength, or competitive positioning\u2014market pricing reflects conviction without evidence."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.38, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains no performance metrics, recent match results, or roster strength assessments for either Gentle Mates or Karmine Corp. MARKET SIGNAL DOMINATES: YES side has risen sharply from 60% (7-day EMA) to 76% (current), with +24.5pp over 7 days and +14.0pp in last 24 hours. This 16pp divergence from EMA suggests recent information flow favoring Gentle Mates. SHARP MOVE SIGNIFICANCE: Apr 10 19:42 UTC +13.0pp jump (largest recent move) occurred ~5 hours before resolution, indicating late-breaking information likely related to team roster, recent scrims, or other match-critical factors not reflected in briefing. SINGLE POSITIVE DATA POINT: Briefing notes Gentle Mates has 'arguably the world's best Yoru player in marteen' with strong double-Duelist composition (bipo on Neon, marteen on Phoenix/Waylay). This is the only substantive competitive signal provided. NO COUNTER-INTEL ON KARMINE CORP: Briefing provides zero positive or negative signals about Karmine Corp. Complete absence of performance data prevents evaluating their roster strength, recent form, or strategic matchups. MARKET STRUCTURE: 76% YES / 24% NO with $93k volume suggests market participants have access to information not in briefing (likely recent scrim results, analyst reports, or team-specific intel from esports communities). VOLATILITY PATTERN: 24-hour volatility of 3.0pp/hr on YES (stable) vs 5.3pp/hr on NO (highly volatile) suggests uncertainty about Karmine Corp's chances, with smart money gradually consolidating around Gentle Mates. TIME-TO-RESOLUTION: ~5 hours remaining. Any major reversal would require unexpected information (roster changes, technical issues, forfeiture threat) with minimal time to propagate. Current market price reflects near-terminal information state. BASE-RATE LIMITATION: Cannot apply historical win-rate statistics for VCT Group Stage matches without knowing: team seedings, historical head-to-head records, recent form trajectories, or coach/analyst consensus pre-match. CONFIDENCE ADJUSTMENT: YES confidence set to 38 (not higher) because market signal dominance (13pp late move) without underlying data justification creates risk of overcorrection. NO confidence set to 28 (lower than YES) reflecting genuine data vacuum on Karmine Corp's competitive viability\u2014unable to assess whether they are dark horse contender or legitimate underdog. RECOMMENDATION: Probability_score of 72 reflects market consensus + single positive Gentle Mates signal + absence of counter-evidence, but both confidence scores remain constrained by severe briefing data deficiency. This is a market-price-driven rather than fundamentals-driven estimate.", "key_factor": "Unable to establish reliable historical baseline for Gentle Mates vs Karmine Corp matchup; insufficient data on both teams' 2026 EMEA Stage 1 performance to determine win probability from first principles."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "Market has rallied sharply +24.5pp over 7 days, with +13.0pp jump on Apr 10 19:42 UTC (just hours before match), suggesting crowd conviction building late. Current YES price 76% reflects strong bullish sentiment, but briefing provides almost NO performance data on either team\u2014only that Gentle Mates has 'world's best Yoru player' (marteen) and double-Duelist strategy. Briefing explicitly states 'limited specific information about Gentle Mates or Karmine Corp's current form'\u2014this is a DATA VOID, not a reason for confidence. Sharp NO-side volatility (5.3pp/hr vs 3.0pp for YES; -22.0pp drop Apr 6) suggests uncertainty and possible capitulation selling into YES rally, not fundamental confidence collapse. Market may be overweighting Gentle Mates' Yoru player reputation without recent match results, team synergy data, or Karmine Corp's actual roster strength. Briefing lacks: head-to-head history, recent Gentle Mates/Karmine Corp match records, win-loss stats, or stage-to-date performance in Group Alpha. 76% price implies Karmine Corp has only 24% chance, yet briefing provides ZERO negative signals about Karmine\u2014absence of evidence is not evidence of absence. With ~5 hours to match resolution, late rally may reflect last-minute betting into FOMO rather than new fundamental information (briefing data is stale: 2026-04-10 19:44 UTC). Adjusted probability to 72% to reflect Gentle Mates' Yoru advantage, but severely reduced confidence_no to 35% due to critical data gaps on Karmine's actual competitive standing.", "key_factor": "Greed"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.68, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "MARKET SIGNAL ANALYSIS: YES side surged +14pp in 24h with a sharp +13pp move at Apr 10 19:42 UTC (5 hours pre-match); NO side experienced mirror -14pp drop at 19:44 UTC. This synchronized reversal suggests coordinated information arrival (roster confirmation, scrim results, or analyst consensus shift) rather than random volatility. TIMING CONTEXT: Match scheduled Apr 10 14:00 ET (~5 hours from data freshness). Sharp moves this close to match start typically reflect harder information (confirmed lineups, last-minute roster changes, or high-confidence pre-match analysis) vs. early-week speculation. DATA ASYMMETRY: Briefing contains detailed stats for FNATIC vs Team Vitality but zero performance metrics for Gentle Mates or Karmine Corp. This gap suggests either: (a) both teams are relatively unknown/lower-tier in EMEA, or (b) search data is stale. Note reference to Gentle Mates' 'world-class Yoru player marteen' and double-duelist innovation hints at competitive pedigree despite limited data. ROSTER SIGNAL: Mention of Gentle Mates' Yoru specialist marteen and strategic double-duelist composition suggests recent roster stability and tactical sophistication\u2014positive signal absent for Karmine Corp in briefing. BETTING VOLUME & SPREAD: $93k USD volume with 76/24 split reflects moderate confidence, not extreme conviction. 4-point spread (YES + NO = 100%) suggests balanced orderbook without manipulation. REVERSE ENGINEERING MARKET MOVE: A +13pp surge 5 hours pre-match (when information density is highest) is more credible than early-week swings. Gentle Mates' move from ~60% EMA (7-day) to 76% current suggests positive late data, not just betting flow. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: YES confidence set at 68 (moderately high due to recent momentum & late-game signal), NO confidence set at 35 (very low\u2014insufficient counter-data on Karmine Corp means we cannot justify >40% belief in their win; data parity would demand ~50 on both sides, but asymmetric data quality prevents it). LIVE EVENT RISK: With ~5 hours to match start, reversal to 50-50 requires forfeit/walkover (low probability in organized VCT). Shares will trade to ~$0.99/$0.01 once result is known but before official resolution\u2014market price is quasi-final. ALTERNATIVE HYPOTHESIS: If market is mispricing, it is on the Gentle Mates (YES) side\u2014overweighting late information. However, the synchronized 13pp move and timing suggest this is deliberate re-rating, not noise.", "key_factor": "Market price surge (+13pp in last 6 hours) suggests late information favoring Gentle Mates, likely from pre-match scrims or roster confirmation, but insufficient public data on either team's current stage performance prevents high-confidence assessment."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "MARKET SIGNAL DIVERGENCE: YES rose sharply +13pp on Apr 10 19:42 UTC (same day match, ~5 hours before resolution), but the briefing provides ZERO recent performance data, head-to-head history, or current standings for either team\u2014this suggests the market moved on information external to the briefing (team announcements, scrim results, lineup confirmations). CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: briefing mentions Gentle Mates' 'double-Duelist approach' and marteen as 'world's best Yoru player,' suggesting confidence in their agent pool diversity; however, no win-loss record, map statistics, or recent form trajectory is provided\u2014this is a red flag for overvaluation based on roster hype rather than performance. KARMINE CORP OPACITY: Karmine Corp receives minimal mention; no roster names, recent results, or tactical tendencies are disclosed\u2014this creates asymmetric risk: if Karmine Corp has form, preparation, or roster advantages (e.g., recent signings, strong map pool), the 24% NO price may severely underweight their chances. TACTICAL META UNKNOWN: the briefing explicitly states 'limited specific information about Gentle Mates or Karmine Corp's current form'\u2014a recent patch, agent nerf (e.g., Yoru changes), or map pool rotation could render marteen's Yoru expertise less valuable than the market assumes. GROUP STAGE CONTEXT MISSING: each group has 6 teams, single round-robin, top 4 advance; the briefing does not reveal standings, playoff implications, or whether either team is already qualified or fighting for survival\u2014this affects motivation, risk-taking, and preparation intensity. VOLATILITY PATTERN: NO side shows 5.3pp/hr volatility (vs YES at 3.0pp/hr); the sharp -14pp swing on Apr 10 19:44 UTC suggests late uncertainty or negative news about Gentle Mates or positive news about Karmine Corp that the briefing does not capture. MODERATE PROBABILITY ASSIGNMENT: YES at 76% market price reflects strong but not dominant confidence; confidence scores capped at 45/38 because the briefing data is structurally insufficient to justify higher certainty on either side\u2014this is a live match with 5 hours to resolution and NO RECENT MATCH RESULTS for either team. BLACK SWAN VECTOR: Karmine Corp's underdog status (24% price) combined with zero performance disclosure creates a classic low-probability flip scenario\u2014if they are a team on form with a favorable map pool or tactical counter to double-Duelist comps, their true win probability could be 35\u201345%, not 24%.", "key_factor": "Karmine Corp's recent roster stability and tactical preparation (unknown from briefing) decisively outmatches Gentle Mates' double-duelist experimental setup, or a key Gentle Mates player (marteen or bipo) suffers unexpected underperformance due to map pool mismatch or meta shift."}], "final_score": 0.6802873563218391, "no_score": 0.34607929515418506, "edge": -0.07471264367816088, "no_edge": 0.10107929515418507, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "YES-side confidence too low: 50% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1856207", "question": "Valorant: Gentle Mates vs Karmine Corp (BO3) - VCT EMEA Group Alpha", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between Gentle Mates and Karmine Corp in the VCT EMEA Group Alpha, initially scheduled for April 10 at 2:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Gentle Mates\" if Gentle Mates win the match against Karmine Corp.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Karmine Corp\" if Karmine Corp win the match against Gentle Mates.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-11T00:30:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-10T18:30:00Z", "yes_price": 0.755, "volume_usd": 93127.11153500006, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["37700793285201716671638873618148495356677277895795156963859864646833056709542", "87779714902843230246171432547899207995419399799244164744942468600671087644416"]}, "key_facts": ["VCT 2026: EMEA Stage 1 results, upcoming matches, and VODs.", "Group Stage: April 1<sup>st</sup> - May 1<sup>st</sup>, 2026.", "Each Group has 6 teams; All matches are Bo3.", "Top Valorant esports teams rankings list and tiers in Europe.", "Top Valorant esports teams rankings list and tiers in GC.", "Top Valorant esports teams rankings list and tiers in China.", "|  |  | R | ACS | K | D | A | +/\u2013 | KAST | ADR | HS% | FK | FD | +/\u2013 |\n ---  ---  ---  ---  ---  ---  --- |\n| kaajak  FNC | neon | 1.20 0.64 1.72 | 262 155 362 | 22 6 16 | /  17 9 8 / | 6 3 3 | +5 -3 +8 | 74% 64% 83% | 175 116 229 | 27% 20% 31% | 4 0 4 | 4 2 2 | 0 -2 +2 |\n| crashies  FNC | sova | 1.18 1.33 1.04 | 242 262 225 | 19 10 9 | /  17 9 8 / | 6 4 2 | +2 +1 +1 | 74% 73% 75% | 174 192 158 | 39% 35% 45% | 2 1 1 | 0 0 0 | +2 +1 +1 |\n| Boaster  FNC | harbor | 1.15 1.25 1.07 | 200 235 170 | 17 9 8 | /  15 8 7 / | 9 7 2 | +2 +1 +1 | 87% 100% 7