026 Winter Regular Season. HMBLE has demonstrated strong performance metrics in the tournament, ranking among the top teams with 2280 GPM (tied for 4th) and showing competitive results including victories over P11 Esports in 24:11 and engagement with top teams like EKO Esports and Colossal Gaming. StoneHenge Esports' performance data is not present in the available search results, limiting direct comparison of their current form and capabilities.", "side_yes_case": ["HMBLE ranks in top-tier GPM (2280, tied 4th best in split) indicating strong economic performance", "HMBLE players demonstrate high individual skill with Tyrone and Vigil posting 18-kill performances in competitive matches", "HMBLE has shown ability to compete in extended high-kill games (88 kills vs EKO Esports, 56:43 duration)", "HMBLE has secured victories against similar-tier opponents in the regular season"], "side_no_case": ["No performance statistics available for StoneHenge Esports limits ability to assess their strengths", "HMBLE's inconsistency shown by wide game duration variance (24:11 vs P11 to 56:43 vs EKO) suggests execution issues", "BO1 format eliminates ability to adapt between games, favoring teams with consistent preparation", "Limited recent head-to-head or direct matchup history between these teams in available data"], "key_context": ["LIT 2026 Winter Split regular season - BO1 format eliminates comebacks and increases variance", "Average game duration across split is 31:58; HMBLE games vary significantly from 24:11 to 56:43", "No direct StoneHenge Esports performance data available in search results", "HMBLE has faced top-tier competition (EKO Esports, Colossal Gaming) during the split", "Tournament average is 36 kills per game across 28 games played"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-10T12:13:44.501791Z"}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-10T23:45:00Z", "winning_side": "YES", "final_yes_price": 1.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-11T14:27:48.552525+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "926a6b2f-8a67-45b7-a2f6-18a7977ba123", "timestamp": "2026-04-10T12:16:33.528290+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1934747", "question": "Counter-Strike: ZOTIX vs bankaPEPSI (BO3) - CCT Europe Contenders #4 Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Lower bracket quarterfinal 2 match between ZOTIX and bankaPEPSI in the CCT Europe Contenders #4 Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 10 at 2:15PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"ZOTIX\" if ZOTIX win the match against bankaPEPSI.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"bankaPEPSI\" if bankaPEPSI win the match against ZOTIX.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonabl