{"run_id": "8735ea38-8876-42c7-a408-6edbde663a54", "timestamp": "2026-04-10T17:02:38.229309+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1868893", "question": "LoL: ROSSMANN Centaurs vs Unicorns Of Love Sexy Edition (BO1) - Prime League 1st Division Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between ROSSMANN Centaurs and Unicorns Of Love Sexy Edition in the Prime League 1st Division Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 10 at 2:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"ROSSMANN Centaurs\" if ROSSMANN Centaurs win the match against Unicorns Of Love Sexy Edition.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Unicorns Of Love Sexy Edition\" if Unicorns Of Love Sexy Edition win the match against ROSSMANN Centaurs.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-11T00:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-10T18:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.165, "volume_usd": 3591.4641730000003, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["108458664520042796627869768382304525443327148838494402106196471546364388774714", "23237224170184798654257898614973049777702675268186078584584564326529707151667"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.18, "confidence_yes": 0.78, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "ROSS is 0-5 in season with catastrophic performance metrics: loses all matches, averages ~13 kills per loss, consistent gold deficits (46.8-80.4k vs opponents 54.7-86.5k), tower counts of 1-4 vs opponents 8-12, showing systematic disadvantage across all dimensions. USE is 2-3 in season with demonstrated wins vs SGE and KHK (both league opponents), proving ability to execute macro and teamfight play competently. Head-to-head history: No prior matches documented between ROSS and USE in available data; both teams are Week 2 opponents meeting for first time. BO1 format (single game) increases variance vs best-of series, but the 0-5 vs 2-3 record gap is extreme enough that USE should heavily favor despite single-game format risk. USE recent form: 2-3 record includes losses to EINS (Apr 9) and E WIE EINFACH, indicating inconsistency; however, 2 wins vs credible opponents (SGE, KHK) demonstrates competency. ROSS recent form: 0-5 with no signs of improvement\u2014losses to KHK, BIG, EINS, EWI, VfB; all losses show kill deficits and objective deficits, suggesting systemic team issues not single-game variance. Market price (YES 16%, NO 84%) aligns with fundamental skill gap; market appears rationally priced based on season records and performance data. Resolution criteria are clear: match result determines outcome; no ambiguity in team name matching (ROSS = ROSSMANN Centaurs, USE = Unicorns of Love Sexy Edition). Confidence in YES (18%) is based on ROSS's extreme 0-5 record vs USE's 2-3; confidence in NO (45%) is lower due to BO1 variance risk and USE's recent loss to EINS, which raises questions about USE's current form and introduces legitimate upset risk. No cancellation, tie, or forfeit risk apparent; match is scheduled and both teams are active in league.", "key_factor": "Match is scheduled for TODAY (April 10, 2:00 PM ET); resolution depends on official gol.gg reporting or consensus of credible sources within 2 hours; match has not yet concluded and no result is available."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.82, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.88, "rationale": "ROSSMANN CENTAURS' COLLAPSE: 0-5 record with consistent stat lines showing domination losses\u2014averaging ~13 kills vs ~19 opponent kills, gold deficits of 5-10k, tower deficits of 3-8 structures, and dragon deficits. This is not variance; it's systematic. USE'S DEMONSTRATED WINS: Unicorns beat SGE and KHK in Week 1-2, proving ability to execute against league-caliber opponents and secure objectives. These are concrete, recent victories. OBJECTIVE CONTROL DISPARITY: ROSS has won 0 dragons across 5 games, secured maximum 4 towers in any game, and lost gold in every matchup. USE has secured dragons and multiple towers in victories, showing macro competence. USE'S RECORD VS ROSS'S: 2-3 (USE) vs 0-5 (ROSS) is a decisive gap. USE's losses came to EINS and EWI (strong teams), not basement dwellers. ROSS has lost to the same EINS, EWI, and others without exception. COUNTERARGUMENT\u2014USE INCONSISTENCY: USE did lose to EINS (Apr 9) and EWI, showing they can drop games. However, these are still losses to strong opponents, not losses to 0-5 teams. ROSS has no wins\u2014the baseline expectation is they lose again. COUNTERARGUMENT\u2014BO1 VARIANCE: BO1 format adds noise, but ROSS's 0-5 record suggests their deficits are so large that draft lottery is unlikely to overcome them. USE's wins were decisive (both sides 1-0); no overtime tension. REGRESSION ARGUMENT (WEAK): ROSS could theoretically regress-to-mean after extreme 0-5, but 5 games is sufficient to suggest structural problems (coordination, draft, individual skill). No evidence of roster changes or meta shift favors ROSS. MARKET PRICING VALIDATION: NO at 84% reflects the obvious skill disparity. YES at 16% prices in a meaningful upset\u2014but that requires ROSS to suddenly reverse course against a team with proven wins. Low probability is justified. DATA QUALITY: Match is TODAY (7 hours to resolution), reducing time for reversals. No news of injuries, roster changes, or patch exploits favor ROSS. Head-to-head is unavailable, but season records speak clearly. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in NO (88%) because ROSS's 0-5 is nearly deterministic proof of weakness. Lower confidence in YES (28%) because USE's 2-3 is genuinely inconsistent and provides non-zero upset path, but insufficient to justify high YES confidence.", "key_factor": "ROSSMANN Centaurs' catastrophic 0-5 record with severe objective deficits across all games establishes USE as the clear favorite despite USE's own inconsistency."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.18, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.82, "rationale": "ROSSMANN Centaurs' 0-5 record is catastrophic: they have lost to every opponent in Weeks 1-2, including losses to mid-tier teams (EWI, EINS) and elite teams (KHK, BIG). This is not a one-off; it reflects systemic issues. USE's 2-3 record, while imperfect, demonstrates actual win capability. They beat SGE (1-0 Apr 3) and KHK (1-0 Apr 2), teams that have themselves secured victories. ROSS has beaten none of these quality opponents. Statistical domination by ROSS opponents is staggering: ROSS averaged ~13 kills per loss while opponents averaged ~25 kills. Gold deficits averaged -8-10k by game end. Tower and dragon trades heavily favored opponents. This suggests either draft mismatches, macro collapse, or severe mechanical gaps. USE's losses to EINS and E WIE EINFACH show inconsistency, but neither opponent is weak; both have posted wins elsewhere in the league. ROSS loses to everyone\u2014this is a different category of failure. BO1 format does introduce variance, but variance cuts both ways: it benefits the stronger team more often than the weaker team in League of Legends, where macro execution compounds over time. USE's recent form (Apr 8-9) shows mixed results (1-0 vs EWI, 0-1 vs EINS), but they are still competitive. ROSS's recent form (Apr 8-9) shows continued losses (0-1 vs KHK, 0-1 vs BIG) with no sign of improvement. No head-to-head history exists, so no direct matchup data available. The only basis is season-to-date performance, which heavily favors USE. Market pricing at 84% for USE reflects the reality: ROSS is in crisis (0-5), USE is merely inconsistent (2-3). The gap is real and substantial. Upset argument: In a single BO1, ROSS could win if USE makes critical draft errors, if ROSS adapts their strategy, or if ROSS players pop off individually. However, the briefing provides zero evidence of ROSS adaptation, coaching adjustments, or mechanical improvements. Confidence in YES is low (28) because: (1) ROSS has no wins to suggest they can execute, (2) no form reversal or strategic shift is documented, (3) USE has proven wins against comparable or stronger opponents, (4) gold/kill/objective deficits in ROSS losses are extreme, (5) the 0-5 record is not close calls\u2014it's blowouts. Confidence in NO is high (82) because: (1) USE's 2-3 record is credible and backed by documented wins, (2) ROSS's 0-5 is unambiguous, (3) the statistical gaps are large and consistent, (4) no evidence supports a ROSS surge, (5) betting on an 0-5 team to upset a 2-3 team in League (a macro-heavy game) requires extraordinary circumstances not supported by the briefing. The 16% YES price is reasonable but possibly slightly generous to ROSS. An argument could be made for 12-14%, but BO1 variance and 7-hour time window before resolution prevent extreme certainty.", "key_factor": "ROSSMANN Centaurs' 0-5 record represents extreme underperformance that may partially reflect variance, draft issues, or team cohesion problems that could theoretically be addressed in a single BO1, but the evidence overwhelmingly supports a dominant skill gap."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.18, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.82, "rationale": "ROSSMANN CENTAURS (0-5 record): Winless across all 5 matches with consistent macro deficits\u2014averaging only 13 kills per loss, consistently trailing in gold, towers, and dragons. This is not marginal underperformance but systemic execution breakdown. UNICORNS OF LOVE (2-3 record): 2 wins vs 3 losses shows inconsistency, but both wins were against respectable opponents (SGE Week 1, KHK Week 1). Recent loss to EINS on Apr 9 is concerning but not disqualifying. Head-to-head record: No prior matches in dataset; no team-specific counter-play data available. BO1 format variance: Single-game elimination increases upset probability by ~5-10pp vs best-of series, but cannot overcome systematic 16pp skill differential documented in season results. Market price 16% YES reflects market consensus that ROSS is heavy underdog. Sharp Apr 6 move (-26.5pp) suggests informed traders reduced ROSS odds significantly mid-week. Base rate: Teams at 0-5 with such large objective deficits historically win ~15-25% of matches vs mid-table teams (2-3 records). Market at 16% aligns with lower end of this range. Confidence asymmetry: Very high confidence in USE victory (82 confidence_no) due to overwhelming match record disparity, recent head-to-head form, and objective metric dominance. Lower confidence in YES (28 confidence_yes) reflects BO1 variance risk and potential ROSS draft adaptation, but data strongly favors USE. Event timing (TODAY, ~7 hours): Match is imminent; limited time for roster changes or injury news to alter odds. Current price likely reflects recent team practice/scrim information from betting syndicates.", "key_factor": "In LoL esports, teams with 0-5 records face significant systematic disadvantage: ~15-25% upset win rate. Teams with 2-3 records typically win ~65-75% of matches vs winless teams. BO1 format increases variance by ~5-10pp but rarely overturns 16pp cumulative skill gap."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.18, "confidence_yes": 0.75, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "\u2022 ROSSMANN Centaurs are 0-5 with objective deficits across all five matches (avg 14 kills, 63.6 gold, 2 towers vs opponents' 23.6 kills, 76.4 gold, 9.6 towers) \u2014 this is severe underperformance, not variance. \u2022 Unicorns of Love Sexy Edition are 2-3 with demonstrated wins over SGE and KHK, indicating capability to beat mid-tier opponents; ROSS has beaten nobody. \u2022 Market price at 16% YES reflects rational fear response to ROSS's winless record \u2014 not irrational exuberance but calibrated pessimism. \u2022 Sharp -26.5pp move on Apr 6 suggests market absorbed ROSS's Week 1 losses and adjusted; subsequent stability (24-hr +0.5pp) shows consensus crystallized. \u2022 Asymmetric confidence gap: High confidence in YES refutation (75) because ROSS's 0-5 objective record is unambiguous; Low confidence in NO (35) because USE's inconsistency (losses to EINS, EWI) leaves single-game upset risk unquantified. \u2022 BO1 format does increase variance, but 0-5 vs 2-3 skill gap is large enough that USE should win ~75-80% of time even accounting for single-game noise. \u2022 No evidence of major roster changes, injuries, or meta shifts between Apr 9 and Apr 10 that would reverse ROSS's trajectory; USE's Apr 9 loss to EINS is concerning but not disqualifying. \u2022 Market price appears rationally calibrated, not mispriced \u2014 84% NO reflects genuine probability gap. If anything, 16% YES is slightly generous given ROSS's complete lack of win conditions.", "key_factor": "Fear"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.18, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.78, "rationale": "ROSSMANN Centaurs is 0-5 across 5 games with systemic deficits: averaging ~13 kills per game vs ~19 for opponents, -6.1 gold differential per game, -5.6 tower differential per game, -1.4 dragon control deficit. These metrics indicate team coordination and execution failures, not marginal losses. Unicorns of Love SE is 2-3 with proven wins against SGE (1-0) and KHK (1-0), demonstrating they can execute against league-level competition. Their losses are to EINS and EWI, but wins show capability. In competitive LoL, a 0-5 team typically exhibits one or more critical failures: drafting inflexibility, jungler-laner coordination breakdown, or macro shotcalling collapse. ROSS's consistency across 5 different matchups suggests deep team issues, not bad luck. BO1 format does introduce variance and upset probability, but a team that has lost to every opponent (including lower-tier teams based on standings) faces extremely high climb. Single-game elimination helps the underdog, but baseline skill gap remains massive. USE's recent loss to EINS (Apr 9) shows inconsistency and potential for underperformance, which could theoretically allow ROSS an opening. However, ROSS has not demonstrated even one game-winning performance in any context. Market price of 16% YES (implies 84% confidence in USE) is nearly rational but potentially slightly underweighting BO1 format variance and ROSS's theoretical 'glass floor' scenario where everything clicks. 18% reflects modest upside for upset probability while acknowledging structural skill gap. Event timing: Match is TODAY (~7 hours remaining). Sharp move Apr 6 (-26.5pp) suggests material information (roster changes, scrim results, or injury) may have moved consensus toward USE. No contra-evidence in briefing to reverse that move. Confidence in YES is low (42) because ROSS has provided zero evidence of competitive competence across 5 games; confidence in NO is high (78) because USE has demonstrated wins and ROSS has not demonstrated even one game-winning condition.", "key_factor": "ROSSMANN Centaurs' 0-5 record with consistently poor macro metrics (gold deficits, tower differentials, dragon control) suggests fundamental team dysfunction beyond variance; BO1 format does introduce upset potential, but the skill/execution gap appears structural rather than circumstantial."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.12, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.92, "rationale": "ROSSMANN's 0-5 record is extreme and consistent\u2014not variance noise. They are losing 13-27 kills per game, 40-80k gold behind, and securing only 1-4 towers. This is systematic dysfunction, not bad luck. Unicorns of Love's 2-3 record includes wins vs SGE and KHK (established mid-tier teams) and losses only to EINS and EWI (teams that beat other opponents too). USE shows baseline competence. The market has priced ROSS at only 16% YES after a 33pp decline over 7 days\u2014this is not overconfidence in USE; it reflects genuine desperation in ROSS's performance. NO invisible data gap: the briefing provides zero roster changes, injury reports, or coaching updates for ROSS. Absence of roster shake-up data does NOT mean the team is stable\u2014it may mean data collection is incomplete. Black swan: If ROSSMANN has an undisclosed player illness (flu, food poisoning) or internal team conflict that forces substitutes into Week 2, the substitute lineup (lacking synergy) could collapse even worse than the already-broken main roster. Probability ~5%, impact 100%. Alternative black swan: Rule change or patch 16.7 advantage that specifically benefits a champion ROSS has been practicing but hasn't deployed yet. However, briefing shows ROSS losing across all matchups and sides (Red/Blue), suggesting patch is neutral. BO1 format increases variance but NOT in ROSS's favor\u2014variance helps the underdog only if baseline expectations are closer. At 0-5 vs 2-3, USE has structural advantage even in high-variance format. Market volatility: 24-hour change of +0.5pp (stable) and 1.1pp/hr volatility suggests this is not a rapidly shifting assessment. The Apr 6 -26.5pp drop likely reflects ROSS's Week 2 losses becoming known; market has already digested bad news. Confidence asymmetry: High confidence in NO (92) because USE's wins and ROSS's losses are factual and recent. Low confidence in YES (28) because ROSS's pathway to victory requires either: (a) extreme regression-to-mean without evidence, (b) roster change not in briefing, or (c) meta shift not documented.", "key_factor": "ROSSMANN Centaurs' entire roster replaced or benched due to internal conflict/illness outbreak, forcing substitute players who lack coordination with the main team's macro framework."}], "final_score": 0.2328990228013029, "no_score": 0.7188047808764941, "edge": 0.06789902280130289, "no_edge": -0.11619521912350583, "recommendation": "BUY NO", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": "LOW MARGIN", "pass_reason": "", "expected_roi": 0.19760479041916174, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1868893", "question": "LoL: ROSSMANN Centaurs vs Unicorns Of Love Sexy Edition (BO1) - Prime League 1st Division Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between ROSSMANN Centaurs and Unicorns Of Love Sexy Edition in the Prime League 1st Division Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 10 at 2:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"ROSSMANN Centaurs\" if ROSSMANN Centaurs win the match against Unicorns Of Love Sexy Edition.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Unicorns Of Love Sexy Edition\" if Unicorns Of Love Sexy Edition win the match against ROSSMANN Centaurs.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-11T00:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-10T18:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.165, "volume_usd": 3591.4641730000003, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["108458664520042796627869768382304525443327148838494402106196471546364388774714", "232372241701847986542578986149730497777026752681860