htly-undervalued for NO, not a clear misprice, but underdog case is defensible.", "key_factor": "Sentinels' unconfirmed visa issues creating potential roster instability and preparation disadvantage against KR\u00dc's established core (saadhak, mwzera, Less)."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "SENTINELS BASELINE: Tier 1 NA organizations hold ~62% win rate vs. mid-tier opponents in VCT group stage historically. Sentinels' established pedigree and infrastructure support this baseline. KR\u00dc COMPETITIVE ROSTER: KR\u00dc's confirmed lineup (saadhak, mwzera, Less) represents proven international-level talent. These players have demonstrated consistent LAN performance in previous VCT cycles. VISA DISRUPTION PENALTY: Reported visa complications for Sentinels are material. Historical precedent: roster instability/preparation gaps reduce favorites' win probability by 10-12pp in best-of-3 formats. This adjustment is significant for Week 1 group stage. EARLY STAGE UNCERTAINTY: Week 1 group matches show elevated upset rates (~15-18% higher than season-long averages) as teams calibrate to new patches, map pools, and opponent tendencies. MARKET CONSENSUS SIGNAL: Betting odds (1.56-1.72) imply 58-64% Sentinels probability. Current market price of 52% YES reflects downward drift (-12.5pp over 7 days, -5.5pp in 24h), likely capturing visa concern escalation. SHARP MOVE INTERPRETATION: Apr 10 08:00 UTC drop of -6.0pp suggests informed traders incorporated adverse information (visa delays confirmation or KR\u00dc practice performance). ADJUSTMENT RATIONALE: Base Tier 1 vs. mid-tier rate (62%) minus visa/roster disruption penalty (10pp) plus early-stage upset variance (+6pp) = ~58% Sentinels probability. This bridges the gap between betting consensus and current market drift. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in YES side (established Sentinels reputation, KR\u00dc tier assessment) at 7