urs to resolution. Confidence asymmetry: HIGH confidence_yes (62) because betting markets still back Sentinels and org prestige is real; MODERATE confidence_no (58) because visa impact magnitude is unquantified and could be minor or catastrophic.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "Sentinels are Tier 1 North American org with institutional competitive infrastructure; KR\u00dc Esports (Brazilian team) has proven players (saadhak, mwzera, Less all international-caliber) but lower organizational resources. Betting market consensus across multiple books converges on 58-64% Sentinels (1.56-1.72 odds), suggesting professional oddsmakers have already factored visa concerns into pricing. Market price has fallen 12.5pp in 7 days (55% \u2192 52.5% current), indicating late-market movement toward KR\u00dc; this corrective drift is consistent with emerging roster uncertainty becoming known to sophisticated bettors. Week 1 group stage matches do produce upsets due to lack of synergy/preparation, but Sentinels' higher seed/ranking and BO3 format (requires consistency across multiple maps) mitigates upset probability vs. single-map games. Visa issues are high-impact but ambiguous: briefing mentions 'potential visa issues affecting Sentinels' roster composition' without clarity on number of players affected or substitute availability; if 1-2 players are impacted, org quality gap may persist. KR\u00dc's international roster (esp. saadhak) brings LAN experience and firepower, but playing on North American server/venue in Week 1 group stage typically favors local orgs with established bootcamp infrastructure. BO3 format and Group Omega stage (implies group-based advancement) suggests match is early elimination round; teams will be pre-prepared for opponent tendencies, reducing chaos factor. Match resolves in ~8 hours; no new roster/visa announcements expected to materially shift odds at this point unless official org statement drops.", "key_factor": "Visa-related roster instability in Week 1 group stage is a material force multiplier for underdog performance, but Sentinels' organizational tier-1 infrastructure and consistent betting consensus (58-64% implied) suggests the disruption is partially priced in by professional oddsmakers."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.48, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "VISA ISSUE RED FLAG: The briefing explicitly mentions 'potential visa issues affecting Sentinels' roster composition' \u2014 this is NOT a rumor, it's cited as NEWS SUMMARY material. In esports BO3s, a stand-in player or fractured roster coherence is catastrophic, especially Week 1 when synergy is already fragile. MARKET REPRICING SIGNAL: YES odds fell 12.5pp over 7 days and -5.5pp in 24 hours, with a sharp -6pp move on Apr 10 08:00 UTC (likely when visa complications became public or confirmed). The market is already pricing in player uncertainty, yet 52% YES still assumes Sentinels execute. One more roster confirmation = steeper drop. KR\u00dc'S PROVEN CORE: saadhak, mwzera, and Less are not randoms \u2014 they're established Brazilian/Latin American Tier 1 competitors with tournament pedigree. In a best-of-3 where Sentinels may be 4v5 or running a sub, KR\u00dc's cohesion advantage is material. WEEK 1 ADJUSTMENT CHAOS: Group stage Week 1 matches are historically volatile because teams are still calibrating to tournament patch, maps pool, and opponent tendencies. A destabilized Sentinels roster amplifies this volatility in KR\u00dc's favor. ABSENCE OF SENTINELS STATS: The briefing states 'maps and detailed statistics unavailable' \u2014 we have no recent head-to-head, map pool overlap, or agent comfort data. This is unusual for a Tier 1 org; it may indicate the match was hastily scheduled around visa delays or preparation was incomplete. BETTING CONSENSUS \u2260 GROUND TRUTH: External betting books (1.56-1.72) imply 58-64% Sentinels win, but those odds were set before or during visa uncertainty. Market prices often lag on personnel disruption until the moment of match start. MORALE & PREPARATION GAP: Sentinels likely spent the last 48-72 hours in visa/logistics hell; KR\u00dc, if traveling was smoother, may have had cleaner prep. First-match jitters hit harder when you're also managing eligibility uncertainty. TIMING: Event is TODAY (match likely already live or about to start per 8-hour window). Reversal requires Sentinels to either forfeit, play severely understaffed, or lose map control early due to coordination breakdown. All are plausible if visa relief was last-minute or a sub is playing.", "key_factor": "Sentinels' visa disruptions manifest as a last-minute roster substitution or player availability crisis that severely compromises their preparation and coordination in a Week 1 BO3 where map veto and agent selection require full-roster synergy."}], "final_score": 0.5282608695652173, "no_score": 0.4848780487804879, "edge": 0.013260869565217326, "no_edge": -0.00012195121951208421, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 53% for YES (need \u226557%); YES-side confidence too low: 66% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1731427", "question": "Valorant: Sentinels vs KR\u00dc Esports (BO3) - VCT Americas Stage 1 Group Omega", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between Sentinels and KR\u00dc Esports in the VCT Americas Stage 1 Group Omega, initially scheduled for April 10 at 5:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Sentinels\" if Sentinels win the match against KR\u00dc Esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"KR\u00dc Esports\" if KR\u00dc Esports win the match against Sentinels.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a wi