{"run_id": "995d6cd6-03f0-4778-b4ef-541dae0a7511", "timestamp": "2026-04-10T19:31:51.916142+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1929587", "question": "Counter-Strike: Inner Circle Academy vs bond1e (BO3) - LORGAR RANKINGS Closed Qualifier Play-In", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Lower bracket semifinal 2 match between Inner Circle Academy and bond1e in the LORGAR RANKINGS Closed Qualifier Play-In, initially scheduled for April 10 at 1:30PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Inner Circle Academy\" if Inner Circle Academy win the match against bond1e.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"bond1e\" if bond1e win the match against Inner Circle Academy.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-11T00:45:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-10T18:45:00Z", "yes_price": 0.265, "volume_usd": 10283.833072000001, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["114101313994114876071927046502881282089912026613026416974132022688242873837875", "71899609226354069966124591180568149652789278530863688645938767794351999706429"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: Inner Circle Academy must win the BO3 match against bond1e in the LORGAR RANKINGS Closed Qualifier Play-In Lower Bracket Semifinal 2. CURRENT MARKET SIGNAL: YES trading at 26%, NO at 74% \u2014 market strongly favors bond1e. This 48-point gap reflects either significant real-world evidence or a convergence event (match imminent or result becoming clear). EVENT TIMING CRITICAL: Market ends in ~5 hours (2026-04-10 23:45 UTC, ~5 hours from data timestamp of 19:31 UTC). This is TODAY/IMMINENT. The sharp volatility in price history (17.5pp drop, 25pp spike, 30pp drop in Apr 10 afternoon) suggests market has digested new information post-match scheduling or warm-up indicators. CASE FOR INNER CIRCLE ACADEMY (YES): Single recent dominant performance (13-3 vs mrg on Overpass) shows map control capability. Eastern European/Ukrainian regional presence may indicate team stability. CASE FOR BOND1E (NO): Recent 2-1 series win with two convincing 13-8 victories demonstrates current form and match-winning experience in this qualifier. Shows ability to execute across multiple maps. Market consensus has shifted -24pp in 24 hours toward bond1e, suggesting either observed warm-up performance, roster information, or scout data. DATA QUALITY ASYMMETRY: Only one recent completed map shown for Inner Circle Academy (vs mrg). bond1e has full series context (2-1 vs HYPERSPIRIT with map scores). Insufficient head-to-head history, no direct comparative stats, no map pool analysis, no player form metrics beyond single-match samples. MARKET PRICE MOVEMENT INTERPRETATION: Volatility spikes on Apr 10 afternoon (match day) likely reflect real-time information: team arrivals, warm-up results, lineup confirmation, or broadcast indicators. The -30pp swing at 19:30 UTC (just 1 hour before data snapshot) followed by sustained 74% NO pricing suggests market observers detected bond1e strength or Inner Circle Academy weakness immediately before match window. PROBABILISTIC ASSESSMENT: Market at 26% YES reflects either (a) bond1e genuinely stronger based on observed evidence, or (b) market mispricing correcting toward consensus. Given imminent timing and price history showing decisive shift, the former is more likely. A 48pp discrepancy this close to match time is not easily reconciled with pure noise. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: confidence_yes = 35 (limited direct evidence supporting Inner Circle Academy; single dominant map win insufficient to overcome competitive parity in Bo3 format). confidence_no = 38 (bond1e's recent series win and market consensus are credible, but limited historical depth means we cannot be highly confident; unknown variables in live performance, map selection strategy, current player condition). RESOLUTION CRITERIA COMPLIANCE: Criteria are clear and unambiguous for normal match completion. Team name matching is straightforward (both names are distinct and unlikely to trigger the 50-50 clause). Main risk is operational (match delay >7 days, forfeit before start, or cancellation) rather than criteria ambiguity\u2014these would trigger 50-50 resolution, but current scheduling suggests match occurs on April 10. FINAL ESTIMATE: Probability of Inner Circle Academy winning is approximately 28%, reflecting the market's confidence in bond1e offset slightly upward due to genuine uncertainty in limited data and Bo3 variance. However, confidence in this estimate is moderate on both sides due to data sparsity.", "key_factor": "Insufficient historical data on both teams' competitive records, map pools, and head-to-head matchups; reliance on single recent matches with limited sample size for calibration."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE (NO) STRENGTHS: bond1e has concrete recent match evidence\u2014a 2-1 series victory over HYPERSPIRIT with two convincing 13-8 wins on Anubis and Overpass, proving they can execute under pressure in this exact tournament format and online environment. bond1e's recent form shows resilience: despite losing one map, they secured the series, indicating ability to adapt and close out Best of 3 matches\u2014the exact format of today's matchup. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS: Inner Circle Academy's case relies heavily on a single data point\u2014a 13-3 stomp of mrg on Overpass. One dominant map performance against a weaker opponent (mrg lost 3-13) does not establish consistent competitive parity across a BO3. NO DIRECT HEAD-TO-HEAD HISTORY: The briefing explicitly states 'limited direct performance data available' and 'limited head-to-head historical data.' Market pricing at 74% for NO reflects the scarcity of comparative data\u2014bond1e's recent series win is the strongest available signal. INNER CIRCLE ACADEMY DATA GAP: Only one recent map result provided for ICA (vs mrg); no evidence of BO3 series performance, map pool consistency, or how they handle loss scenarios. This contrasts with bond1e's demonstrated BO3 experience. REGIONAL CONTEXT INSUFFICIENT: While ICA may be 'established' in Eastern European scene, this qualifier includes international or mixed-region teams. Regional dominance does not guarantee success in a cross-regional closed qualifier. MARKET MOMENTUM SUPPORTS NO: Despite extreme volatility (sharp -17.5pp, +25pp, -30pp swings on Apr 10), the market has settled at 74% for NO with 24-hour falling trend of -24.0pp toward bond1e. This suggests informed participants are backing bond1e's recent match-proven status. bond1e's 2-1 series win is MORE RELEVANT than ICA's single-map victory: BO3 format directly mirrors today's match structure, making bond1e's proven ability to win series in this exact tournament setup the strongest predictive signal available. YES side weakness: 'Close 2-1' framing for bond1e misses the key fact that they WON the series convincingly on the maps that mattered. Winning 13-8 twice is dominant, not inconsistent. TIMING URGENCY (TODAY, ~5 hours to resolution): No meaningful new information can emerge to shift this heavily data-constrained market. Bond1e's recent series win will remain the strongest available signal until match execution reveals new information. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in NO (72) due to bond1e's concrete recent series evidence; lower confidence in YES (35) because ICA's single-map result is insufficient to overcome the lack of BO3 context and recent match experience.", "key_factor": "bond1e's recent series win (2-1) and consecutive 13-8 map victories demonstrate superior consistency and match-readiness against comparable competition in this qualifier."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "UNDERDOG STRENGTH \u2014 Inner Circle Academy's 13-3 scoreline vs mrg on Overpass is significantly more dominant than bond1e's 13-8 victories; a 10-point margin gap suggests higher firepower and map mastery. UNDERDOG STRENGTH \u2014 bond1e's 2-1 series required three maps to secure; they are not closing out opponents cleanly, whereas Inner Circle Academy dispatched a single map with decisive control. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS \u2014 Only one recent match data point available for Inner Circle Academy (vs mrg). Confidence in extrapolating performance across full BO3 against different opponent is limited. FAVORITE STRENGTH \u2014 bond1e has proven they can win BO3 series in THIS qualifier (vs HYPERSPIRIT), demonstrating match-format execution and resilience (recovering from map 3 loss context). FAVORITE STRENGTH \u2014 bond1e's two consecutive 13-8 wins (Anubis, Overpass) show consistency across different map pools; Inner Circle Academy's 13-3 is one-map data only. MARKET SIGNAL \u2014 Price has collapsed from 50% EMA to 26% current over 24 hours (-24pp), indicating sharp information revelation favoring bond1e. Sharp -30pp move at 19:30 UTC suggests late roster/form update. CRITICAL DATA GAP \u2014 No head-to-head history between these teams. No recent form data for Inner Circle Academy beyond single match. No player-level statistics or lineup stability reported for either team. TIMING PRESSURE \u2014 Event resolves in ~5 hours (TODAY). Market's recent massive swings suggest informed bettors/bookmakers detected bond1e advantage very recently; insufficient time for reversal. QUALIFIER CONTEXT \u2014 Both are Play-In teams, indicating relatively balanced competitive tier. However, bond1e's recent series win proves BO3 execution; Inner Circle Academy unproven in series format in available data. REALISTIC UPSET PATH \u2014 Inner Circle Academy wins if Overpass map pool dominance translates across full series AND bond1e's map inconsistency (lost map 3 to HYPERSPIRIT) repeats under pressure. HONEST ASSESSMENT \u2014 While Inner Circle Academy has one strong data point, bond1e's recent BO3 win + market consensus reversal + lack of counter-evidence for Inner Circle Academy's sustainability suggests bond1e is favored on available evidence. Underdog probability reflects legitimate but narrow path to upset.", "key_factor": "Inner Circle Academy's dominant 13-3 recent victory on a key map (Overpass) demonstrates superior map control and tactical discipline compared to bond1e's inconsistent 2-1 series win."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "MARKET CONTEXT: YES price fell 24pp in 24hrs (50% \u2192 26%), with extreme volatility (-17.5pp, +25.0pp, -30.0pp in 3 hours on Apr 10). This suggests late-breaking information or sharp trading pressure toward NO, not fundamental model shift. IMMINENT TIMING: Event resolves in ~5 hours (TODAY). Sharp reversal now requires significant new intel (team roster changes, withdrawal, forfeiture). Current price likely reflects late-arriving trader conviction or information asymmetry favoring bond1e backers. INNER CIRCLE ACADEMY (YES): Single dominant map (13-3 over mrg on Overpass) shows strong form, but one map \u2260 BO3 predictive power. No head-to-head history vs bond1e. Ukrainian regional context suggests mid-tier competitive level. bond1e (NO): Recent BO3 series win (2-1 vs HYPERSPIRIT, 13-8/13-8 on two maps) demonstrates map consistency and match-day execution. Two 13-8 victories indicate controlled play, not luck. However, lost third map (Overpass), suggesting map vulnerability or fatigue. HISTORICAL BASE RATE: Regional qualifier BO3s between teams with similar limited data show ~50/50 splits when recent form is mixed. bond1e's series win (2-1) is more predictive than Inner Circle's single-map blowout, all else equal. MARKET MISPRICING SIGNAL: 26% YES reflects strong NO conviction. Without clear public-facing roster changes or injury news in briefing, 24pp overnight drop suggests either (a) private discord/team info leaking to insiders, (b) sharp traders betting on bond1e late, or (c) statistical overreaction to volatility. Base rate for single-map dominance \u2192 BO3 win is ~45-50%, not 26%. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes (35) < confidence_no (38). YES side has only one map of evidence; NO side has recent series win. Neither team has reliable historical track record. Insufficient data on either side to assign high confidence. RECOMMENDATION: Current 26% YES undervalues Inner Circle Academy's dominant recent map, but market may have legitimate late intel. Base rate suggests 40-50% range is more justified than 26%, but imminent timing and sharp sell-off warrant respect. Set probability at 28 (slightly below base rate, reflecting market signal) with LOW-TO-MODERATE confidence on both sides.", "key_factor": "In regional CS:GO/CS2 qualifiers with limited historical data, teams with recent dominant single-map victories (~13-3) win BO3 advancement matches ~45-55% of the time; teams with recent BO3 series wins (~2-1) advance ~50-55% of the time. Head-to-head data absent."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "Market has collapsed from 50% EMA to 26% YES in 24 hours (-24pp), driven by sharp volatility spikes on Apr 10 (\u00b117.5pp to \u00b130pp swings). Panic selling pattern evident: large coordinated moves suggest information cascade or influential community call against Inner Circle Academy, not gradual repricing. Briefing provides asymmetric data: one strong datapoint for YES (13-3 dominant win) vs two datapoints for NO (2-1 series win with 13-8 map wins), but depth is thin for both. bond1e's 2-1 victory is recent match experience; Inner Circle Academy's 13-3 shows map dominance but is single-map snapshot \u2014 insufficient for confident team comparison. No head-to-head history, limited roster/form history, and Ukrainian regional context creates uncertainty neither side can credibly resolve from briefing alone. Current 26% YES price reflects extreme risk-off sentiment disproportionate to quality of evidence; a 13-3 stomp is a legitimate positive signal that market has over-discounted. Low total volume ($10.3k) and high volatility suggest shallow liquidity and retail panic rather than institutional confidence in NO thesis. Confidence asymmetry justified: YES data (strong recent map performance) is concrete; NO data (series win) is real but doesn't prove BO3 matchup outcome. Both sides lack depth for high conviction. Event is TODAY/IMMINENT (5 hours to match): sharp moves this late are typically emotional, not informational \u2014 indicates crowd panic over true edge discovery. Market may be overstating bond1e's resilience and understating Inner Circle Academy's momentum; 26% YES is plausible but likely overshoots fair value given sparse data.", "key_factor": "Fear"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "Inner Circle Academy's 13-3 Overpass victory vs mrg is a strong single-map performance, but one map is insufficient to assess BO3 capability\u2014different map pools, veto strategy, and psychological resilience across three maps are distinct skills. bond1e's 2-1 series win (13-8, 13-8 wins; Overpass loss) demonstrates match experience and ability to close series under pressure\u2014higher-order strategic evidence than single-map data. Both teams are in Play-In bracket of a closed qualifier: this typically means tier-2/3 regional teams with limited international exposure; competitive variance is high and rosters may lack deep BO3 tournament experience. Market price swing of -17.5pp, +25pp, -30pp in 3.5 hours (Apr 10 18:00-19:30 UTC) is extreme for a ~5-hour pre-match window; suggests either: (1) sharp information (roster changes, illness, leaked scrim results) not in briefing, or (2) low-liquidity sentiment cascade. Treat with caution. NO side (bond1e at 74%) is overweighted relative to the confidence we can assign: bond1e has one recent series win, but no historical H2H, no broader tournament performance, and limited roster strength indicators in briefing. YES side (Inner Circle Academy at 26%) is underweighted: the 13-3 dominant map result is real evidence of current form, and bond1e's narrow series win (2-1, losing map 3) could indicate fatigue or inconsistency. Absence of HLTV rating data, player ratings, or recent tournament placements for either team prevents peer comparison; confidence in both directions is constrained. Online format removes travel/environmental variables but typically favors teams with stable ping and infrastructure\u2014no data provided on either team's connectivity stability. With ~5 hours to resolution, reversal from 26% to 50%+ would require credible pre-match information (forfeiture, roster issue) to emerge; current price likely reflects modest but genuine edge to bond1e, not certainty.", "key_factor": "Market pricing at 26% YES reflects bond1e's recent series win momentum and 2-1 match experience, but single-map sample sizes and thin competitive data on both teams in this qualifier tier create high uncertainty; price movement volatility (-24pp in 24h) signals information asymmetry or sentiment swing rather than fundamental team strength revelation."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "Market has collapsed 24pp in 24 hours with violent swings (-17.5pp, +25pp, -30pp in 3.5 hours on Apr 10), signaling extreme uncertainty or late-breaking information not captured in briefing. bond1e demonstrated series-winning experience (2-1 vs HYPERSPIRIT) with two convincing 13-8 map victories; Inner Circle Academy's only cited evidence is a single 13-3 stomp vs weak opponent (mrg), which is insufficient to establish form. Briefing provides almost no roster/player-level data for either team\u2014no fragging stats, no lineup confirmations, no recent head-to-head history; this absence is a red flag for hidden roster changes or personnel issues. Online format + Ukrainian/Eastern European regional servers = known vulnerability to connectivity disruptions; a single player's technical failure in BO3 can cascade into map losses or walkover scenarios. Play-In matches often involve newly formed or partially assembled rosters; Inner Circle Academy's 'academy' designation suggests possible lineup instability, substitute rotations, or unconfirmed player availability. Market volatility spike (+25pp swing) suggests late cash/information flow; this could indicate bond1e odds improving due to last-minute intel (player confirmed for match, Inner Circle roster concern, etc.). Resolution criteria allow 50-50 outcome only if match is not played, delayed >7 days, forfeited pre-start, or cancelled\u2014but if match begins and one team forfeits, the other wins outright; technical failures mid-series on online platform favor the already-leading team (bond1e, if ahead after Game 1). Briefing silence on recent roster moves, injuries, or player availability for Inner Circle Academy is conspicuous; no counter-evidence prevents a same-day lineup surprise. bond1e's 2-1 series win shows resilience (came back after losing third map vs HYPERSPIRIT, suggesting mental composure); Inner Circle's single blowout win lacks pressure-match context.", "key_factor": "Inner Circle Academy player(s) experience unexpected technical failure, internet connectivity drop, or client crash during critical map(s) in the BO3, forcing a disadvantageous restart or partial forfeit scenario that resolves to bond1e victory."}], "final_score": 0.2942857142857143, "no_score": 0.7030601092896175, "edge": 0.029285714285714304, "no_edge": -0.0319398907103825, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 52% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1929587", "question": "Counter-Strike: Inner Circle Academy vs bond1e (BO3) - LORGAR RANKINGS Closed Qualifier Play-In", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Lower bracket semifinal 2 match between Inner Circle Academy and bond1e in the LORGAR RANKINGS Closed Qualifier Play-In, initially scheduled for April 10 at 1:30PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Inner Circle Academy\" if Inner Circle Academy win the match against bond1e.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"bond1e\" if bond1e win the match against Inner Circle Academy.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-11T00:45:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-10T18:45:00Z", "yes_price": 0.265, "volume_usd": 10283.833072000001, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["114101313994114876071927046502881282089912026613026416974132022688242873837875", 