 briefing contains a critical data inconsistency: it references a NACL standings table but does NOT list Maryville University or NRG Esports in the visible standings, suggesting either a data extraction error, wrong league tier, or that one/both teams are not primary NACL competitors\u2014this fundamentally undermines probability estimation."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.32, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing provides NACL standings table but neither Maryville University nor NRG Esports appears in the published roster \u2014 suggests both may be academy/lower-tier squads or the standings table is incomplete/outdated. CONTRARIAN SIGNAL: Market has risen +10pp over 7 days (YES strengthening) despite zero new competitive data in briefing \u2014 indicates off-chain information (scrims, roster announcements, or internal intel) driving sentiment rather than match history. SHARP MOVES PATTERN: Three major drops on YES (-6pp, -6pp, -5pp) in last 48 hours; highest volatility on YES side (2.4pp/hr vs 1.4pp/hr NO) suggests genuine uncertainty and late-stage news injection rather than settled expectation. NRG INFRASTRUCTURE PARADOX: NRG is established org but NO evidence of LoL roster strength in briefing \u2014 only NRG Academy mentioned in VALORANT context; main roster may be thin or newly formed, lacking game-ready depth. MARYVILLE COLLEGIATE ANGLE: University teams occasionally outperform academy squads due to fresh scrim prep and less-jaded mentality; if Maryville has scraped together a coherent 5-stack with recent bootcamp, they may exploit overconfidence. PATCH/META WINDOW: Briefing silent on current LoL patch; recent system updates (item rework, jungle changes) can favor certain comp styles; if Maryville prepped for specific meta and NRG is caught mid-adaptation, upset becomes plausible. STAKES ASYMMETRY: Maryville is fighting for relevance (potential relegation bracket team); NRG may be coasti