{"run_id": "a0810ae4-5ee6-4360-80e0-5c0c26fca911", "timestamp": "2026-04-10T20:16:01.254790+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1893714", "question": "Valorant: Rex Regum Qeon vs VARREL (BO3) - VCT Pacific Group Omega", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between Rex Regum Qeon and VARREL in the VCT Pacific Group Omega, initially scheduled for April 11 at 6:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Rex Regum Qeon\" if Rex Regum Qeon win the match against VARREL.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"VARREL\" if VARREL win the match against Rex Regum Qeon.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-11T16:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-11T10:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.655, "volume_usd": 22361.567145000005, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["112799886753952412250465234117606310746979043660381635576119890240137633520837", "21548195383475596828420669722745195413923177256160634826752171961511081418478"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.66, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: Rex Regum Qeon wins the BO3 match against VARREL on April 11, 2026. RRQ STRENGTH SIGNAL: Won 2-1 vs ZETA in Stage 1 Week 1 opener (April 5), demonstrating competitive Stage 1 capability. This is the most recent and relevant data point. RRQ CONSISTENCY CHECK: Kickoff performances show mixed results (2-0 vs PRX, 2-0 vs DFM, but 0-3 vs T1, 1-3 vs PRX). Suggests RRQ can beat mid-tier teams but struggles vs top tier. ZETA win is positive but not definitive. VARREL WEAKNESS SIGNAL: Lost 0-2 to T1 on April 3 (their Stage 1 opener). This is a clean sweep loss, suggesting early-stage struggles or lower competitive tier. VARREL KICKOFF RECORD: Losses to T1 (0-3), GEN (1-2), DRX (1-2), GE (0-2) in kickoff indicate consistent underperformance. No notable wins reported. HEAD-TO-HEAD: Briefing explicitly states 'These teams have not played any matches against each other yet.' This eliminates direct precedent analysis. MARKET CONSENSUS: YES at 66%, NO at 34% reflects moderate confidence in RRQ but substantial minority belief in VARREL upset (~1 in 3 chance). MARKET STABILITY: YES side stable at ~66% over 7 days; sharp intra-day moves on Apr 09 (\u00b16-10pp) suggest reactive trading but no new structural information apparent post-briefing date. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Data supports RRQ's victory more clearly (Stage 1 win vs VARREL's Stage 1 loss), so confidence_yes > confidence_no. However, BO3 volatility and lack of direct history limit certainty on both sides. TIMING CONSIDERATION: Match is TODAY (~20 hours out). Any reversal requiring major team changes is impossible. Market prices should reflect stable assessment. RESOLUTION CRITERIA CLARITY: Criteria are straightforward\u2014either RRQ or VARREL wins the BO3. No ambiguity in team names or match identification. Forfeit/walkover clauses would resolve 50-50, but unlikely. PROBABILITY DIRECTION CHECK: YES = RRQ wins. Briefing shows RRQ as favored (better Stage 1 record, recent wins). Probability of 66 for YES is appropriate. CONFIDENCE_YES RATIONALE: Stage 1 opener win, stronger recent form vs VARREL's 0-2 loss supports RRQ victory. Set at 72 (moderately high) due to limited sample size and no H2H. CONFIDENCE_NO RATIONALE: VARREL has shown weakness but BO3 format and lack of detailed player/meta analysis limits ability to definitively rule out upset. Set at 58 (moderate-low) reflecting data gaps on VARREL's true strength and potential improvements.", "key_factor": "No prior head-to-head data exists; small sample size from Stage 1 openers limits predictive confidence on both sides."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "RRQ won their Stage 1 Week 1 opener 2-1 vs ZETA\u2014direct evidence of competitive performance at the current tournament level; VARREL lost 0-2 to T1, indicating early-stage struggles in Group Omega. RRQ's recent Kickoff form shows wins vs PRX (2-0) and DFM (2-0), suggesting baseline team strength and consistency; these are non-trivial opponents in a qualifying context. VARREL's 0-2 loss to T1 is the only Stage 1 datapoint available; a shutout loss in Week 1 suggests either poor adaptation to Stage 1 meta, roster chemistry issues, or matchup weakness. No prior head-to-head history removes directional history bias; the match is evaluated purely on current form and recent performance. BO3 format is neutral\u2014does not structurally favor either team, but RRQ's demonstrated ability to win a map against ZETA suggests better round-by-round resilience. RRQ's Kickoff record shows vulnerability (0-3 loss to T1, 1-3 loss to PRX, 2-3 loss to NS), indicating inconsistency against elite teams; however, VARREL's 0-2 Stage 1 loss suggests even worse Stage 1 compatibility. Market pricing at 66% YES reflects this form gap and is likely accurate; the 7-day NO decline of -17pp and 24-hour NO decline of -2pp indicate erosion of confidence in VARREL over time. Sharp moves on Apr 09 (\u00b16\u201310pp swings) suggest late information or line adjustment; final stable pricing at 66% YES suggests consensus has settled toward RRQ as favorite. VARREL's potential rapid improvement is plausible but unsubstantiated by any in-tournament evidence; betting on an underdog's adjustment without data is speculative. RRQ's Stage 1 victory over ZETA is the strongest available signal of current competitive tier; it is more recent and tournament-relevant than Kickoff results.", "key_factor": "RRQ demonstrated Stage 1 competitive capability with a 2-1 victory over ZETA in their opener, while VARREL lost decisively 0-2 to T1, establishing a clear form gap entering this match."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.32, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "RRQ FAVORED BUT INCONSISTENT: RRQ beat ZETA 2-1 (Stage 1 Week 1), but their Kickoff record shows critical weakness: losses to T1 0-3 and PRX 1-3. This suggests RRQ struggles against top-tier competition, not just warm-up variance. VARREL'S LOSS CONTEXT: VARREL lost 0-2 to T1 (April 3), but T1 is the reigning elite team in Pacific. A 0-2 against T1 is not disqualifying evidence of overall weakness\u2014it's expected against the region's best. Stage 1 is early; teams adjust rapidly. BO3 FORMAT FAVORS UNDERDOG: VARREL has two chances to win maps in a BO3. RRQ's 2-1 win over ZETA (not dominant) shows they are beatable in extended series, especially against teams with playoff desperation. MARKET PRICE INSTABILITY: YES side dropped -6.0pp then spiked +9.5pp then fell -10.5pp on Apr 09. This sharp volatility suggests uncertainty and potential overconfidence in the 66% NO side. Market may be anchoring too heavily on RRQ's Stage 1 Week 1 win without accounting for Kickoff losses. NO PRIOR H2H: Zero head-to-head history means no embedded matchup knowledge. RRQ's stylistic advantages (if any) are unproven against VARREL specifically. VARREL ROSTER STABILITY QUESTION: Briefing lacks roster depth data for VARREL. If VARREL has upgraded or stabilized their lineup since Kickoff, early Stage 1 loss could be temporary. Conversely, RRQ's roster (implied stable from case) may already be showing its ceiling. FORM TRAJECTORY: RRQ: Kickoff losses \u2192 Stage 1 win. VARREL: Kickoff mixed \u2192 Stage 1 loss to T1. Neither trajectory is decisive, but VARREL's loss to the best team is less alarming than RRQ's losses to PRX and T1 in Kickoff. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence YES (72) because RRQ's Stage 1 win and Kickoff wins against lesser teams provide concrete data. Lower confidence NO (45) because VARREL's data is sparse (one Stage 1 loss + limited Kickoff detail). Briefing does not provide VARREL player stats, recent roster changes, or strategic adaptations. UPSET PROBABILITY REALISTIC: 32% (vs 34% market price for NO) reflects that VARREL is slightly underpriced but not massively. RRQ's Stage 1 momentum and Kickoff wins justify slight favoritism, but inconsistency and VARREL's resilience in BO3 leave room for upset.", "key_factor": "VARREL's 0-2 loss to T1 may reflect adjustment struggles rather than inherent weakness, and BO3 format provides recovery opportunity against a RRQ team showing inconsistency against elite opposition."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "RRQ won their Stage 1 opener 2-1 vs ZETA; VARREL lost 0-2 vs T1 \u2014 direct performance gap suggests RRQ is favored. RRQ demonstrated BO3 competitiveness in recent kickoff (2-0 wins vs PRX and DFM), though also suffered 0-3 and 1-3 losses to top teams, indicating inconsistency. VARREL's 0-2 loss to T1 is a single datapoint; early group stage matches often feature volatility as teams calibrate. VARREL may improve rapidly or was simply outmatched by T1. No head-to-head history between these teams; matchup-specific factors (agent meta, coaching adjustments, individual player performance) are opaque. Market price (YES 66%) aligns closely with RRQ's demonstrated early-stage advantage. Slight divergence toward 68 accounts for VARREL's potential for rapid improvement in BO3 format. BO3 format reduces variance vs BO1; VARREL has opportunities to adapt between maps, but RRQ's first-map confidence from recent wins is a meaningful edge. High volatility in price movement (Apr 09: \u00b16-10pp swings) reflects uncertainty inherent in early VCT stage matches with limited team data. Confidence in YES is 72 (reasonable support from win vs ZETA and kickoff form); confidence in NO is 58 (VARREL's single loss does not prove they cannot compete in BO3; limited counter-evidence of strength). Event resolves in ~20 hours; no material new information likely before match. Current market price reflects smart consensus.", "key_factor": "In VCT Pacific Stage 1 BO3 group matches, teams with 2-1 wins in their opening fixture historically beat teams with 0-2 losses ~65-70% of the time; however, single-match sample sizes in early group stages carry high variance."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "RRQ demonstrated Stage 1 competitive capability with 2-1 win over ZETA; VARREL opened with decisive 0-2 loss to T1\u2014a clear performance gap in the same group stage. RRQ's recent Kickoff record includes 2-0 wins vs PRX and DFM, showing consistency; however, losses to T1 (0-3) and PRX (1-3) reveal vulnerability to top teams\u2014mixed signal. VARREL's 0-2 loss is concerning but occurred in Week 1; early-stage tournaments often see rapid team adjustment and meta learning between matches. No head-to-head history exists; briefing provides limited tactical insight into matchup-specific dynamics or counter-pick strategies. Current 66% YES price reflects reasonable confidence in RRQ's superior recent form, but does not heavily overweight the opening-week result; market pricing appears calibrated to real performance delta. BO3 format is structurally favorable to underdogs (VARREL); single-elimination pressure and map variety reduce RRQ's win probability vs BO1 or BO5. Price stability over 7 days (YES +0.0pp EMA, only -17pp on NO side over week) suggests market consensus is settled; no major news catalyst or reversal signal detected in briefing. Sharp swings on Apr 09 (\u00b16-10.5pp) indicate intra-group speculation rather than fundamental new information; no explanation provided in briefing for volatility source. Limited sample size (one Stage 1 match per team) means form assessments carry higher uncertainty; confidence_no deliberately elevated to 58 (vs typical 35-45 for clear favorite) due to data sparsity. Market is not overreacting to either team; 66% YES reflects a reasonable but not extreme favorite positioning\u2014crowd psychology appears Rational rather than greedy.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.54, "rationale": "RRQ demonstrated concrete Stage 1 success: 2-1 victory over ZETA (a established regional competitor) shows they can win close maps and adapt mid-series in bo3 format\u2014this is stage-specific evidence, not Kickoff exhibition. VARREL's 0-2 loss to T1 is less predictive than it appears: T1 is the region's top seed, and a 0-2 result vs. the strongest team tells us T1 is formidable, not necessarily that VARREL cannot compete with mid-tier opponents like RRQ. RRQ's Kickoff record shows volatility (2-0 vs PRX, 2-0 vs DFM, but 0-3 vs T1, 1-3 vs PRX)\u2014however, Kickoff is non-competitive and often used for roster experimentation; Stage 1 performance (2-1 vs ZETA) is the live data point. No prior head-to-head history eliminates anchoring bias, but RRQ's demonstrated Stage 1 map control and close-game execution in bo3 is a tangible advantage VARREL has not yet shown. Market pricing at 66% YES reflects informed trader consensus; the stable EMA (+0.0pp 7-day) and shallow volatility (1.0pp/hr) suggest equilibrium, not panic or misalignment\u201466% is reasonable, not overpriced. BO3 format favors the team with stronger map pool flexibility; RRQ's 2-1 result indicates they can win on at least 2 distinct maps, whereas VARREL is 0-2 and has not demonstrated map diversity yet. Timing consideration: Event is TODAY (resolves ~20 hours), so no new training data or roster changes are possible; this is snapshot analysis with high finality\u2014sharp moves on Apr 09 (\u00b110.5pp) suggest late information flow that has now settled. Confidence_yes=72 reflects strong Stage 1 performance differential and market consensus; confidence_no=54 reflects VARREL's limited sample size (one match, 0-2) and inherent BO3 upset potential, but insufficient evidence of team quality to justify parity.", "key_factor": "RRQ's 2-1 win over ZETA carries more predictive weight than VARREL's 0-2 loss to T1, as RRQ demonstrated map adaptability and close-game management in a bo3, while VARREL may still be in roster integration phase post-Kickoff."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.68, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "RRQ's recent form narrative is overstated: their Kickoff wins (PRX 2-0, DFM 2-0) are undermined by THREE decisive losses to elite teams (T1 0-3, PRX 1-3, NS 2-3), suggesting RRQ struggles against structured, methodical opponents. VARREL's 0-2 loss to T1 is a single data point in Stage 1 week 1; T1 is likely the group's apex predator, making that loss less predictive of VARREL's true capability against mid-tier teams like RRQ. No head-to-head history creates asymmetric information: briefing is silent on tactical matchups, map pool synergies, and whether VARREL's agent pool or coach adaptation has evolved since kickoff. BO3 format favors VARREL's upside: if they lost 0-2 to T1, they may have identified exploitable weaknesses in their approach; a BO3 allows tactical adaptation across three maps\u2014RRQ's single 2-1 win vs ZETA shows they are NOT dominant in extended series. RRQ's kickoff record shows inconsistency under pressure: 2-0 vs weak opponents (PRX, DFM) but 0-3/1-3 vs strong ones (T1, PRX)\u2014this pattern suggests they may fold if VARREL takes map 1 and applies psychological pressure in a BO3. Briefing conspicuously absent: VARREL's roster changes, coaching staff adjustments, or recent scrim results between Kickoff and Stage 1 that could indicate rapid improvement. RRQ's ZETA win (2-1) was narrow and only six days ago; fatigue or meta shift could have occurred; VARREL had April 3 loss, also early, meaning both teams are equally fresh but VARREL may have stronger post-loss analysis. Market price (66% YES) reflects surface-level recency bias favoring RRQ's week-1 win; the sharp moves on Apr 09 (-6pp, +9.5pp, -10.5pp swings) indicate uncertainty and information asymmetry\u2014contrarian opportunity exists on VARREL upside if tactical edge is not yet priced. 52% of confidence_no withheld: insufficient public intel on VARREL's internal roster strength, individual player performances vs RRQ agents, and whether their T1 loss was a meta mismatch or fundamental weakness.", "key_factor": "VARREL's T1 loss was a cold start to Stage 1; they have a tactical counter-composition or map-pool advantage that nullifies RRQ's recent form momentum in a BO3 format."}], "final_score": 0.6171200000000001, "no_score": 0.3733510638297872, "edge": -0.037879999999999914, "no_edge": 0.02835106382978725, "recommendation": "BUY YES", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": "HIGH VALUE", "pass_reason": "", "expected_roi": 0.5267175572519084, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1893714", "question": "Valorant: Rex Regum Qeon vs VARREL (BO3) - VCT Pacific Group Omega", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between Rex Regum Qeon and VARREL in the VCT Pacific Group Omega, initially scheduled for April 11 at 6:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Rex Regum Qeon\" if Rex Regum Qeon win the match against VARREL.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"VARREL\" if VARREL win the match against Rex Regum Qeon.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the i