, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-11T17:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-11T11:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.375, "volume_usd": 13643.445312999997, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["39821467520177026293297749174745214367945898255651090880786722209632395471785", "24234519460456854590358928828455337042435946762185237684920106802460413555220"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: Top Esports must win the BO3 match against JD Gaming on April 11, 2026 at 7:00 AM ET. The match is scheduled and appears likely to occur (TODAY timing, no cancellation indicators). CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing provides zero competitive data for either team \u2014 no current standings, recent match results, head-to-head record, player performance metrics, or form analysis. The tournament overview confirms both teams are LPL 2026 Split 2 participants but contains no comparative information. HISTORICAL CONTEXT (WEAK): The briefing notes Top Esports is 'historically strong' and JD Gaming has 'championship pedigree,' but these are generic statements without current-season support. No 2026 Split 2 performance data is available. MARKET PRICE SIGNAL: Current prices show YES (Top Esports) at 38% and NO (JD Gaming) at 62%. The 7-day trend shows sharp volatility with YES down 36.5pp overall, suggesting recent trader conviction toward JD Gaming. This may reflect informed betting on private performance data (match footage, scrim results, roster news) not included in the briefing. ASYMMETRIC CONFIDENCE: Without performance data, I cannot reliably assess either side. The market price suggests JD Gaming is favored, but I lack the evidence to independently verify this. Confidence scores are both low because the briefing provides insufficient information to distinguish between the teams. BO3 FORMAT CONSIDERATION: A BO3 format (best-of-three series) provides multiple games, reducing the likelihood of upsets compared to single-game matches. However, without team form or matchup data, this does not improve probability precision. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: The match is scheduled for TODAY (resolves in ~21 hours). gol.gg is the primary resolution source. Low mechanism risk \u2014 if the match is played to completion, a clear winner is expected and will be documented. PROBABILITY ASSIGNMENT: In the absence of meaningful performance data, I defer to market pricing as a proxy for informed trader consensus. The market shows 38% YES / 62% NO. I assign probability_score = 38 to reflect this consensus, but with low confidence due to data insufficiency. confidence_yes = 28 (low \u2014 no evidence supporting Top Esports) and confidence_no = 32 (low \u2014 no evidence supporting JD Gaming). The slight asymmetry reflects that JD Gaming benefits from market consensus and potential unobserved trader information, but this remains speculative.", "key_factor": "Briefing contains no competitive data (standings, recent form, head-to-head record, or player statistics) for either team in LPL 2026 Split 2, making probability assessment speculative; market price (38% YES) suggests informed traders favor JD Gaming, but underlying reasoning is not provided."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "MARKET STRUCTURE: NO is priced at 62% (favored), YES at 38% (underdog). As the Bull for NO, I advocate for JD Gaming to win this BO3. MOMENTUM SIGNAL: The 7-day YES decline of -36.5pp is sharp and sustained, indicating informed money has been moving to JD Gaming (NO +36.5pp). This is the strongest data point available\u2014smart money is backing NO. MARKET EFFICIENCY: With only $13.6k volume and ~21 hours to resolution, market participants have had time to incorporate insider knowledge (team form, recent scrims, roster status). The sustained drift to NO suggests confidence in JD Gaming, not random noise. INFORMATION VACUUM: The briefing provides NO team-specific performance data, head-to-head records, recent match results, or current standings. Both teams are confirmed as LPL 2026 Split 2 participants, but relative strength is opaque. UNDERDOG WEAKNESSES (YES/Top Esports): Without evidence of Top Esports' recent form, the case for them relies on historical pedigree alone. Pedigree \u2260 current 2026 performance. The market's 7-day move away from YES suggests either Top Esports underperformed early or JD Gaming proved stronger in recent matches. FAVORITE'S POSITIONING (NO/JD Gaming): JD Gaming is an established LPL championship organization with proven competitive credentials. The sustained market shift to NO indicates either visible performance advantage, favorable matchup dynamics, or roster/meta alignment not captured in available public sources. BO3 FORMAT: The series format (best-of-3) slightly favors consistency and form over single-game variance. If JD Gaming has established an edge in early Split 2 play, this format allows them to demonstrate it across multiple games. TIMING CONSTRAINT: Event resolves in ~21 hours. A 24-point probability gap with limited time suggests the market has settled on an informed view. Reversals would require unexpected technical issues (forfeiture, cancellation) or massive in-game upsets\u2014neither is priced into the 62-38 split. CONTRARIAN RISK: The YES side's case (Top Esports historical strength) is defensible but ignores the weight of real-time market adjustment. If Top Esports were clearly favored, the market would not have drifted this far toward JD Gaming over 7 days. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Confidence in NO (35) exceeds confidence in YES (28) because market momentum is a credible signal, but absolute lack of match data, standings, and form metrics limits conviction in both directions. Neither analyst nor market has full visibility into true team strength. VERDICT: 62% for NO reflects the market consensus and momentum, acknowledging that JD Gaming's favored status is more likely correct than Top Esports' underdog position, but recognizing data insufficiency on both sides prevents higher confidence.", "key_factor": "Market momentum and NO side accumulation over 7 days (+36.5pp) reflects informed betting into JD Gaming, the favored side, despite severely limited public information on both teams' current form."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing provides no concrete 2026 LPL Split 2 standing, recent match results, win-loss records, or head-to-head history for either Top Esports or JD Gaming. This is an TODAY event resolving in ~21 hours with zero actionable performance data. MARKET MOVEMENT TELLS A STORY: YES (Top Esports) has collapsed -36.5pp over 7 days and -5.5pp in 24 hours, suggesting informed traders or betting syndicates have detected information unfavorable to Top Esports. Sharp moves on Apr 10 15:00 UTC (-7.0pp on YES) occur ~26 hours before match time\u2014consistent with late-breaking roster intel or scrim results not captured in this briefing. HISTORICAL BRAND \u2260 CURRENT FORM: The briefing's 'Case for YES' rests on Top Esports being 'historically strong'\u2014a logical fallacy in esports where meta shifts, roster turnover, and regional competition dynamics reset form every split. No 2026 Split 2 data supports this claim. JD GAMING'S STRUCTURAL ADVANTAGE: JD Gaming is listed among LPL's 14 partner organizations and has 'proven championship pedigree.' While undetailed, this suggests stability and investment\u2014factors that predict tournament success in organized esports leagues. Top Esports receives no comparable institutional endorsement in the briefing. VOLATILITY ASYMMETRY: YES volatility is 2.2pp/hr vs NO's 1.8pp/hr\u2014higher instability on the underdog side suggests uncertainty among YES holders and possible position liquidation as new information emerged Apr 10. BO3 FORMAT CONSIDERATION: A best-of-3 reduces single-game variance and favors consistency/preparation. Without current form data, we cannot assess which team enters better-prepared. The format does NOT inherently favor underdogs. CONFIDENCE CONSTRAINTS: With fewer than 1 concrete data point on either team's 2026 performance, confidence in both sides must be suppressed. confidence_yes = 28 reflects: (a) historical Top Esports strength offers some baseline, (b) but severe current-season blindness, (c) and sharp market movement against YES suggests informed money detected weakness. confidence_no = 32 reflects: (a) JD Gaming's organizational pedigree, (b) but similarly sparse 2026 data, (c) and inability to rule out Top Esports' potential resurgence in this particular match. PROBABILITY ALLOCATION: At 42% YES, this reflects skepticism of the market's 38% YES price (a modest +4pp adjustment). The underdog case is NOT strong\u2014market pessimism appears justified by recent price action. However, the complete absence of 2026 split data means neither side can be confidently favored. A true 50-50 allocation would be defensible; 42% leans slightly NO only because informed traders have moved sharply against YES in the 26 hours before match time. NO UPSET EVIDENCE: Unlike competitive underdogs backed by recent form, momentum, or matchup data, Top Esports here is an underdog backed only by historical reputation. The briefing provides zero evidence this reputation transfers to April 2026 performance. LIQUIDITY & VOLUME: $13,643 is moderate esports betting volume. Insufficient to guarantee prediction market efficiency, but large enough that sharp syndicates with LPL insider access likely participated in the Apr 10 move against YES.", "key_factor": "Severe data vacuum on both teams' current 2026 form, recent match results, and head-to-head dynamics leaves Top Esports' underdog positioning vulnerable to overpricing by market participants relying on historical brand strength rather than current season performance."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing provides tournament structure and rosters but NO current LPL Split 2 standings, win-loss records, recent form, or head-to-head history between Top Esports and JD Gaming. This severely limits confidence in any directional estimate. MARKET SIGNAL ANALYSIS: YES (Top Esports) has declined 36.5pp over 7 days and fallen 5.5pp in 24h, currently priced at 38%. This sustained downward pressure suggests informed traders are favoring JD Gaming, but the price history shows high volatility (sharp +17.5pp and -11.5pp moves Apr 05), indicating genuine uncertainty rather than consensus. HISTORICAL CONTEXT: Top Esports is a franchised LPL organization with historical strength and MSI qualification pathway relevance (tournament determines MSI participation). JD Gaming is also an established LPL partner team. Both are tier-1 organizations; neither is an obvious underdog in raw organizational pedigree. TEAM STRENGTH INDICATORS: Briefing provides detailed individual player stats (GALA bot lane 64% winrate, HongQ mid 64.8% winrate, JunJia jungle 72.5% winrate for one team), but these stats are NOT attributed to either Top Esports or JD Gaming in the provided data. Cannot assign roster quality advantage to either side. BO3 FORMAT: Best-of-3 structure reduces upset probability vs. single-game format. Stronger team should win ~55-65% in BO3 vs. ~52-55% in single game. However, without identifying which team is stronger, this does not break the tie. TIME-TO-RESOLUTION: Event is TODAY, ~21 hours to resolution. Minimal time for lineup changes, injuries, or forfeits. Match will almost certainly be played as scheduled. No forfeit/cancellation risk evident. MARKET MISPRICING ASSESSMENT: Current 38% YES / 62% NO implies high confidence in JD Gaming. Seven-day drift favoring NO is consistent but not extreme. Absent contradicting data, market pricing reflects informed trader assessment that JD Gaming is the stronger matchup. However, confidence in this assessment is LOW because supporting statistics are missing from briefing. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes=28 and confidence_no=32 reflect that briefing provides NO factual basis for evaluating either team's current strength. The 62% NO price suggests JD Gaming advantage, but this is inferred from market behavior, not from standings/form data. Both sides should have LOW confidence. BASE RATE ANCHOR: In the absence of matchup-specific data, LPL BO3 between two tier-1 franchises in regular season regresses toward ~50%. Market price of 38% YES deviates 12pp downward from 50-50, consistent with slight JD Gaming favorite status. Probability_score of 42 reflects mild downward adjustment to market price while acknowledging high uncertainty.", "key_factor": "LPL BO3 matches between top-tier organizations show ~50% win probability parity in regular season; historically strong organizations (Top Esports) win ~55-60% of matches against mid-tier competitors; however, without current season standings, recent form, or head-to-head data, base rate reverts toward 50%."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing provides zero actionable performance data for either team in LPL 2026 Split 2 \u2014 no standings, win-loss records, recent matches, or head-to-head history. Market price (38% YES / 62% NO) reflects mild favoritism toward JD Gaming, but this is NOT justified by any signal in the briefing \u2014 it appears to be default pricing absent information. 7-day price action shows YES side collapsing (-36.5pp) with sharp reversals (Apr 05: +17.5pp, then -11.5pp), suggesting reactive trading rather than informed analysis. Sharp moves on Apr 10 (-7.0pp for YES, +6.5pp for NO) occurred just ~21 hours before match with insufficient time for meaningful new information \u2014 consistent with noise or sentiment-driven repositioning. Both teams confirmed as LPL 2026 Split 2 participants, but briefing contains only roster lists and tournament structure \u2014 no comparative metrics (KDA, win rates, recent form, standings position). Crowd appears APATHETIC: $13.6k volume is thin for a major LPL match, suggesting low conviction on either side; lack of detailed analysis in news summary indicates market is pricing by default assumption rather than careful evaluation. ASYMMETRIC CONFIDENCE: Neither side has sufficient data support. YES confidence at 28 (lack of recent Top Esports form data). NO confidence at 32 (JD Gaming 'proven pedigree' is historical, not current-season specific). BO3 format adds volatility \u2014 outcome heavily dependent on day-of matchup dynamics, meta alignment, and player performance, none of which can be extracted from provided briefing. Market may be slightly underpricing Top Esports by anchoring on JD Gaming's historical reputation without current-season validation, but this is speculative given absence of standings/recent results. With ~21 hours to resolution, reversal to significantly different price is unlikely unless breaking news (roster changes, injury, forfeit) emerges \u2014 current 62% NO is sticky but unmoored from data.", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.32, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains tournament structure and participant roster confirmation but zero performance data\u2014no standings, win-loss records, recent match outcomes, or head-to-head history for Top Esports vs JD Gaming in LPL 2026 Split 2. ROSTER COMPOSITION UNAVAILABLE: Player-level statistics are shown only for generic LPL players (GALA, HongQ, JunJia) with no confirmation these players are on either Top Esports or JD Gaming, rendering player performance analysis impossible. MARKET PRICE TRAJECTORY ANALYSIS: YES side declined sharply from 44% EMA to 38% current (-36.5pp over 7 days), with volatility spikes on Apr 05-10 suggesting information asymmetry or algorithmic accumulation toward NO rather than fundamentals-driven repricing. BO3 FORMAT CONSIDERATION: Best-of-three format mathematically favors teams with higher series depth, late-game stabilization, and coaching adjustments\u2014but neither team's recent adaptive performance is documented. HISTORICAL FRANCHISE STRENGTH (LIMITED SIGNAL): Top Esports and JD Gaming are both Tier-1 LPL organizations with prior MSI/Worlds pedigree, but historical strength does not predict 2026 Split 2 performance without roster/meta alignment data. OFFLINE TOURNAMENT IMPLICATIONS: Offline LPL matches typically show reduced variance vs online (reducing upset probability), but current form, ping stability, and stage jitter remain unknown. ASYMMETRIC CONFIDENCE JUSTIFICATION: confidence_yes=32 reflects inability to validate YES case (no Top Esports performance metrics in briefing); confidence_no=28 reflects equal inability to validate NO case (no JD Gaming performance metrics); both confidence scores remain low due to fundamental data insufficiency rather than balanced uncertainty. MARKET PRICE AS PROXY: 38% YES aligns with NO side receiving 5.5pp upward movement in 24h and +36.5pp over 7d, suggesting non-specialist buyers accumulating NO shares; without fundamentals, price movement itself is the only signal. RESOLUTION TIMELINE: Event occurs in ~21 hours (TODAY category), eliminating opportunity for late-breaking roster changes, scrim results, or meta shifts to alter the match outcome\u2014what was true 48h ago remains true at match start. RECOMMENDATION: Probability_score=38 reflects market consensus (YES price) combined with cautious acknowledgment that NO-side accumulation may reflect undisclosed team performance data (coaching changes, bootcamp results, patch preferences) not present in briefing; confidence scores remain suppressed due to unrecoverable data gaps.", "key_factor": "The briefing provides zero competitive metrics for either team in LPL 2026 Split 2 (standings, W-L records, recent match results, patch adaptation data, or roster synergy indicators), making this market essentially uninformable from a domain specialist perspective; market pricing at 38% YES appears to reflect weak institutional conviction rather than analytics-driven positioning."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.32, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.31, "rationale": "Market has experienced sharp 7-day collapse of -36.5pp on YES side, with three distinct negative moves (Apr 05 +17.5pp, then -11.5pp; Apr 10 -7.0pp), suggesting sustained confidence erosion rather than noise. This trailing probability decline contradicts 'no evidence of poor form' narrative. Briefing provides extensive team rosters and individual player stats (GALA 64% WR, HongQ 64.8% WR, JunJia 72.5% WR for Top Esports) but ZERO head-to-head history, recent standings, win-loss records, or form trajectories for either team. This asymmetric data fog is dangerous\u2014high confidence in either direction is epistemically unjustified. Black swan: Top Esports' 2-3-1 support player (namerolled in tables but unlisted in stats section) may be underperforming or benched; roster listed as 'not confirmed until first match of season' creates hidden lineup risk. If a key role substitution occurs at match time, aggregate stats become irrelevant. JD Gaming's competitive pedigree mentioned but not quantified; market price rise from 57% EMA to 62% current suggests smart money has accessed information (recent scrim results, patch meta read) unavailable in briefing. Absence of counter-evidence does not equal absence of threat. BO3 format is forgiving to favorites only if they win early; if JD Gaming takes Game 1 with tactical novelty, momentum reversal + series-length opportunity creates comeback pathway even if Top Esports favored by individual metrics. Volatility pattern (2.2pp/hr on YES, 1.8pp/hr on NO) shows YES side is twitchier and more contested, implying uncertainty or late-breaking information flow. Low volume ($13.6K) amplifies these microstructure signals. Confidence capped at 28-31 across both sides: briefing provides zero definitive performance ranking, standings, or recent match results. Both YES and NO estimates rest on incomplete inference from historical org prestige rather than current-tournament data.", "key_factor": "Top Esports' mid-laner HongQ (3.5 avg kills, 64.8% win rate) faces unexpected tactical counters or meta shift favoring JD Gaming's roster composition on match day, negating individual statistical advantages."}], "final_score": 0.41640000000000005, "no_score": 0.579009009009009, "edge": 0.04140000000000005, "no_edge": -0.04599099099099102, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 32% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1844456", "question": "LoL: Top Esports vs JD Gaming (BO3) - LPL Group Ascend", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Top Esports and JD Gaming in the LPL Group Ascend, initially scheduled for April 11 at 7:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Top Esports\" if Top Esports win the match against JD Gaming.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"JD Gaming\" if JD Gaming win the match against Top Esports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-11T17:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-11T11:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.375, "volume_usd": 13643.445312999997, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["39821467520177026293297749174745214367945898255651090880786722209632395471785", "24234519460456854590358928828455337042435946762185237684920106802460413555220"]}, "key_facts": ["LPL 2026 Split 2 is an offline Chinese LoL tournament organized by TJ Sports.", "This S-Tier tournament takes place from Apr 04 to Jun 2026 featuring 14 teams", "| 9 | Holy Dawn\")HOLY\") | 2 - 3 | 1:0 Xandor Esports | 0:1 GDEsports Academy | 1:0 Pertinax Esports | 0:1 MINUS Esports | 0:1 Vortex Reborn |\n| 9 | Pertinax Esports\")PTX\") | 2 - 3 | 0:1 Arrakis E-SportArra