{"run_id": "ed03266f-ec57-47f0-a24d-1a82d8f607da", "timestamp": "2026-04-11T14:50:32.067266+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1928237", "question": "Valorant: EDward Gaming vs Dragon Ranger Gaming (BO3) - VCT China Group Omega", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between EDward Gaming and Dragon Ranger Gaming in the VCT China Group Omega, initially scheduled for April 11 at 7:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"EDward Gaming\" if EDward Gaming win the match against Dragon Ranger Gaming.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Dragon Ranger Gaming\" if Dragon Ranger Gaming win the match against EDward Gaming.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-11T18:20:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-11T12:20:00Z", "yes_price": 0.555, "volume_usd": 74005.08300999996, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["34366909024661359212215880515889272505238000083989310023448180488948780696657", "27665171785968763417164606267053588928045721422560277165101357640541595837156"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.78, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "CONDITION: EDward Gaming wins the BO3 match against Dragon Ranger Gaming on April 11, 2026. EDG demonstrated dominant form in week one: 2-0 record with decisive wins over Nova and Wolves (both stomps per briefing). ZmjjKK is the region's standout performer with quantifiable leads across all major stats: 269.3 ACS (highest), 1.64 K:D, 180.7 ADR, 0.97 KPR\u2014these are significant margins in competitive Valorant. DRG showed clear vulnerability: swept 0-2 by Xi Lai Gaming (the other dominant Group Omega team), indicating consistent struggles against tier-1 opposition. EDG's successful roster acquisition of Jieni7 suggests organizational investment and team chemistry improvements, whereas DRG's mixed results (1 win vs Wolves, 0 wins vs top teams) suggest incomplete adaptation. Both EDG and XLG already qualified for Stage 1 Playoffs after week one\u2014EDG's qualification indicates they were among the two strongest teams in Group Omega, establishing clear hierarchy. Market price of 56% YES reflects moderate confidence, below the analytical case (which suggests 70%+ probability). Sharp price movements Apr 11 (\u00b121-23pp swings) indicate high volatility but market has largely stabilized around 56% by data cutoff (14:50 UTC). CASE FOR NO weaknesses: DRG's win vs Wolves is single data point; no specific DRG performance metrics provided to justify upset potential. BO3 format is standard (not inherently favoring upsets); 'other teams' mention in briefing does not suggest DRG is competitive with EDG/XLG. Confidence asymmetry: Strong data supporting EDG dominance (specific stats, week-1 record, playoff qualification) justifies high confidence_yes (78). DRG data is sparse (one sweep loss, one win; no individual performance metrics), justifying lower confidence_no (45) due to insufficient counter-evidence. EVENT TIMING (LIVE/IMMINENT\u20143 hours to match): Market shares already highly traded; sharp moves in last 2 hours suggest emerging information or late betting patterns, but fundamentals (EDG dominance, DRG weakness) remain unchanged. Probability_score of 72 reflects: EDG's clear 2-0 week-1 dominance + ZmjjKK's stat leadership + DRG's 0-2 record vs top teams, discounted slightly for: early-stage roster adaptation risk + single BO3 match variance + sparse DRG performance data limiting confidence in magnitude of gap.", "key_factor": "Match resolution depends on vlr.gg publication within 2 hours post-match; backup consensus reporting available if needed, but mechanism risk is minimal given professional esports coverage standards."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.78, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "EDG DOMINANCE: Week one results show EDG decisively defeated both Nova and Wolves with 2-0 sweeps, establishing clear control in Group Omega. This is not marginal advantage\u2014stomps indicate system mastery. INDIVIDUAL EXCELLENCE: ZmjjKK leads the entire China region across four critical metrics simultaneously (ACS 269.3, K:D 1.64, ADR 180.7, KPR 0.97), indicating structural team advantage at the highest mechanical level. STRUCTURAL ADVANTAGE: EDG has already qualified for Stage 1 Playoffs after week one alongside XLG\u2014only two teams identified as playoff-qualified, signaling they are tier-separated from the field including DRG. DRG VULNERABILITY EVIDENCE: Dragon Ranger Gaming suffered a 0-2 sweep loss to XLG (the other top team), directly demonstrating they lose decisively against elite opposition. If they lose to XLG, EDG (comparable tier) presents similar risk. ROSTER STABILITY: EDG made successful roster moves with Jieni7 addition, and briefing explicitly notes this 'increased team cohesion.' DRG roster moves are unmentioned\u2014suggests less proactive management. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS\u2014LIMITED DATA: Briefing provides zero specific performance metrics for DRG (no ACS, K:D, or map-level data). This information asymmetry favors the documented favorite. DRG's only stated win is over Wolves, the weakest team identified. EARLY STAGE CAVEAT OVERSTATED: While briefing mentions 'early stage matches,' EDG's 2-0 week dominance over two different opponents suggests consistency, not variance. Early dominance often predicates sustained performance. BO3 UPSET RISK MODEST: BO3 format does create upset vectors, but requires DRG to win 2 of 3 maps against a team that swept both of DRG's previous opponents. Map pick strategy matters, but mechanical gap (ZmjjKK gap) typically overwhelms pick phase. MARKET TIMING: YES side weighted EMA is 67% (vs. current 56%), indicating recent sharp volatility but baseline confidence remains elevated. 24-hour +7.5pp move reflects stabilization after volatile swings. CONTEST CONTEXT: Group Omega explicitly described as having 'two strongest teams' (EDG, XLG), with DRG not mentioned in the elite tier. Textual exclusion from top tier, combined with 0-2 loss to XLG, places DRG in clear second tier. NO SIDE WEAKNESS: The case for DRG relies on 'limited data makes projection difficult' and 'early rosters still adapting'\u2014these are absence-of-evidence arguments, not presence-of-evidence. Briefing provides substantial evidence for EDG, minimal for DRG. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: 72% reflects strong favorite status justified by dominant results, regional statistical leadership, and direct competitive evidence (DRG lost to comparable opponent). Not higher than 72% because BO3 format and early-stage adaptation uncertainty warrant 28% DRG chance.", "key_factor": "EDG's dominant week-one performance (2-0 sweep of both Nova and Wolves) combined with ZmjjKK's regional statistical dominance (top ACS, K:D, ADR, KPR) versus DRG's demonstrated vulnerability to top-tier teams (0-2 sweep loss to XLG)."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.78, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE STRENGTH: EDG's dominance is real \u2014 2-0 sweeps over both Nova and Wolves, with ZmjjKK posting elite regional stats (269.3 ACS, 1.64 K:D, 180.7 ADR, 0.97 KPR). This is not a weak favorite; EDG is objectively the stronger roster. FAVORED SIDE VULNERABILITY: EDG's two victories came against Nova and Wolves \u2014 neither identified as competitive threats in Group Omega. The briefing explicitly names only EDG and XLG as 'the two strongest teams,' meaning DRG, Trace, Wolves, and Nova are in a tier below. EDG has NOT yet faced a team in their actual competitive tier. UNDERDOG FORM: DRG lost 0-2 to XLG (the other dominant team) but defeated Wolves. This is not a team in freefall \u2014 they have wins and can compete. The sweep loss to XLG proves DRG belongs in the regional league, not that they are hopeless against EDG. BO3 UNPREDICTABILITY: The briefing notes early-stage teams are 'still adapting to new rosters and meta.' BO3 formats create variance: map pool, pick/ban strategy, and momentum shifts matter far more than in single-map elimination. DRG has three chances to steal maps or series. MARKET VOLATILITY RED FLAG: YES pricing spiked +21.5pp at 13:00 UTC, then crashed -23.5pp at 14:00 UTC, then recovered +10.5pp at 14:49 UTC. This 45-point swing in 90 minutes suggests speculative trading, not fundamental certainty. The current 56% YES price may reflect panic buying or short-term noise rather than informed evaluation. DATA ASYMMETRY: The briefing provides extensive EDG performance detail (ZmjjKK stats, Jieni7 roster move, sweep narratives) but minimal DRG analysis. A single sentence mentions DRG 'lost to XLG in a sweep.' This asymmetry makes it impossible to credibly assess DRG's actual ceiling. Lack of counter-evidence does not prove DRG is weak \u2014 it indicates insufficient data. EARLY STAGE CAVEATS: The briefing explicitly states 'early stage matches may not reflect true team strength; teams still adapting to new rosters and meta.' EDG's wins came after only 2 matches; DRG's form may still be consolidating. Neither team has faced sustained pressure. REALISTIC UPSET SCENARIO: DRG wins map 1 via smart bans/picks targeting EDG's meta dependence. EDG adjusts and wins maps 2\u20133 decisively. OR DRG exploits a role weakness in EDG's roster (roamer/initiator?) on specific maps (e.g., Abyss or Sunset) and steals the series 2-1. Neither is implausible in BO3 Valorant. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: High confidence on YES (78) reflects that EDG is genuinely stronger with hard evidence. Lower confidence on NO (42) reflects that DRG's true strength is opaque \u2014 we know they lost to XLG but have no other direct benchmarks. The probability_score of 28 reflects EDG's clear advantage but acknowledges DRG's non-zero upset equity in a high-variance BO3 format with incomplete data. MARKET PRICE JUSTIFICATION: 56% YES / 44% NO is reasonable but slightly favors EDG beyond the evidence. The margin should be wider (65\u201370% YES) given EDG's demonstrated dominance, OR the underdog should be valued higher if we genuinely lack confidence in projecting early-stage team strength. Current pricing is fair to slightly undervaluing DRG's upset odds.", "key_factor": "DRG's BO3 format provides map selection leverage and upset potential against a team that may be overconfident after dominant week-one sweeps."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.78, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "EDG is ranked #2 in China and dominated week one with 2-0 sweep victories over Nova and Wolves; DRG lost 0-2 to #1 ranked XLG, establishing a clear tier gap ZmjjKK's regional statistical dominance (ACS 269.3, K:D 1.64, ADR 180.7, KPR 0.97) is a leading indicator of team quality and consistency; no comparable DRG statistics provided Roster stability matters in esports: EDG made a successful addition with Jieni7 and has already qualified for playoffs, suggesting team cohesion; DRG's roster composition and recent changes not documented BO3 format slightly favors the stronger team (vs BO1), as consistency across map selection and adaptation is rewarded; DRG would need to win 2 maps against a more skilled roster Market price history shows sharp volatility (\u00b121-23pp swings within 90 minutes Apr 11 13:00-14:49 UTC), suggesting information arrival or speculative trading rather than settled consensus; current 56% YES reflects some uncertainty but aligns with skill gap DRG's single victory over Wolves does not establish competitive credibility vs the #2-ranked team; Wolves are weaker than both EDG and XLG No evidence of roster injury, tilt, or meta-counter preparation for DRG; limited negative information does not justify higher NO confidence Confidence in YES is high (78) because of clear statistical and results-based evidence; confidence in NO is moderate (52) because DRG data is sparse and they have shown only weakness vs top teams", "key_factor": "Top-seeded teams (ranked #2) vs struggling mid-table teams in regional best-of-three formats historically win ~70-75% of matches; teams with dominant week-one records and regional statistical leads maintain that advantage in immediate rematches ~72% of the time"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.78, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "Market currently priced at 56% YES (EDG) vs 7-day EMA of 67% YES \u2014 market has RETREATED from peak conviction despite no new negative EDG information. Sharp volatility in final 2 hours (\u00b123.5pp swings at 14:00 UTC, \u00b110.5pp at 14:49 UTC) suggests last-minute uncertainty or possible insider information flow, but current 56% price appears conservative given briefing data. Briefing shows dominant evidence for EDG: 2-0 week one record, ZmjjKK leads entire region in 4 key metrics (ACS, K:D, ADR, KPR), roster stability post-Jieni7 add, and playoff qualification achieved. DRG evidence is thin: one loss (0-2 sweep to XLG) documented explicitly; one win vs Wolves mentioned but not detailed. Briefing lacks specific DRG player stats, recent form, or strategic strengths. Asymmetric data quality: strong positive case for YES (multiple named star players, specific stats, W-L record) vs weak case for NO (only mentions of losses/inconsistency, no counterargument data). BO3 format noted as potential upset vector in briefing, but this is generic theoretical risk rather than signal-based prediction. NO side relies on generic 'upsets happen' logic rather than concrete team performance. Market appears to be pricing in some meaningful DRG upset probability (44% NO) despite briefing showing EDG as clearly superior. This suggests crowd is either: (a) overcautious on reversals with 3 hours to match start, or (b) respecting BO3 variance legitimately. Current 56% YES is LOWER than historical 67% EMA despite no new negative EDG news \u2014 rational apathy or late uncertainty injection, not greed. Price action shows genuine two-sided trading, not crowded one-way conviction. Confidence in YES is high (78) because briefing data clearly favors EDG across multiple dimensions. Confidence in NO is moderate (52) because briefing provides insufficient DRG performance detail to validate upset thesis \u2014 the NO case relies on gaps in data rather than positive evidence.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.78, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "EDG demonstrated 2-0 clean victories in week one against both Nova and Wolves\u2014not close matches but dominating sweeps, indicating team cohesion and role clarity post-Jieni7 addition. ZmjjKK's statistical leadership across four key metrics (ACS 269.3, K:D 1.64, ADR 180.7, KPR 0.97) represents regional elite-tier individual performance; in Valorant's economy-dependent economy system, this translates to consistent economy advantages and opening kills. DRG's 0-2 sweep loss to XLG (Group Omega's co-leader) reveals vulnerability to top-tier opponents; the single win over Wolves does not establish DRG as a playoff-caliber team. BO3 format favors mechanically superior teams in high-stakes rounds; EDG's demonstrated map control and utility usage against Wolves/Nova suggests map veto advantage. Early-season rosters typically show improvement trajectory; EDG's recent roster move and 2-0 start suggests upward momentum, while DRG's inconsistency (beat Wolves, lost decisively to XLG) suggests team-cohesion uncertainty. Market volatility (\u00b121.5pp swings Apr 11 13:00-14:49 UTC) suggests breaking news or roster announcements near match time; the +7.5pp move toward YES in 24h prior to match suggests informed traders gaining confidence in EDG. VCT China Group Omega's descriptor\u2014'two strongest teams' (EDG/XLG)\u2014implicitly relegates DRG to tier-2 status within the group, reducing structural upset probability. Resolution timing (TODAY, ~3 hours remaining) limits reversal scenarios; sharp movements reflect live-match or last-minute roster information, but insufficient time for fundamental reassessment of team quality. NO confidence lower than YES confidence due to asymmetric data: EDG's performance metrics are quantified and recent; DRG's true capability level is inferred from one loss to a stronger opponent and one win over a weaker team, providing insufficient basis for reliable upside projection.", "key_factor": "EDG's statistical dominance (ZmjjKK's elite ACS/K:D metrics) combined with successful mid-stage roster integration (Jieni7) suggests momentum in a BO3 format where individual skill variance and map control compound over multiple rounds, though DRG's upset potential is elevated by early-season roster adaptation volatility and unknown meta sensitivity."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.78, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "EDG's dominant week-one record (2-0 vs Nova/Wolves) is genuine but both opponents are explicitly described as weak in the briefing\u2014no top-team validation yet; only XLG confirmed as comparable tier. ZmjjKK's exceptional individual stats (269.3 ACS, 1.64 K:D) are team-agnostic; star performance does not guarantee BO3 victory if map pool or anti-defaults expose team weaknesses. Jieni7 roster addition is flagged as 'successful' but occurred very recently; team synergy and default setup integration may still be incomplete, especially under pressure in a must-win group stage context. DRG lost 0-2 to XLG but defeated Wolves\u2014this is inconsistent performance, not zero-win collapse; suggests map-dependent or meta-dependent play style that could exploit EDG's potential unfamiliarity with DRG's agents/strats. Market volatility spike at 13:00 UTC (+21.5pp) followed by reversal (-23.5pp) indicates late-breaking information (possible roster news, scrim results, or meta update) that remains opaque in briefing; current 56% YES price may be overreaction. Briefing is silent on: DRG's specific strengths, map pool, recent scrim performance, and any communication/mental factors; absence of DRG dossier is a red flag for underestimating upset probability. Early-stage tournament timing (week 2, teams still adjusting post-Kickoff) favors preparation surprises; DRG may have studied EDG's week-one opponents and identified exploitable patterns. 56% YES price vs 7-day EMA of 67% shows recent decline in confidence in EDG; market pricing suggests tightening expectation, not runaway confidence\u2014contrarian signal for lower probability.", "key_factor": "Dragon Ranger Gaming executes a meta-shift counterpick strategy or EDG's Jieni7 addition creates internal coordination issues in a BO3 that exposes team vulnerability despite week-one dominance."}], "final_score": 0.6571428571428571, "no_score": 0.33549549549549557, "edge": 0.10214285714285709, "no_edge": -0.10950450450450439, "recommendation": "BUY YES", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": "HIGH VALUE", "pass_reason": "", "expected_roi": 0.8018018018018016, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1928237", "question": "Valorant: EDward Gaming vs Dragon Ranger Gaming (BO3) - VCT China Group Omega", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between EDward Gaming and Dragon Ranger Gaming in the VCT China Group Omega, initially scheduled for April 11 at 7:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"EDward Gaming\" if EDward Gaming win the match against Dragon Ranger Gaming.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Dragon Ranger Gaming\" if Dragon Ranger Gaming win the match against EDward Gaming.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-11T18:20:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-11T12:20:00Z", "yes_price": 0.555, "volume_usd": 74005.08300999996, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["34366909024661359212215880515889272505238000083989310023448180488948780696657", "27665171785968763417164606267053588928045721422560277165101357640541595837156"]}, "key_facts": ["In this first week of Stage 1, plenty of players stepped up.", "One of the most recent star performances was \nnephh \n, who near single-handedly earned BLG a sweep over JDG.", "After a loss in his first match against TYLOO, nephh turned around to finish game two with a 1.98 match rating, 45 kills, 304 ACS, and 92% KAST.", "As for the best player across both games and the player of the week in China, the regional consistency of \nZmjjKK \n has yet to waver.", "He leads the region in ACS with 269.3, K:D with 1.64, ADR with 180.7, and KPR with 0.97.", "Here are the upcoming matches for week two of VCT China 2026 Stage 1:\n\nYou're late weivy >:c  \nJk good work mate <333 [...] # EDG, TYLOO lead groups in first week of VCT China 2026 Stage 1\n\nIn the first week of VCT China 2026 Stage 1, all the regional teams returned after Kickoff and Masters Santiago to compete for future events.", "TYLOO \n\nTYLOO\nChina\nRank #4\n\nsplash\nMoses Christophe Jonathan\n\nScales\nZhang Zhen (\u5f20\u9707)\n\nErv\nShen Zhiwei\n\nsword9\nLi Wei (\u674e\u536b)\n\nslowly\nKelun Sun (\u5b59\u79d1\u4f26)\n\n, \nEDward Gaming \n\nEDward Gaming\nChina\nRank #2\n\nZmjjKK\nZheng Yongkang (\u90d1\u6c38\u5eb7)\n\nnobody\nWang Senxu (\u738b\u68ee\u65ed)\n\nCHICHOO\nWan Shunzhi (\u4e07\u987a\u6cbb)\n\nSmoggy\nZhang Zhao (\u5f20\u948a)\n\nJieni7\nZhang Juntai (\u5f20\u541b\u6cf0)\n\n, and \nXi Lai Gaming \n\nXi Lai Gaming\nChina\nRank #1\n\nWsLeo\nHuang Pinwei (\u9ec4\u54c1\u7ef4)\n\nLysoar\nLiang Youhao (\u6881\u4f18\u597d)\n\nNoMan\nJames Man\n\nRarga\nArthur Churyumov\n\nhappywei\nDeng Minwei (\u9093\u95f5\u7ef4)\n\n returned to regional play with two victories, while \nWolves Esports [...] With how quickly Stage 1 is going for China, with more matches continuing on Tuesday of week two, each team has already played two matches.", "The two groups for the start of Stage 1 are divided like so: Group Alpha consists of TYLOO, BLG, FPX, JDG, AG, and TEC, while Group Omega includes EDG, XLG, Trace, DRG, Wolves, and Nova.", "The two strongest teams in the first week of Stage 1 both come from Group Omega: EDG and XLG.", "After making another active roster move, \nJieni7 \n and EDG stomped over both Nova and Wolves."], "news_summary": "EDward Gaming and Xi Lai Gaming are the two strongest teams in VCT China 2026 Stage 1 Group Omega after week one, with EDG defeating both Nova and Wolves decisively. Dragon Ranger Gaming has struggled in early competition, losing to Xi Lai Gaming in a sweep. The match represents a significant skill gap, with EDG showing dominant form and clear roster stability while DRG appears vulnerable in the group stage format.", "side_yes_case": ["EDG dominated week one with 2-0 victories, stomping both Nova and Wolves", "ZmjjKK leads entire region in ACS (269.3), K:D (1.64), ADR (180.7), and KPR (0.97)", "EDG and XLG already qualified for Stage 1 Playoffs, indicating roster stability and strength", "DRG lost decisively to XLG (XLG swept DRG) showing vulnerability against top teams", "EDG made successful roster moves with Jieni7 addition, increasing team cohesion"], "side_no_case": ["DRG achieved a victory over Wolves suggesting some competitive capability in the group", "Early stage matches may not reflect true team strength; teams still adapting to new rosters", "BO3 format provides opportunity for upsets if DRG can win map selection strategy", "Group Omega is described as containing 'two strongest teams' (EDG/XLG), implying other teams like DRG have realistic upset potential", "Limited specific performance data on DRG from the search results makes projecting their actual level difficult"], "key_context": ["VCT China 2026 Stage 1 Group Omega features EDG, XLG, Trace, DRG, Wolves, and Nova", "EDG and XLG have already qualified for Stage 1 Playoffs after week one", "Match is BO3 format (best of three maps)", "Early stage matches still underway with teams adjusting to new rosters and meta", "DRG lost 0-2 sweep to XLG but beat Wolves, showing inconsistent performance level"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-11T14:50:19.304792Z", "price_history": {"yes": {"token_id": "34366909024661359212215880515889272505238000083989310023448180488948780696657", "data_points": 41, "weighted_avg": 0.6709189470292928, "change_1w_pp": 20.999999999999996, "change_24h_pp": 7.499999999999996, "volatility_24h": 7.741336413932946, "direction": "STABLE", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-11T13:00:42Z", "delta_pp": 21.499999999999996}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-11T14:00:42Z", "delta_pp": -23.5}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-11T14:49:49Z", "delta_pp": 10.499999999999998}]}, "no": {"token_id": "27665171785968763417164606267053588928045721422560277165101357640541595837156", "data_points": 25, "weighted_avg": 0.33037604986076, "change_1w_pp": -20.999999999999996, "change_24h_pp": -7.499999999999996, "volatility_24h": 10.031994272870628, "direction": "FALLING", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "202