The 7-day weighted average shows YES at only 41% until the massive +36pp move 10 minutes before briefing timestamp. This suggests either: (a) the match started and NAVI Junior took an early advantage, or (b) breaking news/roster information emerged. Either way, the market repricing reflects recent information not fully captured in the briefing's static data. BO3 FORMAT & GROUP STAGE: Single match in group stage is high-variance, but NAVI's documented experience and organizational backing provide marginal edge over an unknown opponent. RESOLUTION RISK (SECONDARY): Criteria are clear \u2014 first team to win the match wins the market. No forfeit/walkover has been mentioned. VLR.gg resolution source is standard for Valorant. Minimal mechanism risk. PROBABILITY ASSESSMENT: The late market surge (74% YES) aligns with NAVI Junior's structural advantages and near-zero data on Lost Puppies. However, lack of real-time match data prevents ultra-high confidence. A 72% probability acknowledges NAVI's edge while respecting the missing information on Lost Puppies' actual strength. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: confidence_yes = 62 (good data on NAVI, organizational advantage, late market move supports YES) but tempered by uncertainty about whether the late move reflects actual match advantage or speculative betting. confidence_no = 48 (almost no data on Lost Puppies; cannot assess their true capability; this side is under-informed in the briefing).", "key_factor": "Insufficient performance data on Lost Puppies prevents full confidence in either outcome; market may be reacting to real-time information (match may be live or just concluded at briefing time 14:50 UTC)."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.71, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "MARKET MOMENTUM IS REAL: YES rose +44pp over 7 days and +34.5pp in 24 hours, culminating in a massive +36pp surge at 14:50 UTC (just 2+ hours before 19:00 UTC match start). This timing suggests late-arriving informa