{"run_id": "c8940532-c3d6-40ca-b546-865dcaea0dad", "timestamp": "2026-04-11T14:52:20.055707+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1914567", "question": "Valorant: UNIWAY vs EVOPLAY (BO3) - VCL NORTH//EAST Group B", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between UNIWAY and EVOPLAY in the VCL NORTH//EAST Group B, initially scheduled for April 11 at 9:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"UNIWAY\" if UNIWAY win the match against EVOPLAY.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"EVOPLAY\" if EVOPLAY win the match against UNIWAY.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-11T19:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-11T13:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.17, "volume_usd": 2652.0941480000006, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["30393971398643434270410705966409148849729889580241095099813414143982508581182", "63361979686974251386857497546284980098505682147523496425761572395996348022157"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.22, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: UNIWAY must win the BO3 match to resolve YES. Current market prices (17% YES / 83% NO) imply strong market belief in EVOPLAY victory. RECENT FORM: UNIWAY shows mixed results in group stage (1-2 loss in Round 1, 2-0 win in Round 2). EVOPLAY's documented result is 2-0 win vs XtremeDogs. Both teams qualified for Stage 2, but EVOPLAY's full record is not provided. MARKET VOLATILITY SIGNAL: Sharp moves in past 2 hours (-7pp YES at 14:51 UTC, +17.5pp NO at 14:51 UTC) indicate late-breaking information about match status, team status, or recent developments not captured in briefing data. This volatility immediately before a LIVE event suggests market participants have information suggesting EVOPLAY is now favored more strongly. TIMING: Match scheduled for April 11, 9:00 AM ET. Briefing timestamp is 2026-04-11 14:52 UTC (~4 hours from resolution). The match should be starting or underway. The sharp downward move on YES side in final hour is consistent with market adjustment to match being underway or near-certain information about EVOPLAY's performance. DATA GAPS: Limited performance data for EVOPLAY (only one documented match result). Cannot assess full roster strength, head-to-head tactical matchups, or EVOPLAY's tier within Group B. UNIWAY's recent upward trajectory (qualifier results + 2-0 Round 2) is positive but Round 1 loss shows inconsistency. INFERENCE FROM MARKET: The 83% NO price, combined with late sharp moves favoring NO, suggests market has observed match-related information (possibly early game results, or team roster/status confirmation) pointing to EVOPLAY. In LIVE/IMMINENT events, such late moves carry high signal weight. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Higher confidence in NO (~42%) than YES (~35%) because: (1) market has recent signal via sharp moves; (2) EVOPLAY demonstrated 2-0 capability; (3) UNIWAY showed Round 1 inconsistency. Lower YES confidence due to lack of detailed EVOPLAY performance history and inability to verify what specific market signal triggered the 14:51 UTC moves. NO EVIDENCE OF CANCELLATION/FORFEIT: No briefing evidence of match cancellation, forfeit, or walkover. Assuming match is being played legitimately for scoring purposes.", "key_factor": "Match is LIVE/IMMINENT (resolves in ~4 hours); sharp price movement in last 2 hours (-7pp at 14:51 UTC, +17.5pp NO side) suggests market has very recent information about match status or team performance that is not reflected in the briefing document."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.22, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "EVOPLAY is heavily favored at 83% (NO), reflecting market consensus that EVOPLAY will win this BO3 match. EVOPLAY's Round 1 result: 2-0 victory vs XtremeDogs demonstrates offensive firepower and map control in Group B\u2014a direct measure of competitive strength within this specific tournament context. UNIWAY's recent form is mixed: Round 1 loss (1-2) followed by Round 2 win (2-0). The loss to a Group B opponent in Round 1 is a significant weakness that undermines their credibility as favorites. UNIWAY's qualifier wins (vs FB2, WLG, DIE) occurred before the group stage and may not translate to current form against tournament-hardened opponents like EVOPLAY. Head-to-head record is 0-0; no prior matchup data exists. The market's 83% confidence in EVOPLAY likely reflects recent tournament performance (2-0 win) versus UNIWAY's inconsistency (1-2 loss in the same round). EVOPLAY's single documented tournament result is unambiguously stronger than UNIWAY's mixed 1-2, 2-0 sequence. In a BO3 with limited data, a 2-0 win is more decisive evidence than a split record. UNIWAY's 2-0 win vs FB2 (with exie's 384 ACS) is positive momentum, but it came AFTER their Round 1 loss\u2014suggesting inconsistency under pressure rather than peak form. Low overall data availability for both teams increases uncertainty, but EVOPLAY's tournament win is concrete evidence; UNIWAY's qualifier wins are pre-tournament and less relevant. Market sharp moves in last 24 hours show NO gaining +17.5pp at 14:51 UTC (4 hours before match), suggesting late-arriving information or professional action favoring EVOPLAY. YES side experienced volatile swings (-41.0pp at 14:00 UTC), indicating weak conviction in UNIWAY support; NO side shows stable, rising trend (+34.5pp over 7 days), suggesting sustained confidence in EVOPLAY. For YES (UNIWAY) to win, they must overcome: (1) their own Round 1 tournament loss, (2) EVOPLAY's demonstrated 2-0 dominance in the same tournament, and (3) a 66-point market deficit with only 4 hours to reversal\u2014an implausible scenario. Underdog scenario (UNIWAY wins) would require UNIWAY to have significantly improved from their 1-2 loss in just one match cycle, contradicting the typical consistency of competitive Valorant teams. EVOPLAY's weaker data footprint (limited match history shown) is a minor weakness, but their 2-0 result outweighs uncertainty. UNIWAY's explicit 1-2 loss is more damaging than unknown attributes. Confidence in NO is high (72%) because EVOPLAY's tournament result is unambiguous; confidence in YES is lower (35%) due to UNIWAY's clear Round 1 failure and limited contrarian evidence.", "key_factor": "EVOPLAY's dominant 2-0 victory in Round 1 against Group B competition combined with UNIWAY's Round 1 loss (1-2) establishes EVOPLAY as the stronger early-stage performer in this competition."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "UNIWAY MOMENTUM: Recent 2-0 victory over FB2 (Round 2) with exie posting 384 ACS represents sharp upward trajectory after Round 1 loss. Suggests team adjusted mid-tournament; BO3 format rewards adaptation. QUALIFIER PEDIGREE: UNIWAY's Stage 2 Qualifier performance (2-0, 2-1, 2-0 record) demonstrates consistent ability to win series against qualifying opposition. Qualifier opponents may have included stronger talent than FB2. EVOPLAY OPACITY: Only one documented match result (2-0 vs XtremeDogs, Round 1). XtremeDogs also lost 0-2 to TL.A in Round 2, suggesting XtremeDogs may be bottom-tier opponent. EVOPLAY's true competitive level is unclear; single win insufficient baseline. HEAD-TO-HEAD VOID: No prior matches between teams means no exploitable patterns; both teams enter as unknowns to each other. Early-stage BO3s often go to teams with superior adaptation mid-series. MARKET OVERCONFIDENCE ON NO: 83% price on EVOPLAY rests heavily on a single 2-0 win against a team that went 0-4 in two documented matches. Market may have conflated one result with tier dominance. UNIWAY'S ROUND 1 LOSS CONTEXT: 1-2 loss to unnamed opponent is concerning but does NOT indicate weakness if opponent is higher seed. In 8-team round-robin, placement varies; UNIWAY rebounded sharply. VOLATILITY SPIKE: Price history shows +30.5pp YES swing at Apr 11 13:00 UTC, then -41.0pp crash at 14:00 UTC. Sharp reversal suggests information release (possibly unfavorable to UNIWAY, e.g., roster update, illness) or algorithmic selling. Current 17% likely overshoots true edge. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: NO side data (EVOPLAY's single 2-0 win) is thinner than YES side data (UNIWAY's recent 2-0 plus qualifier record). Confidence_no set to 72 (not higher) due to EVOPLAY's minimal sample size and XtremeDogs' demonstrated weakness. TIMING PRESSURE: Event TODAY, resolving in ~4 hours. Market prices reflect real-money betting pressure; late-day sharp move to NO (-41pp at 14:00) may signal informed action BUT may also reflect panic or line-movement cascade rather than fundamental edge. OUTCOME EDGE: If EVOPLAY is genuinely stronger, 83% is reasonable. If EVOPLAY is roughly equal tier and merely benefited from weaker Round 1 opponent, YES at 17% is underpriced. Briefing data insufficient to distinguish; bet YES only if accepting high variance. VERDICT: UNIWAY remains underdog but not hopelessly so. Recent form trajectory, qualifier credentials, and EVOPLAY's minimal evidence base suggest 28% is fair; market's 17% implies ~3:1 EVOPLAY edge, which rests on thinner data than UNIWAY's. Confidence_no capped at 72 due to EVOPLAY opacity.", "key_factor": "UNIWAY's momentum surge from Round 1 loss (1-2) to Round 2 dominant victory (2-0) shows adaptive capability and potential to exploit EVOPLAY's limited tournament visibility."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.22, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "MARKET STRUCTURE: Current YES price (17%) is significantly lower than the 50% theoretical base rate for a head-to-head match with no prior history. RECENT FORM ASYMMETRY: UNIWAY shows momentum (1-2 loss then 2-0 win in consecutive rounds) vs EVOPLAY with only one documented result (2-0 vs XtremeDogs). Upward trajectory favors YES, but trajectory sample is minimal (n=2 recent matches). OPPONENT QUALITY UNKNOWN: XtremeDogs (EVOPLAY's opponent) has not been characterized in tier/strength data provided. Cannot assess whether EVOPLAY's 2-0 was dominant against weak competition or strong competition. QUALITATIVE PERFORMANCE: UNIWAY's Round 2 win featured high ACS (384) suggesting individual player execution; however Round 1 loss (1-2) demonstrates vulnerability to Group B competition in same stage. CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing provides no roster strength comparison, coaching reputation, map pool analysis, agent meta alignment, or player-level matchups. This severely limits predictive confidence on both sides. MARKET VOLATILITY SIGNAL: Sharp 41pp swing on YES side (Apr 11 14:00 UTC) followed by 7pp reversion suggests recent information (likely team announcement, scrim results, or odds cascade) rather than stable fundamental shift. High volatility (19.6pp/hr YES vs 7.0pp/hr NO) indicates low confidence among traders. TIMING CONTEXT: Event is TODAY (~4 hours remaining). Lack of consensus convergence to 1-2% or 98-99% suggests no definitive public information (roster changes, withdrawals, forfeits) has emerged; match is expected to proceed. BASE RATE CALIBRATION: Without head-to-head history and minimal team performance data, true probability should trend toward 50%. Market price of 17% reflects market belief in EVOPLAY edge, but edge magnitude cannot be validated from briefing. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFICATION: confidence_yes (28) > confidence_no (35) because UNIWAY's recent 2-0 win is documented fact; confidence_no capped at 35 (not higher) because EVOPLAY's full record and opponent context are opaque. PROBABILITY ANCHOR: Set to 22 (below market 17%) to reflect base-rate regression toward 50% given data scarcity, while acknowledging UNIWAY's recent upward form provides slight edge over true coin flip. Market may have overweighted EVOPLAY's single documented win.", "key_factor": "VCL stage group matches are typically ~55-60% predictable based on pre-match seeding/qualification strength; BO3 formats reduce variance slightly. Head-to-head matchups with no prior history default to ~50% base rate absent significant roster/performance differentiators."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.22, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "Market price (17% YES / 83% NO) reflects strong conviction that EVOPLAY will win, but briefing provides asymmetric evidence. UNIWAY's trajectory is improving: lost R1 (1-2) but dominated R2 (2-0 vs FB2) with standout individual performance (384 ACS from exie). EVOPLAY's single documented result is a 2-0 win, but against XtremeDogs\u2014which itself lost 0-2 to TL.A in R2, suggesting XtremeDogs may be bottom-tier in the group. No head-to-head history between teams; predictive confidence is structurally limited for both sides despite market certainty. UNIWAY's qualifier results (2-0, 2-1, 2-0) suggest capability to beat mid-tier opponents; current 17% odds imply near-certain EVOPLAY dominance, which is not supported by available data. Extreme 24-hour volatility on YES side (-21.0pp, sharp moves +30.5pp then -41.0pp) suggests emotional trading and forced liquidations, not fundamental re-evaluation. NO side shows shallow rise (+21.0pp, 7.0pp/hr volatility) with less conviction intensity than YES panic, suggesting crowded fear trade rather than rational conviction. Market appears to have overweighted EVOPLAY's single result and underweighted UNIWAY's recent momentum and stronger qualifier pedigree. For LIVE/IMMINENT event: with ~4 hours to match, sharp price movements and extreme volatility indicate retail/emotional positioning rather than information-driven repricing. Rational apathy detected: briefing shows no definitive skill gap or roster data; market pricing 83% NO as if one team is clearly superior, contradicting limited sample evidence.", "key_factor": "Fear"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.22, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "LIVE EVENT: Match resolves in ~4 hours; market volatility (\u00b141pp swings in last 24h) reflects real-time in-game updates or roster/map announcements; final sharp moves at 14:51 UTC (+17.5pp NO, -7.0pp YES) suggest late information favoring EVOPLAY. MARKET SIGNAL: NO side (83%) is substantially overweighted vs. YES (17%), but EMA-weighted history shows YES collapsed from 37% \u2192 17% (24h: -21pp), while NO climbed 64% \u2190 43% (24h: +21pp). This directional shift mid-tournament is significant. FORM ANALYSIS: UNIWAY 1-2, then 2-0 is a micro-rebound; two matches insufficient for trend confirmation in BO3 round-robin. Qualifier results (March 22-28) are 2-3 weeks old and involve different team composition/meta. EVOPLAY OPAQUITY: Only one documented result (2-0 vs. XtremeDogs). No qualifier history, player ACS stats, or agent composition data in briefing. This asymmetric information transparency is Valorant-specific: tier-2 EU orgs often have unpredictable roster depth. HEAD-TO-HEAD: Zero prior matchups; no veto history, map pool, or stylistic comparison available. In BO3 Valorant, map bans can swing 30-40% winrate depending on team's map pool strength\u2014entirely unknown here. AGENT META & AGENT POOL: Briefing shows agent names (Viper, Omen, Neon, Skye, Chamber, Killjoy, Harbor) but no pick/ban discipline data. Valorant meta shifts month-to-month; if patch changes occurred between qualifier (March) and April 11, historical data is stale. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong confidence in EVOPLAY's upside (confidence_no = 42) is tempered by limited sample; strong confidence in UNIWAY's downside (recent loss, qualifier vulnerabilities) only justified if Round 1 loss is predictive (confidence_yes = 35, not higher). MARKET PRICING CONTRADICTION: 17% YES / 83% NO implies EVOPLAY is ~5:1 favorite. The briefing's 'news summary' is neutral-to-slightly-bullish on UNIWAY (qualifier wins, Round 2 victory), yet market decisively favors NO. This suggests either: (1) real-time information (roster news, scrim results, map draws) has leaked post-briefing compilation, or (2) EVOPLAY's 2-0 win had higher ACS/round differentials than briefing conveys. RESOLUTION RISK: If match is delayed >7 days, resolves 50-50; if forfeit before start, also 50-50. Given VCL NORTH//EAST operational history and April 11 scheduled time, on-time completion is highly likely, but adds 1-2% floor to both sides' edge. INFERENCE: Late-game market moves (14:51 UTC +17.5pp NO, -7.0pp YES) in LIVE context suggests insiders saw map draw, roster confirmations, or scrim leaks favoring EVOPLAY. Respect this signal: 22% YES reflects UNIWAY's upside (recent form, qualifier credentials) offset by EVOPLAY's apparent operational advantage and market's 5:1 conviction.", "key_factor": "UNIWAY's recent 2-0 victory shows map-control execution capability, but their 1-2 loss in Round 1 and qualifier-era close-call (12-14 scoreline) reveal fragility under pressure; EVOPLAY's 2-0 dominance over XtremeDogs is more strategically opaque without agent ban/pick data."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.22, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "UNIWAY's recent 2-0 vs FB2 is inflated by recency bias\u2014they lost their Round 1 match 1-2, showing early-stage inconsistency and potential mid-series collapse patterns. EVOPLAY's 2-0 victory over XtremeDogs is the ONLY documented Group B performance available; the briefing provides zero stat lines, ACS data, or map-specific results for EVOPLAY, making their true competitive tier completely opaque. The briefing is conspicuously silent on EVOPLAY's full roster strength, recent form trajectory, and individual player performance\u2014this absence of counter-evidence is a major red flag for underestimating them. UNIWAY's Qualifier run (2-0, 2-1, 2-0) predates the actual Group Stage by 1+ week; Stage 2 meta, patch shifts, or anti-strat adjustments by Group B teams may have leveled the playing field since then. No head-to-head history exists; EVOPLAY has not faced UNIWAY before and may exploit unfamiliar map bans, agent compositions, or playstyle mismatches that UNIWAY's recent opponents (FB2, VR2) did not. Market volatility is extreme (+30.5pp spike Apr 11 13:00, then -41.0pp crash 14:00, then +17.5pp at 14:51)\u2014this suggests late information (roster updates, coach decisions, injury/illness reports) is moving odds away from the consensus 37% EMA baseline; the NO side ralli