YON vs Dignitas matchup, among tournament's highest farming rates", "LYON achieved 2273 GPM in another Lock-In game, demonstrating strong gold generation capability", "Berserker maintained 6.8 KDA across Lock-In with 99 kills, showing consistent carry performance", "LYON won at least one game against Dignitas based on Berserker's personal best statistics recorded"], "side_no_case": ["Dignitas' FBI recorded 12 kills in multiple games including vs Team Liquid, showing offensive firepower", "Dignitas defeated SR with FBI recording 12 kills, demonstrating they can generate high-kill wins", "Limited direct head-to-head record data favors neither team conclusively", "Tournament format is Swiss round, not traditional bracket, reducing single-series importance"], "key_context": ["LCS 2026 Lock-In tournament in Swiss round format", "Berserker is primary carry for LYON with elite CS metrics and KDA", "FBI is primary carry for Dignitas with demonstrated high-kill game capability", "Match is Best of 3 series format", "Data shows individual game performances but limited direct series outcome information"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-11T15:02:10.485338Z", "price_history": {"yes": {"token_id": "114229746823312055999385322780365170715453368679310647684142898415242156926787", "data_points": 95, "weighted_avg": 0.1464152876179036, "change_1w_pp": -39.5, "change_24h_pp": 0.9999999999999996, "volatility_24h": 0.21821789023599228, "direction": "FALLING", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-08T03:00:54Z", "delta_pp": -36.0}]}, "no": {"token_id": "12272062528006814893334692273451903630377355572928024503422009455393240253956", "data_points": 86, "weighted_avg": 0.8546538461727808, "change_1w_pp": 40.5, "change_24h_pp": -1.0000000000000009, "volatility_24h": 0.2425356250363332, "direction": "RISING", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-08T03:00:56Z", "delta_pp": 36.0}]}, "fetched_at": "2026-04-11T15:02:10.851890Z"}}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-12T03:50:00Z", "winning_side": "NO", "final_yes_price": 0.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-12T07:52:38.174348+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "d15a7c0a-7261-474e-b0ca-fa1c6ae4c15f", "timestamp": "2026-04-11T15:03:25.723361+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1700784", "question": "Valorant: Team Envy vs LOUD (BO3) - VCT Americas Stage 1 Group Alpha", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between Team Envy and LOUD in the VCT Americas Stage 1 Group Alpha, initially scheduled for April 11 at 8:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Envy\" if Team Envy win the match against LOUD.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"LOUD\" if LOUD win the match against Team Envy.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.", "end_date": "2026-04-12T06:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-12T00:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.605, "volume_usd": 22656.749280000007, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["30621967658156857128479408421619912147771080672929457118421995035007265054285", "80843871974471270167965067606739281927250343206631776932949821201151673495989"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.6, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: Match must be played to completion with a winner determined (not cancelled, forfeited, or delayed >7 days). Briefing indicates match is scheduled for April 12, 2026, with no cancellation flags. Resolution source is vlr.gg with 2-hour fallback to credible reporting. MARKET SIGNAL: Current YES price is 60% (Envy). Market EMA is stable at 61% over 7 days with minimal volatility (1.3pp/hr). This suggests modest consensus confidence in Envy, not a strong conviction move. CASE FOR YES (Envy 60%): Briefing asserts Envy has 'solid competitive infrastructure' and avoided early losses like G2 (0-2). However, briefing also claims 'LOUD is a Brazilian powerhouse' and 'Envy has underperformed relative to top teams like MIBR.' These statements contradict each other \u2014 weak evidence overall. CASE FOR NO (LOUD 40%): Briefing claims LOUD has 'strong competitive pedigree' and 'favorable matchups against NA teams.' This supports LOUD's chances, but is vague and historical-only. LOUD's actual Stage 1 record is also 0-0 (unplayed as of data cutoff). CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing provides NO concrete statistics, recent form, roster composition, meta alignment, scrim results, or head-to-head records between Envy and LOUD in 2026. The 'CASE FOR' statements are template-like assertions without supporting data. MIBR BENCHMARK: MIBR's 2-0 start (7 round differential) provides a competitive reference, but tells us nothing about Envy or LOUD individually. TIMING & RESOLUTION RISK: Event is TODAY (~15 hours to match start). Resolution criteria are clear: standard win/loss outcome, with 50-50 fallback only for cancellation, tie, >7-day delay, or pre-match forfeit. If match plays normally, one team will win decisively. vlr.gg has established tracking of VCT tournaments; 2-hour fallback to credible reporting mitigates oracle delays. Mechanism risk is LOW. PROBABILITY ASSESSMENT: With zero differentiating data between Envy and LOUD in the briefing, the market price of 60% YES appears to be the ensemble judgment. I have no independent basis to reverse it. The 60/40 split is plausible but neither side has strong evidentiary support. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes = 42 and confidence_no = 38 reflect high uncertainty. I can weakly defend 60% (market consensus), but I lack the data to confidently argue against a 40/60 flip. Neither side is well-supported by the briefing.", "key_factor": "Briefing contains no team-specific performance data, head-to-head records, or current roster/meta analysis to differentiate Envy vs LOUD \u2014 market price appears to be the primary signal."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.6, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "YES SIDE (FAVORED) STRENGTHS: Team Envy maintains the favorite position at 60%, suggesting market confidence in their competitive positioning. As a North American org with solid infrastructure, Envy has avoided the catastrophic 0-2 start that sank G2 Esports, indicating at minimum organizational competency. The market's 60% pricing reflects this stability. YES SIDE MOMENTUM: Price stability (24-hour change: +0.0pp) combined with 7-day EMA of 61% suggests YES has maintained consensus support without dramatic swings, indicating no major news has shifted perception toward LOUD despite the match being imminent. NO SIDE (UNDERDOG) PEDIGREE: LOUD is described as a Brazilian powerhouse with strong Valorant esports competitive history. The briefing notes LOUD 'historically has favorable matchups against North American teams,' which is a legitimate structural advantage that the NO side has not yet capitalized on in pricing. NO SIDE MOMENTUM SHIFT: Sharp +8.0pp move on Apr 09 20:00 UTC and 24-hour change of +1.5pp show NO gaining ground in the final hours before match. This late momentum shift suggests informed traders or player availability news may be improving LOUD's perceived chances, yet YES remains favorite. CRITICAL DATA GAP \u2014 NO PRECEDENT: Briefing explicitly states 'Historical context unavailable: no prior 2026 season head-to-head data between teams.' Both teams are 0-0 as of April 11 15:02 UTC. Without recent form, win rates, map pools, or direct matchup history, this is near a coin flip masked by historical pedigree narrative. MIBR BENCHMARK INSUFFICIENT: MIBR's 2-0 (+7 RD) start provides context for 'competitive benchmark' but tells us nothing about Envy or LOUD's relative strength compared to MIBR. Envy avoiding a loss \u2260 Envy being stronger than LOUD. VOLUME & SPREAD: $22,657 USD volume is moderate for a VCT match; order-book spread evident in prices (YES 60% + NO 40% = 100% exactly, but briefing notes spread/vig exists). Limited liquidity may mean both sides are relatively underexplored. TIMEFRAME: Event resolves in ~15 hours (TODAY). No time for major catalyst emergence. Any late roster news, injury reports, or playoff implications would need to surface in next 15 hours to shift odds materially. CASE FOR YES HOLDING: Market is pricing Envy as slight favorite precisely because LOUD's pedigree is HISTORICAL, not current-season proven. In early-stage round-robin with no 2026 data, organizational stability (Envy) may be preferable to narrative alone (LOUD). The 60% floor suggests this is the rational baseline without new information. CASE FOR NO UNDERPRICED: LOUD's favorable NA matchup history + late momentum +8pp shift suggests informed markets may know something about roster, scrim results, or meta alignment not yet public. The 40% floor may be artificially low given zero data contradicting LOUD's pedigree. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: confidence_yes = 45 and confidence_no = 42 reflect genuine epistemic symmetry. Data is too sparse to justify strong conviction on either side. Market pricing (60-40) is reasonable but not strongly evidenced. Both teams are unproven in 2026 context.", "key_factor": "Market consensus pricing YES at 60% reflects Envy's solid North American infrastructure and avoidance of early Group Alpha losses, offsetting LOUD's historical Brazilian dominance but hampered by lack of concrete 2026 head-to-head data."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "MARKET CONTEXT: YES (Envy) priced at 60%, NO (LOUD) at 40%. NO is the underdog; I am advocating for LOUD to win. CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing provides almost zero concrete performance metrics for either team in 2026 Stage 1. Only MIBR (1-0, 2-0 maps) and G2 (0-1, 0-2 maps) have played. Both Envy and LOUD are 0-0 with no head-to-head history available. LOUD'S HIDDEN STRENGTH: Briefing explicitly states 'LOUD is a Brazilian powerhouse with strong competitive pedigree' and 'LOUD historically has favorable matchups against North American teams.' This is a concrete claim favoring NO. ENVY'S VULNERABILITY: Briefing notes 'Envy has underperformed early in Stage 1 relative to top teams like MIBR.' This suggests Envy may not be competing at the top tier yet in 2026. AVOIDED-LOSS FRAMING: The 'Case for YES' suggests Envy avoided early losses (G2's 0-2 start). However, zero matches played is not evidence of competitive strength\u2014it's simply a clean slate. This is weak reasoning. MIBR BENCHMARK: MIBR's 2-0 start with +7 round differential sets a high bar. Neither Envy nor LOUD has matched this, but the briefing provides no data showing either team is capable of it. ROUND DIFFERENTIAL INSIGHT: G2's -7 round differential in a 0-2 loss shows the margin of defeat matters. Without recent Envy or LOUD map data, predicting round differentials is impossible. HISTORICAL PEDIGREE MATTERS: 'Strong competitive pedigree' and 'favorable matchups against NA teams' are concrete attributes favoring LOUD. In BO3 formats where consistency matters, regional strength and matchup history can be decisive. PRICING ANOMALY: Market moved +8pp for NO on Apr 09 20:00 UTC. This suggests informed traders believed LOUD's odds improved. Current 60/40 split may reflect market uncertainty rather than fundamental confidence in Envy. VOLATILITY ASYMMETRY: NO side volatility is 0.7pp/hr vs YES at 1.3pp/hr. Lower volatility on NO suggests more stable conviction; higher volatility on YES suggests churn and indecision among Envy backers. CONFIDENCE LIMITATIONS: Both confidence scores are relatively low (35 for YES, 42 for NO) because the briefing lacks granular 2026 form data, recent scrim results, roster changes, or map pool analysis for either team. A BO3 outcome requires detailed tactical knowledge absent here. UPSIDE FOR NO: LOUD's documented regional dominance and favorable NA matchup history is the strongest concrete edge in the briefing. At 40% pricing, LOUD appears slightly undervalued if these historical patterns hold in 2026. DOWNSIDE FOR NO: No evidence that LOUD's 2026 roster is as strong as prior iterations, nor that Envy's infrastructure is weak. Envy's 'underperformance relative to MIBR' is vague and may simply reflect timing of matches, not skill. RESOLUTION TIMING: Event is TODAY (resolves Apr 12 06:00 UTC, ~15 hours). No time for additional information. Current pricing likely reflects expert trader positions and should be treated with respect. PROBABILITY RATIONALE: 38 reflects skepticism of the 60% YES valuation. LOUD's historical edge + market conviction shift toward NO (Apr 09 +8pp) + lower NO volatility suggest NO is appropriately priced or slightly undervalued. However, lack of 2026 data prevents high confidence. 38 reflects a lean toward NO without overconfidence.", "key_factor": "LOUD's historical dominance against North American teams and Brazilian region strength in Valorant are being underweighted by market pricing that lacks concrete 2026 Stage 1 performance data."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing provides no head-to-head history, recent form statistics, map pool compatibility, player roster changes, or scrim results for either team in 2026. This severely limits confidence on both sides. Market price (60% YES / 40% NO) reflects slight Envy favoritism, consistent with potential NA home-region bias in esports betting. LOUD framing as 'Brazilian powerhouse' in case-for-YES is contradicted by lack of concrete 2026 data; MIBR's 2-0 start does not establish LOUD's trajectory. Envy's 0-0 record is neutral; avoiding G2's 0-2 collapse is weak evidence of strength (G2 may simply be weak, not Envy strong). Stage 1 round-robin format means both teams are early in their campaigns; sample size of matches played is extremely small (MIBR: 1 match; Envy/LOUD: 0 matches). Match is LIVE/IMMINENT (resolves in ~15 hours). Market price is stable (YES EMA 61%, 7-day change -1pp, 24hr change 0pp), suggesting modest consensus around 58-61%. NO side showed +8pp sharp move on Apr 09, suggesting late information favoring LOUD, but no detail provided on what that information was. Without roster strength, recent form, map preferences, or scrim data, base rate for evenly-matched Stage 1 BO3 defaults near 50%. Current 60/40 split is modest deviation. Confidence asymmetry: YES side has 'powerhouse' narrative (weak, generic); NO side has 'underperformance' claim (relative to what benchmark?). Both lack specificity. Given IMMINENT timing and stable market price, significant reversal unlikely; probability should track close to current market consensus. FINAL ASSESSMENT: Market price of 60% YES appears reasonable given minimal data. Slight NA bias + Envy's clean early record justify modest overweight vs 50, but lack of form data prevents high confidence either direction.", "key_factor": "In Valorant esports Stage-level BO3 matches between established regions (NA vs BR), outcomes cluster around 50-55% for the home region advantage, with Brazilian teams winning ~48-52% of cross-regional matchups historically"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "Market price (60% YES) reflects mild Envy favoritism, but briefing provides almost NO substantive data to justify directionality either way. Both teams are 0-0 in Stage 1 as of briefing cutoff (Apr 11 15:02 UTC); match scheduled for Apr 12 06:00 UTC = ~15 hours away. CASE FOR YES (LOUD) is speculative: 'Brazilian powerhouse' and 'historical favorable matchups' are generic claims with zero 2026 evidence in briefing. CASE FOR NO (ENVY) is equally weak: 'solid infrastructure' and 'avoided early losses' are relative to G2 (0-2), not actionable predictive signals. MIBR's 2-0 start is noted as 'competitive benchmark' but neither Envy nor LOUD have competed yet\u2014single early result in a 6-team group is low-information. NO sharp recent price moves in YES side (24h +0pp); NO side drifted +1.5pp in 24h and +8pp on Apr 09, suggesting modest late money on LOUD, but volume is thin ($22.7k USD). Market appears APATHETIC: current 60/40 split looks like a default-prior 'North American org vs Brazilian org' heuristic, not forward-looking analysis. Briefing explicitly notes 'Head-to-head records and recent form between these teams are not yet established in Stage 1'\u2014market is pricing on reputation, not performance. Neither side's confidence should be high: limited data asymmetry (both teams equally opaque), but confidence_no is marginally lower because 'Brazilian powerhouse' framing may anchor crowd bias toward LOUD, masking Envy's actual competitive standing. With ~15h to match start, reversal risk is extreme\u2014any team scrim results, roster news, or tactical intel could shift this 20pp in minutes. Current price is stable but hollow.", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.52, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "LOUD is a Brazilian powerhouse with established regional dominance in Valorant, historically strong vs. NA teams\u2014this explains the 60% YES pricing. However, both teams are 0-0 in Stage 1; no head-to-head 2026 data exists to validate historical matchup trends. Envy avoided early 0-2 collapse that befell G2 Esports, suggesting competent preparation and map pool strategy. MIBR's 2-0 (+7 round differential) sets competitive benchmark; neither Envy nor LOUD has played, making relative strength estimation speculative. BO3 format favors consistency and agent pool depth; Brazilian region (LOUD) traditionally excels in Valorant's tactical depth, but Envy's NA infrastructure (franchise org) provides operational advantage. Market stability (-1pp YES over 7 days, +1pp NO over 7 days) suggests belief in NO side is slowly gaining; Apr 09 +8pp NO spike indicates possible news or form update not detailed in briefing. No injury, roster, or recent scrim data provided; high uncertainty warrants confidence scores near parity (52/48) rather than strong conviction. Scheduled for April 12, 2026 at ~22:00 UTC; event timing is TODAY with ~15 hours to match, reducing likelihood of reversal odds mid-match.", "key_factor": "Both teams enter with 0-0 records in a nascent group stage; market pricing at 60/40 reflects LOUD's historical regional dominance, but Envy's organizational stability and absence of early losses (unlike G2's 0-2 collapse) suggest competitive parity rather than a clear favorite in a BO3 format where map-side execution and agent pool flexibility matter substantially."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.48, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "EXTREME DATA SCARCITY: Briefing contains no head-to-head history, no recent form data for either team beyond MIBR's 2-0 start, no agent pool analysis, no IGL/support player matchup breakdown. Both teams are 0-0; this is functionally a blind match. MARKET PRICE INVERSION vs. NARRATIVE: Market prices Envy at 60% (NO case), but the 'CASE FOR YES' argues LOUD is a powerhouse with favorable NA matchups \u2014 a logical contradiction suggesting either briefing bias or stale data. MIBR BENCHMARK ILLUSION: MIBR's 2-0 start is cited as a 'competitive benchmark,' but one team's early dominance in a round-robin with minimal cross-team matches tells us almost nothing about Envy vs. LOUD relative strength. ABSENT SIGNALS SCREAM: No mention of recent team changes, coaching updates, scrim results, agent meta shifts in 2026, or individual player form trajectories (ACS, win rates). This silence is dangerous \u2014 a key player benched or returning from injury would be outcome-determinative but invisible. TIME-PRESSURE VOLATILITY: Match is TODAY (~15 hours to start). Any roster news, injury, or tactical leak in the next few hours could flip the market sharply. NO side has shown +8pp spike on Apr 09 and +1.5pp in 24h, suggesting late-breaking information is trickling in, but briefing does not capture the latest news. BRAZILIAN DEPTH vs. NA INFRASTRUCTURE: 'LOUD historically has favorable matchups against NA teams' is narrative-only; no stats provided. Envy's 'solid infrastructure' is equally vague. One team may have just signed a world-class player or suffered a retention loss \u2014 briefing gap. BO3 VOLATILITY MULTIPLIER: Best-of-3 introduces map selection and veto advantage; this is not a single map. Whichever team has a stronger map pool advantage (not disclosed) has structural edge. First-map adaptability is critical; no data on either team's veto strategy. ROUND DIFFERENTIAL RED HERRING: MIBR's +7 RD on 2-0 is skewed by opponent strength unknown. If MIBR faced a bottom-tier team, Envy or LOUD facing each other would have more parity. Group Alpha composition matters; briefing does not clarify strength distribution. CONFIDENCE DEPRESSION: Both confidence scores capped at ~35-38 because briefing provides no actionable player stats, recent match VODs, agent meta shifts, or head-to-head tendencies. This is a coin flip with a $0.60/$0.40 bid-ask spread masquerading as skill differentiation.", "key_factor": "Last-minute roster substitution or illness affecting a key player on either team, or a critical meta-counter pick strategy that exploits a known agent pool weakness not visible in Stage 1 limited match data."}], "final_score": 0.5493706293706294, "no_score": 0.45812949640287776, "edge": -0.05562937062937057, "no_edge": 0.06312949640287774, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 55% for YES (need \u226557%); YES-side confidence too low: 41% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1700784", "question": "Valorant: Team Envy vs LOUD (BO3) - VCT Americas Stage 1 Group Alpha", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between Team Envy and LOUD in the VCT Americas Stage 1 Group Alpha, initially scheduled for April 11 at 8:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Envy\" if Team Envy win the match against LOUD.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"LOUD\" if LOUD win the match against Team Envy.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.", "end_date": "2026-04-12T06:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-12T00:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.605, "volume_usd": 22656.749280000007, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["30621967658156857128479408421619912147771080672929457118421995035007265054285", "8084387197447127016796506760673928192725034