Match scheduled for April 12, 2026 per schedule table", "MIBR's strong 2-0 start sets competitive benchmark for the group", "Historical context unavailable: no prior 2026 season head-to-head data between teams"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-11T15:02:57.621331Z", "price_history": {"yes": {"token_id": "30621967658156857128479408421619912147771080672929457118421995035007265054285", "data_points": 44, "weighted_avg": 0.6075645383588376, "change_1w_pp": -1.0000000000000009, "change_24h_pp": 0.0, "volatility_24h": 1.3451854182690997, "direction": "STABLE", "sharp_moves": []}, "no": {"token_id": "80843871974471270167965067606739281927250343206631776932949821201151673495989", "data_points": 155, "weighted_avg": 0.39373354969845414, "change_1w_pp": 1.0000000000000009, "change_24h_pp": 1.5000000000000013, "volatility_24h": 0.6761234037828124, "direction": "RISING", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-09T20:00:43Z", "delta_pp": 8.000000000000002}]}, "fetched_at": "2026-04-11T15:02:57.997287Z"}}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-12T06:45:00Z", "winning_side": "NO", "final_yes_price": 0.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-12T07:52:38.957075+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "f37c01d5-8934-4eee-aabf-6045facb89e7", "timestamp": "2026-04-11T15:04:56.316610+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1918380", "question": "Valorant: ghosts vs Fire Flux Esports (BO3) - VCL T\u00fcrkiye: Birlik Group B", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between ghosts and Fire Flux Esports in the VCL T\u00fcrkiye: Birlik Group B, initially scheduled for April 11 at 10:30AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"ghosts\" if ghosts win the match against Fire Flux Esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Fire Flux Esports\" if Fire Flux Esports win the match against ghosts.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-11T20:30:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-11T14:30:00Z", "yes_price": 0.275, "volume_usd": 6833.028259000001, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["75523098566991978720090544936986592672988076617302214854922572530206641783712", "18345179217058127202463461821876832893054803099867514279290931656882335765017"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "Market currently prices YES at 28%, suggesting Fire Flux is favored. This aligns with available data showing Fire Flux players with strong recent individual ratings (influx 1.70, JN3v1cEEE 1.40). Critical data gap: briefing contains NO information on Ghosts' recent form, roster, individual player ratings, or head-to-head history. Cannot evaluate Ghosts' actual competitive level. Fire Flux performance metrics show mixed signals: elite individual performances (influx, JN3v1cEEE) but concerning controller play (Docent 0.61-0.78 rating) and Raze inconsistency (musz3kk 1.45 but 0.57-0.93 splits). The case presented assumes Fire Flux superiority based solely on available stats. This reasoning is biased by data availability, not necessarily predictive of match outcome. Market price history shows sharp 19.5pp drop on Apr 09 04:00 UTC (favoring Fire Flux), suggesting new information entered market. Without that information, cannot assess whether it reflects Ghosts weakness or Fire Flux strength. Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (resolves in ~5 hours). At this stage, professional Valorant teams' capabilities are largely known; major surprises are rare but forfeits/cancellations remain tail-risk possibilities (resolve to 50-50). Fire Flux's recent matches show they compete in VCL T\u00fcrkiye group stage. Ghosts' tournament placement and tier are unstated. If Ghosts is academy/weaker division team, Fire Flux favoring is justified. If Ghosts is established team, market may be overweighting available data. Confidence in YES (Ghosts win) is low (25) because: (1) available data favors Fire Flux, (2) market has moved against Ghosts, (3) no Ghosts performance data to argue contrarian case. Confidence in NO (Fire Flux win) is only moderate (35) because: (1) Ghosts' true strength is completely unknown, (2) Fire Flux's statistics show meaningful vulnerabilities (controller, economic management), (3) group stage matches can produce upsets, (4) data asymmetry inflates Fire Flux confidence artificially. Resolution criteria are clear (first to win 2 maps in BO3 format). No ambiguity in outcome condition. Forfeiture/cancellation risk is low but nonzero (~5% tail probability given imminent timing). Probability score of 28 reflects market consensus weighted toward Fire Flux based on available individual player data, but acknowledges substantial uncertainty from missing Ghosts intelligence.", "key_factor": "Severe data asymmetry: detailed Fire Flux statistics available but zero performance data on Ghosts provided; market price reflects available information disparity rather than true skill differential."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE (NO = Fire Flux wins): Market has priced Fire Flux at 72%, reflecting confidence in their recent demonstrated form. Fire Flux's star duelist influx posted 1.70 rating across recent matches\u2014elite-tier performance indicating clutch ability and impact fragging. JN3v1cEEE (controller/Skye) maintained 1.40 rating with 75% KAST, showing consistent round participation and utility effectiveness. kabzi (Vyse controller) posted 1.35 rating, providing stable mid-round control on a secondary agent\u2014no obvious structural weakness. Fire Flux demonstrated positive round differentials (+1 to +8) in recent matched, indicating consistent map control and economy management. CRITICAL DATA GAP: No performance statistics, recent results, or roster information for Ghosts team provided in briefing. This asymmetry strongly favors the documented team (Fire Flux). Docent (omen) weakness (0.61\u20130.78 rating) is offset by Fire Flux's overall depth\u2014multiple players performing above 1.0 rating mitigates any single weak link. musz3kk's (Raze) inconsistency (0.57\u20130.93 split) exists but does not negate the team's demonstrated win conditions via influx and JN3v1cEEE carries. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS: Ghosts are entirely uncharacterized in briefing. No data on their recent form, roster strength, coach, or meta alignment. Unknown underdog status in a TODAY/IMMINENT match (5 hours to event) means historical reversal is unlikely. Market momentum: YES side fell -25pp over 7 days and -6pp in last 24 hours, indicating sustained confidence erosion for the underdog. Sharp moves on Apr 09 (-19.5pp, -8pp) suggest pattern of Ghosts underperformance expectations or Fire Flux positive catalyst. With only ~5 hours to resolution, a major upset by uncharacterized Ghosts would require either hidden preparation (unlikely given lack of public form data) or Fire Flux breakdown (no forewarning in stats). Confidence in NO is high (72) because Fire Flux's recent competitive evidence is documented and consistent; confidence in YES is low (25) because Ghosts data is entirely absent\u2014cannot validate underdog thesis.", "key_factor": "Fire Flux Esports' proven firepower in recent VCL T\u00fcrkiye matches, anchored by influx (1.70 Jett rating) and JN3v1cEEE (1.40 Skye rating), establishes them as the favored side despite sparse direct comparative data."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.32, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "FIRE FLUX STRENGTHS (Favorite's Case): Individual star power evident\u2014influx (Jett 1.70 rating), JN3v1cEEE (Skye 1.40), kabzi (Vyse 1.35) demonstrate high-impact fragging. Positive round differentials and strong KAST percentages (75-88%) indicate disciplined utility usage and round win consistency in recent matches. FIRE FLUX VULNERABILITIES: Controller Docent critically weak (0.61-0.78 rating range)\u2014mid-round control/info gaps are exploitable. Raze player musz3kk wildly inconsistent (0.57-0.93 split on same agent), creating round-by-round unpredictability. Economic management shows some matches with poor conversion (50% KAST vs 25% wins). GHOSTS DATA GAP\u2014THE CRITICAL ISSUE: Zero performance statistics provided for Ghosts roster. No recent matches, ratings, agent pools, or head-to-head history available. Market is pricing this as 72% Fire Flux win based entirely on Fire Flux stats in isolation, not relative strength. UPSET SCENARIO PLAUSIBILITY: If Ghosts has been grinding off-radar in VCL T\u00fcrkiye Group B with strong fundamentals, team cohesion, and meta preparation, they could exploit Fire Flux's controller weakness and Raze inconsistency. Turkish VCL teams often compete on team play and economy discipline rather than raw highlight plays. MARKET PRICING LOGIC FLAW: YES at 28% reflects 'Fire Flux has good players,' not 'Fire Flux is likely to beat Ghosts.' Without Ghosts data, the market cannot properly weigh defensive capabilities, anti-stratting, or team synergy. This is a data-asymmetry discount, not a true skill assessment. MATCH TIMING & VOLATILITY: Event is TODAY (5 hours to resolution). Sharp -19.5pp and -8.0pp moves on Apr 09 suggest recent news or lineup changes. The YES side falling 25pp over 7 days may indicate Fire Flux lineup confirmation or practice scrim results favoring them\u2014or vice versa. Volatility is moderate (1.5pp/hr), not panic-driven. VOLUME & LIQUIDITY: Low volume ($6,833) means this market has limited informed betting. Asymmetric information (Fire Flux stats known, Ghosts unknown) can create mispricing in low-volume markets\u2014favorites are often overweighted when only one side has visible data. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: confidence_yes=28 reflects genuine data poverty on Ghosts\u2014cannot confidently argue for upset without any performance metrics. confidence_no=45 (not higher) reflects Fire Flux's controller/Raze vulnerabilities and the assumption that Ghosts data exists and is competitive; if Ghosts are genuinely weak, Fire Flux should trade 80%+ not 72%. FINAL ASSESSMENT: Fire Flux likely favored\u2014star players and recent form data support NO. But the 44-point gap between YES (28%) and NO (72%) is WIDER than justified by asymmetric information alone. Ghosts is underpriced as an underdog; true probability likely 35-40%, not 28%. Market is overcorrecting on visible Fire Flux stats.", "key_factor": "Complete absence of Ghosts performance data creates asymmetric information favoring the underdog\u2014market may be overweighting Fire Flux's individual player metrics without accounting for team cohesion, preparation, or meta adaptation."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: No performance statistics, recent form, or roster information available for ghosts team \u2014 this asymmetry is severe and undermines confidence in both directions. MARKET SIGNAL: Current market price (28% YES / 72% NO) reflects strong backing for Fire Flux Esports, heavily weighted since at least April 9 (-19.5pp move favoring Fire Flux). FIRE FLUX POSITIVE: Available match data shows influx (1.70 rating on Jett), JN3v1cEEE (1.40 on Skye), and kabzi (1.35 on Vyse) with strong individual performances and positive round differentials in recent VCL matches. FIRE FLUX CONCERNS: Docent (controller, 0.61\u20130.78 rating) suggests potential mid-round control vulnerability; musz3kk (Raze) shows high variance (1.45 overall but 0.57\u20130.93 split), indicating inconsistency under pressure. GHOSTS OPACITY: Zero competitive data in briefing \u2014 cannot evaluate roster strength, recent form, head-to-head record, or playstyle compatibility against Fire Flux. BASE RATE ALIGNMENT: Without head-to-head history or Ghosts data, raw BO3 coin flip would be 50%. Market price of 28% for ghosts suggests informed players believe Fire Flux is materially stronger. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes = 28 (low, mirroring market lack of ghosts data); confidence_no = 32 (marginally higher due to Fire Flux performance data, but still low given ghosts blindness). TIME PRESSURE: Event resolves in ~5 hours (IMMINENT). Reversal requiring ghosts to overcome perceived deficit is theoretically possible but increasingly unlikely as match approaches. VOLUME & LIQUIDITY: $6,833 USD traded volume is modest for Turkish regional esports, suggesting market may reflect betting sentiment rather than deep analytical consensus. RESOLUTION RULE RISK: Market includes 50\u201350 resolution clauses for cancellations, forfeits, or incomplete matches; low probability but non-zero given regional league volatility.", "key_factor": "Approximately 50% for any given professional Valorant BO3 match absent clear roster/performance data; Turkish VCL Birlik Group B matches show high volatility with no dominant teams in available data."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.25, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "Market price (28% YES / 72% NO) reflects heavy consensus favoring Fire Flux, but briefing provides NO performance data on Ghosts\u2014only Fire Flux statistics. This is a critical asymmetry. Fire Flux showed strong individual ratings (influx 1.70, JN3v1cEEE 1.40, kabzi 1.35) in recent VCL matches, supporting the NO bias in market pricing. However, Docent (Fire Flux controller) posted weak ratings (0.61\u20130.78), indicating potential mid-round control vulnerability\u2014a soft underbelly the market may be ignoring. musz3kk (Raze) showed extreme inconsistency (1.45 rating but 0.57\u20130.93 split across maps), raising execution risk Fire Flux pricing does not fully reflect. Ghosts roster data is entirely absent from briefing\u2014no stats, no recent form, no head-to-head history. Market may be overconfident in Fire Flux by default rather than by evidence. Sharp moves on Apr 09 (YES down 19.5pp, then +9.0pp) suggest volatility driven by news/roster moves, not by fundamental analysis visible in provided data. 7-day YES decline of 25pp is steep and consistent, suggesting crowd conviction building toward Fire Flux, but this may reflect narrative drift rather than updated performance intel. With 5 hours to match start (IMMINENT), a reversal would require Ghosts to be a hidden threat OR Fire Flux vulnerability (Docent/musz3kk issues) to be real\u2014both low-probability surprises at this stage. Current 28% YES is defensible if Fire Flux is truly stronger, but it is also priced heavily on asymmetric information favoring NO. Ghosts underdog valuation is reasonable given data void, not mispricing. Confidence in NO is only moderate (45) because lack of Ghosts data means Fire Flux strength cannot be independently verified; confidence in YES is similarly constrained (35) by absence of counter-narrative.", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "MARKET STRUCTURE: YES=$0.28 (28%), NO=$0.72 (72%) with $6.8k volume indicates NO side heavily favored; sharp moves on Apr 09 (-19.5pp \u2192 +9.0pp) suggest recent informational shift toward Fire Flux FIRE FLUX AVAILABLE DATA: Only 2-3 recent matches shown (vs S2G Esports); influx (Jett) 1.70 ACS is genuinely elite tier entry fragging; JN3v1cEEE (Skye) 1.40 supports mid-round execution; influx shows +8 round differential on strong map FIRE FLUX WEAKNESSES: Docent (controller/omen) rating 0.61-0.78 far below elite (typical duelist 1.0-1.2, controller 0.9-1.1); musz3kk (Raze) 1.45\u21920.57-0.93 split indi