c\u2014confidence_no is capped at 72 due to inability to validate whether Ghosts are stronger than the stats suggest. FIRE FLUX STRUCTURAL WEAKNESS: Docent (controller/omen player) rated 0.61\u20130.78 across matches\u2014significantly below team average. Controllers dictate mid-round economy and site takes in Valorant; poor controller play systematically loses rounds regardless of fragger performance. This is a critical vulnerability if Ghosts' stratcaller can exploit it. STAT INFLATION CAVEAT: Fire Flux's high-rated fraggers (influx 1.70, JN3v1cEEE 1.40) are measured against S2G Esports, not Ghosts. S2G may be weaker tier; Fire Flux's ACS and rating spikes could evaporate against a stronger opponent. No evidence Fire Flux maintains this form against peers. RAZE INCONSISTENCY: musz3kk's Raze shows volatile splits (1.45 avg but 0.57\u20130.93 range), suggesting poor consistency under pressure. Duelist volatility is match-deciding in BO3 format\u2014one off-round by the primary entry fragger can cascade into a map loss. HISTORICAL ABSENCE: No head-to-head record or recent Ghosts match data provided. Market price (28% YES, 72% NO) reflects this information vacuum\u2014traders are pricing in Fire Flux as heavy favorite, but that may be purely because Ghosts' data is missing, not because Fire Flux is objectively superior. MARKET MOMENTUM REVERSAL: YES side dropped 25pp over 7 days (39\u219214 EMA), suggesting confidence erosion or late-stage information favoring Fire Flux. However, with only ~5 hours to match start and asymmetric data quality, sharp moves could reflect whale positioning rather than genuine form intelligence. META/MAP POOL SILENCE: Briefing shows agent picks (Jett, Skye, Omen, etc.) but NO insight into which specific maps will be played, veto order, or whether Ghosts possess a map-specific advantage or anti-strat composition. BO3 format means 2 maps out of ~7 tier\u2014Ghosts could own a crucial map pool that Fire Flux players underperform on. TIMING CRUNCH: Match resolves in ~5 hours. For Ghosts to flip this at 24% probability requires a major structural edge (roster advantage, coaching adjustment, mental resilience, or meta counter-pick). With minutes to start, only a pre-match substitution, injury to a Fire Flux star (extremely low-probability event), or a tactical innovation by Ghosts' coach can swing it. KABZI AND JN3v1CKK CARRY RISK: Two of Fire Flux's top performers rely on utility (Vyse, Skye). If Ghosts' IGL successfully anti-stratifies these agents (e.g., forcing unoptimal ult usage or off-positioning), Fire Flux's win condition collapses faster than raw stats suggest. COUNCIL CONSENSUS TRAP: Market is 72/28 split, implying near-consensus that Fire Flux wins. In low-information matches, consensus often overweights one data point (Fire Flux's recent stats) and ignores the absence of counter-data (Ghosts' performance, head-to-head, team synergy). Ghosts could be a quietly improving roster with stronger fundamentals than Fire Flux's flashy fraggers.", "key_factor": "Ghosts executes a last-minute roster substitution or tactical pivot specifically designed to counter Fire Flux's individual star power (influx on Jett, JN3v1cEEE on Skye), exploiting a meta shift or map pool advantage not captured in the briefing's stale statistical snapshots."}], "final_score": 0.273696682464455, "no_score": 0.7270845481049564, "edge": -0.0013033175355450233, "no_edge": 0.0020845481049563963, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 49% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1918380", "question": "Valorant: ghosts vs Fire Flux Esports (BO3) - VCL T\u00fcrkiye: Birlik Group B", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between ghosts and Fire Flux Esports in the VCL T\u00fcrkiye: Birlik Group B, initially scheduled for April 11 at 10:30AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"ghosts\" if ghosts win