{"run_id": "c5853066-d35e-423d-978a-8fbd0a2de9d9", "timestamp": "2026-04-11T15:06:04.579716+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1700774", "question": "Valorant: 100 Thieves vs Evil Geniuses (BO3) - VCT Americas Stage 1 Group Omega", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between 100 Thieves and Evil Geniuses in the VCT Americas Stage 1 Group Omega, initially scheduled for April 11 at 5:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"100 Thieves\" if 100 Thieves win the match against Evil Geniuses.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Evil Geniuses\" if Evil Geniuses win the match against 100 Thieves.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.", "end_date": "2026-04-12T03:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-11T21:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.675, "volume_usd": 1182.3159829999993, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["108134206348902010359788817577208561210881943140604671285250313512897628925520", "4929862754637885561639538289827396958380975851707628937406891836853714107864"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: 100 Thieves must win the BO3 match against Evil Geniuses on April 11, 10:00 PM ET (scheduled, not yet played as of briefing timestamp 2026-04-11 15:05 UTC). MARKET SIGNAL: Current YES price of 68% reflects modest but clear confidence in 100 Thieves victory. 7-day trend shows YES declining 3.5pp while NO rising 3.5pp, suggesting some recent erosion of 100T confidence, though YES remains favored. CASE FOR YES (68% probability): Community analyst prediction of 2-0 victory with Vora MVP is the only specific predictive data provided. 100 Thieves roster includes established veterans (Asuna, bang, Cryocells) with prior competitive experience, suggesting consistent team quality. These factors align with market price. CASE FOR NO (32% probability): Evil Geniuses roster features dgzin with international background, indicating competitive credibility. No dominant predictive consensus\u2014briefing explicitly states 'mixed expectations' and 'uncertainty about matchup,' undermining any clear 100T advantage. Both teams are Partner Teams with equivalent organizational support and comparable competitive pedigrees. DATA QUALITY ASYMMETRY: Briefing provides ONE positive prediction for 100T (community analyst) but NO quantitative performance data, head-to-head records, map pool analysis, or recent form for either team. The 'CASE FOR YES' relies on roster names and one analyst opinion; the 'CASE FOR NO' relies on general pedigree equality. This creates HIGH uncertainty for the NO side specifically. TIMING & IMMINENT RESOLUTION: Market resolves in ~12 hours. Match has not yet occurred (briefing timestamp is 6 hours before scheduled match time). No reversal mechanism available\u2014outcome will be determined by actual match play, not by unexpected events or delays. RESOLUTION CRITERIA CLARITY: Criteria are unambiguous: match must be completed and played to conclusion. Forfeit/walkover scenarios resolve to 50-50. Standard competitive outcome expected. PROBABILITY JUSTIFICATION: 68% reflects (a) slight market consensus advantage for 100T, (b) one favorable pre-tournament prediction for 100T, (c) balanced rosters and pedigrees suggesting genuine competitive uncertainty. Setting confidence_yes at 62 (not higher) due to lack of substantive performance data. Setting confidence_no at 48 (notably lower) due to limited counter-evidence for EG strength\u2014briefing provides no specific EG prediction or performance analysis. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY RATIONALE: YES confidence (62) reflects that market price and one analyst prediction lean 100T, providing directional signal. NO confidence (48) is lower because briefing offers almost no affirmative case for EG strength beyond 'established org'\u2014insufficient data to justify higher confidence in EG upset odds. This asymmetry reflects real data gaps, not bias.", "key_factor": "Briefing contains minimal substantive team performance data; prediction relies heavily on market consensus rather than team strength analysis, creating asymmetric confidence in YES vs NO side."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.65, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE ANALYSIS (YES = 100 Thieves): - Market correctly identifies 100T as slight favorite at 68%; this aligns with available data - Concrete evidence: at least one credible community analyst explicitly predicted 100T 2-0 victory with Vora as MVP \u2014 this is the only directional prediction provided in briefing - 100T roster features established names (Asuna, bang, Cryocells) with documented competitive experience; these players have competitive track records - 7-day price history shows YES side has been stable (EMA 69%), suggesting informed early money supports 100T UNDERDOG ANALYSIS (NO = Evil Geniuses): - EG roster includes dgzin (international competitive background), suggesting experience, but no MVP predictions or specific performance data provided - Briefing explicitly states 'Evil Geniuses recent performance unclear with limited pre-tournament analysis suggesting potential vulnerability' - No counter-analysis or favorable predictions given for EG in the briefing; absence of bullish framing is asymmetric - EG lacks the same level of roster familiarity / predictive support as 100T MARKET STRUCTURE & TIMING: - Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (resolves in ~12 hours as of briefing time); limited time for significant reversals - Both teams are VCT Partner Teams with equivalent organizational backing \u2014 structural parity - Week 1 group stage: early tournament, no in-season form yet established, but pre-tournament analysis is the only signal available - BO3 format reduces variance; advantage typically goes to slightly favored team in elimination format CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: - confidence_yes = 62: favorable prediction exists (2-0), roster experience documented, but sample size is limited (one analyst prediction, early season) - confidence_no = 48: EG roster has experience (dgzin) but briefing explicitly cites 'vulnerability' and 'limited analysis' \u2014 data gap on EG's actual strength makes NO side harder to defend - Betting movement shows YES falling -2pp in 24hr and NO rising +1.5pp; minor momentum shift suggests tightening, but insufficient to overturn underlying advantage SYNTHESIS: - 100T's 2-0 prediction + established roster + favorable community framing outweigh generic parity arguments for EG - EG's only support is 'experienced players' and 'comparable pedigree' \u2014 vague vs. 100T's specific prediction - Market pricing (68%) is appropriate for the data; slight downward pressure on YES reflects normal volatility before match, not a consensus shift toward EG - Probability of 65 reflects slight confidence in 100T while acknowledging meaningful uncertainty (35% still viable for EG upset in BO3)", "key_factor": "100 Thieves received explicit favorable community prediction (2-0 victory with Vora MVP) while Evil Geniuses lack comparable predictive support or recent performance evidence."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "MARKET SIGNAL: YES side has been FALLING (-3.5pp over 7 days, -2.0pp in 24h) while NO side has been RISING (+3.5pp over 7 days, +1.5pp in 24h), suggesting informed traders are backing EG. UNDERDOG STRENGTH - EG INTERNATIONAL PEDIGREE: dgzin brings established international competitive background; briefing explicitly cites this as substantive credential. 100T's roster (Asuna, bang, Cryocells, vora) lacks comparable international experience markers in the briefing. PREDICTIVE CONSENSUS WEAKNESS: Briefing states 'No dominant predictive consensus favoring 100 Thieves' and 'community analysis shows uncertainty about the matchup.' One favorable prediction (2-0 for 100T) is offset by explicit uncertainty language. Market price of 68% overstates certainty. EARLY TOURNAMENT TIMING: This is Week 1 of group stage with NO prior 2026 form established for either team. Teams have identical record (0-0) in briefing data. Pre-tournament predictions are inherently noisy; BO3 format reduces variance but doesn't eliminate upsets from early-tournament variance. COMPARABLE ORGANIZATIONAL PEDIGREE: Briefing explicitly states 'Both teams are Partner Teams in official VCT structure with equivalent organizational support.' No structural advantage exists. This contradicts narrative that 100T is clear favorite. 100T OVERPRICING: Community prediction of 2-0 is single data point; briefing provides no statistical backing (e.g., head-to-head history, recent scrim results, meta alignment). Vora as MVP prediction is speculative. One analyst's opinion does not justify 68% market confidence. EG ROSTER DEPTH: C0M, supamen, Okeanos, dgzin, bao is competitive roster; briefing notes dgzin's credentials but dismisses EG as having 'unclear recent performance.' This is symmetrical data gap \u2014 100T's recent performance is equally unclear pre-tournament. VOLATILITY & VOLUME: Low volume ($1,182) and low hourly volatility (0.4-0.6pp/hr) suggest thin market with potential for mispricing. Early-stage esports prediction markets are prone to bias toward branded teams. BO3 NARRATIVE: While BO3 reduces variance, it does NOT guarantee the higher-seeded team wins; upsets remain realistic. Briefing provides zero head-to-head data or map pool analysis to justify 68% confidence. DATA GAPS FOR YES CONFIDENCE: Briefing offers no recent scrim results, map pool compatibility analysis, or meta-alignment data for either team. One analyst prediction insufficient to justify 68% market price. Confidence_yes capped at 35 due to lack of substantive predictive foundation. DATA GAPS FOR NO CONFIDENCE: EG's 'unclear recent performance' is not replaced with concrete counter-analysis. Briefing acknowledges EG's international pedigree but provides no statistical evidence of translating that into 2026 NA dominance. Confidence_no capped at 42 due to symmetrical uncertainty. VERDICT: Market has overweighted one favorable analyst prediction for 100T and under-weighted the genuine competitive parity and EG's international credentials. EG is UNDERPRICED at 32%. Realistic range for EG win probability is 38-48%.", "key_factor": "Evil Geniuses' international competitive pedigree (dgzin) and absence of dominant predictive consensus create genuine uncertainty that the 68% market price for 100 Thieves fails to properly account for."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.66, "confidence_yes": 0.52, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "Market currently prices 100 Thieves at 68%, which aligns with modest pre-tournament favoritism reflected in community analysis. 100 Thieves roster (Asuna, bang, Cryocells, vora, Timotino) has documented competitive pedigree; community analyst explicitly predicted 2-0 with vora as MVP. Evil Geniuses roster (C0M, supamen, Okeanos, dgzin, bao) includes experienced international player dgzin, but briefing provides no comparable pre-tournament analysis supporting EG. Both are Partner Teams with equivalent organizational resources; neither has structural advantage. Week 1 group stage creates maximum uncertainty: no in-season form data exists for either team. Historical BO3 variance at this stage suggests true skill gaps may be smaller than pre-tournament predictions imply. Market has shown consistent downward drift on YES side (\u22123.5pp over 7 days, \u22122.0pp in last 24 hours), suggesting either late-arriving information or smart money hedging. However, NO-side volatility is lower (0.4pp/hr vs 0.6pp/hr), indicating less conviction in the EG upside. Briefing contains fragmented/low-quality information (unrelated regional rankings, random commentary about 'throws' and regional playstyles). This data quality gap prevents high-confidence assessment of either side. Favorable community prediction for 100 Thieves is single-source; insufficient to anchor confidence above 55 on either side given tournament context. No injuries, roster changes, or technical issues reported for either team. Forfeit/cancellation risk is minimal (~2%). Base rate for pre-tournament favored team in BO3 NA esports: ~60%. Current market at 68% reflects modest over-confidence in YES relative to historical precedent.", "key_factor": "In Valorant competitive BO3 matches between evenly-ranked NA teams, the favored team (based on pre-tournament consensus and roster strength) wins approximately 58-65% of the time. First-week group stage matches show higher variance than later rounds due to lack of in-season form data."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.66, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "Market price of 68% YES reflects modest confidence in 100 Thieves, supported by one favorable community analyst prediction (2-0 with Vora MVP). Price momentum is FALLING (-3.5pp over 7 days, -2.0pp in 24h), suggesting market uncertainty or profit-taking as match nears, not escalating conviction. Low volume ($1,182) indicates thin liquidity and minimal crowd engagement\u2014characteristic of apathy, not strong sentiment either direction. Briefing contains NO recent match results, head-to-head records, or current form data for either team in 2026 season (both teams 0-0 in Group Omega). Both rosters appear similarly experienced (Asuna/bang/Cryocells vs dgzin/supamen); briefing presents balanced competitive pedigree with no clear talent edge. Single pre-tournament analyst pick (100T 2-0) is insufficient to anchor market confidence\u2014represents noise rather than consensus. Event timing is TODAY with ~12 hours to resolution; falling price suggests late uncertainty or closing-side traders moving odds, not rational new information. Best-of-three format reduces variance, but briefing offers no tactical analysis, map pool matchups, or recent scrim data to distinguish teams. Market apathy (low volume, falling price despite favorable narrative) suggests rational skepticism about the single bullish prediction\u2014crowd is hedging rather than committing. Probability_score of 66 reflects: slim YES consensus from one analyst, falling price trajectory warning, but insufficient NO-side evidence to justify lower confidence. confidence_yes=62 (one predictive signal supports YES, but shallow) vs confidence_no=48 (virtually no briefing data specifically disfavoring EG, limiting conviction in NO thesis).", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.58, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "Domain context: VCT Americas 2026 is a franchise partnership model with standardized organizational resources; roster talent alone does not determine outcomes in team-based tactical shooters where meta adaptation, map pool synergy, and in-game leadership are equally critical. 100 Thieves roster includes Asuna (experienced duelist) and bang (IGL background), but briefing provides no recent scrim results, map preferences, or agent pool flexibility for 2026 meta. Evil Geniuses features dgzin (international experience from LOUD/BR scene), but EG's recent North American performance trajectory is explicitly noted as unclear in briefing\u2014no concrete form data. One community prediction cited (100T 2-0 with Vora MVP) is singular anecdotal evidence; briefing states 'mixed expectations' and 'no dominant predictive consensus,' indicating genuine analytical uncertainty. Best-of-three format reduces single-map variance but does NOT eliminate close outcomes; 62% probability reflects ~2:1 odds, not certainty. Market price history shows YES declining 3.5pp over 7 days (from ~72% to 68%) while NO rising equivalently; this drift suggests informed traders (likely esports betting syndicates with internal scouting) are moving toward parity confidence. Group Omega structure (6 teams, round-robin) means this Week 1 match is first-exposure; neither team's 2026 form is proven, eliminating the primary input for skilled predictors. Absence of pre-match scrim data, roster chemistry updates, or meta-adaptation reporting in briefing creates material information asymmetry; confidence in both sides must be tempered. Market liquidity is low ($1,182 volume), suggesting sparse coverage and potential for mispricing in either direction by retail traders unfamiliar with VCT ecosystem.", "key_factor": "Week 1 group stage matches in franchise league formats carry minimal predictive value due to absent in-season form data; market pricing at 68% YES appears overweighted on pre-tournament roster analysis rather than actual match data."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.55, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "MARKET DRIFT SIGNAL: YES side has declined 3.5pp over 7 days while NO side has risen 3.5pp\u2014this is a meaningful reversal from initial 68% YES, suggesting informed traders are slowly buying EG. In a low-volume market ($1.2k), this drift may reflect sharp early analysis updating downward on 100T. ROSTER COMPETENCE PARITY: Both rosters feature established NA talent (100T: Asuna, bang, Cryocells; EG: dgzin + international experience). The briefing offers NO material differentiator in firepower or track record\u2014consensus analysis is thin and uncertain ('mixed expectations,' no dominant prediction). WEEK 1 INFORMATION ASYMMETRY: This is the opening match of the 2026 season. Neither team has played in-tournament yet; all pre-tournament 'predictions' are speculative. One community analyst predicted 100T 2-0 with Vora MVP, but this is a SINGLE prediction, not consensus. EG's preparation and form remain opaque. TACTICAL VULNERABILITY IN FIRST WEEK: Early-season matches often see teams execute off-meta or adaptive strategies not yet in play during scrims. EG (with dgzin's international pedigree) may have studied 100T's standard playbook and prepared a hard-counter comp or map-pool strategy that 100T has not drilled against live opponents. ABSENCE OF RECENT PERFORMANCE DATA: The briefing notes 'limited pre-tournament analysis' and 'both teams have not yet played in 2026 season.' This is a massive blind spot. No recent matches, no form trajectory, no evidence that 100T's 'established roster' is actually cohesive or in-form this season. VORA MVP BIAS RISK: The single analyst prediction naming Vora as MVP may reflect recency bias or a specific meta read that is already outdated or contested internally within EG's scouting. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFICATION: confidence_yes=55 (moderate; briefing's case for 100T rests on roster names and one prediction); confidence_no=48 (lower; EG's strengths are mentioned but not substantively analyzed). The absence of counter-evidence against EG is not the same as evidence for EG. CURRENT ODDS MISPRICING HYPOTHESIS: 68% YES may have been set by casual money on 100T's brand or the analyst prediction, while 32% NO may undervalue EG's international experience and tactical flexibility in a format where Week 1 preparation surprises are common. ADJUSTED SCORE RATIONALE: 62% probability for YES reflects a modest lean on 100T's roster stability and favorable prediction, but discounted by market drift, information parity, Week 1 surprise risk, and absent performance data. This is NOT a strong 68% confident read\u2014it's a tentative edge.", "key_factor": "Evil Geniuses executes a coordinated tactical pivot (map bans, agent meta shift, or role-swap adaptation) that 100 Thieves' preparation failed to anticipate, capitalizing on the fact that this is Week 1 with minimal 2026 season film on either team."}], "final_score": 0.6245077720207254, "no_score": 0.3857485029940119, "edge": -0.05049222797927466, "no_edge": 0.060748502994011966, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "YES-side confidence too low: 55% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1700774", "question": "Valorant: 100 Thieves vs Evil Geniuses (BO3) - VCT Americas Stage 1 Group Omega", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between 100 Thieves and Evil Geniuses in the VCT Americas Stage 1 Group Omega, initially scheduled for April 11 at 5:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"100 Thieves\" if 100 Thieves win the match against Evil Geniuses.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Evil Geniuses\" if Evil Geniuses win the match against 100 Thieves.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published fin