{"run_id": "2b3ef32d-4f51-4060-bcb8-e05b599b6620", "timestamp": "2026-04-11T15:07:02.725300+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1918385", "question": "Valorant: TEAM SCARS vs Be\u015fikta\u015f Esports (BO3) - VCL T\u00fcrkiye: Birlik Group A", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between TEAM SCARS and Be\u015fikta\u015f Esports in the VCL T\u00fcrkiye: Birlik Group A, initially scheduled for April 11 at 1:30PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"TEAM SCARS\" if TEAM SCARS win the match against Be\u015fikta\u015f Esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Be\u015fikta\u015f Esports\" if Be\u015fikta\u015f Esports win the match against TEAM SCARS.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-11T23:30:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-11T17:30:00Z", "yes_price": 0.205, "volume_usd": 3635.0734020000004, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["107033269676290603575957877546208973927815282042784628555526424304107128081947", "58336741498932037149875144811358003319228082804552825031574349495638949237466"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.22, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: TEAM SCARS must win the BO3 match against Be\u015fikta\u015f Esports in VCL T\u00fcrkiye Birlik Group A scheduled for April 11, 2026 at 1:30 PM ET. EVENT TIMING: Event is TODAY (resolves in ~8 hours). Match is imminent; outcome will be determined within hours. MARKET PRICING SIGNAL: YES trading at 20% (NO at 80%) indicates strong market consensus favoring Be\u015fikta\u015f. This is a 4:1 underdog position for TEAM SCARS. PRICE HISTORY ANALYSIS: YES side has fallen sharply (-31pp over 7 days), with sharp sell-off on Apr 09. This decline suggests new information or updated assessments heavily favored Be\u015fikta\u015f. Sharp moves are inconsistent with random noise. ORGANIZATIONAL TIER: Be\u015fikta\u015f Esports is an established organization with greater infrastructure/resources. TEAM SCARS is less established. In esports, organizational depth typically correlates with roster quality and support. PERFORMANCE DATA GAP: Briefing provides NO actual stats (ACS, K/D, ADR, KAST, or maps won). All statistical tables show only '/' placeholders. Cannot assess relative skill, form, or recent trajectory. HEAD-TO-HEAD: Zero documented prior matches. No historical edge exists for either team. ROSTER CONTINUITY: TEAM SCARS roster listed (doozy, Ro0t, Frostt, b3zginn, Elyxo) but no performance context provided. Roster names alone are insufficient to predict outcome. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: Both teams in same group stage format with identical structural constraints. No tiebreaker implications mentioned or visible. MARKET CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong market signal (20% YES) combined with recent sharp downward moves suggests informed traders have additional information not visible in briefing. Market may reflect insider knowledge, scrim results, or roster news. UNDERDOG RISK: YES = 22% reflects market consensus + modest additional weight to the organizational tier gap. TEAM SCARS is genuine underdog but not impossible (22% reflects ~4.5:1 against, reasonable for established vs. lesser-known team). CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: confidence_yes = 28 (low) because briefing provides zero statistical evidence to support YES; relying on market pricing and absence of negative indicators. confidence_no = 32 (similarly low) because briefing contains no affirmative evidence of Be\u015fikta\u015f strength either\u2014only organizational tier inference. Asymmetry is slight because data gap affects both sides equally. RESOLUTION MECHANISM RISK: Minimal. Match is BO3 with clear winner format (not forfeit/tie/cancellation). VLR.gg is primary source with 2-hour fallback to credible reporting. Valorant matches are well-streamed and documented. No significant mechanism risk to flagging.", "key_factor": "Briefing contains no actual performance data, head-to-head history, or comparative statistics\u2014probability is driven entirely by market pricing and organizational tier inference rather than measurable competitive evidence."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.78, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE (NO) STRENGTHS: Be\u015fikta\u015f Esports is an established esports organization with institutional resources, infrastructure, and brand recognition that typically co