CE COLLAPSE SIGNAL: YES dropped 31pp over 7 days (from ~50% to 20%), with violent swings on Apr 09 (\u00b112.5pp, \u00b19.5pp, \u00b18.5pp). This indicates insider information or leaked roster/meta intel favoring Be\u015fikta\u015f entered the market mid-week. The briefing does not disclose what triggered those moves\u2014suggesting the council is trading on rumor, not fact. BO3 FORMAT VOLATILITY: A best-of-three is highly sensitive to map pool mismatches. If SCARS has a 2-map spike (e.g., Bind + Sunset specialists) and Be\u015fikta\u015f defaults to a generic meta, SCARS can steal 2-0. One map ban and one bad read on economy or agent selection flips the series. ROSTER UNCERTAINTY (CONCEALED): Be\u015fikta\u015f Esports is a branded org, but VCL T\u00fcrkiye regional teams often field academy squads or substitute lineups. No confirmation that Be\u015fikta\u015f fielded their 'A' roster vs. a developmental lineup. If SCARS faces a weakened or unfamiliar Be\u015fikta\u015f squad, the resource gap evaporates. TIMING COMPRESSION: Match is TODAY, ~8 hours until resolution. No updates to the briefing after 15:06 UTC suggest no major last-minute changes have surfaced. However, Valorant rosters can change 1\u20132 hours before match start due to illness, disputes, or coaching decisions. The low confidence in NO (35) reflects this void. MARKET STRUCTURE WEAKNESS: $3,635 total volume is very thin for an 8-hour window. Be\u015fikta\u015f -80% pricing may reflect only a handful of large bets by informed regional players, not genuine consensus. A coordinated prop bet by SCARS backers or a leaked vod review of Be\u015fikta\u015f's recent scrims could spike YES back to 35\u201345% in the final hour. COUNCIL BLIND SPOT: Every other analyst likely assumes Be\u015fikta\u015f wins because (a) they are branded, (b) SCARS stats are hidden, and (c) price has fallen. But the price fall itself may be noise from a single leveraged bet or a false leak. The briefing provides no independent verification of relative team strength beyond org size\u2014a terrible proxy in regional Valorant.", "key_factor": "TEAM SCARS deploys an unconventional agent meta or map pick strategy (likely on a permaban or map control selection) that Be\u015fikta\u015f has not prepared for, combined with a stand-in or roster swap at the last minute that shifts team synergy dynamics unpredictably."}], "final_score": 0.3110344827586206, "no_score": 0.62432, "edge": 0.10603448275862062, "no_edge": -0.17068000000000005, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 36% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1918385", "question": "Valorant: TEAM SCARS vs Be\u015fikta\u015f Esports (BO3) - VCL T\u00fcrkiye: Birlik Group A", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between TEAM SCARS and Be\u015fikta\u015f Esports in the VCL T\u00fcrkiye: Birlik Group A, initially scheduled for April 11 at 1:30PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"TEAM SCARS\" if TEAM SCARS win the match against Be\u015fikta\u015f Esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Be\u015fikta\u015f Esports\" if Be\u015fikta\u015f Esports win the match against TEAM SCARS.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of cre