{"run_id": "47b34bec-99d1-4aba-99bb-16d8aa6912fe", "timestamp": "2026-04-11T15:08:15.373382+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1902247", "question": "Mobile Legends Bang Bang: RRQ Hoshi vs Alter Ego (BO3) - MPL Indonesia Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Mobile Legends Bang Bang match between RRQ Hoshi and Alter Ego in the MPL Indonesia Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 11 at 9:15AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"RRQ Hoshi\" if RRQ Hoshi win the match against Alter Ego.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Alter Ego\" if Alter Ego win the match against RRQ Hoshi.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://liquipedia.net/mobilelegends/Main_Page. However, if https://liquipedia.net/mobilelegends/Main_Page has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-11T19:25:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-11T13:25:00Z", "yes_price": 0.365, "volume_usd": 1488.5543619999999, "category": "mobile-legends-bang-bang", "clob_token_ids": ["26390261475816042263599742144372128448365886030203481363922465164847676151190", "53216909613958940382319011249996172894359945619930454184799829885659458747347"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.36, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.68, "rationale": "TIMING CRITICAL: Event is TODAY with ~4 hours to resolution. Market prices have stabilized after sharp moves, suggesting recent information ingestion (15:07 UTC +24pp spike on YES side). MARKET CONSENSUS ALIGNMENT: Current YES price of 36% aligns closely with betting odds implying ~30-40% for Alter Ego (underdog at 1.42-1.52), confirming RRQ Hoshi is market favorite. BETTING MARKET DATA: RRQ Hoshi favored at 2.35-2.80 odds across sportsbooks vs Alter Ego 1.42-1.52, suggesting informed market consensus estimates RRQ Hoshi ~60-70% win probability. NO CONTRADICTORY INTEL: Briefing provides no recent form data, head-to-head records, roster changes, or injury updates that would contradict the market-implied probability. CASE FOR YES (RRQ Hoshi): Established top-tier team with stronger historical positioning; favored across all betting markets; market odds imply 60-70% win probability. CASE FOR NO (Alter Ego): Underdog status suggests non-trivial upset potential; all-Indonesian roster with possible home region advantage; BO3 format inherently volatile (only need 1 map to score). LIVE MATCH DYNAMICS: The +24pp YES spike at 15:07 UTC (within last hour) may reflect in-match betting activity or early game results. For a LIVE event, this suggests real-world information is flowing into prices. RESOLUTION CRITERIA CLARITY: Clear match-win conditions; standard BO3 format; Liquipedia is primary source with 2-hour grace period for final publication. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in YES assessment (72) reflects strong market consensus + betting odds alignment. Moderate confidence in NO assessment (68) reflects genuine BO3 upset potential and limited granular form data, but this asymmetry is appropriate given data quality gap. PROBABILITY SCORE RATIONALE: 36% reflects current market price and betting odds consensus. This is NOT a default; it represents genuine underdog probability for Alter Ego, not a coin flip.", "key_factor": "Match is LIVE/IMMINENT (resolves in ~4 hours); sharp price movements (+24pp YES at 15:07 UTC suggest real-time information flow; outcome may already be partially determined but not yet officially published."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.36, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "NO (Alter Ego) is correctly priced as the market favorite at 64%, but the +15pp surge for YES in 24h and +24pp sharp move at 15:07 UTC today signal either emerging technical problems for RRQ Hoshi, a lineup/preparation concern, or credible upset catalyst that late-arriving market participants are recognizing. External betting markets show RRQ Hoshi at 2.35\u20132.80 odds (59\u201370% implied), which would support 60%+ for YES \u2014 yet Polymarket shows only 36% YES, indicating THIS market is either pricing in fresh adverse information about the favorite, or NO side is overvalued. RRQ Hoshi's pedigree as 'established top-tier team' is stated but not evidenced with 2026 season form. Early season regular-play (week 2\u20133 of a March 27\u2013May 24 grind) is volatile; sample size is minimal for both teams. Alter Ego weaknesses (multi-game org, all-Indonesian roster with 'less established' elite MLBB track record) are real structural disadvantages, but the +24pp YES spike 2 hours before event suggests market learned something that contradicts the 'weak underdog' narrative. BO3 format inherently favors consistency and champion pedigree, which should favor RRQ \u2014 yet the sharp volatility and large YES moves in final hours indicate uncertainty about whether RRQ is truly the dominant team in this specific matchup at this stage of the season. Market spread and low volume ($1,489 USD) imply thin liquidity and potential for uninformed or late trades to distort prices. The 15:07 UTC +24pp YES and -10.5pp NO moves suggest a single coordinated bet or information release, not gradual consensus building. Confidence in NO (64% market price) is moderate rather than high: the late-day YES surge and discrepancy with external betting markets (which favor RRQ more strongly) indicate the market is pricing uncertainty, not certainty. If this were truly a clear NO win, volatility would be lower and the YES side would not have gained 15pp in 24h. Confidence in YES is similarly constrained: no head-to-head form data, no explanation of what changed in the last 4 hours, and the external betting consensus still favors RRQ. The spike could be a contrarian trap or a signal of real new information \u2014 impossible to distinguish with the data provided. Advocating for the NO favorite: RRQ Hoshi's betting-market consensus, top-tier pedigree, and BO3 format all favor the more established team. Alter Ego's all-Indonesian roster and underdog status are genuine weaknesses. However, the market's own repricing (YES +15pp, massive 24h volatility) contradicts the idea that NO is a confident favorite \u2014 it reads as a 64% lean on limited information, not a 75%+ conviction call.", "key_factor": "Market repricing from 25% \u2192 36% YES in last 24 hours suggests new information or uncertainty emerging about RRQ Hoshi's favoritism status despite NO remaining the consensus favorite at 64%."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "MARKET STRUCTURE: YES priced at 36% is the genuine underdog. Market consensus heavily favors NO (64%), supported by external betting odds (RRQ 2.35-2.80 vs Alter Ego 1.42-1.52), implying ~60-70% RRQ win probability across multiple independent sportsbooks. PRICE ACTION ANALYSIS: Sharp +24pp spike for YES at 15:07 UTC (90 min before match) is CRITICAL \u2014 this reversal from -13pp decline suggests informed traders moved significantly toward RRQ Hoshi very late. This is evidence OF the favorite's strength, not weakness; sophisticated money entering at the last moment typically reflects genuine edge. OPPOSING THE UPSET: The -13pp drop at 14:00 UTC followed by +24pp recovery at 15:07 UTC shows volatility but a NET recovery to ~38% for YES. This pattern is consistent with last-minute line-movement favoring the established favorite, not the underdog. UNDERDOG DATA GAPS: Briefing provides NO recent head-to-head results, NO current season form data for either team, NO roster/coaching changes, NO injury reports. This absence of counter-evidence is the ONLY foundation for an upset argument, but absence \u2260 strength. STRUCTURAL UNDERDOG CASE: Alter Ego is all-Indonesian with home region advantage and potential team chemistry. BO3 format means they only need one map win to secure a point and create pressure. MDL Indonesia is tier-B but Alter Ego as 'multi-game esport organization' suggests some infrastructure. RRQ HOSHI ESTABLISHED POSITIONING: Briefing explicitly states RRQ Hoshi has 'stronger historical positioning in MPL Indonesia as an established top-tier team.' This is direct evidence of a quality gap, not market overreaction. Multiple sportsbooks independently converged on 2.35-2.80 odds. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong evidence supports NO (sportsbook consensus, historical positioning, late informed trading). Evidence for YES is thin: organizational name recognition, home region, and hope. Confidence_no = 72 reflects justified conviction; confidence_yes = 35 reflects genuine data scarcity on upset drivers. EARLY SEASON CONTEXT: Both teams are in week 2-3 of a 9-week regular season (March 27 - May 24). Early season volatility exists, but sportsbooks have already priced this in \u2014 they do not show wide disagreement. REALISTIC UPSET SCENARIO: Alter Ego wins if: (1) RRQ Hoshi has internal issues not yet public, (2) map pools favor Alter Ego's hero pool, (3) coaching adjustments catch RRQ off-guard. None of these are supported by briefing data; they are pure speculation. VERDICT: RRQ Hoshi is favored for documented reasons (historical strength, multi-book consensus, late informed money). Alter Ego has NO concrete form evidence to justify an upset. Probability_score = 38 reflects that YES is underpriced RELATIVE to pure coin flip (50), but NOT underpriced relative to evidence. Market appears fairly calibrated.", "key_factor": "Sharp +24pp price spike at 15:07 UTC today (90 minutes before match) suggests late information flow favoring RRQ Hoshi, but BO3 format and absent recent form data create genuine upset pathway for Alter Ego."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.36, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "Market pricing (36% YES / 64% NO) reflects ~36-64 split, which is MORE favorable to the underdog (Alter Ego) than external sportsbook odds (which imply 60-70% for RRQ Hoshi) External betting consensus (RRQ Hoshi 2.35-2.80 odds) implies 55-65% win probability, but Polymarket shows only 36% for YES \u2014 suggests either market mispricing toward Alter Ego OR information asymmetry favoring underdog Sharp price movement +24pp in final 2 hours before match (Apr 11 15:07 UTC) on YES side suggests late money/insider information flowing toward RRQ Hoshi, but current price still below sportsbook consensus High 24-hour volatility (7.6pp/hr for YES) and major reversals (-13pp, then +24pp same day) indicate uncertainty and potential late information or disagreement among traders BO3 format structurally favors underdogs: Alter Ego only needs 2 maps to win, reducing RRQ Hoshi's need to sweep; historical upset rates in BO3 are higher than BO1 Team data gaps: No recent head-to-head record, current season standings, or individual player form provided \u2014 cannot validate whether RRQ Hoshi's historical elite status remains true in 2026 Season 17 Alter Ego's all-Indonesian roster and home region advantage (in Indonesia competition) may be underweighted by external sportsbooks but factored into Polymarket pricing Early regular season timing (week 2-3 of 17-week season) means less accumulated form data; early season upsets are statistically more common than mid/late season Current Polymarket price (36%) aligns roughly with historical underdog win rates in BO3 esports (~35%); external odds may overvalue the favorite Confidence in YES is moderate (42%) because late sharp movement suggests genuine RRQ Hoshi edge but market price still favors Alter Ego; confidence in NO is lower (38%) because external consensus clearly favors RRQ Hoshi and we lack recent performance data to validate Alter Ego's strength", "key_factor": "In esports BO3 matches, betting favorites with 60-70% implied win probability win ~65% of the time; underdog upsets in BO3 format occur at ~35% rate historically"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.55, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "Market price (36% YES) sits SIGNIFICANTLY BELOW external sportsbook consensus (60-70% implied for RRQ Hoshi) \u2014 Polymarket is underpricing the favorite by ~20-30 percentage points. Sharp move at Apr 11 15:07 UTC shows +24pp swing on YES, -10.5pp on NO \u2014 suggests late informed money arrived backing RRQ Hoshi, but price has NOT fully recovered to sportsbook levels. Volatility spike (7.6pp/hr on YES, high amplitude swings) indicates uncertainty/panic trading rather than stable conviction \u2014 crowd may be