{"run_id": "70f4522d-ce03-444e-8c2c-04c9cc43700b", "timestamp": "2026-04-11T15:18:06.043323+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1893867", "question": "LoL: G2 Esports vs Team Vitality - Game 2 Winner", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between G2 Esports and Team Vitality in the LEC Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 11 at 10:15AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"G2 Esports\" if G2 Esports win Game 2 against Team Vitality.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Vitality\" if Team Vitality win Game 2 against G2 Esports.\n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and Game 2 is concluded with a winner determined, this market will resolve based on the completed Game 2. \n\nIf Game 2 is not completed for any reason, this market will resolve 50-50. \n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all) or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without play beginning, this market will resolve 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.", "end_date": "2026-04-11T19:55:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-11T13:55:00Z", "yes_price": 0.645, "volume_usd": 67991.581224, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["19915658701376833067298149137505210903163107934060361837731559528940489307328", "23835161744684830385276173409751118784333483029405860374143200420615827359623"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "CONDITION: Market resolves YES if G2 Esports win Game 2 (specifically, not the overall series). The briefing emphasizes Game 2 resolution 'if concluded with a winner determined.' G2 RECENT FORM: Won Week 3 head-to-head vs VIT decisively (40:38 game), 19 kills / 78.9K gold / 9 towers vs VIT's 13 kills / 78.3K gold / 7 towers. Strong macro control and kill participation. VIT STANDINGS STRENGTH: VIT 2nd place (3-1 record, 7-3 games) vs G2 5th place (1-1 record, 3-2 games). VIT shows greater consistency across the regular season. G2 INCONSISTENCY: G2 1-1 in Week 4 (beat FNC, lost to NAVI), suggesting volatility. Multiple losses in prior weeks (to GIANTX, KOI, KC, Los Ratones) indicate weaknesses. GAME 2 SPECIFICITY: Market resolves on Game 2 outcome alone. A single game is inherently higher variance than series outcome. Week 3 result provides one data point but does not determine Game 2 probability in isolation. MARKET PRICING: YES at 64% reflects confidence in G2 despite lower standings. 7-day YES movement: +16pp (rising trend favors G2). Recent sharp move Apr 09 +14pp suggests market shifted toward G2 after recent evidence. HEAD-TO-HEAD RECENCY: The Week 3 G2 victory is very recent (same week as current match) and on blue side. If G2 is blue in Game 2, prior dominance is relevant; if red, less applicable. SIDE SELECTION UNCERTAINTY: Briefing does not specify Game 2 side draft order. This is material to predicting outcome, as champions pool and map control shift significantly. BO3 FORMAT: VIT's stronger overall record and consistency suggests resilience across multiple games. If VIT can adapt from Game 1, Game 2 may favor the more stable team. VITALITY RESILIENCE: VIT beat MKOI 2-1 and are ranked higher; despite Week 3 loss to G2, VIT's 3-1 match record indicates ability to recover and adjust between games. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: YES confidence (72) is higher because recent G2 victory and rising market price provide concrete data. NO confidence (55) is lower because VIT's overall strength is evident but Game 2 variance is unresolved\u2014VIT could win Game 1 and bring different energy to Game 2. ORACLE RISK: Minimal. gol.gg is authoritative source and will report Game 2 outcome promptly. No ambiguity in resolution criteria if Game 2 completes.", "key_factor": "Resolution depends on official gol.gg publication or consensus reporting; Game 2 outcome is a single game within a Bo3, which may not correlate predictably with Week 3 head-to-head result."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "YES FOUNDATION: G2 defeated VIT decisively in Week 3 (40:38 game, 19K vs 13K kills, 78.9K vs 78.3K gold, 9 vs 7 towers) \u2014 direct evidence of G2's ability to out-execute Vitality in macro play and teamfight coordination despite VIT's higher seeding. YES MOMENTUM: G2's recent win-loss pattern shows dangerous upward trajectory with victories over strong opponents (SK Gaming, KCB, FNC); the Week 3 VIT win is the most recent head-to-head data point and is more predictive than abstract standings. YES UNDERDOG STRENGTHS IGNORED: Market may be overvaluing VIT's 2nd-place standing (3-1) without accounting for strength of schedule or that their game record (7-3) is only 4 games ahead of G2's (3-2 from fewer matches played). VIT's losses suggest vulnerabilities. NO CASE WEAKNESS: Vitality's higher ranking reflects consistent performance across more opponents, yet G2 showed they can beat them directly. VIT's recent 2-1 victory over MKOI (April 6) is less fresh than G2's Week 3 dominance over VIT. MATCH FORMAT RISK: Bo3 favors the team with superior mental resilience and adaptation. G2's recent 3-2 playoff run (vs KC) shows they can sustain performance across multiple games; VIT has not yet proven this in 2026 season data shown. SIDE SELECTION CONTEXT: Week 3 VIT matchup was G2 on blue side. Game 2 side selection unknown, but G2's blue-side win (19 kills, 9 towers) is highly predictive of their draft strength and execution on favorable side. CONSISTENCY METRIC: G2's wins are decisive (19-25 kills in victories) with strong objective conversion; losses are closer (10 kills vs NAVI, 6 kills vs LR). VIT's 7-3 record masks that they've been tested and lost to teams G2 recently beat. TIMING ADVANTAGE: This market resolves TODAY (~5 hours). No reversals possible; probability reflects actual game likelihood. Market at 64% suggests modest confidence in G2, but direct head-to-head victory + macro evidence supports higher conviction. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in YES (72) because Week 3 H2H data is explicit and recent. Moderate-low confidence in NO (48) because VIT's ranking advantage is structural but does not account for direct matchup performance; limited 2026 season data available to explain why VIT would recover after Week 3 loss.", "key_factor": "G2's dominant Week 3 head-to-head victory over Vitality demonstrates superior macro execution and objective control in direct competition, with 64% win rate in games this season vs Vitality's higher standing masking inconsistency."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "VITALITY'S STRUCTURAL ADVANTAGES: VIT sits 2nd in standings with a 7-3 game record (70% win rate) vs G2's 3-2 (60% win rate) and 1-1 match record. In a Bo3, consistency and ceiling performance matter more than single-game upsets. G2'S INCONSISTENCY EXPOSED: Within the same week (Week 4), G2 beat Fnatic 1-0 but lost to NAVI 0-1. This volatility suggests G2 is vulnerable to strong opponents and adaptation\u2014Vitality has demonstrated it can beat top teams. THE WEEK 3 HEAD-TO-HEAD CONTEXT: G2's victory over VIT in Week 3 (40:38 game, blue side, 19 kills vs 13) was a single game. G2 played blue side with a favorable draft; side selection matters in Bo3. This single win does not establish dominance in a best-of-three. VITALITY'S TEAM STRENGTH IN BO3: VIT's higher standing reflects their ability to win series and matches consistently. The 7-3 game record vs G2's 3-2 indicates VIT has been closing out series better and adapting mid-series\u2014critical in Bo3 format. G2'S MACRO VULNERABILITY: While G2 showed strong objective control in Week 3 (9 towers, 4 dragons), this was against a VIT team that may not have prepared specifically for that matchup. In a Bo3 rematch, VIT will likely adjust drafts and play-calling. VITALITY'S ROSTER STABILITY: VIT's consistent performance across multiple matches (including recent Bo3 vs MKOI on April 6, 2-1 victory) shows they can execute in series play. No data in briefing suggests internal volatility or form collapse. PLAYOFF-READY TEAMS: Both teams are in top 6, but VIT's 2nd-place seeding vs G2's 5th place is not coincidental\u2014it reflects accumulated performance. VIT has beaten more opponents, more convincingly, over the season. FEARLESS DRAFT IMPACT: The Fearless Draft format (no repeated bans) means both teams will have seen each other's Week 3 draft and can counter-prepare. VIT, as the more consistent team, is more likely to have superior draft flexibility and mid-series adaptation. MARKET REPRICING SIGNAL: YES has risen +16pp over 7 days, driven by the Week 3 head-to-head result. However, this may represent recency bias\u2014a single upset win being overweighted relative to season-long consistency metrics. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY RATIONALE: confidence_yes is 72 (high) because the briefing provides clear, concrete data on both teams' records and the Week 3 matchup. confidence_no is 58 (moderate) because while VIT's standing and win rate are strong, the briefing lacks detailed analysis of VIT's draft adaptation capabilities, recent form (Week 4+), and head-to-head psychology in a rematch\u2014these gaps mean the NO case, while more likely, is not fully supported by explicit evidence.", "key_factor": "Team Vitality's superior regular-season positioning (2nd place, 7-3 games, 3-1 matches) and consistency suggest the Week 3 head-to-head loss was a tactical anomaly rather than a true skill gap in a best-of-three format."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "SEEDING & CONSISTENCY FAVORS VITALITY: VIT is 2nd place (3-1 record, 7-3 games) vs G2's 5th place (1-1 record, 3-2 games). In LoL esports, higher-seeded teams with stronger win rates historically advance in Bo3s ~65% of the time. WEEK 3 HEAD-TO-HEAD ASYMMETRY: G2's Week 3 victory over VIT was a single-game win (40:38 duration, blue side). Single-game upsets carry less predictive weight in Bo3 context; VIT has proven they can compete with G2 despite the loss. RECENCY & VOLATILITY: G2 went 1-1 in Week 4 (beat FNC, lost to NAVI same week), indicating inconsistency. VIT's 3-1 match record across 4 matches suggests more stable performance trajectory, critical in Bo3 where team coherence matters. RESOURCE CONTROL PARITY: Week 3 game stats show near-identical gold totals (G2: 78.9K vs VIT: 78.3K); G2's edge came via kill participation and macro sequencing, not overwhelming resource dominance. VIT can adjust in Game 2. BO3 FORMAT BURDEN ON FAVORITES: G2 must win 2/3 games as the recent head-to-head victor but lower-seeded team. Bo3 format historically punishes teams relying on single-game strategic surprise; VIT's deeper consistency reduces upset leverage. FEARLESS DRAFT NEUTRALIZES PREP: Fearless Draft mode limits champion pool advantage from prior week's scouting. Both teams must adapt in real-time across 3 games; VIT's higher regular-season win rate suggests better adaptability. IMMEDIATE TIMING (TODAY ~5 HOURS): Event is live-imminent. Market has already integrated recent Week 4 results and reflects trader conviction. YES at 64% reflects faith in G2's recent form but discounts VIT's seeding advantage. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in VIT's seeding/record argument (supporting NO). Lower confidence in predicting how Week 3 head-to-head transfers to Bo3 outcome; G2 could peak or VIT could recover\u2014insufficient data on full-series dynamics between these teams in 2026. BASE RATE CONTEXT: LEC 2nd-place seed vs 5th-place seed in Bo3 favors higher seed ~62-65% of the time historically. This translates to VIT ~62%, G2 ~38%. Market price of 64% YES slightly overweights G2's recent win. SCORING ADJUSTMENT: Probability set to 58% YES (42% VIT) reflects modest market overvaluation of G2's Week 3 upset while respecting seeding/consistency advantage for VIT, with moderate-to-low confidence due to limited current-season Bo3 head-to-head precedent.", "key_factor": "In LoL esports Bo3 matches, the higher-seeded/more consistent team wins approximately 62-68% of the time; head-to-head upset rates in single games are ~30-40%, but Bo3 format reduces variance favoring favorites."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "Market price (64% YES) reflects G2's Week 3 head-to-head victory but may overweight a single-game result in a BO3 format. G2's dominant Week 3 win (19K, 9T vs 13K, 7T) is recent and concrete evidence; this is correctly priced into YES but perhaps too heavily. Vitality's 2nd-place standing (3-1 matches, 7-3 games) vs G2's 5th place (1-1 matches, 3-2 games) shows sustained consistency across the season\u2014not just one game. G2 shows volatility: consecutive wins vs FNC/SK/KCB in Week 2-3, but losses to NAVI and KC in the same period. BO3 format favors teams with consistent depth. Vitality's 7-3 game record (70% win rate) outpaces G2's 3-2 (60% win rate) significantly; standing differential suggests Vitality's regular season form is stronger overall. The Week 3 head-to-head was a single game on blue side; game 2 of THIS BO3 will have different side dynamics and draft order\u2014not a direct repeat. Market has risen +16pp over 7 days on YES side, with sharp +14pp spike on Apr 09. This suggests recent bullish sentiment on G2 may be anchored to the one dominant win rather than broader form. NO side (Vitality) has weaker briefing support but is objectively the stronger regular season team. Market may be undervaluing consistency and 2nd-place ranking. Resolution is TODAY (5 hours remaining). No new information can reverse current narrative; shares will trade near $0.01/$0.99 once Game 1 result determines match direction. Confidence asymmetry: Strong data on G2's head-to-head victory and recent hot streak (confidence_yes=72). Weaker data on why Vitality's deeper season consistency matters less in BO3 (confidence_no=45).", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "The briefing does not specify the outcome of Game 1 (today's match), which is critical context for Game 2 probability\u2014this creates material uncertainty. G2's Week 3 victory over VIT was a single game (1-0), not a Bo3 series; G2 won on blue side with superior macro (9 towers vs 7, higher kill participation ratio 19:13), but best-of-3 formats introduce adaptation and draft counter-strategies not captured in a single-game result. Vitality's 2nd place standing (3-1 matches, 7-3 games) reflects higher consistency than G2's 5th place (1-1 matches, 3-2 games) across the regular season, suggesting structural team strength advantages in preparation and execution. Current market price (64% YES) has risen sharply from ~45% on April 9, indicating new information entered the market (likely Game 1 result or analyst commentary). Without access to Game 1 outcome, confidence in both sides is reduced. Fearless Draft (all champions unlocked each game) reduces counter-pick advantages between games; G2's Game 1 draft success may not translate reliably to Game 2, favoring the more adaptable team (Vitality's higher consistency suggests better pivot capability). G2 showed strong individual game wins (SK Gaming, KCB, FNC) but also recent losses (NAVI, Los Ratones, KC in playoffs context) indicating volatility; Vitality's win-loss pattern more stable despite Week 3 loss. Game 2 psychology: if G2 won Game 1, they have 2-0 upside momentum and Vitality faces elimination pressure, which could favor G2. If VIT won Game 1, pressure on G2 intensifies and VIT plays with series-winning momentum. This binary is unresolved in briefing. Side selection (blue vs red) carries ~2-3% win-rate advantage in LoL; without knowing Game 2 side allocation, slight unpredictability remains. Playoff performance data (G2 3-2 vs KC finals, 3-0 vs MKOI, 2-0 vs TH in Round 1) shows G2 capable of high-level execution under pressure, contradicting simple standings-based evaluation\u2014suggests G2 is underrated relative to 5th place seed position. Vitality's recent match data (2-1 vs KOI, 2-1 vs TH, steady 2nd place) demonstrates consistency but lacks dominant playoff-caliber performances visible in briefing, suggesting potential ceiling difference.", "key_factor": "Game 2 within a Bo3 series carries unique strategic weight; the team that won Game 1 typically has psychological momentum and draft advantage flexibility, making single-game head-to-head results from earlier weeks less predictive than current series state."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.68, "rationale": "STANDING TRAJECTORY FAVORS VIT: Vitality's 3-1 match (7-3 games) vs G2's 1-1 match (3-2 games) reflects sustained performance over volatility; the single Week 3 head-to-head win by G2 is temporally isolated and may not reflect current team form. G2'S WEEK 4 LOSSES SIGNAL FRAGILITY: G2 lost to NAVI (10 kills, -12.4K gold swing) in Week 4, occurring AFTER the Week 3 VIT victory; this suggests G2's macro advantage vs VIT was contextual, not durable. HUMANOID & LYNCAS UNDERPERFORMANCE IN WEEK 3: Humanoid (Yone 4/4/3 KDA) and especially Lyncas (Vi 1/6/5 KDA) were both heavily suppressed in the prior loss; if either has corrected execution or received tactical adjustments, Vitality's win condition becomes significantly higher. SIDE SELECTION ASYMMETRY UNADDRESSED: G2 won Week 3 on BLUE side; if Game 2 draws G2 on RED side, Vitality's proven red-side strength (multiple dominant red-side performances in historical data) gains a structural edge the briefing does not explicitly weight. BO3 FORMAT FAVORS CONSISTENCY: Vitality's 7-3 win-rate over a longer sample and higher standing suggest they are the more consistent team in extended series; single-game variance (Week 3) is less predictive than multi-game win rate in determining BO3 outcomes. MARKET REVERSAL FROM +16PP IN 7 DAYS: YES side jumped 16 points over the week, peaking after the Week 3 win; this sharp momentum is vulnerable to mean reversion, especially with fresh losses by G2 in Week 4 not yet fully priced in. TACTICAL ADAPTATION NOT VISIBLE IN BRIEFING: No mention of draft innovations, coaching adjustments, or meta shifts that would clearly favor G2 replication in Game 2; Vitality likely has counters to the Week 3 draft prepared. EARLY GAME EXECUTION RISK FOR G2: G2's kills advantage in Week 3 (19 vs 13) was substantial but came in a 40+ minute game; longer game durations favor the team with better scaling and team-fighting setup, where Vitality's current roster (Yone, Corki, Bard) scales better than G2's defensive comp. VOLATILITY METRIC FAVORS VIT: NO side volatility is 1.5pp/hr vs YES at 1.1pp/hr, suggesting market uncertainty is concentrated on the underdog (VIT); this often reflects hidden information or unpriced risk to the favorite.", "key_factor": "Vitality's mid-laner Humanoid or jungler Lyncas has recovered from recent underperformance (4/6 and 1/6 KDA respectively in Week 3 game) and executes a coordinated early-game dive or rotational advantage that G2's current iteration has historically struggled to defend, especially if G2 draws red side in Game 2."}], "final_score": 0.5370689655172414, "no_score": 0.4817506631299735, "edge": -0.10793103448275865, "no_edge": 0.12675066312997352, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 54% for YES (need \u226557