{"run_id": "40d89f1f-2635-43a8-bc52-ca3b5b3ae1c3", "timestamp": "2026-04-11T23:03:08.165327+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1935430", "question": "Counter-Strike: BESTIA Academy vs Vexa (BO3) - CCT South America Challengers #1 Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Upper bracket round 1 match between BESTIA Academy and Vexa in the CCT South America Challengers #1 Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 11 at 5:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"BESTIA Academy\" if BESTIA Academy win the match against Vexa.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Vexa\" if Vexa win the match against BESTIA Academy.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-12T03:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-11T21:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.72, "volume_usd": 27365.80684699999, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["76812080311039133196993803632474706432485093607139622912650591040448339399688", "32987854364196236016838864334701446868392438063715115949665397592091971367746"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "BESTIA Academy shows recent wins (Atrix 2:0, Magicos 2:1, Procyon 2:0) demonstrating competitive capability at this tournament tier. BESTIA Academy's record is mixed but trend-positive in early April: won 2:0 vs Procyon (Apr 5) after losses to ex-KR\u00dc and MIBR Academy (Apr 2-4). Multiple 0:2 losses to ex-KR\u00dc, MIBR Academy, and ALKA indicate vulnerability to stronger opponents, suggesting inconsistent form. Vexa has no performance data in briefing; ranked #39 in South America by HLTV (1 point) vs BESTIA Academy's more active tournament presence; suggests significant skill gap favoring BESTIA Academy. Market price of 72% YES reflects substantial confidence in BESTIA Academy; upward movement of +10.5pp over 24 hours suggests late shift toward favorites or match intel. Sharp move on Apr 11 01:00 UTC (+20.5pp on YES) followed by partial retracement (-12.0pp at 07:00 UTC) indicates volatility, possibly pre-match intelligence or lineup changes. BO3 format favors better-prepared team; BESTIA Academy's tournament infrastructure (academy status, consistent scheduling) vs Vexa's minimal recent activity. Briefing explicitly notes 'no recent match data for Vexa' limiting comparative analysis; market may have access to pre-match stats, odds adjustments, or scout reports not in briefing. Event timing is TODAY (~4 hours to resolution); at this stage, market reflects near-complete information; low likelihood of major reversals unless surprise withdrawal/forfeit. Forfeit/walkover scenarios resolve to 50-50 per criteria, but such events are rare in organized CCT tournaments; normal competitive outcome highly likely.", "key_factor": "No recent match data available for Vexa, creating significant information asymmetry; market may be pricing in pre-match intelligence unavailable in briefing."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "BESTIA Academy is the clear market favorite at 72%, and the briefing provides tangible support for this positioning: recent wins against Procyon (2:0 on Apr 5), Magicos (2:1 on Mar 31), and Atrix (2:0 on Mar 29) demonstrate recent positive momentum in close tournament windows. Market momentum reinforces confidence: YES prices rose +10.5pp over 7 days with a sharp +20.5pp jump on Apr 11 01:00 UTC, suggesting informed traders or bookmakers obtained information confirming BESTIA Academy's edge. Vexa is ranked #39 in South America (1 HLTV point) and #32 in Brazil rankings with no recent match history in the briefing\u2014this absence of data is itself a weakness signal. The inability to assess Vexa's current form, roster stability, or map pool creates asymmetric risk favoring the known quantity. BESTIA Academy, while showing inconsistency (losses to ex-KR\u00dc, MIBR Academy, ALKA, UNO MILLE), competed in multiple Tier 2/C-Tier tournaments in March-April 2026 and demonstrated wins in the weeks leading to this playoff match. Academy team designation suggests organized coaching, scrim infrastructure, and player development systems that a lower-ranked challenger team may lack. The BO3 format favors the team with better map pool and adaptability\u2014BESTIA Academy's recent matches show competitive play across Nuke, Inferno, and other maps, suggesting flexibility needed for best-of-three play. BESTIA Academy's inconsistency (alternating wins/losses) is partially mitigated by the context that they were playing stronger opponents (ex-KR\u00dc is a recognized name, MIBR Academy is main-squad affiliated). Recent wins came against tier-appropriate competition. Vexa's deep anonymity in ranking (1 HLTV point, no match history provided) and lack of recent tournament appearances raises questions about roster cohesion, preparation time, and competitive readiness for a playoff environment. A team with near-zero ranking points is statistically unlikely to upset a recent-form team with multiple documented wins. Short event timing (TODAY, ~4 hours to resolution) limits possibility of reversals from training data. The market has settled at 72% YES after recent volatility, suggesting that whichever catalysts drove the Apr 11 01:00 UTC +20.5pp jump (e.g., roster confirmation, analyst reports, or insider information) remain in effect. Confidence in YES is HIGH (72) because BESTIA Academy's recent record is documented and positive relative to invisible competition. Confidence in NO is LOW (35) because Vexa's complete absence from the briefing means critical information (roster form, recent wins, head-to-head history) cannot be used to build a counter-case\u2014this asymmetry justifies lower confidence on the underdog side despite formal 28% pricing. The market appears correctly calibrated: BESTIA Academy's documented recent wins + academy infrastructure + Vexa's anonymity + BO3 map-pool advantage justify a 70%+ probability without overconfidence. The 72% price reflects genuine edge rather than mispricing.", "key_factor": "BESTIA Academy's recent string of map-pool versatility and recent wins (Procyon 2:0, Magicos 2:1, Atrix 2:0) combined with academy infrastructure advantage against an unranked Vexa team with zero available performance data."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.32, "confidence_yes": 0.55, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "BESTIA Academy shows extreme volatility: wins 2:0 vs Procyon, then loses 0:2 to ex-KR\u00dc same day (April 5); wins 2:1 vs Magicos, then 0:2 to UNO MILLE within days. This alternating pattern signals instability, not form. Recent comprehensive record reveals BESTIA lost 0:2 to MIBR Academy (April 2), 0:2 to ALKA (April 2), and 0:2 to ex-KR\u00dc twice (April 4-5). These are not random losses\u2014multiple 0:2 sweeps suggest structural weaknesses in map execution or tactical preparation. BESTIA's only notable wins in April came against Procyon (2:0) and lower-tier opponents; no wins vs established regional competition (FURIA, Legacy, ex-KR\u00dc). The team's strength tier is significantly below the top-2 South American squads. HLTV rankings place Vexa at #39 South America and #32 Brazil (1 HLTV point each as of April 6); BESTIA Academy is not even ranked in top-40, suggesting Vexa may be marginally competitive or similar tier. Market's 72% YES price assumes BESTIA is significantly stronger than available ranking data supports. Zero match history provided for Vexa in briefing prevents comparative analysis, but lack of data cuts both ways: Vexa's recent opponents/results unknown, creating asymmetric uncertainty that favors upset scenarios. Teams with hidden form advantage often trade at underdogs in regional online events. Playoff format (single elimination, BO3) increases volatility vs. regular season. BESTIA's inconsistency and Vexa's mystery form make binary outcomes more likely than the smooth 72/28 split suggests. Market price movement shows +10.5pp swing for YES and -10.5pp for NO over 24 hours, with sharp April 11 reversal (-12pp for YES), indicating recent uncertainty or new information. This volatility is unusually high for 4 hours before match start, suggesting smart money remains unsure. BESTIA Academy's designation as 'academy team' does not guarantee superior play in Challengers circuit; academy rosters sometimes underperform vs. independent motivated teams due to development-phase focus rather than peak performance. No evidence in briefing that Vexa is weaker; absence of data is not evidence of weakness. Underdog at 28% pricing may deserve 35-40% based on BESTIA's demonstrated inconsistency and low absolute rating. Confidence in YES (55) reflects BESTIA's isolated wins and academy infrastructure, but tempered by severity and frequency of 0:2 losses. Confidence in NO (62) reflects strong concern over BESTIA volatility and unknown Vexa strength, but limited by near-zero Vexa data forcing reliance on negative inference.", "key_factor": "BESTIA Academy's severe inconsistency and pattern of heavy losses to mid-tier opponents despite isolated wins suggests vulnerability to an underrated Vexa team in a high-stakes playoff format."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.58, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "- BESTIA Academy ranks #39-40 in South America HLTV rankings (1 HLTV point); Vexa ranks #32-39 (1 HLTV point) \u2014 effectively peer-level teams with minimal ranking separation.\n- Recent form mixed: BESTIA won 2:0 vs Procyon and 2:1 vs Magicos (late Mar/early Apr), but suffered 0:2 losses to ex-KR\u00dc, MIBR Academy, ALKA, and UNO MILLE \u2014 no clear dominance pattern.\n- Zero head-to-head or recent Vexa match data in briefing limits comparative strength assessment; cannot identify Vexa's recent form, win rate, or map pool.\n- Market price 72% YES is elevated relative to historical base rate (~55-60%) for academy-tier peer matchups; suggests market has access to intel (player roster updates, scrim results, or recent form) not present in briefing.\n- Sharp market moves (\u00b120.5pp Apr 11 01:00 UTC) suggest late information influx or professional betting activity; 72% reflects recent confidence but also high volatility signal.\n- BO3 format and TODAY timing (4 hours to match) means minimal time for further reversals; current odds likely reflect proximate knowledge.\n- Confidence_yes = 58: BESTIA Academy's recent mixed record and academy-tier competition level justifies moderate lean toward YES, but lack of Vexa data and elevated market price vs. historical baseline create uncertainty.\n- Confidence_no = 42: Insufficient data on Vexa's actual strength, recent form, and head-to-head tendencies; cannot robustly justify a NO case beyond peer-level ranking parity.", "key_factor": "Academy-tier Counter-Strike teams win ~55-65% of matches vs. unranked/low-ranking competitors in regional C-Tier tournaments; BO3 format slightly favors higher-ranked/more consistent teams."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "BESTIA Academy has recent wins (Magicos 2:1, Atrix 2:0, Procyon 2:0) but heavily inconsistent record with multiple 0:2 losses to mid-tier opponents (ex-KR\u00dc, MIBR Academy, ALKA, UNO MILLE) Current 72% YES price reflects academy team pedigree and recent positive momentum, but volatility in last 24h (+10.5pp swing) suggests reactive trading rather than conviction Critical data gap: Vexa has zero recent match history in briefing\u2014cannot assess their current form, roster quality, or head-to-head tendencies. Market is pricing YES partly by elimination. HLTV rankings show Vexa ranked #32-39 in South America (1 HLTV point) vs BESTIA's implied academy tier\u2014suggests BESTIA has structural advantage, but low ranking points indicate both teams operate at similar competitive level Market shows Rational vibe: 72% YES reflects legitimate form edge, but 28% NO is underpriced given complete absence of Vexa data. If Vexa is competent, NO side offers value. Sharp 20.5pp move upward on Apr 11 01:00 UTC followed by 12pp reversal suggests late information influx or line-shopping, not fundamental shift in team quality BO3 format reduces upset probability vs BO1, supporting BESTIA as slight favorite, but inconsistency (alternating W-L) signals team volatility that 72% price may not fully reflect Confidence_YES high (72) due to demonstrable recent wins and academy structure; confidence_NO low (45) due to complete information void on Vexa\u2014cannot properly evaluate underdog case without performance data Event timing (TODAY, 4 hours to resolution) limits reversal likelihood; any last-minute news would already be baked into volatile 24h trading pattern", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "BESTIA Academy's recent record (last 10 days): 4 wins, 5 losses across multiple C/B-tier tournaments\u2014demonstrates competitive participation but not dominance; wins cluster on April 5-6 (Procyon 2:0, BIG Academy 1:2 comeback). Pattern analysis: BESTIA loses cleanly to ex-KR\u00dc (0:2, 1:2) and MIBR Academy (0:2)\u2014these are demonstrably stronger teams; beats weaker opponents (Atrix 2:0, Magicos 2:1, Procyon 2:0)\u2014suggests tier-appropriate seeding in Challengers bracket. Vexa HLTV ranking: #39 South America as of April 6, 2026 (1 point)\u2014barely-tracked team status; BESTIA Academy not explicitly ranked but competes in higher-tier tournaments; ranking asymmetry implies skill gap, though rankings can lag amateur scene activity. Zero head-to-head or recent Vexa match data in briefing\u2014cannot assess Vexa's current form, map pool, or player consistency; this is critical missing information for BO3 prediction. BO3 format advantage: BESTIA's map pool shows competence (Nuke, Inferno wins recorded); BO3 length favors prepared teams with coaching\u2014academy structure suggests better preparation than unranked challengers. Market price history signal: YES side surged +20.5pp on Apr 11 01:00 UTC, then corrected -12pp at 07:00 UTC; suggests community information influx (likely player roster, scrim results, or odds model update) followed by skepticism\u2014current 72% reflects post-correction consensus. Event timing critical: Match is TODAY (~4 hours), making substantial reversal unlikely; if Vexa were clearly superior, market would have compressed harder given L1 betting syndicate activity; persistence of 28% NO suggests non-trivial upset potential or genuine uncertainty on Vexa's capability. Institutional factor: BESTIA Academy branding implies BESTIA org's main roster coaching/infrastructure spillover; Vexa's four-letter moniker and unranked status suggest independent stack with less formal support. Confidence asymmetry justified: BESTIA Academy's recent tournament activity and ranking visibility provide actionable data; Vexa opacity (no match records, minimal HLTV footprint, ranking floor at 1 point) means NO side cannot be confidently assessed\u2014confidence_no must stay low.", "key_factor": "BESTIA Academy's recent form shows volatility against tier-comparable opponents, but the academy designation signals institutional backing; however, the complete absence of Vexa match history in HLTV records creates severe asymmetric information that should suppress confidence in any directional estimate."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.68, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "BESTIA Academy shows extreme volatility: 5 wins and 6 losses in last 11 matches across mixed competition levels, with no clear trajectory\u2014recent wins vs. weaker teams (Atrix, Procyon, Magicos) are offset by crushing losses to ex-KR\u00dc (1:2, 0:2) and academy rivals (MIBR Academy 0:2). Zero Vexa match data exists in briefing\u2014no recent results, map pool, player form, or head-to-head history provided; market is pricing BESTIA at 72% YES largely on name recognition and academy infrastructure, not on competitive intelligence. Market moved +20.5pp for YES on Apr 11 01:00 UTC then -12pp at 07:00 UTC, suggesting sharp disagreement and potential information asymmetry; neither consensus nor external news visible in briefing to justify 72% conviction. BO3 format favors the underdog with preparation\u2014if Vexa has scouted BESTIA's map bans, weak sides (Nuke vulnerability hinted in losses?), or player tendencies, a 2:0 or 2:1 upset is structurally plausible in a single-elimination playoffs match where one bad series ends the run. BESTIA lost to UNO MILLE 0:2 and ex-KR\u00dc twice (1:2, 0:2) recently, yet market shows no reflection of 'form cliff' vs. academy peers\u2014this compression suggests traders are overweighting recent micro-wins and underweighting consistency. Absence of Vexa data is the black swan: if Vexa is a rising team, roster-stable, or has developed chemistry, market opacity creates 25-35% true probability space that 72% YES does not price. BESTIA faced BIG Academy (mixed 1:2 loss, 2:0 win) and Passion UA (0:2 loss) in Urban Riga Open\u2014international exposure but no synergy evident; Vexa domestic focus may grant psychological advantage in local meta. Event timing: LIVE/IMMINENT (4 hours to match)\u2014sharp move volatility suggests late-hour betting on incomplete information; if Vexa roster news or leaked anti-BESTIA prep surfaces in final hours, reversal to 40-50% YES is rapid.", "key_factor": "Vexa executes a coordinated tactical innovation or map-specific preparation strategy that exploits BESTIA Academy's inconsistent recent form and lack of available scouting data, capitalizing on low market expectations to secure a BO3 upset."}], "final_score": 0.6278038379530917, "no_score": 0.40298412698412694, "edge": -0.09219616204690828, "no_edge": 0.12298412698412692, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "YES-side confidence too low: 67% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1935430", "question": "Counter-Strike: BESTIA Academy vs Vexa (BO3) - CCT South America Challengers #1 Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Upper bracket round 1 match between BESTIA Acade