 issues would already be known. Reversal would require unexpected developments with minimal time. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Cannot independently verify either team's strength due to missing competitive data. Confidence in YES estimate is LOW (35) because reliance on market price signal alone. Confidence in NO estimate is also LOW (32) because no counter-evidence exists. Both sides equally data-starved. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: Source is gol.gg with fallback to credible reporting within 2 hours. No ambiguity in team name matching (both names are standard abbreviations). Minimal oracle risk. FORFEIT/CANCELLATION RISK: Criteria establish 50-50 resolution for cancellations or walkouts. No briefing evidence of health issues, visa problems, or logistical concerns that would trigger this clause. PROBABILITY ASSIGNMENT: Market price of 64% for YES reflects aggregated information from informed traders. Without contradicting data, adopting market-implied probability is reasonable. Modest adjustment downward (64\u219264) reflects uncertainty, but no strong reason to deviate significantly from market consensus.", "key_factor": "Briefing contains only LCK meta statistics and no team-specific data (rosters, recent form, head-to-head records) for either BNK FEARX or DN SOOPers, making competitive analysis impossible."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.64, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "MARKET STRUCTURE: YES is priced at 64% (favorite) vs NO at 36% (underdog), with YES showing +13.5pp 7-day momentum (+16.5pp spike on Apr 05, +7.5pp on Apr 07). This rising trend and current favorite status suggest informed markets have positioned toward FEARX. MOMENTUM ANALYSIS: YES side gained 13.5pp over 7 days while NO side fell 13.5pp. Sharp move on Apr 05 (+16.5pp YES) suggests new information favored FEARX; Apr 07 volatility shows market confidence solidifying around the 64% level despite minor corrections. UNDERDOG WEAKNESSES: NO side (DN SOOPers) has no specific performance data presented in briefing. Absence of positive information, combined with falling market odds, suggests SOOPers lacks notable recent wins or is perceived as weaker in current LCK meta. META ALIGNMENT UNKNOWN: Briefing shows Corki/Sion at 100% WR and Anivia/Gnar/Pantheon at 66.67% WR in LCK 2026 Rounds 1-2, but does not specify which team proficiency with these champions. FEARX's favorite status may reflect superior meta adaptation or draft skill. CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains NO direct team rosters, win-loss records, recent form, or head-to-head history for BNK FEARX vs DN SOOPers. Cannot independently verify why FEARX is favored beyond market pricing itself. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes = 45 (market consensus visible but unvalidated by team data) and confidence_no = 35 (SOOPers underdog status unclear without counter-evidence). Market may be correct, but limited intel constrains conviction on either side. TIMING CONSIDERATION: Event resolves TODAY (15 hours to match start). Odds movement has stabilized; no further reversal catalysts evident in briefing. FEARX's 64% reflects pre-match settled market consensus rather than late-breaking news. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: BO3 format means FEARX must win 2 of 3 games. Market-implied 64% for series win is reasonable given typical competitive balance, but without team-specific data, this remains inference from price action rather than fundamental analysis. ADVOCATE POSITION: As the Bull for the favorite, FEARX's rising odds from ~50% to 64% over one week signals informed capital flow toward FEARX. Market participants with access to team intel, recent scrims, or meta meta-game appear to favor FEARX. The question is whether they are right. UNDERDOG CASE (why NOT to go higher on YES): SOOPers name recognition and lack of negative information could indicate a competitive lower-tier team capable of upset. BO3 format allows underdog to steal 1-2 games. Without roster/form data, cannot rule out 30-40% upside for SOOPers.", "key_factor": "Market consensus (64% YES) reflects accumulated betting information and professional analysis favoring BNK FEARX, though the briefing lacks direct team-specific data to independently validate this edge."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains zero team-specific performance metrics, roster compositions, or recent match histories for either BNK FEARX or DN SOOPers. All available data consists of generic LCK meta statistics (Corki/Sion 100% WR, Anivia 66.67% WR) unlinked to either team's proficiency. MARKET PRICING APPEARS OVERCONFIDENT: YES side has risen +13.5pp over 7 days with sharp moves on Apr 05 (+16.5pp) and Apr 07 (+7.5pp), yet briefing provides NO justification for this upward drift. This suggests market momentum may be driving YES pricing rather than fundamental team strength. UNDERDOG CASE FOR NO: Without evidence of FEARX superiority (roster depth, recent wins, meta adaptability), the 64% YES price assumes FEARX dominance without supporting data. DN SOOPers' underdog status (36%) may reflect market narrative bias rather than actual competitive weakness. BO3 FORMAT FAVORS ADAPTABILITY: Best-of-3 series allow teams to adjust drafts and strategies between games. A team with superior meta reading or counter-pick preparation (unknown for both teams) could exploit weaknesses invisible in pre-match data. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: Rounds 1-2 of LCK spring season typically feature unpredictable results as teams are still calibrating meta interpretation and roster synergy. Early-season matches have higher upset potential than established tournament standings suggest. VOLUME & SPREAD SIGNAL UNCERTAINTY: $23,533 trading volume is modest; the YES/NO prices not summing to 100% (64%+36%=100%) indicates a tight orderbook spread, suggesting informed traders are also uncertain. CONFIDENCE LIMITATIONS: Confidence_yes set to 28 (low) beca