on sub or injury not yet public could dramatically shift the BO3 outcome\u2014SOOPers could have prepared a roster surprise. REVERSE INFORMATION ASYMMETRY: Market has priced BNK FEARX heavily (64%) despite zero comparative data. This suggests consensus bettors are relying on brand recognition, historical pedigree, or external scouting reports entirely absent from the briefing. A contrarian edge exists if DN SOOPers has quietly improved or BNK FEARX is overrated on legacy. NO SIDE UNDER-PRICED: NO side (36%) lacks any stated weaknesses or disqualifying factors in the briefing. The absence of negative data on SOOPers is itself suspicious\u2014this could be a sleeping underdog with minimal public coverage but strong internal preparation. DRAFT FLEXIBILITY UNKNOWN: Briefing does not detail either team's champion pool depth, flex picks, or counter-pick strategies. In BO3 format, teams that can shift meta adaptation mid-series (e.g., SOOPers pivoting to Anivia/Gnar lanes BNK cannot contest) gain a massive edge. TIMING PRESSURE: Event resolves TODAY in ~15 hours. If a roster announcement, injury report, or scrim leak breaks in final hours favoring SOOPers, market cannot correct and shares will trade at distorted prices until resolution. CONFIDENCE SEVERELY DEPRESSED ON BOTH SIDES: absence of direct competitive intel means neither YES nor NO side can be defended with high conviction. Confidence scores capped at 35/32 reflect fundamental data insufficiency, not close competitive balance. MARKET PRICE INCONSISTENCY: YES at 64%, NO at 36% = 100% vig accounted for, but no underlying match statistics justify this 28-point gap. Either YES is overconfident on legacy bias, or briefing is deliberately withholding SOOPers' recent form data (possible if SOOPers has been hiding scrim results).", "key_factor": "DN SOOPers fields an unexpected roster substitution (likely mid or support) that exploits BNK FEARX's scouting gap, or a critical meta champion (Corki/Sion/Anivia) that BNK cannot draft/play at elite level despite recent market confidence."}], "final_score": 0.5853508771929825, "no_score": 0.4243478260869566, "edge": -0.0496491228070175, "no_edge": 0.0593478260869566, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "YES-side confidence too low: 33% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1867384", "question": "LoL: BNK FEARX vs DN SOOPers (BO3) - LCK Rounds 1-2", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between BNK FEARX and DN SOOPers in the LCK Rounds 1-2, initially scheduled for April 12 at 4:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"BNK FEARX\" if BNK FEARX win the match against DN SOOPers.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"DN SOOPers\" if DN SOOPers win the match against BNK FEARX.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting di