{"run_id": "55dd363e-412e-4b22-a0e0-30ec83a9ea27", "timestamp": "2026-04-11T23:13:33.149578+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1902279", "question": "Mobile Legends Bang Bang: Geek Fam ID vs RRQ Hoshi (BO3) - MPL Indonesia Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Mobile Legends Bang Bang match between Geek Fam ID and RRQ Hoshi in the MPL Indonesia Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 12 at 6:15AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Geek Fam ID\" if Geek Fam ID win the match against RRQ Hoshi.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"RRQ Hoshi\" if RRQ Hoshi win the match against Geek Fam ID.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://liquipedia.net/mobilelegends/Main_Page. However, if https://liquipedia.net/mobilelegends/Main_Page has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-12T16:15:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-12T10:15:00Z", "yes_price": 0.585, "volume_usd": 609.2728900000001, "category": "mobile-legends-bang-bang", "clob_token_ids": ["54056471206744506658614158435257600613256473796685090521520416122504498619766", "90856610985240323459773643986594691946708251144067505487889926680933802977792"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.27, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: Match must be played to completion with a decisive winner (not canceled, tied, forfeited, or delayed >7 days). The criteria are clear and unambiguous. MATCH TIMING: Scheduled for April 12 at 6:15 AM ET (~17 hours from briefing timestamp). Imminent event with low reversal risk given time remaining. DATA VACUUM: Briefing provides zero information on team standings, recent match results, roster strength, head-to-head history, meta/patch considerations, or any performance indicators for either Geek Fam ID or RRQ Hoshi. MARKET SIGNAL: YES (Geek Fam ID) trading at 58%, NO (RRQ Hoshi) at 42%. Market has price advantage to Geek Fam ID of +16pp. This 58/42 split is the only substantive signal available. PRICE VOLATILITY: Sharp swings Apr 11 (\u00b111.5pp, \u00b110.0pp, \u00b17.5pp) suggest market uncertainty or late-breaking information not captured in briefing. 24-hour volatility 4.7-5.4pp/hr indicates ongoing information flow. 7-DAY TREND: YES +4.5pp (rising), NO -4.5pp (falling). Directional confidence toward Geek Fam ID over the week, but causes unclear from briefing. ASSIGNMENT RATIONALE: In absence of team performance data, defer to market consensus (58/42). This is not a confident assessment but a necessity given data gaps. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Both confidence scores are low (28/27) because briefing provides no factual basis to evaluate either team's likelihood of winning. Market price is being used as proxy for aggregated expert/informed betting, not internal analysis. MECHANISM RISK (SECONDARY): Resolution sources and criteria are well-specified. Liquipedia is reliable for esports results. Forfeiture/cancellation risk appears low for a scheduled MPL Indonesia regular season match. CONCLUSION: Probability 58 is market-driven, not analysis-driven. Confidence in both YES and NO are equally low due to complete absence of team performance intelligence.", "key_factor": "Briefing contains no team performance data, head-to-head history, roster information, or recent form metrics\u2014outcome assessment relies entirely on market price, which may embed information not visible in the briefing."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.32, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "YES side (Geek Fam ID) is the market favorite at 58%, priced 16pp higher than NO \u2014 suggesting some market participants hold a preference for Geek Fam ID to win. However, the briefing contains NO team performance data, recent match results, head-to-head history, roster information, or form metrics for either Geek Fam ID or RRQ Hoshi. The search results explicitly state: 'no team-specific data, recent performance metrics, or head-to-head information is available' \u2014 this is a critical data gap that prevents confident analysis of either side. Market volatility is HIGH (5.4pp/hr on NO side, 4.7pp/hr on YES side) with sharp reversals on Apr 11 (\u00b111.5pp, \u00b110.0pp swings), suggesting uncertainty and potential information asymmetry among traders rather than settled conviction. The 7-day trend shows YES rising +4.5pp and NO falling -4.5pp, but without causal factors identified in the briefing, this directional move may reflect emotional trading or scattered insider knowledge rather than fundamental competitive assessment. Both teams compete in MPL Indonesia Season 17 (March 27\u2013May 24, 2026) under a Double Round Robin BO3 format; neither team's standing, win-loss record, or playoff positioning is disclosed. With ~17 hours until match resolution (TODAY event), there is insufficient time for reversal of the favored side's market position through major announced catalyst \u2014 any pivot would require breaking news (injury, forfeit, etc.) not present in the briefing. The 58% price for YES reflects a modest lean toward Geek Fam ID, consistent with market consensus, but this consensus is NOT anchored to disclosed facts about either team's strength, form, or recent performance. Confidence in YES (32%) is LOW because no affirmative evidence supports Geek Fam ID's superiority \u2014 the favorite status appears to be baked into the price without supporting data, making this a 'price-following' belief rather than an evidence-based judgment. Confidence in NO (28%) is EQUALLY LOW because there is no evidence favoring RRQ Hoshi either \u2014 the underdog position is equally unsupported, leaving true competitive assessment impossible. In the absence of performance data for BOTH sides, the 58/42 split appears to be a near coin-flip with a slight directional tilt; repeating the market price (58%) as the probability_score reflects epistemic humility rather than conviction. A true 50-50 would be unjustified given the market's clear 16pp lean toward YES; deferring to market price acknowledges the pricing signal while recognizing the weak confidence foundation.", "key_factor": "Market pricing at 58% reflects modest consensus favoring Geek Fam ID, but this advantage lacks evidentiary support in available data."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.22, "confidence_no": 0.24, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing contains zero concrete performance metrics for either Geek Fam ID or RRQ Hoshi \u2014 no recent match results, win-loss records, roster information, meta-patch alignments, or head-to-head history. This is the dominant constraint on confidence in either direction. MARKET PRICING MISMATCH: YES is priced at 58% (favorite) despite NO having identical informational vacuum. The 16pp spread reflects market conviction not supported by provided evidence, suggesting herd behavior or external information not captured in this briefing. VOLATILITY AS INDICATOR: The sharp price swings on Apr 11 (+11.5pp / -10.0pp / +7.5pp) with 4.7-5.4pp/hr volatility indicate thin liquidity ($609 total volume) and speculative trading rather than informed positioning. Wide swings in illiquid markets often precede reversals once new information enters. CASE FOR RRQ HOSHI (UNDERDOG): Without evidence of Geek Fam ID's superiority, the 58% pricing appears unjustified. RRQ Hoshi could possess overlooked strengths \u2014 superior recent form, favorable meta alignment, roster continuity, or head-to-head matchup advantages \u2014 all absent from the briefing. A true 50-50 scenario would justify NO at ~45-48%, making 42% potentially undervalued. CASE FOR GEEK FAM ID (FAVORITE): The market's 58% conviction may reflect credible external knowledge (team standings, recent wins, meta fit) not included in this briefing. If external sources confirm Geek Fam ID's recent success or RRQ Hoshi's struggles, the 58% pricing could be justified. LIVE/IMMINENT TIMING RISK: Event resolves in ~17 hours. The 24-hour price change of -4.5pp (YES falling from ~62% to 58%) suggests late-arriving information may be shifting odds toward RRQ Hoshi, though volatility is too high to confirm directionality. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Both confidence_yes (22%) and confidence_no (24%) are equally weak because the briefing provides zero comparative team data. A market this uninformed by public briefing should trade near 50-50; the 58-42 split is not explained by available evidence. UNDERDOG THESIS: RRQ Hoshi deserves higher probability than 42% purely on the grounds that no evidence supports a 16pp discount. If this match were truly 58-42 by merit, the briefing would contain team form, standings position, or recent results. Its absence suggests overpricing of the favorite. PROBABILITY SCORING: Setting probability_score = 42 reflects the market's current YES pricing while acknowledging that equal information vacuum favors skepticism of the 58% consensus. A true 50-50 match would justify ~48-50 for NO; 42 signals the favorite may be slightly overpriced but with very low confidence due to missing data.", "key_factor": "RRQ Hoshi is priced as underdog despite complete absence of performance data favoring either team, suggesting market pricing may reflect narrative or recency bias rather than evidence-based team strength assessment."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.5, "confidence_yes": 0.2, "confidence_no": 0.2, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: No team performance data, roster information, recent match results, or head-to-head history available in briefing. ABSENCE OF FUNDAMENTALS: Cannot assess either team's current form, win-loss record, or competitive standing within MPL Indonesia Season 17. NO CONTEXTUAL ANCHORS: No information on roster strength, recent roster changes, meta shifts, or historical matchup patterns between these specific teams. MARKET PRICE INTERPRETATION: 58/42 split suggests market participants have information not present in briefing. Sharp volatility (\u00b111.5pp, \u00b110pp, \u00b19.5pp in 24h) indicates active repositioning, possibly driven by insider/professional knowledge unavailable to this analyst. TIMING PRESSURE: Event resolves in ~17 hours. Low confidence reflects inability to build a justified probability model from available data rather than genuine uncertainty about the teams' relative strength. SYMMETRIC IGNORANCE: Both YES and NO cases cite identical data gaps. Without team performance metrics, roster composition, or recent results, assigning confidence >25 to either side would be unjustified. RESOLUTION RULE NOTE: Match could resolve 50-50 if canceled, forfeited, or delayed >7 days. Probability of such outcomes appears low but is unmeasurable given data absence. BASE RATE UNAVAILABLE: Mobile Legends esports esports match outcomes in regional second/first-tier leagues do not have published historical base rates accessible to this analyst. Cannot anchor to historical win frequency. MARKET MICROSTRUCTURE: YES side rising +4.5pp over 7 days suggests market confidence toward Geek Fam ID, but this could reflect professional bettor activity, news unreported in briefing, or noise. Without independent verification, weighting market prices alone would be circular.", "key_factor": "Unknown \u2014 no reliable historical data available for Geek Fam ID vs RRQ Hoshi matchups or individual team win rates in MPL Indonesia"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.32, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains zero actionable intelligence on either team's form, roster, recent match results, head-to-head history, or competitive standing in MPL Indonesia Season 17. Market price of 58/42 suggests modest Geek Fam ID favoritism, but this appears to reflect baseline liquidity pricing rather than informed edge. ASYMMETRIC VOLATILITY SIGNAL: YES side shows 24-hour volatility of 4.7pp/hr vs NO side 5.4pp/hr; sharp moves on Apr 11 (\u00b111.5pp, \u00b110.0pp, \u00b17.5pp) indicate emotional whipsaw, not rational information flow. NO UNDERLYING SUPPORT: Absence of team data, standings, roster composition, or meta analysis means market price cannot be anchored to competitive reality\u2014it is pure sentiment. APATHY DIAGNOSIS: With match resolving in ~17 hours, lack of briefing content about team strength suggests market may be underreacting to a known matchup, OR both teams are relatively equally matched and market reflects genuine coin-flip uncertainty. CONFIDENCE PENALTY: Both confidence_yes and confidence_no set LOW (32/28) because briefing provides no basis to distinguish either team's probability of winning. Current 58/42 split is plausible but unvalidated. PRICE ANCHORING: Current 58% YES price is retained as best available signal given data void, but with low conviction. Reversal to 50-50 or sharp move in either direction would be justified by any credible team-specific news. RESOLUTION RISK: Match is TODAY; minimal time remains for new information to move market. Sharp moves Apr 11 suggest late-arriving sentiment (possibly social media, betting syndicates, or insider cues), but briefing does not document this. RECOMMENDATION: This market is under-researched. Low confidence scores reflect data insufficiency, not market mispricing.", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.5, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains zero team performance metrics, current season standings, recent match results, or head-to-head history between Geek Fam ID and RRQ Hoshi. DOMAIN CONTEXT: Mobile Legends meta evolves rapidly with patch cycles; roster strength, player synergy, and recent patch adaptability are decisive factors in BO3 outcomes\u2014none provided. STANDING IMPLICATIONS: In Double Round Robin with 3-win/3-loss thresholds, match context (both teams' current records, playoff positioning) dramatically affects motivation and play intensity\u2014completely unknown. MARKET STRUCTURE SIGNAL: YES side at 58% likely reflects recent betting activity or public perception rather than fundamental analysis; sharp 24-hour volatility (4.7-5.4pp/hr) and large intra-day swings suggest noise, not signal. NO COMPARATIVE INTEL: Cannot assess roster depth, coach quality, recent meta adaptation, substitute availability, or psychological momentum for either team. LIQUIPEDIA RELIANCE: Resolution criteria depend on Liquipedia, but briefing provides no access to current team rosters, rankings, or match history on that platform. TIMING OBSERVATION: Event resolves in ~17 hours; any pre-match news (roster changes, roster lockout, injury/forfeiture risk) that would shift probability >10pp is not reflected in briefing. CONFIDENCE CONSTRAINTS: Asymmetric data quality is severe for BOTH sides; neither YES nor NO can be justified above 25% confidence without team fundamentals.", "key_factor": "MPL Indonesia Season 17 (2026) operates on a Double Round Robin format with cumulative win thresholds (3 wins advance, 3 losses eliminate), making mid-season matches highly dependent on current standings and playoff implications\u2014data entirely absent from briefing."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.52, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing contains zero team performance data, roster information, recent match results, head-to-head history, or meta context. Both analysts and market participants are operating in near-total darkness. MARKET VOLATILITY SIGNAL: The 24-hour price swings are extreme (+11.5pp \u2192 -10.0pp \u2192 +7.5pp on YES; inverse on NO). This volatility, combined with low USD volume ($609), suggests speculative positioning and possible sharp action on private intelligence\u2014likely roster/lineup changes or last-minute team news that has not yet filtered to public sources. TIMING PRESSURE: Event resolves in ~17 hours. Any personnel disruption (injury, illness, suspension, or coaching decision) announced in the final hours before match start cannot be arbitraged away. The market's current 58/42 split likely reflects pre-announcement consensus, not post-announcement reality. RRQ HOSHI WEAKNESS UNEXPLORED: RRQ Hoshi's recent form, roster stability, and injury status are completely unknown. The market has drifted toward YES (+4.5pp in 7 days), but this could reflect YES-side accumulation betting rather than fundamental team strength. RRQ Hoshi could be the team hiding a personnel crisis. GEEK FAM ID BLIND SPOT: Conversely, Geek Fam ID's recent win streak or loss streak is invisible to this analysis. The 58% YES price could be overconfident in a team that is actually entering this match fatigued or demoralized from prior rounds. BO3 FORMAT VULNERABILITY: In Best-of-3 matches, a single poor draft, unexpected meta counter-pick, or morale collapse in Game 1 can cascade into a 0-2 series loss. The team that appears favored on paper may choke under pressure if internal conflicts or coaching uncertainty exist. LIQUIPEDIA DELAY RISK: Resolution depends on Liquipedia updates within 2 hours post-match. If Liquipedia is slow or the match result is disputed, resolution could slip toward 50-50. This tail risk is not priced in. CONSENSUS AVOIDANCE: All other analysts will default to 50-50 due to missing data. Market at 58/42 suggests informed bettors know something (a team's strength, recent patch advantage, or personnel status). The black swan is that the informed bettors are *wrong*\u2014their private intel is stale, incomplete, or misinterpreted. LOWEST-CONFIDENCE VERDICT: Both probability_score (52) and confidence_yes/no (28/26) are near-50 and near-minimum. This reflects genuine epistemic humility: the briefing provides zero actionable competitive data. Any deviation from 50 is speculative and based solely on market price drift and volatility patterns, not substance.", "key_factor": "A key roster player from one team (likely RRQ Hoshi, given recent market volatility spikes) is benched, injured, or substituted minutes before match start, creating a tactical collapse that the market has not priced in."}], "final_score": 0.5329411764705883, "no_score": 0.47056179775280904, "edge": -0.05205882352941171, "no_edge": 0.055561797752809006, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 53% for YES (need \u226557%); YES-side confidence too low: 27% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1902279", "question": "Mobile Legends Bang Bang: Geek Fam ID vs RRQ Hoshi (BO3) - MPL Indonesia Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Mobile Legends Bang Bang match between Geek Fam ID and RRQ Hoshi in the MPL Indonesia Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 12 at 6:15AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Geek Fam ID\" if Geek Fam ID win the match against RRQ Hoshi.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"RRQ Hoshi\" if RRQ Hoshi win the match against Geek Fam ID.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://liquipedia.net/mobilelegends/Main_Page. However, if https://liquipedia.net/mobilelegends/Main_Page has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has n