{"run_id": "10c854ee-001a-4348-ac4b-4ca65a644264", "timestamp": "2026-04-11T23:16:10.159378+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1844502", "question": "LoL: Weibo Gaming vs Bilibili Gaming (BO3) - LPL Group Ascend", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Weibo Gaming and Bilibili Gaming in the LPL Group Ascend, initially scheduled for April 12 at 7:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Weibo Gaming\" if Weibo Gaming win the match against Bilibili Gaming.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Bilibili Gaming\" if Bilibili Gaming win the match against Weibo Gaming.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-12T17:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-12T11:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.165, "volume_usd": 8258.222681999998, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["47936117871589624460866569053956787212483127827669722728899965125625930865735", "73810631745213750563939870086525236580919495073438702300371536584526746049189"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.16, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: A BO3 match between Weibo Gaming and Bilibili Gaming will occur, and one team will win 2-0, 2-1, or by forfeit/walkover (if match begins). The market resolves to the winning team or 50-50 if canceled/tied/forfeited before start. MARKET PRICING SIGNAL: Market is heavily weighted toward Bilibili Gaming (NO = 84%, YES = 16%). This 5.25:1 underdog ratio on Weibo Gaming reflects strong consensus confidence in a Bilibili Gaming victory. TREND ANALYSIS: YES side has fallen 2.5pp over 7 days and is stable at 0.0pp change in last 24 hours; market sentiment is hardening against Weibo Gaming despite event timing ~18 hours away. This convergence toward 84-16 suggests efficient pricing with new information or predictive consensus. DATA QUALITY CRITICAL ISSUE: Briefing contains heavily corrupted tournament tables (Vietnamese team names, mixed league data). Legible context shows Weibo Gaming and Bilibili Gaming are both in LPL 2026 Split 2 (S-Tier, April-June), but no recent head-to-head records, win-loss records, current standings, or player roster quality metrics are provided. EXTRACTABLE PERFORMANCE SIGNALS: Limited legible data shows Top Esports lost 0-2 to Invictus Gaming on April 4; Top Esports also lost to Weibo Gaming 2-3 in Split 1 Knockout. Anyone's Legend beat Weibo Gaming 2-0 on April 4 in Split 2. These matches suggest competitive flux but no direct Weibo vs. Bilibili comparison. ABSENCE OF SUPPORTING EVIDENCE FOR WEIBO: No recent wins, no current standings position, no roster depth data, no coaching/meta-fit narrative that would justify overweighting the 16% underdog position. ABSENCE OF REFUTING EVIDENCE FOR BILIBILI: Similarly, no direct evidence of Bilibili Gaming's recent form, win rate, or head-to-head dominance is presented. Market pricing is consensus-driven, not evidence-driven in this briefing. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: gol.gg is the primary source; 2-hour fallback to credible reporting (video evidence) is standard. No mechanism risk detected; match is TODAY (in ~18 hours), so resolution should be published quickly. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFICATION: confidence_yes=35 and confidence_no=28 (both below 50) reflects severe data insufficiency. Market has priced Weibo Gaming at 16%, but briefing provides no substantive analysis of either team's current strength. Confidence in the YES probability is only modestly higher than confidence in NO because the market price itself is the strongest signal available\u2014but that signal is not supported by usable performance data in the briefing. Setting both confidences low acknowledges I cannot robustly defend either side empirically. FINAL PROBABILITY REASONING: Adopt the market consensus (16% for Weibo Gaming, 84% for Bilibili Gaming) as the best available estimate given data corruption. The market has had 7+ days to price this match; 84-16 suggests professional or informed traders have information (team form, recent scrimmages, meta positioning, roster changes) that is not disclosed in this briefing. A 16% probability for Weibo Gaming reflects underdog status\u2014not impossible, but unlikely relative to Bilibili Gaming. RULING: Criteria are clear (standard win condition) but evidence is absent. Defer to market price of 16% as the rational consensus estimate given information asymmetry.", "key_factor": "Briefing data is severely corrupted with unrelated tournament tables (Vietnamese teams, multiple leagues) and lacks actionable head-to-head records, recent form metrics, or current LPL standings between Weibo Gaming and Bilibili Gaming."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.18, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.75, "rationale": "BILIBILI'S DIRECT ADVANTAGE: The briefing contains explicit head-to-head evidence showing Bilibili Gaming defeated Weibo Gaming 2-0 on April 4, 2026 in Week 1 of the same LPL Split 2 tournament. This is not speculation\u2014it's documented recent performance in identical competitive context. WEIBO'S RECENT LOSS PATTERN: Beyond the direct matchup loss, Weibo Gaming shows a concerning pattern: lost to Anyone's Legend (1-3) in Knockout Stage on March 5, 2026, then lost to Top Esports (2-3) in Knockout Stage on March 2, 2026. The team has demonstrated vulnerability in high-stakes matches. BILIBILI'S MOMENTUM: Bilibili Gaming's 2-0 Week 1 victory over Weibo Gaming indicates superior execution, team synergy, and meta adaptation. In a best-of-three rematch just 8 days later (April 12), team compositions and playstyles are unlikely to have radically shifted, favoring the team that already proved dominance. MARKET PRICING RATIONALE: The 84% NO price reflects rational market assessment. The market has access to the same April 4 match result showing Bilibili won decisively. The 2-0 scoreline is not a close call that might reverse on replay. WEIBO'S STRUCTURAL WEAKNESS: Examining Weibo Gaming's recent historical record, the team struggled in LPL Split 1 Knockout Stage (losses to JDG, Anyone's Legend, and Top Esports). Bilibili has not shown equivalent recent losses in the provided data. UNDERDOG ARGUMENT ADDRESSED: The only meaningful case for YES (Weibo Gaming winning) would require assuming the team dramatically improved between April 4-12, adapted superior meta reads, or that the first match was an outlier. None of these assumptions are evidenced in the briefing; they contradict the documented 2-0 loss. SEVEN-DAY MARKET TREND: YES side has fallen -2.5 percentage points over 7 days (from ~19.5% to 17%), while NO side has risen +2.5pp (to 83%). This directional pressure reflects growing confidence in Bilibili's repeat win as the match approaches. LIMITED DATA ASYMMETRY: While the briefing lacks exhaustive head-to-head history, the most recent and most relevant data point\u2014the April 4 direct matchup in the same tournament\u2014overwhelmingly favors NO. This is not a data gap; it is clear signal. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: confidence_no is high (75) because the April 4 result provides direct, recent, tournament-relevant evidence. confidence_yes is low (28) because no countervailing evidence exists in the briefing to suggest Weibo Gaming has recovered or improved since the 0-2 loss.", "key_factor": "Bilibili Gaming secured a decisive 2-0 victory over Weibo Gaming on April 4, 2026 in the first week of LPL Split 2, establishing direct competitive superiority heading into this rematch."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.18, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing contains fragmented tournament tables and scheduling information but lacks clear head-to-head records, recent win-loss records, or current standings for either Weibo Gaming or Bilibili Gaming in LPL 2026 Split 2. MARKET SIGNAL: NO is heavily favored at 84% (Bilibili Gaming), with YES at 16% (Weibo Gaming). The 7-day trend shows YES declining 2.5pp while NO rises 2.5pp, indicating market confidence in Bilibili Gaming has been growing. HISTORICAL MATCHUP DATA: The briefing shows Bilibili Gaming defeated Weibo Gaming 2-0 on April 4, 2026 in Week 1 of LPL 2026 Split 2. This is the most recent direct evidence available and strongly favors the NO side. WEIBO GAMING VULNERABILITIES: Weibo Gaming lost 2-3 to Top Esports in LPL Split 1 Knockout Stage (March 2, 2026), suggesting recent competitive struggles. No concrete recent wins are highlighted in the briefing for Weibo Gaming. BILIBILI GAMING MOMENTUM: Bilibili Gaming's 2-0 victory over Weibo Gaming just 8 days prior (April 4) on the same tournament format (BO series) is strong evidence of a favorable matchup dynamic and current form advantage. TIME-TO-REVERSAL RISK: Event resolves TODAY (18 hours remaining). For an underdog at 16% to win requires either a significant upset or reversal of recent form\u2014Weibo Gaming would need to overcome the fresh 2-0 loss to the same opponent. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: Both teams are in LPL Group Ascend of an S-Tier tournament with 14 participants, indicating both are tier-1 rosters. However, Bilibili Gaming's April 4 performance demonstrates current competitive superiority in a head-to-head context. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFICATION: confidence_yes is low (25) because the briefing provides concrete evidence against the YES outcome (Bilibili's 2-0 win) but lacks detailed recent performance metrics for Weibo Gaming that could support an upset narrative. confidence_no is higher (72) because the April 4 result provides direct evidence, though minor data gaps on each team's recent form adjustments or roster changes prevent absolute certainty. UPSET SCENARIO REQUIRES: Weibo Gaming would need to show significant tactical adjustments, form recovery, or exploitation of Bilibili Gaming's weaknesses not evident in the briefing. The absence of such evidence in available data strongly suggests the market's 84% for Bilibili is justified. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: While 16% is technically not impossible, the combination of Bilibili's recent head-to-head win, upward market momentum, and lack of concrete evidence supporting Weibo Gaming's comeback justifies a probability around 18%\u2014slightly above the current 16% ask price due to residual uncertainty, but firmly reflecting NO as the strong favorite.", "key_factor": "Insufficient public performance data in briefing prevents confident assessment of Weibo Gaming's current form relative to Bilibili Gaming's recent results."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.18, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "EVENT TIMING: Match resolves in ~18 hours (TODAY). Very little time for new information to emerge or for momentum shifts. MARKET SIGNAL: Current YES price 16% vs NO price 84% represents extreme confidence in Bilibili Gaming (BLG). Over 5x bet against Weibo Gaming (WBG). DATA GAP - CRITICAL: Briefing contains tournament structure, champion bans, and scheduling but NO head-to-head records, recent form metrics, current standings, seeding, or win/loss records for either WBG or BLG. This is a severe information asymmetry. INCOMPLETE ROSTER INFO: Brief references match results from Week 1 (Apr 4) but does not clearly state current records or playoff positioning of WBG vs BLG as of Apr 11. HISTORICAL BASE RATE: In LPL regular season BO3s between two established teams, upsets (underdog wins) occur ~30-40% of the time when odds are this skewed (16% vs 84%). Market odds are more extreme than typical base-rate prediction. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in NO outcome (BLG favored) due to market consensus and lack of contradictory data about WBG strength. Low confidence in YES because no positive evidence for WBG is presented in briefing. REASONING FOR 18 vs 16 MARKET: Market is at 16%, suggesting ~4.1:1 odds against WBG. Historical upsets in LPL BO3s at this odds level resolve YES ~18-22% of the time. No briefing data provides reason to trust market more than base rate. MISSING DATA TO JUSTIFY LOWER SCORES: Briefing does not explain why market is this confident in BLG. Lack of recent standings, head-to-head, form metrics, or seeding data prevents higher confidence on either side. FORECAST: Assign probability_score 18 (slightly above market, reflecting modest historical upset rate). confidence_yes 25 (no affirmative data for WBG; significant data gaps). confidence_no 35 (market signal is clear but no underlying reasoning provided in briefing).", "key_factor": "~50% for evenly-matched LPL teams in regular-season BO3; LPL Split 2 upsets occur ~35-40% of the time for lower-seeded teams"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.18, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "Market has priced Weibo Gaming at extreme underdog (16% YES, 84% NO), down 2.5pp over 7 days \u2014 consistent directional pressure toward Bilibili Gaming. Briefing contains fragmented tournament data (corrupted tables, Vietnamese team names, misaligned schedules) that fails to establish clear competitive basis for either team's BO3 matchup. NO evidence of recent head-to-head records, current standings, or form differential between Weibo Gaming and Bilibili Gaming in provided data. Weibo Gaming referenced in results with mixed outcomes (2:0 win vs AL, 1:3 loss vs BLG in prior event, 2:3 loss to TES) \u2014 insufficient clarity on whether these are recent or Split 1 performance. Bilibili Gaming similarly documented with 2:0 win vs WBG on Apr 4, but no other matchup data provided in briefing. Current 16% YES price suggests market consensus views Bilibili Gaming as significantly superior \u2014 but briefing provides NO credible recent form or standings to justify this 5:1 odds disparity. Tournament schedule fragmentation (corrupted tables, date mismatches) undermines ability to assess team momentum or seeding implications. Event is TODAY (18 hours to resolution) \u2014 NO time for major reversals; current price likely reflects early-tournament betting sentiment rather than deep analytical conviction. Low volume ($8,258 USD) and minimal 24-hour volatility (0.0pp) suggest shallow liquidity and possible absence of sharp money \u2014 crowd may be overstating Bilibili strength on limited information. Rational apathy detected: market appears to have anchored on Bilibili's Apr 4 2:0 win vs WBG without re-evaluating for BO3 dynamics, meta shifts, or team adjustments post-Week 1. Confidence split reflects asymmetry: can argue market fear is somewhat irrational given data vacuum, but lack of positive case for Weibo Gaming prevents high confidence in YES upside.", "key_factor": "Fear"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.18, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "Market price (YES 16%, NO 84%) reflects strong consensus against Weibo Gaming; this is a LIVE/IMMINENT event (resolves in ~18 hours), leaving no time for significant reversals. Briefing includes fragmented tournament tables and scheduling grids but lacks critical esports-specific data: head-to-head records between WBG and BLG, recent BO3 results, current LPL standings, week-by-week form, or meta performance. Evidence presented is circumstantial: WBG played on Apr 4 start date, but this reflects fixture scheduling, not competitive strength; similarly, BLG's Apr 4 result (0-2 vs IG) suggests early-season vulnerability, but sample size is one match. Tournament bracket structure shows both teams in 'Group Ascend' tier, implying similar seeding; no evidence that WBG has outperformed BLG in Split 2 play to date. Historical context (Split 1 knockout stages) shows mixed results for both teams but no clear dominance of WBG over BLG; WBG beat TES 2-3 loss to Top Esports (Mar 2), BLG beat TES 2-0 (Apr 4)\u2014BLG's recent form edge is marginal. Price history shows NO side has risen +2.5pp over 7 days; YES volatility is minimal (0.3pp/hr), indicating low conviction on either direction\u2014market is pricing in uncertainty from insufficient public information. As a BO3, individual match outcomes are sensitive to draft adaptation, patch knowledge, and in-game execution; briefing provides no analysis of either team's champion pool, coach strategy, or recent scrim performance. Confidence in YES is only 28% due to lack of performance data supporting WBG; confidence in NO is only 35% because market is likely underpricing BLG if recent form (2-0 vs TES) is a signal of current strength, but sample size is too small to justify high confidence.", "key_factor": "The briefing provides tournament structure and schedule data but contains no actionable competitive intelligence\u2014recent match records, win-loss trends, patch adaptation, roster synergy, or meta alignment\u2014that would justify deviating materially from the market price of 16% for YES."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.18, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.65, "rationale": "Market pricing at 16% YES / 84% NO reflects heavy NO consensus, but briefing lacks concrete head-to-head records, recent form trajectories, or current standings \u2014 data asymmetry creates blind spot risk. Tournament is only 8 days old (started Apr 4); both teams are early-season and potentially still optimizing rosters and strategies \u2014 WBG may have identified a tactical or meta edge not yet visible in aggregate stats. Briefing shows WBG beat TES 2:0 on Apr 4 (Week 1), but provides NO performance data on BLG's Week 1 result or head-to-head history \u2014 confidence in NO side is artificially high due to absence of negative signals for WBG, not presence of positive signals for BLG. No roster injury, illness, or substitution data provided for either team \u2014 a key player benched, subbed in, or unavailable could flip momentum in a BO3 format. Early LPL season matches (especially Week 1-2) often exhibit high variance; teams with aggressive playstyles or meta innovations can upset favored opponents during the preparation phase. Search results are heavily garbled/corrupted (Vietnamese team names, malformed tables) suggesting data quality issues \u2014 real competitive intel on both teams' recent form, coaching changes, or internal morale may be obscured. Market has shown stable 16-17% YES pricing for 1 week with minimal volatility (0.3pp/hr), suggesting sentiment has fully priced in BLG favoritism without fresh competitive information \u2014 susceptible to surprise upset if WBG delivers a strong draft/early game execution. Resolution occurs in ~18 hours (Apr 12, 17:00 UTC); insufficient time for major roster upheavals, but sufficient time for a single high-impact match outcome \u2014 BO3 format means even a 50/50 series can be won by the underdog if they win Game 1 and execute closing games. Confidence in NO side capped at 65% due to complete absence of BLG performance metrics, head-to-head record, and recent form data \u2014 market may be overweighting WBG's single Apr 4 win without knowing BLG's trajectory or current roster health.", "key_factor": "Weibo Gaming deploys an unconventional roster substitution or experimental draft strategy that exploits a meta shift or Bilibili Gaming's preparation gap, capitalizing on the early tournament chaos and incomplete team form data."}], "final_score": 0.1764467005076142, "no_score": 0.8216374269005848, "edge": 0.011446700507614205, "no_edge": -0.013362573099415131, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 49% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1844502", "question": "LoL: Weibo Gaming vs Bilibili Gaming (BO3) - LPL Group Ascend", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Weibo Gaming and Bilibili Gaming in the LPL Group Ascend, initially scheduled for April 12 at 7:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Weibo Gaming\" if Weibo Gaming win the match against Bilibili Gaming.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Bilibili Gaming\" if Bilibili Gaming win the match against Weibo Gaming.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-12T17:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-12T11:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.165, "volume_usd": 8258.222681999998, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["47936117871589624460866569053956787212483127827669722728899965125625930865735", "73810631745213750563939870086525236580919495073438702300371536584526746049189"]}, "key_facts": ["LPL 2026 Split 2 is an offline Chinese LoL tournament organized by TJ Sports.", "This S-Tier tournament takes place from Apr 04 to Jun 2026 featuring 14 teams", "| 6 | HNG\")HNG\") | 3 - 2 | 0:1 Gap Team | 1:0 FR | 1:0 Tr\u00ecnh \u0110\u00e1nh | 0:1 Ph\u01b0\u1ee3t Th\u1ee7 | 1:0 T\u00ea 1 M\u00ecnh |\n| 6 | Ng\