{"run_id": "ac9c0b70-250c-45c7-9ab3-d3555788569d", "timestamp": "2026-04-12T17:11:45.454778+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1951968", "question": "Valorant: Bitfix Gaming vs UNIWAY (BO3) - VCL NORTH//EAST Group B", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between Bitfix Gaming and UNIWAY in the VCL NORTH//EAST Group B, initially scheduled for April 12 at 11:30AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Bitfix Gaming\" if Bitfix Gaming win the match against UNIWAY.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"UNIWAY\" if UNIWAY win the match against Bitfix Gaming.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-12T21:30:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-12T15:30:00Z", "yes_price": 0.6, "volume_usd": 365.29525099999995, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["16620826239770641324548226256572353273829625643462165293256608588366547201260", "109746018195905902294400431132451003706253745573475572713957107503467357922600"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.5, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: No performance metrics, standings, recent results, or roster information available for either team in the briefing. No head-to-head historical record between Bitfix Gaming and UNIWAY exists in the provided data. No current Group B standings or win-loss records provided to establish team strength hierarchy. Market price (60% YES / 40% NO) suggests modest Bitfix Gaming favoritism, but this is unsupported by any substantive briefing data. Both teams are VCL North//East competitors in a BO3 group stage match, but competitive context is entirely missing. The 'CASE FOR YES' and 'CASE FOR NO' in briefing are purely symmetrical absence arguments \u2014 neither side presents actionable evidence. No recent form trajectory, roster composition, map pool strength, or meta-adaptation data available. Market volatility (sharp 24-point moves) suggests information asymmetry or late-breaking news not reflected in briefing. Without team data, assignment of probability above 50 would be pure speculation masquerading as analysis. Confidence scores are deliberately set low (25/25) to reflect epistemic humility in face of complete information vacuum on both sides. Resolution criteria are clear and unambiguous; the risk is analytical, not mechanical.", "key_factor": "Complete absence of team performance data, roster information, head-to-head records, or current standings for either Bitfix Gaming or UNIWAY makes any directional assessment impossible."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "YES (Bitfix Gaming) is favored at 60% with an upward 7-day trend (+7.5pp), suggesting accumulating conviction despite low volume ($365 USD) and high volatility (13.1pp/hr 24h). The 24-hour price action is extremely volatile (sharp -12.5pp, +7.0pp, -24.0pp moves), indicating uncertainty and live information injection close to match start (event is TODAY, ~4 hours to resolution). Sharp reversal at 17:00 UTC today (-24pp on YES) signals a significant new data point\u2014possibly live match intelligence, roster updates, or betting-market informed trading. This suggests NO may have gained objective advantage very recently. Briefing explicitly states: 'no specific data, recent results, roster information, or head-to-head records for Bitfix Gaming or UNIWAY' available. This is a critical data gap for BOTH sides, severely limiting confidence in either direction. The market's 60% YES pricing does not reflect strong underlying fundamental conviction\u2014it reflects a modest 20pp edge in a low-conviction, high-variance market where neither team's true strength is documented. The CASE FOR YES relies entirely on absence of negative data ('no negative performance data available'), which is logically weak. Absence of evidence is not evidence of absence. The CASE FOR NO equally weak: 'no positive performance data' does not prove weakness. The symmetry of missing data for both teams should drive both probabilities toward 50%, not support 60/40. Volatility of 13-14pp/hour in the final hours before a LIVE event suggests genuine uncertainty about match outcome, not confidence in the favorite. If Bitfix were clearly stronger, prices would stabilize higher. The recent -24pp sharp move on YES (17:00 UTC, ~4 hours before match) is inconsistent with YES being the true favorite. This recentMove suggests emerging evidence favoring NO or revealing Bitfix weakness. Confidence in YES is justified at only ~42 because: (1) no roster/form data supports Bitfix, (2) recent sharp price reversal contradicts the 60% level, (3) low volume ($365) and high volatility indicate low-conviction pricing, (4) BO3 format does not inherently favor either unknown team. Confidence in NO is equally limited at ~38 because: (1) no positive Bitfix data exists, but also no Bitfix losses documented, (2) we cannot quantify why NO has gained ground except via recent trading, (3) no head-to-head history exists to evaluate UNIWAY's competitive edge. As an advocate for the favored side (YES/Bitfix), the evidence is thin. The market is pricing Bitfix at a modest 20pp edge, but that edge is not anchored in documented team strength\u2014it is inertial pricing with low conviction, as shown by volatility and recent reversals. The -24pp reversal 4 hours before match start is a red flag for the YES side. Smart money is often early; this move may reflect information cascading into the market that the briefing does not yet capture. Probability of 58 reflects: (1) modest YES market consensus (60%) weighted down by recent sharp reversal, (2) absence of fundamental data supporting either side, (3) live-event risk that neither team's true strength is proven, (4) probability that the market's 60% is overcounting YES after the late reversal. Final call: Bitfix Gaming is favored, but barely. The market is uncertain. The recent price action suggests NO may have legitimate claim to 45%+ probability. 58 reflects a slight edge to YES that could easily flip with match-start conditions or live roster news.", "key_factor": "Market consensus favoring Bitfix Gaming (60% YES) reflects accumulated information not fully captured in the briefing, likely including live match performance or team strength signals."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confide