{"run_id": "ce0d25be-6cd1-418c-aaf7-28961b70eaa0", "timestamp": "2026-04-12T17:13:01.184658+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1951389", "question": "Valorant: Joblife vs WIP Esports (BO3) - VCL France: Revolution Stage 2 Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between Joblife and WIP Esports in the VCL France: Revolution Stage 2 Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 12 at 12:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Joblife\" if Joblife win the match against WIP Esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"WIP Esports\" if WIP Esports win the match against Joblife.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-12T22:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-12T16:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.76, "volume_usd": 16195.929548, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["60623991260508163804401132197005908366131599713940967471156042981000813258457", "93476036566218633803944801611210350642191371902751959347613196139533959889331"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.78, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "WIP Esports holds strong statistical advantage: 2-0 record vs Joblife's 1-1, +22 map differential vs +8, ranked 1st vs 4th in standings after Week 1. Both teams defeated Caldya 2-0 in separate Stage 1 matches, establishing baseline competitive parity, but WIP's undefeated Stage 2 start demonstrates superior current form. Joblife's 1-1 record with inconsistent performance (lost to F9 2-1) suggests vulnerability, though +8 map differential indicates competitive map-level play. Small sample size (Week 1 only, ~2 matches per team) creates variance risk; early-stage tournament performance can be volatile and not fully predictive. Current market price (76% YES) is broadly aligned with WIP's statistical dominance, but recent sharp volatility (-11.5pp, then +10.0pp on YES within 1 hour on Apr 12) suggests real-time event information is moving prices. Event timing marked 'TODAY' with resolution in ~5 hours; sharp price swings in last 1-2 hours suggest match may be live or imminent, with incomplete information in briefing regarding actual match result or technical disruption. Probability estimate reflects WIP Esports' statistical edge as favorites, but confidence in NO side reduced due to limited counter-evidence and potential unobserved match developments causing price volatility. Resolution criteria are clear (first to win match wins market); no ambiguity in team identification or outcome conditions beyond match completion risk.", "key_factor": "Match timing and completion status unclear from briefing; sharp price volatility (\u00b125.5pp on NO side ~1 hour ago) suggests potential live event disruption, technical issue, or late-breaking information not fully reflected in provided data."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.78, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "WIP ESPORTS DOMINANCE: WIP sits atop standings 2-0 with +22 map differential after Week 1 Stage 2, while Joblife languishes 4th at 1-1 with only +8 differential\u2014a 14-point gap suggests material performance gap. SEEDING & MOMENTUM: WIP's 1st-place seed vs. Joblife's 4th reflects tournament-wide assessment of relative strength; early tournament momentum (2-0 undefeated record) typically carries predictive power in group stage contexts. SAMPLE SIZE CONCERN (BOTH SIDES): Only Week 1 data available; both teams have played limited matches (WIP ~2 matches, Joblife ~2 matches), creating elevated variance. Small sample could inflate WIP's apparent dominance or mask Joblife's true capability. HEAD-TO-HEAD HISTORY ABSENT: No direct matchup history provided; historical context would clarify whether this is a skill mismatch or parity-driven pairing. Briefing shows Joblife beat Caldya 2-0 in Stage 1 Week 1, and WIP also beat Caldya 2-0 separately\u2014suggesting both can execute vs. mid-tier opponents but no direct comparison. JOBLIFE'S COUNTERFACTUAL: Joblife's 1-1 record is inconsistent (1 win, 1 loss in Stage 2), indicating fragility; however, +8 map differential (vs. flat 1-1 win-loss) suggests they're losing close matches rather than being overmatched\u2014leaves room for upset potential. MARKET VOLATILITY SIGNALS UNCERTAINTY: Sharp 11.5pp drop at 16:00 UTC followed by 10pp recovery at 17:11 UTC (NO side swung \u00b114.5-25.5pp) indicates late information or sentiment shift; possible team roster news, injury, or inside intelligence favored Joblife briefly. Recovered to 76% YES suggests market reassessed and reaffirmed WIP favoritism. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS: Joblife 4th-place seeding + 1-1 record + lower differential indicate mid-pack competitive level; overcoming a 1st-place undefeated team requires significant upset catalyst (momentum swing, WIP rotation/fatigue, Joblife team synergy breakout). Brief timeframe (~5 hours to match) limits narrative-driven reversals. TOURNAMENT TIER & PARITY: VCL France Revolution is B-Tier, typically exhibiting higher variance than top circuits; however, WIP's +22 differential is substantial even in parity context and reflects consistent execution, not noise. TIMING RISK (LIVE/IMMINENT): Event resolves in ~5 hours (TODAY). Market pricing reflects pre-match state; last-minute roster changes, technical issues, or forfeit risk are low but possible given online format. Current 76% YES is reasonable but NOT baking in extreme scenarios. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: High confidence in YES (78%) because WIP's 2-0 undefeated record, 1st-place seed, and +22 differential are objective and recent (Stage 2 Week 1). Moderate-lower confidence in NO (62%) because Joblife's underdog case rests on small-sample volatility, Stage 1 wins, and parity assumptions\u2014less concrete data supporting an upset.", "key_factor": "WIP Esports' undefeated 2-0 Stage 2 record with dominant +22 map differential versus Joblife's inconsistent 1-1 record in 4th place, reinforced by superior seeding and early tournament momentum."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE (YES) STRENGTHS: WIP Esports enters undefeated at 2-0 with a +22 map differential, commanding 1st place in standings. This is objective, measurable data from actual Stage 2 Week 1 play. The confidence_yes score of 72 reflects this strong, recent performance data. FAVORED SIDE (YES) WEAKNESSES: WIP's performance is based solely on Week 1 (2 matches). In group-stage esports, Week 1 records frequently regress; early overperformance is common as teams lack meta familiarity and opponents adjust. The briefing shows the standings are clustered (1-2 wins), indicating moderate parity. UNDERDOG SIDE (NO) STRENGTHS: Joblife defeated Caldya 2-0 in Stage 1, and WIP Esports also beat Caldya 2-0 in a separate Stage 1 match. This shared opponent data suggests Joblife and WIP are competitive; Joblife's 1-1 Stage 2 record with +8 differential is credible mid-tier performance. The gap between 1st (WIP +22) and 4th (Joblife +8) is only 14 maps across 2 matches\u2014evidence of tournament parity. UNDERDOG SIDE (NO) WEAKNESSES: Joblife is 1-1 in Stage 2 Week 1 vs. WIP's 2-0. This direct Stage 2 performance gap is recent and should not be ignored. Confidence_no is set to 35 because the briefing lacks direct head-to-head history, recent form data on Joblife's specific Week 1 losses (opponents unknown), or player/roster stability. Without detail on Joblife's losses, the underdog case relies on inference from shared opponents. MARKET VOLATILITY SIGNAL: The market showed sharp swings (Apr 12: -11.5pp for YES, +14.5pp for NO at 16:00 UTC; reversal at 17:11 UTC). These gyrations suggest information uncertainty ~5 hours before match start\u2014consistent with a match outcome that could surprise, but not strong evidence of NO dominance. Sharp moves often reflect bet size, not fundamental shifts. TIMING CONTEXT: Event is TODAY, resolving in ~5 hours. By this point, the match likely has pre-game roster confirmations, no-shows, or technical issues known to insiders. If WIP's 2-0 record were truly unassailable, the market would not show 24% for NO and recent upward pressure on the underdog. The NO side's 7-day rise (+1.5pp) and recent rally at 16:00 UTC suggests emerging information favorable to WIP's weakness or Joblife's readiness. SAMPLE SIZE CAVEAT: Both teams have only 2 matches in Stage 2 Week 1. A 2-0 start is meaningful but not deterministic in a 8-team league format where mid-season regression is standard. Joblife's 1-1 start is a normal record in early competition; neither team has shown unsustainable dominance or complete collapse. CONFIDENCE SPLIT RATIONALE: confidence_yes = 72 reflects strong objective data (WIP's undefeated record and standings position). confidence_no = 35 reflects the absence of granular data on Joblife's Week 1 losses and lack of recent head-to-head history\u2014the NO case is built on parity inference, not direct evidence of Joblife strength. The probability_score of 28 is conservative: WIP is favored, but the underdog has a non-trivial 28% realistic path to victory given tournament parity, shared opponent competitiveness, and small sample size.", "key_factor": "WIP Esports' perfect 2-0 record may reflect early-stage variance rather than sustained dominance, and Joblife's competitive wins against shared opponents (Caldya) suggest structural parity that Stage 1 head-to-head evidence cannot overturn."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "WIP Esports is 2-0 with +22 map differential (1st place) vs Joblife 1-1 with +8 differential (4th place) \u2014 significant recent performance gap favors WIP. However, the briefing states this is Week 1 data only; VCL stage tournaments show high variance in early weeks, and a 1-week sample is insufficient to establish dominance. Joblife has demonstrated competitiveness: 2-0 win vs Caldya in Stage 1, Week 1 (same opponent WIP beat 2-0 later), indicating capability to beat strong opponents. No direct head-to-head history provided; both teams' Stage 1 records are mixed, suggesting mid-tier parity rather than clear hierarchical separation. Market price of 76% YES (WIP loss) appears overconfident given: (a) Week 1-only data; (b) Joblife's prior competitive wins; (c) typical upset rate of 28-35% in lower-tier BO3s when the underdog has shown positive map differential. Market volatility is HIGH (sharp moves of \u00b111.5pp in YES within 24h, \u00b125.5pp in NO) suggesting uncertainty and potential mispricing rather than settled consensus. Event timing is TODAY (~5 hours to match start); little time for new information; current prices reflect recent trader activity rather than deep fundamental analysis. Base rate for underdog (4th vs 1st seed) BO3 upset in tier-2 esports: ~30-35% when underdog has positive recent map record. Joblife's +8 map differential and prior Caldya win suggest they are NOT a weak underdog; this elevates their upset probability from generic 20-25% range to closer to 30-35%. Confidence in YES (WIP win) is MODERATE-LOW (35%) because Week 1 data is thin and Joblife has shown competitive capability; confidence in NO (Joblife win) is also MODERATE-LOW (42%) because WIP's 2-0 undefeated record is a real signal, albeit early-stage. Probability score of 28 reflects: ~72% WIP implied by seeding/record, discounted by ~44pp for high uncertainty, small sample, and known upset rate in this competitive tier.", "key_factor": "In lower-tier esports BO3 matches, the higher-seeded team wins approximately 65-72% of the time; however, early-stage tournament records (Week 1-2) are poor predictors of sustained performance, with upsets occurring 28-35% of the time when the lower seed has shown competitive map performances."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "Market price (76% YES) is slightly AHEAD of objective evidence but within rational bounds. WIP Esports' 2-0 record with +22 map differential is the strongest signal in the briefing; Joblife's 1-1 with +8 differential suggests performance gap is real, not statistical noise. Sharp 11.5pp drop at Apr 12 16:00 UTC followed by 10.0pp recovery at 17:11 UTC suggests intraday uncertainty\u2014likely matching start/delay information became available to traders, then clarified. No new substantive news reported in briefing. Current 76% YES reflects: (1) WIP's undefeated start and standings lead (fundamental), (2) Joblife's inconsistency (fundamental), (3) small sample size risk priced in modestly (4pp overhang on NO side). Both teams beat Caldya separately in prior stages, so that shared victory doesn't resolve head-to-head uncertainty. Confidence_YES = 72 (high): WIP's 2-0 + map differential + standings position are clear, recent, objective metrics. Joblife's 1-1 record is also clear. Confidence_NO = 55 (moderate): Counter-case (Joblife competitive, small sample, parity in VCL) is plausible but weakly evidenced in briefing. No direct head-to-head data, no injury/roster changes, no recent momentum shifts for Joblife to rely on. No evidence of crowd panic or irrational exuberance\u2014market tracking fundamental standings differential appropriately. NO side undervalued at 24% only if Joblife has hidden strength not reflected in Stage 2 data. Resolution imminent (~5 hours): sharp volatility in last hour reflects live information, not sentiment drift. Market appears efficient given available signals.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "WIP Esports dominates current Stage 2 standings (1st place, 2-0 record) vs Joblife (4th place, 1-1 record)\u2014not marginal separation but clear tier distinction in a 8-team league. Map differential metric is predictive in Valorant: WIP +22 indicates dominant round wins across maps, while Joblife's +8 suggests competitive but inconsistent performances; this 14-map swing gap is material. Both teams beat Caldya in Stage 1 (separate weeks), but WIP's Stage 2 dominance over broader opponent pool (2-0, 4 maps won) suggests higher current ceiling than Joblife's mixed results. BO3 format favors team with momentum and map pool confidence; WIP's undefeated start provides psychological and strategic advantage in preparation. Market price movement (YES down 1.5pp over 24h, sharp -11.5pp spike at 16:00 UTC then +10pp recovery) reflects late-stage uncertainty, possibly due to lineup changes, scrim results, or meta shifts not detailed in briefing\u2014suggests informed traders reducing YES conviction. Small tournament sample size (Week 1 only for Stage 2) creates variance, but WIP's +22 differential is not a close-game artifact; it indicates dominant execution. Joblife's head-to-head history vs Stage 1 opponents shows vulnerability to F9 (loss 1-2) and UCAM (0-2), but Stage 2 metrics limited to two matches. Current YES price (76%) overweights Joblife relative to standings and performance data; brief suggests market correction underway (falling trend). WIP Esports' seeding position (1st) post-Week 1 is determinative in early-stage round-robin; typically top seed converts ~70-75% against 4th-seed in BO3. No injury/roster/coaching changes mentioned in briefing; assume stability. Event timing (TODAY, ~5 hours to start) means no new information will surface; current market prices reflect latest available data.", "key_factor": "WIP Esports' 2-0 Stage 2 record with +22 map differential represents statistically significant competitive superiority over Joblife's 1-1 start; in best-of-3 Valorant, a team with established momentum and map control advantage typically converts 70-75% win probability in regional qualifier-tier matches."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "WIP Esports' 2-0 start is inflated by Week 1 only \u2014 early tournament records are historically volatile in B-Tier Valorant, especially with small map sample size (4 maps = limited meta exposure). Joblife's 1-1 record masks competitive individual performances (+8 differential = close map losses, not blowouts) \u2014 suggests they are closer in skill than standings imply. Critical data gap: NO DIRECT HEAD-TO-HEAD HISTORY between these teams in Stage 2 \u2014 market is overweighting current standings without matchup-specific intel (map pool mismatch, playstyle compatibility unknown). Market volatility spike at Apr 12 16:00 UTC (-11.5pp on YES) suggests late information arrival or lineup concern about Joblife; sharp reversal at 17:11 UTC (+10pp) indicates weak conviction in that correction \u2014 potential flip-flopping on incomplete news. Both teams previously competed against Caldya with identical 2-0 results in different matches \u2014 suggests competitive parity and that Caldya was an outlier opponent, not a tier differentiator. Joblife's recent Stage 1 losses (to UCAM, PXL 1-2) show resilience against stronger opponents; WIP Esports has no comparable Stage 1 difficulty data, raising overperformance risk. VCL France standings show clustered wins (1-2 records common) \u2014 early Week 1 seeding is unreliable for BO3 prediction; momentum and preparation matter more than 2 match records. Black swan: if Joblife has swapped agents/controller (common tactical pivots in French Valorant) or identified a WIP Esports map pool weakness (e.g. Sunset or Haven dominance expected but untested in Stage 2), BO3 format heavily favors the prepared underdog. Market price (76% YES) reflects recency bias toward WIP's undefeated start; NO side confidence is low (48) because briefing provides no evidence of WIP Esports' weaknesses, only surface standing strength.", "key_factor": "Joblife roster substitution or tactical pivot exploits WIP Esports' Stage 2 over-reliance on Week 1 meta reads, countering their map pool preparation with unexpected agent compositions or map bans."}], "final_score": 0.5721266968325792, "no_score": 0.459468085106383, "edge": -0.1878733031674208, "no_edge": 0.219468085106383, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "YES-side confidence too low: 63% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1951389", "question": "Valorant: Joblife vs WIP Esports (BO3) - VCL France: Revolution Stage 2 Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between Joblife and WIP Esports in the VCL France: Revolution Stage 2 Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 12 at 12:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Joblife\" if Joblife win the match against WIP Esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"WIP Esports\" if WIP Esports win the match against Joblife.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the 