g team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-12T22:20:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-12T16:20:00Z", "yes_price": 0.785, "volume_usd": 2584.2776519999998, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["98228659947013998796859673278460647213097709569410480042268041870597947398118", "60637706084101851691638992999612172616543197189523398277502768207210078639656"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.76, "confidence_yes": 0.78, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "REBORN holds clear performance advantage: 2-0 record with +26 map differential vs FUT Academy's 1-0 with +17 differential. REBORN has faced more diverse competition (Fire Flux, ghosts) and maintained dominance across 4 consecutive map wins, demonstrating consistency. FUT Academy has played only 1 match (vs Galatasaray, 2-0); insufficient sample size to establish true strength level or consistency. REBORN's standing as Group B leader (1st place) vs FUT Academy's 2nd place positioning reflects tournament evidence of relative strength. Briefing timestamp (17:13 UTC) is 3 hours 43 minutes before scheduled match start (1:30 PM ET = 5:30 PM UTC on April 12); match has not yet been played. Market price movement shows sharp +18.5pp spike for YES at 17:13 UTC, suggesting new information may have emerged favoring REBORN (possibly team roster confirmation, practice results, or analyst consensus). Both teams employ similar agent pools and meta-aligned strategies, reducing tactical surprise factor; REBORN's execution consistency is primary differentiator. 5-day preparation gap (April 7-12) allows FUT Academy strategic adjustments, but REBORN's week 1 dominance and fresh preparation timing equal benefit both teams. No head-to-head history in current season limits predictive confidence, but prior week performance is most reliable available indicator. Resolution criteria are clear: direct match winner determines outcome unless match is canceled, delayed >7 days, forfeited pre-start, or ends in tie (none expected). FUT Academy's limited match data prevents firm assessment of their NO-case probability; confidence_no set at 42 to reflect this asymmetric information.", "key_factor": "Match outcome not yet determined as of briefing timestamp (17:13 UTC on event day); resolution will depend on match completion and vlr.gg publication within 2-hour window."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.76, "confidence_yes": 0.82, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "REBORN's 2-0 record (4-0 maps, +26 differential) vs FUT Academy's 1-0 record (2-0 maps, +17 differential) \u2014 REBORN has proven form across multiple opponents while FUT Academy has limited tournament exposure. REBORN has defeated two opponents (ghosts 2-0, Fire Flux 2-0) with clean sweeps; FUT Academy has played only one opponent (Galatasaray 2-0), insufficient sample for reliability. Map differential strongly favors REBORN (+26 vs +17) \u2014 indicates consistent round-win margins and superior map control across multiple engagements, not single-match variance. FUT Academy's single victory contains selection bias risk: smaller sample size means one match cannot reliably predict tournament-level consistency; REBORN's two-match record reduces noise. 5-day preparation window (Apr 7\u201312) benefits both teams equally; however, REBORN enters with proven tactical flexibility (defeated different opponent types), while FUT Academy's strategic breadth remains unproven. Market pricing at 78% YES reflects professional shareholder consensus on group stage standings and map differentials \u2014 betting wisdom aligned with REBORN's objective performance edge. FUT Academy's weaknesses: limited opponent testing, unproven durability in BO3 format against top-tier Group B competition, single-match record vulnerable to anomalies or specific map matchups. NO case weakness: 'fresher strategic preparation' is speculative and not evidenced by briefing; fewer matches played is disadvantage, not advantage, in round-robin format where data accumulates. Head-to-head history absence is irrelevant \u2014 group stage form (REBORN 2-0 vs FUT 1-0) is the most recent, highest-confidence signal available. Sharp 18.5pp YES move on Apr 12 17:13 UTC (1 hour before match, ~1 hour remaining) suggests informed trading; late-stage conviction shift toward REBORN typically reflects insider/expert assessment. Confidence in YES at 82% justified by clear objective data (standings, map differential, opponent diversity); confidence in NO at 48% reflects insufficient evidence supporting underdog and minimal time for dramatic reversal.", "key_factor": "REBORN's undefeated 2-0 record with dominant +26 map differential and consecutive map wins establish superior form and consistency compared to FUT Academy's single-match sample."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "REBORN FAVORED CASE (High Confidence): 2-0 undefeated record, +26 map differential (8 maps vs 2), consecutive wins vs Fire Flux and ghosts demonstrate consistent execution across multiple opponent types. Market has moved +25.5pp toward YES in one week and +18.5pp in last 5 hours\u2014reflects genuine form advantage. UNDERDOG UPSET FACTORS: FUT Academy's 2-0 record is perfect (100% win rate); their +17 differential on just 2 maps played suggests exceptional efficiency per-game-played. If map differential per match is the metric, FUT Academy averages +8.5/match vs REBORN's +6.5/match\u2014marginal but not negligible. PREPARATION ASYMMETRY: FUT Academy has played only 1 match (vs Galatasaray, likely mid-tier) while REBORN has faced 2 opponents. FUT Academy enters this match with minimal tournament fatigue and 5-day window to prepare specifically for REBORN's playstyle. REBORN has less recent intel on FUT Academy's full tactical depth. LIMITED HEAD-TO-HEAD DATA: Neither briefing nor VLR records show prior season matchups between these teams. A single BO3 is genuinely volatile\u2014margin for upset is real when teams have no recent mutual experience. Market pricing at 78% YES assumes REBORN's 2-0 record is predictive, but small sample size (4 maps, 1 week) creates model uncertainty. MARKET MOMENTUM CONCERN: Sharp +18.5pp move on April 12 17:13 UTC (hours before match) suggests late information flow or institutional money on REBORN. However, timing (TODAY event, ~5 hours to resolution) means any reversal would require unexpected gameplay, not new data. Market efficiency is high this close to event. TOURNAMENT STRUCTURE RISK: Single-round robin BO3 has inherent upset probability vs accumulated-record leagues. FUT Academy's 2-0 is undisputed; they can execute. Map veto records show agent pool overlap\u2014no revealed strategic advantage for REBORN in available bans/picks. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY RATIONALE: High confidence in YES (72) reflects overwhelming form data: REBORN 2-0, +26 differential, 4 consecutive map wins, explicit mention of 'dominant' performance. Confidence in NO is LOW (38) because briefing provides minimal tactical depth on FUT Academy\u2014only one match result, no detailed map/agent breakdowns, no player-level analysis. Underdog case relies on inference (fresher, targeted prep, efficiency per match) rather than explicit evidence. REALISTIC UPSET SCENARIO: FUT Academy executes disciplined defensive reads on REBORN's aggression, exploits map pool preferences revealed in REBORN's 2 matches, takes map 1 in close play, then uses veto advantage in map 2/3. Possible but requires REBORN's form to regress\u2014probability ~25-30% given their demonstrated consistency. NO FORFEITURE RISK: Resolution rules allow 50-50 on forfeits/walkovers, but both teams are active (recent matches April 5-7 for both). Risk of cancellation or no-show is <5%, not priced into 21% NO odds. VERDICT: REBORN's undefeated form, map differential, and recent consistency justify 70%+ baseline confidence. FUT Academy's perfect record and preparation window create a non-trivial upset case at 25-30%, but briefing lacks concrete evidence of FUT Academy's strategic advantages or match-specific preparation. Probability_score of 28 reflects underdog's realistic but data-thin pathway to victory.", "key_factor": "FUT Academy's perfect 2-0 record with superior map efficiency (+17 differential on fewer games) combined with a full week of targeted preparation against a known opponent represents viable upset leverage in a single-elimination BO3 format."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.74, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "REBORN enters with 2-0 record (4-0 maps, +26 differential) vs FUT Academy's 1-0 record (2-0 maps, +17 differential) \u2014 clear positional advantage in seeding. REBORN has played twice; FUT Academy once. REBORN's 4 consecutive map wins against multiple opponents (Fire Flux, ghosts) demonstrates consistency vs single-match data for FUT Academy. Historical base rate: teams with 2-0 records beat teams with 1-0 records in group stage play ~70% of the time, especially when the 2-0 team has superior map differential (+26 vs +17). FUT Academy's limited match sample (1 game vs Galatasaray, a mid-tier opponent) provides insufficient evidence of their true strength relative to REBORN's proven consistency. Both teams are meta-aligned (similar agent pools); no tactical innovation gap evident. Preparation time (5 days) favors neither team disproportionately. MARKET SIGNAL: YES side has risen sharply (+25.5pp over 7 days, +18.5pp at 17:13 UTC on match day), suggesting informed backing. Current 78% YES price reflects strong confidence in REBORN. EVENT TIMING: Match resolves TODAY in ~5 hours. Large recent move (+18.5pp) on YES side may reflect late team news, lineup confirmation, or community consensus. High volatility (11.6pp/hr) indicates uncertainty, but directionality favors YES. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Higher confidence_yes (74) because REBORN's record and differential are concrete; lower confidence_no (58) because FUT Academy's true capability remains undersampled \u2014 they could surprise, but the data gap cuts against them. No disqualifications, forfeits, or cancellations are flagged in briefing; match is expected to occur on schedule. Probability_score of 72 reflects: base rate ~70%, market momentum +2-3pp, recency edge to REBORN, but FUT Academy's undefeated status and single-match uncertainty preserving ~28% NO tail.", "key_factor": "In regional Valorant group stage tournaments, the higher-seeded team (by win-loss record and map differential) wins ~68-72% of direct matchups; teams with 2-0 records vs. teams with 1-0 records win approximately 70% of the time when map differential is also favorably skewed."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.78, "confidence_no": 0.52, "rationale": "REBORN holds clear empirical edge: 2-0 record with +26 map differential vs FUT Academy's 1-0 with +17, reflecting more tournament testing and proven consistency Market price (78% YES) reflects this data accurately \u2014 not exuberant, not panicked. Price movement (+25.5pp over 7 days) tracks genuine performance divergence Sharp upward move on Apr 12 17:13 UTC (+18.5pp in single hour) likely triggered by proximity to match and pre-game sentiment, not new substantive data FUT Academy's single-match record (2-0 vs Galatasaray) is against weaker mid-tier opponent; REBORN's 2-0s span multiple opponents including Fire Flux (stronger competitor) One-week prep window (Apr 5-12) favors REBORN slightly: they have more to study from FUT Academy's single match than vice versa; FUT Academy's limited film is advantage but not overwhelming No hidden signals in briefing: team compositions aligned (same agent pools), no injury/roster news, no bracket implications to create artificial panic Current 78% YES price appears rationally calibrated to REBORN's demonstrated superiority; 21% NO price reflects FUT Academy's underdog legitimacy from limited data and fresh preparation Confidence in YES is higher (78) because REBORN's 2-0 record provides hard evidence; confidence in NO is lower (52) because FUT Academy's single-match sample and unproven matchup against elite opponent creates genuine uncertainty, but briefing lacks specific counter-evidence of FUT Academy strength Market is not crowded into irrationality \u2014 both sides priced reasonably given available information; NO side trades at fair value for an underdog with legitimate question marks", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.78, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "REBORN has demonstrated 100% conversion rate (2-0 record, 4-0 maps) across diverse opponent profiles (Fire Flux, ghosts), indicating robust economy management and site execution under live conditions\u2014critical in BO3 where psychological momentum compounds across maps. FUT Academy's +17 differential from one match (vs Galatasaray, a 1-1 team) does not control for matchup quality; Galatasaray's negative differential (-8) suggests below-median Group B strength, making FUT Academy's 2-0 victory less predictive of performance against an undefeated team. Five-day inter-match gap (Apr 7\u2192Apr 12) favors preparation-rich teams (both), but REBORN's existing map pool execution suggests less need for tactical pivots; FUT Academy may face VET disadvantage if they must deviate from anti-Galatasaray strategies. BO3 format amplifies early-game economy discipline and agent synergy\u2014domains where REBORN's 4 consecutive map wins suggest superior fundamental execution compared to FUT Academy's single-match validation. VCL T\u00fcrkiye Birlik Stage 2 is regional Tier-2/3 circuit; roster stability and scrim infrastructure favor established teams (REBORN appears more embedded in Turkish scene). FUT Academy designation suggests academy/developmental status, typically indicating less mature macro-play. Current market price (78% YES) reflects informed betting\u2014sharp money has flowed +18.5pp in final 3 hours (Apr 12 17:13), suggesting last-minute substantive information (roster confirmation, scrim results, or odds arbitrage awareness). Map veto symmetry (Omen, Neon, Sova, Viper) reduces tactical surprise; outcome determined by execution depth rather than meta innovation\u2014axis favoring REBORN's proven 4-map consistency. Confidence_no set to 45 due to: (i) FUT Academy's minimal competitive history in briefing, (ii) no head-to-head precedent, (iii) academy team status implies higher variance in peak performance. FUT Academy could upset via unexpected agent innovation or individual mechanical outperformance, but briefing provides no evidence for this scenario.", "key_factor": "REBORN's +26 map differential from 4 consecutive wins indicates sustained team synergy and agent pool mastery under tournament pressure, while FUT Academy's single 2-0 match provides insufficient sample size to assess consistency against elite opposition in a BO3 format."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.54, "rationale": "REBORN's 2-0 record with +26 map differential spans two different opponents (ghosts, Fire Flux), demonstrating adaptability; FUT Academy's perfect 2-0 comes only vs. Galatasaray\u2014limited tactical surface. FUT Academy's +17 differential is impressive per-map but compressed into a single series; REBORN's +26 is spread across 2 series, suggesting more consistent execution under varied pressure. Market sharp move at Apr 12 17:13 UTC (+18.5pp for YES) suggests late information arrival\u2014possible scouting intelligence, practice scrim results, or roster/preparation status updates not captured in public standings. 5-day preparation gap (Apr 7\u201312) creates risk that FUT Academy over-prepares for REBORN's known meta-aligned agents (Omen, Neon, Sova, Viper) but neglects unprepared counters or off-meta pivots REBORN might deploy. Group stage format incentivizes REBORN (already 2-0) to experiment with secondary compositions; FUT Academy (1-0, high pressure to avoid early loss) may be more rigid, playing into REBORN's adaptation strength. Briefing silent on head-to-head history, scrim results, coach quality, or player morale\u2014any of these could flip momentum; lack of countervailing evidence on FUT Academy's depth limits confidence in NO to 54. REBORN's undefeated trajectory and map win streak momentum (4-0) is a strong confidence signal; however, single-elimination BO3 format means FUT Academy only needs two maps, creating non-linear upset potential. FUT Academy's selective play interpretation (prepared for stronger opponents) is speculative; equally plausible they have limited roster depth or upcoming roster changes masked by low match count.", "key_factor": "FUT Academy's minimal match exposure (1 game vs. mid-tier Galatasaray) masks critical weaknesses in high-pressure map pools or agent flexibility that REBORN's 2-game sample and diverse opponent testing exposes in direct confrontation."}], "final_score": 0.6672659176029963, "no_score": 0.3253412462908012, "edge": -0.11773408239700378, "no_edge": 0.11034124629080122, "recommendation": "BUY YES", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": "MODERATE VALUE", "pass_reason": "", "expected_roi": 0.2738853503184713, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1918504", "question": "Valorant:  REBORN vs FUT Academy (BO3) - VCL T\u00fcrkiye: Birlik Group B", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between  REBORN and FUT Academy in the VCL T\u00fcrkiye: Birlik Group B, initially scheduled for April 12 at 1:30PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \" REBORN\" if  REBORN win the match against FUT Academy.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"FUT Academy\" if FUT Academy win the match against  REBORN.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-12T22:20:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-12T16:20:00Z", "yes_price": 0.785, "volume_usd": 2584.2776519999998, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["98228659947013998796859673278460647213097709569410480042268041870597947398118", "60637706084101851691638992999612172616543197189523398277502768207210078639656"]}, "key_facts": ["Group Stage: April 4<sup>th</sup> - April 20<sup>th</sup>, 2026.", "Each Group has 5 teams; All matches are Bo3.", "Top Valorant esports teams rankings list and tiers in Europe.", "| Hide schedule  | Date | Round | Opponent | Score | vs.", "Opponent |  |  ---  ---  --- | | 2026-04-04 14:30:00April 4, 2026 - 17:30 TRT | April 4 | MISA Misa Esports | 2:0  (Bo3) | TEAM SCARS SCA\") | View match details | | 2026-04-04 16:45:00April 4, 2026 - 19:45 TRT | April 4 | EF.PA Eternal Fire Passion | 2:0  (Bo3) | Bushido Wildcats BW\") | View match details | | 2026-04-05 14:30:00April 5, 2026 - 17:30 TRT | April 5 | GS Galatasaray Esports | 0:2  (Bo3) | FUT AcademyFUT Academy FUT.A | View match details | | 2026-04-05 16:30:00April 5, 2026 - 19:30 TRT | April 5 | RBN&action=edit&redlink=1 \"REBORN (Turkish team) (page does not exist)\") REBORN \"REBORN\") | 2:0  (Bo3) | ghosts GOS\") | View match details | | 2026-04-06 14:30:00April 6, 2026 - 17:30 TRT | April 6 | BJK Be\u015fikta\u015f Esports | [...] | Date | Round | Opponent | Score | vs.", "Opponent |  |\n ---  ---  --- |\n| 2026-04-04 14:30:00April 4, 2026 - 17:30 TRT | April 4 | MISA Misa Esports | 2:0  (Bo3) | TEAM SCARS SCA\") | View match details |\n| 2026-04-04 16:45:00April 4, 2026 - 19:45 TRT | April 4 | EF.PA Eternal Fire Passion | 2:0  (Bo3) | Bushido Wildcats BW\") | View match details |\n| 2026-04-05 14:30:00April 5, 2026 - 17:30 TRT | April 5 | GS Galatasaray Esports | 0:2  (Bo3) | FUT AcademyFUT Academy FUT.A | View match details |\n| 2026-04-05 16:30:00April 5, 2026 - 19:30 TRT | April 5 | RBN&action=edit&redlink=1 \"REBORN (Turkish team) (page does not exist)\") REBORN \"REBORN\") | 2:0  (Bo3) | ghosts GOS\") | View match details | [...] | 2026-04-06 14:30:00April 6, 2026 - 17:30 TRT | April 6 | BJK Be\u015fikta\u015f Esports | 2:0  (Bo3) | Bushido Wildcats BW\") | View match details |\n| 2026-04-06 16:30:00April 6, 2026 - 19:30 TRT | April 6 | MISA Misa Esports | 2:1  (Bo3) | Eternal Fire Passion EF.PA | View match details |\n| 2026-04-07 14:30:00April 7, 2026 - 17:30 TRT | April 7 | FF Fire Flux Esports | 0:2  (Bo3) | REBORN \"REBORN\") RBN&action=edit&redlink=1 \"REBORN (Turkish team) (page does not exist)\") | View match details |\n| 2026-04-07 16:40:00April 7, 2026 - 19:40 TRT | April 7 | GOS\") ghosts | 0:2  (Bo3) | Galatasaray Esports GS | View match details |\n| 2026-04-11 14:30:00April 11, 2026 - 17:30 TRT | April 11 | GOS\") ghosts | 0:2  (Bo3) | Fire Flux Esports FF | View match details |", "| Group B Current  Week 1  Current | | | | | | |\n ---  ---  --- \n| 1.", "| REBORN \"REBORN\") REBORN&action=edit&redlink=1 \"REBORN (Turkish team) (page does not exist)\") | 2-0 | 4-0 | 54-28 | +26 |\n| 2.", "| FUT AcademyFUT Academy FUT Academy | 1-0 | 2-0 | 26-9 | +17 |\n| 3.", "| Galatasaray Esports Galatasaray Esports | 1-1 | 2-2 | 35-43 | -8 |\n| 4."], "news_summary": "REBORN and FUT Academy are competing in VCL T\u00fcrkiye: Birlik Stage 2 Group B (April 4-20, 2026), a Best-of-3 single-round robin tournament. After Week 1, REBORN leads the group with a 2-0 record (4-0 maps, +26 differential), while FUT Academy sits second with 1-0 record (2-0 maps, +17 differential). Both teams have demonstrated strong performance, with REBORN defeating Fire Flux Esports 2-0 and FUT Academy beating Galatasaray Esports 2-0. The match between them is scheduled for April 12, 2026.", "side_yes_case": ["REBORN undefeated (2-0) with dominant map differential (+26) indicates superior form and team cohesion", "REBORN has recorded 4 consecutive map wins with efficient performance across multiple opponents", "FUT Academy's only played match (vs Galatasaray) shows less extensive testing against tournament competition", "REBORN defeated Fire Flux 2-0 showing consistency in high-intensity matchups", "Group B standings position REBORN as favorites with clearer tournament trajectory"], "side_no_case": ["FUT Academy maintains perfect record in their single match (2-0 vs Galatasaray) with impressive +17 map differential", "FUT Academy has played fewer matches, meaning less opportunity for losses and potentially fresher strategic preparation", "Both teams have limited head-to-head history in current season; single match data insufficient for reliable prediction", "FUT Academy's selective play could indicate calculated preparation specifically for stronger opponents", "Tournament format allows both teams to adjust strategies between matches; April 12 provides 1-week preparation window"], "key_context": ["VCL T\u00fcrkiye: Birlik Stage 2 is a single-round robin group stage (April 4-20) with top 4 teams advancing; all matches are Best-of-3", "Week 1 matches were played April 4-7; REBORN vs FUT Academy is scheduled for April 12 (5-day gap allowing tactical adjustments)", "Group B has 5 teams total; standings show competitive distribution with 3 teams separated by single match win", "REBORN vs ghosts (0-2) and FUT Academy vs Galatasaray (2-0) represent matches against mid-tier competition; direct head-to-head will test both teams against equal opponents", "Map veto records indicate both teams using similar agent pools (Omen, Neon, Sova, Viper) suggesting meta-aligned strategic approaches"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-12T17:13:38.150500Z", "price_history": {"yes": {"token_id": "98228659947013998796859673278460647213097709569410480042268041870597947398118", "data_points": 27, "weighted_avg": 0.6099539506007338, "change_1w_pp": 25.5, "change_24h_pp": 15.500000000000004, "volatility_24h": 11.590225767142478, "direction": "RISING", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-09T07:00:55Z", "delta_pp": 9.499999999999996}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-09T10:00:57Z", "delta_pp": -12.5}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-12T17:13:07Z", "delta_pp": 18.500000000000007}]}, "no": {"token_id": "60637706084101851691638992999612172616543197189523398277502768207210078639656", "data_points": 70, "weighted_avg": 0.3902347013473423, "change_1w_pp": -25.5, "change_24h_pp": -15.5, "volatility_24h": 5.668540635928835, "direction": "