{"run_id": "1651ab2f-0f73-4ed8-ae21-1706a7aa3dd4", "timestamp": "2026-04-12T17:20:30.696438+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1957893", "question": "Dota 2: Team Liquid vs Natus Vincere (BO3) - DreamLeague Western Europe Closed Qualifier Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Dota 2 Upper bracket round 2 match between Team Liquid and Natus Vincere in the DreamLeague Western Europe Closed Qualifier Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 12 at 2:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Liquid\" if Team Liquid win the match against Natus Vincere.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Natus Vincere\" if Natus Vincere win the match against Team Liquid.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://www.dotabuff.com. However, if https://www.dotabuff.com has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-13T00:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-12T18:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.59, "volume_usd": 13269.660179999999, "category": "dota-2", "clob_token_ids": ["69067852428622012291262386632776915994001435989763827900136454337096849124782", "93464336379451145084337188550949849490490856391607548050623041534461621391675"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "MATCH STATUS AMBIGUITY: The briefing states 'Natus Vincere and Nigma Galaxy in DreamLeague S29 WEU CQ that took place on April 12, 2026' but the market is for Team Liquid vs Natus Vincere on the same date/tournament. It is unclear if the Liquid-Navi match has already occurred, is scheduled for later on April 12, or has been canceled. MISSING CRITICAL DATA: No results for either team in DreamLeague S29 WEU Closed Qualifier Playoffs are present in the briefing. All Liquid results reference other tournaments (PGL Wallachia, Premier Series, EPL). No Navi results at DreamLeague CQ are provided. LIQUID'S RECENT FORM (Mixed): Liquid won 2-0 vs HEROIC (March 14), beat YeS 2-1 and VP 2-1 (early April), but lost 0-2 to NGX (April 7) and 1-2 to L1GA (April 8). Form is inconsistent across tier-1 and tier-2 opponents. NAVI'S RECENT FORM (Unknown): Only one Navi result provided: HEROIC beat Navi 2-1 in PGL Wallachia Round 4 (March 10). No other recent Navi playoff results across relevant tournaments provided. Navi's DreamLeague CQ form cannot be assessed. MARKET PRICE MOVEMENT SIGNAL: YES dropped 16.5pp in 24 hours (63% to 59%), suggesting late-breaking information shifted sentiment toward Navi. However, the briefing provides no explicit reason for this move, creating uncertainty about its cause. RESOLUTION CRITERIA CLARITY: Criteria are clear on resolution mechanics (team win, forfeit handling, delays). Team name matching criteria are explicit and should not create ambiguity for 'Team Liquid' vs 'Natus Vincere'. HEAD-TO-HEAD UNKNOWN: No direct competitive history between Liquid and Navi in the briefing; relative strength cannot be inferred from direct matchups. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: DreamLeague S29 WEU CQ Playoffs carries qualification stakes, but briefing lacks team seeding, bracket position, or recent CQ-specific performance to differentiate the teams. DUAL PERSPECTIVE: Liquid shows competitive tier-1 capability (beat HEROIC, YeS, VP) but also loses decisively to strong opponents (0-2 NGX). Navi's strength is obscured; one loss to HEROIC is insufficient to assess tier. Market movement toward Navi suggests informed traders detected an edge, but briefing does not support visible evidence of that edge. CONSERVATIVE ASSIGNMENT: Given severe data asymmetry (Liquid's recent form somewhat visible, Navi's DreamLeague form absent) and match status ambiguity, probability centers near 50 with slight downward bias toward Liquid (42) reflecting market repricing away from YES. Both confidence scores remain low due to missing critical data.", "key_factor": "Briefing data is severely incomplete: no direct head-to-head history, no current roster information, no recent DreamLeague Closed Qualifier Playoffs results for either team, and conflicting tournament references (Navi vs Nigma Galaxy on April 12 vs. Navi vs Liquid on April 12) create ambiguity about match status."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "YES SIDE STRENGTH: Liquid secured back-to-back victories in DreamLeague S29 WEU OQ2 just yesterday/today (Apr 10-11), including a dominant 2-0 shutout vs Levant, indicating they are in tournament rhythm for this DreamLeague event. YES SIDE STRENGTH: Liquid's tier-1 playoff wins at PGL Wallachia (2-0 vs HEROIC on Mar 14, wins vs TSpirit, BB) show capability against top-tier opposition in high-stakes playoff environments. YES SIDE STRENGTH: Liquid's Premier Series Decider win (2-1 vs YeS on Apr 7) and victories over VP (2-1) in early April demonstrate consistent ability to win playoff matches at similar stakes. YES SIDE STRENGTH: The market has priced Liquid at 59%, reflecting favoritism that appears justified by their more recent DreamLeague-specific preparation vs broader tournament play. NO SIDE WEAKNESS: Navi's recent competitive data is sparse in the briefing; only confirmed result shows them facing Nigma Galaxy at DreamLeague S29 WEU CQ on Apr 12 at 12:00 UTC, but no result provided, suggesting either uncertainty or a less dominant recent record. NO SIDE WEAKNESS: Liquid's losses (0-2 to NGX on Apr 7, 1-2 to L1GA on Apr 8, 1-2 to NGX on Apr 10) cluster in Premier Series playoffs, not DreamLeague qualifiers\u2014suggesting tournament-specific inconsistency rather than fundamental weakness in DreamLeague format. MARKET SIGNAL CONCERN: YES side fell 16.5pp in past 24 hours (63% \u2192 59%), indicating either late-breaking information about Navi, injury concerns, or contrarian betting despite Liquid's DreamLeague qualifier success. INCOMPLETE DATA: Briefing lacks Navi's recent match history, win-loss record, or head-to-head context vs Liquid, making NO side confidence asymmetrically lower; cannot fully evaluate Navi's form or specific strengths. TIME-CRITICAL: Event occurs TODAY (~7 hours), resolving imminently\u2014limited opportunity for narrative reversal; current pricing reflects real-time intelligence about team readiness. VERDICT: Liquid's documented DreamLeague-specific wins and tier-1 playoff experience justify YES favoritism, but 16.5pp recent decline and lack of Navi data suggest market uncertainty is partially rational; 58% reflects confidence in Liquid's edge while acknowledging non-trivial underdog risk.", "key_factor": "Team Liquid's recent DreamLeague S29 WEU OQ2 qualifier wins (2-0 vs Levant, 1-0 vs IC, 1-0 vs Platoon on April 10-11) demonstrate tournament-specific momentum heading into the Closed Qualifier Playoffs."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.52, "confidence_no": 0.68, "rationale": "UNDERDOG CASE FOR NO (Na'Vi): Market has shifted -16.5pp toward NO in 24 hours, suggesting material new information or smart money recognizing Na'Vi's viability; this sharp move is NOT random noise in a TODAY event with 7-hour resolution window. LIQUID'S INCONSISTENCY: Briefing shows Liquid lost 0-2 to NGX (April 7), then 1-2 to L1GA (April 8), then 1-2 to NGX again (April 10)\u2014three losses in four playoff matches across multiple tournaments in early April; this is NOT the form of a 59% favorite. LIQUID'S RECENT RECORD CONTEXT: While Liquid beat HEROIC 2-0 (March 14) and won some earlier April matches, the most recent PREMIER SERIES playoff results (April 8-10) show Liquid dropping 2 of 3 matches; recency matters in esports form assessment. NA'VI DATA OPACITY: Briefing states Na'Vi 'faced Nigma Galaxy at DreamLeague S29 WEU CQ on April 12' but provides NO score or outcome; unable to assess Na'Vi's momentum or current form heading into this match\u2014this is a major asymmetry favoring the underdog narrative. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: This is DreamLeague S29 WEU CLOSED QUALIFIER playoffs, a high-stakes qualifier; Na'Vi's presence here suggests they are a legitimate regional contender; seeding/bracket position unknown but both teams clearly qualified for playoffs. MARKET EFFICIENCY CHECK: 59% YES pricing assumes Liquid is clearly favored, yet the briefing data shows Liquid 1-2 in their last three playoff matches (April 8, 10, 10) against similar-tier opponents; 59% may overweight historical wins from March and underweight April form collapse. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Confidence in YES is moderate (52) because Liquid's recent losses are concrete but mixed with earlier wins; confidence in NO is stronger (68) because the 16.5pp market shift in a TODAY event combined with NO scoring data and Liquid's April struggles provides clearer evidence for upset potential. BO3 FORMAT ADVANTAGE: Best-of-3 favors the team with better overall form and adaptability; if Na'Vi has cohesion and Liquid is tilting (suggested by playoff losses), Na'Vi can steal this in a tiebreaker game 3. RESOLUTION TIMING: Event resolves in ~7 hours; market has already moved sharply; if Na'Vi were clearly outmatched, sharp bettors would not have pushed NO from 25% to 41% in 24 hours without fresh intelligence or observable form data. VERDICT: Liquid remains slightly favored based on historical wins and tier-1 tournament credentials, but Liquid's April playoff collapse (3 consecutive losses in competitive matches) combined with complete lack of Na'Vi outcome data and smart-money market shift warrants 38% for NO (i.e., 62% for Liquid\u2014below current 59% YES price, suggesting NO is UNDERPRICED relative to Liquid's recent form deterioration).", "key_factor": "Team Liquid's recent inconsistency (losses to NGX 0-2 and L1GA 1-2 in April playoffs) suggests vulnerability against a determined Na'Vi side competing at DreamLeague with unclear but potentially strong recent form."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.48, "confidence_yes": 0.32, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing does NOT provide the actual scheduled match result or current status. The event timing shows TODAY (resolves in ~7 hours), yet no outcome confirmation exists in the provided data. MARKET SIGNAL ANALYSIS: YES price fell sharply 16.5pp on Apr 12 at 14:00 UTC, suggesting material negative information emerged for Team Liquid. This sharp move occurred hours before the ~2PM ET scheduled match time. TEAM LIQUID RECENT FORM: Mixed results in April 2026 \u2014 won 2-0 vs HEROIC and 2-1 vs multiple opponents (YeS, VP), but lost 0-2 to NGX (Apr 7) and 1-2 to L1GA in playoffs, showing inconsistency against tier-1 opposition. NATUS VINCERE CONTEXT: Briefing mentions Navi faced Nigma Galaxy on Apr 12 at 12:00 UTC in DreamLeague S29 WEU CQ, but no result provided. If this match occurred immediately before the Liquid vs Navi scheduled match, fatigue or momentum effects are unknown. HEAD-TO-HEAD DATA: No direct recent matchup history provided between Liquid and Navi in briefing. Cannot assess team-specific dynamics. SHARP PRICE MOVE INTERPRETATION: The -16.5pp drop on Apr 12 14:00 UTC is material and occurred near the scheduled match time. This likely reflects either a team roster issue, live match observation disadvantageous to Liquid, or an announced postponement/cancellation. Without explicit confirmation of the match status, confidence in either outcome must be depressed. RESOLUTION RISK: If the match was postponed or cancelled (as suggested by the price crash timing), it may resolve 50-50 per market rules. This adds substantial ambiguity. BASE RATE: Dota 2 BO3 matches between tier-1 European teams are highly variable (45-55% for either side). Without clear momentum, direct history, or confirmed match status, a near-midpoint estimate is warranted. CONFIDENCE PENALTY: Both confidence scores are deliberately LOW due to fundamental data gaps: (1) no confirmation the match occurred, (2) no head-to-head history, (3) ambiguous post-Apr-12-14:00 market signal, (4) unknown Navi momentum from their Apr 12 match.", "key_factor": "In competitive Dota 2 BO3 matches between tier-1 European teams with mixed recent form, the base rate is approximately 50-55% for either team to advance, depending on head-to-head history and current momentum."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.54, "confidence_yes": 0.52, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "Sharp 16.5pp drop in YES price at Apr 12 14:00 UTC suggests informed traders obtained new information ~2 hours before match start, indicating market efficiently processed late-breaking data. Current 59% YES price reflects modest Liquid edge, consistent with mixed recent form: Liquid beat HEROIC (2-0), VP (2-1) but lost to NGX (0-2), L1GA (1-2)\u2014shows tier-1 ceiling but also vulnerability to upper-bracket opponents. Navi context is murky: briefing shows Navi vs Nigma Galaxy match on Apr 12 but match details are incomplete; unclear if Navi won, lost, or what momentum status is entering this matchup. Market volatility (9.5pp/hr) is high for ~7-hour window to resolution, but sharp move occurred early (14:00 UTC) leaving 3+ hours for repositioning\u2014late-breaking signal (roster changes, player absence, technical issues) likely triggered the drop. Asymmetric data quality: Liquid's recent match history is clear and rich; Navi's recent form and tournament status in this specific event is vague. Briefing notes Navi played Nigma but does NOT confirm Navi's outcome or seeding impact on Liquid matchup. Both confidence scores depressed (52/48) due to critical information gap on Navi's current status, tournament bracket positioning, and what exactly triggered the 16.5pp repricing at 14:00 UTC\u2014insufficient detail to assign high confidence either direction. 59% YES price is NOT irrational given Liquid's slightly superior recent track record, but the precision of pricing is unwarranted given incomplete briefing data on Navi. NO side (41%) appears undervalued only if Navi's recent form is weak; if Navi won their Apr 12 match convincingly, 41% NO is too low and market may be slow to adjust. Time-to-reversal tension: 7 hours remain; any major news (lineup announcement, player illness, technical postponement) would need to surface imminently to swing 59\u219241 range meaningfully before lock.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.54, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA INTEGRITY ISSUE: The briefing's match history tables are malformed and contain HTML artifacts, duplicate entries, and unclear tournament sequencing, making definitive recent-form analysis unreliable for probability estimation. TIMING ANOMALY: The NEWS SUMMARY states 'Navi faced Nigma Galaxy at DreamLeague S29 WEU CQ on April 12, 2026' \u2014 the same date and tournament as the scheduled Liquid vs Navi match. This suggests either Navi played a different round/bracket stage immediately before this match (rapid turnaround) or the match may have been rescheduled/delayed, introducing uncertainty. TEAM LIQUID FORM ASSESSMENT: Extractable data shows Liquid with mixed recent results \u2014 wins vs HEROIC (2-0), YeS (2-1), VP (2-1), but losses to NGX (0-2 on April 7, 1-2 in playoffs on April 10) and L1GA (1-2). This inconsistency against mid-tier opponents suggests volatile form rather than dominant trajectory. NATUS VINCERE FORM: Insufficient clean data on Navi's recent DreamLeague qualifier performance. The brief references Navi vs Nigma on April 12 but provides no outcome; unable to assess Navi's momentum or bracket position heading into the Liquid matchup. MARKET PRICE DYNAMICS: Sharp 16.5pp move favoring NO (Navi) on Apr 12 14:00 UTC, exactly when Navi's DreamLeague match vs Nigma would have occurred. This suggests market reaction to a Navi victory or superior performance, but briefing does not confirm outcome \u2014 implies sophisticated traders have external information not present in this briefing. RESOLUTION RISK: Match scheduled for April 12 2:00 PM ET (~6 hours prior to briefing timestamp of Apr 12 17:20 UTC). Event timing marked 'TODAY' with ~7 hours to resolution. If match has already occurred, market prices reflect known outcome trading; if not yet played, high volatility and sharp move suggest credible external information favors Navi. OPERATIONAL CONTEXT: Both teams competing in multiple tournaments simultaneously (PREMIER SERIES, DreamLeague OQ/CQ, PGL Wallachia) typical of esports qualification season. Fatigue, player rotation, or draft adaptation across rapid-fire matches could favor a team with clearer recent momentum. CONFIDENCE DEPRESSION: Corrupted data sources and unresolved Navi vs Nigma outcome create asymmetric information penalty. Cannot confidently evaluate Navi's true form, patch adaptation, or draft strategy heading into Liquid match. MODEST YES LEAN: Market currently 59% YES, but sharp recent move to 41% NO suggests sophisticated correction. Assigning 54% YES reflects slight lean toward Liquid (established franchise, partial positive recent record) but with suppressed confidence due to data gaps and post-match trading volatility signal.", "key_factor": "The briefing contains fragmented and corrupted match data that obscures critical recent form signals, and the NEWS SUMMARY references a Navi vs Nigma Galaxy match on April 12 rather than confirming Navi's availability for the scheduled Liquid vs Navi matchup \u2014 a potential reschedule or substitution scenario that materially affects competitive assessment."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.65, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing states Navi faced Nigma Galaxy at DreamLeague S29 WEU CQ on April 12 at 12:00, yet this market allegedly scheduled for April 12 at 2:00 PM ET (~7:00 UTC equivalent). Timeline is muddled\u2014unclear if Navi already played today or if match is still pending. MARKET MOMENTUM REVERSAL: YES tumbled 16.5pp in sharp move on Apr 12 at 14:00 UTC. This sharp reversal suggests NEW information emerged (likely Navi's result vs Nigma or Liquid's recent form update) that materially shifted trader confidence toward NO. LIQUID'S FORM IS VOLATILE, NOT DOMINANT: Recent Premier Series playoffs show 1-2 loss to L1GA (Apr 8) and 1-2 loss to NGX (Apr 10). Liquid won vs HEROIC 2-0 (Apr 9), but alternating strong/weak performances in high-pressure formats indicate inconsistency under playoff pressure. FIXTURE SATURATION & FATIGUE SIGNAL: Liquid played 5 matches in 3 days (April 8-10 Premier Series), then pivoted to DreamLeague OQ matches (April 10-11). Playing in upper bracket today after minimal rest increases injury/mental fatigue risk, particularly in BO3 grinding. NAVI'S COMPETITIVE PROFILE OBSCURED: Briefing provides almost no recent Navi match history except the Nigma face-off. Their early-April results are not documented. This absence makes it impossible to assess whether Navi is trending hot or cold\u2014CLASSIC underdog information asymmetry. HEROIC ANOMALY: Liquid beat HEROIC 2-0 on Mar 14, but HEROIC also appears on Liquid's match history multiple times. This suggests repeated rematches in the same tournament cycle\u2014possible fatigue in reading meta, or Heroic adapted between Mar 14 and now (Heroic lost to MOUZ 0-2 on Apr 8, showing recent weakness). UPPER BRACKET POSITION = HIGH-STAKES FORMAT: Both teams are fighting for DreamLeague qualification. Upper bracket losses eliminate or severely damage bracket position. Liquid's inconsistency (wins vs mid-tier, losses vs NGX/L1GA) under high-pressure playoff conditions is a RED FLAG for TODAY. ABSENCE OF DIRECT H2H: No recent Liquid vs Navi match data provided. Without head-to-head or map pool overlap clarity, market is pricing on team reputation alone, not matchup-specific intel. Navi may have a theoretical edge Liquid traders cannot see. TIMING CRITICALITY: Event is TODAY, resolving ~7 hours from briefing timestamp. No time for lineup changes or roster swaps, but injury/illness (especially after fatigue-heavy schedule) or last-minute coaching adjustment could favor the team with better adaptation speed under pressure. CONTRARIAN LEAN: Market currently 59% YES, but YES side is FALLING and NO side RISING. Late-hour traders (often sharp) are shifting toward Navi. Combined with Liquid's recent close-bracket losses and fatigue signal, the 59% YES price may be stale consensus from early-week betting.", "key_factor": "Natus Vincere deploys a pocket meta pick or tactical innovation specifically designed to counter Liquid's recent draft patterns, combined with Liquid roster fatigue from back-to-back Premier Series and DreamLeague matches across 48 hours."}], "final_score": 0.4810725552050473, "no_score": 0.5368768768768769, "edge": -0.10892744479495264, "no_edge": 0.12687687687687688, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Contrarian call: council prob 54% < 70% threshold; Contrarian call: NO-side confidence 48% < 80% threshold", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1957893", "question": "Dota 2: Team Liquid vs Natus Vincere (BO3) - DreamLeague Western Europe Closed Qualifier Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Dota 2 Upper bracket round 2 match between Team Liquid and Natus Vincere in the DreamLeague Western Europe Closed Qualifier Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 12 at 2:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Liquid\" if Team Liquid win the match against Natus Vincere.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Natus Vincere\" if Natus Vincere win the match against Team Liquid.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://www.dotabuff.com. However, if https://www.dotabuff.com has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\