(this is Week 1, match timing suggests earlier games already played\u2014no data on either team's W-L record THIS tournament); (3) map pool matchups or veto dynamics; (4) any coaching/tactical changes. VCT 2026 is explicitly a 'new season with potentially updated rosters and meta shifts'\u2014this is a competitive reset signal, yet briefing relies almost entirely on 2023-2025 aggregate data. That lag is a blind spot. Leviat\u00e1n's 2024-2025 wins vs. G2, NRG, and KR\u00dc demonstrate they CAN beat top-tier opponents; the case for YES is built on HISTORICAL dominance, not current season performance. BO3 format + 10-hour window means minimal time for roster news/injuries to be reflected in market pricing. If a key Cloud9 player is illness-struck or benched in the hours before match start, market will not adjust meaningfully. Market price (57% YES) reflects moderate confidence, not overwhelming conviction; 7-day rise of +3pp suggests slow upward drift, not sharp conviction\u2014indicative of uncertainty being repriced gradually rather than informed by concrete new intel. Black swan: If Leviat\u00e1n has identified a tactical/meta counter to Cloud9's playstyle (e.g., agent comp advantage, site execution timing) OR has rotated in a high-performing substitute (regional stand-in, academy player with fresh prep), Cloud9's historical record becomes tactical noise. BO3 allows Leviat\u00e1n to adapt bans/picks across maps; one map win + momentum swing could flip series. Confidence in YES (72) reflects strong historical record and market consensus, but confidence in NO (54) is artificially suppressed by data gaps\u2014we have almost NO current-season intel on Leviat\u00e1n's actual strength or roster health this year, which should lower conviction in the YES narrative.", "key_factor": "Leviat\u00e1n executes a fresh meta adaptation or roster substitution (e.g., stand-in player, tactical innovation targeting Cloud9's map pool weaknesses) that cloud9 has not prepared for, converting historical matchup dominance into irrelevance in a single BO3."}], "final_score": 0.57, "no_score": 0.42426315789473684, "edge": 0.0, "no_edge": -0.005736842105263207, "recommendation": "BUY YES", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": "HIGH VALUE", "pass_reason": "", "expected_roi": 0.7543859649122808, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1700801", "question": "Valorant: Cloud9 vs Leviat\u00e1n Esports (BO3) - VCT Americas Stage 1 Group Alpha", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between Cloud9 and Leviat\u00e1n Esports in the VCT Americas Stage 1 Group Alpha, initially scheduled for April 12 at 5:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Cloud9\" if Cloud9 win the match against Leviat\u00e1n Esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Leviat\u00e1n Esports\" if Leviat\u00e1n Esports win the match against Cloud9.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.", "end_date": "2026-04-13T03:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-12T21:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.57, "volume_usd": 56754.110753999994, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["22857921000622385995940539269549464587304217497730044339578261329919998819734", "63767421704783462614534417404247857545846937996242126282531639248699219357929"