ame differential in LCK CL Rounds 1-2 represents a fundamental competitive gap; academy teams rarely recover from this depth of early-season collapse against established CL opponents like DRX Challengers without roster intervention or meta shifts."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.18, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "Gen.G Global Academy enters with a stark 0-4 record and -5 game differential, which is historically predictive of continued poor performance in immediate rematches. Market has been falling sharply since Apr 10-11 (-30.5pp over 7 days), indicating strong consensus formation around DRX superiority; this confidence is reflected in NO side climbing to 80%. CONTRARIAN BLIND SPOT: The briefing contains almost no substantive data on Kiwoom DRX Challengers' own recent form, roster stability, or meta adaptation\u2014we are betting on an unknown opponent. Gen.G's champion pool data shows flexibility across K'Sante, Skarner, Ahri, Ashe, Seraphine compositions; if DRX's draft lacks diversity or has a key player underperforming in Bo3 format, Gen.G could exploit this. Best-of-3 format intrinsically favors the team with the higher adaptation ceiling; Gen.G's 0-4 record may mask draft/coaching adjustments not visible in aggregate stats. STRUCTURAL RISK: No head-to-head history provided; LCK Challengers matches can exhibit high variance in early-season play due to roster instability, coaching changes, or meta misalignment. PSYCHOLOGICAL FACTOR: Gen.G Academy may be in a 'nothing to lose' mentality after 0-4 start; DRX may be overconfident or complacent given heavy market favor (80%). Market pricing at 20% YES reflects consensus view; however, confidence_no is capped at 72 due to absence of any DRX-specific performance data\u2014council risks overweighting limited Gen.G intel. EVENT TIMING (TODAY, ~17 hours to resolution): Any late-breaking roster/injury news favorable to Gen.G or detrimental to DRX could flip shares, but w