e moves, indicating coordinated backing or insider knowledge of regain's strength relative to Zomblers. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: CCT North America is a mid-tier regional circuit; neither team appears in major international tournament coverage (PGL Bucharest, BLAST Rotterdam noted in briefing), suggesting regional-level play. BO3 FORMAT STABILITY: Best-of-three playoff matches in CS2 are deterministic once played; no inherent upset bias unless teams are severely mismatched in preparation or roster health. TIMING CRITICALITY: Event timing is TODAY (~5 hours to resolution). Match likely already in progress or completed. If completed, shares should have traded to extremes ($0.01 or $0.99); current pricing at 28/72 suggests match may be ongoing or result pending official confirmation. BETTING PATTERN INTERPRETATION: The -26pp collapse on YES suggests either (a) regain confirmation of stronger roster/form became public late, or (b) Zomblers roster issues/forfeiture risk emerged. Without source data, cannot distinguish. NO CONFIDENCE IN EITHER DIRECTION: Absence of team statistics, recent form, or head-to-head data means confidence in both YES and NO estimates must be severely depressed. MARKET PRICE ANCHOR: Current 28/72 split reflects aggregated smart money; in information-vacuum matches, market consensus often outperforms unfounded speculation. CONSERVATIVE STANCE: Adopt market-implied probability (28%) as baseline, with low confidence on both sides due to data insufficiency.", "key_factor": "Severe data vacuum on both team rosters, recent form, and head-to-head history makes confident prediction impossible; market pricing at 28/72 appears driven by recent sharp betting moves rather than public information."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.24, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "Market has collapsed 30.5pp over 7 days with a sharp -26pp drop on Apr 12 at 22:36 UTC (~5 hours before match). This is NOT gradual repricing \u2014 it suggests new information (roster change, injury report, or tactical intel) emerged late, not pre-existing fundamentals. Briefing contains zero competitive data on either team: no recent match results, no roster lists, no head-to-head history, no LAN placements. This void is suspicious for a match about to be played in 5 hours on a structured playoff stage. The only roster change mentioned in briefing is ScreaM's return to a different org (FUT/Clutchain), with no connection to Zomblers or regain. Absence of roster continuity reporting for these two teams is a red flag for potential last-minute personnel shifts. CCT tournaments are mid-tier regional competition, not tier-1 majors. Teams at this level have higher injury/illness rates, less deep benches, and more volatile personnel than BLAST/PGL events. A stand-in playing BO3 is plausible and impactful. 72% market confidence in regain suggests consensus is strong but built on zero data provided in briefing. Consensus without evidence is vulnerable to a single tactical or personnel surprise. BO3 format amplifies the impact of individual fragging power and map pool synergy. A substitute player (even mid-tier tier-2) can cost a BO3 series if regain's preparation assumed the original Zomblers lineup. Market volatility on NO side (4.1pp/hr) is LOWER than YES side (15.0pp/hr), suggesting informed traders on the NO side are confident but not hedging uncertainty \u2014 typical of a move based on single new fact (e.g. roster report) rather than probabilistic debate. Event timing is TODAY with 5-hour window. Any major reversal must occur now or during the match. Late-breaking roster news (player pulled for quarantine, emergency substitution) is the only remaining catalyst with 100x impact. Briefing explicitly states 'no details provided about these two teams' performances, rosters, or head-to-head matchups.' Market odds of 28/72 with NO rising and YES falling indicate traders possess out-of-briefing information (likely a roster or form signal). The contrarian play is: what if that information is incomplete or misinterpreted, and Zomblers has a hidden lineup advantage (sub is actually a young star, or regain's reported roster is stale)?", "key_factor": "Zomblers' roster contains a substitute or academy player filling for a key fragger due to illness/injury sustained between group stage and playoffs, reducing firepower in a BO3 format where map pool depth and individual fragging power are decisive."}], "final_score": 0.27370786516853934, "no_score": 0.7267368421052631, "edge": -0.006292134831460683, "no_edge": 0.006736842105263152, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 27% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1944807", "question": "Counter-Strike: Zomblers vs regain (BO3) - CCT North America Series #4 Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Quarterfinal 2 match between Zomblers and regain in the CCT North America Series #4 Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 12 at 5:30PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Zomblers\" if Zomblers win the match against regain.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"regain\" if regain win the match against Zomblers.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-13T03:30:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-12T21:30:00Z", "yes_price": 0.28, "volume_usd": 19514.727827, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["31595149289954387051316551062955819753655594638009720438498051590292066650300", "62222657555555293806597967054073621262692079371733458679586393549244523374947"]}, "key_facts": ["If team dont win nothing, theyre not tier1?", "Bro, so CCT tournaments who won it, tier1 teams?", "Bro ur brain so small, now era vitality, they winning", "Group Stage: Two double-elimination format (GSL) Groups.", "Each group has 4 teams; All matches are Bo3.", "Top two teams from each group advance to the Playoffs.", "Group Stage: March 3<sup>rd</sup> - March 22<sup>nd</sup>, 2026.", "Choose theme:\n\nLiveESL Challenger League Season 51 North America Cup 3\n\nInControl ()\n\nregain ()\n\n03:00AMPGL Bucharest 2026\n\nMIBR\n\n3DMAX\n\n06:00AMPGL Bucharest 2026\n\nAstralis\n\nEYEBALLERS\n\n09:00AMPGL Bucharest 2026\n\nFUT\n\nB8\n\n12:00PMPGL Bucharest 2026\n\nThe MongolZ\n\nPARIVISION\n\n05:30PMCCT Season 3 North America Series 4\n\nAkimbo\n\nInControl\n\nHe's back!", "April 8, 2026 07:51PM\n\nWritten by Mnmzzz\n\n# Breaking: ScreaM returns to action six years after hanging up the mouse\n\nThe 31-year-old fragger will look to roll back the clock on the Franco-Belgian roster.", "[...] ScreaM's road back to competitive Counter-Strike first began in 2025 when he joined FUT as a sixth-man and streamer alongside the organization's short-lived French lineup."], "news_summary": "The search results do not contain specific information about a Counter-Strike match between Zomblers and regain in the CCT North America Series #4 Playoffs. The results mention that CCT Season 3 North American Series #4 uses a Bo3 format with double-elimination GSL groups where top two teams advance to playoffs, but no details are provided about these two teams' performances, rosters, or head-to-head matchups. Recent competitive CS2 news focuses on other tournaments (PGL Bucharest 2026, BLAST Rotterdam) and roster changes (ScreaM's return to Clutchain).", "side_yes_case": ["Insufficient data on Zomblers to assess competitive position", "No recent performance metrics or roster information available for either team", "CCT tournaments are established competitive events with structured playoff formats"], "side_no_case": ["Insufficient data on regain to assess competitive position", "No head-to-head record or recent match history between the teams", "Neither team appears in major tournament coverage or tier-1 competition results mentioned"], "key_context": ["CCT North America Series #4 uses Bo3 format in both group stage and playoffs", "Double-elimination GSL group stage format means teams have multiple opportunities", "Search results do not contain specific team rosters, recent form, or direct match information", "No player performance statistics or recent match results for either Zomblers or regain are provided", "Prediction requires data not present in available search results"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-12T22:37:14.507331Z", "price_history": {"yes": {"token_id": "31595149289954387051316551062955819753655594638009720438498051590292066650300", "data_points": 8, "weighted_avg": 0.42922145332874834, "change_1w_pp": -30.5, "change_24h_pp": -26.5, "volatility_24h": 15.01943185787443, "direction": "FALLING", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-12T22:36:50Z", "delta_pp": -26.0}]}, "no": {"token_id": "62222657555555293806597967054073621262692079371733458679586393549244523374947", "data_points": 39, "weighted_avg": 0.5431363821798181, "change_1w_pp": 30.500000000000004, "change_24h_pp": 26.0, "volatility_24h": 4.068217700285594, "direction": "RISING", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-11T16:00:39Z", "delta_pp": 13.000000000000005}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-12T22:00:41Z", "delta_pp": 17.000000000000004}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-12T22:36:39Z", "delta_pp": 6.500000000000005}]}, "fetched_at": "2026-04-12T22:37:15.200362Z"}}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-13T03:30:00Z", "winning_side": "NO", "final_yes_price": 0.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-13T18:32:23.455280+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "50937f21-2e6b-4442-a16e-c6bfc90a4d6a", "timestamp": "2026-04-12T22:42:32.517387+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1957254", "question": "Dota 2: REKONIX vs Execration (BO3) - DreamLeague Southeast Asia Closed Qualifier Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Dota 2 Lower bracket round 1 match between REKONIX and Execration in the DreamLeague Southeast Asia Closed Qualifier Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 13 at 12:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"REKONIX\" if REKONIX win the match against Execration.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Execration\" if Execration win the match against REKONIX.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://www.dotabuff.com. However, if https://www.dotabuff.com has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-13T10:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T04:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.595, "volume_usd": 5836.930782000001, "category": "dota-2", "clob_token_ids": ["19645993083358442742427887978464820084450555715756805695840451792503250217278", "41283529597162218208049873685158223403789744271665435012088618769770690675923"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.52, "confidence_yes": 0.38, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "REKONIX recent form is mixed: won 2-0 vs XctN and VRJ (mid-tier opponents), lost 0-2 to GLYPH, and lost to Team Nemesis in DreamLeague S29 SEA CQ playoffs, indicating inconsistent playoff performance. REKONIX also lost 0-2 to Tundra and GL at ESL One Birmingham, suggesting vulnerability against strong opposition when pressure is highest. Execration's recent performance data is completely absent from briefing\u2014no match results, roster composition, recent form, or head-to-head records available. Without Execration performance data, cannot perform meaningful comparative analysis; market price of 60% YES appears to rest on information not provided in briefing. REKONIX qualified for DreamLeague playoffs, demonstrating baseline competency, but playoff context differs from group stage; lower bracket R1 suggests early pressure to advance. SEA region is highly competitive with frequent roster changes; briefing notes daze replacing Zayac at REKONIX, which may have affected team chemistry or playstyle. No direct head-to-head matchup data between REKONIX and Execration exists in briefing to calibrate probability meaningfully. Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (resolves in ~11 hours); insufficient time for game outcome reversals, but both teams' actual competitive form may differ from historical snapshots. Resolution criteria are clear and unambiguous\u2014standard win/loss determination via DotaBuff with reasonable fallback to credible reporting. Market mispricing assessment: 60% YES is above 50%, implying REKONIX is slight favorite, but briefing shows REKONIX lost more recently to playoff-level teams than won; this suggests potential YES side overvaluation relative to visible data, but Execration data gap prevents confident contradiction.", "key_factor": "Insufficient performance data for Execration and lack of direct head-to-head history between teams makes meaningful probabilistic analysis unreliable."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "REKONIX MOMENTUM: Won 2-0 against XctN and VRJ in RES Unchained 4 SEA CQ just 10 days ago; qualified for DreamLeague playoffs indicates they cleared group stage, suggesting above-average regional strength. ROSTER CATALYST: The briefing mentions 'daze' replacing Zayac with positive commentary ('played great this series, had some very clutch saves'); this roster adjustment appears stable and functional going into playoffs. PATTERN OF INCONSISTENCY: REKONIX lost 0-2 to GLYPH (mid-tier), Team Nemesis (in DreamLeague), Tundra (0-2), and GL (0-2). They show a clear bifurcated record: beating weaker teams decisively but struggling against playoff-level opposition. EXECRATION OPACITY: Briefing provides NO performance data on Execration whatsoever\u2014no recent matches, win-loss record, roster status, or head-to-head history. This asymmetry is critical: YES is favored at 60% despite complete absence of Execration context. LOWER BRACKET DYNAMICS: REKONIX is in Lower Bracket Round 1, suggesting they lost their upper bracket match. This is their 'second chance' match\u2014motivation and pressure are elevated, but so is elimination risk. MARKET PRICING RATIONALE: 60% YES suggests market confidence in REKONIX as the slightly favored team, but the lack of Execration data means this may reflect only REKONIX's mixed track record, not a comparative advantage. TIMING VULNERABILITY: Match resolves in ~11 hours (TODAY). No time for new intelligence; market prices reflect stale April 12 data. Late roster changes or illness could favor either team with minimal advance notice. WHY YES CONFIDENCE IS CAPPED AT 62: While REKONIX has playoff qualification and recent wins, their 0-2 losses to mid-and-top-tier teams (GLYPH, Team Nemesis, Tundra, GL) show they are vulnerable to organized opponents. The underdog Execration remains unmeasured. WHY NO CONFIDENCE IS LOW AT 48: Without any Execration performance data, it is impossible to confidently argue why they should be favored. This is a data gap, not evidence of weakness. Execration could be a rising team, a veteran squad, or entirely unknown. PROBABILITY JUSTIFICATION: 58% reflects slight YES favoring (matching market near 60%) while acknowledging asymmetric information. REKONIX's playoff qualification + recent wins slightly outweigh their losses to stronger teams, but Execration's unmeasured strength prevents high confidence either direction.", "key_factor": "REKONIX's recent wins against XctN and VRJ demonstrate playoff-caliber execution, but inconsistent performance against stronger teams creates meaningful uncertainty."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.55, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "REKONIX VULNERABILITIES (favoring NO upset): REKONIX shows a clear pattern of losing decisively to playoff-caliber teams\u20140-2 losses to GLYPH, Team Nemesis, Tundra, and GL across recent tournaments. This is not close competition; these are clean sweeps. Against lower-mid-tier teams (XctN, VRJ) they win 2-0, but that gulf in performance is stark. EXECUTION INCONSISTENCY: In a HIGH-PRESSURE BO3 playoff format, inconsistency is amplified. REKONIX's ability to collapse 0-2 to GLYPH immediately after beating XctN 2-0 suggests mental fortitude or draft adaptation issues in back-to-back games\u2014critical in BO3. EXECRATION DATA GAP: The briefing provides ZERO direct performance metrics for Execration in this qualifier. No recent match results, no roster stability information, no draft patterns. This is the core reason confidence in the favorite (YES) is only moderate. If Execration is a respectable SEA team that qualified for playoffs, they likely have comparable or superior recent form to REKONIX. ROSTER CONTEXT NEUTRAL: The briefing mentions daze joining REKONIX instead of Zayac, with positive commentary on daze's performance ('clutch saves'). However, this is anecdotal and from limited sample (mentioned in context of one series vs. Team Nemesis\u2014which REKONIX still lost). Roster changes can be destabilizing in BO3s. MARKET MISPRICING SIGNAL: YES is priced at 60%, which reflects a 20-point premium over a coin flip. This premium rests on REKONIX's wins vs mid-tier teams and playoff qualification alone. However, qualification into playoffs does not equal BO3 matchup strength; both teams qualified. The briefing offers zero evidence REKONIX is stronger than Execration in a head-to-head playoff scenario. SEA REGION PARITY: The briefing explicitly notes SEA region is 'highly competitive with multiple strong teams.' This context suggests wide variance in team strength and suggests Execration, if competitive enough to reach playoffs, likely sits in the same tier as REKONIX rather than below. TIMING PRESSURE: Event is TODAY (11 hours to match). There is insufficient time for new data to shift the narrative. Market pricing reflects historical record, but REKONIX's recent form is mixed-to-poor against equivalent opposition. Execration's unknown form is *not* a weakness\u2014it's a data vacuum that could cut either way. WHY EXECRATION DESERVES 38-40%+: REKONIX has legitimate recent losses to teams that suggest Execration (another playoff qualifier) is plausibly equal or superior. The market's +20 confidence in YES lacks supporting evidence beyond REKONIX's group-stage wins. In BO3 playoffs, one team's demonstrated weakness (losing 0-2 to competitors of similar tier) is a material disadvantage. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes=55 (moderate) because REKONIX's playoff qualification and RES Unchained wins provide some objective support for YES. But confidence_no=72 (higher) because the briefing provides zero counterargument to the Execration threat\u2014no data refuting their strength. The absence of Execration data, combined with REKONIX's documented losses to playoff-tier opposition, tilts the underdog case. RESOLUTION NOTE: Market will resolve on DotaBuff within 2 hours of match conclusion. BO3 format means one team wins 2 games. Given REKONIX's 0-2 pattern against peers, Execration has a tangible upset path if their form is on par with or exceeds REKONIX's baseline.", "key_factor": "Execration's lack of documented recent performance data masks potential roster strength or meta-favorable composition that could exploit REKONIX's demonstrated inconsistency against top-tier opposition."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.52, "confidence_yes": 0.38, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: No direct head-to-head history between REKONIX and Execration is provided in the briefing. This severely limits confidence in either direction. REKONIX MIXED FORM: Recent record shows 2-0 wins vs mid-tier teams (XctN, VRJ) but 0-2 losses to stronger opposition (GLYPH, Team Nemesis, Tundra, GL). Pattern suggests inconsistency or meta/matchup sensitivity. REKONIX PLAYOFF QUALIFICATION: Successfully reached DreamLeague S29 SEA CQ Playoffs, indicating they cleared group stage. This alone is base-rate favorable but insufficient to overcome mixed playoff-level results. EXECRATION DATA ABSENT: Briefing provides zero Execration performance data, recent form, roster composition, or head-to-head record. Cannot evaluate NO side meaningfully. LOWER BRACKET CONTEXT: This is a lower bracket round 1 match, meaning both teams have already lost once. Pressure and momentum factors are unknown for both sides. MARKET PRICE ALIGNMENT: Current market prices (60% YES / 40% NO) slightly favor REKONIX but not dramatically. This suggests modest confidence in REKONIX without overwhelming evidence. BO3 FORMAT: Best-of-3 allows for some team adaptability between games; single-game upsets less likely than in BO1. REKONIX's inconsistency across opponents makes BO3 harder to predict. SEA REGION COMPETITIVENESS: Southeast Asia Dota 2 is highly competitive with multiple tier-1 caliber teams. No team should be heavily favored without strong recent data. ROSTER CHANGE NOTED: Briefing mentions daze replacing Zayac at Natus Vincere with positive commentary ('played great'), but this appears to reference a different team, not REKONIX or Execration directly. Minimal relevance. TIME-TO-RESOLUTION: Event is TODAY (~11 hours). Market has low volume ($5,837 USD) suggesting limited professional/informed trading. Pricing may reflect general sentiment rather than sharp analysis. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in REKONIX assessment (recent results are visible), but very low confidence in Execration evaluation (zero data). Confidence scores reflect this asymmetry rather than false balance.", "key_factor": "In BO3 playoff matches between evenly-matched Dota 2 regional teams, base rate is approximately 50-50, with slight variance based on recent form and head-to-head records."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.48, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "Market pricing REKONIX at 60% YES reflects mild confidence, but briefing data is asymmetrically sparse\u2014strong evidence of REKONIX's losses (0-2 to GLYPH, Team Nemesis, Tundra, GL) contrasts with wins vs weaker teams (XctN, VRJ). Critical data gap: NO DATA on Execration's recent form, strength, or head-to-head record vs REKONIX. Market cannot properly price uncertainty when one side is opaque. REKONIX pattern shows feast-famine dynamic: dominates mid-tier opponents but loses cleanly to playoff-caliber teams. Execration's tier placement is unknown\u2014cannot determine if they fall into 'weaker' or 'stronger' bracket. Briefing note on daze substitution (replacing Zayac) shows roster churn and adaptation mid-qualifier. Positive anecdotal sentiment ('he played great'), but insufficient sample to confirm durability in high-pressure BO3. Event is TODAY (~11 hours to resolution). At this stage, raw market price (60/40) reflects current consensus, but that consensus lacks Execration intelligence. Market may be underweighting unknown underdog value. 60% YES pricing suggests moderate confidence in REKONIX, not exuberant greed. However, greed/fear distinction is muted because briefing provides no emotional signals from analysts or crowd\u2014purely mechanical data. Rational apathy detected: market is pricing a team with known volatility (REKONIX) at a relatively strong 60% on what appears to be incomplete information. Neither crowd is panicking or euphoric\u2014they are simply defaulting to available data bias. Confidence scores depressed symmetrically because briefing fails to establish Execration's competitive baseline. Assigning 60/40 without that baseline is guesswork disguised as precision. Both YES and NO confidence scores warrant caution (~32-35 range).", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.45, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "REKONIX recent record shows clear tier-based performance split: 2-0 wins vs XctN/VRJ (mid-tier), 0-2 losses vs GLYPH/Tundra/GL/Team Nemesis (established teams), indicating skill ceiling vulnerability under playoff pressure. No direct head-to-head data exists between REKONIX and Execration in briefing; market price of 60% YES appears to rely on REKONIX's group-stage advancement qualification rather than matchup-specific evidence. REKONIX roster stability is unclear\u2014briefing mentions daze replacing Zayac pre-DreamLeague, suggesting recent adjustment period; new supports require calibration time in BO3 playoff formats where opponent read becomes critical. Lower bracket round 1 context: REKONIX advanced but faced Team Nemesis (stronger qualifier) in S29 SEA CQ; Execration's bracket positioning and path unknown, preventing seed-strength inference. SEA meta in April 2026 features 'new/reworked items' per briefing; REKONIX's item build consistency (visible in RES Unchained matches) may not translate to evolved meta if Execration has adapted faster. BO3 format amplifies adaptation: if Execration has recent scrim data on daze's support style, game 2-3 reads could favor the prepared opponent; REKONIX's mixed form (2-2 in last 4 qualifier matches) suggests inconsistency. Market price (60% YES) may overshoot REKONIX probability due to 'team advanced to playoffs' heuristic\u2014advancement doesn't guarantee lower-bracket victory against peers. Execration reputation in SEA largely absent from briefing; absence of negative data is NOT evidence of weakness\u2014could indicate lower media coverage rather than poor performance. Time-to-reversal risk: Event occurs in ~11 hours (TODAY), making last-minute roster changes (disqualification, forfeiture) low-probability but non-negligible for esports; tie/cancel \u2192 50-50 resolution is possible but rare.", "key_factor": "REKONIX exhibits a classic 'mid-tier crusher/top-tier vulnerability' pattern typical of rising SEA teams\u2014strong against bracket peers but exposed against established powerhouses, making this lower-bracket matchup inherently volatile despite the 60% market price."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "REKONIX's record is bifurcated: 2-0 wins vs mid-tier teams (XctN, VRJ) but 0-2 losses vs qualified/international opposition (GLYPH, Team Nemesis, Tundra, GL). This suggests they are a second-tier SEA team, not a favorite. Market currently prices YES at 60%, but briefing shows REKONIX lost to Team Nemesis in DreamLeague S29 CQ\u2014a team also in this playoff bracket. This prior loss is a direct playoff-level indicator favoring NO. Daze substitution for Zayac is a MAJOR roster change noted in briefing as controversial ('skeptical when they announced daze'). While daze 'played great' in one series, one strong series does not guarantee BO3 consistency under playoff pressure vs a team that may have scouted the new lineup. Briefing explicitly states 'Limited direct head-to-head data is available between REKONIX and Execration specifically'\u2014this asymmetric information gap means market confidence in YES is likely overblown. We have NO strength data on Execration. Briefing notes 'new patch was the introduction of several new and reworked items'\u2014meta shifts favor teams with adaptive draft pools. REKONIX's recent losses to top teams suggest they may lag in meta adaptation vs hungrier underdog opponents like Execration. Lower bracket Round 1: both teams are already in playoffs, but REKONIX's prior loss to Team Nemesis indicates they may be lower seeded. Execration's seed/prior result is unknown\u2014if they beat a stronger team to reach this round, they have momentum. BO3 format amplifies variance: if REKONIX loses Game 1 (high likelihood given their inconsistency), psychological pressure + Zayac/daze chemistry uncertainty in Games 2-3 could compound the deficit. Market price 60/40 YES/NO is only moderately favoring REKONIX. Given the briefing's emphasis on REKONIX's losses to qualified teams and the daze substitution risk, this price likely reflects minimal edge for REKONIX and significant underpricing of Execration's upset potential.", "key_factor": "Execration exploits a recent meta shift or patch-favored hero pool that REKONIX's roster\u2014particularly with the daze substitution for Zayac\u2014has not practiced extensively enough to counter in a high-pressure BO3 playoff setting."}], "final_score": 0.47728187919463083, "no_score": 0.5415527950310559, "edge": -0.11771812080536914, "no_edge": 0.13655279503105588, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Contrarian call: council prob 54% < 70% threshold; Contrarian call: NO-side confidence 46% < 80% threshold", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1957254", "question": "Dota 2: REKONIX vs Execration (BO3) - DreamLeague Southeast Asia Closed Qualifier Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Dota 2 Lower bracket round 1 match between REKONIX and Execration in the DreamLeague Southeast Asia Closed Qualifier Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 13 at 12:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"REKONIX\" if REKONIX win the match against Execration.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Execration\" if Execration win the match against REKONIX.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://www.dotabuff.com. However, if https://www.dotabuff.com has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather th