|\n| 2025 |  Season 25  Season 26  Season 27 |\n| 2026 |  Season 28  Season 29 |", "Participants ; Team Yandex \u00b7 1st \u00b7 Kazakhstan watson \u00b7 Russia ; Team Spirit \u00b7 2nd \u00b7 Ukraine Yatoro \u00b7 Russia ; PARIVISION \u00b7 3rd \u00b7 Russia Satanic \u00b7 Ukraine", "View the complete Dota 2 profile for \u0445\u0435\u0445) on Dotabuff.", "View the complete Dota 2 profile for ALOHADANCE on Dotabuff.", "The biggest change in the new patch was the introduction of several new and reworked items into the game."], "news_summary": "REKONIX and Execration are competing in the DreamLeague Season 29 Southeast Asia Closed Qualifier Playoffs (BO3 format). Based on available match data, REKONIX has shown mixed recent performance, losing 0-2 to GLYPH in RES Unchained 4 SEA CQ qualifiers while winning against XctN and VRJ. Team Nemesis defeated REKONIX in at least one recorded DreamLeague S29 SEA CQ matchup. Limited direct head-to-head data is available between REKONIX and Execration specifically.", "side_yes_case": ["REKONIX won 2-0 against XctN and VRJ in recent RES Unchained 4 SEA CQ matches, demonstrating competitive capability", "REKONIX has qualified for DreamLeague playoffs, indicating sufficient team strength to advance past group stages", "Recent roster/meta shifts in SEA region may favor REKONIX's current composition"], "side_no_case": ["REKONIX lost 0-2 to GLYPH in RES Unchained 4 SEA CQ, showing inconsistent performance against qualified opposition", "REKONIX lost to Team Nemesis in DreamLeague S29 SEA CQ, indicating vulnerability in playoff-level competition", "REKONIX also lost 0-2 to both Tundra and GL at ESL One Birmingham, suggesting struggles against stronger international teams"], "key_context": ["DreamLeague Season 29 SEA Closed Qualifier Playoffs - BO3 format determines advancement", "REKONIX shows pattern of stronger performance against mid-tier teams but weaker results against top-tier opposition", "Limited publicly available data on Execration's recent performance in these qualifiers", "Match timing April 2026, during active competitive Dota 2 season with frequent roster changes", "SEA region is highly competitive with multiple strong teams; playoff pressure differs from group stage"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-12T22:42:18.455709Z", "price_history": null}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-13T10:10:00Z", "winning_side": "YES", "final_yes_price": 1.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-13T18:33:22.486402+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "358b3307-fca0-42b1-a6a3-595c99668116", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T00:31:09.879567+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1935490", "question": "Counter-Strike: Vasco Esports vs ALKA (BO3) - CCT South America Challengers #1 Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Upper bracket round 1 match between Vasco Esports and ALKA in the CCT South America Challengers #1 Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 12 at 7:45PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Vasco Esports\" if Vasco Esports win the match against ALKA.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"ALKA\" if ALKA win the match against Vasco Esports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-13T05:45:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-12T23:45:00Z", "yes_price": 0.7, "volume_usd": 1198.9512939999997, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["45456157639330080416851379966305032643009230656164803033000944926823766017722", "104587518505070310744169761509034924290540321996670547585641076408554587318515"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: Match must complete with Vasco Esports winning the BO3 against ALKA. Criteria are clear and unambiguous regarding resolution (straight win resolves to winner; forfeit/no-play resolves 50-50). DATA GAP \u2014 FUNDAMENTAL ANALYSIS: Briefing contains zero team rosters, recent form, head-to-head records, or regional ranking data for either Vasco Esports or ALKA. Both teams compete in C-Tier/Valve Tier 2 South American online tournament with minimal international coverage. MARKET SIGNAL STRENGTH: YES side has risen +25.5pp in last 24 hours and +12.0pp over 7 days, now trading at 70% (current market price). This sharp upward movement (+21.5pp spike on Apr 12 02:00 UTC) suggests informed trading activity or late-breaking intelligence about Vasco's competitive position or ALKA's roster/form issues. TIMING AND VOLATILITY: Event is TODAY (resolves in ~5 hours). Sharp price moves (-13.5pp, +21.5pp, -8.0pp on Apr 12) within hours of match suggest real-time information was being priced in. NO side dropped -37.5pp in 24 hours, indicating directional conviction toward Vasco. VOLUME AND LIQUIDITY: Low volume ($1,199 USD) limits confidence that market price reflects deep analytical consensus. However, in small esports markets, even modest volume can represent informed regional players with direct knowledge of South American scene. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes=45 and confidence_no=42 reflect equivalent data poverty on both sides. Market price action (70% YES) is the primary signal available, but insufficient fundamental data prevents high confidence in either direction. A true 50-50 coin flip would be justified if not for recent market momentum. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: Probability_score of 68 weights market-implied 70% slightly downward (2-point haircut) to account for low volume and data opacity, but respects the directional conviction shown by recent sharp moves. This reflects: 'market is favoring Vasco, but confidence in that signal is modest due to lack of fundamental context.' RESOLUTION MECHANISM: HLTV.org is primary source; fallback to consensus reporting if delayed. No red flags for ambiguous team name matching (Vasco/ALKA are distinct and unambiguous). Match completion risk (forfeit/cancellation) is real but appears low given tournament is live and proceeding on schedule.", "key_factor": "No team-specific performance data, roster composition, or head-to-head history available in briefing; probability heavily reliant on market price action rather than fundamental competitive analysis."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE MOMENTUM: YES has surged +25.5pp in the last 24 hours and +12.0pp over 7 days, indicating strong directional conviction from traders with potential insider or team knowledge. SHARP MONEY SIGNAL: The sharp upward move (+21.5pp at Apr 12 02:00 UTC) followed by subsequent volatility suggests informed bettors with regional South American connections backing Vasco, likely overcoming initial uncertainty. CURRENT PRICE REFLECTS CONSENSUS: 70% YES pricing is now 11pp higher than 7-day EMA (59%), indicating the market has recently updated in Vasco's favor\u2014this adjustment is typically information-driven rather than noise. BO3 FORMAT STABILIZES FAVORITES: Best-of-three reduces single-map variance; if Vasco is favored by informed bettors, the multi-map format actually reinforces their advantage by reducing upset probability. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS: NO side has collapsed -37.5pp in 24 hours and -24.0pp over 7 days\u2014this is not consolidation but capitulation, suggesting ALKA's perceived weakness has become clearer to market participants. LIMITED PUBLIC DATA CUTS BOTH WAYS: While the briefing lacks head-to-head history and HLTV rankings, this opacity actually supports the YES premium\u2014regional bettors (likely South American, with direct access) are buying Vasco at 70%, implying they possess local knowledge traders without such access cannot exploit. TIMING URGENCY: Match resolves in ~5 hours (IMMINENT). The large 24-hour moves indicate the market was repricing based on recent information (roster changes, scrim results, injury reports) that the public briefing has not captured. VOLATILITY ASYMMETRY: YES volatility (5.4pp/hr) is slightly lower than NO (5.5pp/hr) despite higher price and larger moves, suggesting YES accumulation by confident holders rather than panic buying. MARKET EFFICIENCY TEST: At 70%, YES is not extreme (not 85%+), indicating realistic uncertainty persists. The price reflects that despite Vasco backing, this remains a competitive South American matchup where ALKA retains ~30% realistic upset potential. UNDERDOG COUNTERPOINT: ALKA's 30% price is NOT negligible; in a BO3, a Tier 2 underdog with regional pedigree can exploit map veto, tactical adaptation, or momentum swings. The market has NOT discounted ALKA entirely, which is prudent given data scarcity. DATA GAP RISK: Confidence is moderate (42/38) because no team form, roster, or head-to-head evidence is presented. The 70% price is driven by trader behavior, not public fundamentals. A sudden withdrawal or roster announcement could swing the market sharply. VERDICT: Vasco Esports is favored by informed regional backing evidenced in price action, but the case is informational opacity rather than demonstrable dominance. Probability_score of 68 reflects the market's recent +25.5pp repricing while acknowledging the significant data limitations that prevent higher confidence.", "key_factor": "Market conviction (YES up +25.5pp in 24h) reflects private information or betting syndicate knowledge unavailable in public briefing, suggesting informed backing of Vasco despite data scarcity."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.35, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing explicitly states 'No HLTV rankings, recent results, or roster composition data available for either Vasco Esports or ALKA.' This is a C-Tier South American online tournament with minimal international coverage, making any probability assessment highly speculative. MARKET VOLATILITY INDICATES INFORMATION VACUUM: YES prices surged +25.5pp in 24 hours (from ~44% to 70%) with extreme hourly swings (-13.5pp, +21.5pp, -8.0pp). This pattern suggests reactive trading driven by fragmentary information or hype rather than informed analysis of team quality. UNDERDOG PRICING WEAKNESS: NO (ALKA) has fallen -37.5pp in 24 hours and -24pp over 7 days despite identical data availability for both teams. The market appears to be backing a favorite narrative without evidence, which is precisely where underdogs are mispriced. BO3 FORMAT FAVORS UNCERTAINTY: Best-of-three matches are inherently less predictable than single maps. With zero comparative data on either team's recent form, map pool consistency, or head-to-head history, BO3 outcomes in low-tier regional tournaments are near-random. VASCO SUPERIORITY UNSUBSTANTIATED: The briefing provides ZERO evidence that Vasco Esports is the stronger team. The 70% YES pricing appears to be anchored on team name recognition, sponsorship profile, or market momentum rather than competitive merit. SOUTH AMERICAN SCENE PARITY: Regional tournaments in smaller scenes (South American CS2) typically feature tighter skill distributions among competitors. Dominant favorites are rarer in C-Tier regional challengers than in international events. TIMING & EXECUTION RISK: Match was scheduled for April 11-12 ET, now resolving TODAY (April 13, 05:45 UTC). The event timing is LIVE/IMMINENT. Sharp price moves in the final hours (Apr 13 00:30 UTC: -12.0pp on NO) suggest late-breaking information (roster changes, health issues, connection problems, or insider knowledge), but this data is NOT reflected in the briefing\u2014ALKA may have received negative information driving sharp selloff. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: confidence_yes=25 and confidence_no=28 because BOTH sides suffer equally from data poverty. However, the 70% YES pricing suggests the market has information we lack. That confidence floor applies to both directions. CONTRARIAN POSITIONING: Market is heavily favored toward Vasco (70%) despite zero published evidence. Underdog value exists at 30% pricing IF the teams are genuinely closer than the spread suggests\u2014and absence of data in a low-tier tournament is consistent with them being similarly skilled. REALISTIC UPSET SCENARIO: ALKA could win via: (1) superior map preparation on the three BO3 maps, (2) Vasco's roster having recent turnover/focus issues not yet public, (3) ALKA having regional anti-meta adapted to South American meta, or (4) execution variance in a tight matchup. None of these can be ruled out given zero competitive baseline. PROBABILITY RATIONALE: At 35% for ALKA, this reflects genuine epistemic humility: the market's 70% Vasco conviction *may* be justified by private information or regional scouting, but the briefing provides ZERO supportive evidence. Absent evidence, 30% pricing for the underdog in a BO3 regional tournament is undervalued.", "key_factor": "ALKA's underdog status combined with severe data asymmetry and volatile market behavior suggesting uninformed pricing rather than genuine Vasco Esports superiority."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: No team rosters, head-to-head history, recent form, HLTV rankings, or win rates available for Vasco Esports or ALKA in briefing. MARKET PRICE SIGNAL (YES 70% \u2192 62%): YES side has risen sharply (+25.5pp in 24h, +12pp in 7d) with high volatility (5.4pp/hr), including a +21.5pp jump Apr 12 02:00 UTC. This pattern suggests late-breaking information (possible roster changes, player availability, scrim results, or insider speculation) rather than fundamental team strength. TIMING RISK: Event resolves in ~5 hours (TODAY). Sharp recent reversals (\u221213.5pp \u2192 +21.5pp \u2192 \u22128.0pp on Apr 12) indicate market uncertainty or rapid information updates. Once match is LIVE, shares will trade toward $0.01/$0.99 as outcome becomes clear. TOURNAMENT TIER RATIONALE: C-Tier/Valve Tier 2 South American online events have limited scouting, inconsistent participation, and lower competitive depth than international events. Historical base rates for such tournaments approach 50/50 due to parity and unpredictability. ASYMMETRIC CONFIDENCE: YES confidence (35) and NO confidence (32) are both LOW because briefing provides no factual data on team strength, roster, recent performance, or head-to-head matchups. Cannot justify high confidence in either direction. MARKET VOLATILITY INTERPRETATION: The 24h swing of \u00b137.5pp on NO side and \u00b125.5pp on YES side, combined with near-50% base-rate expectation, suggests either: (a) late-breaking roster/availability news favoring one team, or (b) speculation/thin liquidity ($1.2k volume). Treated YES 70% as likely overweighting this signal. PROBABILITY ADJUSTMENT: Starting from ~50% base rate for regional C-Tier parity, apply modest upward adjustment (+12pp) to YES for late-market momentum, but heavily discount confidence due to information vacuum. Result: 62% YES, acknowledging both the price signal and the high uncertainty. BO3 FORMAT STABILIZER: Best-of-three reduces single-map variance, slightly favoring more consistent/experienced teams. No data on which team (if either) qualifies as 'more consistent' in this context.", "key_factor": "In lower-tier regional CS2 tournaments (C-Tier/Valve Tier 2), outcomes are highly volatile and unpredictable due to limited public data, inconsistent roster stability, and sparse historical precedent. Base rate for any given team in such events: ~50% \u00b1 variance proportional to information asymmetry."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.27, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains ZERO substantive intelligence on either Vasco Esports or ALKA \u2014 no head-to-head history, recent form, roster composition, or regional rankings provided. Market price at 70% YES reflects strong conviction in Vasco despite informational vacuum \u2014 this is sentiment-driven, not evidence-driven. Sharp 24-hour volatility (+25.5pp on YES in 24h, then -8.0pp) and large intra-day swings (-13.5pp, +21.5pp) suggest reactive trading to untracked information (likely social signals, Discord chatter, or regional betting forums not captured in briefing). Low volume ($1,199 USD) in low-tier regional match indicates small, potentially illiquid market dominated by informed local bettors or arbitrage bots \u2014 crowd sentiment may not reflect true competitive balance. Briefing explicitly states 'limited international coverage' and 'unpredictable matchups' for C-Tier Valve Tier 2 \u2014 70% confidence in either team is overconfident given information asymmetry. EVENT TIMING (TODAY, ~5 hours to resolution): rapid share price moves in final hours suggest late information arrived (roster changes, injury, scrim results, betting syndicates), but this intel is NOT documented in briefing. BO3 format REDUCES variance v