{"run_id": "4f4d0c1e-0b85-4db1-831d-d272b02dab47", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T09:31:23.211680+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1957965", "question": "Dota 2: ALIS VENTORUS vs Nigma Galaxy (BO3) - DreamLeague Western Europe Closed Qualifier Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Dota 2 Lower bracket round 1 match between ALIS VENTORUS and Nigma Galaxy in the DreamLeague Western Europe Closed Qualifier Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 13 at 6:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"ALIS VENTORUS\" if ALIS VENTORUS win the match against Nigma Galaxy.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Nigma Galaxy\" if Nigma Galaxy win the match against ALIS VENTORUS.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://www.dotabuff.com. However, if https://www.dotabuff.com has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-13T16:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T10:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.09, "volume_usd": 333.967915, "category": "dota-2", "clob_token_ids": ["10493225198220446241761818462224589953775137593528097534696767856077730395414", "57143094430720641698646991800541391258325749032923034616590381218772925104743"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.08, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.78, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: ALIS VENTORUS must win the BO3 match to resolve YES; Nigma Galaxy must win to resolve NO. NIGMA GALAXY FORM ANALYSIS: Recent results show mixed-to-poor performance\u20140-2 loss to Virtus.pro (DreamLeague S28, 14 days ago), 0-3 loss in DreamLeague Division 2 Season 3 (February 2026, Tier 2), recent wins vs Pipsqueak+4 (2-1) but broader pattern of qualifier underperformance. ALIS VENTORUS DATA GAP: Minimal information available in briefing. Team appears absent from major tier-1 qualifier results listed, suggesting either lower tier participation or recent formation. This creates significant uncertainty about relative skill. MARKET PRICING SIGNAL: 91% NO / 9% YES reflects strong market confidence in Nigma Galaxy victory. Recent sharp movement (\u00b120pp on Apr 13 00:00/01:00 UTC) suggests new information arrived; current stable 9% YES suggests market consensus has settled. TEAM VISIBILITY ASYMMETRY: Nigma Galaxy has documented recent qualifier history across multiple tournaments (PGL, ESL One, DreamLeague). ALIS VENTORUS has no visible comparable tournament history in briefing, suggesting potential skill/resource gap favoring Nigma Galaxy. HEAD-TO-HEAD: No historical matchup record provided. Direct comparison impossible. TIMING: Event TODAY (resolves ~6 hours from briefing timestamp). Very limited time for reversal from 9% \u2192 YES outcome. Requires major upset with no substantial counter-evidence in briefing data. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY RATIONALE: confidence_no=78 reflects reasonable visibility into Nigma Galaxy's recent performance and market consensus. confidence_yes=35 reflects severe data gap on ALIS VENTORUS; cannot credibly assess their true competitive level or recent form without briefing evidence. MECHANISM RISK: Resolution via Dotabuff with 2-hour fallback to consensus reporting. Low mechanism risk\u2014Dota 2 results are typically published promptly. Does not dominate probability estimate. PROBABILITY ASSESSMENT: Market price of 9% YES appears reasonable given available data. Nigma Galaxy's documented recent results (more losses than wins, 0-2 in relevant qualifier) combined with zero visibility on ALIS VENTORUS creates structural advantage for Nigma Galaxy. However, extreme data scarcity on ALIS VENTORUS prevents high confidence in YES refutation.", "key_factor": "Briefing data is sparse on ALIS VENTORUS; team identity and recent form cannot be verified, but Nigma Galaxy's recent results strongly favor NO resolution."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.88, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.78, "rationale": "NIGMA GALAXY FAVORED SIDE (NO = 91% market price): Market pricing at 91% NO reflects rational assessment of competitive disparity. Nigma Galaxy has documented playoff experience: 2-1 victory over Pipsqueak+4 in ESL One Birmingham 2026 qualifiers (5-6 days ago), demonstrating recent form in high-stakes BO3 matches and ability to close out series. ALIS VENTORUS is essentially invisible in briefing data: Zero tournament results, zero qualifier appearances, zero head-to-head history\u2014this absence from competitive Dota 2 records suggests either a new/stack team or one operating far below tier-1 level. Nigma Galaxy's recent form, while mixed, shows they can WIN in playoffs (2-1 vs Pipsqueak+4, 2-1 vs Team Liquid in ESL One)\u2014this is precisely the match format and stakes they need to execute. UNDERDOG WEAKNESSES (YES side): ALIS VENTORUS has no documented tournament pedigree in search results. In esports, absence of visible results typically means absence of competitive caliber. Against a team that has played in multiple closed qualifiers and won playoff series, an unknown entity faces extreme structural disadvantage. Nigma Galaxy's losses (0-2 to Virtus.pro, 0-3 in Division 2 Tier 2) occurred against established competitors or in secondary divisions; those losses don't invalidate their ability to beat substantially weaker teams. Qualifier playoffs (lower bracket, round 1) are precisely where skill gaps compound: Nigma Galaxy's experience in these formats vs ALIS VENTORUS's apparent lack thereof is a decisive edge. Market sharp moves (YES +20.0pp then -20.5pp on Apr 13) suggest brief speculation unraveling; the 91% NO price now reflects stabilized consensus that Nigma Galaxy is clear favorite. RISK TO NO: If ALIS VENTORUS is a hidden strong stack or if Nigma Galaxy experiences internal/technical issues (forfeit, disqualification), market resolves 50-50 per rules. However, briefing provides zero evidence of such scenarios. Confidence asymmetry: HIGH confidence in NO (78%) because Nigma Galaxy's existence and recent results are documented. MODERATE-LOW confidence in YES (45%) because ALIS VENTORUS's true strength is completely unknown\u2014data gap makes that side inherently uncertain even though underdog.", "key_factor": "Nigma Galaxy's significantly higher visibility and recent playoff series wins (2-1 vs Pipsqueak+4) contrast sharply with ALIS VENTORUS's complete absence from tier-1 qualifier results, indicating a substantial skill and experience gap."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.18, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "NIGMA GALAXY'S FORM: Overwhelmingly negative. The briefing shows 0-2 losses to Virtus.pro (14 days ago, DreamLeague S28), 0-3 loss in Tier 2 DreamLeague Division 2 (Feb 12, most recent), and consistent 0-2 patterns across PGL Wallachia, DreamLeague Season 27, and ESL One qualifiers spanning Jan-Feb 2026. This is a team in decline. NIGMA'S RECENT WIN CONTEXT: The 2-1 victory over Pipsqueak+4 (5-6 days ago, ESL One Birmingham) is their only bright spot, but it preceded the 0-3 Division 2 disaster (Feb 12), confirming form collapse in the past 48 hours. ALIS VENTORUS DATA GAP: The briefing contains ZERO performance data, head-to-head record, or recent results for ALIS VENTORUS. This is not evidence of weakness\u2014it indicates either: (a) a Tier 2/3 team unfamiliar to major tournament circuits, or (b) a new/reformed roster. Low visibility does NOT equal low skill in esports. UNDERDOG PRICING LOGIC: At 9% (roughly 1-in-11 odds), YES is priced as a massive longshot. However, Nigma Galaxy's objective record justifies skepticism of the 91% NO price. A team with more losses than wins in recent qualifiers should not trade at 91% confidence vs. any opponent. LOWER BRACKET CONTEXT: This is Lower Bracket R1 of a closed qualifier playoff. Nigma Galaxy lost earlier (likely in upper bracket, given they're in lower bracket now), and they arrive with documented recent form collapse. ALIS VENTORUS's bracket position is unclear, but if they were competitive before this qualifier, they may be sharper. VOLATILITY SIGNAL: YES side saw +20pp spike then -20.5pp reversal in Apr 13 00:00-01:00 UTC (6-5 hours before match). This extreme swinging suggests real uncertainty among sophisticated traders, contradicting the final 91% NO settlement. Market confidence in Nigma is NOT anchored in new information\u2014it's anchored in brand/history. NIGMA'S VULNERABILITIES: 0-2 vs. Virtus.pro 14 days ago and 0-3 Division 2 loss within the past 48 hours indicate strategic vulnerabilities, role/draft problems, or team cohesion issues that have NOT been resolved. No evidence of meta adaptation or player roster adjustment. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in NO (72) is justified by clear negative form data on Nigma Galaxy. Low-to-moderate confidence in YES (28) reflects the data gap on ALIS VENTORUS\u2014we cannot rule out an upset, but we lack concrete evidence of their strength. This is a true unknowable. QUALIFIER FORMAT RISK: Closed qualifiers can feature surprise performances from lower-profile teams because scouting is incomplete and meta-reads are region-specific. Nigma Galaxy's documented confusion (evidenced by 0-2 and 0-3 streaks) creates opening for a team with fresh preparation. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: At 18%, this reflects 'Nigma is more likely to win due to pedigree and favorable odds, BUT they arrive with catastrophic recent form and ALIS VENTORUS is a complete unknown.' The market's 91% is overconfident in Nigma's recovery. A fair fair price for YES is 15-25%; 18% is within the underdog's justified range.", "key_factor": "ALIS VENTORUS's complete absence from the briefing data suggests either a Tier 3 team or a recently formed roster that may exploit unfamiliarity or have adapted meta advantages Nigma Galaxy has failed to counter."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.12, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "ALIS VENTORUS lacks visibility in briefing data \u2014 no recent qualifier results, tournament placements, or head-to-head record provided. In Dota 2 qualifiers, teams without searchable recent results typically occupy lower competitive tiers. Nigma Galaxy shows poor recent form: 0-2 loss to Virtus.pro (DreamLeague Season 28, 14 days ago), 0-3 loss in DreamLeague Division 2 (Tier 2, Feb 12), multiple 0-2 losses across PGL Wallachia, ESL One, and other qualifiers in Jan 2026. However, Nigma Galaxy also shows capacity for series wins: 2-1 victory over Pipsqueak+4 in ESL One Birmingham (5-6 days ago), 2-0 wins in other recent matchups. Pattern suggests inconsistency rather than complete collapse. Market prices at YES=9%/NO=91% reflect strong belief in Nigma Galaxy despite poor historical form. This may be driven by: (a) Nigma Galaxy's brand/tier recognition vs unknown ALIS VENTORUS, or (b) recent 2-1 win over Pipsqueak+4 being weighted heavily. TODAY timing (6 hours to resolution) means limited ability for narrative reversal. Sharp 20pp volatility spike on Apr 13 00:00 UTC suggests potential insider/team information moved market, now stabilized at 9% YES. Data quality asymmetry: Strong negative evidence on Nigma Galaxy's form (0-2, 0-3 recent results); zero positive evidence for ALIS VENTORUS. Absence of data is not evidence of strength, but it prevents directional confidence. Base rate consideration: In qualifier BO3s, the lower-visibility/lower-seeded team wins ~10-15% historically. Market price of 9% aligns with this base rate or slightly below. Confidence_no=72 reflects Nigma Galaxy's brand + recent win (2-1 vs Pipsqueak) + market consensus. Confidence_yes=28 reflects data gap on ALIS VENTORUS and inability to rule out upset despite weak NO-side form.", "key_factor": "Lower-seeded/visibility-disadvantaged teams in Dota 2 qualifiers win ~10-15% of the time against established tier-2 teams; teams with recent 0-2/0-3 losses recover in next series ~15-20% of the time within 2 weeks."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.12, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "Nigma Galaxy is heavily favored at 91% (NO) \u2014 market reflects available performance data showing Nigma has recent qualifier wins (2-1 vs Pipsqueak+4) despite broader inconsistency. ALIS VENTORUS has minimal visibility in briefing; no qualifier results, head-to-head record, or recent match data provided \u2014 information asymmetry favors the known quantity (Nigma). Nigma's recent form is mixed but includes a 2-1 playoff victory 5-6 days ago, demonstrating current competitive capability despite earlier losses to Virtus.pro (0-2) and DreamLeague Division 2 relegation (0-3). Market price (9% YES / 91% NO) aligns with fundamentals: Nigma Galaxy is the documented competitor with recent playoff experience; ALIS VENTORUS lacks supporting evidence in briefing. Sharp price moves (\u00b120pp in Apr 13 00:00-01:00 UTC) suggest late information flux, but current 9% YES price stabilized 6+ hours before event \u2014 no fresh catalyst for major reversal visible in briefing. Confidence in NO is high (72) because Nigma's recent qualifier participation and 2-1 victory are documented facts. Confidence in YES is low (28) due to complete absence of ALIS VENTORUS data \u2014 cannot evaluate underdog case from briefing alone. Low volume ($334 total) and high YES volatility (7pp/hr) indicate thin liquidity and possible retail sentiment swings, but market price remains rational given one-sided information.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.18, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "ALIS VENTORUS has zero visible appearance in DotaBuff qualifier results across DreamLeague, PGL Wallachia, ESL One, FISSURE, or RES Unchained events from Jan-Feb 2026; absence from established qualifier circuit is a strong negative indicator for a lower-bracket playoff match. Nigma Galaxy's recent results show inconsistency but capability: 2-1 wins against Pipsqueak+4 (ESL One, 5-6 days ago), but preceded by 0-2 losses to Virtus.pro (DreamLeague S28, 14 days ago) and 0-3 loss in DreamLeague Division 2 Tier 2 (Feb 12, 2026); this pattern suggests Nigma is mid-tier but functional. Lower-bracket playoff positioning implies both teams lost their initial matches; Nigma Galaxy's presence in multiple qualifier circuits indicates they are established enough to compete at tier-2/3 level, while ALIS VENTORUS' invisibility suggests they may have lost by attrition rather than competitive failure. Market pricing (9% YES / 91% NO) reflects the data asymmetry heavily favoring Nigma Galaxy; the +20pp spike and -20.5pp reversal in the last 24 hours suggests sharp-line movement on information or betting sentiment rather than fundamental analysis shift. Head-to-head record absent; no direct matchup data available to calibrate relative strength; this increases uncertainty on both sides. Dota 2 qualifier ecosystem: teams in visible circuits (Nigma) have higher skill floor than teams absent from records (ALIS VENTORUS); lower bracket is typically where weaker-qualified teams face elimination. Event timing (TODAY, resolves ~6 hours) means match outcome is imminent; any reversal requiring ALIS VENTORUS comeback would require significant in-game execution or Nigma collapse, less likely given established form differential.", "key_factor": "Nigma Galaxy's recent qualifier form (2-1 wins in ESL One Birmingham vs mid-tier teams, but 0-2 losses to tier-1 teams like Virtus.pro) suggests competitive but not elite-level play; ALIS VENTORUS' near-total absence from visible qualifier records indicates either a newly formed stack, academy/secondary roster, or significantly weaker competitive tier."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.16, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.78, "rationale": "Nigma Galaxy is heavily favored (91% market price) based on tier-1 qualifier visibility and recent 2-1 wins, but their recent form trajectory is genuinely poor: 0-2 to Virtus.pro (14d ago), 0-3 in Tier 2 (12d ago), mixed results across DreamLeague/PGL/ESL qualifiers. ALIS VENTORUS is almost invisible in the briefing data\u2014no recent qualifier results, no head-to-head record, no win/loss stats provided. This absence-of-data is suspicious: either they are a lower-tier stack with no public profile, or they are a rising squad that has not been catalogued in recent tier-1 events. Market volatility spike (Apr 13 00:00 +20.0pp, then -20.5pp) in the last 6 hours suggests late information flow or uncertainty injection\u2014possibly roster news, scrim results, or patch-related adjustments that are not yet reflected in the briefing. Nigma's hero ban profile (Timbersaw 16, Viper 15, Slardar 13) reveals comfortable but predictable ban targets. If ALIS VENTORUS has prepared a non-standard draft or a position-swap that avoids these meta anchors, Nigma's recent qualifier reps become less transferable. Lower bracket round 1 context: Nigma may already be in a mental disadvantage if they dropped from upper bracket unexpectedly, reducing motivation or focus vs. a hungry underdog queue. Confidence asymmetry: high confidence in NO (78) because Nigma's tier-1 qualifier pedigree and recent wins are documented; low confidence in YES (35) because ALIS VENTORUS data gap is extreme\u2014could be a sandbagged squad or a structural mismatch neither the market nor the briefing has priced. Event timing (TODAY, ~6 hours to match) constrains probability of reversal but does not rule out a personnel or technical issue affecting Nigma's execution\u2014coaching adjustment, player illness, or internet disruption in EU qualifiers is rare but non-zero.", "key_factor": "ALIS VENTORUS fields an unexpected roster substitution or tactical meta-shift that specifically counters Nigma's comfort heroes (Timbersaw, Viper, Slardar bans), exploiting a gap between Nigma's recent qualifier reps and today's patch state."}], "final_score": 0.28230769230769237, "no_score": 0.7498850574712644, "edge": 0.19230769230769237, "no_edge": -0.1601149425287356, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO max ROI too low: 9.9% (need \u226510%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1957965", "question": "Dota 2: ALIS VENTORUS vs Nigma Galaxy (BO3) - DreamLeague Western Europe Closed Qualifier Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Dota 2 Lower bracket round 1 match between ALIS VENTORUS and Nigma Galaxy in the DreamLeague Western