data\u2014cannot extract win conditions, team playstyles, or mechanical skill gaps. Event timing is TODAY with ~5-hour window; any reversal from current 38% YES probability would require dramatic underdog performance with minimal time for corrections\u2014shares will consolidate near $0.01/$0.99 post-match resolution regardless of current pricing inefficiency. Confidence asymmetry: confidence_yes (35) and confidence_no (32) both low because briefing provides match structure and roster names but zero direct predictive signals (recent W-L, head-to-head, form trajectory, or expert consensus opinion).", "key_factor": "LCK academy/challenger rosters are fundamentally different competitive entities from main LCK teams; organizational affiliation does not reliably predict secondary-tier performance, and sparse match history in emerging 2026 split severely limits predictive confidence on both sides."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.32, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "MARKET MOVEMENT RED FLAG: YES crashed 34.5pp in 24 hours with a -36.5pp sharp move at 10:01 UTC today (4 hours before match start). This is not gradual drift\u2014it is panic selling or inside information about a team/roster problem. BRIEFING SILENCE ON ROSTERS: The document provides extensive draft and stats data for Nongshim Challengers vs T1 Academy and FEARX Youth, but ZERO roster/player names, substitution history, or recent lineup confirmations for TODAY's match vs Hanwha. This absence during a LIVE event is suspicious. ACADEMY LEAGUE VOLATILITY: LCK CL 2026 Split 2 is inaugural with all-ten-org rosters. Academy teams rotate personnel, promote/demote on short notice, and have weaker bench depth than main league. A surprise sub in a BO3 is far more likely here than in LCK main. HANWHA'S MAIN ROSTER STRENGTH MISMATCH: Briefing notes Hanwha main roster went 3-1 in Rounds 1-2, yet their Challengers team has NO visible match record in search results. This asymmetry suggests either (a) the Challengers roster is stronger than expected and under-scouted, or (b) recent lineup changes have occurred that briefing does not capture. TIMING & VOLATILITY PATTERN: Sharp +36pp move for NO at 10:00 UTC followed by match start in ~5 hours implies real-time intel or scheduled roster announcement. Academy league rosters are sometimes finalized or changed on match day. BO3 ADAPTATION PENALTY: A forced substitution in game 1 of a BO3 is catastrophic\u2014Nongshim would have no time to practice a new composition with the stand-in. Hanwha (if healthy) gains adaptation advantage. DATA ASYMMETRY: Briefing shows NO confidence-building match records for Hanwha Challengers specifically, yet market is now favoring them 59%. This suggests traders have external intel (roster confirmations, scrims, or known roster issues with Nongshim) not reflected in the document. CONTRARIAN POSITION: If every other analyst assumes Nongshim is favored due to documented recent matches, they miss that those matches may have featured a healthier/different roster than today. The market's late swing suggests a known availability problem has surfaced for Nongshim.", "key_factor": "Nongshim Esports Academy suffers a critical roster availability issue (key player illness, family emergency, or last-minute substitution) immediately before or during the BO3, forcing reliance on an untested stand-in mid or jungle."}], "final_score": 0.4003738317757009, "no_score": 0.5749049429657795, "edge": -0.00962616822429907, "no_edge": -0.015095057034220538, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 38% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1935072", "question": "LoL: Nongshim Esports Academy vs Hanwha Life Esports Challengers (BO3) - LCK Challengers League Rounds 1-2", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Nongshim Esports Academy and Hanwha Life Espor