{"run_id": "004e8866-7a68-490c-9f27-ab331835527a", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T10:02:41.035116+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1962110", "question": "Dota 2: Vici Gaming vs Team Resilience (BO3) - DreamLeague China Closed Qualifier Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Dota 2 Upper bracket final match between Vici Gaming and Team Resilience in the DreamLeague China Closed Qualifier Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 13 at 8:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Vici Gaming\" if Vici Gaming win the match against Team Resilience.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Resilience\" if Team Resilience win the match against Vici Gaming.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://www.dotabuff.com. However, if https://www.dotabuff.com has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-13T18:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T12:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.745, "volume_usd": 2274.682413, "category": "dota-2", "clob_token_ids": ["58096344416322589261800759171394543645007738216712090661007350347617836515513", "2471990590002154751109319861209802520220170571207732988520080453331807069600"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.74, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: YES resolves if Vici Gaming defeats Team Resilience in the BO3 Upper bracket final; NO resolves if Team Resilience wins. The criteria are clear and unambiguous. CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing contains NO substantive information on either team's current strength, roster, recent form, or head-to-head matchup. Search results reference 'TBD' bracket entries and historical matches from 2024-2025, but nothing actionable about this specific April 13, 2026 matchup. MARKET PRICE AS PROXY: YES side at 74% likely reflects betting consensus that Vici Gaming is the stronger team. Vici Gaming is historically a top-tier Chinese Dota 2 organization; Team Resilience's competitive tier is entirely unknown from briefing data. ASYMMETRIC CONFIDENCE: confidence_yes (35) is significantly lower than the 74% probability_score because the market price is NOT supported by evaluable fundamentals in the briefing\u2014it is a consensus bet on brand/historical reputation. confidence_no (25) is even lower because there is virtually no counter-evidence or data on Team Resilience's actual strength either. TIMING RISK: EVENT TIMING = TODAY with match scheduled April 13 08:00 ET and resolution deadline 18:00 UTC (April 13). The match likely beg