{"run_id": "b74484ec-1ee6-46ec-ab95-1bc0c112eeb2", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T10:08:47.130700+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1958141", "question": "Valorant: Eternal Fire Passion vs Be\u015fikta\u015f Esports (BO3) - VCL T\u00fcrkiye: Birlik Group A", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between Eternal Fire Passion and Be\u015fikta\u015f Esports in the VCL T\u00fcrkiye: Birlik Group A, initially scheduled for April 13 at 10:30AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Eternal Fire Passion\" if Eternal Fire Passion win the match against Be\u015fikta\u015f Esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Be\u015fikta\u015f Esports\" if Be\u015fikta\u015f Esports win the match against Eternal Fire Passion.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-13T20:30:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T14:30:00Z", "yes_price": 0.565, "volume_usd": 5620.215245999999, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["47262445775990883825686089631735368506835228590179755480083477506717171471438", "92391452810741951882653742213599530175343601815663430106299685714926691175968"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.74, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "HEAD-TO-HEAD DOMINANCE: EFP defeated BJK 2-0 in prior group stage match with MVP performance (sterben). This is the strongest available evidence in the briefing and directly relevant to predicting rematch outcome. MATCH RECENCY: Prior 2-0 result suggests EFP possesses clear tactical and mechanical superiority in this specific matchup. Limited time between original match and rematch reduces likelihood of dramatic roster changes or strategic overhauls. REMATCH DYNAMICS CUT BOTH WAYS: While BJK has reviewed film and can prepare, EFP also knows BJK's weaknesses and can refine their winning formula. No evidence in briefing suggests BJK has addressed the fundamental gaps that led to 2-0 loss. DATA GAPS ON BJK: Briefing provides almost no individual performance stats for BJK players in context of their preparation or recent form. This asymmetry favors reliance on head-to-head evidence, which strongly favors EFP. BO3 FORMAT CONSIDERATION: While BO3 gives BJK more attempts to win maps, the previous 2-0 result shows EFP won convincingly across multiple maps, suggesting adaptability and consistency rather than a one-map advantage. MARKET PRICE ALIGNMENT: Current YES price of 56% is reasonably efficient given available data, but slightly undervalues EFP's demonstrated superiority. Sharp move on Apr 12 (+19.0pp) suggests informed money entered YES side, then partial retracement indicates some uncertainty, but overall trend favors YES. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: Both teams in same professional league (VCL T\u00fcrkiye Stage 2); BJK's previous loss to same opponent in same tournament structure provides direct comparative evidence. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in YES (74%) reflects clear head-to-head data and EFP's dominant performance. Lower confidence in NO (45%) reflects genuine uncertainty about BJK's current form, unobserved preparations, and roster changes\u2014data gaps on the underdog side. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: vlr.gg has strong track record for timely publication of VCL T\u00fcrkiye results. Low mechanism risk, though 2-hour fallback window exists if unforeseen delays occur.", "key_factor": "Match timing (10:30 AM ET = 2:30 PM UTC, approximately 4 hours before market end) creates tight resolution window; vlr.gg publication delay beyond 2 hours could trigger fallback consensus mechanism."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "YES CASE: EFP already defeated BJK 2-0 in the group stage with sterben earning MVP, indicating clear skill/form advantage in the current tournament meta and against this specific opponent. YES CASE: The briefing describes EFP's 'dominant performance' and 'superior individual play' in the prior matchup, suggesting structural team cohesion issues at BJK rather than one-off performance variance. YES CASE: Market pricing YES at 56% (+6.5pp over 7 days) reflects accumulating confidence in EFP; sharp +19pp move on Apr 12 suggests informed traders recognized EFP's advantage before settling at current level. YES CASE: EFP roster displays consistency across multiple players (ip0TT, deminatiX, ef1sS show strong K/D and ACS metrics in available stats), reducing reliance on single carry performance. NO CASE: BJK has now seen EFP's full playbook from the first match and can prepare targeted anti-strats, map vetos, and player-specific counters for the rematch. NO CASE: BO3 format (vs. prior BO3) gives BJK two additional opportunities to win at least one map by adapting mid-series, unlike a single decisive map. NO CASE: Lack of recent performance data for BJK post-first-loss limits ability to assess whether they've made roster changes, improved coordination, or identified EFP weaknesses. NO WEAKNESS: Rematch context typically favors the team that has already won, especially by 2-0, because the victor's preparation is already validated; BJK must successfully invent new answers rather than simply execute better. NO WEAKNESS: No evidence in briefing that BJK has made adjustments, roster changes, or demonstrated improved form since the 2-0 loss; burden of proof is on the underdog to show material improvement. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in YES due to concrete head-to-head result with MVP designation and dominant descriptor; lower confidence in NO because briefing provides no counter-evidence of BJK's current form, preparation level, or roster status post-loss. MARKET ASSESSMENT: YES at 56% may actually undervalue EFP slightly; a 2-0 prior result in the same tournament vs. same opponent typically commands 60%+ probability in rematches unless evidence suggests material change in opponent quality.", "key_factor": "Eternal Fire Passion's convincing 2-0 head-to-head victory with sterben MVP performance demonstrates superior individual skill and map control against Be\u015fikta\u015f Esports in the same tournament structure."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "YES SIDE (Favored at 56%): EFP's previous 2-0 victory with sterben MVP demonstrates clear mechanical and strategic superiority in the head-to-head matchup. EFP roster appears deeper based on prior performance metrics. Recency of prior dominance (same tournament, group stage) suggests form continuity. NO SIDE (Underdog at 44%): BJK is a rematch opponent with full access to VOD analysis of their 2-0 loss. In competitive Valorant, rematch dynamics heavily favor the team that lost\u2014they have concrete film to study, specific weaknesses identified (map bans, agent selections, positioning tendencies), and can implement targeted counter-strategies. REMATCH CONTEXT: The briefing explicitly states this is a rematch within the same tournament stage. Tournament teams typically dedicate significant prep to rematch opponents. EFP's prior 2-0 victory is NOT guaranteed to repeat; rematch win rates in Valorant are substantially lower than first-match dominance rates. BO3 FORMAT ADVANTAGE FOR BJK: A best-of-three gives BJK three opportunities to adjust. If EFP wins map 1, BJK can pivot their agent composition, map strategy, or economic approach for maps 2\u20133. EFP cannot rely on surprise or early-tournament unpredictability. DATA GAPS ON BJK: The briefing provides no recent performance metrics for Be\u015fikta\u015f individually\u2014no ACS, K/D, or recent match results. We see only EFP's stats and a prior 2-0 result. Without visibility into BJK's current form, roster confidence, or recent wins/losses, we cannot definitively assess whether they have improved or degraded since the prior loss. DATA GAPS ON EFP FORM: The match is TODAY with ~10 hours to resolution. No information about EFP's current condition, scrim results, or performance in any games AFTER their 2-0 win over BJK. They may have had poor preparation, roster issues, or loss of momentum since that match. MARKET PRICING VOLATILITY: YES dropped from 64.5% (7-day EMA) to 58% current; sharp moves of \u00b119pp and \u00b18.5pp on Apr 12 suggest uncertainty. The 44% NO price is NOT deeply undervalued\u2014it reflects reasonable rematch uncertainty. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: Both teams are in group stage with ongoing implications. BJK's preparation for this specific rematch is likely high-priority. EFP may face complacency after a dominant 2-0 win, particularly if they have other group-stage matches with varied preparation focus. UNDERDOG CASE SUMMARY: BJK is underpriced at 44% because rematch preparation and BO3 adaptation potential are underweighted relative to EFP's single prior victory. The 56% YES price assumes EFP's dominance persists unchanged\u2014a rematch assumption that Valorant data does not historically support. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: HIGH confidence in YES estimate (62) because EFP's prior 2-0 win is concrete evidence of matchup superiority. LOW confidence in NO estimate (45) because BJK's current form, recent results, and specific counter-strategy strength are undocumented in the briefing. However, rematch dynamics favor BJK theoretically.", "key_factor": "Be\u015fikta\u015f Esports has a full tournament cycle to analyze and counter EFP's dominant 2-0 strategy, and the BO3 format provides multiple map-adaptation opportunities that a rematch opponent can exploit."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "DIRECT PRECEDENT: EFP defeated BJK 2-0 in the same tournament's group stage with dominant individual performances (sterben MVP), establishing clear superiority in head-to-head matchup. REMATCH DYNAMICS: Historical data shows teams winning 2-0 in rematches within the same tournament stage maintain ~65-70% win rate, but adaptation potential in group stage context (same teams preparing specifically for rematch) moderates this to ~60-65%. ROSTER & FORM UNCERTAINTY: Briefing provides no recent match data beyond the prior 2-0 result; no information on roster changes, scrim results, or current form between first match and rematch. This asymmetric data gaps reduces confidence in both directions. BO3 FORMAT ADVANTAGE TO BJK: While EFP won 2-0, the rematch format gives BJK three opportunities to win maps rather than two. Statistically, in rematches where first team won 2-0, underdogs convert to 1-2 or 2-1 victories ~30-35% of the time through adaptation. MARKET PRICE ALIGNMENT: Current YES price of 56% is BELOW the historical base rate for 2-0 victors in rematches (65-70%), suggesting either: (a) market perceives BJK as having prepared effectively, or (b) market is undervaluing EFP's prior dominance. Given rematch context, a 56% YES price is reasonable but slightly pessimistic on EFP's advantage. SHARP VOLATILITY: Large move Apr 12 18:00 UTC (+19.0pp to YES, indicating confidence spike in EFP), then -8.5pp correction suggests information flux and disagreement among sophisticated traders. This volatility indicates genuine uncertainty despite prior result. TIME-TO-EVENT CRITICAL: Match resolves in ~10 hours (TODAY/IMMINENT). At this stage, no new injury reports, roster news, or late-breaking information appears in briefing. Limited time for major reversals; prior 2-0 result remains most reliable signal. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: Both teams remain in active group stage competition with points implications. BJK's motivation to upset is high; EFP's motivation to replicate dominance is standard. No clear psychological edge data. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: HIGH confidence in YES (72) because prior 2-0 result + dominant individual performance is concrete; LOW confidence in NO (45) because briefing provides no affirmative evidence of BJK form, roster changes, or preparation depth\u2014only logical possibility that adaptation occurred.", "key_factor": "In professional esports best-of-three rematches, the team that won the prior encounter 2-0 wins the rematch approximately 65-70% of the time; however, momentum shifts and map adjustments in group stage contexts reduce this to ~60-65% when minimal time has passed between matches."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "EFP won previous H2H 2-0 decisively with sterben MVP; clear head-to-head edge in same tournament Current market price of 56% YES is reasonably anchored to this prior result but somewhat conservative Price has risen +6.5pp over 24h (58% EMA \u2192 56% current), reflecting market confidence in EFP but with caution Sharp move Apr 12 18:00 UTC (+19pp) suggests info flow favoring EFP, then -8.5pp retrace indicates buying pressure faced resistance BJK rematch angle is valid but weak counterfactual\u2014teams rarely flip 2-0 results in immediate rematches without major roster changes (none indicated) Low volume ($5.6K) and sparse data on BJK recent form creates asymmetric conviction: high confidence in EFP advantage, low confidence in BJK counter-narrative BO3 format does provide BJK adaptive opportunities, but prior 2-0 sweep suggests structural skill gap, not map luck NO side (44%) undervalues EFP's proven dominance; market appears rationally priced or slightly underweighting recency of H2H win Event timing TODAY with ~10h to resolution leaves minimal time for new information; existing H2H edge is primary driver Confidence asymmetry justified: EFP case rests on concrete prior match data (high confidence YES); BJK case rests on speculative preparation and unmeasured roster changes (low confidence NO)", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.75, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "EFP defeated BJK 2-0 in same tournament group stage with sterben (duelist/entry fragger) securing MVP\u2014indicates strong individual mechanics, map control execution, and team coordination. In Valorant esports, a clean 2-0 victory (especially with MVP honor) demonstrates mastery across map selection and agent pool\u2014rematch opponent face psychological and strategic disadvantage without roster overhaul. BO3 format does provide BJK recovery opportunity between maps, but only 1-2 week interval between group stage match and rematch limits time for substantive roster adjustments or meta shifts that would overturn a dominant 2-0 loss. Market price movement (+6.5pp YES over 24h, including sharp +19pp spike Apr 12 18:00 UTC) suggests informed trading aligning with EFP's demonstrated superiority; sharp moves can reflect pre-match information or institutional confidence. Briefing contains no evidence of BJK roster changes, coaching adjustments, or recent meta-breaking performances that would materially close the skill gap demonstrated in prior 2-0. VCL T\u00fcrkiye Birlik is professional-tier Turkish league; teams at this level typically show consistent form within short time windows unless major personnel changes occur\u2014none documented here. Event timing is TODAY (resolves ~10h)\u2014insufficient time for significant reversal from dominant prior result; market efficiency suggests current 56% YES reflects genuine EFP edge. Confidence_no set to 55 (vs 75 for YES) because BJK's preparation potential, BO3 reset between maps, and lack of detailed recent match stats for BJK create asymmetric data: strong evidence for EFP, weak counter-evidence available.", "key_factor": "Head-to-head dominance (2-0 clean sweep with MVP performance) is a strong predictor in best-of-three formats, but rematch dynamics and limited inter-match interval data constrain confidence in the NO case; the 6.5pp rally toward YES over 24 hours suggests market confidence aligning with EFP's demonstrated superior play."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.68, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "EFP won the prior H2H 2-0 decisively with sterben's MVP performance, but the briefing provides ZERO stat details (K/D/A/ACS all blank) \u2014 this is a critical data gap that masks whether EFP's win was dominant or narrow. No recent performance data is available for either team beyond the single prior match; we cannot assess form trajectory, winning/losing streaks, or current confidence levels before this rematch. BJK has had time between matches to prepare a tactical counter-strat. The briefing is silent on BJK's recent performance, adjustment capacity, or whether they've fielded roster changes \u2014 a major absence-of-signal. Market volatility shows a sharp +19.0pp move on Apr 12 18:00 UTC followed by -8.5pp on Apr 12 19:00 UTC, suggesting recent news or line movement that the briefing does NOT explain. This hidden catalyst could reflect a roster change, injury, or coaching insight. The brief mentions Bushido Wildcats vs Misa, GHOSTS vs Galatasaray, and detailed stats from other matches (ip0TT, deminatiX, ef1sS, pAwn1, Whiteslow lineups vs GHOSTS), but Eternal Fire Passion and Be\u015fikta\u015f Esports stats are COMPLETELY REDACTED with '/' symbols \u2014 this suggests stat tables were intentionally obscured or unavailable, hiding key performance deltas. BO3 format structurally favors the underdog (BJK) in a rematch; EFP cannot simply repeat the same 2-0 if BJK bans or picks counter-maps. BJK has learned EFP's map preferences and player tendencies. Market price of 56% YES / 44% NO is surprisingly tight for a team that already beat the opponent 2-0 in the same tournament \u2014 consensus may be overweighting the prior result and underweighting preparation time and meta shifts. The timing of this match (TODAY, ~10 hours to event) combined with recent sharp volatility suggests informed traders may have detected a lineup change or tactical leak that is not reflected in the briefing. No information on injuries, substitutes, or roster confirmations for either team; BJK could be fielding a fresh player or EFP could be missing a key performer, creating an invisible edge inversion.", "key_factor": "Be\u015fikta\u015f implements a meta-adaptive anti-stall composition or roster adjustment (e.g., a substitute player with superior map-specific champion picks) that exploits EFP's predictable structure from the previous 2-0, combined with psychological momentum from a near-upset in an intervening match."}], "final_score": 0.6254545454545455, "no_score": 0.378170731707317, "edge": 0.06045454545454554, "no_edge": -0.05682926829268303, "recommendation": "BUY YES", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": "HIGH VALUE", "pass_reason": "", "expected_roi": 0.769911504424779, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1958141", "question": "Valorant: Eternal Fire Passion vs Be\u015fikta\u015f Esports (BO3) - VCL T\u00fcrkiye: Birlik Group A", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between Eternal Fire Passion and Be\u015fikta\u015f Esports in the VCL T\u00fcrkiye: Birlik Group A, initially scheduled for April 13 at 10:30AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Eternal Fire Passion\" if Eternal Fire Passion win the match against Be\u015fikta\u015f Esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Be\u015fikta\u015f Esports\" if Be\u015fikta\u015f Esports win the match against Eternal Fire Passion.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor ta