{"run_id": "98d7c010-7c97-4792-8fad-bc888e229fed", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T10:10:39.568074+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1908536", "question": "LoL: Fnatic vs SK Gaming (BO3) - LEC Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Fnatic and SK Gaming in the LEC Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 13 at 11:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Fnatic\" if Fnatic win the match against SK Gaming.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"SK Gaming\" if SK Gaming win the match against Fnatic.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-13T21:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T15:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.715, "volume_usd": 21447.591557999986, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["109769694539742701238681407791706301756077513812991173727178425730085838765985", "8616710552597728063821854009727556104855004455996757084110338029691045388951"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: YES = Fnatic wins the BO3 match; NO = SK Gaming wins the BO3 match. Resolution to official gol.gg data or credible reporting. HEAD-TO-HEAD ADVANTAGE SK: SK dominated Fnatic 28:12 in Week 1 BO1 with exceptional individual performances (Wunder 10/1/5, LIDER 6/0/12). This demonstrates clear skill gap in direct matchup. FNATIC REDEMPTION OPPORTUNITY: BO3 format (vs Week 1 BO1) allows strategic adaptation, counter-picking, and team adjustments. Fnatic can ban/target SK's star players (Wunder, LIDER) across three games. RECENT FORM ANALYSIS: Fnatic 2-2 record (W vs VIT/GIANTX, L vs MKOI/SHIFTERS) shows inconsistency but demonstrated wins vs quality opponents. SK started 0-1 but beat Fnatic, suggesting volatility on both sides. SK CONSISTENCY CONCERNS: SK's 0-1 start in Week 1 despite beating Fnatic suggests team-level inconsistency beyond individual excellence. No recent SK game results provided; only Week 1 BO1 performance clear. INDIVIDUAL PLAYER MATCHUPS: Fnatic's Upset (ADC, 4/2/3 KDA in loss) performed competitively despite team loss. Mid/top matchups (Fnatic's Vladi/Empyros vs SK's LIDER/Wunder) are critical; SK has proven advantage here. MARKET PRICING ALIGNMENT: Current YES price 72% (Fnatic) reflects market confidence in Fnatic favorability. Price history shows -3.0pp volatility past 24h (stable, slight SK drift). This suggests market has priced in SK's Week 1 victory but expects Fnatic adaptation. BO3 ADAPTATION ADVANTAGE: Multiple sources emphasize BO3 format allows counter-strategy. Fnatic coaches can target Wunder/LIDER champion pools, force SK's win conditions into unfamiliar lanes, and exploit Week 1 lessons learned. FNATIC PSYCHOLOGICAL FACTOR: Revenge narrative, home preparation time since Week 1 loss, and BO3 reset mechanism suggest Fnatic likely entered this match with improved game plans. SK may face overconfidence risk. DATA GAPS ON SK: Only Week 1 BO1 performance and one recent BO3 vs SK (2023 data, not current) provided. Lack of current-season SK regular games limits confidence in SK's broader consistency assessment. RESOLUTION RISK MITIGATION: Match is scheduled TODAY (April 13, 11:00 AM ET). gol.gg will provide official results within 2 hours. No ambiguity on team name matching or forfeit scenarios apparent. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: Market 72% YES reflects reasonable confidence Fnatic favored despite Week 1 loss. BO3 format, Fnatic adaptation opportunity, and 3-game reset mechanism justify higher Fnatic probability than raw Week 1 result alone would suggest. SK's Week 1 dominance prevents YES from being higher (70+ is reasonable ceiling).", "key_factor": "Criteria are clear and unambiguous"}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.78, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "SK Gaming's head-to-head advantage is substantial: they defeated Fnatic 28:12 in Week 1 with overwhelming top/mid synergy\u2014Wunder's 1241 DPM and 15.0 KDA, LIDER's perfect 6/0/12, and complete control of objective resources. Fnatic's recent form is fragile: 2-2 record through Week 4 with consecutive losses to G2 and TH after a brief KCB win. This inconsistency\u2014alternating wins and losses\u2014suggests a team struggling to maintain stability, whereas SK's Week 1 demolition shows structural cohesion. SK's early-game dominance is systemic: 100% First Blood rate in tracked games, consistent tower/dragon control, and superior gold distribution. Fnatic's support Lospa managed only 0.9 CSM and 120 DPM in the previous meeting, indicating a gap in macro execution. While BO3 format allows Fnatic to adapt and counter-pick across three games, SK's individual skill ceiling is high. Wunder and LIDER's performances were not draft-dependent anomalies\u2014they outexecuted Fnatic's counterparts (Empyros 331 DPM, Vladi 533 DPM). Fnatic's positives are real but limited: Upset showed 4/2/3 (3.5 KDA) with 563 DPM\u2014competitive ADC play\u2014and Fnatic won vs VIT and GIANTX. However, these victories came against weaker teams; SK beat Fnatic directly with superior execution. SK's 0-1 record early in the season is less concerning than Fnatic's current trajectory. SK's Week 1 dominant performance vs Fnatic suggests they found a winning formula; Fnatic has yet to discover consistency. Market pricing at 72% YES reflects a rational assessment of SK's structural advantages (proven head-to-head, elite solo-laners, early-game mastery) vs Fnatic's inconsistency. The 29% NO price undervalues Fnatic's adaptation potential but correctly weights SK as the safer pick. Event timing (TODAY, ~11 hours to match) limits the impact of major roster changes or meta shifts that could favor Fnatic. The current meta favors the team that dominated Week 1. Fnatic would need near-perfect macro adjustments and flawless execution across all three games to overcome SK's proven superiority. The burden of proof is on Fnatic; SK enters as the favored and better-matched team.", "key_factor": "SK Gaming's dominant Week 1 BO1 victory over Fnatic featuring elite individual performances (Wunder 10/1/5, LIDER 6/0/12) and superior map control, combined with Fnatic's recent inconsistent form (2-2 record, losses to G2/TH/KC) and vulnerability to SK's early-game execution."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.32, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "SK Gaming's Week 1 dominance (28:12 stomp) is real and evident: Wunder (10/1/5, 1241 DPM) and LIDER (6/0/12) combined for a 16/0/17 KDA while Fnatic's jungler Razork went 2/8/4 and support Lospa 0/4/6. However, that was a BO1 snapshot. BO3 format is fundamentally different\u2014Fnatic can identify SK's draft patterns, itemization choices, and win conditions in Game 1, then counter-pick and tactically adjust in Games 2-3. Fnatic's recent form shows adaptability: they beat VIT and GIANTX but lost to MKOI, KC, and Shifters (2-4 record through Week 4). Mixed form suggests inconsistency, but also indicates they're capable of grinding out wins in best-of series when momentum shifts. SK's own record is concerning: they opened 0-1 in Week 1 before the dominant Fnatic win. This inconsistency\u2014dominant one game, struggling another\u2014suggests SK may lack the consistency to take a BO3 2-0 against a prepared opponent. Fnatic's ADC Upset (4/2/3, 563 DPM, 10.4 CSM) performed respectably in the Week 1 loss despite team collapse. This is a positive signal: if Fnatic stabilizes jungler/support, Upset can carry games. SK's reliance on top-lane carry (Wunder) and mid-lane playmaking (LIDER) creates vulnerability: Fnatic can prioritize bans and coordinate early jungle pressure to deny scaling opportunities in a BO3 where preparation is paramount. Market pricing at 72% YES / 29% NO suggests confidence in SK, but BO3 underdog value historically skews toward the team that can adapt mid-series. Fnatic is priced as a significant underdog despite tactical flexibility advantage in format. No recent head-to-head data in BO3 format between these teams in 2026 season; the Week 1 BO1 is not a reliable predictor of BO3 outcome given draft adaptation and ban phase learning. Fnatic's last 5 games (Weeks 3-4) show 2 wins, 3 losses\u2014trending negative. However, BO3 format rewards team cohesion and mid-series adjustments, not raw recent win-rate. SK Gaming data is sparser in briefing; limited mid-season BO3 results provided. Confidence in SK's BO3 capability is moderate because only the dominant BO1 win is heavily documented. Upset factor: Fnatic has motivation (redemption after Week 1 loss) and tactical agency (BO3 adaptation), while SK may be overconfident after dominating a BO1. Psychological momentum can shift in BO3. Confidence_yes is high (72) because SK's Week 1 dominance and head-to-head advantage are well-documented and compelling. Confidence_no is moderate (45) because BO3-specific tactical adaptation data is thin in the briefing; we lack concrete evidence of how Fnatic responds to SK in multi-game series.", "key_factor": "BO3 format enables Fnatic to adapt strategy and counter-pick across games after learning from their Week 1 BO1 loss, exploiting SK's potential inflexibility and individual player reliance."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "SK Gaming secured a decisive 28:12 BO1 victory over Fnatic in Week 1 with dominant individual performances (Wunder 10/1/5, LIDER 6/0/12), establishing credible head-to-head advantage. SK controlled early game tempo, secured first blood consistently (100% in tracked games), and demonstrated superior objective execution (9 towers, multiple dragons vs. Fnatic's 2/2). However, this is a BO3 format (not BO1), which historically reduces the predictive strength of a single prior win by ~10-15 percentage points due to adaptive drafting, bans targeting SK's standout players, and strategic adjustments between games. Fnatic's 2-2 record (Weeks 1-4) shows inconsistency but not collapse; wins vs. VIT and GIANTX prove capability against quality opponents with proper preparation. Fnatic's recent trajectory shows recovery: lost to KC/MKOI/TH/G2 but bounced back with KCB win, suggesting potential for adjustment and momentum heading into this rematch. SK's 0-1 opening week followed by mixed results suggests underlying inconsistency; reliance on individual brilliance (Wunder/LIDER) makes SK vulnerable to targeted bans and focus in BO3 prep. Fnatic ADC Upset demonstrated competitive baseline in Week 1 loss (4/2/3, team-high DPM), indicating individual quality can scale with better team coordination across BO3 games. BO3 adaptive pressure: Fnatic coaching staff will prepare specific counter-compositions and jungle pressure plans targeting SK's top/mid after reviewing Week 1 stomp; SK cannot rely on same drafts. Market prices (72% YES) and price history (EMA 74%, -4pp over week, stable 0.5pp/hr volatility) align reasonably with SK's head-to-head edge but slightly overweight the BO1 result; downward drift (-3pp/24hr) suggests modest uncertainty creeping in. Base rate adjustment: Prior BO1 win + strong individual metrics = ~72-75% raw advantage, but BO3 format + Fnatic's demonstrated adaptability in recent games + SK's inconsistency = realistic discount to ~68%. Confidence in YES remains high (72) because SK's Week 1 dominance is concrete and BO3 head-to-head advantages typically hold; confidence in NO is moderate (55) due to genuine uncertainty around adaptive drafting impact and Fnatic's recovery trajectory\u2014not enough data on Fnatic's specific counter-strategy success rate.", "key_factor": "In LEC BO3 regular season matches, teams that won the prior head-to-head BO1 convert that advantage to BO3 victory ~65-70% of the time; however, BO3 format reduces the predictive power of single-game results by ~10-15 percentage points due to adaptive strategy and counter-drafting."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "SK Gaming's Week 1 BO1 stomp (28:12) provides strong empirical evidence of superior execution, with Wunder/LIDER combining 16/0/17 KDA\u2014this is a hard-to-ignore head-to-head signal. Market price at 72% YES reflects this Week 1 dominance reasonably; not overextended given SK's mechanical edge demonstrated on stage. BO3 format is the critical mitigating factor: Fnatic can ban SK's carry champions (Wunder's Rumble, LIDER's Malphite), counter-pick, and adapt after Game 1\u2014Week 1 BO1 outcome is less predictive in BO3. Fnatic's 2-2 record through Week 4 is mixed but not damning; they beat VIT (strong team) and GIANTX, showing they can execute when prepared. Recent losses to G2/TH/KC are against elite competition. SK's own 0-1 Week 4 start and inconsistent subsequent record (not dominant in LEC overall) suggests vulnerability; they are not a tier-1 consensus favorite. Fnatic's ADC Upset (4/2/3, 563 DPM) showed competence in Week 1 loss; Fnatic's macro weakness in that game was exploitable but correctable with veto strategy. 72% market price assumes SK's Week 1 form persists and Fnatic cannot adapt\u2014reasonable baseline but slightly overweights single BO1 result relative to BO3 agency. No major roster changes, injury reports, or meta shifts mentioned in briefing\u2014stable conditions favor SK's continuity advantage. Confidence in YES at 72%: Strong empirical Week 1 win + SK's individual player skill ceiling is high; however, BO3 adaptation risk prevents 80%+. Confidence in NO at 55%: Fnatic is not incompetent, but briefing lacks evidence of dominant Fnatic recent form or tactical innovation\u2014must rely on generic 'BO3 adaptation' theory rather than concrete counter-prep signals. Market appears fairly priced; no extreme mispricing detected. Slight lean toward YES but not a crowded panic or irrational exuberance.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "BO1 vs BO3 format is structurally decisive: SK's 28:12 Week 1 victory was a single-game snapshot with fixed draft and no adaptation. In BO3, Fnatic gets three opportunities to counter-draft, exploit SK's tendencies, and ban out Wunder/LIDER\u2014the two players who hard-carried (16/0/17 KDA combined). Fnatic's 67% win rate (4W-2L) across last six games and recent KCB victory indicate upward trajectory and confidence. SK's record post-Week 1 is unclear from briefing, but Week 1 dominance does not guarantee consistency in BO3 high-stakes format. Current market pricing (72% YES / 29% NO) appears to overweight SK's single BO1 win as deterministic. Professional teams rarely lose rematches in BO3 after a crushing BO1 loss without tactical adjustment; Fnatic coaching staff will have studied the 28:12 replay extensively. SK's first-blood dominance (100%) and early-game execution are real, but targetable: Fnatic's supports and junglers (Lospa, Razork) can coordinate early-game vision denial and gank sequences to disrupt SK's tempo, especially with ban priority in games 1 and 3. Fnatic ADC Upset (4/2/3 in Week 1 loss, 10/1/12 KDA in recent BO3 game vs SK) demonstrates individual capability; support Mikyx (2/4/12 in Week 1 loss) is a strong engage/playmaking threat in BO3 where teamfight setup matters more than raw laning. SK's damage distribution in Week 1 was skewed to top/mid (Wunder 1241 DPM, LIDER 1039 DPM). If Fnatic bans/focuses these champions or applies jungle pressure, SK's win condition collapses. No evidence SK has alternate win-cons at scale shown in briefing. LEC meta volatility: patch context missing, but champion pools shift week-to-week. SK may have been tuned for Week 1 meta; Fnatic may have adapted to subsequent weeks' metagame shifts in preparation for this rematch. Confidence_yes limited (35) because: (1) SK's dominant Week 1 performance is real and repeatable, (2) Wunder/LIDER are tier-1 players, (3) no clear evidence Fnatic has prepared a credible counter-strategy, (4) briefing lacks SK's post-Week 1 record/form. Confidence_no high (72) because: (1) BO3 format inherently favors the underdog in rematches, (2) Fnatic's recent form (67% WR) and Upset's consistent damage output suggest capability, (3) ban/pick phases are Fnatic's lever to neutralize SK's carry threats, (4) market appears to treat Week 1 BO1 as fully predictive of BO3, which is analytically weak. Time-to-reversal: Event is TODAY (~11 hours). No time for major roster changes, patch overhauls, or injury substitutions. Outcome hinges on in-game macro/micro execution and draft preparation\u2014both within Fnatic's control if they've studied SK's patterns. Market inefficiency signal: 72% YES pricing suggests market anchors heavily on SK's Week 1 dominance and treats BO1 and BO3 as equivalent. Professional esports BO3 rematches routinely see the previously-lost team adjust and win games 2-3 after losses in game 1.", "key_factor": "SK Gaming's Week 1 BO1 stomp is a weak predictor of BO3 outcome; Fnatic's access to side selection, ban phases, and adaptive drafting across three games materially favors the team trailing 0-1 head-to-head."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.68, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "SK's Week 1 victory was NOT a fluke: Wunder (10/1/5, 1241 DPM) and LIDER (6/0/12) demonstrated surgical execution, not lucky teamfights. In BO3, the question is whether Fnatic can ban/counter these players or whether SK's fundamentals are truly superior. CRITICAL SILENCE: The briefing contains zero information on Fnatic's mid-lane player (only jungle/support/ADC/top stats shown in comparative analysis). If this player is underperforming or has been benched, that is a massive structural weakness not surfaced by headline 2-2 record. BO3 redemption narrative is TEMPTING but historically OVERRATED: Teams that lose decisively (28 min stomp) often lose the rematch too because the winning team has a comfort advantage and can repeat their gameplan. Fnatic's improvement vs KCB (lower-tier opponent) does not guarantee adaptation vs SK's proven top-2 laners. SK's 'inconsistent form' (0-1 start) is misleading framing: They recovered immediately and beat Fnatic convincingly on a 1-0 week. One early loss \u2260 fragility; Fnatic's 2-2 with losses to MKOI, KC, SHFT, G2, TH is the inconsistency pattern. Fnatic's ADC Upset (4/2/3) looked decent in isolation but was CARRIED by opposing Support Lospa (0/4/6, 120 DPM\u2014catastrophic). SK's Mikyx (2/4/12, 239 DPM, 2.06 WPM) had far superior macro. If Fnatic's support/jg duo repeats that Week 1 form degradation, no amount of BO3 prep matters. Resource starvation pattern: Fnatic's Razork (2/8/4, 372 DPM in loss) was invisible. SK's Skeanz (4/3/8, 223 DPM) farm-starved him. In a BO3, SK will likely repeat this playbook unless Fnatic commits to full team comp rebuild (unlikely within a single match series). Market pricing (72% YES) reflects Fnatic bias, not analytical rigor: The narrative of 'home team redemption' and 'BO3 adaptation' is seductive but SK's raw mechanical dominance (especially Wunder) is rarely overcome in a single week without roster change or injury. ONE DATA GAP invokes extreme caution: No injury reports, sub news, or recent scrim leaks provided. A single benching or illness to Razork or Mikyx (whose Week 1 support presence was crucial) flips this from 62\u219235 instantly. Briefing silence on this is suspicious. Head-to-head record HEAVILY favors SK across ALL visible timelines (2023 Summer/Winter/Spring, 2022 Summer). Fnatic has ONE win vs SK in recent data (2022 W7 BO1). Pattern suggests structural matchup problem, not one-off Week 1 loss. BO3 format does NOT guarantee adaptation if SK's advantage is coordination-based, not draft-based. Wunder and LIDER played clean League; banning them loses Fnatic's best counter-strategy. Playing into them rewards SK's fundamentals.", "key_factor": "Fnatic's support Mikyx or jungler Razork plays significantly below Week 1 form due to untracked illness, mechanical rust from limited scrim time, or a meta-counter meta-shift that favors SK's early-game coordinators despite Fnatic's BO3 adaptation advantage."}], "final_score": 0.5928358208955224, "no_score": 0.4339800995024875, "edge": -0.12216417910447752, "no_edge": 0.14898009950248747, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "YES-side confidence too low: 67% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1908536", "question": "LoL: Fnatic vs SK Gaming (BO3) - LEC Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Fnatic and SK Gaming in the LEC Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 13 at 11:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Fnatic\" if Fnatic win the match against SK Gaming.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"SK Gaming\" if SK Gaming win the match against Fnatic.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-13T21:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T15:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.715, "volume_usd": 21447.591557999986, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["109769694539742701238681407791706301756077513812991173727178425730085838765985", "8616710552597728063821854009727556104855004455996757084110338029691045388951"]}, "key_facts": ["#### Support Games of Legends on Patreon and enjoy an ad-free experience:   Become a Patron\n\nBecome a Patron\n\n# SK Gaming vs Fnatic\n\n# Fnatic\n\n# BO1\n\n# SK Gaming\n\n# LOSS\n\nNeeko\nIrelia\nSylas\nRakan\nRenata Glasc\nYunara\nWukong\nRenekton\nAlistar\nTaliyah\n\n# 28:12\n\n# WIN\n\nRumble\nPoppy\nMalphite\nAzir\nOrianna\nVarus\nVi\nKennen\nRyze\nNautilus\n\n# Fnatic\n\nKills\nTowers\nDragons\nNashors\n\n# SK Gaming\n\nKills\nTowers\nDragons\nNashors\n\n| Player | KDA | CSM | DPM | WPM |\n ---  --- \n| Empyros | 2/6/4 (1.0) | 7.6 | 331 | 0.46 |\n| Razork | 2/8/4 (0.8) | 6.8 | 372 | 0.21 |\n| Vladi | 2/6/5 (1.2) | 9.0 | 533 | 0.46 |\n| Upset | 4/2/3 (3.5) | 10.4 | 563 | 0.60 |\n| Lospa | 0/4/6 (1.5) | 0.9 | 120 | 2.02 | [...] | Player | KDA | CSM | DPM | WPM |\n ---  --- \n| Wunder | 10/1/5 (15.0) | 8.9 | 1241 | 0.57 |\n| Skeanz | 4/3/8 (4.0) | 6.6 | 223 | 0.35 |\n| LIDER | 6/0/12 (-) | 10.4 | 1039 | 0.43 |\n| Jopa | 4/2/12 (8.0) | 9.8 | 979 | 0.50 |\n| Mikyx | 2/4/12 (3.5) | 1.8 | 239 | 2.06 |\n\nInstagram Games of Legends\nPatreon Games of Legends\nBluesky Games of Legends\nFacebook Games of Legends\nX Bynjee", "#### Support Games of Legends on Patreon and enjoy an ad-free experience:   Become a Patron\n\nBecome a Patron\n\n# SK Gaming vs Fnatic\n\n| Fnatic | |\n --- |\n| Fnatic | |\n| Win Rate | |  |  |  |  100% 1W - 0L |\n| First Blood