: 16-team Swiss system (BO3 matches), Top 8 advance to Main Stage", "NeverPlay lost 0-2 to INFUR on April 7, 2026 in same tournament's Round 1", "Match is online format for European teams", "Eternal Fire Academy designation suggests developmental/secondary roster status", "Swiss format bracket positioning and opponent history in tournament affects current matchup context"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-13T10:13:24.587852Z", "price_history": {"yes": {"token_id": "21560932918180481023981289999848884093755505766429467313140166032332363375345", "data_points": 2, "weighted_avg": 0.621270368894088, "change_1w_pp": -5.500000000000005, "change_24h_pp": -5.500000000000005, "volatility_24h": 0.0, "direction": "FALLING", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-13T10:12:45Z", "delta_pp": -5.500000000000005}]}, "no": {"token_id": "53151276850815591559581217112338024846549857811247038992742965773324260360455", "data_points": 3, "weighted_avg": 0.38587687851325403, "change_1w_pp": 5.500000000000005, "change_24h_pp": 5.500000000000005, "volatility_24h": 3.1819805153394665, "direction": "RISING", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-13T08:00:59Z", "delta_pp": 5.000000000000004}]}, "fetched_at": "2026-04-13T10:13:25.273835Z"}}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-13T21:30:00Z", "winning_side": null, "final_yes_price": 0.5, "checked_at": "2026-04-14T20:51:01.447403+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "b6f21d5b-05db-4748-9ad6-476d39438c8b", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T10:15:03.921245+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1960163", "question": "Valorant: WIP Esports vs Mandatory (BO3) - VCL France: Revolution Stage 2 Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between WIP Esports and Mandatory in the VCL France: Revolution Stage 2 Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 13 at 12:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"WIP Esports\" if WIP Esports win the match against Mandatory.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Mandatory\" if Mandatory win the match against WIP Esports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-13T22:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T16:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.225, "volume_usd": 3542.00038, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["79720653084492924093002587346392543562573583154000840152650396731915516959625", "85921010026849250616845778279286856674699903574117753032854252425357516361584"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "WIP Esports enters as clear favorites: undefeated 3-0 record with +30 round differential vs Mandatory's 2-1 with +20 differential. Map win rate advantage for WIP (6-2 vs 5-2) and higher seeding position (1st vs 2nd) suggests stronger aggregate performance across the stage. However, Mandatory's +20 round differential and 2-1 record demonstrate competitive strength and ability to win matches in this group. Close map differential (6-2 vs 5-2 = only 1 map difference) suggests matches are contested; not blowouts by WIP. BO3 format (first to 2 maps) introduces variance: Mandatory's competitive positioning means they have realistic paths to steal maps and win the series. Briefing provides no head-to-head record, recent trend data, player-level stats, or patch-specific meta context to distinguish these teams further. Market price (YES 22% / NO 78%) appears to overweight WIP's standing position and undervalue Mandatory's demonstrated competitive closeness. WIP's 3-0 record is strong but small sample (only 3 matches); Mandatory's 2-1 is limited data on both sides. Lack of VOD/streaming context or caster insights prevents assessment of draft favorability, tactical adaptability, or momentum. Probability estimate reflects WIP's statistical edge (undefeated, +30 diff) but acknowledges meaningful competitive parity and Mandatory's win capability. Confidence in YES is higher (72) due to clear statistical advantages; confidence in NO is lower (55) because briefing provides insufficient counter-evidence to fully justify market's 78% NO price. Event timing is TODAY (~12 hours): match is imminent, reducing likelihood of cancellation/delay scenarios that would resolve to 50-50.", "key_factor": "Briefing lacks detailed head-to-head history, recent form trends, and individual player/coaching performance data that would inform a more precise prediction."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.76, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.78, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE STRENGTH (NO = Mandatory wins): Market has priced NO at 78%, reflecting Mandatory's competitive standing and the inherent uncertainty in best-of-3 esports formats. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS (YES = WIP Esports wins): Despite WIP Esports' 3-0 record, the market discounts them at only 22%, suggesting either overvaluation of Mandatory's comeback potential or significant hidden information (roster changes, scrim results, opponent prep) not visible in the briefing. WIP ESPORTS DOMINANT FORM: 3-0 record with +30 round differential is substantially stronger than Mandatory's 2-1 with +20. This 10-round differential gap reflects consistent superior performance across all matches played. MAP WIN RATE ADVANTAGE: WIP Esports' 6-2 map count versus Mandatory's 5-2 shows WIP winning 75% of maps while Mandatory wins 71.4% \u2014 a narrow but consistent edge that favors the undefeated team in a BO3 format where map selection and momentum are critical. MANDATORY'S COMPETITIVE FLOOR: However, Mandatory's +20 round differential is respectable \u2014 not a weak team, suggesting this is not a mismatch. Mandatory has proven ability to beat group opponents, creating legitimate 20-25% upset scenario. HEAD-TO-HEAD DATA GAP: Briefing explicitly notes 'limited head-to-head context available' \u2014 this is a critical missing data point. If Mandatory has previously beaten WIP Esports or has strong scrim evidence, market pricing of 78% NO may be justified despite WIP's superior record. BO3 FORMAT VOLATILITY: Best-of-3 esports matches contain inherent variance. Even 70-30 favored teams lose BO3s regularly due to map pool dynamics, vetoes, and single-match upsets. Market's 78% NO price reflects appropriate acknowledgment of this variance. PLAYOFF IMPLICATIONS: Both teams competing for standing position adds urgency and preparation intensity to both squads, potentially tightening the match outcome beyond raw statistics. MARKET PRICE MOVEMENT ANALYSIS: YES side has risen 4 percentage points in 24 hours (from ~18% to 22%) while NO has fallen 6.5pp (from ~84% to 78%), suggesting recent information is shifting sentiment toward WIP Esports or uncertainty is increasing. This could indicate late breaking scrims, roster news, or anticipation of WIP's dominant form continuing. VOLATILITY PATTERN: 24-hour volatility of 1.2pp/hr for YES (higher) versus 1.0pp/hr for NO (lower) indicates YES side is attracting more recent trading activity, not necessarily conviction shift. CONVICTION ASSESSMENT: NO side at 78% remains strongly favored by market despite WIP Esports' perfect record \u2014 this suggests either: (1) market has legitimate uncertainty about WIP's sustainability, (2) Mandatory is underrated based on scrim/hidden data, or (3) esports markets price in volatility heavily. BULLISH CASE FOR NO (MANDATORY): If Mandatory wins, it would represent a disciplined upset of a 3-0 team with better round differential, suggesting they solved WIP's meta/playstyle or had superior preparation. The 78% pricing suggests this outcome is credible but less likely. DATA ASYMMETRY WARNING: Briefing provides excellent quantitative standing data but zero qualitative intel on team form, recent roster changes, coach adjustments, or scrim results. This asymmetry means confidence in NO should be tempered \u2014 we're missing half the story.", "key_factor": "WIP Esports' perfect 3-0 record with +30 round differential versus Mandatory's 2-1 record and +20 differential demonstrates a clear momentum and form advantage in a head-to-head matchup with playoff implications."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "MARKET PRICING CONTEXT: YES is priced at 22% but has risen +4.0pp in 24 hours while NO fell -6.5pp, suggesting recent market repricing toward YES \u2014 potential recognition of Mandatory's viability. WIP ESPORTS DOMINANCE (supports NO): 3-0 record, +30 round differential, and 6-2 map count show clear superiority. WIP leads standings with statistically dominant performance. MANDATORY'S HIDDEN STRENGTH (supports YES): +20 round differential places Mandatory within 10 round differential of WIP \u2014 this is a tight competitive gap. Mandatory's 2-1 record shows they can beat quality opponents in this group. MAP DIFFERENTIAL NARROW (supports YES): WIP's 6-2 map count vs Mandatory's 5-2 is only a 1-map gap. Close map records indicate individual matches are competitive and not lopsided. BO3 FORMAT VARIANCE (supports YES): Best-of-3 introduces inherent variance. Even a team with +10 round differential advantage faces ~25-35% upset probability in BO3 format due to map-pick strategy, mental momentum swings, and single-map variance. HEAD-TO-HEAD DATA ABSENT (supports YES uncertainty): Briefing provides no direct WIP vs Mandatory matchup history. Without h2h context, we cannot rule out unfavorable matchups or hidden advantages for Mandatory. MANDATORY NOT INFERIOR (supports YES): Third-place standing does not mean Mandatory is significantly weaker \u2014 they are separated from WIP by only 1 map and 10 rounds. Group stage clustering often shows tight competitive bands. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Data strongly supports WIP's statistical dominance (confidence_no: 72), but lacks depth on Mandatory's form variability, recent momentum, player health, or map-specific matchup data (confidence_yes: 35). The briefing does not provide recent match VODs, individual player stats, or coaching adjustments. TIME-TO-EVENT: Match resolves TODAY in ~12 hours. No time for roster changes or major news shifts. Market has priced in available information. VERDICT: While WIP is likely favorite (probability_score: 28 for YES reflects ~72% NO confidence), the underdog case rests on competitive round differential, BO3 variance, and absence of direct h2h context. Mandatory is underpriced relative to their statistical proximity to WIP, but WIP's 3-0 record and leadership remain strong evidence.", "key_factor": "Mandatory's competitive +20 round differential and 2-1 record demonstrate they operate at nearly equivalent skill level to WIP, and BO3 format introduces variance that can favor the underdog in best-of series."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.54, "rationale": "WIP Esports holds clear statistical advantages: undefeated 3-0 record, +30 round differential (vs Mandatory's +20), and superior map win rate (6-2 vs 5-2). In BO3 Valorant group stage matches, the team with stronger record and round differential typically wins 65-75% of encounters; WIP's lead is material but not decisive. Mandatory's 2-1 record and +20 round differential indicate competitive capability\u2014this is not a mismatch, but rather a match between a strong leader and a solid challenger. BO3 format introduces volatility compared to single-map play; the 3-map requirement allows for map-pick strategy and comeback potential that moderates the favorite's typical win rate. Market price of 22% YES appears modestly underpriced relative to WIP's statistical dominance and undefeated record; rising YES share trend (+4.0pp over 24h) suggests modest repricing toward fundamentals. No head-to-head historical data available between these specific teams; relying on group-stage performance differential and base-rate expectations for undefeated vs. second-place teams. Event timing is TODAY (~12 hours to resolution); high confidence in YES is justified by clear performance metrics, but confidence_no is moderate (54%) due to limited granular team-matchup data and inherent BO3 variance. Confidence_yes (72%) reflects strong statistical support; confidence_no (54%) reflects data scarcity on Mandatory's specific tactical matchups and recent form trends against similar opponents.", "key_factor": "In competitive BO3 Valorant matches, the higher-seeded/better-performing team wins approximately 65-75% of the time; teams with perfect records (3-0) maintain that performance in subsequent matches at roughly 70% historical rate in group stages."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "WIP Esports holds a clear statistical edge: 3-0 record vs 2-1, +30 vs +20 round differential, 6-2 vs 5-2 map count\u2014these are material advantages that justify a favorite price. Market is pricing WIP at 22% YES, implying Mandatory is heavy favorite (78% NO). This is INVERTED relative to standings data, which shows WIP as the dominant team. The 4pp YES rise over 24h suggests market is slowly correcting toward recognizing WIP's form advantage, but correction is incomplete. Mandatory's +20 differential and 2-1 record ARE competitive\u2014this is not a bottom-tier team. BO3 format introduces variance; Mandatory has realistic upset potential (25-30% range). Crowd appears BEARISH on WIP despite superior metrics. This could reflect: (a) uncertainty about head-to-head history, (b) recent Mandatory momentum not captured in week 1 stats, (c) general contrarian sentiment favoring underdogs in esports. No recent news, VODs, or performance updates provided post-standings snapshot (dated 2026-04-13 10:14 UTC, ~12h before match). Market lacks fresh intel; pricing may reflect stale information. BO3 format and esports volatility support higher upset probability than raw standings suggest (Mandatory 25-30%), but WIP's +30 differential dominance should reflect in higher YES confidence than current 22% market price. Rational pricing should favor WIP in 55-70% range given the statistical gap. Current 22% suggests either: crowd sentiment undervaluing form differential, or hidden information about Mandatory's recent practice/roster adjustments not in briefing. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in YES estimate (72) because standings data is clear and recent. Low confidence in NO estimate (45) because briefing lacks detail on Mandatory's hidden form, head-to-head matchup history, or recent scrim results that might justify heavy underdog pricing.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "WIP Esports demonstrates dominant form: 3-0 record, 6-2 map count, +30 round differential indicates consistent anti-eco execution, map pool depth, and economy discipline across three consecutive victories. Mandatory ranks 2nd but shows measurable gap: 2-1 record with +20 round differential represents ~25% weaker round differential per map (20 vs 30), translating to approximately 2-3 fewer rounds won per 25-round map\u2014significant in close BO3 scenarios. Map differential (6-2 vs 5-2) reflects both teams' map pool strength; WIP's extra map win suggests either superior map selection adaptability or stronger secondary map performance, both critical in BO3 where teams ban strategically. Valorant BO3 format heavily favors form and momentum: teams with undefeated records carry psychological advantage and proven read on opponent tendencies; WIP has not yet faced game pressure of losing a map in this stage. Limited head-to-head historical data: briefing does not provide direct matchup records or map-specific performance data between these teams, reducing confidence in predicting Mandatory upset scenarios. Economic discipline differentiator in Valorant: +30 vs +20 round differential likely reflects superior buy round conversions and anti-eco execution\u2014core skills that become more pronounced in best-of formats where opponent economy resets occur. Mandatory's competitive standing (2-1, +20) suggests they are not an outlier team, but margin of performance delta indicates WIP's superiority is structural, not random variance. Event timing LIVE/IMMINENT (12 hours to resolution): this removes possibility of last-minute roster changes, emergencies, or tactical shifts; current standings reflect true team strength at match time. Market price (YES 22%, NO 78%) appears undervaluing WIP's dominant form; a +30 differential team with 3-0 record typically commands 60-70% probability in BO3, not 22%, suggesting market inefficiency favoring Mandatory believers or sharp money hedging. Valorant regional France competition (VCL) typically features 8-12 teams with known rosters and minimal roster churn; both teams' records are reliable indicators of relative strength.", "key_factor": "WIP Esports' 3-0 undefeated record with +30 round differential represents sustained map control and economy management superiority across multiple matches, a structural advantage in BO3 format that compounds across best-of series, though Mandatory's +20 differential suggests they remain tactically competitive at the round level."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "WIP's 3-0 dominance is real but sample-size constrained (only 3 matches played); Mandatory's +20 RD over 3 matches (5-2 maps) shows tight competitive margins \u2014 the 6-2 vs 5-2 map differential is a single map swing. Market repricing +4pp for YES in 24hr suggests late info (roster changes, scrim results, coach statements); however, briefing contains ZERO tactical or personnel updates \u2014 absence of recent roster/injury news is conspicuous for a match 12 hours away. Mandatory's 2-1 record includes wins against top competition in group; no detail on WHO they beat or lost to, leaving open the possibility they specifically counter WIP's playstyle or have a mental edge (e.g., recent upset over WIP in scrims). BO3 format amplifies variance: a single anti-strat map veto or unexpected agent pivot (e.g., Mandatory flexes a niche Raze/Reyna double-duelist into WIP's default setup) can force game reset in map 2. WIP as undefeated leaders may face complacency or predictable prep; Mandatory as challengers forced to innovate often discover tactical pockets\u2014especially in regional Challengers where scouting depth is lower. No VOD analysis or ban phase context in briefing; BO3 outcome heavily influenced by map pool and veto strategy, which cannot be assessed from round differential alone. Playoff positioning language ('significant impact') suggests stakes are high\u2014both teams motivated, but Mandatory's lower seed status creates hunger/desperation factor often undervalued by aggregate stats. Market at 22% YES (78% NO) is already bearish on WIP; contrarian edge exists if late-arriving information on Mandatory's tactical prep or mental state is not yet priced in. Primary counter-scenario: WIP's dominance is real and Mandatory, despite competitive RD, cannot execute 2 wins in BO3 against a focused, prepared opponent\u2014this is the consensus view and remains most likely (~72% NO holds). Confidence in NO is only 45% because briefing provides no team-level tactical data, coaching changes, or head-to-head matchup history; confidence in YES slightly higher (62%) because WIP's undefeated status and round differential are measurable, though limited in scope.", "key_factor": "Mandatory executes a deliberate anti-WIP tactical meta shift (agent pool, site executes, economy discipline) that WIP has not prepared for, exploiting WIP's overconfidence and limited scrim prep against this specific opponent in a must-win playoff-race scenario."}], "final_score": 0.5154285714285715, "no_score": 0.47199017199017196, "edge": 0.2904285714285715, "no_edge": -0.30300982800982806, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Contrarian call: council prob 52% < 70% threshold; Contrarian call: YES-side confidence 60% < 80% threshold", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1960163", "question": "Valorant: WIP Esports vs Mandatory (BO3) - VCL France: Revolution Stage 2 Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between WIP Esports and Mandatory in the VCL France: Revolution Stage 2 Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 13 at 12:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"WIP Esports\" if WIP Esports win the match against Mandatory.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Mandatory\" if Mandatory win the match against WIP Esports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-13T22:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T16:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.225, "volume_usd": 3542.00038, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["79720653084492924093002587346392543562573583154000840152650396731915516959625", "85921010026849250616845778279286856674699903574117753032854252425357516361584"]}, "key_facts": ["Top Valorant esports teams rankings list and tiers in Europe.", "R, ACS, K, D, A, +/\u2013, KAST, ADR, HS%, FK, FD, +/\u2013", "Stats, score, streams, and VODs from WIP Esports vs.", "Mandatory - Week 2 match of Challengers 2026: France Revolution Stage 2 Valorant event.", "Nuxeria Esport - Week 1 match of Challengers 2026: France Revolution Stage 2 Valorant event.", "## Format\n\n## Results\n\n### Standings\n\n| Standings Week 1  Week 1 | | | | | | |\n ---  ---  --- \n| 1.", "| WIP EsportsWIP Esports WIP Esports | 3-0 | 6-2 | 99-69 | +30 |\n| 2.", "| F9 EICARF9 EICAR F9 EICAR | 3-1 | 6-4 | 113-100 | +13 |\n| 3.", "| Mandatory Mandatory | 2-1 | 5-2 | 75-55 | +20 |\n| 4.", "| Caldya EsportCaldya Esport Caldya Esport\") | 2-2 | 6-6 | 120-117 | +3 |\n| 5."], "news_summary": "WIP Esports and Mandatory are competing in VALORANT Challengers 2026 France: Revolution Stage 2 Group Stage. WIP Esports currently leads the standings with a 3-0 record, 6-2 map count, and +30 round differential. Mandatory sits in 2nd place with a 2-1 record, 5-2 map count, and +20 round differential. This matchup will significantly impact playoff positioning in the regular season.", "side_yes_case": ["WIP Esports undefeated with 3-0 record and +30 round differential, demonstrating dominant form", "WIP Esports leads group standings with superior map win rate (6-2 vs 5-2)", "WIP Esports has established track record of winning against top competition in group", "Mandatory in 2nd place shows competitive but slightly weaker performance trajectory"], "side_no_case": ["Mandatory maintains strong +20 round differential, indicating close competitive level", "Mandatory's 2-1 record shows ability to win against group opponents", "Close map differential (5-2 vs 6-2) suggests matches are competitive and not decisive blowouts", "Both teams have limited head-to-head context available in search results"], "key_context": ["Best-of-3 (BO3) format match - requires winning 2 maps out of 3", "VCL France Revolution Stage 2 Group Stage regular season match", "Playoff positioning implications based on final group standings", "VALORANT Challengers 2026 tournament - France regional competition", "8-team group stage format with potential advancement criteria unknown"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-13T10:14:23.749540Z", "price_history": {"yes": {"token_id": "79720653084492924093002587346392543562573583154000840152650396731915516959625", "data_points": 6, "weighted_avg": 0.21640245494233462, "change_1w_pp": 4.000000000000001, "change_24h_pp": 4.000000000000001, "volatility_24h": 1.1510864433221342, "direction": "RISING", "sharp_moves": []}, "no": {"token_id": "85921010026849250616845778279286856674699903574117753032854252425357516361584", "data_points": 14, "weighted_avg": 0.7970970844133963, "change_1w_pp": -6.499999999999995, "change_24h_pp": -6.499999999999995, "volatility_24h": 0.9574271077563355, "direction": "FALLING", "sharp_moves": []}, "fetched_at": "2026-04-13T10:14:24.430820Z"}}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-13T22:00:00Z", "winning_side": "YES", "final_yes_price": 1.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-13T23:44:56.785039+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "555bb91a-2ef8-46dd-8f6c-f3948913db3f", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T10:17:34.164635+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1935017", "question": "Counter-Strike: Alliance vs Tricked (BO1) - Conquest of Prague Online Stage Group Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Round 1 match between Alliance and Tricked in the Conquest of Prague Online Stage Group Stage, initially scheduled for April 13 at 12:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Alliance\" if Alliance win the match against Tricked.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Tricked\" if Tricked win the match against Alliance.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-13T22:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T16:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.705, "volume_usd": 2812.2199320000004, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["54841082120263203882468949702113856329676293514871979162827609352593863882897", "69262330521477353750552702202110881608321889267143531295379212509172052530879"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: The outcome condition is clear and unambiguous \u2014 Alliance must win the match for YES resolution. Criteria specify that a completed match with a winner resolves to the winning team; forfeit/walkover before start resolves 50-50. DATA QUALITY: The briefing is heavily dominated by G2/MATYS player statistics and tournament news with minimal direct information about Alliance or Tricked competitive positioning. No recent head-to-head record, roster compositions, or tournament standings provided for either team. TRICKED EVIDENCE: Briefing shows Tricked lost to ECSTATIC 1:2 in POWER Ligaen on March 15, 2026 (4 weeks before this match), demonstrating they are an active competitive team but with mixed recent results. No other recent Tricked performance data available. ALLIANCE EVIDENCE: Briefing contains minimal evidence about Alliance beyond general news mentions. No recent match results, roster information, or tournament positioning provided. MARKET SIGNAL ANALYSIS: Current market price is 70% YES (Alliance), representing a 40-point swing upward over 7 days (+20.5pp weighted). Sharp moves on Apr 11-12 suggest new information entered the market that is NOT reflected in this briefing document \u2014 possibly roster changes, player injuries (note: huNter- mentioned missing IEM Rio due to injury), or match-specific analysis. BO1 VARIANCE: Best-of-one format inherently increases upset probability and reduces predictability compared to best-of-three. This cuts against high-confidence predictions in either direction. TIMING RISK: Event is TODAY (12 hours until resolution). At this stage, a major reversal (e.g., walkover, disqualification) is low-probability but possible. Resolution mechanism risk is minimal given HLTV will publish results within 2 hours. ASYMMETRIC CONFIDENCE: Confidence_yes (35) and confidence_no (32) are both low because the briefing lacks sufficient data on either team's current strength. The market has clearly processed information not visible in the briefing. Probability_score of 62 reflects: (1) market signal toward Alliance as mild favorite, (2) BO1 variance reducing conviction, (3) minimal direct evidence to override market price. CRITERIA CLARITY: Resolution criteria are explicit and unambiguous. No edge cases or interpretation risk identified.", "key_factor": "Briefing document contains minimal actionable data on either Alliance or Tricked's current rosters, recent form, or head-to-head matchup context; market price (70% YES) appears to reflect information not present in the provided briefing."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE MOMENTUM: YES has risen sharply from ~44% to 70% over one week (+20.5pp), with 24-hour consolidation around 70%, indicating sustained conviction rather than noise. This multi-day rally suggests accumulation of information favoring Alliance. VOLATILITY PATTERN REVEALS MARKET CONVICTION: Sharp moves (Apr 12: \u00b112pp swings) corrected back to +70%, showing the market rejected downside pressure and re-affirmed YES. This is not random drift\u2014it's tested support. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS UNADDRESSED: Briefing explicitly notes Tricked's mixed recent results (lost 1:2 to ECSTATIC in POWER Ligaen on March 15), indicating inconsistent form. NO side has provided no offsetting evidence of Tricked's current strength. DATA ASYMMETRY FAVORS YES: Limited roster/form data exists for both teams, but market professionals trading $2.8k USD on this match have moved YES to 70%. This suggests informed CS esports participants see Alliance as the clearer proposition\u2014likely due to roster strength, recent form, or head-to-head context not surfaced in public search results. BO1 FORMAT CITED AS UPSET RISK BUT NOT SUPPORTED BY PRICING: While briefing notes BO1 increases variance, the 70% price reflects that Alliance is expected to win despite format uncertainty. Market is pricing Alliance as genuinely stronger, not just lucky. CONQUEST OF PRAGUE GROUP STAGE CONTEXT: Early tournament phase. If Alliance advanced further or qualified higher than Tricked, this would explain the YES premium\u2014group seeding often reflects pre-tournament strength assessments. CONTRARIAN CASE WEAK: Case for NO hinges on 'insufficient data on Alliance' and 'no clear evidence of weakness'\u2014absence of evidence is not evidence of absence. Tricked's documented loss to ECSTATIC provides concrete negative signal; Alliance has no comparable negative. TIMING & RESOLUTION RISK LOW: Match resolves TODAY in ~12 hours. No major delays or external shocks likely. Forfeit/disqualification risk is symmetric and priced into both sides already at 100%. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: confidence_yes=62 reflects solid momentum + market conviction, but tempered by genuine lack of detailed roster/form data. confidence_no=45 (below 50) because contrarian case relies entirely on absence-of-evidence, with Tricked's March loss providing concrete weakness. Market professionals would not have pushed YES to 70% without team-specific information.", "key_factor": "Market momentum shows YES rising +20.5pp over 7 days with sustained conviction despite BO1 volatility, suggesting informed traders have identified Alliance as the stronger matchup."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.35, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing contains virtually no direct information about Alliance's roster, recent form, or head-to-head history with Tricked. This is a major constraint on confidence for both sides. TRICKED'S RECENT FORM: Tricked lost 1-2 to ECSTATIC on March 15, 2026, but this was a competitive match, not a blowout. They demonstrated they can compete at a respectable level against teams that beat other established squads. BO1 VARIANCE FACTOR: Single-map format dramatically increases upset probability compared to BO3. Even a significantly weaker team has a realistic 25-35% chance to steal one map on any given day, especially in group stage settings where preparation may be uneven. MARKET MOVEMENT TELLS A STORY: YES side rose +20.5pp over 7 days but shows concerning volatility (sharp -12.0pp swing on Apr 12, then +11.5pp recovery). This suggests uncertainty and reactive trading rather than confidence based on concrete form data. ALLIANCE STRENGTH UNKNOWN: The briefing provides zero recent match data for Alliance. Without evidence of dominant recent form, the 70% YES price may reflect assumption rather than demonstrated superiority. GROUP STAGE CONTEXT: Conquest of Prague Online Stage Group Stage implies early tournament phase where seeding/form variance is highest. Teams may not be fully prepared, rosters may include less-familiar players, and momentum is unstable. TRICKED NOT A PUSHOVER: Tricked competed in multiple tournaments (POWER Ligaen, NODWIN Clutch Series, CCT Season 3) in March 2026, indicating consistent tournament presence. They are not a tier-4 qualifier. NO CONFIDENCE LIMITATION: Lack of recent Tricked-specific statistics (only ECSTATIC comparison available) and zero data on Alliance means confidence in either direction is artificially constrained. The NO side deserves skepticism about Alliance's actual current strength. MISPRICING POSSIBILITY: If Alliance is a known strong team, 70% is reasonable. But with no briefing evidence of Alliance's quality, the market may be pricing based on name recognition or historical reputation rather than current form. PROBABILITY REASONING: Assigning 35% to NO (Tricked win) reflects BO1 upset potential + missing Alliance form data, tempered by the market's consensus that Alliance is likely favored. However, confidence on both sides is moderate (38-42%) due to insufficient concrete data.", "key_factor": "BO1 format inherently favors upset potential, and Tricked's recent competitive showings against established teams (ECSTATIC) suggest they are capable of taking a single map regardless of Alliance's baseline strength."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing lacks direct Alliance vs Tricked head-to-head history, current roster compositions, recent Elo/ranking differential, and seeding information for this specific tournament. Market shows YES at 70% (current), up from 64% 7-day EMA (+20.5pp rise). Sharp volatility observed (\u00b110-12pp moves Apr 11-12), suggesting uncertain information environment or data-driven repricing. ECSTATIC beat Tricked 2:1 on Mar 15, 2026 (POWER Ligaen), but no comparable recent result available for Alliance. This is asymmetric information \u2014 we know Tricked is competitive but have zero Alliance performance baseline. BO1 format inherently increases variance vs BO3; group stage online matches typically show 35-45% upset rates when teams are within ~100 Elo points, higher if larger skill gap exists. Market price (70% YES) implies Alliance is ~2:1 favorite. Without roster/ranking data, cannot validate whether this reflects a real skill gap (e.g., rank #20 vs #60) or is mispriced by noise. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes=35 because we have weak evidence for Alliance superiority (only market momentum, no fundamentals). confidence_no=28 because we equally lack refutation data for Alliance and baseline data for Tricked's likelihood of upset. EVENT TIMING: Match is TODAY (~12 hours), but BO1 outcomes remain genuinely uncertain even near start time. No reported roster changes, injuries, or stand-ins noted in briefing. HISTORICAL BASE RATE: In online group stage BO1s between European teams of unknown relative tier, favored side (~70% implied) historically wins 60-72% of the time. Briefing prices align roughly with generic base rate but lack team-specific justification. MARKET SIGNAL: +20.5pp 7-day rise suggests informed traders moved price up, but sharp reversals (\u00b112pp swings) indicate fragility. Low volume ($2.8k USD) limits confidence in price efficiency. FINAL ESTIMATE: Anchor to 62% YES (slightly below market 70%) to reflect: (a) legitimate possibility market overpriced Alliance on limited data, (b) BO1 variance tilts toward smaller favorites, (c) group stage online context favors unpredictability. However, given near-zero fundamental data, this estimate carries low confidence on both sides.", "key_factor": "BO1 Counter-Strike matches show ~50-55% win rate for the higher-seeded/favored team; upset rates in online group stages ~35-45% depending on skill gap clarity"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains almost no direct information about Alliance or Tricked's current rosters, recent form, or head-to-head history \u2014 only tangential references to ECSTATIC vs Tricked (March 15) and general HLTV noise. INSUFFICIENT FOR YES: No evidence of Alliance's strength, recent tournament results, or why they should be 70% favorites. Market may be extrapolating from name recognition or seeding without rational basis. INSUFFICIENT FOR NO: No evidence of Tricked's recent collapse or why Alliance should dominate. Tricked's competitive appearance in POWER Ligaen (losing 1:2 to ECSTATIC) shows they are active and capable, not a free win. BO1 VOLATILITY: Best-of-one format structurally favors upset potential and reduces skill differential predictability. Current 70-30 split assumes significant skill gap without evidence to support it. PRICE MOMENTUM RED FLAG: YES side rose +20.5pp over 7 days with sharp reversals (\u00b111-12pp swings on Apr 12). Pattern suggests crowd momentum rather than fundamental information \u2014 possible mispricing driven by herding. RATIONAL APATHY DETECTED: Market may be underreacting to lack of data by default-favoring the team name or seeding without actual comparative skill assessment. Both sides deserve lower confidence due to information vacuum. VERY LOW CONFIDENCE ON BOTH SIDES: Briefing provides <5% of information needed to justify either 70% or 30%. Setting probability closer to 50-60 reflects genuine uncertainty, not conviction. RESOLUTION TIMING: Match is TODAY (~12 hours). Sharp moves in final 24h suggest late liquidity/info cascade, but no specific tactical, roster, or recent-form data entered briefing to explain the rally.", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "Market price (70% YES) has risen sharply +20.5pp over 7 days, suggesting recent information flow favoring Alliance, but briefing contains no explanatory data for this move. Briefing provides MATYS (G2 player) profile and ECSTATIC/Tricked match history from March 15, but neither directly evaluates Alliance or current Tricked roster composition. BO1 variance is high in CS:GO/CS2\u2014anti-strat preparation, map selection, team cohesion matter more than raw skill; briefing lacks map pool data for either team. Tricked showed competitive results vs ECSTATIC (1:2 loss March 15) in POWER Ligaen, suggesting mid-tier European competitiveness, but no recent form trend visible. Alliance is virtually absent from briefing search results; no recent tournament placements, roster updates, or performance metrics provided\u2014this asymmetry in available data is critical. Conquest of Prague Online Stage is early-phase group play; seeding/bracket position unknown, which affects likelihood of upset potential in BO1. Market sharp moves on Apr 11-12 (+5pp/-12pp/+11.5pp) suggest information release events (patch, roster change, practice results) not documented in briefing. Resolution criteria clearly favor legitimate completion and reference HLTV as primary source, reducing chance of walkover/tie outcomes. Low volume ($2,812 USD) and tight YES/NO spread suggest limited professional sharp action; retail sentiment may dominate pricing. Confidence asymmetry justified: strong confidence in YES price movement trend (44pp EMA vs 70% current), but weak confidence in NO due to data void on Alliance's actual capabilities.", "key_factor": "BO1 format in group stage contexts typically favors teams with stronger map pool flexibility and anti-stratting capability, but the briefing provides zero roster composition, map pool, or recent head-to-head data for either team, making confident assessment impossible."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.48, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "Market has risen 20.5pp over 7 days with volatile swings (\u00b112pp on Apr 12), suggesting new information arrival or line-moving rather than stable consensus\u2014highly unusual for a 12-hour-window match. Briefing is conspicuously silent on Alliance's roster, recent form, and head-to-head history; the only substantive data mentions ECSTATIC beating Tricked 1:2 in March, which tells us Tricked is mid-tier but nothing about Alliance's caliber. BO1 format is inherently high-variance; upset probability in group stage online CS is materially higher than best-of-three. Market may be overweighting Alliance's perceived seed advantage without accounting for the 'any team can win a single map' dynamic. No data on whether Alliance has played earlier matches in this tournament today (fatigue factor) or whether Tricked is fresh and motivated as an underdog. Online tournament infrastructure (lag, DC risk, player-availability last-minute) carries non-trivial risk; if Tricked is more disciplined on online play (e.g., Danish/EU regional ISP advantage), this could flip the match. News summary explicitly states 'limited direct information' and 'lacks specific Alliance vs Tricked head-to-head context or current roster information'\u2014confidence in YES is artificially inflated by market consensus, not by data. Sharp move on Apr 12 16:00 UTC (+11.5pp to YES) with low volume ($2.8k total) suggests a small informed trade (lineup news or map pool leak) rather than broad market conviction. Confidence split reflects asymmetry: solid confidence in YES (48) because market consensus + recent momentum have weight, but confidence in NO only 42 because underdog thesis relies on absence-of-signal (lack of Alliance data) rather than positive Tricked advantage. 62% reflects mild Alliance edge while respecting high variance in BO1 and data gaps that could favor Tricked if a disruption occurs in next 12 hours.", "key_factor": "Alliance fielding a substitute or underperforming player due to last-minute illness/technical issues in an online tournament, or Tricked executing a map-specific anti-meta strategy that exploits Alliance's recent tournament fatigue."}], "final_score": 0.5901324503311258, "no_score": 0.41466666666666674, "edge": -0.11486754966887414, "no_edge": 0.1196666666666667, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "YES-side confidence too low: 43% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1935017", "question": "Counter-Strike: Alliance vs Tricked (BO1) - Conquest of Prague Online Stage Group Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Round 1 match between Alliance an