{"run_id": "53321843-2e36-4a3e-b18a-42dcc45027f5", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T10:18:19.591623+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1908559", "question": "LoL: GIANTX vs Shifters (BO3) - LEC Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between GIANTX and Shifters in the LEC Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 13 at 1:15PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"GIANTX\" if GIANTX win the match against Shifters.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Shifters\" if Shifters win the match against GIANTX.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-13T23:15:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T17:15:00Z", "yes_price": 0.805, "volume_usd": 53086.18831399998, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["2186437101677581535076283054463917107503215772236448502107470133320617094336", "46652673040091135463169415645149680421049685217394512723308420428150192732634"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.76, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "GIANTX holds a 2-1 record (Week 2) and sits in 2nd place in LEC standings, demonstrating early-season competitive form. Shifters' specific record and recent performance is unavailable in the briefing, creating significant information asymmetry. Market currently prices YES at 80% and has been relatively stable (EMA 84%, 7-day change +5.5pp), suggesting consistent backing for GIANTX. Recent price movement shows 24-hour decline of -6.0pp on YES (slight profit-taking or minor doubt), but overall trend remains bullish for GIANTX. A BO3 format favors the stronger prepared team; GIANTX's mid-table standing is respectable but not dominant, leaving room for upset. No direct head-to-head data, recent roster changes, or form analysis is provided for either team in the briefing. Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (resolves in ~13 hours); sharp late moves are unlikely given match is hours away, so current 80% YES reflects settled market consensus. Market depth is moderate ($53k volume), suggesting reasonable but not exceptional liquidity. The 80% YES price implies Shifters have ~20% chance\u2014not impossible for an LEC partner team, but GIANTX's superior recorded standing justifies higher confidence. Reducing YES probability slightly from market price (76 vs 80) to account for unknown Shifters performance and inherent BO3 variance. Confidence in YES is moderately high (72) due to GIANTX's standing, but confidence in NO is low (38) due to complete absence of Shifters performance data in briefing.", "key_factor": "Insufficient performance data on Shifters limits confidence in the NO side; market pricing appears reasonable but could shift sharply on new team performance information before match start."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.76, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "GIANTX holds a 2-1 record placing them second in LEC standings after only Week 2, indicating consistent team quality and competitive execution early in the season. Market pricing at 80% for YES reflects confidence in GIANTX's demonstrated form; the 24-hour dip of -6.0pp appears to be normal volatility rather than fundamental deterioration. Shifters' specific performance record is absent from the briefing despite being an official LEC partner team, suggesting they lack the early-season success that GIANTX has shown. The CASE FOR NO relies entirely on Shifters' organizational legitimacy as a partner team, not on actual performance data\u2014a weak counter-narrative given GIANTX's measurable 2-1 record. GIANTX's positioning ahead of most of the field (only behind Natus Vincere 2-0) in a competitive ten-team league signals they are a mid-to-upper tier competitor, not a marginal squad. The BO3 format favors the stronger team; GIANTX's demonstrated consistency across multiple wins provides confidence they can secure at least one of three games. Event timing (TODAY, ~13 hours to resolution) leaves minimal room for narrative reversal; the market has settled near 80% after a week of price discovery. Market volume of $53K is adequate, suggesting informed pricing rather than illiquidity distortion. Confidence in YES is high (72) because GIANTX's record is concrete; confidence in NO is low (38) because Shifters' performance is completely opaque in the briefing, making it impossible to mount a strong counter-case beyond institutional legitimacy.", "key_factor": "GIANTX's 2-1 record and top-2 standings (second only to Natus Vincere) demonstrates superior early-season performance compared to Shifters' undisclosed record."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "GIANTX's 2-1 record is not dominant\u2014it places them second, but Week 2 results in a 10-team league provide limited predictive power. A 2-1 start does not indicate dominance in BO3 formats. The briefing provides ZERO performance metrics for Shifters: no wins/losses, no recent match results, no player-level data. This is a critical data gap that makes confidence in the underdog side necessarily low, but it also means we cannot assume GIANTX is clearly superior. Shifters is listed as an official LEC partner team\u2014same organizational tier as GIANTX. Partner status implies equivalent resources, coaching, and infrastructure. No organizational or franchise-level advantage exists for GIANTX. Market pricing at 80% YES reflects heavy confidence in GIANTX, but this pricing appears driven by GIANTX's 2-1 record alone. In early-season BO3 play, a 2-1 record does not justify 80% confidence in a knockout matchup without comparative performance data on the opponent. The briefing notes that INZONE London Clash 2025 (a tournament result) shows GIANTX as runner-up to Fnatic. This is positive form data but is from a prior season tournament\u2014relevance to LEC 2026 Spring is limited. BO3 format introduces variance: even a weaker team has 33% baseline upset potential (win 2-0 or 2-1). GIANTX's 2-1 regular season record does not translate directly to 80% BO3 match win probability without opponent context. Price history shows YES side declined -6.0pp in last 24 hours and sharp moves suggest market volatility. Recent sharp moves (Apr 12 19:00 UTC -7.5pp) indicate uncertainty creeping in closer to match time, potentially reflecting late information or market correction. NO side has been falling over 7 days (-5.0pp), suggesting market consensus has hardened on GIANTX. However, with <13 hours to match and minimal Shifters-specific data, this consensus may reflect lack of information rather than genuine competitive knowledge. The case for YES relies entirely on GIANTX's 2-1 record. The case for NO notes that Shifters' competitive level is completely unknown\u2014this asymmetry in data favors YES confidence but does not justify 80% odds for a BO3 match where opponent quality is opaque. Upset scenario: Shifters could have strong recent form, favorable matchups (top/mid laners), or strategic preparation that the briefing does not capture. LEC matches are often decided by meta adaptation and team synergy, not early-season W-L record alone. Confidence split reflects this asymmetry: HIGH confidence in YES (72%) because GIANTX's 2-1 record is real and documented. LOW confidence in NO (32%) because Shifters' data is absent, limiting ability to build a substantive underdog case beyond 'unknown challenger' logic.", "key_factor": "Shifters' competitive pedigree as an official LEC partner organization and the absence of any performance data suggesting they are significantly weaker than GIANTX's modest 2-1 record."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.68, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "GIANTX holds a 2-1 record and is currently ranked 2nd in LEC standings (Week 2), indicating demonstrated competitive performance against the league field. Shifters' specific record and standing are not provided in briefing; this is a critical data gap that prevents confident assessment of matchup difficulty. Market price (80% YES) is somewhat aggressive relative to limited available information. A 2-1 team vs. an unspecified opponent does not typically justify 80% confidence in BO3 format. Adjusted probability of 72% reflects: (a) GIANTX's documented early success, (b) absence of contradictory data on Shifters' weakness, (c) discount for market overconfidence, (d) BO3 format allows for upset potential vs. single-elimination. LEC is a top-tier professional league with parity among partner teams; 2-1 record is solid but not dominant. Historical base rate for top-2 teams in early-season BO3s against field opponents is ~70%, not 80%. Recent market volatility (6pp swing in 24h, sharp moves on Apr 8-12) suggests some uncertainty or new information; this contradicts 80% pricing if briefing data is current. Confidence in YES (68%) reflects solid data on GIANTX's performance. Confidence in NO (42%) is LOW because Shifters' competitive level is entirely unknown\u2014no record, no recent results provided. If Shifters are legitimately weak (relegated from upper tier or newly promoted), 72% understates GIANTX's edge. If Shifters are equally competitive, 72% is generous to GIANTX. Match resolves in ~13 hours (LIVE/IMMINENT). Reversal of the 72% outcome would require GIANTX roster/coaching failure or Shifters outperforming their standing significantly\u2014possible but not probable. Recommend discount from market price (80\u219272) due to: information asymmetry favoring GIANTX, BO3 format resilience, and absence of data supporting the market's confidence level.", "key_factor": "In LEC regular season BO3 matches, higher-seeded/higher-performing teams (2+ win records) defeat lower-seeded/lower-performing teams approximately 65-75% of the time in early-season matchups where opponent data is sparse."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.76, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "Market price (80% YES) reflects modest information asymmetry favoring GIANTX, consistent with their 2-1 Week 2 record vs. unknown Shifters standing. GIANTX's top-2 positioning (2nd place behind Na'Vi) provides concrete evidence; Shifters' performance data absent from briefing creates valuation uncertainty. Current 80/19 split is NOT crowded exuberance\u2014it appropriately prices GIANTX as favorites while preserving 19-20% upset probability for a known LEC team. Price stability over 7 days (77-84pp EMA range) suggests market has digested available info; no sharp reversals in final 24h indicate equilibrium. Recent volatility (Apr 12 -7.5pp YES) may reflect late uncertainty or position-squaring, but 13-hour window to resolution limits reversal probability. KEY DATA GAP: Shifters' record/standings entirely absent\u2014prevents quantitative edge case assessment. If Shifters are 2-1 or better, market may be overstating GIANTX. BO3 format reduces single-upset risk; best-of-three favors stronger team (GIANTX's 2-1 record), but 1-0 comeback scenarios are plausible. No recent head-to-head results, meta shifts, or roster changes provided to justify 80% as mispriced. Market appears efficiently calibrated to information scarcity. Sentiment is RATIONAL: crowd is not exuberant (80% is reasonable favorite odds, not 90%+) nor panicked (NO at 19% still values Shifters' LEC pedigree). Modest adjustment downward from 80 to 76 reflects Shifters' unknown strength + BO3 reset probability, but high YES confidence (72) justified by GIANTX's concrete standing.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.68, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "GIANTX demonstrated 2-1 record in Week 2 of LEC 2026 Spring, placing them 2nd in standings behind Na'Vi (2-0), indicating early-season momentum and team cohesion. Shifters' specific record, roster quality, and recent performance are absent from briefing\u2014critical gap for competitive esports betting where meta, patch knowledge, and player form are decisive. Market pricing at 80% YES reflects confidence in GIANTX's early advantage, but no team-specific data on Shifters' strengths (e.g., draft flexibility, mid-game macro, team fighting) limits validation of the 80% line. BO3 format favors teams with established read on meta and consistent execution; GIANTX's 2-1 week suggests they've already adapted to current patch. Price history shows -6.0pp drop in YES over 24h and sharp move on Apr 12 (-7.5pp), suggesting late-stage uncertainty or information arrival about team status (injury, roster changes, scrim results). In esports, Week 2 records can be misleading if GIANTX faced weaker opponents; no head-to-head history or strength-of-schedule data provided. Shifters' appearance as 'participating LEC partner team' confirms they meet organizational standards but does not imply competitive equivalence to 2-1 teams. Insufficient data on Shifters prevents robust NO-side confidence; confidence_no set to 35 due to missing roster, record, and recent form.", "key_factor": "Early-season LEC standings (Week 2) are predictive but volatile; GIANTX's 2-1 record reflects limited sample size, and Shifters' competitive standing cannot be reliably assessed from the briefing document, creating asymmetric information favoring the YES side but with moderate confidence."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.71, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "GIANTX's 2-1 record is solid but not dominant\u2014a BO3 format rewards tactical preparation and meta reads, where an underdog with superior map prep or champion pool synergy can steal games. Briefing is conspicuously silent on: (a) Shifters' actual W-L record, recent form trajectory, or momentum; (b) head-to-head matchup history; (c) specific player performances, champion pools, or draft tendencies for either team. Market has experienced sharp reversals (Apr 08 +12pp, Apr 09 -9pp, Apr 12 -7.5pp on YES side), suggesting underlying uncertainty or information asymmetry that isn't fully resolved by standings alone. 80% YES pricing assumes GIANTX's 2-1 record translates to 4:1 odds in a single BO3\u2014this is a significant extrapolation from early-season standings with no win-rate or matchup-specific data. BO3 format is particularly vulnerable to mental/tactical flips: if Shifters enter with a 'nothing to lose' mentality or a recent scrim-driven innovation that counters GIANTX's known draft/playstyle, they can steal map 1, then apply pressure in games 2-3. Absence of Shifters performance data is a critical blind spot\u2014if they are secretly strong (e.g., 1-0 in early weeks, strong week 2 despite limited mentions) or have a roster change/injury recovery that boosts their ceiling, odds are mispriced. Time-to-reversal constraint applies: with ~13 hours to match start, roster news, injury updates, or scrim leaks could emerge that shift the narrative, but market liquidity ($53k) and stable price suggest consensus is partially locked in. Confidence in YES is moderate-to-good (71) because GIANTX's 2-1 standing is real and second-place positioning suggests competitive quality; confidence in NO is deliberately suppressed (45) because Shifters' true competitive level is entirely opaque in the briefing\u2014this asymmetry reflects genuine data risk on the underdog side.", "key_factor": "Shifters execute a surprise meta adaptation or roster adjustment (substitute player, last-minute tactical pivot, or recent scrim results favoring their playstyle) that exploits a GIANTX predictability or champion pool weakness not visible in aggregate standings."}], "final_score": 0.6734545454545454, "no_score": 0.3163773584905661, "edge": -0.13154545454545463, "no_edge": 0.12137735849056613, "recommendation": "BUY YES", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": "LOW MARGIN", "pass_reason": "", "expected_roi": 0.24223602484472043, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1908559", "question": "LoL: GIANTX vs Shifters (BO3) - LEC Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between GIANTX and Shifters in the LEC Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 13 at 1:15PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"GIANTX\" if GIANTX win the match against Shifters.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Shifters\" if Shifters win the match against GIANTX.\n\nI