{"run_id": "68e8c33f-fdf3-4241-a26c-b6349e9256b2", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T10:19:49.203238+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1842267", "question": "Counter-Strike: B8 vs Natus Vincere (BO3) - IEM Rio Group B", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Upper bracket quarterfinal 2 match between B8 and Natus Vincere in the IEM Rio Group B, initially scheduled for April 13 at 10:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"B8\" if B8 win the match against Natus Vincere.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Natus Vincere\" if Natus Vincere win the match against B8.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T00:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T18:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.185, "volume_usd": 71972.28440200009, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["19468732107850826124910683854873553648656766893335941507216915527138203216208", "101687252252173407855874001007234632961004698674586298741585377230015905139695"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.18, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "CONDITION: B8 wins the BO3 match against Natus Vincere in IEM Rio Group B Upper bracket quarterfinal 2. RANKINGS & COMPETITIVE DISPARITY: Na'Vi is #2 globally; B8 is #18. This 16-position gap reflects a tier-1 vs mid-tier matchup with substantial skill differential. STATISTICAL EVIDENCE: Na'Vi's 1.16 rating + 74.5% KAST vs B8's 1.11 rating + 71.4% KAST shows Na'Vi's superior fundamentals across economy management, utility usage, and map control. ROSTER QUALITY: Na'Vi lineup (Aleksib, iM, b1t, w0nderful, makazze) represents established, proven talent. B8 lacks comparable individual player pedigree and international LAN experience. BO3 FORMAT RISK FOR UNDERDOG: Best-of-3 requires consistency across 2-3 maps. Underdogs have lower win probability in extended series vs single-map contests; B8 must win 2 maps against a mechanically superior team. MARKET PRICING ALIGNMENT: YES priced at 18% with 7-day EMA at 19% and stable trajectory suggests market has efficiently priced B8's underdog status based on available information. HISTORICAL PRECEDENT: Head-to-head data from tier-1 vs lower-ranked matchups typically shows ~80-85% win rate for the higher-ranked team in premier tournaments. TRAVEL/PREPARATION PARITY: Both teams are Eastern European; Brazil location affects both equally, no material disadvantage to either. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: Match is TODAY (imminent); HLTV publication within 2 hours is standard; no substantial oracle delay risk. Outcome will trade at market extremes ($0.01/$0.99) within minutes of match conclusion. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Extensive data supports Na'Vi's dominance (ranking, stats, roster quality). B8 upside scenarios (map veto advantage, preparation edge, tactical innovation) are speculative and lack supporting evidence. Confidence_yes=72 (strong NO case) but confidence_no=58 (limited data on B8's specific countermeasures or recent form trends).", "key_factor": "Match timing and resolution source (HLTV within 2 hours) with TODAY deadline suggests outcome will be clear before official resolution, reducing oracle risk materially."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.18, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.92, "rationale": "NO SIDE (FAVORED) \u2014 STRUCTURAL DOMINANCE: Na'Vi is ranked #2 globally with demonstrably superior stats (1.16 rating, 74.5% KAST) vs B8's 1.11 rating and 71.4% KAST. In BO3 format, consistency across multiple maps strongly favors the higher-ranked, more fundamentally sound team. NO SIDE \u2014 ROSTER PEDIGREE: Na'Vi's lineup (Aleksib in-game leading, supported by elite peers) has proven success at major LANs. B8, ranked #18, lacks equivalent roster stability and international tournament experience required to compete at tier-1 level. NO SIDE \u2014 RANKING DISPARITY: A 16-position gap in global rankings (#2 vs #18) reflects real skill differential. Historical data strongly shows tier-1 teams defeat lower-ranked challengers in head-to-head matchups, especially in BO3 where map pool mastery and adaptability separate tiers. NO SIDE \u2014 BO3 CONSISTENCY REQUIREMENT: Best-of-3 format demands consistency across map vetoes, side selection, and anti-stratting. Na'Vi's tier-1 infrastructure and coaching provide advantages B8 cannot replicate with lower-ranked roster composition. YES SIDE (UNDERDOG) \u2014 WEAK CASE: The briefing contains no evidence of B8 form improvement, recent upsets, player transfers, or map-specific strengths that would enable them to overcome a #2-ranked team. No tactical innovations or recent wins vs tier-1 teams are documented. YES SIDE \u2014 REGIONAL RIVALRY IRRELEVANT: While both teams are Ukrainian/Eastern European, regional history does not offset the 16-ranking gap. No head-to-head record is provided that would suggest B8 has competitive history vs Na'Vi. YES SIDE \u2014 TRAVEL/LOGISTICS MINIMAL FACTOR: Both teams face identical Brazil travel conditions. This cannot be a significant B8 advantage when Na'Vi's superior fundamentals and experience mitigate logistical disadvantages. MARKET PRICING VALIDATION: The 82% NO price reflects accurate consensus. The 18% YES price is generous to B8; upsets at this ranking disparity (Tier-1 vs Tier-3) occur <20% of the time in professional CS. Market is appropriately calibrated. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in NO (92%) because briefing data strongly supports tier-1 superiority across all metrics. Confidence in YES is only 28% due to complete absence of mitigating factors or B8 strengths that could justify their underdog status beyond random variance.", "key_factor": "Natus Vincere's #2 global ranking, superior individual skill (1.16 rating vs 1.11), and proven tier-1 LAN pedigree create a structural advantage that B8's #18 ranking and weaker fundamentals cannot overcome in a BO3 format."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.18, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.82, "rationale": "MARKET CONTEXT: YES is priced at 18% ($0.18), reflecting strong market consensus for NO. Market has been stable (\u00b11pp over 7 days, low volatility 0.7pp/hr), suggesting efficient pricing with minimal uncertainty. FAVORITE'S STRENGTHS (NO = Na'Vi at 82%): Natus Vincere ranked #2 globally with elite roster (Aleksib, iM, b1t, w0nderful, makazze). Recent stats show 1.16 rating and 74.5% KAST \u2014 superior to B8's 1.11 rating and 71.4% KAST. Proven LAN experience at major tournaments. Significant 16-rank gap (#2 vs #18) reflects real competitive disparity. UNDERDOG'S CASE (YES = B8): B8 is a Ukrainian team with regional rivalry knowledge of Na'Vi's playstyle and tendencies. BO3 format offers multiple map opportunities \u2014 any single map can be stolen through superior preparation, niche map picks, or anti-strategies. B8's 1.11 rating is not dramatically worse than Na'Vi's 1.16 (only 0.05 gap) \u2014 within margin where upsets occur. Briefing lacks head-to-head historical matchup data between these specific rosters, leaving open possibility of unknown competitive history favoring B8. CRITICAL DATA GAPS: Briefing provides minimal concrete evidence about B8's recent tournament results, map pool strengths, or specific matchup history vs Na'Vi. No information on B8's preparation level, roster chemistry changes, or recent form trajectory. News section contains mostly incoherent or unrelated tournament gossip (FUT, JW, Vitality references) with no direct B8 analysis. This severely limits upside case for YES. REALISTIC UPSET SCENARIO: B8 could steal 2-1 through: (1) dominating a specific map B8 specializes in while Na'Vi under-prepares, (2) early-tournament rust from Na'Vi despite their ranking, (3) psychological underdog advantage or tactical surprise. However, briefing provides ZERO evidence B8 possesses any of these factors. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in NO (82%) because briefing provides multiple concrete metrics (ranking, rating, KAST, LAN experience) all favoring Na'Vi. Low confidence in YES (28%) because briefing lacks concrete evidence of B8's strengths \u2014 only shows their weaknesses. No recent tournament wins, upset potential data, or map pool advantages mentioned for B8. Market price of 18% appears justified by data scarcity favoring the underdog. TIMING CONSIDERATION: Event is TODAY (resolves in ~14 hours). Match is live/imminent. Market pricing is stable with no