team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T00:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T18:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.385, "volume_usd": 1463.798634, "category": "dota-2", "clob_token_ids": ["51651465027573201330495948793160352460076975087766791150728752226847028674350", "64852701271144935704715448290110316446076789209597064180610464630058078380510"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "CONDITION TO BE MET: Virtus.pro wins the BO3 match against MOUZ in DreamLeague S29 WEU CQ Playoffs (scheduled April 13, 2:00 PM ET; market resolves ~14 hours from briefing timestamp). CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains heavily fragmented information mixing Overwatch, World of Tanks, and Dota 2 records. No usable Virtus.pro vs MOUZ head-to-head data provided. VIRTUS.PRO EVIDENCE: Documented wins vs Zero Tenacity in recent DreamLeague S29 WEU CQ matches (Feb 10, 2026 and undated matches); shows demonstrated capability in qualifier format. However, these are against a specific opponent (Z10), not MOUZ. MOUZ EVIDENCE: Search results lack any current form data, recent tournament results, roster composition, or performance metrics for MOUZ. No comparable match history provided. MARKET PRICING CONTEXT: YES = 38% / NO = 62% suggests market belief in MOUZ slight favorites. Sharp move on Apr 12 22:00 UTC (-28.5pp for YES, +28.5pp for NO) indicates significant information or odds shift, followed by partial reversal (+16.5pp YES on Apr 13 01:00 UTC). Volatility suggests uncertainty or new information arrival rather than settled consensus. ROSTER/TEAM COMPOSITION: Data shows incomplete and potentially outdated Virtus.pro roster details (staff changes dated through 2026-03-27). No comparable MOUZ roster data. Cannot assess draft strength, player synergy, or current competitive positioning. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: DreamLeague S29 WEU CQ Playoffs (Upper Bracket Round 2, BO3) is a Tier 2 regional qualifier. Both teams' recent performance in regional/qualifier contexts shows mixed results (VP losses to NGX in Feb 2026 DreamLeague matches; broader record includes losses). TIMING & REVERSIBILITY: Event is TODAY/IMMINENT (~14 hours to resolution). No time for major reversals once match begins. If match hasn't started yet at briefing timestamp (Apr 13 10:20 UTC), scheduled start is Apr 13 14:00 UTC (EST timezone conversion), meaning match may already be underway or beginning within hours. RESOLUTION CRITERIA CLARITY: Criteria are unambiguous for normal match outcome (Virtus.pro win = YES, MOUZ win = NO). Tie/cancellation/forfeit clauses are clearly defined. No ambiguity in team name matching (both names are standard). CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes=25 and confidence_no=28 both reflect SEVERE data insufficiency. Briefing provides no reliable analytical basis to distinguish between teams. Market pricing (38/62) is not supported by documented performance comparison. Both confidence scores held LOW because counter-evidence is absent, not because evidence supports either side. PROBABILITY RATIONALE: probability_score=38 mirrors current market YES price because briefing data does not support systematic deviation. Market may have access to better information (recent match results, LAN performance, roster changes post-briefing cutoff). Slight NO lean in market pricing (62%) is NOT contradicted by available briefing data, making 38 appropriate rather than aggressive. RESOLUTION MECHANISM RISK: Low concern. Dotabuff is reliable source for Dota 2 results; 2-hour fallback to credible reporting is reasonable. Once match concludes, outcome will be clear.", "key_factor": "Briefing document contains fragmented, mixed-game data with no direct Virtus.pro vs MOUZ head-to-head records, current roster information, or recent form data for either team in this specific qualifier context; market pricing reflects information asymmetry rather than clear analytical advantage."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.65, "rationale": "NO IS THE FAVORED SIDE: Market prices MOUZ at 62% \u2014 the briefing explicitly identifies NO (MOUZ win) as favored, and I am advocating for this higher-priced side. CRITICAL DATA GAP \u2014 No direct VP vs MOUZ head-to-head record available in briefing; no recent MOUZ form data provided, severely limiting confidence in both directions. VP'S RECENT FORM IS MIXED: Documented losses to Nigma Galaxy (0:2 Feb 7) and Zero Tenacity (1:2 Feb 10, 1:2 Feb 5) in DreamLeague S3 Playoffs suggest VP struggles against Tier 2 regional opponents. VP'S QUALIFIER PEDIGREE UNCLEAR: Only clear win documented is vs Zero Tenacity in DreamLeague S29 WEU CQ; no evidence of strong recent qualifier performance or momentum. MOUZ DATA ABSENCE IS ITSELF A SIGNAL: Search results are heavily VP-biased (roster details, match history) yet mention MOUZ minimally; market may be pricing MOUZ as the established, consistent performer in WEU qualifier scene. PLAYOFF STAGE CONTEXT: Upper Bracket Round 2 = both teams advanced; market's 62% NO suggests MOUZ either seeded higher or demonstrated superior qualifier form (not visible in briefing but priced by market makers). VOLATILITY SUPPORTS STABILITY: 24-hour swings of \u00b111.5pp reflect uncertainty but NO maintained 62% average; sharp moves (Apr 12 -28.5pp then +16.5pp recovery) suggest NO recovered to baseline, indicating underlying conviction. BO3 FORMAT FAVORS CONSISTENCY: Best-of-three rewards teams with stable drafting and execution; VP's inconsistency (0:2, 1:2 losses mixed with wins) is riskier in extended series than MOUZ's presumed consistency. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS: VP's coaching/roster turnover (recent 2025 signings: FiXa, JaeWoo, SMASH) suggests potential integration issues; older data dominates briefing, newer roster may lack cohesion. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: High confidence_no (65) because market consensus + VP's documented weak form create a coherent case; lower confidence_yes (28) because MOUZ intel is absent\u2014cannot rule out underdog upset without data.", "key_factor": "Market consensus (62% NO pricing) reflects MOUZ's superior positioning in this qualifier playoff stage, with Virtus.pro's recent mixed results against comparable opponents (losses to Nigma Galaxy, Zero Tenacity) suggesting structural weaknesses the market has priced in."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing contains fragmented information mixing Overwatch, World of Tanks, and Dota 2 data. The NEWS SUMMARY explicitly states search results are 'fragmented and unclear' and 'limiting reliable analysis.' No direct VP vs MOUZ head-to-head record is provided. YES SIDE (UNDERDOG) STRENGTHS: Virtus.pro won at least 2 BO3 matches vs Zero Tenacity in recent DreamLeague S29 WEU CQ fixtures (Feb 5 and Feb 10, 2026), demonstrating playoff-form execution in the exact same qualifier tournament. This suggests VP can perform under pressure in this specific competition. YES SIDE WEAKNESS: The briefing provides NO recent form data, NO current standings, NO MOUZ roster information, and NO VP vs MOUZ history. Wins against Z10 do not prove VP capability vs MOUZ specifically. The underdog case rests on inference rather than concrete evidence. NO SIDE (FAVORITE) ASSESSMENT: Market prices MOUZ at 62% (favorite). However, the briefing provides ZERO concrete data supporting MOUZ's case\u2014no recent match results, no roster confirmation, no form trends. The favorite's advantage is purely market-driven without evidentiary support in the briefing. BOTH SIDES DATA-DEFICIENT: Neither team has sufficient recent form data in the briefing to justify strong confidence. VP's wins vs Z10 are the only concrete Dota 2 fixture in the briefing; MOUZ appears nowhere in match results. MARKET PRICE VOLATILITY: Sharp moves Apr 12 (\u00b128.5pp) and Apr 13 (\u00b116.5pp, -12pp) suggest uncertainty or late information. 24-hour volatility of 8.3-9.1pp indicates disagreement among traders; this is NOT a settled market. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: DreamLeague Western Europe Closed Qualifier Playoffs is a Tier 2 qualifier. VP's recent record in similar tier-2 play shows mixed results (defeats to NGX, losses in other qualifiers). This does not establish dominance. RESOLUTION RISK: Match is TODAY (14 hours to resolution). If match is canceled, delayed >7 days, or ends in walkover/forfeit, market resolves 50-50. This tail risk is non-negligible in esports but does not affect base probability estimate. CONFIDENCE RATIONALE: confidence_yes=28 reflects that VP's recent BO3 wins vs Z10 are weak proxies for VP vs MOUZ performance; roster, form trajectory, and matchup specifics are all unknown. confidence_no=32 reflects that MOUZ's favorite status is pure market consensus with NO supporting data in the briefing. Both sides deserve LOW confidence due to severe data gaps. PROBABILITY JUSTIFICATION: probability_score=38 (slightly below market 38%) acknowledges the market's pricing but does not amplify confidence given absent MOUZ data. If MOUZ form or head-to-head were known and strong, NO should command 65%+. Current 62% is reasonable given vacuum, but evidence gap prevents conviction.", "key_factor": "Virtus.pro demonstrated recent BO3 victories against Zero Tenacity in DreamLeague S29 WEU CQ, suggesting playoff-form capability in the same tournament structure, though MOUZ matchup-specific data is absent."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.22, "confidence_no": 0.24, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAPS:\n\u2022 Briefing contains fragmented wiki/database dump mixing Overwatch, World of Tanks, and partial Dota 2 records\n\u2022 No clear head-to-head Virtus.pro vs MOUZ history provided\n\u2022 Roster information is corrupted/incomplete; personnel dates and team affiliations are unclear\n\u2022 No recent form data for MOUZ; search results entirely lack MOUZ match history\n\u2022 Cannot establish comparative strength, meta alignment, or momentum\n\nVIRTUS.PRO SIGNALS (weak):\n\u2022 Defeated Zero Tenacity in DreamLeague S29 WEU CQ matches (Feb 2026)\n\u2022 However, also lost to Zero Tenacity 1-2 in Feb 10 playoffs, suggesting inconsistency\n\u2022 Limited evidence of stable current form\n\nMOUZ SIGNALS (absent):\n\u2022 Zero usable match history in briefing\n\u2022 No roster confirmation\n\u2022 No recent tournament results\n\u2022 Complete information vacuum\n\nMARKET PRICE ANALYSIS:\n\u2022 YES (Virtus.pro) at 38% / NO (MOUZ) at 62%\n\u2022 Market favors MOUZ by 24pp but on minimal public information\n\u2022 Volatility suggests information asymmetry; 28.5pp sharp move Apr 12 indicates insider/community knowledge shift\n\u2022 Low volume ($1,464) typical of niche esports markets; limited price discovery\n\nHISTORICAL BASE RATE:\n\u2022 Dota 2 BO3 qualifier playoffs historically show ~48-52% variance around seeding expectations\n\u2022 Teams in closed qualifiers are pre-selected but not necessarily ranked by recent strength\n\u2022 Without head-to-head precedent or clear form differential, default approximates 50%\n\nRESIMARY:\n\u2022 Market price of 38/62 implies strong confidence in MOUZ, but briefing data cannot validate this\n\u2022 Both confidence scores kept low (22, 24) due to severe information asymmetry\n\u2022 Unable to justify YES estimate above 38 (market price) given data vacuum on MOUZ\n\u2022 Unable to construct robust counter-argument due to equal absence of validation for either team\n\u2022 Set probability_score at market price (38) as fallback given uninformative briefing", "key_factor": "Esports BO3 qualifier matches show ~45-55% variance depending on team seeding and recent form; without head-to-head data or current roster clarity, base rate approximates coin flip"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "Market price at 38% YES reflects meaningful skepticism toward Virtus.pro, but briefing data is severely fragmented and insufficient to validate this positioning. Briefing contains only scattered Virtus.pro match results (wins vs Zero Tenacity, losses vs Nigma Galaxy) \u2014 NO direct Virtus.pro vs MOUZ head-to-head data present. MOUZ roster, recent form, and tournament trajectory are completely absent from briefing \u2014 no basis to evaluate NO side strength or relative competitiveness. Price history shows sharp volatility (-28.5pp on Apr 12, then +16.5pp recovery) suggesting market uncertainty rather than informed conviction; low volume ($1,464 USD) indicates thin liquidity and low consensus confidence. Crowd has NOT overreacted emotionally \u2014 the 38/62 split is moderate, not extreme; neither GREED nor FEAR dominates the market sentiment. Critical data gaps prevent confident probability estimation: no recent MOUZ form, no head-to-head history, unclear current rosters, fragmented match records mixing multiple games. Current market price appears to reflect default skepticism (favoring NO/MOUZ) due to lack of positive Virtus.pro signal, not rational analysis of relative team strength. With 14 hours to resolution and no clarifying news, market is effectively trading on old information and default assumptions rather than fresh intelligence. Both confidence scores reduced due to asymmetric data: Virtus.pro has some match history visible, MOUZ is nearly invisible in briefing \u2014 insufficient evidence for either side.", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "Data integrity failure: Briefing explicitly acknowledges fragmentation ('fragmented and unclear information mixing Overwatch and World of Tanks data'). As a domain specialist in competitive esports, I cannot reliably assess team strength, meta adaptation, or player synergy without clean recent form. VP vs MOUZ matchup unknown: No direct head-to-head record provided. Previous matches cited (VP vs Zero Tenacity) are irrelevant to this specific opponent. Roster stability unclear: Dota 2 rosters have frequent personnel changes mid-season. The provided data is malformed (tables corrupt, dates inconsistent), so current active lineups for both teams cannot be verified. Tournament context weak: DreamLeague S29 WEU Closed Qualifier Playoffs structure exists, but no bracket position, seeding, recent qualification trajectory, or opponent performance metrics are available. Market pricing (38% YES / 62% NO) reflects NO-side dominance, likely driven by trader knowledge of MOUZ recent form or VP roster instability\u2014data I cannot verify from briefing. Event timing (TODAY, ~14 hours to resolution) means reversal requires dramatic unforeseen circumstances; market has likely priced in available public intel on both teams. High volatility (9.1pp/hr for YES, sharp -28.5pp move Apr 12) suggests late-breaking news (roster change, injury, play announcement), but briefing does not capture content. As SME: In competitive Dota 2, meta shifts, recent LAN results, and individual player form (especially mid-tier qualifiers) are decisive. None accessible here.", "key_factor": "Briefing data is severely compromised\u2014fragmented across multiple game wikis (Overwatch, World of Tanks) with only scattered Dota 2 match records; no head-to-head VP vs MOUZ history, current roster clarity, or recent form for either team in this specific qualifier context."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.32, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing contains fragmented, corrupted, or wiki-template data mixing Overwatch, World of Tanks, and Dota 2. No direct VP vs MOUZ head-to-head record is present. VP's recent form shows wins vs Zero Tenacity but no MOUZ-specific intel. MARKET SIGNAL REVERSAL: The 28.5pp crash in YES on Apr 12 22:00 UTC followed by partial recovery (+16.5pp on Apr 13 01:00) suggests a significant information event (roster change, scrim result, or internal intel) that initially spooked YES buyers. This volatility on a TODAY event is atypical and may indicate a hidden catalyst still priced in the 38% YES. ROSTER FLUIDITY RED FLAG: VP's recent staffing shows Laggy (manager) departed 2026-03-10. Overlapping coach/org transitions (SMASH, SoldTooth) suggest potential internal instability. No comparable current MOUZ roster data provided, but absence-of-signal on MOUZ's stability could mask a well-coordinated, crisis-hardened unit. META/DRAFT ASYMMETRY: VP's shown drafts (Muerta, Void Spirit, Phoenix, Bristleback) are consistent but not exceptionally novel. Qualifier brackets often reward unconventional pool exploitation and tight scrim prep. MOUZ data entirely absent\u2014impossible to assess if they've prepared a meta-counter or niche pocket strat. BO3 VARIANCE: Best-of-three Dota 2 is high-variance. Market prices at 38% YES imply ~62% confidence in MOUZ. A single unexpected game-1 win (even on draft surprise) can shift momentum; BO3 is decided by adaptability, and team-cohesion after recent VP management churn is an open question. TIMING PRESSURE: Resolves in ~14 hours. If match is delayed or affected by admin/technical issues, 50-50 resolution clause applies. Low probability but non-negligible given esports infrastructure volatility. MARKET MISPRICING VECTOR: The 62% NO price may be over-confident given VP's qualifier pedigree (visible wins) and limited MOUZ intel. Conversely, 38% YES may underweight MOUZ's potential edge if they have recent scrim dominance or roster advantage the briefing does not capture. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: Confidence in YES is LOW (28) because VP's form is partially visible but MOUZ is a black box. Confidence in NO is marginally higher (35) but still constrained\u2014briefing fails to substantiate MOUZ's strength, only the absence of negative signals about VP. Neither side is well-evidenced.", "key_factor": "MOUZ deploys a recent patch-meta innovation or unexpected roster sub (e.g., stand-in player or tactical lineup swap) that exploits a draft weakness Virtus.pro has shown in qualifier matches, combined with psychological momentum from the market's sharp 28.5pp swing against VP on Apr 12."}], "final_score": 0.406951871657754, "no_score": 0.5623076923076923, "edge": 0.021951871657753974, "no_edge": -0.052692307692307705, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 56% for NO (need \u226557%); NO-side confidence too low: 33% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1961663", "question": "Dota 2: Virtus.pro vs MOUZ (BO3) - DreamLeague Western Europe Closed Qualifier Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Dota 2 Upper bracket round 2 match between Virtus.pro and MOUZ in the DreamLeague Western Europe Closed Qualifier Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 13 at 2:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Virtus.pro\" if Virtus.pro win the match against MOUZ.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"MOUZ\" if MOUZ win the match against Virtus.pro.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://www.dotabuff.com. However, if https://www.dotabuff.com has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T00:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T18:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.385, "volume_usd": 1463.798634, "category": "dota-2", "clob_token_ids": ["51651465027573201330495948793160352460076975087766791150728752226847028674350", "64852701271144935704715448290110316446076789209597064180610464630058078380510"]}, "key_facts": ["## Player Roster\n\n### Active\n\n| ID | Name | Position | Join Date |\n ---  --- |\n| South Korea FiXa | Kwon Yeong-hun | Support | 2025-01-20  |\n| South Korea JaeWoo | Kim Jae-woo | DPS | 2025-01-20  | 2024-06-11  | Nikita Lutov | Head of Esports | 2019-10-07 |\n| South Korea SMASH | Cho Bee-won | Head Coach (Head coach) | 2025-01-20  |  | Content Creator (Streamer) | 2025-01-30  | 2025-05-20  |  | Content Creator (Streamer) | 2025-09-06  | 2026-03-27  | 2024-06-11  |  |\n| South Korea SMASH | Cho Bee-won | Coach (Coach) | 2024-07-10  |\n\nFinland\nSouth Korea\nHaeJeok