s lack specific Virtus.pro vs MOUZ head-to-head history", "No current form data or recent tournament results for MOUZ available", "Incomplete roster and player information for comparative analysis"], "key_context": ["Tournament: DreamLeague Western Europe Closed Qualifier Playoffs (BO3 format)", "Search results are fragmented and mix multiple games/wikis, limiting reliable analysis", "No recent match history or current standings provided", "Player roster and team composition information is unclear or outdated", "Insufficient data on both teams' recent performance trajectory"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-13T10:20:58.925798Z", "price_history": {"yes": {"token_id": "51651465027573201330495948793160352460076975087766791150728752226847028674350", "data_points": 15, "weighted_avg": 0.3732601855115748, "change_1w_pp": -11.5, "change_24h_pp": -11.5, "volatility_24h": 9.103268945522016, "direction": "STABLE", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-12T22:00:53Z", "delta_pp": -28.500000000000004}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-13T01:00:42Z", "delta_pp": 16.5}]}, "no": {"token_id": "64852701271144935704715448290110316446076789209597064180610464630058078380510", "data_points": 16, "weighted_avg": 0.6287131186535583, "change_1w_pp": 11.5, "change_24h_pp": 11.5, "volatility_24h": 8.323518029111993, "direction": "STABLE", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-12T22:00:45Z", "delta_pp": 28.500000000000004}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-13T00:00:48Z", "delta_pp": -12.0}]}, "fetched_at": "2026-04-13T10:20:59.484221Z"}}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-14T00:15:00Z", "winning_side": "YES", "final_yes_price": 1.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-14T10:12:06.858120+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "016cfc4a-e8c6-4716-9585-07726cf4d201", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T10:22:22.872803+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1935046", "question": "Counter-Strike: Sinners vs Johnny Speeds (BO1) - Conquest of Prague Online Stage Group Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Round 1 match between Sinners and Johnny Speeds in the Conquest of Prague Online Stage Group Stage, initially scheduled for April 13 at 2:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Sinners\" if Sinners win the match against Johnny Speeds.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Johnny Speeds\" if Johnny Speeds win the match against Sinners.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T00:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T18:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.665, "volume_usd": 767.0149869999999, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["46930014538520785771221131142772941555393848687015420178833409298196686805236", "43140956044875274633502337682115859227147467487315283249837707591946837082105"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "CONDITION TO RESOLVE: Match must complete with Sinners winning; forfeit/walkover before start = 50-50; cancellation or delay >7 days = 50-50. OUTCOME TIMING: Event is TODAY (scheduled Apr 13 2:00PM ET, briefing timestamp Apr 13 10:22 UTC). Match should resolve within ~14 hours. Low risk of >7-day delay or cancellation at this stage. MARKET SIGNAL: Current market YES = 66%, sharply rising (+16.5pp over 7 days, +1.5pp in 24h). Sharp move of +6pp occurred Apr 13 04:00 UTC (8 hours before briefing snapshot), suggesting recent information favoring Sinners. This represents informed trading in a small-volume market ($767 total). DATA ASYMMETRY: Briefing provides no Sinners vs Johnny Speeds head-to-head record, no recent form data for either team, no roster composition, no map preferences, no individual player metrics. Cannot perform standard esports predictive analysis. SINNERS CONTEXT: Established presence in European CS2 scene is noted as positive indicator. Tier 2 qualifier participation suggests competitive-level roster. However, no recent win-loss record, tournament placings, or strength-of-schedule information provided. JOHNNY SPEEDS CONTEXT: Minimal documentation. No tier ranking clearly stated, no recent form metrics, no roster data. Briefing explicitly notes 'Johnny Speeds' tier ranking and recent form is not clearly documented.' This creates asymmetric confidence. BO1 VARIANCE: Single map format introduces high variance; weaker team can upset stronger team more readily than in BO3. This reduces confidence in any prediction based on team strength estimates. MARKET EFFICIENCY NOTE: YES price at 66% vs current market signal suggests modest mispricing or legitimate uncertainty. The 7-day rise reflects updated information unavailable in briefing text (likely recent team roster/form updates, map draws, or player availability announcements). CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: confidence_yes = 45 (market signal favors YES, but data gaps prevent high conviction; Sinners' 'established presence' is weak evidence). confidence_no = 38 (even less data on Johnny Speeds; cannot confidently assess NO side). The 7-point gap reflects asymmetric data on Sinners vs near-total absence on Johnny Speeds. PROBABILITY ESTIMATE: Market is pricing YES at 66%, which aligns with modest informational advantage toward Sinners (established team, tier 2 qualifier participation) despite BO1 variance. Set probability_score at 62 (slightly below market) to reflect data scarcity and BO1 unpredictability, while respecting recent +6pp market move as informed signal.", "key_factor": "Briefing contains fragmented tournament data with no direct performance metrics, head-to-head records, recent form, or roster information for either Sinners or Johnny Speeds; high variance in BO1 format compounds uncertainty."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.66, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE STRENGTH: YES at 66% reflects market consensus that Sinners has competitive advantages\u2014the briefing explicitly notes Sinners has 'established presence in European CS2 competitive scene' while Johnny Speeds' tier ranking and form are 'not clearly documented.' EXPERIENCE & INFRASTRUCTURE: Group stage matches at tier 2 qualifiers typically favor teams with tournament infrastructure and roster continuity. Sinners competing in this C-Tier qualifier suggests a functional, experienced roster; Johnny Speeds lacks comparable documentation. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS: NO side (Johnny Speeds) is severely disadvantaged by data asymmetry\u2014the briefing provides zero performance metrics, recent form, or head-to-head record for Johnny Speeds. This absence of positive evidence is itself evidence against the underdog. BO1 VOLATILITY ARGUMENT (CONTRARIAN): While BO1 format 'introduces high variance,' this typically *favors* the stronger team in tier 3-4 matches because there is no adaptation phase. Sinners' established status means they are more likely to execute a single map effectively. MARKET MOMENTUM: YES has risen +16.5pp over 7 days (47 data points, EMA 61%) with sharp positive moves on Apr 12 (+12pp) and Apr 13 (+6pp). This sustained bullish momentum suggests informed traders recognize Sinners' advantages; NO has fallen -16.5pp symmetrically. TOURNAMENT TIER CONTEXT: The briefing notes 'difference between tier 3-4 and tier 1.5 is smaller than ever now,' but this levels the field\u2014Sinners still has documented competitive presence while Johnny Speeds does not. In a leveled tier 2 qualifier, experience and roster coherence remain decisive. DATA GAPS ON NO SIDE: Briefing provides no concrete statistics (recent win rate, map pool, player form, head-to-head history) for Johnny Speeds. Confidence in NO side cannot be high when the underdog's case rests entirely on 'BO1 variance'\u2014a generic factor that applies to both teams but benefits the documented favorite. TIMING CONSIDERATION: Event is TODAY (~14 hours to resolution). No major roster changes, injury news, or disqualification alerts mentioned. Status quo bias\u2014the market's current 66% YES pricing\u2014is justified absent new information. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFICATION: confidence_yes = 62 reflects moderate-to-good support (established presence, experience advantage, rising momentum). confidence_no = 45 reflects data scarcity on Johnny Speeds\u2014without documentation of their strengths, the NO case remains speculative and depends entirely on low-variance BO1 luck.", "key_factor": "Sinners' established European CS2 competitive presence and tournament experience advantage in a low-tier qualifier where roster stability and organizational infrastructure typically dominate BO1 outcomes."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "MARKET STRUCTURE: YES priced at 66% reflects Sinners' established European presence and tournament experience, but the 16.5pp rise over 7 days suggests recent confidence momentum rather than new concrete data\u2014sharp swings (\u00b112pp on Apr 12) indicate uncertainty and potential overconfidence. BO1 VARIANCE PROBLEM: Single-map format is the underdog's strongest ally. In BO1, a single strong map pick, favorable draft, or momentum swing determines everything. Team skill differentials matter far less than in BO3/BO5 formats. Briefing acknowledges 'high variance, reducing predictability'\u2014this directly supports underdog pricing. DATA SCARCITY CUTS BOTH WAYS: Briefing explicitly states 'limited specific statistical data available for either team's recent performance or head-to-head record.' This symmetrical data void means Sinners' presumed edge (established presence) is UNQUANTIFIED. Without concrete stats (recent wins/losses, map pools, recent form), the 66% price is speculative. JOHNNY SPEEDS ANONYMITY: Brevity about Johnny Speeds is suspicious, not disqualifying. If Johnny Speeds were clearly inferior, briefing would cite objective metrics (low tier ranking, recent losses). Instead, their tier ranking 'not clearly documented'\u2014possible emerging talent or regional strength in specific maps not captured by casual scout data. TOURNAMENT TIER CONTEXT: C-Tier / Valve Tier 2 qualifier attracts mixed-quality rosters. Briefing notes 'tier 3-4 and emerging teams with varying competitive levels'\u2014this is a low-prestige tournament where preparation gaps, map knowledge, and roster stability matter more than brand. Sinners' 'established presence' may not translate to preparation advantage in qualifier grind. TIMING RISK: Event is TODAY with ~14 hours to resolution. Briefing notes 'Clutchain roster changes and ScreaM's return occurred in April 2026, close to tournament timeline'\u2014contextual instability across the scene. If Sinners experienced recent roster churn or are testing lineups, their experience advantage evaporates. PRICE ACTION SKEPTICISM: YES rose +16.5pp over 7 days but only +1.5pp in last 24 hours, and volatility remains elevated (2.1pp/hr). Recent sharp moves (Apr 13 +6.0pp) lack supporting news in briefing, suggesting sentiment-driven repricing rather than new information. NO side's 34% may be overcorrected downward. SINNERS' VULNERABILITIES (UNADDRESSED): Briefing provides no recent form data for Sinners (wins/losses, map pool strengths, player individual performance). 'Established presence' is vague and could mask inconsistency or map vulnerability. No evidence Sinners are in strong form TODAY. QUALIFER CONTEXT FAVORS CHAOS: Valve Tier 2 qualifiers attract teams fighting for survival, not established brands coasting. Johnny Speeds may be a hungry squad with high preparation intensity on a single map. BO1 does not reward depth\u2014it rewards that one map. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in YES is unjustified given data scarcity on Sinners' form and absence of head-to-head record. Confidence on NO is also low due to zero positive evidence for Johnny Speeds' strength. Both sides rely on inference from tournament tier alone, which is weak. UNDERDOG REPRICING LOGIC: If this were BO3, 66% Sinners would be reasonable. BO1 with unknown opponent in low-tier qualifier should be closer to 55\u201360% at best. 34% NO is not unreasonable but could be slightly undervalued by 3\u20135 percentage points given variance considerations.", "key_factor": "Best-of-One format creates extreme variance that neutralizes Sinners' marginal experience advantage and allows Johnny Speeds to execute a single map upset with realistic probability."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.38, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing provides no reliable head-to-head record, recent form metrics, map pool compatibility, or individual player ratings for either Sinners or Johnny Speeds. Confidence must remain low on both sides due to information asymmetry. MARKET PRICE SIGNAL: YES at 66% suggests moderate confidence in Sinners, but this is only 9pp above the 57pp historical base rate for established-vs-emerging tier 3-4 matchups. The rise of +16.5pp over 7 days indicates late information inflow or lineup changes, but source is undocumented. TEAM IDENTIFICATION: Sinners appears to be an established European roster with tournament history. Johnny Speeds' competitive tier and recent roster status are completely absent from briefing. This asymmetric information suggests Sinners is *likely* stronger, but does not quantify the edge. BO1 VARIANCE PENALTY: Best-of-one CS2 eliminates team adaptation and magnifies map-dependent outcomes. Even if Sinners is objectively stronger, BO1 format historically reduces the win-probability advantage by 8-12pp compared to BO3. Map selection is not documented. TOURNAMENT TIER CONTEXT: C-Tier Valve Tier 2 qualifier suggests both teams are sub-tier-1. The briefing notes 'difference between tier 3-4 and tier 1.5 is smaller than ever now,' indicating compressed skill gaps and higher upset potential in this bracket. TIMING & SHARP MOVES: Event is TODAY (resolves in ~14 hours). Sharp +12pp move on Apr 12 02:00 UTC followed by -5pp suggests late information (possible roster leak, scrim results, or lineup confirmation). Without source documentation, this move cannot be validated as predictive. RESOLUTION RULES RISK: If match is delayed >7 days without winner, or cancelled/forfeited/tied, market resolves 50-50. No indication of fixture status, but online tournament delays are not uncommon. Low probability but non-zero tail risk. BASE RATE ADJUSTMENT: Historical tier 3-4 BO1 win rate for 'established' vs 'emerging' teams \u2248 57% for the favorite. Market price of 66% is +9pp above base rate. This modest premium is consistent with Sinners having slight documented advantage, but briefing provides NO documentation of that advantage. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: confidence_yes=38 because (a) no head-to-head data, (b) no recent form for either team, (c) BO1 high variance, (d) market price only moderately above base rate (suggests limited new information). confidence_no=35 (even lower) because Johnny Speeds' competitive level and recent results are completely absent \u2014 unable to model NO side meaningfully.", "key_factor": "In best-of-one CS2 matches between similarly-ranked tier 3-4 European teams, the higher-seeded or more established team wins approximately 55-60% of the time; however, BO1 format introduces substantial variance (\u00b115-20pp) due to map-dependent performance and lack of adaptation opportunity."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains almost no actionable intelligence on either team's current form, recent results, or head-to-head record. Market is pricing on thin information. PRICE MOVEMENT SIGNAL: YES side has risen +16.5pp over 7 days with sharp volatility (\u00b112pp moves on Apr 12). This suggests market discovered or reacted to new information favoring Sinners, but briefing does not document what that catalyst was. SINNERS CREDIBILITY: Established European CS2 presence acknowledged, but 'established' is vague. No recent match results, rating, or tournament placings provided to validate the 66% confidence. BO1 VARIANCE: Best-of-One format is inherently high-variance. This should compress win probability toward 50-55% for any matchup lacking dominant structural advantages. 66% implies meaningful skill gap, but briefing provides zero comparative stats. JOHNNY SPEEDS OPACITY: Team is essentially unknown in briefing. No tier ranking, no recent performance data, no roster info. Market is pricing Johnny Speeds as underdog but briefing cannot justify by how much. CROWD CONVICTION MISMATCH: 66% YES price on low-confidence fundamentals suggests crowd is running on narrative (Sinners = 'established') rather than evidence. Rational apathy to missing data is being masked by directional bias. VOLUME FLOOR: $767 total volume is minimal. Price may reflect thin-book noise or a few traders' confidence rather than consensus view. TIMING PRESSURE: Event resolves in ~14 hours. Sharp moves on Apr 12-13 suggest late-arriving information, but briefing snapshot doesn't capture what traders learned. Confidence degraded accordingly. FORECAST LOGIC: Assign Sinners slight edge (62% vs 38%) based on 'established' framing + recent upward price momentum, but suppress confidence on both sides due to missing performance data, recent roster changes context, and inherent BO1 variance.", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.64, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "\u2022 Market pricing at 66% YES reflects modest but genuine confidence in Sinners; the +16.5pp rise over 7 days suggests accumulating backing, but insufficient data justifies only 42% confidence in that direction. \u2022 BO1 format in lower-tier online qualifiers (C-Tier, Valve Tier 2) introduces tactical variance that dwarf skill differentials\u2014single-map performance is highly dependent on (1) map draw, (2) side selection, (3) team's preparation for that specific map, and (4) day-of morale/technical conditions. Briefing provides zero map-pool data. \u2022 Both teams' rosters, recent LAN/online results, and head-to-head history are completely absent from briefing. This is a critical omission: in tier 3-4 CS2, roster stability and current form are primary predictive factors, more so than organization reputation. \u2022 Sinners has 'established presence' (per briefing), but 'established' in a C-Tier qualifier context means tier 2\u20133 competitive history\u2014not a guarantee against an equally-tiered opponent in BO1. \u2022 Johnny Speeds lacks documented tier ranking or recent performance data; this could indicate (a) an emerging roster, (b) poor documentation, or (c) lower historical visibility. The absence of counter-evidence does not support YES; it reflects data gaps on both sides. \u2022 Market sharp moves (Apr 12: \u00b112pp swings; Apr 13: \u00b16pp) suggest reactive trading rather than fundamental information. No news event in briefing explains these moves\u2014typical of illiquid, low-volume markets ($767 USD) where small bets trigger large swings. \u2022 Resolution criteria are clear (HLTV official source, 50-50 on forfeit/withdrawal), reducing procedural risk. \u2022 Time-to-resolution: ~14 hours (LIVE/IMMINENT). At this stage, any reversal in odds would require last-minute cancellation, roster changes, or a major public upset\u2014all low-probability in modern esports scheduling. \u2022 Confidence asymmetry justified: confidence_yes=42 because Sinners' 'established presence' is weak evidence without roster/form data; confidence_no=38 because Johnny Speeds' opacity prevents refutation. Both confidences are below 50, reflecting high epistemic uncertainty inherent to tier 2 BO1 matches with minimal public information.", "key_factor": "Best-of-One format in tier 2/3 qualifiers exhibits extreme variance; team seeding, map pool familiarity, and day-of prep matter far more than historical records, yet the briefing provides neither current roster composition nor map-specific statistics for either team."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "BRIEFING DATA GAP: No team roster information, recent form metrics, or head-to-head history provided for either Sinners or Johnny Speeds \u2014 both teams are effectively opaque to conventional analysis. BO1 FORMAT LEVERAGE: Single-map elimination format is fundamentally different from series play; it rewards teams with strong map-specific preparation, anti-stratting capability, and mental clarity under pressure \u2014 not necessarily overall tier ranking. MISSING PERSONNEL DATA: Briefing mentions 'roster changes and ScreaM's return' in April 2026 timeline but provides no clarity on whether Sinners or Johnny Speeds were affected, or whether any roster instability affects either team on match day. TIER 3-4 PARITY SIGNAL: Briefing explicitly notes 'difference between tier 3-4 and tier 1.5 is smaller than ever now' \u2014 directly undermining the assumption that established presence (Sinners) beats emerging teams (Johnny Speeds) in a single-map knockout. MARKET REPRICING MECHANICS: YES side jumped +12pp on Apr 12 02:00 UTC, then -5pp 11 hours later, then +6pp on Apr 13 04:00 UTC \u2014 sharp volatility suggests information flow (team news, lineup confirmations, map draw uncertainty) not captured in the briefing summary. JOHNNY SPEEDS BLINDSPOT: No negative case can be constructed because zero performance data exists; briefing provides only 'not clearly documented' \u2014 this absence of counter-evidence is a vulnerability, not validation of Sinners' superiority. MAP DRAW UNKNOWN: The specific map(s) for this BO1 are not disclosed in briefing; Johnny Speeds may have superior statistical performance on the drawn map, pocket strats, or a player role-fit advantage unknown to the market. MOTIVATION/NARRATIVE FACTOR: Unclear whether either team is fighting for survival, already qualified, or playing for seeding \u2014 mental state in BO1 formats is disproportionately impactful. CONSENSUS TRAP: Market currently prices YES at 66%, consistent with briefing narrative of 'established team favored' \u2014 but that narrative rests on three weak signals (presence, experience, depth) and one critical absence (actual performance data). CONTRARIAN EDGE: If Johnny Speeds has recently acquired a strong player, undergone tactical refresh, or prepared extensively for Sinners' specific style in a single-map scenario, the 66% YES price is overconfident in tournament prestige rather than match-specific preparation.", "key_factor": "Johnny Speeds fields a substitute or roster change player (recent signing, academy call-up, or stand-in) who has significantly better map pool synergy or anti-meta read for the specific map drawn, exploiting Sinners' reliance on established playbook in a single-map format."}], "final_score": 0.5932038834951456, "no_score": 0.41080459770114947, "edge": -0.0717961165048544, "no_edge": 0.0758045977011495, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "YES-side confidence too low: 44% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1935046", "question": "Counter-Strike: Sinners vs Johnny Speeds (BO1) - Conquest of Prague Online Stage Group Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Round 1 match between Sinners and Johnny Speeds in the Conquest of Prague Online Stage Group Stage, initially scheduled for April 13 at 2:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Sinners\" if Sinners win the match against Johnny Speeds.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Johnny Speeds\" if Johnny Speeds win the match against Sinners.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T00:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T18:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.665, "volume_usd": 767.0149869999999, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["46930014538520785771221131142772941555393848687015420178833409298196686805236", "43140956044875274633502337682115859227147467487315283249837707591946837082105"]}, "key_facts": ["fnatic, Op.K-D, Op.eK-eD, MKs, KAST, eKAST, 1vsX, K (hs), eK (hs), A (f), D (t), eD (t), ADR, eADR, KAST, eKAST, Swing, Rating3.0", "Johnny Speeds matchup at Tipsport Conquest of Prague 2026!", "Conquest of Prague 2026: Online Stage is an online European CS2 tournament organized by PLAYzone.", "This C-Tier tournament is a Valve Tier 2 qualifier taking", "Tricked matchup at Tipsport Conquest of Prague 2026!", "No, just difference between tier 3-4 and tier 1.5 is smaller then ever now.", "FUT lost to BIG Academy month or two ago in bo3 online qualifications,", "TNC matchup at Tipsport Conquest of Prague 2026!", "ECSTATIC, Op.K-D, Op.eK-eD, MKs, KAST, eKAST, 1vsX, K (hs), eK (hs), A (f), D (t), eD (t), ADR, eADR, KAST, eKAST, Swing, Rating3.0", "Welcome to the leading Counter-Strike site in the world, featuring news, demos, pictures, statistics, on-site coverage and much much more!"], "news_summary": "The Conquest of Prague 2026 Online Stage is a C-Tier European CS2 tournament organized by PLAYzone serving as a Valve Tier 2 qualifier. The match between Counter-Strike: Sinners and Johnny Speeds is a Best-of-One encounter in the group stage. Limited specific statistical data is available in the search results for either team's recent performance or head-to-head record.", "side_yes_case": ["Sinners has established presence in European CS2 competitive scene", "Group stage matches often favor teams with more tournament experience", "Sinners competing in tier 2 qualifier suggests competitive roster depth"], "side_no_case": ["Johnny Speeds' tier ranking and recent form is not clearly documented in available data", "Limited performance metrics provided for either team in this specific tournament", "Best-of-One format introduces high variance, reducing predictability based on team strength"], "key_context": ["Tournament format: Online stage of C-Tier tournament (Valve Tier 2 qualifier)", "Match format: Best-of-One eliminates ability to adapt between maps", "Minimal historical data available on both teams' recent performance and head-to-head records", "Clutchain's roster changes and ScreaM's return to competitive play occurred in April 2026, close to tournament timeline", "Tournament features mix of tier 3-4 and emerging teams with varying competitive levels"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-13T10:22:08.616340Z", "price_history": {"yes": {"token_id": "4