ice": 0.785, "volume_usd": 19419.197537, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["45136248168018391017592351390247825161526506828776300651305412096704580632815", "60595176746032694068808064887693802446043835302932254501490435474640758402540"]}, "key_facts": ["Welcome to the leading Counter-Strike site in the world, featuring news, demos, pictures, statistics, on-site coverage and much much more!", "Astralis have booked a place in the grand finals of PGL Bucharest, doing so via a campaign that has seen them lose only two maps and claim series victories", "Ismailcan D\u00f6rtkarde\u015f known as XANTARES, is a 30 year old Counter-Strike player from Turkey, currently playing for Aurora.", "Eyeballers, JW Gives Birth On Stage And The Child Is Carried By Donk And Zywoo.", "No Other Then Jame Will Be The Messiah And His Children To Suffer The Sin Of", "Esports League Super Cup is an online/offline Russian CS2 tournament organized by CIS Esports League ...", "### Game Timeline\n\n[edit]\n\n{\"colors\":[\"#5d5d16\",\"#7a5a1d\",\"#fbecdf\",\"#31519c\",\"#dbeded\",\"#b12a2a\",\"#b12a2a\",\"#54711b\"],\"data\":[{\"name\":\"Counter-Strike\",\"values\":[{\"y\":\"2022-08-31\"},{\"y\":\"now\"}]},{\"name\":\"Apex Legends\",\"values\":[{\"y\":\"2022-11-04\"},{\"y\":\"now\"}]},{\"name\":\"Dota 2\",\"values\":[{\"y\":\"2023-11-13\"},{\"y\":\"now\"}]},{\"name\":\"Warcraft\",\"values\":[{\"y\":\"2024-03-11\"},{\"y\":\"now\"}]},{\"name\":\"Mobile Legends\",\"values\":[{\"y\":\"2024-07-16\"},{\"y\":\"now\"}]},{\"name\":\"Chess\",\"values\":[{\"y\":\"2025-02-18\"},{\"y\":\"now\"}]},{\"name\":\"PUBG\",\"values\":[{\"y\":\"2026-02-27\"},{\"y\":\"now\"}]},{\"name\":\"Fortnite\",\"values\":[{\"y\":\"2026-03-28\"},{\"y\":\"now\"}]}],\"size\":{\"height\":\"330\",\"width\":250,\"pwidth\":100},\"domain\":[\"2022\",\"now\"],\"minValue\":10000000000,\"div\":\"horizontaltimeline-0\"}\n\n## Achievements\n\n[edit] [...] ## Achievements\n\n[edit]\n\n| Date | Place | Tier | Tournament | Prize |\n ---  --- \n| 2025-08-24 | 11th | S-Tier | Esports World Cup 2025 | $525,000 |\n| 2025-04-01 | 33rd - 64th | S-Tier | 2025 Liquipedia Ultimate Logo Series \n\nExtended list of results\")\n\n## Corporate Structure\n\n[edit]\n\nValerii \"L3rich\" Kharitonov  \nFounder  \n2022-??-??", "\u2014 Present\n\nAdalyat \"krookie\" Mamedov  \nCEO  \n2024-07-01 \u2014 Present\n\nAlexander \"Lk-\" Lemeshev  \nHead of Esports  \n2025-06-21 \u2014 Present\n\nCenk \"Sunvita\"\" Sevin\u00e7  \nCS2 Manager  \n2025-04-05 \u2014 Present\n\n## Gallery\n\n[edit]\n\n### Rosters\n\n[edit]\n\n#### Counter-Strike\n\n[edit] [...] [edit]\n\n### Rosters\n\n[edit]\n\n#### Counter-Strike\n\n[edit]\n\n Aurora Gaming at Esports World Cup 2025  \n  From left to right:  \n  jottAAA \u2219 Wicadia \u2219 woxic \u2219 XANTARES \u2219 MAJ3R\n Aurora Gaming upon winning Skyesports Grand Slam 2024  \n  From left to right:  \n  brain \u2219 Norwi \u2219 Lack1 \u2219 BELCHONOKK \u2219 KENSi \u2219 deko\n\n#### Apex Legends\n\n[edit]", "Russia\nRussia\nRussia\nRussia\nRussia\n\n|  |\n\n|  |\n\n## Results\n\n## References\n\n#### About\n\n#### Affiliated Sites [...] Logo\n\n###### General\n\n###### Specific\n\n# GLuck Yungstar 2026: Series #1 - Open Qualifier #2\n\n|  |  |\n --- |\n| Upcoming Events |  GLuck Yungstar 2026: Series #1 |\n| Ongoing Events |  |\n| Recent Events |  GLuck SixSeven Season 1 |\n| | Past Events | | |  ---  | 2026 |  GLuck SixSeven Season 1  GLuck StarPearl Season 2  Rofl Streamers Battle  GLuck StarPearl Season 1 |  | | 2025 |  GLuck Yungstar 2025  LanDaLan #3  BetBoom W Cup #2  MELBET Media League Season 2  KHL Star Strike Season 2  PARI RIVALS  LanDaLan #2  MELBET Media League Season 1  LanDaLan #1 | | 2024 |  BetBoom Aunkere Cup 2x2 #1  BetBoom All-Star 2x2 #2 | | 2023 |  Copa BetBoom 2023  Hard Play Cup #8  Hard Play Cup #7 | | | [...] | Past Events | | |\n --- \n| 2026 |  GLuck SixSeven Season 1  GLuck StarPearl Season 2  Rofl Streamers Battle  GLuck StarPearl Season 1 |  |\n| 2025 |  GLuck Yungstar 2025  LanDaLan #3  BetBoom W Cup #2  MELBET Media League Season 2  KHL Star Strike Season 2  PARI RIVALS  LanDaLan #2  MELBET Media League Season 1  LanDaLan #1 |\n| 2024 |  BetBoom Aunkere Cup 2x2 #1  BetBoom All-Star 2x2 #2 |\n| 2023 |  Copa BetBoom 2023  Hard Play Cup #8  Hard Play Cup #7 |\n\nRussia\nValve\n\n## Contents\n\n## About\n\n### Format\n\n### Prize Pool\n\nClosed Qualifier\n\nClosed Qualifier\n\n## Participants\n\n|  |  |\n --- |\n| 1 | Ukraine Edward |\n| 2 | Azerbaijan EmilShe1n\") |\n| 3 | Russia Dosia |\n| 4 | Kazakhstan AdreN \"AdreN (Kazakh player)\") |\n| 5 | Ukraine fostar |\n\nUkraine\nAzerbaijan\nRussia\nKazakhstan\nUkraine\n\n|  |\n\n|  |", "0.00 0.50 1.00 1.50 2.00 2.26 chelleos rekonz"], "news_summary": "Aurora Gaming and HOTU are set to face off in a Best-of-3 match at IEM Rio 2026 Group B. Aurora features experienced players including XANTARES, a 30-year-old Turkish veteran, and has competed at S-tier events like the 2025 Esports World Cup. Limited specific information is available about HOTU's roster composition and recent form. Both teams are competing in a prestigious international tournament that draws top-tier Counter-Strike talent.", "side_yes_case": ["Aurora has XANTARES, an experienced 30-year-old veteran with proven international pedigree", "Aurora competed at S-tier Esports World Cup 2025, demonstrating ability to compete at highest levels", "Aurora won Skyesports Grand Slam 2024, showing tournament-winning capability", "Limited public information about HOTU suggests potentially less established competitive profile"], "side_no_case": ["Insufficient data provided on HOTU's current roster strength and individual player ratings", "No recent head-to-head match results between Aurora and HOTU available for analysis", "Aurora's 2025 Esports World Cup placement (11th) indicates vulnerability against elite competition", "IEM Rio is high-pressure international stage where any team can perform unexpectedly"], "key_context": ["IEM Rio 2026 is S-tier international tournament attracting top global Counter-Strike teams", "Match format is Best-of-3, requiring consistency across multiple maps", "Group B stage implies teams are in early tournament phases with unknown bracket implications", "Search results lack specific recent form data, head-to-head records, or HOTU roster information for accurate assessment", "Aurora's recent tournament appearances span 2024-2025 with mixed results at highest tiers"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-13T10:24:28.635361Z", "price_history": {"yes": {"token_id": "45136248168018391017592351390247825161526506828776300651305412096704580632815", "data_points": 46, "weighted_avg": 0.7935854041498112, "change_1w_pp": -2.9999999999999916, "change_24h_pp": -2.0000000000000018, "volatility_24h": 0.8944271909999166, "direction": "STABLE", "sharp_moves": []}, "no": {"token_id": "60595176746032694068808064887693802446043835302932254501490435474640758402540", "data_points": 46, "weighted_avg": 0.20638907943414694, "change_1w_pp": 1.0000000000000009, "change_24h_pp": 1.9999999999999991, "volatility_24h": 0.8944271909999155, "direction": "STABLE", "sharp_moves": []}, "fetched_at": "2026-04-13T10:24:29.207384Z"}}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-14T03:25:00Z", "winning_side": "YES", "final_yes_price": 1.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-14T10:12:08.949031+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "7c1e7727-22e2-4162-b224-94658cf6b384", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T10:25:28.551066+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1892927", "question": "LoL: paiN Gaming vs FURIA Esports (BO3) - CBLOL Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between paiN Gaming and FURIA Esports in the CBLOL Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 13 at 5:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"paiN Gaming\" if paiN Gaming win the match against FURIA Esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"FURIA Esports\" if FURIA Esports win the match against paiN Gaming.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T03:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T21:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.145, "volume_usd": 20640.601293, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["39373675295037328833547050543519511075469965665368883525472791423854857412912", "46784607294219669715123582020395005869982907364604940956733916238847060209487"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.14, "confidence_yes": 0.85, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "FURIA dominates statistical record: 64% win rate (14-8) vs paiN's 29% (4-10), a 35-point gap in a competitive BO3 setting. Team standings show FURIA ranked 2nd overall, paiN ranked 7th of 8 teams in CBLOL 2026 Split 1. Game metrics favor FURIA: 32:20 avg duration vs 33:23, positive gold differential (+145) vs paiN's negative (-144). paiN Gaming shows severe structural weakness: -144 GD indicates poor teamfighting and resource conversion despite individual game wins. FURIA has elite player talent (Duduhh, Rabelo, Trigger in multikill/KDA leaderboards) with strong individual performances. BO3 format amplifies the importance of team consistency; FURIA's superior win rate is more predictive in multiple-game series than single games. paiN's recent wins (vs Leviatan, Los Grandes) occurred in CBLOL Cup 2026 (preliminary); current Regular Season performance is poor. No head-to-head data provided, but FURIA's 2nd-place standing vs paiN's 7th-place standing suggests significant skill gap. Market price of 14% YES reflects probabilistic assessment; 86% NO aligns with betting market consensus on FURIA's dominant position. Resolution criteria are unambiguous: first team to win BO3 resolves match to that team; no ambiguity on team identification. Forfeiture/walkover scenarios unlikely given both teams are active in tournament; cancellation risk minimal given event is offline and scheduled for TODAY. Confidence in YES outcome is moderate (85) due to strong empirical data on team performance; confidence in NO is lower (45) because BO3 upsets are possible, but FURIA is heavily favored.", "key_factor": "Criteria are clear and unambiguous; primary risk is resolution source delay beyond 2 hours, but outcome determination is straightforward win/loss."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.83, "confidence_yes": 0.85, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE STRENGTH (NO = FURIA wins): FURIA ranks 2nd in CBLOL with 64% win rate across 22 games (14-8), demonstrating sustained consistency. paiN Gaming is 7th of 8 teams with only 29% win rate (4-10), a 35-percentage-point gap indicating fundamental performance disparity. UNDERDOG WEAKNESSES (YES = paiN wins): paiN's -144 gold differential is the worst in the league (second-worst is -125 for Leviatan), indicating systematic gold economy problems. Their 33:23 avg game duration vs FURIA's 32:20 suggests paiN struggles to close games efficiently. FURIA'S CONSISTENT DOMINANCE: FURIA posted league-best GPM stats (2355 GPM vs paiN's lack of top-5 appearance in either CBLOL Cup or Split 1 rankings). Duduhh (FURIA ADC) ranks among league's elite farmers (10.25 CSM, 11.9 CSM peak). This depth indicates systemic execution quality. BO3 FORMAT FAVORS FAVORITE: While BO3 reduces single-match variance, it amplifies consistent superiority. paiN must win 2 of 3 games against a team that beats them structurally\u2014FURIA's 64% baseline means they win ~73% of BO3s against an average opponent; vs a 29% team, FURIA's probability rises further. paiN'S GAME VICTORIES DON'T SIGNAL COMPETITIVENESS: Despite showing wins vs Leviatan and Los Grandes, paiN's 4-10 record reflects cherry-picked wins amid systemic weakness. Single-game variance exists in any BO3, but paiN's low baseline (29%) makes upset probability low even with upset potential acknowledged. HEAD-TO-HEAD HISTORICAL CONTEXT MISSING: Briefing lacks direct paiN vs FURIA matchup history from Split 1. However, large standings gap (2nd vs 7th) and one-sided team-level metrics (gold differential, game duration, individual player rankings) strongly predict repeat outcome. FURIA's 2nd-place position is not fluky\u2014earned over 22 games. MARKET PRICING JUSTIFIED: 86% NO (FURIA) is rational. A 35 percentage-point win-rate gap, negative team gold differential on paiN, and FURIA's consistent top-2 positioning justify strong favorite pricing. Market has correctly identified structural mismatch. UNDERDOG COUNTERARGUMENT ACKNOWLEDGED BUT WEAK: paiN's occasional wins prove they can execute a single game. However, winning 2 of 3 against FURIA requires either sustained performance improvement (no evidence in recent data) or FURIA's collapse (no precedent in 14-8 record). The variance room for upset is narrower than typical BO3. TIMING CONSTRAINT: Event is TODAY (resolves ~17 hours). No mid-season roster changes, meta shifts, or injury news provided in briefing. paiN cannot bridge a 35 percentage-point gap via preparation overnight; FURIA's structural advantage persists to match time. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in YES (85) due to clear statistical dominance (rankings, GD, GPM, KDA leaders all favor FURIA). Confidence in NO (72) is lower because BO3 upsets remain possible and head-to-head history is absent from briefing, creating small but real model uncertainty on the underdog side.", "key_factor": "FURIA's dominant 64% win rate (14-8) and 2nd-place standing vs paiN's severe underperformance (29% win rate, 4-10, 7th place, -144 GD) creates a structural competitive gap that BO3 format amplifies rather than erases."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.18, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.82, "rationale": "FURIA's dominance is structural and comprehensive: 64% win rate (14-8) vs paiN's 29% (4-10) represents a 35-point gap\u2014the largest in the league by far. FURIA ranks 2nd; paiN ranks 7th of 8 teams. Gold differential reinforces the gap: FURIA at +145 GD shows consistent gold generation edge; paiN at -144 GD shows systematic deficit accumulation. FURIA's avg game duration (32:20) vs paiN (33:23) suggests FURIA closes games faster. Individual game data shows paiN CAN win: They defeated Leviatan and Los Grandes in recent matches with strong performances (Trigger: 12.16 CSM; Ceo: 11.28 CSM; Rabelo: 15 kills in one game). This proves technical ceiling exists. However, wins are sporadic anomalies: paiN's 4-10 record means 10 losses\u2014nearly 3x their wins. Consistency favors FURIA heavily in a BO3 where 2 wins end the series. One upset game \u2260 series upset. BO3 format mitigates variance somewhat but still rewards better teams: While a single-game upset is plausible (paiN can win 1 game), winning 2 of 3 against FURIA is a much higher bar. FURIA's superior macro (Gold Per Minute ranks: FURIA 2257 in Split 1, paiN absent from top 5) suggests sustainability. Head-to-head history absent: Briefing does not provide direct paiN vs FURIA matchup data, preventing identification of specific tactical or meta advantages paiN might exploit. This is a significant data gap. Recent form deterioration: YES prices fell 36 percentage points over 7 days (from ~50% to 14%), with sharp moves on Apr 09 suggesting informed market repricing downward. Large volume ($20k+) and multiple sharp reversals suggest institutional participation aware of team status. Market undervaluation assessment: At 14%, paiN would need ~18-20% win probability to fairly price the upset in BO3 terms (accounting for single-game variance). Current 14% prices in near-zero head-to-head success or systematic weakness beyond statistics shown. Upset scenario is narrow but real: paiN takes Game 1 via meta pocket pick or preparation advantage; momentum carries into Game 2 upset win. FURIA's superior consistency makes this unlikely but not impossible given BO3 volatility. Confidence asymmetry: Strong confidence in NO (82) due to clear statistical dominance, large sample size (14+ wins for FURIA, 10+ losses for paiN), and tournament structure. Confidence in YES only 28 because paiN's isolated game wins prove capability exists, but no clear path to 2-win series visible in briefing data.", "key_factor": "paiN Gaming's occasional game-level victories (e.g., vs Leviatan, Los Grandes) demonstrate technical capability exists despite systemic underperformance, creating narrow upset potential in BO3 variance."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.18, "confidence_yes": 0.78, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "FURIA dominates on win rate: 64% (14-8) vs paiN's 29% (4-10) \u2014 a 35pp differential that is substantial and consistent across extended sample (22 games each). Standings positioning: FURIA ranks 2nd in CBLOL; paiN ranks 7th of 8 teams, indicating FURIA has demonstrated superior competitive level. Gold differential strongly favors FURIA: +145 GD vs paiN's -144 GD, suggesting FURIA controls game economy and macro play decisively. Game duration metric slightly favors FURIA (32:20 vs 33:23), indicating faster win closure \u2014 a minor edge but consistent with stronger play. BO3 format reduces variance: Best-of-three matchups heavily favor the stronger team; a 35pp win-rate gap typically translates to ~75-85% series win probability for the higher seed. No head-to-head data provided: Cannot identify team-specific matchup dynamics, but large aggregate performance gap dominates in absence of recent direct history. paiN has won individual games (vs Leviatan, Los Grandes): True, but these are outliers in a 4-10 record; consistency of performance across 22 games is far more predictive than isolated victories. Market price (14% YES / 86% NO) is slightly overweighting NO, but not dramatically misaligned with base rates for this win-rate differential. Confidence_yes=78: Strong data supporting FURIA favoritism; win rate, rankings, and metrics all align clearly. Confidence_no=42: Limited head-to-head context and no recent meta/patch notes to assess whether paiN has made mid-season adjustments; BO3 upsets do occur but are rare at this skill differential.", "key_factor": "In professional LoL team matchups, the higher-ranked team (by win rate and standings position) wins approximately 75-85% of series when facing a significantly lower-ranked opponent (35+ percentage point gap). BO3 format slightly reduces upset probability vs single games."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.18, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "MASSIVE STRUCTURAL ADVANTAGE FOR FURIA: 64% win rate (14-8) vs paiN's 29% (4-10) represents a 35pp gap \u2014 one of the largest disparities in the league standings. This is not noise; it's a fundamental performance gulf. paiN Gaming is 7th of 8 teams with league-worst -144 gold differential. FURIA is 2nd with +145 GD. The briefing shows paiN consistently losing macro game decisively. Market price at 14% YES (86% NO) appears RATIONAL, not panicked. The 7-day collapse from 50% to 14% reflects market participants learning that paiN is genuinely terrible this split, not a temporary slump. BO3 FORMAT FAVORS STRONG TEAMS: While single-game variance exists, best-of-three matches reward consistent execution over 2-3 games. paiN's 4-10 record suggests systemic issues, not bad luck. FURIA will likely win 2-0 or 2-1. Individual paiN wins vs Leviatan and Los Grandes noted in briefing, but Los Grandes is 4th (57% WR) and Leviatan is 5th (45% WR). Beating weaker teams \u2260 capability to beat 2nd-place FURIA in a BO3. Market shows sharp volatility on Apr 09 (\u00b16-8pp swings), but price has STABILIZED at 14-15% since. This suggests volatility was pricing in uncertainty that has now resolved toward FURIA confidence. NO HEAD-TO-HEAD DATA PROVIDED: Briefing lacks recent paiN vs FURIA results. This is a data gap on both sides \u2014 cannot confirm historical patterns. However, the aggregate standings speak louder than specific matchup history. SENTIMENT READING: Market is FEAR-driven but JUSTIFIED. The 86% NO price reflects fear of paiN Gaming's weakness, not irrational panic. This is appropriate fear calibrated to reality. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in YES (probability FURIA wins) because the structural data is overwhelming. Lower confidence in NO only because we lack direct head-to-head tactical data and specific player form trends for this exact matchup. Match resolves in ~17 hours (TODAY). No time for news reversals. Market price is likely to stick or tighten further toward 0.01/0.99 if FURIA takes game 1 decisively. RISK TO THIS ANALYSIS: If paiN has recently recovered form or FURIA is overconfident, BO3 upset is possible (~10-15% true probability). But briefing shows no evidence of paiN improvement \u2014 last data points them at 4-10 with -144 GD.", "key_factor": "Fear"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.14, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "FURIA's 64% win rate vs paiN's 29% represents a 35pp delta\u2014exceptionally large in professional play; such disparities rarely reverse in single series absent extraordinary circumstances. paiN Gaming's -144 gold differential is league-worst by significant margin; FURIA's +145 GD shows inverse structural advantage in resource accumulation\u2014a core LoL competency. BO3 format amplifies consistency: while single-game upsets are possible, winning 2-of-3 games requires sustained execution. paiN's 4-10 record suggests systematic issues (draft, macro, mechanics) affecting multiple games. FURIA's secondary metrics (32:20 avg game duration vs 33:23, higher KDA leaders like Duduhh at 10.25 CSM ranking) indicate superior early-game control and objective conversion\u2014both series-critical in BO3. Historical head-to-head data absent from briefing; however, standing-based prediction is robust in round-robin leagues where teams face similar competition pools. The 2nd vs 7th gap is highly predictive. Recent match examples show paiN victories only vs lower-ranked teams (Leviatan 45%, Los Grandes 57%); no wins vs top-4 teams recorded. FURIA has consistent wins vs playoff-contention teams. Market price of 14% YES aligns tightly with pre-match expectations given structural dominance; sharp move history (\u00b18pp on Apr 09) suggests noise from betting flows, not material new information. BO3 meta favors adaptability and team synergy\u2014both metrics where 64% vs 29% win rate suggests FURIA holds decisive advantage. paiN would need multiple upsets within single series (low probability stacked events). Event timing is TODAY with ~17 hours to resolution; no reversal catalysts (roster changes, emergency substitutions, server issues hinted at in briefing) are evident or credible at this late stage.", "key_factor": "In competitive BO3 formats, cumulative team strength metrics (win rate, gold differential, KDA consistency) are highly predictive of series outcomes, and a 35-percentage-point win-rate gap with negative gold differential indicates structural team weaknesses that are difficult to overcome in multi-game contests."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.08, "confidence_yes": 0.92, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "FURIA is overwhelming favorite: 64% win rate (14-8), 2nd place; paiN is 29% win rate (4-10), 7th place with -144 gold differential \u2014 a 35pp gap reflects sustained, systematic weakness. paiN's individual game victories (vs Leviatan, Los Grandes) are exceptions in a 4-10 record; winning 2+ games in a BO3 vs a 64% FURIA team requires sustained execution paiN has not demonstrated. BLACK SWAN: paiN's standout performers (Trigger: 12.16 CSM high, 10 kills in games; Stepz: 19.6 KDA in Split 1) carry disproportionate weight in their limited wins. If either is benched, replaced, or absent due to roster management/health, paiN loses a critical edge and becomes even more vulnerable. Briefing silent on: roster continuity, recent injuries, substitutes available, internal team health, or whether players were tested/available in last 48 hours before match. BO3 format magnifies team quality gap; paiN would need to steal 2 games at 25%+ conversion rate. A key player absence drops that probability to ~5-12%. Market price of 14% YES is already skeptical; if a late roster announcement (within hours of match) reveals a sub or injury, paiN's true odds collapse to single digits, and sharp traders who had signal could push YES to 5-8% before resolution. FURIA's depth and stable roster consistency (no standout player dependency; balanced kills/gold) makes them resilient to injury, whereas paiN relies on spike performances from 1-2 players.", "key_factor": "paiN Gaming's ADC Trigger or jungler Stepz becomes unavailable due to illness, injury, or substitute-roster activation, forcing a roster swap into an unfamiliar or underperforming lineup."}], "final_score": 0.25767578124999996, "no_score": 0.7042406876790832, "edge": 0.11267578124999997, "no_edge": -0.15075931232091677, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 50% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1892927", "question": "LoL: paiN Gaming vs FURIA Esports (BO3) - CBLOL Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between paiN Gaming and FURIA Esports in the CBLOL Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 13 at 5:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"paiN Gaming\" if paiN Gaming win the match against FURIA Esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"FURIA Esports\" if FURIA Esports win the match against paiN Gaming.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T03:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T21:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.145, "volume_usd": 20640.601293, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["39373675295037328833547050543519511075469965665368883525472791423854857412912", "46784607294219669715123582020395005869982907364604940956733916238847060209487"]}, "key_facts": ["CBLOL 2026 Split 1 is an offline Brazilian LoL tournament organized by Riot Games.", "This S-Tier tournament takes place from Mar 28 to Jun 06 2026 featuring 8", "# \n\n# Team ranking\n\nCBLOL Cup 2026 Team standings\n\n