 Pentakill leaderboard."], "news_summary": "paiN Gaming and FURIA Esports are set to compete in a CBLOL Regular Season BO3 match. In the CBLOL Cup 2026 standings, FURIA holds a strong 64% win rate (14-8) while paiN Gaming significantly lags with only 29% win rate (4-10), placing them 7th of 8 teams. Recent CBLOL 2026 Split 1 match data shows paiN competed against RED Canids but the outcome of that specific match is unclear from available data.", "side_yes_case": ["FURIA maintains 64% win rate in CBLOL Cup 2026 (14-8 record), ranking 2nd overall", "paiN Gaming severely underperforming with league-worst 29% win rate (4-10 record) and -144 GD", "FURIA has significantly better game metrics including lower game duration (32:20 vs 33:23) and positive gold differential", "paiN Gaming ranked 7th of 8 teams, showing consistent weakness across recent competition"], "side_no_case": ["paiN Gaming showed individual game victories in recent matches including against Leviatan and Los Grandes", "Match-to-match variance in BO3 format allows upsets; paiN has demonstrated ability to win games despite poor overall record", "Specific head-to-head history between these two teams not provided in available data", "Recent meta shifts or patch changes could impact team preparation differently"], "key_context": ["CBLOL 2026 Split 1 regular season runs Mar 28 - Jun 06, 2026 (offline tournament)", "FURIA significantly outranks paiN in standings: 2nd vs 7th place with 35 percentage point win rate gap", "BO3 format provides multiple games, reducing single-game variance but favoring consistent team performance", "Data covers CBLOL Cup 2026 (appears to be preliminary/qualifier tournament) with recent matches from late January-early February 2026"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-13T10:25:14.987567Z", "price_history": {"yes": {"token_id": "39373675295037328833547050543519511075469965665368883525472791423854857412912", "data_points": 103, "weighted_avg": 0.21024807528723666, "change_1w_pp": -36.0, "change_24h_pp": -0.5000000000000004, "volatility_24h": 0.8844725358464596, "direction": "FALLING", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-09T05:00:45Z", "delta_pp": -6.0}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-09T07:00:43Z", "delta_pp": 8.000000000000002}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-09T08:00:44Z", "delta_pp": -7.500000000000001}]}, "no": {"token_id": "46784607294219669715123582020395005869982907364604940956733916238847060209487", "data_points": 123, "weighted_avg": 0.7907409609283285, "change_1w_pp": 36.0, "change_24h_pp": 0.5000000000000004, "volatility_24h": 0.8187763655859311, "direction": "RISING", "sharp_moves": [{"timestamp": "2026-04-09T05:00:43Z", "delta_pp": 5.999999999999995}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-09T07:00:41Z", "delta_pp": -7.9999999999999964}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-09T08:00:41Z", "delta_pp": 7.499999999999996}]}, "fetched_at": "2026-04-13T10:25:15.557453Z"}}}, "resolution": {"resolved_at": "2026-04-14T03:00:00Z", "winning_side": "NO", "final_yes_price": 0.0, "checked_at": "2026-04-14T10:12:09.641570+00:00", "source": "gamma_api"}, "analysis": {"kind": "missed_opportunity", "summary": "Missed opportunity \u2014 council favored NO at 70% (6/7 agents, 1 high-conv) but PASSed. Reason: NO-side confidence too low: 50% (need \u226567%)", "agents_with_winner": [{"agent": "The Bear", "prob": 0.18, "side": "NO", "side_conf": 0.82, "key_factor": "paiN Gaming's occasional game-level victories (e.g., vs Leviatan, Los Grandes) demonstrate technical capability exists despite systemic underperformance, creating narrow upset potential in BO3 variance."}, {"agent": "The Rules Lawyer", "prob": 0.14, "side": "NO", "side_conf": 0.45, "key_factor": "Criteria are clear and unambiguous; primary risk is resolution source delay beyond 2 hours, but outcome determination is straightforward win/loss."}, {"agent": "The Domain Specialist", "prob": 0.14, "side": "NO", "side_conf": 0.45, "key_factor": "In competitive BO3 formats, cumulative team strength metrics (win rate, gold differential, KDA consistency) are highly predictive of series outcomes, and a 35-percentage-point win-rate gap with negative gold differential indicates structural team weaknesses that are difficult to overcome in multi-game contests."}, {"agent": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "prob": 0.18, "side": "NO", "side_conf": 0.42, "key_factor": "In professional LoL team matchups, the higher-ranked team (by win rate and standings position) wins approximately 75-85% of series when facing a significantly lower-ranked opponent (35+ percentage point gap). BO3 format slightly reduces upset probability vs single games."}, {"agent": "The Sentiment Analyst", "prob": 0.18, "side": "NO", "side_conf": 0.35, "key_factor": "Fear"}, {"agent": "The Contrarian", "prob": 0.08, "side": "NO", "side_conf": 0.28, "key_factor": "paiN Gaming's ADC Trigger or jungler Stepz becomes unavailable due to illness, injury, or substitute-roster activation, forcing a roster swap into an unfamiliar or underperforming lineup."}], "agents_against_winner": [{"agent": "The Bull", "prob": 0.83, "side": "YES", "side_conf": 0.85, "key_factor": "FURIA's dominant 64% win rate (14-8) and 2nd-place standing vs paiN's severe underperformance (29% win rate, 4-10, 7th place, -144 GD) creates a structural competitive gap that BO3 format amplifies rather than erases."}], "median_prob": 0.18, "coin_flip": false}}
{"run_id": "26e1e834-f6dd-4e40-a8a0-9e7a00ba4903", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T10:27:14.721806+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1920643", "question": "Valorant: LYON vs STREAMER ARENA (BO3) - VCL Latin America North ACE Masters Group A", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between LYON and STREAMER ARENA in the VCL Latin America North ACE Masters Group A, initially scheduled for April 13 at 6:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"LYON\" if LYON win the match against STREAMER ARENA.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"STREAMER ARENA\" if STREAMER ARENA win the match against LYON.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T04:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T22:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.66, "volume_usd": 812.738368, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["65614446698510255837575039784601015854654268682553547836953888239066564192122", "91636247710676367710649314207198346569796738589616930685730068323902086143534"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "LYON demonstrates consistent individual performance: Mephisto (1.51-1.68 rating across recent matches), Feniz (1.00-1.35 rating with 70-88% KAST), Jow (1.19-1.39 rating), Kess (1.01-1.65 rating), Logan (0.99-1.38 rating) showing distributed fragging power. Team-level coordination evident: LYON defeated FUSION (BO3) with all five players posting competitive ratings (1.05-1.68 range), indicating balanced utility and economy management rather than single-carry dependency. Feniz's controller play (viper/omen) consistently enables team success with high KAST percentages (70-88%) and positive +/- metrics, suggesting strong utility setup and round-winning contributions. Mephisto's waylay/initiator consistency (1.31-1.73 rating, 83-96% KAST) indicates reliable map control and entry fragging across diverse map pools. No performance data provided for STREAMER ARENA in briefing limits confidence in probability assessment; cannot evaluate opponent's recent form, agent flexibility, or head-to-head matchup dynamics. Market price at YES 66% suggests modest consensus confidence in LYON, slightly lower than briefing performance data would justify; recent 24-hour movement shows -5.5pp on YES (declining confidence). BO3 format allows LYON to adapt across multiple maps; historical data shows strong adaptation capability with consistent player performances across different map vetoes. Event timing TODAY (resolves ~18 hours) with match scheduled April 13 6:00 PM ET - match likely already completed or imminent; market volatility (2.8pp/hr YES, 5.3pp/hr NO) suggests unresolved match status as of briefing timestamp. Absence of STREAMER ARENA data is material constraint: cannot assess whether opponent has comparable individual firepower, recent tournament placement, or potential counter-strategies to LYON's meta picks. LYON's Kess shows variable sova/fade performance (0.56-1.65 rating range) and Logan's controller play (0.95-1.38 rating) represent potential defensive weaknesses if opponent exploits utility gaps, though sample size is limited.", "key_factor": "STREAMER ARENA performance data entirely absent from briefing; assessment relies heavily on LYON statistics without comparable opponent evaluation."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "LYON's recent performance data is substantial and consistent: Mephisto averages 1.3+ rating across multiple matches (1.68 vs FUSION, 1.51 vs LAZER, 1.31 vs LAZER), demonstrating elite entry/waylay play that translates across maps. LYON's team composition shows distributed fragging power\u2014Feniz (1.0-1.35 rating), Jow (1.21-1.39 rating), Kess (1.01-1.65 rating), Logan (0.95-1.38 rating)\u2014indicating no single-carry dependency and thus stronger tournament resilience. Feniz's controller/viper play provides utility win conditions with elite KAST percentages (74-88%), enabling team to win rounds through information and utility advantage rather than pure gunplay alone. BO3 format favors LYON's demonstrated adaptability: across multiple opponents (Contra, FUSION, LAZER), LYON shows varied agent comfort and consistent round-win trading, suggesting flexible map strategy. Market repricing: YES side fell from 73% EMA to 66% current (\u22125.5pp in 24hr), yet the data quality gap (LYON matches detailed; STREAMER ARENA absent) argues against this decline\u2014market may be overcorrecting to uncertainty. STREAMER ARENA performance statistics are entirely absent from the briefing, preventing comparative analysis of that team's firepower, utility setup, or recent form\u2014this is a critical asymmetry favoring the known quantity (LYON). NO side confidence is constrained by lack of STREAMER ARENA data: cannot verify opponent's rating distribution, duelist/initiator quality, or controller reliability, making risk assessment impossible on the underdog side. LYON's Kess shows variable sova/fade ratings (0.79-1.65) but high floor in ult-dependent utility rounds; Logan's lower individual ratings (0.95-0.99) offset by elite KAST (84-94%), suggesting macro discipline over individual fragging peaks. Potential weakness: LYON's slightly lower headshot consistency (14-37% HS%) on some agents suggests aim-dependent vulnerability if STREAMER ARENA leverages aggressive duelists\u2014but without opponent data, cannot quantify this risk. Timing factor: Match is TODAY (resolves in ~18 hours), meaning significant reversal of LYON's 66% odds would require STREAMER ARENA to demonstrate unexpected elite-tier performance in a single BO3\u2014high burden of proof for underdog in single-elimination. Market volatility (2.8pp/hr on YES) suggests informed traders maintaining positions; the +39.0pp spike on Apr 09 (potentially LYON qualifier win or roster confirmation) followed by stabilization at 73% EMA implies consensus solidified before recent 5.5pp decline. Briefing confirms BO3 format and Group A context but provides no evidence of STREAMER ARENA's tournament tier, recent results, or roster strength\u2014YES side's advantage is data-backed consistency, not opponent weakness demonstration.", "key_factor": "LYON's demonstrated team depth and Mephisto's elite consistency (1.3-1.7 rating across recent matches) establish clear competitive advantage in a BO3 format where adaptation