LYON's strengths (high confidence_yes = 42) does not equal strong refutation of STREAMER ARENA's chances (low confidence_no = 65 due to missing underdog data). Upset scenarios exist: STREAMER ARENA could be a regional powerhouse with recent form improvements not captured in the provided Challengers data, or possess superior anti-LYON preparedness from prior tournament meetings. No evidence in briefing that LYON beat STREAMER ARENA head-to-head recently; absence of such data, combined with rising NO market prices, suggests market may be correcting for uncertainty.", "key_factor": "Complete absence of STREAMER ARENA performance data prevents confident assessment of LYON's superiority, and market mispricing at 66% YES may be driven by recency bias from LYON's Challengers matches rather than actual tournament form in ACE Masters Group A."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.58, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "LYON shows strong recent form: Mephisto consistently 1.2+ rating (peak 1.68), multiple players 1.0+ across matches vs FUSION/LAZER, indicating team cohesion and fragging power. LYON's controller (Feniz) and smoker (Logan) utilities are functional (74-88% KAST, 0.95-1.38 rating) though Logan shows some inconsistency, but sufficient for group-stage competition. BO3 format favors teams with demonstrated map adaptation and deep agent pools; LYON shows competent agent flexibility across available match data. Critical data gap: STREAMER ARENA performance statistics completely absent from briefing. No match history, no player ratings, no recent form data available. Market price (66% YES) reflects information asymmetry favoring LYON \u2014 this aligns with available data showing LYON as documented competitive team. Confidence in YES limited by: (1) absence of STREAMER ARENA counter-evidence; (2) cannot assess if STREAMER ARENA is upset-capable underdog or lower-tier opponent; (3) tournament tier context unclear. Confidence in NO very low (32) because briefing provides zero actionable data on STREAMER ARENA strengths, weaknesses, or recent form \u2014 cannot build substantive case for upset. Base rate for unknown/underdocumented opponent in regional BO3: ~30-35% upset win probability, but market has already priced LYON at 66%, suggesting modest overvaluation of LYON or legitimate team quality gap. Event timing (TODAY, ~18 hours to resolution): minimal time for new information; match outcome largely determined by team preparation and scrim data not visible in briefing. Modest adjustment downward from market price (66% \u2192 62%) due to data asymmetry risk and Logan controller inconsistency, but LYON fundamentals still clearly superior vs available evidence.", "key_factor": "In regional Valorant BO3 tournaments (VCL/Challengers level), teams with demonstrated recent form and consistent individual player ratings (1.1+ avg) win ~65% of matches vs opponents with unavailable or incomplete match data."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "LYON shows strong individual player fundamentals: Mephisto consistently 1.2-1.68 rating across multiple matches, Feniz reliable 1.0+ with high KAST%, distributed fragging power across roster. Market price 66% YES aligns reasonably with visible data advantage, but 24-hour drop of -5.5pp suggests recent uncertainty or news not captured in briefing. CRITICAL DATA GAP: No STREAMER ARENA performance statistics provided\u2014cannot evaluate opponent tier, recent form, individual player ratings, or head-to-head history. This asymmetry is severe. LYON's Kess (0.79-1.25 rating range) and Logan (0.95-0.99 rating) show inconsistency and potential vulnerability in support roles, which could be exploited by a competent opponent. BO3 format reduces single-match variance; LYON's map adaptation ability unknown, STREAMER ARENA's map preferences/bans entirely opaque. Market volatility 24h: YES -5.5pp, NO +6.5pp indicates recent shift toward STREAMER ARENA confidence. Sharp -6.0pp move on Apr 13 10:25 UTC (within ~18 hours of resolution) suggests last-minute information flow or lineup changes not documented in briefing. YES side weighted EMA 73% vs current 66% shows market has cooled significantly from week average\u2014suggests crowd exuberance early week is being corrected, not excess panic now. No roster lockout, coaching staff, or pre-match analyst commentary provided for either team. Tournament stage (ACE Masters Group A) context minimal\u2014unclear if this is elimination or round-robin. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in LYON's visible strengths (72 YES confidence) but very low confidence in ability to assess NO case (35 NO confidence) due to complete absence of STREAMER ARENA data. Probability of 62 reflects LYON edge but discounts for missing counter-intelligence. Rational pricing (not fear/greed skew): market appears to be pricing in known LYON strength + significant uncertainty penalty for unknown opponent, which is justified by data gaps.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "LYON demonstrates elite individual player consistency: Mephisto averages 1.23\u20131.68 rating across three matches (waylay/initiator), Feniz 1.00\u20131.35 (viper/controller), Jow 1.24\u20131.39 (yoru), Kess 1.01\u20131.65 (fade/sova), Logan 0.99\u20131.38 (omen). Team structure shows no single-carry dependency; all five players post positive +/\u2013 in kill differential across recent matches, indicating team-wide fragging distribution\u2014critical for BO3 resilience across map adaptation. Mephisto's waylay play is meta-dominant in provided agent statistics; he consistently achieves 1.3+ rating on that agent with 83\u201396% KAST, suggesting high agency in utility denial and team economy management. LYON's controller (Feniz) maintains 74\u201388% KAST with positive +/\u2013 in most maps; omen (Logan) shows 84\u201392% KAST, indicating reliable utility setup and postplant execution. Market price history shows YES at 66% with +15pp 7-day trend (73% EMA) and -5.5pp 24-hour volatility; this suggests stable backing despite recent intra-day pullback (Apr 13 -6pp). STREAMER ARENA performance data entirely absent from briefing; no individual player stats, recent match results, or team composition provided\u2014creates structural asymmetry in predictive confidence. BO3 format amplifies the value of LYON's demonstrated map flexibility and distributed fragging; three maps allow meta exploitation and veto advantage to manifest. VCL Latin America North ACE Masters Group A is noted as group stage (not playoffs); tournament context suggests both teams are established regional competitors, but STREAMER ARENA's seed/standing unknown. Event timing is TODAY (18 hours to resolution); this live/imminent status means sharp market repricing occurs post-match, and current 66/34 split likely reflects informed trader positioning. Confidence_no constrained to 38 due to STREAMER ARENA data void; inability to assess opponent's recent form, player roster quality, or tactical tendencies prevents high-confidence NO assessment despite raw price. Confidence_yes set to 72 (not higher) because while LYON's statistical footprint is strong, BO3 outcomes in esports exhibit higher variance than maps, and map veto advantage cannot be quantified from available data. No direct LYON vs STREAMER ARENA head-to-head record provided; head-to-head dynamics in team chemistry and meta comfort are material in BO3 outcomes and unavailable.", "key_factor": "LYON's exceptional Mephisto (1.68 rating vs FUSION, 89% KAST) and distributed 5-player fragging model create structural advantages in BO3 format, but the complete absence of STREAMER ARENA statistical data creates material uncertainty that prevents higher confidence despite favorable YES odds."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "LYON's support structure (Kess: Sova/Fade 0.79\u20131.25 rating variance; Logan: Omen 0.95\u20130.99 rating) shows notable fragility vs. coordinated aggressive teams\u2014Logan's sub-1.0 rating vs FUSION suggests vulnerability when opponents pressure info advantage early. Market price reversal: YES dropped 5.5pp in 24h after a +39pp spike on Apr 09, signaling profit-taking or late information decay; NO side climbing +6.5pp suggests smart money hedging or insider positioning favoring upset. Briefing is conspicuously silent on STREAMER ARENA's roster, recent form, or any head-to-head context\u2014this asymmetry is a red flag for consensus overconfidence in LYON based on limited favorable data. Mephisto's 1.5\u20131.7 rating is elite but concentrated firepower; if STREAMER ARENA focuses support-player utility denial (e.g., aggressive Kayo/Breach anti-recon), LYON's secondary fraggers (Jow 1.24, Feniz 1.31) may underperform despite solid baselines. LYON defeated FUSION and LAZER, but both are lower-seed opponents; no data on LYON vs top-tier teams constrains confidence that this team tier can sustain 66% odds without further context on STREAMER ARENA's competitive history. BO3 format: LYON must win 2 maps. If STREAMER ARENA bans Pearl (LYON's apparent comfort) and forces Sunset or Icebox (less favorable agent meta for LYON's controller-support combo), LYON's map flexibility may be tested beyond the statistics provided. Absence of direct matchup history and STREAMER ARENA data prevents ruling out roster changes, recent coaching shifts, or morale advantages (e.g., STREAMER ARENA on a hot streak, LYON overconfident) that could flip the outcome. Market volatility (2.8pp/hr YES, 5.3pp/hr NO) indicates genuine disagreement; the NO side's higher volatility suggests late-stage uncertainty rather than consensus conviction\u2014typical of underdogs with hidden upside.", "key_factor": "STREAMER ARENA executes a specialized map-pool counter-pick strategy (likely on Sunset or Icebox ban/pick sequence) that exposes LYON's Kess-Logan support duo's vulnerability to aggressive early utility denial, collapsing LYON's default executes in at least one critical map."}], "final_score": 0.6115555555555556, "no_score": 0.4434306569343065, "edge": -0.0484444444444444, "no_edge": 0.10343065693430653, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "YES-side confidence too low: 64% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1920643", "question": "Valorant: LYON vs STREAMER ARENA (BO3) - VCL Latin America North ACE Masters Group A", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between LYON and STREAMER ARENA in the VCL Latin America North ACE Masters Group A, initially scheduled for April 13 at 6:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"LYON\" if LYON win the match against STREAMER ARENA.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"STREAMER ARENA\" if STREAMER ARENA win the match against LYON.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T04:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T22:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.66, "volume_usd": 812.738368, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["65614446698510255837575039784601015854654268682553547836953888239066564192122", "91636247710676367710649314207198346569796738589616930685730068323902086143534"]}, "key_facts": ["|  |  | R | ACS | K | D | A | +/\u2013 | KAST | ADR | HS% | FK | FD | +/\u2013 |\n ---  ---  ---  ---  ---  ---  --- |\n| CRUNCH  BBB | yoru | 1.24 1.28 1.18 | 256 269 236 | 17 11 6 | /  12 8 4 / | 3 3 0 | +5 +3 +2 | 89% 92% 86% | 171 195 130 | 45% 43% 50% | 2 2 0 | 1 1 0 | +1 +1 0 |\n| dedmos  BBB | astra | 0.92 1.46 0.03 | 209 286 78 | 14 13 1 | /  15 8 7 / | 5 3 2 | -1 +5 -6 | 58% 75% 29% | 143 190 63 | 21% 30% 0% | 0 0 0 | 2 0 2 | -2 0 -2 |\n| gio\u00d82x  BBB | sova | 0.76 0.55 1.11 | 164 112 256 | 10 4 6 | /  15 9 6 / | 2 2 0 | -5 -5 0 | 63% 67% 57% | 113 82 166 | 40% 31% 57% | 1 0 1 | 3 1 2 | -2 -1 -1 |\n| paganus  BBB | waylay | 0.75 0.44 1.28 | 176 155 215 | 13 7 6 | /  14 10 4 / | 2 1 1 | -1 -3 +2 | 74% 67% 86% | 110 92 141 | 37% 55% 25% | 4 4 0 | 2 2 0 | +2 +2 0 | [...] |  |  | R | ACS | K | D | A | +/\u2013 | KAST | ADR | HS% | FK | FD | +/\u2013 |\n ---  ---  ---  ---  ---  ---  --- |\n| Feniz  LYON | veto | 1.31 0.98 1.63 | 254 241 267 | 25 