{"run_id": "eda35713-67d0-48ec-814b-62eb1c6677e1", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T18:26:21.234392+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1963170", "question": "Valorant: UCAM Esports Club vs FALKE ESPORTS (BO3) - VCL Spain: Rising Phase 1 Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant Lower bracket quarterfinal 2 match between UCAM Esports Club and FALKE ESPORTS in the VCL Spain: Rising Phase 1 Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 13 at 2:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"UCAM Esports Club\" if UCAM Esports Club win the match against FALKE ESPORTS.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"FALKE ESPORTS\" if FALKE ESPORTS win the match against UCAM Esports Club.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-13T22:40:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T16:40:00Z", "yes_price": 0.245, "volume_usd": 50274.08927300001, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["57628374770664949582620450542097128678115926684611532310275931410712638839911", "51415966831688563381603021682311584735597072061676340228173182407511718202923"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.22, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: UCAM Esports Club wins the BO3 match (2 maps) vs FALKE ESPORTS. Resolution criteria are unambiguous \u2014 match must be played to completion; forfeits/walkovers resolve 50-50. MARKET SIGNAL: Current price is YES=24% (down sharply from 68% on Apr 13 01:00 UTC, -31.5pp in 24h). The -57pp drop at Apr 13 18:25 UTC suggests new information strongly favored FALKE, likely from live match performance or pre-match roster/form revelation. TIMING CONTEXT: Event is TODAY with ~4 hours to resolution (2026-04-13 22:40 UTC). Match scheduled 2:00PM ET (April 13) = 6:00PM UTC, already begun or recently completed at data cutoff (18:25 UTC). Market price reflects near-real-time outcome signal. AVAILABLE DATA ASYMMETRY: Briefing contains detailed agent selections and map vetoes from multiple past matches (Maps: Haven, Split, Pearl, Lotus, Bind, Fracture, Breeze; agents shown: Neon, Omen, Cypher, Viper, Sova, etc.) but NO win rates, recent head-to-head records, or current roster strength comparisons between UCAM and FALKE. CASE FOR UCAM (YES, ~22%): Search results mention 'UCAM demonstrated competitive performance in recent Challengers matches with strong individual statistics from players like Famsii and B1SK' and 'playoff format experience.' However, no quantified win rate, streak data, or direct comparison to FALKE provided. CASE FOR FALKE (NO, ~78%): Market sharp move (-57pp at 18:25 UTC, ~5.5h before scheduled match conclusion) indicates STRONG real-time signal favoring FALKE. This timing suggests either live match performance (FALKE leading after maps 1-2) or pre-match intelligence (roster advantage, opponent withdrawal threat, or form differential). NO counter-evidence in briefing supports UCAM. DATA QUALITY GAPS: (1) No recent head-to-head results. (2) No win-loss records for either team in Spring 2026. (3) No commentary on roster changes, player injuries, or team cohesion. (4) Map pool data shown is historical; unknown whether UCAM/FALKE's actual map strengths match historical meta. MARKET INTERPRETATION: 24% YES price reflects rational market belief that FALKE has ~78% win probability. Sharp -57pp move at 18:25 UTC (match likely live or just-completed) suggests strong directional signal, not speculative repositioning. This is the most reliable data point available. CONFIDENCE SPLIT REASONING: confidence_yes=28 (low): Minimal positive evidence for UCAM; no recent form, no head-to-head advantage, market pricing and sharp move both favor FALKE. confidence_no=32 (low): Lack of detailed FALKE roster/form data and no direct match metrics prevent high confidence; rely primarily on market signal and inferred match progress. CRITERIA AMBIGUITY: None flagged. Team names are unambiguous; BO3 format is standard; 50-50 provision only applies to cancellation/forfeiture (not applicable here based on market activity). RESOLUTION MECHANISM RISK: Low. VLR.gg is established esports source; 2-hour fallback to 'credible reporting + video evidence' is reasonable for a Spanish regional match. No team name ambiguity. ~5% downward adjustment to confidence_no for potential oracle delay, but outcome resolution itself appears likely by deadline.", "key_factor": "Briefing data contains extensive agent/map veto details but no recent head-to-head records, win rates, or current form metrics for either team; resolution mechanism is clear but outcome assessment is severely data-constrained."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.24, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "NO SIDE MOMENTUM: The market has undergone a dramatic 57pp swing in favor of NO (FALKE) in the last 6 hours, rising from ~19% to 76%. This sharp, recent move typically reflects informed trader activity or updated information about team form, roster status, or matchup dynamics. TIMING & IMMINENCE: Event resolves in ~4 hours. A 57pp move this close to match start is unlikely to be noise\u2014it suggests traders with confidence in FALKE's ability to win are entering at good odds before execution. BRIEFING DATA ASYMMETRY: The briefing provides extensive historical match data and map veto patterns for UCAM across multiple tournaments, but contains NO recent performance metrics, roster updates, or head-to-head data for either team in their current state. This asymmetry is critical. UCAM CASE WEAKNESSES: While UCAM shows historical competitiveness and map flexibility, the briefing notes 'limited specific recent form data for UCAM in direct comparison to FALKE's current state.' No recent win/loss record, player performance, or playoff momentum is documented. FALKE CASE WEAKNESSES: Search results explicitly state 'Search results do not provide FALKE's recent match statistics or roster performance metrics.' We cannot independently justify FALKE's dominance from briefing data alone. MARKET PRICE AS SIGNAL: In a data-scarce environment with imminent resolution, the 76% NO price reflects the collective confidence of active traders. The magnitude and recency of the swing (6 hours before start) suggests this is weighted information, not speculation. LOWER BRACKET CONTEXT: This is a lower bracket quarterfinal\u2014both teams are already in elimination territory, suggesting survival motivation b