METRY: Briefing provides extensive agent/map veto tables from UCAM's recent matches but NO parallel FALKE performance metrics, recent form, or head-to-head history. The council is evaluating UCAM on granular map pick patterns while flying blind on FALKE's current state. This imbalance is itself a red flag. LOWER-BRACKET PSYCHOLOGY: This is a lower-bracket quarterfinal \u2014 both teams have already lost once. UCAM in particular may carry urgency/desperation, while FALKE (if seeded higher) could have morale/preparation gaps. BO3 format amplifies volatility when one team is mentally sharper. PLAYOFF RECENCY: UCAM demonstrated playoff experience in Stage 1, but no data on FALKE's playoff pedigree or clutch performance. Rising/Challengers tournaments reward teams that peak under pressure; insufficient info on FALKE's historical tournament execution. MAP VETO SIGNAL SILENCE: Briefing shows UCAM's veto patterns across multiple iterations, suggesting consistency. But it does NOT show UCAM's recent win rates on their picked/banned maps vs. the current meta. If FALKE has studied UCAM's predictable veto tendencies and prepared specifically for them, this consistency becomes liability. AGENT META SHIFT: The detailed agent selections span multiple prior tournaments (Stage 1, earlier phases). If Valorant received a balance patch or agent nerf between those matches and today (April 13), UCAM's established playbooks could be gutted while FALKE pivoted faster. TIMING PRECISION: Match is 'TODAY' with ~4 hours to resolution. At this stage, final roster confirmations, substitution announcements, and injury/illness disclosures happen in final hours. A single player benched or a stand-in subbed in could flip coaching strategy entirely. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: confidence_yes=35 (weak, due to missing FALKE comparator data and inability to validate UCAM's true recent form vs. current opponent); confidence_no=42 (only slightly higher, because briefing lacks FALKE's recent metrics, their playoff history, and current roster/coaching state). Both sides suffer severe information gaps; market price disparity (76% NO) may overweight the 24% YES collapse without enough countervailing detail.", "key_factor": "UCAM field a roster substitution or tactical pivot specifically tuned to exploit FALKE's recent meta shifts, or FALKE suffers a last-minute player availability/connectivity issue in a lower-bracket match where preparation margins are razor-thin."}], "final_score": 0.26451612903225813, "no_score": 0.7352226720647774, "edge": 0.019516129032258134, "no_edge": -0.019777327935222577, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 35% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1963170", "question": "Valorant: UCAM Esports Club vs FALKE ESPORTS (BO3) - VCL Spain: Rising Phase 1 Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant Lower bracket quarterfinal 2 match between UCAM Esports Club and FALKE ESPORTS in the VCL Spain: Rising Phase 1 Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 13 at 2:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"UCAM Esports Club\" if UCAM Esports Club win the match against FALKE ESPORTS.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"FALKE ESPORTS\" if FALKE ESPORTS win the match against UCAM Esports Club.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has no