but without supporting data, this reflects sentiment rather than informed analysis. CONFIDENCE LIMITATION: Both confidence scores set to 22 (well below 50) due to symmetric ignorance \u2014 neither side can be reasonably evaluated with briefing data alone. PROBABILITY ALIGNMENT: Probability score of 42 mirrors current market price, reflecting the absence of directional evidence favoring either team. This is NOT a 50-50 coin flip, as the market has priced in a slight NO lean; absent contradictory data, deferring to market price is appropriate.", "key_factor": "Insufficient data on either team's current roster, form, or relative skill levels prevents meaningful probability estimation beyond market price reflection."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "MARKET STRUCTURE: NO is priced at 58% vs YES at 42%, establishing clear market consensus favoring FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports. This ~16-point spread in a binary BO1 match reflects genuine edge perception rather than random noise. DATA VACUUM FOR BOTH TEAMS: Briefing contains zero roster info, recent form, head-to-head records, or standings positions for either ZOTIX or FC Famalic\u00e3o. This symmetric information deficit means the market price itself becomes the most reliable signal. ASYMMETRIC CONFIDENCE REQUIRED: Because substantive data is absent for BOTH sides, confidence scores on each side must remain depressed (confidence_yes=25, confidence_no=28). We cannot robustly defend either outcome with evidence-based reasoning. BO1 VARIANCE MITIGATES FAVORITE STATUS: Best-of-1 format inherently reduces skill-based predictability and increases upset probability. A single map eliminates team adaptability. This structural element prevents the NO favorite from being priced higher than ~60%, explaining why 58% is plausible floor. ESEA ADVANCED TIER CONTEXT: Mid-tier European advanced league suggests both teams are regional semi-professionals with volatile