 when briefing is data-poor.", "key_factor": "NO side (FC Famalic\u00e3o) is favored by market pricing at 58%, suggesting better-informed bettors perceive a structural or form advantage despite data scarcity."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains zero substantive information on either team's current roster, recent form, head-to-head record, or competitive standing. Market prices (42% YES / 58% NO) appear to reflect generic favoritism rather than evidence-based analysis. BO1 FORMAT AMPLIFIES UPSET POTENTIAL: Single-map matches inherently favor variance and momentum over skill stratification. Even a significantly weaker team can win a BO1 if they prepare a specific map pick or execute a single strong performance. This structural feature should floor ZOTIX's win probability above its apparent skill disadvantage. MARKET MISPRICING SIGNALS: The 16-point spread (58% vs 42%) suggests the market has confidence differentiating these teams. However, with no roster data, recent results, or form metrics provided in the briefing, this spread cannot be justified by evidence\u2014it may reflect betting heuristics or one-sided information. UNDERDOG ADVOCACY: ZOTIX at 42% is genuinely underpriced IF: (a) recent form favors ZOTIX but was not captured in the briefing, (b) map pool advantage exists for ZOTIX, (c) roster changes or key player acquisition happened after data collection, or (d) FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports are overrated in the market's mind. FAVORITE VULNERABILITY: FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports at 58% lacks supporting evidence in the briefing. No wins, standings position, or roster quality data is presented. The favorite is being backed by assumption, not substance. LEAGUE CONTEXT: ESEA Advanced Europe is mid-tier competitive CS. Teams at this level show high variance in single-map outcomes. A 58% favorite in BO1 is not extreme, but without data differentiating the teams, the spread is speculative. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Both confidence scores are LOW (28 and 26) because the briefing provides essentially zero concrete performance or roster data for either side. This is a data-starved market. The 42% probability reflects market consensus only, not analytical conviction. TIMING CONSIDERATION: Match resolves TODAY (~7 hours away). No time for new information to emerge. Market pricing will likely tighten toward binary outcomes as match start approaches, but current prices cannot be validated against briefing evidence. VERDICT: ZOTIX as underdog is NOT underpriced on evidence (there is no evidence). However, the complete absence of data means both teams' true strength is unknown. Holding YES at 42% reflects market consensus while acknowledging that BO1 variance and missing roster/form data create legitimate upset potential. Confidence in both directions is minimal.", "key_factor": "Best-of-1 format creates inherent variance that can neutralize skill gaps, and complete absence of concrete team data means market pricing may reflect generic assumptions rather than actual roster strength or recent form."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.5, "confidence_yes": 0.2, "confidence_no": 0.2, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: No roster information, recent form, head-to-head records, or standings position provided for either ZOTIX or FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports Search results contain only general ESEA Season 53 structure and unrelated roster changes; neither team appears in visible standings or match data BO1 format inherently high-variance: single-map elimination creates elevated upset potential vs. BO3, suggesting base equilibrium near 50% Current market price (42% YES / 58% NO) implies modest NO favoritism, but no briefing data justifies directional confidence in either direction Without team skill assessment, recent performance, map pool synergies, or player form, cannot establish which team is favored Match is TODAY (resolves ~7 hours), leaving no time for additional information discovery \u2014 confidence must remain LOW on both sides Base rate for mid-tier Counter-Strike BO1 matches: unknown to high precision; assuming ~50% win distribution absent team-specific data Market mispricing cannot be detected without player/roster/form data; current 42/58 split may reflect informed traders with private knowledge or may be noise Given symmetrical information vacuum, probability_score defaults to 50 (genuine coin flip per instructions); both confidence scores capped at 20 due to severe data insufficiency", "key_factor": "BO1 Counter-Strike matches at mid-tier competitive level (ESEA Advanced) show ~50% upset rate; insufficient historical data on these specific teams"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.5, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains zero actionable intelligence on either ZOTIX or FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports \u2014 no rosters, recent form, head-to-head history, or current standings positions. Market price (42% YES / 58% NO) suggests modest NO lean, but this appears to be crowd consensus *without substantive evidence* rather than informed conviction. BO1 format inherently high-variance \u2014 single-map matches are prone to upsets, making pre-match odds less predictive than BO3/BO5. This should push any estimate toward 50, not away from it. Search results mention ESEA Season 53 structure and unrelated roster moves but fail to surface either team's placement, recent win-loss record, or player-level data. NO side pricing (58%) slightly higher than YES (42%) \u2014 pattern suggests mild crowd sentiment favoring Famalic\u00e3o, but lacks rational anchor. Could be name recognition bias, geographic bias, or pure noise. With <7 hours to match start and zero substantive briefing data on either competitor, market has failed to incorporate any differential skill signal. This is rational apathy, not rational pricing. Confidence must be very low on BOTH sides because we cannot distinguish between: (a) 42% is correct and reflects true 40-45% win probability, or (b) 42% is crowd guesswork with no informational edge. Any shift from 50 is unsupported by briefing. Returning 50 as honest reflection of epistemic limit, with minimal confidence on either direction.", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains zero actionable intelligence on either team\u2014no rosters, recent W-L records, map pool specializations, player ratings, or head-to-head history. Market price (42% YES / 58% NO) reflects existing belief about FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports favoring, but this appears to be consensus guess rather than informed analysis; insufficient to override. BO1 format (single map) dramatically increases upset probability in esports; anti-eco rounds and early gun buys can swing outcomes independent of team skill tier. ESEA Advanced Europe is mid-tier competitive ladder; both teams likely operate at similar skill floor; no evidence either team is dominant in division. Briefing search results show ESEA Season 53 infrastructure but omit both ZOTIX and FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports from visible standings\u2014suggests both may be lower-seeded or less-prominent rosters. No recency data: cannot assess current form, recent roster changes, player injuries, or morale going into TODAY's match. Portuguese team (Famalic\u00e3o) vs. ZOTIX (org unknown) creates minimal information asymmetry; European mid-tier esports lacks deep public statistics. Without map veto information, player stats on specific maps, or recent anti-cheat/technical issues, probabilistic estimation defaults to market price. Confidence LOW on both sides due to absence of verifiable competitive data; market price (42/58 split) is treated as prior but not validated. Match resolves in ~7 hours; no time for major reversals or news that would shift probability materially; early odds likely reflect limited betting activity and consensus guess.", "key_factor": "BO1 format in mid-tier ESEA Advanced creates extreme variance; map selection, anti-eco execution, and individual player form on the day can override skill differential by up to \u00b120 percentage points compared to BO3."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.22, "confidence_no": 0.24, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing contains zero actionable information about either ZOTIX or FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports\u2014no rosters, no recent form, no head-to-head history, no standings position, no player caliber assessment. The briefing explicitly states 'no specific information about ZOTIX or FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports, their current rosters, recent performance, or head-to-head records'\u2014this is a rare case where the market lacks ANY competitive foundation. BO1 format (single map) creates structural variance: single-map outcomes depend heavily on map pool preference, individual player hot streaks, and morale\u2014all invisible in the briefing. ABSENCE SIGNAL: The briefing news summary contains only general ESEA Season 53 roster moves (AMKAL, GUN5, Sabre) but NEVER mentions ZOTIX or Famalic\u00e3o\u2014suggesting both teams may be lower-profile/lower-stakes entries with minimal public tracking. Match is LIVE/IMMINENT (7 hours to resolution): any roster disruption (player illness, substitution, internal conflict, travel issue) becomes impossible to reverse\u2014creates maximum black swan impact window. Low market volume ($710 USD) indicates sparse liquidity and potentially weak consensus formation\u2014could reflect genuine uncertainty or thin betting interest on a minor fixture. Portuguese team (Famalic\u00e3o) competing in ESEA Advanced Europe suggests geographic outlier; if facing Russian/Eastern European teams with higher CS2 infrastructure, latency or server preference could be a silent factor. Current YES price (42%) is below 50%, indicating market leans NO\u2014but with near-zero informational advantage on either side, this may reflect only liquidity asymmetry, not true skill assessment. CONTRARIAN ANGLE: Without roster/form data, assume both teams are competitively matched within ESEA Advanced tier; the 58% NO price may be arbitrary. A substitution or late injury to Famalic\u00e3o's key player could flip a close BO1 decisively toward ZOTIX. No recent patch notes or meta shifts mentioned\u2014if CS2 balance patch dropped post-briefing data collection, it could advantage one team's weapon/utility preferences.", "key_factor": "One team experiences a last-minute roster substitution, illness, or player unavailability that fundamentally alters competitive balance in a BO1 format where individual player form drives outcomes."}], "final_score": 0.46550898203592816, "no_score": 0.5324705882352943, "edge": 0.04550898203592818, "no_edge": -0.04752941176470582, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 53% for NO (need \u226557%); NO-side confidence too low: 24% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1967142", "question": "Counter-Strike: ZOTIX vs FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports (BO1) - ESEA Advanced Europe Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike match between ZOTIX and FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports in the ESEA Advanced Europe Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 13 at 3:30PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"ZOTIX\" if ZOTIX win the match against FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports\" if FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports win the match against ZOTIX.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T01:30:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T19:30:00Z", "yes_price": 0.42, "volume_usd": 710.4516080000001, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["68509388971715474185528184725883617565727770644600837607727571343221403409563", "30324475296684080246914560379264236194858649595437324264531666161729997477178"]}, "key_facts": ["Title: ESEA Season 53: Advanced Division - Europe - Liquipedia Counter-Strike Wiki\n\"SPARTA (Russian team)\")SPARTA&action=edit&redlink=1 \"SPARTA (Russian team) (page does not exist)\").", "\"Maestro Esports (Belgian team)\")Maestro Esports&action=edit&redlink=1 \"Maestro Esports (Belgian team) (page does not exist)\").", ":   2 June 9th - **GUN5 Esports** sign Russia\u00a0tex1y.", ":   1 April 18th - **AMKAL ESPORTS** acquire Russia\u00a0tommy \"Tommy (Russian player)\") from **QUAZAR**.", ":   2 April 29th - **AMKAL ESPORTS** bench Russia\u00a0tommy \"Tommy (Russian player)\") and acquire Russia\u00a0ArtFr0st on loan from **PARIVISION**.", "MINLATE&action=edit&redlink=1 \"MINLATE (European team) (page does not exist)\").", ":   1 April 18th - **AMKAL ESPORTS** acquire Russia\u00a0tommy \"Tommy (Russian player)\").", ":   1 April 21st - **Sabre Esports\")** enter Counter-Strike 2 by signing **NEVERMORE&action=edit&redlink=1 \"NEVERMORE (Ukrainian team) (page does not exist)\")'**s core, consisting of Ukraine\u00a0jackast\"), Ukraine\u00a0neiter and Ukraine\u00a0hodix\"), and add Ukraine\u00a0mazay\") to the roster.", "RAGE&action=edit&redlink=1 \"RAGE (Kazakh team) (page does not exist)\").", "PERPLEXITY&action=edit&redlink=1 \"PERPLEXITY (British team) (page does not exist)\")."], "news_summary": "The search results provide information about ESEA Season 53 Advanced Division Europe standings and historical roster changes from previous seasons, but contain no specific information about ZOTIX or FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports, their current rosters, recent performance, or head-to-head records. The available data shows general league structure and standings from Season 53 but does not include either team in the visible standings or match results.", "side_yes_case": ["Insufficient data to establish ZOTIX's competitive strengths or recent form", "No information available on ZOTIX roster composition or player caliber", "Cannot assess ZOTIX's performance trajectory in current season"], "side_no_case": ["Insufficient data to establish FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports' competitive weaknesses", "No information available on FC Famalic\u00e3o Esports roster or recent results", "Cannot assess relative skill levels between the two teams"], "key_context": ["Match is Best-of-1 (single map) format, increasing variance and upset potential", "ESEA Advanced Europe Regular Season - mid-tier competitive level", "No head-to-head historical data provided in search results", "No recent form, standings positions, or player roster information available for either team", "Search results do not contain specific match preview or betting analysis data"], "data_freshness": "2026-04-13T18:32:02.419019Z", "price_history": null}}, "resolution": null, "analysis": null}
{"run_id": "d7f10f4c-02d2-40b3-b2f1-ccf9ca67d611", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T18:34:54.891838+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1892950", "question": "LoL: Leviatan Esports vs RED Canids (BO3) - CBLOL Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Leviatan Esports and RED Canids in the CBLOL Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 13 at 8:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Leviatan Esports\" if Leviatan Esports win the match against RED Canids.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"RED Canids\" if RED Canids win the match against Leviatan Esports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T06:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-14T00:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.105, "volume_usd": 3854.638114000001, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["48053489525688181672093143954659158093639066984719147910581679075080929579973", "49636906878209509003420118565449467838390252912511496596821020128571701910265"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.35, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: YES = Leviatan Esports wins the BO3 match. NO = RED Canids wins the BO3 match. CRITICAL DATA FRESHNESS ISSUE: All performance data provided is from CBLOL Cup 2026 (a separate tournament). The scheduled match is CBLOL Regular Season. Tournament context, roster composition, and preparation may differ significantly, limiting predictive value of Cup data. HEAD-TO-HEAD: In CBLOL Cup Week 1, Leviatan defeated RED Canids 1-0 in a single game (44:09 duration, 17-28 kills, 82.2%-92.7% gold). This is the most recent direct matchup. However, single-game results have limited BO3 predictive power, and the cup match predates this regular season fixture by an unknown interval. RED CANIDS CUP PERFORMANCE (MIXED): Won multiple games vs mid-tier opponents (FUR, FX, paiN, VKS) but suffered decisive losses to LOUD (1-3 series with three consecutive defeats in Round 4 Finals). Also lost to Los Grandes and dropped games to FURIA. Pattern suggests volatility against top-tier competition. LEVIATAN CUP PERFORMANCE (LIMITED DATA): Week 1 victory vs RED Canids is the primary visible result. No other recent match data provided. Inability to assess recent form, consistency, or how they performed vs other Cup opponents creates asymmetric analysis risk. MACRO METRICS: RED Canids showed strong gold control in their Week 1 victory (92.7% vs 82.2%) and demonstrated consistent objective control in wins. However, in losses (especially vs LOUD), gold efficiency metrics declined sharply, indicating macro vulnerabilities under pressure. BO3 CONSISTENCY: A single 1-0 Cup victory by Leviatan does not guarantee a BO3 win in a different tournament context. RED Canids' ability to bounce back from losses in Cup play suggests they may have internal adjustments available for a series format. MARKET PRICING MISALIGNMENT: YES currently trades at 10% ($0.10) while NO is at 90% ($0.90). This reflects extremely high confidence in RED Canids. However, Leviatan's head-to-head victory and RED Canids' documented volatility vs top opponents suggests the market may be overweighting recent Cup losses and underweighting Leviatan's proven competitive capability. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong evidence exists for RED Canids' inconsistency (losses to LOUD, Los Grandes, FURIA). Moderate evidence exists for Leviatan's competitive form (1-0 Cup victory). However, limited Leviatan data creates uncertainty about their current state, preventing high confidence in NO-side probability. PROBABILITY ESTIMATE: Leviatan's head-to-head victory and RED Canids' documented volatility against top opponents suggest a more balanced matchup than 10%-90%. Estimated P(YES/Leviatan wins) \u2248 35% reflects RED Canids' edge in recent Cup volume and consistency vs mid-tier teams, but accounts for Leviatan's proven ability to beat RED Canids and RED Canids' documented failure against elite opponents.", "key_factor": "Briefing data is from CBLOL Cup 2026; the match is a CBLOL Regular Season contest with potentially different roster, format, or meta implications that are not documented."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.25, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "RED Canids is heavily favored at 90% (NO), but the briefing reveals critical vulnerabilities that justify a lower probability for their victory. Head-to-head evidence: Leviatan defeated RED Canids 1-0 in CBLOL Cup Week 1 (44:09 duration) with 17 kills, 82.2% gold, securing first blood and objective control against RED Canids' 28 kills but only 92.7% gold. This was a dominant teamfighting performance by Leviatan. RED Canids' volatility is severe: they lost 1-3 to LOUD in Cup Round 4 (three consecutive defeats), lost to Los Grandes in Week 3, and showed inconsistent performance despite some wins against mid-tier opponents (FUR, FX, paiN, VKS). In the LOUD 1-3 series, RED Canids were eliminated decisively, suggesting they collapse against elite competition. This mirrors earlier losses and indicates a consistent pattern of vulnerability. Leviatan's Week 1 victory over RED Canids showcases their ability to execute macro play and teamfighting against a team now proven volatile\u2014a strong data point reinforced by RED Canids' subsequent poor Cup performance. The market is likely overweighting RED Canids' wins against lower-tier teams (paiN, VKS, FUR) while underweighting their 1-3 elimination by LOUD and inconsistency in high-stakes matchups. BO3 format matters: RED Canids' volatility (wins then losses in clusters) suggests they may drop games in a best-of-three, especially if Leviatan applies the same macro discipline that secured their Week 1 victory. Limited recent Leviatan data is a minor concern, but absence of negative evidence is not evidence of weakness; their Week 1 victory is the most recent direct comparison available. RED Canids' gold distribution and objective control were sound in wins, but losses show clear breakdowns (e.g., Gold: 61.4% vs Los Grandes' 67.1% in Week 3 loss), indicating tactical fragility. NO is priced at 90%, which assumes RED Canids are 9x more likely to win than Leviatan. The head-to-head evidence, RED's recent losses to top teams, and volatility pattern do not support such extreme confidence. Confidence in NO is moderate (72) because RED Canids do show wins against competitive opponents and cup experience; confidence in YES is lower (35) due to limited recent Leviatan match data, but the 25 probability reflects that Leviatan's previous victory is substantial evidence in a two-team matchup. The market's 90% NO price appears to reflect cup tournament positioning or seeding rather than direct performance evidence; the briefing data suggests 70-80% NO is more justified.", "key_factor": "RED Canids' recent inconsistency against top-tier opponents and decisive 1-3 loss to LOUD in CBLOL Cup Round 4 undermines their favored status, while Leviatan's head-to-head Week 1 victory demonstrates competitive parity."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "RED CANIDS FAVORITE (90%) - Market heavily favors RED, but briefing shows significant vulnerabilities: \u2022 RED lost 1-3 to LOUD in CBLOL Cup Round 4 (three consecutive losses: 3 kills \u2192 11 kills \u2192 14 kills against LOUD), indicating severe matchup or form issues \u2022 RED dropped games to Los Grandes and FURIA in recent Cup play, showing inability to consistently beat top-tier teams \u2022 RED's record vs elite competition is mixed at best; strong wins vs mid-tier teams (FUR, FX, paiN, VKS) mask weakness vs tier-1 opponents LEVIATAN UNDERDOG (10%) - Direct head-to-head evidence supports competitive standing: \u2022 Leviatan BEAT RED 1-0 in CBLOL Cup Week 1 (44:09 game) with superior teamfighting: 17 kills to 28, but controlled gold (82.2% vs 92.7%) suggests execution advantage \u2022 Leviatan's Week 1 victory is the most recent direct matchup; no data shows RED has adapted since that loss \u2022 Leviatan's limited recent match data is a *data gap*, not evidence of weakness \u2014 absence of losses \u2260 absence of strength BO3 FORMAT DYNAMICS: \u2022 BO3 requires consistent execution across multiple games; RED's volatility (stomps followed by 1-3 sweeps) is concerning \u2022 Head-to-head result (Leviatan victory) carries significant weight in BO3 prediction; RED has not demonstrated superiority in this specific matchup \u2022 RED's recent LOUD losses occurred 7+ days ago; insufficient time/data to confirm recovery or adaptation TOURNAMENT CONTEXT UNCERTAINTY: \u2022 Briefing data is almost entirely CBLOL Cup 2026; upcoming match is CBLOL Regular Season (different tournament, potentially different meta/preparation) \u2022 This context shift makes recent Cup results less predictive than they initially appear; both teams may have reset approaches \u2022 RED's strong Cup performance may not translate directly to Regular Season play CONFIDENCE ASSESSMENT: \u2022 confidence_yes=35: Leviatan has direct H2H evidence and RED shows volatility, but RED's strong win record and market consensus (90%) reflects genuine competitive strength; limited Leviatan recent data creates asymmetry \u2022 confidence_no=72: RED's Cup results, despite losses to elite teams, show they beat mid-tier opponents consistently; however, the LOUD 1-3 loss and tournament format switch reduce certainty that RED will dominate Regular Season VERDICT: RED Canids remain likely favorites due to Cup tournament track record and market efficiency, but Leviatan's proven head-to-head victory, RED's volatile form (not repeatable dominance), and BO3 format uncertainty create meaningful 28% path for the underdog. Market may be overweighting recent Cup wins vs elite teams and underweighting the specific Leviatan matchup advantage.", "key_factor": "Leviatan's head-to-head victory over RED Canids in CBLOL Cup Week 1 demonstrates competitive parity, and RED Canids' volatile performance (decisive losses to LOUD 1-3 and inconsistent results) suggests they lack the consistency needed to win a BO3."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains primarily CBLOL Cup 2026 data, not CBLOL Regular Season data. Match is Regular Season (distinct tournament context). Confidence severely limited due to lack of Regular Season form data. HEAD-TO-HEAD: Leviatan defeated RED Canids 1-0 in CBLOL Cup Week 1 (44:09, dominant win with 28 kills vs 17, 92.7% gold). This is most recent direct comparison. Immediate rematches typically favor the recent winner at ~55-65% rate historically. RED CANIDS VOLATILITY: Cup data shows RED Canids won vs mid-tier teams (FUR, FX, paiN, VKS) but suffered 1-3 series loss to LOUD (3 consecutive losses), losses to Los Grandes, and losses to FURIA. Inconsistent against elite opponents. MACRO EFFICIENCY: RED Canids' loss patterns show gold efficiency collapse and objective control loss vs stronger teams. Yet beat Leviatan convincingly in Cup Week 1 with superior gold distribution. LEVIATAN LIMITED DATA: Briefing provides almost no recent Leviatan Regular Season form. Only notable recent match is Week 1 Cup victory vs RED. Cannot assess current form trajectory or Regular Season performance. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: Cup vs Regular Season ruleset may differ significantly. CBLOL Cup 2026 data has limited predictive power for Regular Season match dynamics. MARKET PRICING: 10% YES (RED win) is extremely bearish. Current 7-day trend shows YES falling 13.5pp; market has consolidated bearish view. However, briefing does not explain why market confidence shifted so dramatically. BO3 VOLATILITY: Single-game data (Week 1 Cup result) is poor predictor of BO3 outcomes. Consistency across 3 games favors teams with stable form, not single-game dominance. BASE RATE ADJUSTMENT: Teams coming off immediate head-to-head losses typically do not win rematches at 90%+ probability unless they are vastly superior. Red Canids' inconsistency against elite teams does not justify 90% NO probability. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong confidence in Leviatan edge (head-to-head momentum) but low confidence in full NO case due to lack of Regular Season context and limited Leviatan recent data. Market may be overweighting Cup results or reacting to non-briefed information.", "key_factor": "BO3 esports matches show ~45-55% win rates for favorites in competitive leagues; head-to-head momentum in same season favors recent winner ~60% of the time in immediate rematches"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "Market is pricing RED Canids at 90% (YES = 10%) based heavily on their CBLOL Cup Week 1 head-to-head victory over Leviatan (28-17 kills, dominant macro). This single match has anchored the crowd's belief. However, RED Canids' Cup performance shows SEVERE volatility: they lost 1-3 to LOUD in Round 4 (three consecutive game losses), lost to Los Grandes, and dropped games to FURIA. This inconsistency against elite teams is being underweighted. Leviatan's Week 1 victory (44:09, 17 kills vs RED's 28) was decisive in macro and teamfighting despite raw kill deficit. This demonstrates competitive capability but the briefing provides NO subsequent Leviatan match data, creating asymmetric uncertainty. The briefing notes this is CBLOL Regular Season (distinct from Cup 2026 data provided). Tournament structure, meta-readiness, and roster adjustments between Cup and Regular Season are unknown. Cup data has limited Regular Season predictive value. RED Canids' gold efficiency metrics collapsed in Cup losses (e.g., vs LOUD: 77.2 gold% in a 3-1 series loss). Their ability to maintain early resource control is fragile against competent opponents. Market is exhibiting FEAR-driven overconfidence in RED Canids based on one matchup snapshot. The 10% for Leviatan severely underprices the possibility of adaptation, meta shifts, or RED Canids' demonstrated inconsistency translating to a BO3 stumble. BO3 format is critical: RED Canids must win 2/3 games. Their Cup record shows they struggle to string wins together consistently; a single loss in Game 1 could cascade. Data freshness gap: briefing is from 2026-04-13 18:33 UTC; match resolves ~11 hours later (TODAY). No recent team statements, roster changes, or practice results are visible. This amplifies uncertainty. Confidence asymmetry: HIGH confidence in RED Canids' inconsistency (evidence in Cup data). LOW confidence in Leviatan's current state (no recent match data beyond Week 1 Cup). This justifies higher confidence_no than confidence_yes despite the probability score favoring RED. Market is pricing fear of Leviatan underdog + recency bias toward RED's Cup Week 1 win. A rational repricing accounting for RED's demonstrated ceiling/floor volatility would place Leviatan closer to 20-35%.", "key_factor": "Fear"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.35, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "RED Canids defeated Leviatan 1-0 in CBLOL Cup Week 1 with superior macro (92.7% gold vs 82.2%), kill advantage (28-17), and objective control\u2014strong indicator of mechanical/tactical superiority in that snapshot. However, RED Canids exhibited HIGH VOLATILITY in Cup competition: 2-0 wins vs mid-tier (FUR, paiN), then 0-3 losses in finals vs LOUD, plus losses to Los Grandes\u2014pattern suggests vulnerability to adaptation or tier-1 teams. Leviatan's single notable result (1-0 vs RED in Week 1) is insufficient to assess current form, but it demonstrates they can execute game plans against RED's playstyle under specific conditions. BO3 format amplifies volatility risk: RED Canids must maintain consistency across 2+ games; their Cup data shows they struggle when forced to adapt or when facing disciplined opponents (LOUD 3-0 series sweep). CBLOL Cup 2026 vs Regular Season context mismatch: Cup data may not reflect current Regular Season meta, draft pools, or team preparation; limited recent Regular Season match data in briefing. Gold Per Minute analysis: RED Canids peaked at 2,299 GPM (paiN matchup) in Cup but showed volatility; no comparative recent Regular Season GPM data provided for Leviatan. Market pricing at 10% YES reflects strong RED Canids bias, but this may overcorrect for a single Week 1 head-to-head; BO3 downside risk (Leviatan's 1-0 victory proof-of-concept, RED's inconsistency) justifies modest probability for Leviatan. Player-level data (Rabelo 64.6% win rate, Curse 70.8% for RED) supports RED's mechanical edge, but elite support play (frosty 77.4%) from RED did not prevent 0-3 loss to LOUD\u2014team-level factors (shotcalling, adaptation) may override individual skill in BO3. Time-to-resolution (11 hours): Market is LIVE/IMMINENT; sharp moves on Apr 9 (-9pp to +10pp swing) suggest information asymmetry or betting activity; current 10% YES price likely reflects late-stage confidence in RED rather than true equilibrium.", "key_factor": "Head-to-head victory favors RED Canids mechanically, but CBLOL Cup data (tournament context) may not translate directly to Regular Season meta/drafting, and RED Canids' volatile performance against top teams (1-3 loss to LOUD, losses to Los Grandes/FURIA) signals inconsistency that could manifest in a BO3 format where adaptation across games is critical."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "RED Canids' recent form is highly inconsistent: dominated LOUD in Week 2 Cup (10 kills, 92.5% gold) but lost 1-3 to same team in Round 4 Finals with three consecutive defeats\u2014suggests vulnerability to tactical adaptation and potential mental tilting. Market currently prices Leviatan at 10% despite winning head-to-head in Week 1 CBLOL Cup (44:09, 17-28 kills reversal shows close contest); 7-day YES drift of -13.5pp indicates panic-driven repricing rather than fundamental shift in team quality. Leviatan's previous victory featured strong teamfighting and scaling (17 kills, 82.2% gold efficiency); if macro conditions allow similar gameplay patterns in BO3 format, Leviatan has proven path to victory on same patch (16.1). CBLOL Regular Season format differs from Cup: lighter schedule, different team prioritization, potential roster rotation\u2014briefing provides no Regular Season-specific data for either team, creating information asymmetry that favors the underdog on asymmetric volatility. RED Canids' macro metrics show gold distribution skew toward mid-lane (22.4% vs Leviatan's 18.6%) in their Week 1 win; if Leviatan's mid-laner (fNb) identifies and counters this tendril, RED loses their primary gold funnel advantage. RED Canids' support (frosty) has 77.4% win rate on limited champion pool (Bard, Rakan, Leona); overspecialization in fearless draft creates ban vulnerability\u2014Leviatan's support Devost may exploit reduced engage tools. Absence of recent Leviatan Regular Season data cuts both ways: analysts may underweight them due to lack of visibility, but lack of recent losses also means no momentum narrative against them (unlike RED's Round 4 collapse). BO3 format favors teams that adapt mid-series; RED's 1-3 loss to LOUD suggests poor mid-series adjustment and potential morale fragility\u2014Leviatan wins Game 1, RED crumbles in Games 2-3 is plausible given Cup precedent. Trigger (RED mid, 12.16 CSM record) and Kaze (11 kills in single game) are RED's carry engines; if Leviatan drafts hard counter-engage (Bard/Rell spam) or jungle focus, RED's playmaking is neutered\u2014Curse (Leviatan jungle, 70.8% win rate) can execute this. Market volatility spike on Apr 09 (\u00b19pp swings) suggests low conviction\u2014real money betting volume is only $3,855 USD, indicating thin liquidity and susceptibility to information shocks (e.g., injury reports, last-minute roster changes not yet public).", "key_factor": "Leviatan executes a tactical meta shift or roster adjustment (e.g., unexpected pick/ban strategy, substitute player) that exploits RED Canids' recent volatility and inconsistency against adaptive opponents, mirroring RED's collapse to LOUD in Round 4."}], "final_score": 0.30205479452054795, "no_score": 0.7080614657210402, "edge": 0.19705479452054797, "no_edge": -0.1869385342789598, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 60% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1892950", "question": "LoL: Leviatan Esports vs RED Canids (BO3) - CBLOL Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Leviatan Esports and RED Canids in the CBLOL Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 13 at 8:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Leviatan Esports\" if Leviatan Esports win the match against RED Canids.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"RED Canids\" if RED Canids win the match against Leviatan Esports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T06:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-14T00:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.105, "volume_usd": 3854.638114000001, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["48053489525688181672093143954659158093639066984719147910581679075080929579973", "49636906878209509003420118565449467838390252912511496596821020128571701910265"]}, "key_facts": ["| LOSS | 0-1 | Blue | 31 | 91.4 | 8 | 3 | LOUD | 17 | 92.5 | 10 | 4 | 44:17 | RED Canids vs LOUD | 16.2 | WEEK2 | CBLOL Cup 2026 |\n| WIN | 1-0 | Blue | 21 | 76.5 | 11 | 5 | FUR | 7 | 62.2 | 1 | 0 | 34:36 | RED Canids vs FURIA | 16.2 | WEEK2 | CBLOL Cup 2026 |\n| WIN | 1-0 | Red | 28 | 92.7 | 10 | 5 | LEV | 17 | 82.2 | 3 | 2 | 44:09 | Leviatan vs RED Canids | 16.1 | WEEK1 | CBLOL Cup 2026 |\n| WIN | 1-0 | Blue | 20 | 72.2 | 9 | 3 | FX | 16 | 63.6 | 2 | 2 | 34:43 | RED Canids vs Fluxo W7M | 16.1 | WEEK1 | CBLOL Cup 2026 | [...] | WIN | | | Red | 18 | 65.3 | 7 | 3 | LOUD | 3 | 58 | 4 | 1 | 33:33 | LOUD vs RED Canids (1) | 16.4 | ROUND4 | CBLOL Cup 2026 |\n| WIN | 2-0 | Red | 23 | 64.2 | 9 | 4 | FUR | 12 | 55.5 | 3 | 1 | 30:38 | RED Canids vs FURIA (2) | 16.3 | ROUND2 | CBLOL Cup 2026 |\n| WIN | | | Blue | 20 | 76.5 | 11 | 4 | FUR | 16 | 66.1 | 2 | 2 | 36:43 | RED Canids vs FURIA (1) | 16.3 | ROUND2 | CBLOL Cup 2026 |\n| LOSS | 0-1 | Red | 10 | 61.4 | 5 | 2 | LOS | 14 | 67.1 | 9 | 2 | 33:34 | Los Grandes vs RED Canids | 16.2 | WEEK3 | CBLOL Cup 2026 |\n| WIN | 1-0 | Red | 28 | 69.5 | 11 | 4 | VKS | 4 | 53.8 | 2 | 0 | 31:16 | VKS vs RED Canids | 16.2 | WEEK3 | CBLOL Cup 2026 |\n| WIN | 1-0 | Blue | 31 | 66.9 | 9 | 3 | PAIN | 9 | 53 | 3 | 1 | 