{"run_id": "73ecbf00-ad14-4e5d-9e80-053a469c6290", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T18:37:00.254791+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1967483", "question": "Counter-Strike: Marsborne vs Team Aether (BO3) - CCT North America Series #4 Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Semifinal 2 match between Marsborne and Team Aether in the CCT North America Series #4 Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 13 at 8:30PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Marsborne\" if Marsborne win the match against Team Aether.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Aether\" if Team Aether win the match against Marsborne.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T06:30:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-14T00:30:00Z", "yes_price": 0.61, "volume_usd": 4249.073954, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["14780842611423179424268527618407837993540169417623645630632289397937581886379", "41052495392614622619427610457849498922036136034968341465231606142697358637636"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.5, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "Resolution criteria are clear and unambiguous: YES = Marsborne wins the BO3 match; NO = Team Aether wins. Critical data gap: The briefing document provides no actionable information about either team's recent performance, roster strength, win rates, or head-to-head history. Marsborne is confirmed as a US-based active competitive team referenced in HLTV circulation, but Team Aether appears absent from search results entirely. The briefing contains general Counter-Strike player statistics (ZywOo, mezii, apEX, etc.) but neither Marsborne nor Team Aether players appear in elite rankings provided. No recent match records, form trends, coaching staff details, or playoff qualification context available for either team. Current market price (YES 61% / NO 39%) reflects some market consensus favoring Marsborne, but this appears to be the only signal available\u2014insufficient to override symmetric confidence penalties. Event timing is TODAY (~12 hours to resolution), but this does not resolve the fundamental absence of analytical data. Without roster analysis, recent results, meta compatibility, or any competitive intelligence on either side, assigning a probability above or below 50 would constitute unfounded speculation. Setting probability_score at 50 (genuine coin flip) with low confidence scores on both sides (25 each) reflects appropriate epistemic humility given severe data asymmetry and complete absence of team-specific intelligence.", "key_factor": "Briefing document contains no match history, recent form, roster composition, head-to-head records, or competitive performance data for either Marsborne or Team Aether, making any probability estimate beyond coin-flip impossible."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.61, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "YES case (favored at 61%): Marsborne is confirmed as an active US-based competitive team with recent match activity in the 2026 competitive season; the market has priced them as the favorite, suggesting informed traders have identified form, roster strength, or head-to-head advantages that warrant a 61% probability. NO case (underdog at 39%): Team Aether is completely absent from the briefing's search results and HLTV data, making it impossible to assess roster quality, recent form, or competitive standing; this absence could indicate a newer/emerging team, which would typically be underpriced relative to an established favorite. Critical data gap: The briefing explicitly states 'Search results provide limited specific information' and 'lack direct match details, recent form data, or head-to-head records for either team.' Neither team appears in the elite player rankings provided (ZywOo, mezii, apEX, etc.), suggesting both are mid-tier competitive squads. Marsborne identity established: Confirmed US team with competitive activity; FPL/roster references suggest baseline legitimacy in the scene. Team Aether opacity: Zero search results, no roster data, no recent match history in briefing\u2014this is the critical weakness of the underdog position and explains the 22-point spread. Market structure: $4,249 volume is modest; the 61% price may reflect thin liquidity or limited sharp action, but absence of counter-evidence against Marsborne suggests no major upset signal is present. Timing risk mitigated: Event is TODAY (resolves in ~12 hours), so major roster news or withdrawal is unlikely; no forfeit or cancellation signals in briefing. Confidence asymmetry justified: HIGH confidence in YES (35) is low due to near-total absence of Marsborne form data, but confidence in NO (28) is even lower because Team Aether is completely unmeasured\u2014the market's 61-39 split appears to be 'known favorite vs. unknown underdog' rather than a sharp analytical call. Bull case: The market has already priced in uncertainty; Marsborne's confirmed presence and competitive circulation is a marginal advantage over a phantom opponent; the 61% price is reasonable given information vacuum on both sides.", "key_factor": "Market pricing at 61% reflects Marsborne as the slight favorite, likely driven by roster stability or recent playoff momentum in the CCT North America Series."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.29, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing contains NO concrete performance data, recent form, head-to-head records, or roster information for either Marsborne or Team Aether. Both 'CASE FOR YES' and 'CASE FOR NO' sections explicitly state 'insufficient data'\u2014this is a red flag for market mispricing on both sides. UNDERDOG ASYMMETRY: Team Aether is priced at only 39% despite being completely absent from search results. This absence is suspicious\u2014it could indicate: (1) an emerging/rising team the market underestimates, (2) a roster change not yet reflected in public data, or (3) a team that has been grinding ladder/qualifiers without major tournament visibility. MARSBORNE VISIBILITY PARADOX: Marsborne is identified as 'active' and 'in competitive circulation' but appears in generic HLTV.org background data only, not in elite player rankings or recent tournament results. This suggests Marsborne is also a mid-tier team, not a dominant favorite\u2014yet it is priced as a 61% favorite based on thin evidence. NO ELITE PLAYERS IDENTIFIED: The player statistics provided (ZywOo, mezii, apEX, etc.) do not mention any Marsborne or Team Aether roster members. Both teams appear to operate outside the top-tier competitive landscape, making the 61%/39% split potentially arbitrary rather than data-driven. BO3 FORMAT VOLATILITY: Best-of-three matches introduce higher variance than single maps. Without roster/recent form data, a 61/39 split assumes Marsborne has a significant edge\u2014but if both teams are mid-tier unknowns, the true probability is likely closer to a coin flip (50/50). Team Aether at 39% may be *underpriced*. MARKET TIMING: Event resolves TODAY (~12 hours). This short time window means no new match replays, statistics, or public analysis will emerge before resolution. The market is trading on stale or incomplete information. Late-minute reversals are unlikely given timing constraints, but the current pricing may already reflect uncertainty that should favor the underdog more. CASE AGAINST MARSBORNE AS FAVORITE: If Marsborne were significantly stronger, the briefing would include recent tournament wins, recognizable players, or head-to-head dominance. Absence of this evidence contradicts the 61% pricing. The favorite's case rests on being 'known' and 'active'\u2014not on demonstrated superiority. CASE FOR TEAM AETHER: Complete absence from briefing data could mean: (1) Team Aether is a qualifier/emerging squad with no historical baggage, facing an opponent expected to choke under playoff pressure; (2) Team Aether has a recent roster reshuffle that public databases haven't indexed; (3) Team Aether specializes in specific map pools or playstyles that counter Marsborne's approach\u2014information not captured in generic stats. CONFIDENCE LIMITATION: Confidence scores for BOTH sides are set low (28/29) because the briefing provides fewer than 2 concrete data points about either team's recent performance or form. This violates standard analysis thresholds. Without such data, probability_score is essentially an informed guess. PROBABILITY JUSTIFICATION: 38% for YES (62% for NO) reflects: (a) the near-total absence of data favoring Marsborne beyond 'activity'; (b) the asymmetric information gap that may hide Team Aether's actual strength; (c) the coin-flip nature of mid-tier BO3 matches; and (d) slight underdog value for NO at current 39% market price, suggesting a modest uptick to 38-40% is warranted. The 61% YES price appears overconfident given data scarcity.", "key_factor": "Team Aether is entirely absent from competitive intelligence, creating a data vacuum that may mask recent momentum, roster improvements, or hidden strengths that the market has failed to price in."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.5, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains no roster information, recent match results, win rates, or head-to-head records for either Marsborne or Team Aether TEAM AETHER: Completely absent from search results; no performance baseline, player names, or competitive history provided MARSBORNE: Identified as US-based team in competitive circulation, but no recent form data, tournament placements, or player skill metrics provided NO COMPARATIVE METRICS: Neither team appears in elite player rankings (ZywOo, mezii, apEX tiers); cannot infer roster quality PLAYOFF CONTEXT: BO3 format in CCT North America Series #4 suggests playoff stakes, but no seeding information or tournament bracket data provided MARKET PRICING MISMATCH: Current market at 61% YES suggests informed traders have data not present in briefing; pricing may reflect betting market consensus rather than analytical edge EVENT TIMING IMMINENT: Match resolves in ~12 hours with no new information expected; low likelihood of significant pre-match developments that would warrant confidence adjustment LOW VOLUME: $4,249 USD volume suggests thin liquidity; market price may not reflect high conviction RESOLUTION RISK: Forfeiture/disqualification rules create 50-50 resolution edge cases, but match should proceed normally based on tournament schedule BASE RATE UNAVAILABLE: Cannot anchor to Counter-Strike playoff win probabilities without team-specific ELO, historical tournament placement data, or peer-reviewed competitive records ASSYMETRIC CONFIDENCE: confidence_yes and confidence_no both set to 25 due to complete absence of directional evidence for either competitor; coin-flip probability reflects genuine epistemic uncertainty, not default selection", "key_factor": "Unable to establish \u2014 insufficient comparative data on Marsborne and Team Aether competitive records, roster strength, or head-to-head history"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.5, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "Market price (61% YES / 39% NO) reflects a modest lean toward Marsborne, but this appears driven by insufficient data rather than informed conviction. Briefing contains NO actionable intelligence on either team: no recent form, head-to-head records, roster strength comparisons, or player performance metrics for Marsborne or Team Aether. Marsborne confirmed as US-based competitive team with recent activity, but Team Aether is entirely absent from search results\u2014asymmetric information availability rather than predictive signal. Elite CS player rankings (ZywOo, mezii, apEX) provided are irrelevant to this match; neither Marsborne nor Aether rosters appear in top-tier data. 61% YES pricing suggests crowd confidence in Marsborne, but this may reflect bias toward the team with any detectable online presence rather than genuine skill differential. Event timing is TODAY with 12-hour window to resolution\u2014reversal of market sentiment would require unexpected forfeit, cancellation, or late-breaking roster news (low probability). Low volume ($4,249) indicates limited market liquidity and casual participation; price may not reflect professional CS betting intelligence. Absence of counter-narrative in briefing (no Team Aether analysis, no upset indicators) leaves NO side systematically under-researched\u2014true 50-50 uncertainty masked by artificial YES lean. Rational market response to total data void would be 50-50 midpoint; current 61/39 split is sentiment-driven, not evidence-driven.", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.5, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing provides generic HLTV.org content (player rankings, historical tournament results, transfer news) but contains NO specific information about Marsborne or Team Aether rosters, recent form, or direct matchup history. TEAM IDENTIFICATION FAILURE: Marsborne is mentioned only once in passing (US-based, competitive circulation); Team Aether is completely absent from search results, preventing any baseline performance comparison. PLAYER RATING CHARTS IRRELEVANT: The statistical tables (ZywOo 2.18 rating, mezii 1.61, etc.) reference elite-tier players not identified as belonging to either competing team, making them unusable for this specific match prediction. BO3 FORMAT SIGNIFICANCE: Best-of-three requires understanding map veto strategies, team-specific map winrates, and clutch-performance history\u2014none of which exist in the briefing. TIMING PRESSURE: Match resolves in ~12 hours (TODAY), leaving no time for additional scouting; a 50% probability reflects genuine epistemic uncertainty rather than even-odds match reality. MARKET MISPRICING SIGNAL: Current 61% YES / 39% NO odds suggest market participants possess information absent from this briefing; confidence scores must remain depressed to reflect this asymmetry. FORFEIT/DELAY RISK: Resolution criteria allow 50-50 outcomes for cancellations, delays >7 days, or forfeits\u2014non-negligible risk given esports logistical volatility, but insufficient detail to quantify.", "key_factor": "The briefing document contains zero actionable competitive intelligence on either team's current roster composition, recent LAN performance metrics, map pool synergies, or head-to-head records\u2014all essential data points in BO3 prediction analysis."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.45, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "The briefing is almost entirely devoid of actionable data on BOTH teams\u2014no head-to-head records, recent form trajectories, roster confirmations, map pool strengths, or player statistics for either Marsborne or Team Aether. Current market price (61% YES/39% NO) implies confidence in Marsborne, but this confidence appears to rest on name recognition alone rather than competitive data. Team Aether is completely absent from search results while Marsborne is mentioned as active in competitive circulation\u2014this asymmetry is a red flag, not confirmation. Aether's invisibility could indicate: (a) they are an emerging/lower-ranked squad with momentum, (b) they have deliberately low profile (psychological advantage), or (c) they are new/restructured with unfamiliar roster composition. No elite player ratings in the briefing reference either team's roster. The top-tier stats shown (ZywOo, mezii, apEX, etc.) are Tier 1 professionals from orgs like Vitality/NaVi\u2014neither Marsborne nor Aether appear here, suggesting both are mid-tier North American competitors. The briefing contains a cryptic Jame quote about tournament call errors and provisional match order confirmations, hinting at logistical flux. LAN events can be decided by on-site factors: lag compensation awareness, team familiarity with venue, or last-minute roster adjustments. Best-of-three format heavily favors teams with deep map pools and mental resilience. A team trailing 0\u20131 facing a win-or-go-home map 3 often exhibits clutch mentality shifts; the briefing provides no data on either team's psychological profile in high-pressure scenarios. Absence of data on Aether\u2014their recent event results, player roles, IGL strategy, or regional pedigree\u2014means the 39% NO price may be artificially suppressed. An underdog with strong fundamentals can exploit overconfidence. Event timing is TODAY (~12 hours to resolution), leaving no time for reversal via external disruption (injury mid-series unlikely to flip outcome unless catastrophic). Market probability reflects current belief, not new evidence. With this little data, the 61\u201339 split is pseudo-confident noise. A genuine 50\u201350 flip could come from Aether executing a map-veto strategy, anti-meta defensive setup, or Marsborne experiencing in-game miscommunication on LAN. Market volume ($4,249 USD) is moderate; if sharp money has moved post-briefing, 61% may represent late smart money on Marsborne. But given the data vacuum, contrarian hypothesis: Aether is being underpriced due to low profile, not inferior skill.", "key_factor": "Team Aether has a roster or tactical innovation (e.g., recent stand-in, map pool exploit, or mental edge from underdog momentum) that the briefing's silence on their existence entirely masks."}], "final_score": 0.49523560209424083, "no_score": 0.5092896174863388, "edge": -0.11476439790575915, "no_edge": 0.11928961748633882, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Contrarian call: council prob 51% < 70% threshold; Contrarian call: NO-side confidence 26% < 80% threshold", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1967483", "question": "Counter-Strike: Marsborne vs Team Aether (BO3) - CCT North America Series #4 Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Semifinal 2 match between Marsborne and Team Aether in the CCT North America Series #4 Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 13 at 8:30PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Marsborne\" if Marsborne win the match against Team Aether.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Aether\" if Team Aether win the match against Marsborne.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T06:30:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-14T00:30:00Z", "yes_price": 0.61, "volume_usd": 4249.073954, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["14780842611423179424268527618407837993540169417623645630632289397937581886379", "41052495392614622619427610457849498922036136034968341465231606142697358