{"run_id": "5a412827-f99d-40ce-9e2c-3ef8c79e9fbe", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T19:26:51.374908+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1938836", "question": "Rainbow Six Siege: Twisted Minds vs Fnatic (BO3) - Europe MENA League Kickoff Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Rainbow Six Siege Upper bracket quarterfinal 1 match between Twisted Minds and Fnatic in the Europe MENA League Kickoff Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 13 at 12:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Twisted Minds\" if Twisted Minds win the match against Fnatic.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Fnatic\" if Fnatic win the match against Twisted Minds.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://liquipedia.net/rainbowsix/Main_Page. However, if https://liquipedia.net/rainbowsix/Main_Page has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T00:15:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T18:15:00Z", "yes_price": 0.835, "volume_usd": 1586.013984, "category": "rainbow-six-siege", "clob_token_ids": ["67117106279918067100983193625051154051560853341324454427176028551313101387731", "54118081053813484982883120147756207398582435648309686633816244383744318354099"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.68, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing contains extensive esports data but NONE for Rainbow Six Siege competition. Search results show Twisted Minds competing in Rocket League and Warzone (different esports), not R6S. No R6S rosters, recent form, head-to-head records, or competitive standing information available. MARKET SIGNAL DOMINANCE: With zero fundamental data available, probability assessment must rely on market price action. YES side currently prices at 84%, having risen +34pp over 7 days and +42pp in 24 hours. This represents strong market conviction favoring Twisted Minds. PRICE MOMENTUM ANALYSIS: YES side experienced three sharp moves: -22.5pp (Apr 12 16:00 UTC), +26.5pp (Apr 13 04:00 UTC), +15.5pp (Apr 13 19:26 UTC). The recent +15.5pp move and current 84% price suggest late-stage information flow favoring Twisted Minds, likely from betting syndicates, insiders, or direct observer reports. TIMING CONTEXT: Event is TODAY (resolves in ~5 hours). At this late stage, market price reflects very recent intelligence about team preparation, roster status, technical readiness, or early match observations. Large asymmetric moves this close to resolution typically reflect substantive information rather than speculation. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION - YES SIDE: Market price of 84% is strong but not extreme. Confidence_yes set to 35 (low-moderate) because: (1) no fundamental data validates this price, (2) late-stage market moves can reflect rumors or incomplete information, (3) esports outcomes remain inherently uncertain without team-level intelligence. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION - NO SIDE: Confidence_no set to 28 (very low) because: (1) market has systematically repriced toward YES, (2) no counter-arguments available from briefing data, (3) Fnatic is not mentioned in any available results, (4) inability to assess whether Fnatic has structural weaknesses, roster issues, or are heavy underdogs at baseline. ASYMMETRIC DATA QUALITY: Strong price signal on YES side (market consensus, momentum, late timing) contrasts sharply with complete absence of NO-side validation data. This asymmetry justifies lower confidence on NO side despite using market signal for probability estimate. RESOLUTION CRITERIA: Clear and unambiguous. Match is BO3, resolved on Liquipedia with fallback to credible reporting if Liquipedia silent within 2 hours. No structural ambiguity in how winner will be determined. MARKET STRUCTURE: YES at 84% vs NO at 17% suggests market believes Twisted Minds are heavily favored. Asymmetric pricing (totals 101%) reflects orderbook spread but direction is clear: YES is dominant consensus. FINAL PROBABILITY LOGIC: Probability_score of 68 represents compromise: accepting market price signal (which favors YES at 84%) but downweighting it moderately due to complete absence of team-level fundamental data, risk of late-stage mispricing, and inherent esports uncertainty. Setting probability below market price (68 vs 84) reflects epistemic humility given data gaps.", "key_factor": "Briefing document contains zero relevant Rainbow Six Siege performance data for either Twisted Minds or Fnatic; probability relies entirely on market prices and price momentum rather than team fundamentals."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.58, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "MARKET MOMENTUM IS THE PRIMARY SIGNAL: YES has surged 42pp in 24h and 34pp over 7 days, with three sharp upward moves (+26.5pp, +15.5pp). NO has fallen consistently. This sustained, multi-move rally on a live event suggests informed traders have conviction in Twisted Minds. VOLATILITY ASYMMETRY FAVORS YES: YES volatility (11pp/hr) is 41% higher than NO (7.8pp/hr), indicating more aggressive positioning and confident capital flowing toward Twisted Minds as match approaches. CURRENT 84% PRICE REFLECTS SIGNIFICANT CONFIDENCE: Market is not hedging or uncertain\u2014it has moved decisively to price Twisted Minds as the heavy favorite. Large moves on same-day events typically reflect real information (lineup, recent scrims, team status). FNATIC WEAKNESS: No credible counter-evidence in briefing. Fnatic appears as a team in G2 match history (G2 beat FNC 7-0 on Apr 8, 2026), but no direct R6S competitive standing, roster depth, or recent form for Fnatic is provided. This asymmetric data gap favors the favorite. TWISTED MINDS DATA GAP, BUT FAVORED: No specific R6S match history or roster data provided for either team, but the market has moved 42pp toward Twisted Minds in 24h. In live/imminent events, large same-day rallies often reflect new information traders are seeing (team availability, scrim results, meta advantage). UPWARD MOMENTUM LATE IN TRADING CYCLE: Sharp +15.5pp move at 19:26 UTC (less than 5 hours before 00:15 UTC resolution) suggests closing information flow favoring Twisted Minds. Late rallies on imminent events often precede favorable outcomes. UNDERDOG (NO) LACKS DEFENSE: With only 17% market price and declining share of volume, Fnatic has not attracted sufficient counter-positioning. If Fnatic had plausible strength, contrarian traders would be backing them\u2014absence of this suggests limited confidence in an upset. A-TIER TOURNAMENT CREDIBILITY: Europe MENA League 2026 Kickoff is confirmed A-Tier (Ubisoft/Blast organized), lending legitimacy to the market and suggesting traders have access to meaningful competitive intel. CONFIDENCE TEMPERED BY DATA SCARCITY: Neither team's R6S roster, recent playday performance in EML 2026, nor head-to-head record is documented in briefing. This limits conviction on both sides. However, market momentum is the strongest signal when direct competitive data is absent in a live event. PLAYOFF BO3 FORMAT: Best-of-three favors the stronger team and reduces upset variance. If Twisted Minds is truly favored, the longer format reinforces the edge. RESOLUTION IMMINENT (5 HOURS): At this stage, major reversals require unexpected external events (roster withdrawals, DQ, technical issues). The 84% price reflects high probability Twisted Minds simply plays and wins\u2014not a high bar to clear at match start.", "key_factor": "Strong market momentum (+42pp in 24h, +34pp in 7d) and sharp upward moves suggest informed betting flow favoring Twisted Minds despite data scarcity."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.22, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains ZERO Rainbow Six Siege performance data for either Twisted Minds or Fnatic\u2014search results returned only Rocket League and Warzone records for Twisted Minds, making any high-confidence prediction analytically indefensible. MARKET OVERCONFIDENCE SIGNAL: YES price surged +42pp in 24hrs (+34pp over 7 days) with extreme volatility (11pp/hr), suggesting speculative momentum rather than information-driven repricing. Sharp moves on Apr 13 (+26.5pp, +15.5pp) occurred with no new data released. UNDERDOG CASE FOR FNATIC: At 17% (severely underpriced given data void), Fnatic benefits from: (1) market's apparent unfamiliarity with both teams in R6S context, creating pricing bias toward the name traders recognize; (2) possibility of superior recent form, roster stability, or meta adaptation not captured in briefing; (3) upper bracket quarterfinal BO3 format favors consistency\u2014Fnatic could be the steadier performer. TWISTED MINDS VULNERABILITIES: No evidence in briefing of recent R6S dominance, tournament results, or meta-game competency. Twisted Minds' strong Rocket League and Warzone records are irrelevant to R6S prediction and may have created false confidence among market participants. STRUCTURAL WEAKNESS IN YES PRICING: 84% probability for a team with zero R6S form data in the briefing reflects speculation, not analysis. The 24-hour momentum surge (+42pp) is suspiciously large for an event 5 hours from resolution with no new intel\u2014suggests retail/momentum trading rather than informed repositioning. FNATIC HIDDEN STRENGTH SCENARIO: If Fnatic is an established R6S powerhouse (not revealed in briefing), the market's focus on Twisted Minds' other-game success creates underpricing. Upper bracket BO3 format (not single elimination) rewards experience and consistency\u2014Fnatic's familiarity with EML structure could be decisive. CONFIDENCE LIMITATIONS: Both confidence_yes (25) and confidence_no (28) are LOW due to identical data scarcity. Cannot validate either team's R6S credentials, recent patch adaptation, roster changes, or head-to-head record. Market is pricing on noise, not signal. TIME-TO-REVERSAL CONTEXT: Event resolves TODAY in ~5 hours. No time for new performance data to emerge. Current 84/17 split is the final market view\u2014but it rests on a foundation of zero R6S intelligence, making it susceptible to sudden reversal post-match if Fnatic wins. PROBABILITY RATIONALE: Assigning 22 to YES reflects skepticism of the 84% overconfidence while acknowledging Twisted Minds could legitimately be superior (absent evidence either way). Fnatic at 78 implied probability (100-22) is higher than raw market odds, reflecting the data void's upward bias on the favorite.", "key_factor": "Severe data vacuum on both teams' R6S form makes market's 84% confidence in Twisted Minds structurally unjustified; Fnatic could exploit unfamiliarity or preparation advantage."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains no Rainbow Six Siege match history, team rosters, recent form, or head-to-head records for either Twisted Minds or Fnatic in R6S. Search results conflate Twisted Minds' Rocket League/Warzone achievements with R6S competition. MARKET SIGNAL ASYMMETRY: YES side currently trades at 84% with strong 7-day uptrend (+34pp, 24-hour +42pp). Sharp move Apr 13 19:26 UTC (+15.5pp) suggests real-time information (possibly match lineup, roster changes, or betting syndicate activity) not captured in briefing. TIMING URGENCY: Event resolves in ~5 hours (TODAY). For LIVE/IMMINENT esports matches, market prices become information-efficient as match approaches. 84% YES suggests market participants have substantive information about team form, recent scrims, roster status, or meta advantage. CONFIDENCE PENALTY: Unable to independently verify YES confidence due to zero R6S performance data. Cannot evaluate Twisted Minds' recent R6S tournament placements, map pool strength, or player skill ratings. Cannot assess Fnatic's current roster or competitive standing in EML 2026. BASELINE INFERENCE: In competitive esports BO3 playoffs, favorites (>75% implied) typically reflect either: (a) dominant recent form, (b) superior roster/skill differential, or (c) favorable meta matchup. Market consensus suggests Twisted Minds holds at least one of these advantages. REGRESSION TO 62%: Starting from market price 84%, adjusting downward to 62% reflects: (i) general volatility in esports betting (upsets occur ~15-25% of time even for heavy favorites), (ii) BO3 format permits comebacks, (iii) online tournament fatigue/server issues as wildcard, (iv) absence of corroborating briefing evidence for such a wide margin. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: confidence_yes=28 reflects inability to justify 84% from available data. confidence_no=25 mirrors this \u2014 insufficient counter-evidence to validate Fnatic upset probability. Neither side merits high confidence given information asymmetry.", "key_factor": "Insufficient R6S team performance data; market pricing suggests 84% YES implies strong pre-match information not available in briefing"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.27, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains NO Rainbow Six Siege performance data for either Twisted Minds or Fnatic. Search results show Twisted Minds in Rocket League/Warzone only, not R6S. MARKET PRICE DISCONNECT: YES side jumped +42pp in 24hr (+34pp over 7d), but no supporting evidence in briefing explains this massive rally. Classic symptom of crowd momentum divorced from fundamentals. SHARP VOLATILITY SPIKE: Apr 13 19:26 UTC +15.5pp move on YES side with zero new information provided in briefing. Suggests crowd trading rather than information-driven repricing. APATHY vs GREED HYBRID: Market is greedily buying YES at 84% despite complete absence of team form, roster strength, or head-to-head data. Crowd appears overconfident in an information vacuum. SPREAD SIGNAL: YES/NO sum to ~101%, indicating moderately healthy orderbook depth. $1,586 volume is thin for such conviction pricing (84%), suggesting retail-driven sentiment rather than sharp money. TIME PRESSURE AMPLIFIES EMOTION: Match resolves TODAY in ~5 hours. At this stage, late money chasing YES likely reflects hype/social signals rather than fundamental analysis. No time for reversal. BOTH SIDES EQUALLY BLIND: Cannot justify confidence above 30 for either side. Briefing provides zero R6S competitive context, recent form, or strategic advantages for either team. CROWD PSYCHOLOGY READ: Crowd has decided YES wins without evidence. This creates a potential contrarian value on NO at 17%, but equally risky since we have no counter-data either. MARKET EFFICIENCY VERDICT: Price does not reflect rational uncertainty. A true 50-50 scenario (no data) should trade 50-50 after spread. Instead, 84-17 split suggests crowd consensus override of epistemic humility. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: Assigning 62% YES reflects slight lean toward market consensus (84% is too extreme given zero supporting detail), but heavily discounted confidence on both sides due to complete information deficit.", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.72, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains only Rocket League and Warzone esports records for 'Twisted Minds'; zero Rainbow Six Siege match history, roster composition, or 2026 EML performance metrics provided. FNATIC R6S PRESENCE UNKNOWN: Search results show G2 Esports R6S data (including recent 7-0 vs FNC on Apr 8), but 'FNC' abbreviation context and Fnatic's current roster/recent form in R6S not provided in briefing. MARKET TIMING RISK: Event is TODAY with ~5 hours to resolution (LIVE/IMMINENT). The +42pp YES movement in 24h and +34pp over 7d suggests material new information entered the market (likely player availability, roster confirmations, or leaked scrim results) NOT documented in this briefing. SHARP MOVE PATTERN: Apr 13 19:26 UTC +15.5pp move (2.75h before stated 12:00 PM ET match start; ~5h before current UTC deadline) indicates possible legitimate pre-match intelligence update, but briefing does not capture the catalyst. LIQUIDITY CONTEXT: $1,586 USD volume is modest for same-day esports BO3; suggests informed betting rather than casual action, increasing weight of unobserved signal. BO3 FORMAT SENSITIVITY: Best-of-three reduces variance vs. single map; requires team depth across meta map pools. Without roster/map preference data, cannot assess whether either team has structural advantage. TOURNAMENT TIER VALIDATION: EML 2026 Kickoff confirmed as A-Tier online tournament (Mar 30 - Apr 24); Upper bracket QF1 is high-stakes, but no playoff bracket structure or seeding provided. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY RATIONALE: confidence_yes=45 reflects that market sentiment and rapid YES price movement suggest informed backing, but zero verifiable R6S data means the YES case rests entirely on unobserved market signal. confidence_no=32 is lower because NO case has even less informational support\u2014Fnatic's R6S standing and recent form are entirely absent from briefing. RESOLUTION CLARITY: 50-50 tiebreaker clause exists only for cancellation, forfeit, or >7d delay; likely outcome is clean win/loss with official Liquipedia publication within 2h post-match. PROBABILITY RATIONALE: Assign 72% YES (hence 28% NO) as a soft deference to rapid market repricing into match time, acknowledging that esports betting markets often embed real-time roster/scrim intelligence 2-6h before match start. However, low confidence_yes reflects absence of documentable R6S form data; the 72 is a directional estimate based on market signal strength, not technical team analysis.", "key_factor": "Market pricing (84% YES) reflects sharp upward movement in the 24 hours before a same-day BO3 match, but the briefing contains zero verifiable R6S team data, rosters, recent form, or head-to-head records for either competitor\u2014creating asymmetric information risk where market sentiment may be driven by non-public pre-match intelligence rather than documented performance."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.32, "confidence_yes": 0.18, "confidence_no": 0.22, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA VOID: The briefing contains ZERO Rainbow Six Siege match history, rosters, recent form, or head-to-head records for either Twisted Minds or Fnatic. The search results are primarily Rocket League and Warzone data\u2014completely irrelevant to R6S competitive dynamics. MARKET PRICE SPIKE AS NOISE: The YES side jumped +42pp in 24 hours and +34pp over 7 days, with sharp volatility (11pp/hr). This aggressive run-up with only 5 hours to match start suggests traders are reacting to rumor, unconfirmed roster news, or social media hype rather than hard competitive evidence. FNATIC'S HISTORICAL R6S PEDIGREE: Fnatic is one of Europe's most established R6S organizations with a long franchise history in the region. Market is pricing them at 17% despite no visibility into current roster quality, recent win/loss streaks, or map-pool matchups\u2014a dangerous assumption that legacy = current weakness. INVISIBLE PERSONNEL LEVERAGE: No data on Fnatic's recent lineup changes, player injuries, or substitutions. A single roster swap (benching underperformer, inserting a high-fragger or IGL) in the 48 hours before match could completely invert tactical balance. Twisted Minds may have no preparation for it. MAP POOL MISMATCH BLINDSPOT: R6S outcomes are heavily determined by map bans/picks. The briefing contains zero information on which maps favor which team's defensive holds, roaming styles, or hard-breacher setups. Fnatic could have a 60-40 advantage on 2 of 3 maps without market showing awareness. META SHIFT NOT REFLECTED: If Ubisoft pushed a recent balance patch favoring anchors or site-denial (Fnatic's presumed strength) over aggressive roaming, the 84% Twisted Minds price does not account for it. Operator buffs/nerfs can swing competitive outcomes by 10-15% overnight. PSYCHOLOGICAL MOMENTUM REVERSAL: Twisted Minds may be perceived as 'favorites' due to recent tournament wins in other esports (Rocket League, Warzone), but R6S player pools and team cohesion are distinct. Fnatic could enter with underdog hunger and team chemistry Twisted Minds lacks despite aggregate pedigree. MATCH TIMING & FATIGUE: The match resolves at 00:15 UTC on Apr 14 (5 hours from briefing time). Both teams may have played qualifiers or group matches in preceding days. Fatigue, server lag, or technical setup issues could favor the fresher or more adaptable roster\u2014undetectable from standings alone. LIQUIDITY & SHARP ACTION: Only $1,586 USD volume suggests retail/casual traders dominating the buy side on YES. Low liquidity makes the market vulnerable to a single informed R6S analyst or team insider betting heavy on Fnatic, triggering a reversal. 50-50 RESOLUTION RISK: If match is forfeited, disqualified, or delayed >7 days, market resolves 50-50. No visibility into either team's administrative standing or potential league-level disputes that could trigger a no-contest outcome.", "key_factor": "Fnatic deploys a roster substitution or tactical innovation (map pool exploitation, operator meta shift, or personnel swap) that the briefing provides zero visibility into, neutralizing Twisted Minds' perceived dominance."}], "final_score": 0.6073417721518987, "no_score": 0.42781725888324873, "edge": -0.2276582278481013, "no_edge": 0.2628172588832487, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "YES-side confidence too low: 34% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1938836", "question": "Rainbow Six Siege: Twisted Minds vs Fnatic (BO3) - Europe MENA League Kickoff Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Rainbow Six Siege Upper bracket quarterfinal 1 match between Twisted Minds and Fnatic in the Europe MENA League Kickoff Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 13 at 12:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Twisted Minds\" if Twisted Minds win the match against Fnatic.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Fnatic\" if Fnatic win the match against Twisted Minds.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf th