{"run_id": "14e45503-7aa2-4778-8bb4-1536ec6e6c03", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T22:57:25.817012+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1918543", "question": "Valorant: Alliance Guardians vs QoR (BO3) - VCL North America: Stage 2 Group Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant Round 5 match between Alliance Guardians and QoR in the VCL North America: Stage 2 Group Stage, initially scheduled for April 13 at 7:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Alliance Guardians\" if Alliance Guardians win the match against QoR.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"QoR\" if QoR win the match against Alliance Guardians.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T04:30:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-13T22:30:00Z", "yes_price": 0.35, "volume_usd": 1385.366141, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["69600105900936699361990805146620912845395253640672513024105039671451895643462", "108127830738231344993585889482070686321749163626554540349403827581711754005817"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.32, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: Market resolves YES if Alliance Guardians win the BO3 match; NO if QoR wins. Criteria are clear and unambiguous for a completed match. CRITICAL TIMING ISSUE: Scheduled match was April 13, 2026 at 19:00 EDT (~13:57 UTC). DATA FRESHNESS is 2026-04-13 22:57 UTC (approximately 9 hours after scheduled start). EVENT TIMING marked as 'TODAY' with end date 2026-04-14 04:30 UTC suggests market resolves in ~6 hours. Match has likely already been played. MARKET PRICE SIGNAL: YES = 35%, NO = 65%. Current market pricing heavily favors QoR, with 7-day trend showing YES falling 18pp and NO rising 18.5pp. This represents strong market confidence in a QoR victory. DATA QUALITY: Briefing provides zero performance metrics, head-to-head records, recent form data, or player statistics for either team. Cannot independently verify which team is favored based on competitive strength. CASE FOR YES (Alliance Guardians): Match confirmed scheduled; both teams active in Stage 2. No substantive performance data supports this outcome. CASE FOR NO (QoR): Market pricing strongly favors QoR (65% vs 35%). QoR confirmed active in Stage 2 (April 6 match vs SRB noted). Market consensus is QoR are favorites, but briefing provides no explanation for this preference. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: vlr.gg is primary source; 2-hour fallback to credible reporting. No mechanism risk flagged. Forfeit/walkover would resolve 50-50, but no indication of such outcome. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes = 25 and confidence_no = 28 reflect severe data gaps on BOTH sides. Market signal is clear (favors NO), but briefing lacks any underlying justification. Cannot confidently defend the market's 65% QoR probability without performance data. Similarly, cannot confidently argue for Alliance Guardians without data. Both sides have poor evidential foundation.", "key_factor": "Briefing contains no performance data, head-to-head records, or team statistics for either Alliance Guardians or QoR; match may already be underway or completed given EVENT TIMING = TODAY and DATA FRESHNESS timestamp of 2026-04-13 22:57 UTC (well after scheduled 2026-04-13 19:00 EDT start)."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.65, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "NO IS THE MARKET CONSENSUS: The market has moved decisively toward QoR (NO side +18.5pp over 7 days), with YES falling from ~51% to 33%. This sustained directional movement suggests informed traders have downgraded Alliance Guardians or upgraded QoR\u2014a signal worth respecting in a live esports market. QoR ROSTER CONFIRMED ACTIVE: QoR has documented participation in Stage 2 matches (vs SRB on April 6), proving roster stability and tournament readiness. No matching recent activity confirmation exists for Alliance Guardians in the briefing. ALLIANCE GUARDIANS DATA VOID: The briefing explicitly states 'limited direct head-to-head or recent form data available for Alliance Guardians.' This asymmetry favors the team WITH visibility (QoR). Absence of positive form indicators is a weakness. SHARP MOVES FAVOR NO: QoR-favorable moves (NO +11pp on Apr 12 05:00 UTC) align with the overall trend. These sharp moves in a low-liquidity market ($1,385 USD) suggest deliberate repositioning by knowledgeable actors. UNDERFUNDED UNDERDOG: YES side at 35% is the underfunded position in a $1,385 market; NO at 65% has absorbed more conviction capital. Esports markets with this profile tend to reflect real competitive imbalance. TIMING RISK FOR YES: Event is LIVE/IMMINENT (resolves in ~6 hours). Reversal would require Alliance Guardians to overcome a -18pp market swing AND outperform a documented, active roster\u2014very unlikely in a BO3 with no time for narrative shifts. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Confidence in NO is higher (72) than YES (35) because QoR has verifiable recent participation and the market has a clear directional signal, while Alliance Guardians lacks comparable evidence. This reflects real data quality imbalance favoring the favorite. SWISS FORMAT CONTEXT: Both teams are in a 16-team, wins-based advancement system. QoR's prior match appearance proves participation; Alliance Guardians' absence from briefing references is notable and suggests either lower profile or weaker recent record.", "key_factor": "Market consensus shift favoring QoR over the past week (-18pp on YES), combined with QoR's confirmed recent tournament participation and roster stability."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "MARKET SETUP: YES priced at 35% is the underdog. NO at 65% is the favorite. Sharp 18pp YES decline over 7 days suggests confidence shifting toward QoR, but this decline may be driven by liquidity/sentiment rather than concrete form data. DATA ASYMMETRY - CRITICAL GAP: Briefing contains zero direct competitive data for Alliance Guardians (no recent match results, no player stats, no form indicators). QoR has minimal evidence too (one mention of April 6 match vs SRB, player names Derrek/Notexxd listed). This is an INFORMATION VACUUM, not a strength differential. UNDERDOG HIDDEN STRENGTH: Alliance Guardians' lack of visibility in search results could reflect: (1) genuinely emerging team riding recent momentum not yet captured in market pricing, (2) intentional low-profile prep strategy before playoffs, or (3) Swiss pairing algorithm matching them as competitive opponent to QoR. The 35% price may reflect market uncertainty rather than measured weakness. FAVORITE VULNERABILITY: QoR's pricing to 65% is based on equally sparse data \u2014 one April 6 match mention and two player names. There is NO evidence of QoR's recent form trajectory, win-loss record in Swiss, or head-to-head dominance. The 18pp YES decline may be overweighting QoR without justified cause. SWISS STAGE DYNAMICS: At Round 5 (mid-stage), both teams at the same record tier face each other by design. If QoR were significantly stronger, Swiss pairing would have already separated them. This structural reality suggests competitive parity, not 65-35 skew. CONFOUNDING FACTORS: Briefing mentions NRG Academy, Evil Geniuses Academy, YFP \u2014 but these are DIFFERENT teams. No cross-team comparison provided. Alliance Guardians and QoR competitive context is entirely isolated. PRICE MOMENTUM vs FUNDAMENTALS: Sharp moves on Apr 11-12 (\u00b111.5pp, \u00b16.5pp) suggest volatile trader positioning, not new public information disclosed in briefing. Volatility is 0.4-0.5pp/hr \u2014 low absolute movement but relative to small market cap ($1,385 USD) indicates thin liquidity and potential mispricing. TIME-TO-REVERSAL IMPACT: Event is TODAY (~6 hours to kickoff). Market will resolve in hours. Any upset requires Alliance Guardians to execute in real-time BO3 against unknown opponent. With minimal form data for both teams, in-match variance dominates. However, thin briefing data means confidence on BOTH sides must remain low. VERDICT ON UPSIDE: Evidence does not support calling Alliance Guardians a 'strong' underdog \u2014 the briefing simply lacks data. BUT it also does not justify QoR at 65%. A true 65-35 market requires documented proof of QoR superiority; none is present. Alliance Guardians is underpriced relative to the ABSENCE of differentiating information, not relative to negative form. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: confidence_yes = 28 (minimal positive Alliance Guardians form data; relying on structural symmetry and price overextension as proxies). confidence_no = 32 (QoR similarly lacks documented superiority; 65% pricing is not supported by briefing evidence). Both low because briefing data is insufficient for either team.", "key_factor": "Alliance Guardians' limited visibility in briefing data may mask undervalued team form or strategic matchup advantages in a compressed Swiss stage where mid-tier teams are tightly clustered."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.33, "confidence_yes": 0.22, "confidence_no": 0.24, "rationale": "EVENT TIMING: Match is TODAY, scheduled for April 13 2026 at 19:00 EDT (~6 hours from briefing timestamp). At this stage, reversal to YES would require QoR collapse or Alliance Guardians upset \u2014 both low-probability at this time window. MARKET SIGNAL: YES side has fallen 18pp over 7 days (from ~51% to 33%), indicating consistent market drift toward QoR. Sharp moves on Apr 11-12 suggest internal information or odds adjustment by sophisticated participants. Current 35% YES pricing reflects material shift in sentiment. DATA ASYMMETRY (Critical): Briefing provides NO direct head-to-head record, recent win-loss records, player form metrics, or roster strength comparisons for either team. QoR mentioned with specific players (Derrek, Notexxd) in rankings; Alliance Guardians mentioned only by name with no performance context. This creates asymmetric data quality favoring NO confidence assessment. ROSTER/PERFORMANCE CONTEXT: QoR confirmed active in Stage 2 (match vs SRB on April 6). No comparable recent match data for Alliance Guardians provided. Absence of data for one team in esports typically indicates weaker public profile or lower ranking, which markets price as disadvantage. SWISS FORMAT BASE RATE: In 16-team Swiss BO3 formats, the distribution of wins is skewed