0pp YES) suggest market is not genuinely uncertain\u2014consensus has solidified with minimal new information driving repricing. Sharp moves (Apr 11-12) preceded current stability, implying price discovery already occurred; current 35% likely reflects QoR information advantage, not crowd overreaction. Rational apathy detected: market is pricing in available data (QoR visibility + Alliance Guardians invisibility) without emotional excess. Current odds may underestimate Alliance Guardians if they are actually stronger than briefing suggests, but briefing provides no contrary signal. Confidence asymmetry justified: confidence_yes (28) reflects inability to defend Alliance Guardians case beyond 'match is scheduled'; confidence_no (32) reflects modest QoR edge based on player visibility, but uncertainty about Alliance Guardians' true strength keeps both low.", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.34, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "EVENT TIMING CRITICAL: Briefing shows DATA_FRESHNESS at 2026-04-13 22:57 UTC, but END_DATE is 2026-04-14 04:30 UTC (~6 hours remaining). Match was scheduled for 2026-04-13 19:00 EDT (23:00 UTC). This suggests the match is CURRENTLY LIVE or recently concluded. PROBABILITY INTERPRETATION: If match is live/in-progress, the 35% YES price reflects real competitive state (likely map scores, economy, round count) not pre-match odds. A reversal from 35% to 50%+ would require Alliance Guardians to win remaining maps\u2014feasible in BO3 but constrained by remaining time and current state. MARKET PRICE TRAJECTORY: YES side fell 18pp over 7 days and shows -11.5pp spike (Apr 11), then oscillating \u00b16-11pp swings Apr 12-13. Pattern suggests information arrival (likely match start, early results) rather than stable pre-match uncertainty. Current stability (+0.0pp last 24h) suggests prices have converged on live match reality. DATA INSUFFICIENCY: Briefing provides no head-to-head record, recent form metrics, player ratings, or map pool compatibility for Alliance Guardians vs QoR. Case for YES notes 'no recent form data available for Alliance Guardians' \u2014 this asymmetry suggests QoR may be the known stronger competitor, supporting NO-side confidence. ROSTER CONTEXT: QoR roster includes Derrek and Notexxd (named in brief), suggesting established competitive identity. Alliance Guardians lacks equivalent named reference, implying less documented pedigree or newer roster composition. BO3 MECHANICS: In a best-of-3, if match is underway and current state (reflected in 35% YES odds) shows QoR ahead, Alliance Guardians must win remaining maps. Standard BO3 probability: if QoR leads 1-0 (maps), Alliance must win 2 straight (~30-40% baseline if teams evenly matched). The 35% YES price aligns with this scenario. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: confidence_yes=28 (low) because no pre-match performance data supports Alliance Guardians; confidence_no=32 (marginally higher) because QoR is minimally documented but at least named player references exist. Both low due to insufficient esports analytics (missing: recent match VODs, map win rates, agent pool strength, LAN vs online performance). SWISS FORMAT NOTE: Both teams are mid-tournament (Round 5 of Swiss with 4-win target for playoffs). No information on current W-L records provided, limiting strength-of-schedule inference. RESOLUTION RISK: Match scheduled 19:00 EDT on Apr 13 (resolved by 04:30 UTC Apr 14 per market end). If match encountered technical issues, forfeit, or delays >7 days, resolves 50-50 per criteria\u2014low probability given normal tournament operations, but non-zero tail risk.", "key_factor": "In a live BO3 match with ~6 hours to resolution, the 18pp weekly decline in YES odds and current 35% price likely reflects real-time match progression or decisive early map results rather than pre-match sentiment, making reversal probability extremely low unless the briefing timestamp predates actual match start."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "Market fell 18pp over 7 days (33\u219235 recent) with sharp -11.5pp move Apr 11, suggesting late material information shifted sentiment against Guardians; briefing contains NO explanation for this cascade \u2014 typical driver is roster/personnel news. Briefing conspicuously silent on Alliance Guardians' recent form, prior matches, or roster stability \u2014 contrast with QoR name-drop (Derrek, Notexxd mentioned). Absence-of-signal suggests either weak recent performance or lack of public track record, both elevating injury/sub risk. Swiss format at Round 5 (April 13) means both teams are mid-tournament; Guardians' record unknown. If Guardians are 1-3 or 2-2, morale and urgency differ sharply vs QoR \u2014 potential motivation gap if QoR are 3-1 and Guardians are desperate. BO3 format in Valorant is tactically punishing: one substitute or personality clash (comms breakdown, tilt after map 1 loss) can cascade into 0-2. Market volatility (11.5pp swings) suggests micro-information flow; a roster tweak 6h before match would not be in briefing yet. No head-to-head history or map pool analysis provided; Guardians may have structural weakness (e.g., weak Bind/Haven) that QoR exploit. Market price (35% YES) implies Guardians are underdog, yet briefing provides zero evidence of their skill tier or tactical matchup. Current YES price of 35% is already discounting Guardians heavily; contrarian signal is that market may be *overcorrecting* on limited information \u2014 but 7-day downtrend + sharp Apr 11 move suggests informed money, not panic. Confidence in NO is only 42% because the driver (personnel? form?) is hidden. If Guardians' 18pp 7-day drop reflects a known roster concern (injury, suspension, internal drama), that is already priced in. Flip scenario: *no* such issue exists, market overestimated the problem, Guardians' fundamentals are stronger than QoR's. But absence of recent stats makes this speculative. Resolution criteria mention forfeiture/disqualification \u2192 50-50 tie; extremely low probability but non-zero black swan if either org has compliance or financial issues.", "key_factor": "Alliance Guardians fields a substitute or academy-level player mid-series due to last-minute illness/technical issue, severely disrupting team synergy and clutch execution in a BO3 that likely hinges on map 3."}], "final_score": 0.3869154228855721, "no_score": 0.5813740458015266, "edge": 0.03691542288557215, "no_edge": -0.0686259541984734, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 37% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1918543", "question": "Valorant: Alliance Guardians vs QoR (BO3) - VCL North America: Stage 2 Group Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant Round 5 match between Alliance Guardians and QoR in the VCL North America: Stage 2 Group Stage, initially scheduled for April 13 at 7:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Alliance Guardians\" if Alliance Guardians win the match against QoR.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"QoR\" if QoR win the match against Alliance Guardians.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the