um. Probability stays at market price (28% YES) because briefing offers no concrete signal to contradict it, but both confidence scores remain below 50 due to systematic data insufficiency on both sides.", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "T1 ACADEMY FUNDAMENTALS: T1 org maintains systematic player development infrastructure; Academy teams historically seed top-tier challengers into main roster. Feb 2026 3-0 playoff sweep vs NS Challengers demonstrates acute competitive capability at this exact tier. DN SOOPER\u0421 OPACITY: Minimal documented match history, no roster depth data, no 2026 win-loss record in briefing. Unknown variables (roster stability, recent scrims, player injuries) create asymmetric information favoring T1's known strength profile. MARKET PRICE ASYMMETRY: 28% YES / 72% NO reflects heavy T1 Academy favoritism. 7-day YES trend (-22.5pp) suggests information flow toward T1 confidence; sharp move Apr 10 (-26pp on YES) likely represents pre-match T1 hype or DN SOOPers news. ACADEMY TIER VOLATILITY: LCK Challenger matches show higher variance than main LCK (younger rosters, less stable meta prep). Single match BO3 outcome is binomial; even heavy favorite (T1) carries ~25-30% upset risk in academy context. MISSING CRITICAL DATA: No 2026 DN SOOPers match results, no recent T1 Academy form beyond Feb playoff, no head-to-head history, no roster overlap/meta info. Briefing explicitly states 'sparse direct information' and 'incomplete' current form. RESOLUTION TIMING: Event is TODAY (~15h to match). Share prices will rapidly converge to $0.01/$0.99 once match begins/concludes. Current market reflects pre-match consensus but lacks real-time player status updates (illness, substitution) possible in next 15 hours. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: YES confidence (35) reflects that T1 Academy is objectively stronger on available evidence but DN SOOPers remain unmodelable. NO confidence (42) reflects T1's clear historical edge but incomplete 2026 form data limits certainty to 'likely but not overwhelming.'", "key_factor": "T1 Academy's historical dominance in LCK Challengers (3-0 sweep vs NS.C in Feb 2026) is the strongest signal, but incomplete 2026 roster/form data and DN SOOPers' opacity create material uncertainty that market's 72% NO confidence may not fully capture."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.24, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "MARKET SIGNAL: YES side has crashed -22.5pp over 7 days (now 28%), with sharp -26pp move Apr 10 and stabilization, suggesting informed money fled DN SOOPers on internal/roster news not visible in briefing. DATA VOID ON DN SOOPER: Briefing contains almost zero performance data, roster composition, or recent form for DN SOOPers\u2014this asymmetry of information cuts both ways: either DN SOOPers is genuinely inferior (justifying 28%), or their recent trajectory/roster changes are unknown to market. T1 ACADEMY ROTATION RISK: T1 historically rotates academy talent into main roster mid-season and benches academy players when they plateau; if best DN SOOPers academy players were called up or motivation is low in developmental league, this BO3 format punishes complacency. ACADEMY FORMAT VOLATILITY: BO3 in challengers league is not a single-game coin flip; a team that executes one clean win condition in Games 1\u20132 can force Game 3 where mental/momentum shifts are decisive\u201428% YES implies <1 in 3.5 chance, but BO3 upsets are structurally more plausible than single-game upsets. TEMPORAL PROXIMITY: Event is TODAY (15 hours to resolution); if roster changes, injuries, or coaching announcements dropped in last 12 hours in Korean esports channels not reflected in briefing, market has already priced some of this in (hence the -4.5pp 24h move). T1 ACADEMY PEDIGREE CUT BOTH WAYS: February 2026 3-0 vs NS Challengers is 6+ weeks old in esports; meta 