{"run_id": "4740da44-68db-46e6-8478-6bbdcacd030c", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T23:07:32.491445+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1962513", "question": "Valorant: TYLOO vs JD Gaming (BO3) - VCT China Group Alpha", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between TYLOO and JD Gaming in the VCT China Group Alpha, initially scheduled for April 14 at 5:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"TYLOO\" if TYLOO win the match against JD Gaming.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"JD Gaming\" if JD Gaming win the match against TYLOO.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T15:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-14T09:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.665, "volume_usd": 24864.414930000003, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["89586569810267251223175666008432336704125159391376365062897773571855102346536", "19114993550811457972983872656071922354108776327696957668721444666241226689757"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "MATCH CONDITION: Resolution criteria require a decisive match outcome (TYLOO win vs JD Gaming win); ties, cancellations, forfeit-before-start, or delays >7 days resolve 50-50. MARKET SIGNAL: Current YES price of 66% and strong recent momentum (+16.5pp over 7 days, +5.5pp in 24hr) suggests informed traders believe TYLOO is favored; sharp move on Apr 12 (+11pp) indicates new information entered market. EVENT TIMING: Match scheduled for TODAY (Apr 14, 5:00 AM ET / ~16 hours from briefing timestamp); very short time window for cancellation or major reversal, so event is likely to occur as scheduled. CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains only Fnatic/EMEA historical data; no TYLOO or JD Gaming recent form, roster, head-to-head history, or competitive standing provided. This prevents bottom-up analysis of relative strength. CASE FOR YES (TYLOO): Market pricing (66%) and strong upward momentum suggest information asymmetry favoring TYLOO; traders with China region expertise may have access to form/roster data not in briefing. CASE FOR NO (JD Gaming): No data provided to support JDG's chances; briefing references both teams as active in VCT CN but provides zero comparative context. PROBABILITY RECONCILIATION: Market price of 66% YES is reasonable given upward momentum and trader positioning, but lacks evidentiary support from briefing. Conservative adjustment reflects asymmetric data quality rather than skepticism of market signal. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes=45 (market signal present but unsupported by briefing data) and confidence_no=35 (virtually no information to evaluate JDG) reflect profound data gap on both sides; neither side is well-supported. RESOLUTION RISK: VLR.gg resolution source and 2-hour fallback clear; team name identification straightforward (TYLOO vs JD Gaming/JDG Esports); no ambiguity in criteria or name-matching risk. FINAL ESTIMATE: Lean TYLOO based on market momentum and trader behavior, but with low confidence due to absent substantive performance data.", "key_factor": "Briefing contains predominantly EMEA team data (Fnatic) rather than China-region team performance data; no substantive performance history, roster data, or head-to-head records for TYLOO or JD Gaming provided to support probability estimate."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.66, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE (YES = TYLOO at 66%) STRENGTHS: Market has moved +16.5pp over 7 days with a sharp +11.0pp move on Apr 12, indicating accumulation or new information favoring TYLOO; the sustained rise and current 66% pricing suggests confidence from bettors with access to team-specific data not visible in this briefing. UNDERDOG WEAKNESSES (NO = JDG at 34%): JDG's odds have fallen -5.0pp over 7 days, mirroring TYLOO's rise; the divergence in momentum is the most concrete signal available \u2014 market is voting with money toward TYLOO. CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains almost no China team-specific performance metrics, roster info, or head-to-head history; the search results are dominated by Fnatic/EMEA data, not VCT China competitive context. This severely limits confidence on BOTH sides. MOMENTUM AS PROXY: In a data-poor environment, price momentum is often the strongest signal of informed trading. YES has +5.5pp in 24h while maintaining volatility of only 0.7pp/hr, suggesting steady accumulation rather than panic buying or volatility noise. MATCH LOGISTICS SOLID: Both teams confirmed in official VCT CN Week 3 schedule; no cancellation/forfeit signals in briefing; match is imminent (TODAY, ~16h to resolution), reducing reversal risk. TYLOO INFERENCE: No direct stats provided, but the fact that market makers and bettors have bid TYLOO to 66% (a clear favorite but not overwhelming) suggests perceived parity with a slight edge \u2014 consistent with regional strength or recent form unknown to this analyst. JDG VIABILITY: 34% is not a knock-out price; 1-in-3 Bo3 upsets happen regularly in Valorant; JDG's lack of visible recent wins in briefing does not mean they are weak, only that data is unavailable. CONFIDENCE CONSTRAINT: Without team statistics, recent match outcomes, or roster/meta alignment, high confidence on either side is unjustified. YES confidence set to 45 (moderate) because: (i) market momentum is real but limited data window; (ii) TYLOO is favored but not overwhelming; (iii) Bo3 format favors consistency, which is unassessed. NO confidence set to 35 (low) because: (i) falling odds suggest deteriorating case; (ii) underdog in a match with no visible tailwind; (iii) cannot articulate specific weakness of JDG, only absence of positive signal. SPREAD/VIG NOTE: YES + NO = 100%, no apparent arbitrage; market is efficiently priced relative to available information, which is thin.", "key_factor": "Market consensus reflects TYLOO as marginal favorite in a match with severely limited underlying performance data, and the 7-day +16.5pp rise in YES odds suggests informed betting pressure rather than noise."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.34, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing provides match history exclusively for Fnatic (EMEA team), not TYLOO or JD Gaming. No recent performance data, win-loss records, roster strength, or competitive form is available for either Chinese team. MARKET MOMENTUM SIGNAL: YES side has surged +16.5pp over 7 days and +5.5pp in 24h, suggesting market confidence in TYLOO. However, this rise occurred despite zero new concrete evidence in the briefing\u2014a red flag for hype-driven repricing rather than fundamental analysis. SHARP MOVE UNEXPLAINED: The +11.0pp spike on Apr 12 23:00 UTC has no corresponding justification in the provided briefing. Without visibility into what triggered this move, it cannot be validated as information-driven or speculative. UNDERDOG FOUNDATION: JD Gaming (NO @ 34%) is priced as the underdog, yet the briefing contains identical zero evidence for or against either team. This symmetry suggests the market has made a directional bet without clear data differentiation\u2014classic conditions for misprice-able underdogs. CONFIDENCE PENALTY: Both confidence_yes and confidence_no are held at 28 and 26 respectively because the briefing provides fewer than 2 concrete data points about either team's recent performance. This violates the analytical standard required for conviction betting. REGIONAL CONTEXT MISSING: VCT China Stage 1 involves teams competing in a distinct regional ecosystem. Chinese Valorant competitive depth, meta adaptation, and team-specific form trajectories are entirely absent from the briefing. TYLOO's historical standing within CN Valorant is unknown. BO3 VOLATILITY: Best-of-three formats increase upset potential relative to single maps. Without roster, agent pool strength, map pool matchups, or recent series results, BO3 inherent variance is unquantifiable and could favor either side equally. RESOLUTION CRITERIA STABILITY: Match is scheduled for TODAY, 16 hours away. Cancellation risk is minimal per the resolution rules, but forfeiture/disqualification scenarios (both resolve 50-50) are not accounted for in market pricing\u2014small tail risk favoring NO structural integrity. CASE AGAINST YES OVERCONFIDENCE: The 66% price assumes TYLOO superiority despite zero form data, roster comparisons, or head-to-head history in the briefing. Without this foundation, the +16.5pp weekly rally appears speculative rather than analytically grounded. CASE FOR NO UNDERVALUATION: JD Gaming @ 34% may be systematically underestimated if they possess recent momentum, strong individual players, or favorable map pool matchups not captured in the briefing. In data-sparse markets, underdogs often retain hidden value. VOLUME ADEQUACY: $24,864 in total volume suggests light liquidity and potential for retail-driven misprice. With low participation and high YES momentum, the market may have anchored on outdated seeding data or Fnatic confusion rather than live form. ANALYTICAL CONCLUSION: The YES side's dominance (66%) cannot be justified by the briefing's content. Without concrete performance differentials, the probability_score defaults toward the underdog NO side. Market pricing appears disconnected from available evidence, suggesting JD Gaming is UNDERPRICED at 34%.", "key_factor": "Severe data asymmetry\u2014briefing contains zero recent performance, roster, or head-to-head data for either TYLOO or JD Gaming, making the 66% YES price potentially anchored on stale or speculative information rather than current form."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains NO performance metrics, recent results, head-to-head history, roster strength, or form data for either TYLOO or JD Gaming. Search results are dominated by EMEA team data (Fnatic, VIT, etc.), not China region teams. MARKET STRUCTURE: Current YES price of 66% reflects modest but meaningful confidence in TYLOO. The 7-day rise of +16.5pp (sharp +11pp move on Apr 12) suggests information arrival favoring TYLOO, but briefing does not document what that information was. TIMING CONSTRAINT: Event is TODAY (resolves in ~16 hours). Reversal probability is low given imminent resolution. Confidence scores must be depressed due to insufficient evidence, not inflated by market movement. ASYMMETRIC CONFIDENCE: confidence_yes=28 and confidence_no=25 both LOW because briefing lacks independent analytical basis to justify either outcome. Market price (66/34 split) is the primary signal, but without team data, both sides are underspecified. BASE RATE REASONING: Professional Valorant league matches are typically high-information events by match day. The absence of any team performance context suggests either: (a) briefing is incomplete, or (b) data truly unavailable. Either way, analyst should not hallucinate team strength or recent form. MARKET PRICE DIVERGENCE: 66% YES is above 50-50 but not extreme. This is consistent with weak-to-moderate favoritism for TYLOO in the market consensus. Without contradicting data, we defer to market pricing with heavy discount for confidence. PROBABILITY RATIONALE: Probability_score of 62 is pulled down from market price of 66 to reflect uncertainty penalty, but does not invert the market signal. This reflects 'market is probably right directionally, but I cannot validate magnitude.'", "key_factor": "In professional Valorant BO3 matches with symmetric team representation in organized leagues, base rate favors neither team without performance data (~50%). Market pricing shows 66% YES, indicating modest favoritism toward TYLOO."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains almost no China-region team performance data, roster info, or head-to-head history. Most search results are Fnatic/EMEA-focused, not China VCT relevant. YES side has risen +16.5pp over 7 days and +5.5pp in 24h, suggesting market has developed conviction, but on what basis? No recent TYLOO or JDG match results provided to justify the climb. Market is priced at 66/34 (fairly wide spread favoring YES) but briefing provides no evidence supporting either team's strength, form, or competitive standing in VCT China. Rational Apathy: Market appears to have taken a directional position without underlying data transparency. Crowd may be reacting to team reputation, betting volume, or external signals not captured in briefing. Both confidence scores intentionally LOW (28/25): Data asymmetry is severe. Cannot evaluate either side properly without recent match results, team standings, roster quality, or head-to-head history. Probability set to 58 (near-neutral, slight YES lean matching current market price) only because market has already moved there; this reflects resignation to missing info, not conviction. Event timing is TODAY/IMMINENT (~16h to resolution). If market reverses sharply after official team announcements, rosters, or recent scrims become known, current 66 price could collapse quickly. Possible crowd psychology: Market may be overweighting one team's brand name or recent tournament success without VCT China-specific context. Briefing does not support differentiation.", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing documents Fnatic (EMEA-based) match history extensively but provides NO performance metrics, roster info, or recent match outcomes for either TYLOO or JD Gaming (JDG Esports), the two teams in question. MARKET SIGNAL DOMINANCE: Current YES price of 66% and sharp +16.5pp rise over 7 days (+11.0pp spike on Apr 12) suggests informed China-region betting activity, but the briefing provides no underlying competitive intelligence to validate or contest this signal. CHINA VCT CONTEXT ABSENT: The briefing mentions 'VCT 2026: China Stage 1' as a structure but offers zero regional competitive landscape, team tier rankings, or roster depth comparisons between TYLOO and JDG that would inform a principled estimate. INSUFFICIENT HEAD-TO-HEAD DATA: No historical match records, map