a but ZERO comparable depth on TYLOO or JDG. This asymmetry suggests the analyst council may be overweighting readily available EMEA benchmarks rather than focusing on China-specific competitive dynamics. JDG WEEK 2 BASELINE: JDG competed against Titan Esports Club in Week 2 (outcome unknown in briefing). TYLOO faced All Gamers. Without win/loss records or map-level data, neither team's current trajectory is determinable. A 2-0 stomp by JDG in Week 2 would substantially weaken the 66% YES consensus. CHINA REGIONAL VOLATILITY: VCT China is historically less stable than EMEA/Americas in roster coherence and meta adaptation. A single unannounced player substitution (illness, visa delay, or internal roster rotation) in the 16 hours before match start could flip a 66/34 split entirely. ABSENCE-OF-SIGNAL ON FORM: The briefing lists TYLOO vs All Gamers as a completed Week 2 match but provides no score. If TYLOO lost or narrowly won, market bias toward YES becomes more suspicious. If the score is not yet publicly available, late-breaking form data could shift confidence sharply downward. BO3 FORMAT SWING: Best-of-three matches in regional brackets often feature high upset rates when underdogs (JDG, if undervalued) exploit niche agent/map synergies the market hasn't priced in. No agent pool, map ban history, or tactical tendencies are documented in the briefing. SCHEDULING/FATIGUE SIGNAL: Multiple Week 3 matches are listed (TYLOO/JDG, Trace/Dragon Ranger, Titan/FunPlus, BLG/others). If TYLOO played a physically demanding match earlier in the week or JDG benefits from extra rest, this structural advantage is invisible to the briefing. 66% PRICE AS CONSENSUS TRAP: Market is now pricing TYLOO as a clear favorite. With zero granular competitive data, this may reflect coordination among traders with inside knowledge rather than measurable skill edges. Contrarian edge lies in JDG being underpriced IF they have a specific tactical counter (e.g., Sage-heavy composition or map veto advantage). RESOLUTION RISK MITIGATION: Even if match is played, forfeiture/disqualification/walkover clauses resolve to 50-50. While rare, Chinese regional esports occasionally face visa, travel, or administrative delays. No briefing coverage of any such risk lowers confidence on BOTH sides symmetrically.", "key_factor": "TYLOO's recent Week 2 match against All Gamers may mask internal roster instability or a tactical vulnerability to JDG's specific map pool and agent meta that favors aggressive early-round execution."}], "final_score": 0.5614345991561182, "no_score": 0.45067961165048537, "edge": -0.10356540084388188, "no_edge": 0.1156796116504854, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 56% for YES (need \u226557%); YES-side confidence too low: 34% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1962513", "question": "Valorant: TYLOO vs JD Gaming (BO3) - VCT China Group Alpha", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between TYLOO and JD Gaming in the VCT China Group Alpha, initially scheduled for April 14 at 5:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"TYLOO\" if TYLOO win the match against JD Gaming.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"JD Gaming\" if JD Gaming win the match against TYLOO.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T15:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-14T09:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.665, "volume_usd": 24864.414930000003, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["89586569810267251223175666008432336704125159391376365062897773571855102346536", "19114993550811457972983872656071922354108776327696957668721444666241226689757"]}, "key_facts": ["| Date | Tier | Type |  | Tournament | Score | | vs.", "Opponent |  |\n ---  ---  ---  --- \n| April 9, 2026 - 17:00 CEST | S-Tier | Offline | VCT EMEA: Stage 1 - Week 2VCT EMEA: Stage 1 - Week 2 | VCT EMEA: Stage 1 - Week 2 |  | 2 : 0 | VIT | View match details |\n| April 1, 2026 - 17:00 CEST | S-Tier | Offline | VCT EMEA: Stage 1 - Week 1VCT EMEA: Stage 1 - Week 1 | VCT EMEA: Stage 1 - Week 1 |  | 2 : 1 | EF | View match details |\n| February 15, 2026 - 18:00 CET | S-Tier | Offline | VCT EMEA KickoffVCT EMEA Kickoff | VCT EMEA Kickoff |  | 0 : 3 | TL | View match details |\n| February 14, 2026 - 17:00 CET | S-Tier | Offline | VCT EMEA KickoffVCT EMEA Kickoff | VCT EMEA Kickoff |  | 2 : 3 | M8 | View match details | [...] | Febru