{"run_id": "610fdff4-e7ec-48ea-aa9a-14fa4410a661", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T23:11:55.071163+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1935119", "question": "LoL: BNK FearX Youth vs Dplus KIA Challengers (BO3) - LCK Challengers League Rounds 1-2", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between BNK FearX Youth and Dplus KIA Challengers in the LCK Challengers League Rounds 1-2, initially scheduled for April 14 at 6:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"BNK FearX Youth\" if BNK FearX Youth win the match against Dplus KIA Challengers.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Dplus KIA Challengers\" if Dplus KIA Challengers win the match against BNK FearX Youth.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T16:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-14T10:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.375, "volume_usd": 6651.254574999999, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["96078953260429416922479317170059910062890056653989028104411428675132591033904", "110670555279643021530050035756895510959456062560991235204875688365160450596081"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "CONDITION TO RESOLVE: BNK FearX Youth must win the BO3 match against Dplus KIA Challengers in LCK Challengers League Rounds 1-2 on April 14, 2026. BNK FearX Youth team statistics: 37.5% win rate (6-10 record) over 16 games in current 2026 Kickoff season\u2014below-average baseline performance. Positive factors for BNK FearX Youth: Strong jungle (KR Zephyr 65.4% KP), elite bot laner (KR Slayer 3.3 KDA with Ezreal 14.0 KDA, Jhin 20.0 KDA), and mid laner (KR FIESTA 100% WR on Sylas/Akali). Recent 2-0 victory over HLE Challengers shows capability to beat solid opponents. Negative factors for BNK FearX Youth: Top laner (KR Kangin) shows inconsistent performance with multiple 0% win rates and low KDAs; team exhibits high variance (many champions with 0% WR across all roles). Jungle-priority draft strategy (1.6 avg pick order) may be predictable to prepared opponents. Critical data gap: Dplus KIA Challengers statistics are entirely absent from briefing. Cannot evaluate opponent strength, win rate, player performance, or historical matchup record. This asymmetry significantly limits confidence in either direction. Market pricing at 38% YES / 62% NO suggests market consensus favors Dplus KIA Challengers. Market has traded with sharp moves (Apr 10: -28pp, Apr 11: +6pp) but recently stabilized. The 24-point spread may reflect hidden information about Dplus KIA Challengers not in briefing. Historical context from 2025 data: BNK FearX Youth reached 2025 LCK CL Finals (lost 1-3 to KT) and won 2025 Summer split (3-1 vs KT), showing capability for strong play. However, 2026 Kickoff shows regression to 37.5% WR\u2014unclear if this is sample size volatility or declining form. Sample size consideration: 16 games in current season provides decent statistical foundation for team assessment but may not reflect current meta, roster changes, or recent coaching adjustments. Tie/cancellation risk is negligible per resolution criteria; match is scheduled for TODAY (17 hours from briefing timestamp), eliminating delay/cancellation concerns. Confidence asymmetry: Higher confidence in YES assessment due to BNK FearX Youth having measurable performance data. However, absence of Dplus KIA Challengers data means confidence_no should reflect high uncertainty about NO outcome validity.", "key_factor": "Insufficient data on Dplus KIA Challengers makes relative strength assessment unreliable; market pricing may reflect hidden information not visible in briefing."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "NO SIDE FUNDAMENTALS: BNK FearX Youth carries a dismal 6-10 record (37.5% WR) across 16 games in 2026 Kickoff\u2014this is the defining reality. The market's 62% NO backing correctly reflects chronic underperformance by the underdog. ROSTER INCONSISTENCY UNDERMINES YES: While KR Zephyr (jungle, 65.4% KP) and KR Slayer (bot, 3.3 KDA) show individual spark, the roster is littered with 0% win rates across champions and roles. Top laner KR Kangin exemplifies this volatility\u2014multiple 0% WR picks with 0.4\u20133.5 KDA spreads. This suggests poor meta adaptation or skill gaps. PREDICTABLE DRAFT EXPLOITABILITY: BNK FearX's heavy jungle priority (1.6 avg pick order) creates tactical predictability. A prepared opponent like Dplus KIA can counter-pick or deny jungle value, especially if KR Zephyr's high KP represents feast-or-famine dependency rather than stable macro contribution. DATA IMBALANCE FAVORS NO: Briefing provides extensive BNK FearX stats but minimal Dplus KIA intel. Market pricing at 62% NO suggests sophisticated bettors have information asymmetry favoring Dplus KIA. The absence of negative Dplus KIA data is itself a positive signal for NO. RECENT MOMENTUM MURKY FOR YES: BNK FearX's 2-0 win vs HLE Challengers (Week 2) is noted, but no trajectory data confirms sustained momentum into this match. With 16-game sample size and 37.5% overall WR, a single win streak is statistically noise. MARKET PRICE HISTORY CONFIRMS NO DOMINANCE: YES prices fell 12.5pp over 7 days (35% EMA); NO prices rose 12.5pp (65% EMA). A sharp Apr 10 move (-28pp for YES) suggests material information favored NO. Current 24h volatility is muted (\u00b11pp), indicating price stability at NO advantage\u2014not wavering consensus. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS IN BOT LANE CONTEXT: While KR Slayer's Ezreal (100% WR, 14.0 KDA) and Jhin (20.0 KDA) are standout, these are small sample sizes (2 games each). Against a full team like Dplus KIA, isolated bot lane excellence may not overcome systemic team weaknesses. TOP LANE AS ACHILLES' HEEL: KR Kangin's 2.6 KDA and 49.4% KP suggests weak laning or teamfight presence. In a BO3, consistent top-side pressure from Dplus KIA could snowball leads and expose BNK FearX's macro fragility. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY RATIONALE: High confidence_no (72%) reflects abundant BNK FearX underperformance data and market consensus. Moderate confidence_yes (35%) reflects real individual stars (Zephyr, Slayer) but tempered by missing Dplus KIA intel and BNK FearX's structural inconsistency. This asymmetry is justified\u2014NO case is data-rich, YES case relies on spotty champion performances and hope. BO3 FORMAT FAVORS CONSISTENCY: BNK FearX's scattered 0% win rates across champions suggest difficulty adapting within series. Dplus KIA, as the market favorite, likely exhibits more consistent team synergy across games\u2014a BO3 advantage.", "key_factor": "Dplus KIA Challengers' market consensus backing (62% priced) reflects superior overall team strength relative to BNK FearX Youth's 37.5% win rate and inconsistent roster performance."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "BNK FearX Youth underdog status justified: 37.5% WR (6-10) in 2026 Kickoff is genuinely weak, and market correctly prices them as underdogs at 38%. However, the briefing reveals critical asymmetry in individual lane strength\u2014jungle and bot are elite tier (KR Zephyr 65.4% KP; KR Slayer 3.3 KDA, 100% Ezreal, 20.0 KDA Jhin), while top lane (KR Kangin) is liability with low consistency and multiple 0% WR champions. Mid laner KR FIESTA shows hidden upside: Sylas and Akali both 100% WR with 9.0 and 3.5 KDA respectively\u2014elite solo-queue mechanics that could carry early-game skirmishes. Dplus KIA Challengers data is almost completely absent from briefing\u2014no stat lines, KDA values, or recent match history provided. This creates severe information asymmetry favoring upside for YES side. BNK FearX Youth draft strategy (jungle priority at 1.6 avg pick order) is predictable but can be a strength if KR Zephyr matches well into DK Challengers' likely jungle pick\u2014no counterjungling data available. Recent concrete win: BFX defeated HLE Challengers 2-0 in Week 2 (January 2026), but this is the only recent high-confidence data point. Macro inconsistency vs. micro excellence is BFX's profile. Market price history shows YES side rose 1.0pp in 24h and recovered 6.0pp on Apr 11, suggesting informed money detecting undervaluation or momentum shift\u2014worth noting but insufficient for high confidence. Verdict: BNK FearX Youth has elite individual win conditions (jungle-bot) that can win a BO3 against mid-tier Challengers, but overall 37.5% WR and top lane liability argue against heavy YES conviction. Dplus KIA Challengers' unknown strength prevents confidence above 45 for NO. The 38% YES price appears roughly fair given poor macro record, but elite micro pockets (especially Zephyr + Slayer) provide realistic upset path. Setting YES at 42% reflects a team that is likely to lose but has credible 2-3 game win scenarios. Confidence split reflects data gap: HIGH confidence in YES micro strengths (confidence_yes=35 because micro data is solid but macro record undermines), LOW confidence in NO because Dplus KIA Challengers is almost entirely unknown (confidence_no=45, not higher, due to missing opponent stat block).", "key_factor": "BNK FearX Youth's elite jungle-bot synergy (KR Zephyr 65.4% KP, KR Slayer 3.3 KDA with 100% Ezreal WR) can exploit mid-tier Challengers opposition despite poor macro record."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.32, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "BNK FearX Youth season record 6-10 (37.5% WR) is below 50%, but BO3 match-specific outcomes differ from season aggregates; historical base rate for sub-.500 teams in single BO3s is closer to 40-45% win probability, not 37.5% Jungle-centric strength (KR Zephyr 65.4% KP) is real but creates predictable draft patterns; opponents can prepare specific counters to known jungle priority Bot lane (KR Slayer 3.3 KDA, Ezreal 100% WR 14.0 KDA, Jhin 50% WR 20.0 KDA) shows high ceiling but small sample sizes (2-4 games per champion); limited evidence of consistency Mid laner KR FIESTA 100% WR on Sylas/Akali but both on 1-game samples; Syndra (primary pick, 73.3% presence) shows only 50% WR\u2014primary champion is unreliable Top laner KR Kangin exhibits severe inconsistency: 7 different champions with 0% WR and KDAs <2.0; suggests vulnerability in lane pressure matchups Critical data gap: Dplus KIA Challengers stats entirely absent from briefing; cannot evaluate opponent strength, recent form, or head-to-head matchup dynamics; this asymmetry reduces confidence in NO assessment Market currently prices YES at 38%, NO at 62%; this reflects below-average team being underdog, which aligns with 37.5% season record; modest mispricing possible but insufficient evidence to claim major edge LCK Challenger youth teams show historically high variance (BO3 upsets common); 16-game season sample has notable noise; single-match predictions in challengers carry inherent uncertainty Event timing TODAY (~17 hours to match) means no new roster/injury/meta data will emerge; market pricing reflects final information state Confidence gap (45 vs 38) reflects asymmetric data: BNK FearX internal metrics are detailed but Dplus KIA is a blind spot; cannot confidently evaluate NO side without opponent context", "key_factor": "~50% win probability for teams with 37.5% season win rates competing in BO3 challenger-tier matches; youth/academy teams show high variance; limited data on Dplus KIA Challengers creates asymmetric confidence"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.32, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "Market is pricing BNK FearX Youth at 38% YES, reflecting a rational pessimistic view anchored on the team's weak 37.5% win rate (6-10 record) in 2026 Kickoff\u2014a clear fundamental weakness. Fear dominates crowd psychology: market has collapsed 12.5pp toward NO over 7 days, with a sharp -28pp move on Apr 10 suggesting conviction selling. This is NOT irrational panic\u2014it tracks the team's documented poor performance. Individual player strength (Zephyr's 65.4% KP, Slayer's 3.3 KDA, FIESTA's 100% WR on Sylas/Akali) is significantly outweighed by systemic team fragility: top laner Kangin inconsistent, multiple 0% win-rate champions across roster, and overall win rate below 40%. Critical data asymmetry: Dplus KIA Challengers stats completely absent from briefing. Market appears to be pricing solely on BNK's weakness, not on DK strength assessment. Confidence in NO side is LOW because we cannot validate that DK is actually favored. Draft predictability risk: BNK's jungle-priority strategy (1.6 avg pick order) may be exploitable by a prepared opponent, but absence of DK data means we cannot confirm they can execute a counter-strategy. Recent form trajectory unknown: last dated result in data is from 2025 playoffs/older seasons. Current 2026 performance could be recent collapse or seasonal trend\u2014unclear if momentum favors either team heading into TODAY's match. Market price (38% YES) is rationally low but confidence in that valuation is medium (62%) because: (a) BNK's weakness is real and documented, but (b) DK's strength/competence is unmeasured, leaving reversal risk unquantified. NO confidence set at only 35% because market lacks competitive context: if DK is similarly weak, 62% NO could be severe overpricing. The asymmetric data quality suggests market is trading on BNK visibility, not genuine DK strength signal. BO3 format adds variance risk: even weak teams win individual maps. 38% for a BO3 appears reasonable for a sub-40% win-rate team, but without DK baseline, the margin is speculative rather than evidence-based. Time-to-reversal: 17 hours remain. No major roster changes, injury reports, or tactical revelations evident in briefing. Market pricing appears stable and reflecting available information accurately, though incompletely.", "key_factor": "Fear"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.32, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "Win Rate Context: BNK FearX's 37.5% (6-10) is significantly below 50% baseline; in BO3 formats, teams below .400 win rate rarely outperform expectations in high-stakes matches unless facing significantly weaker opponents. Draft Vulnerability: Jungle priority at 1.6 pick order (highest on team) creates predictable ban/counterpick opportunities\u2014advanced LCK teams exploit this through early-game jungle tracking and lane assignments. Individual Talent Mismatch: While KR Zephyr (65.4% KP) and KR Slayer show strong per-game stats, these metrics in a 37.5% win-rate context suggest individual skill does not translate to macro coordination required for BO3 victories. Dplus KIA Unknown Factor: Zero performance data available on Dplus KIA Challengers creates asymmetric information; market pricing at 62% NO reflects sophisticated bettors' assessment of competitive balance\u2014absence of data on DK likely means their roster is stable/known to insiders. Top Lane Instability: KR Kangin's champion pool shows 25-50% win rates on primary picks (Sion, K'Sante) with zero-win-rate experimentation (Yorick, Yasuo)\u2014suggests role inconsistency that becomes critical in BO3 where teams adapt between games. Mid-Laner Volatility: KR FIESTA's 100% WR on Sylas/Akali (sample: 1 game each) inflates expectations; 0% WR on Ahri/Twisted Fate indicates meta adaptation failure, typical of lower-tier challenger teams facing coordinated bans. Sample Size: 16-game snapshot is adequate for individual KDA trends but insufficient for determining team synergy improvements/declines\u2014recency bias toward individual highlights masks systemic mid-game decision-making deficits. Market Signal: Price movement shows -12.5pp YES shift over 7 days but only +1.0pp in last 24 hours; early volatility (Apr 10: -28pp) likely reflects roster/bracket information release, now stabilized at 38% suggesting informed consensus. BO3 Format Risk: Best-of-three requires adaptive strategy across three games; BNK FearX's predictable draft and role inconsistencies become more exploitable across multiple matches than single-game variance would suggest. Confidence Asymmetry Rationale: High confidence in YES analysis (62) due to clear, quantifiable win-rate and draft data; low confidence in NO (35) reflects complete absence of Dplus KIA performance metrics, preventing dual-perspective validation essential for esports prediction.", "key_factor": "BNK FearX Youth's 37.5% win rate and predictable jungle-first draft (1.6 avg pick order) represent structural weaknesses exploitable by a Dplus KIA team with unknown but likely competitive roster composition in a BO3 format."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "BNK FearX Youth's 37.5% win rate (6-10) reflects a struggling team, not a coin-flip contender\u2014baseline should anchor near 30-35% before considering matchup-specific factors. Team's draft predictability (jungle prioritized at 1.6 pick order) is conspicuously absent from competitive analysis; Dplus likely has scouted this pattern and can first-pick deny or counter-pick jungle threats in BO3 format where adaptation compounds across 3 games. KR Kangin (top) shows structural weakness: 2.6 KDA, 49.4% KP, 0% win rates on Sion, Volibear, Zaahen, Yorick, Ambessa, Varus, Yasuo\u20149 different champions with either 0% WR or sub-3.0 KDA. If Dplus targets top-side with gank pressure early, BNK loses a critical macro anchor. Briefing provides zero stats on Dplus KIA Challengers' roster, playstyle, or recent form\u2014absence of data is NOT equivalence. If Dplus is a stronger academy roster (e.g., affiliated with DK or KIA main team), they likely have superior coaching and counter-prep for predictable opponents. KR Slayer's bot dominance (3.3 KDA, 100% WR Ezreal, 50% WR Jhin) depends on reaching item spikes; if Dplus applies early jungle-bot coordination (Zephyr's strength becomes a liability if he must defend bot repeatedly), KR Slayer never gets online. BNK's 2-0 wins over HLE Challengers and 2-1 over DK Challengers occurred in Weeks 1-2 (Jan-Apr 2025); current 2026 Kickoff data is 16 games into the season with no recent momentum signal\u2014form trajectory is hidden, allowing for steeper decline than aggregate 37.5% suggests. KR FIESTA's mid lane success (Sylas 100% WR, Akali 100% WR) is built on 1 game each\u2014sample sizes of 1-4 games per champion are noise, not signal. If Dplus denies Sylas/Akali, FIESTA faces Ryze/Azir/TF where he has 33-0% win rates. BO3 format amplifies coaching adjustments: if BNK loses Game 1 due to jungle gank pattern exploitation, they must deviate from core identity in Games 2-3, playing unfamiliar macro. Dplus benefits from predictability being exposed across 3 matches. Market moved sharply on Apr 10 (YES -28pp, NO +28pp) then partially reversed Apr 11 (+6pp YES); this suggests a catalyst event (likely an official announcement or roster/health update about one team) that briefing does not disclose\u2014hidden information favors DK if the Apr 10 move was DK-negative news that has since stabilized. Confidence in NO side is low (35) because Dplus roster composition is entirely absent; if they possess a clear mechanical or coaching edge, NO probability should be 65-70%, but lacking that intel, I cannot confidently assert DK dominance\u2014hence the probability leans toward BNK upset potential while anchored to their 37.5% baseline and structural weaknesses.", "key_factor": "Dplus KIA Challengers exploits BNK FearX Youth's telegraphed jungle-first draft priority (1.6 avg pick order) with a counter-composition that neutralizes KR Zephyr's 65.4% KP and forces bot lane KR Slayer into unfavorable early matchups before his Ezreal/Jhin win conditions scale."}], "final_score": 0.33644314868804664, "no_score": 0.647728813559322, "edge": -0.038556851311953355, "no_edge": 0.022728813559321992, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 42% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1935119", "question": "LoL: BNK FearX Youth vs Dplus KIA Challengers (BO3) - LCK Challengers League Rounds 1-2", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between BNK FearX Youth and Dplus KIA Challengers in the LCK Challengers League Rounds 1-2, initially scheduled for April 14 at 6:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"BNK FearX Youth\" if BNK FearX Youth win the match against Dplus KIA Challengers.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Dplus KIA Challengers\" if Dplus KIA Challengers win the match against BNK FearX Youth.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T16:00:00Z", "