{"run_id": "cee2134a-f241-48d8-8adc-fb3ed0062178", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T23:23:17.701511+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1796795", "question": "LoL: Invictus Gaming vs Top Esports (BO3) - Esports World Cup China Qualifier Phase 2", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL Lower bracket round 1 match between Invictus Gaming and Top Esports in the Esports World Cup China Qualifier Phase 2, initially scheduled for April 13 at 4:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Invictus Gaming\" if Invictus Gaming win the match against Top Esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Top Esports\" if Top Esports win the match against Invictus Gaming.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T17:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-14T11:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.445, "volume_usd": 108837.68008000002, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["94625042272564344801804488585225860650616778447812730853981941011385568297088", "10796956428283163965849019862698814920332676682593018452759200668782986252749"]}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.44, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.27, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: Match must be completed with a winner declared (not canceled, not forfeit, not delayed >7 days). Criteria are clear and unambiguous. MATCH TIMING: Scheduled April 13, 4:00 AM ET; briefing timestamp April 13 23:22 UTC (~19 hours after scheduled start). Match should have occurred or be imminent. No cancellation reported in briefing. CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains NO actionable competitive intelligence\u2014no current rosters, no recent match results, no head-to-head records, no meta analysis, no seeding/standings information for the qualifier. MARKET PRICE INSIGHT: Current market (YES 44%, NO 56%) reflects market consensus, but with $108k volume and high volatility (\u00b17pp in 24h), pricing appears driven by betting activity rather than information asymmetry resolution. 24-HOUR PRICE MOVEMENT: YES rose +7pp in last 24h while NO fell -6pp, suggesting late activity favoring Invictus Gaming, but without underlying data to justify directional conviction. ORGANIZATIONAL CONTEXT: Both teams are established Chinese LoL organizations. Invictus Gaming has wealthy backing (Wang SiCong); Top Esports has competitive pedigree. Neither factor dominates prediction without roster/form data. RESOLUTION MECHANISM RISK (SECONDARY): gol.gg is reliable source; 2-hour fallback to credible reporting + video evidence is robust. Mechanism risk is LOW (\u22645% impact on final resolution). CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY RATIONALE: Cannot justify high confidence in either direction given complete absence of competitive data. Market pricing (44/56) is reasonable in information void but represents consensus weight, not fundamental analysis. PROBABILITY ESTIMATE: Default to market consensus (44% YES) adjusted slightly for recency (24h uptick in YES buying suggests marginal momentum), but confidence scores remain depressed due to data vacuum on both sides.", "key_factor": "Insufficient competitive data: no current rosters, recent form, head-to-head records, or meta information available to assess either team's likelihood of winning."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.55, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE ANALYSIS (NO = Top Esports at 55%): Top Esports is described as a 'major Chinese LoL organization with competitive pedigree,' positioning it as the more established franchise in LPL ecosystem. The briefing provides organizational legitimacy but lacks recent form data to quantify this advantage. UNDERDOG POSITIONING (YES = Invictus Gaming at 44%): While Invictus Gaming has significant financial backing from Wang SiCong and established organizational infrastructure (founded 2011), the briefing explicitly notes inability to assess current team strength without roster or recent performance data. Wealth alone does not guarantee competitive success in esports. CRITICAL DATA GAPS: The briefing explicitly states 'No recent head-to-head record, current rosters, or recent form data available' and 'Search results did not contain specific information about either team's current competitive standing or recent performance.' This is catastrophic for confident probability estimation in a competitive match. MARKET PRICING SIGNALS: NO side has risen +1.0pp over 7 days (RISING trend) and currently prices at 55%, suggesting marginal professional confidence in Top Esports. YES side fell -1.0pp over 7 days but surged +7.0pp in last 24 hours, indicating recent volatility and possible late money movement. The spread remains narrow (11pp), reflecting genuine uncertainty. TIME-TO-REVERSAL RISK (IMMINENT EVENT): Match resolves in ~18 hours. Given LIVE/IMMINENT timing, any probability above 50 requires strong conviction data. Current pricing is essentially a coin flip with minor Top Esports lean \u2014 this is appropriate given data vacuum. ORGANIZATIONAL FACTORS DO NOT RESOLVE MATCH: Invictus Gaming's billionaire backing (Wang SiCong) is organizational advantage, not match-specific advantage. Top Esports' 'competitive pedigree' is similarly vague without current roster strength, meta fit, or recent Win/Loss record. Neither statement reliably predicts BO3 outcome. CASE AGAINST STRONGER NO CONVICTION: If Top Esports were clearly superior, briefing would contain recent tournament results, head-to-head records, or roster power rankings. Absence of such data suggests market may be relying on brand name rather than performance analysis. CASE AGAINST STRONGER YES CONVICTION: Invictus Gaming's financial resources do not appear to have translated into documented recent success metrics in provided briefing. Without evidence of current form, roster upgrades, or meta advantage, underdog positioning at 44% appears justified. VOLATILITY PATTERN: 24-hour swings (+7pp YES, -6pp NO) in a match occurring TODAY suggest information asymmetry and late-breaking developments not captured in briefing document. This reinforces that confidence levels should remain conservative. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: At 55% NO, market is pricing a slight favorite with genuine uncertainty. This is appropriate. Setting probability_score at 55 (NO wins, thus YES = 45 probability) reflects: (1) marginal Top Esports organizational edge, (2) lack of contradictory evidence, (3) inability to justify higher conviction given data vacuum, (4) imminent resolution timeline preventing major reversals.", "key_factor": "Market equilibrium at 55/44 split reflects genuine uncertainty, with NO side's slight edge driven by Top Esports' established LPL pedigree, but insufficient competitive data prevents high conviction in either direction."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.44, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing explicitly states 'Search results provided limited direct information' and 'No specific match details, recent form data, head-to-head records, or qualifier standings were available.' This is a severe constraint on confidence for BOTH sides. YES SIDE (Invictus Gaming) STRENGTHS: Backed by Wang SiCong (Forbes-ranked wealthy individual), organizational stability since 2011, access to resources. These are structural advantages but do not directly predict match outcome without roster/form data. YES SIDE WEAKNESSES: Zero evidence of current roster quality, recent tournament placings, or head-to-head advantage vs Top Esports. Cannot build a compelling upset case without knowing Invictus Gaming's actual competitive standing. NO SIDE (Top Esports) STRENGTHS: Described as 'major Chinese LoL organization with competitive pedigree.' Market has priced this side at 55% (modest favorite), suggesting some confidence. However, briefing provides NO specific evidence of recent wins, roster strength, or qualifier performance. NO SIDE WEAKNESSES: Equally data-starved as YES side. 'Competitive pedigree' is vague and historical; current form is unknown. Market may be overweighting brand name without recent performance justification. MARKET SIGNAL INTERPRETATION: YES fell 1.0pp over 7 days (trending down) but rose +7.0pp in last 24 hours. This suggests late money moving toward Invictus Gaming. NO is the statistical favorite at 55%, but the tight spread (44% vs 55%) indicates genuine uncertainty in the market itself. UPSET OPPORTUNITY ANALYSIS: For YES to be genuinely underpriced, Invictus Gaming would need hidden advantages (meta fit, recent scrim wins, roster synergy, patch advantage) not captured in search results. Briefing provides zero evidence of these. Conversely, Top Esports' 55% pricing may reflect bookmaker caution rather than strong conviction. TIME-TO-REVERSAL: Event is TODAY (resolves ~18 hours). Market is LIVE/IMMINENT. Any sharp reversal toward YES would require unexpected team performance, roster surprises, or match cancellation \u2014 all low-probability outcomes with minimal time remaining. CONFIDENCE CALIBRATION: Both confidence_yes and confidence_no are set LOW (28 and 26 respectively) because the briefing lacks the granular data needed to strongly differentiate the teams. This is not a coin flip (50) \u2014 the market shows a 55/44 split \u2014 but conviction is limited by data drought. Probability_score of 44 matches current YES market price, reflecting that without contradictory evidence, market consensus is a reasonable baseline when information is scarce. UNDERDOG CASE SUMMARY: Invictus Gaming cannot be credibly positioned as an upset pick when their current roster, recent form, and head-to-head matchup dynamics are entirely unknown. The institutional backing is real but insufficient to overcome the absence of performance data. If this is an upset, it would be a surprise upset without precursors visible in available information.", "key_factor": "Invictus Gaming's institutional backing and established legacy may provide resilience in high-stakes qualifier matches, but the briefing contains zero performance data to support either team."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.44, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.27, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing provides NO current roster information, recent form data, head-to-head records, or recent performance metrics for either team in 2026 CRITICAL DATA GAP: No information on meta patch, recent tournament results, or qualifying round standings that would differentiate the teams Search results contain only organizational background (Invictus Gaming founded 2011 by Wang SiCong) and unrelated roster snippets from other regions/tournaments \u2014 insufficient to assess competitive strength Market price at 44% YES / 55% NO suggests professional traders have some edge information (form, roster changes, recent scrims) not reflected in this briefing BO3 format in high-stakes qualifier typically features evenly-matched teams; extreme asymmetry would be unusual Invictus Gaming has stronger financial backing (Wang SiCong backing) but this does not necessarily translate to current squad strength in April 2026 Top Esports is stated as 'major Chinese LoL organization with competitive pedigree' but no quantitative evidence of recent competitive standing provided 24-hour market movement: YES up +7pp, NO down -6pp suggests recent bullish sentiment toward Invictus Gaming, but this may reflect pre-match analysis unavailable in briefing EVENT TIMING: Match resolves in ~18 hours (TODAY). Reversal from current market consensus requires dramatic shift \u2014 unlikely absent major news (roster change, injury, forfeiture threat) BASE RATE: In regional Chinese LoL qualifiers with no clear dominance signal, expect ~48-52% outcome probabilities; current market split (44/55) reflects modest lean toward NO side CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Both confidence scores deliberately lowered (28/27) due to severe data gap \u2014 briefing insufficient to justify high confidence in either direction RECOMMENDATION: Defer to market price as proxy for professional information. Probability_score mirrors YES market price (44%) due to data insufficiency", "key_factor": "Chinese LoL lower bracket matches historically show near 50-50 split between evenly-matched regional competitors; slight edge to established orgs with deeper resources"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.44, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "\u2022 CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains NO match-specific intelligence \u2014 no recent form, head-to-head records, current rosters, or competitive standing for either team. \u2022 GENERIC BACKGROUND ONLY: Information provided is organizational history (Invictus Gaming founded 2011, Wang SiCong backing) and scattered player data from unrelated tournaments/regions \u2014 none applicable to this specific BO3. \u2022 PRICE REFLECTS UNCERTAINTY, NOT SIGNAL: Current market (44% YES / 55% NO) is nearly symmetric around a slight underdog positioning for Invictus Gaming, consistent with lack of discriminating information. \u2022 24-HOUR VOLATILITY SPIKE: YES side jumped +7pp in last 24 hours (from ~37% to 44%), suggesting intraday sentiment swing, but without underlying news or match analysis in briefing \u2014 indicates emotional repositioning rather than information arrival. \u2022 NO CROWD EXUBERANCE DETECTED: The 55% price on Top Esports is modest (not 70%+), suggesting market is NOT irrationally exuberant despite Top Esports being named first and more established-sounding. \u2022 RATIONAL APATHY DIAGNOSIS: Market has correctly priced uncertainty; the issue is that briefing contains zero competitive intelligence to calibrate either side \u2014 confidence must be LOW on both. \u2022 COIN FLIP WITH SLIGHT TOP LEAN: In absence of data, market default to Top Esports slight favorite (55%) is reasonable (larger org name recognition, potential regional pedigree), but this is speculation, not analysis. \u2022 PROBABILITY SCORE = MARKET PRICE: Setting P(YES) = 44 mirrors current market price because briefing provides no grounds to contradict it \u2014 this is appropriate when information is symmetric. \u2022 DUAL CONFIDENCE BOTH LOW: confidence_yes = 25 and confidence_no = 25 reflects that neither side can be defended with the briefing data available; only organization names and historical background exist.", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.44, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: No current 2026 Spring Split rosters provided for either team\u2014esports outcomes are driven by individual player mechanics, team synergy, and meta adaptation, none of which can be assessed without roster composition. INSUFFICIENT RECENT FORM: Briefing contains no LPL 2026 standings, win-loss records, or recent match results for either team in the current split\u2014essential for assessing momentum and competitive positioning. MISSING HEAD-TO-HEAD: No historical BO3 records between Invictus Gaming and Top Esports in 2025-2026 provided; meta-dependent matchups shift