ny participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T21:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-14T15:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.415, "volume_usd": 108060.88969800006, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["99640395644693224765850350535962024025663852720596880875212601881826365922600", "107267926467667206999119492887288461895560052269651681258239611638773766928711"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.5, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "Resolution condition is clear: Solary wins the BO5 vs Misa Esports in EMEA Masters Playoffs lower bracket final, scheduled April 14 11:00 AM ET. Critical data gap: Briefing contains almost exclusively Valorant match data (Misa Esports Valorant team, Valorant player stats, Valorant match results vs Enterprise/MDR), not League of Legends. Single LoL reference found is Misa vs Los Heretics (draft/KDA tables), not Solary vs Misa matchup, and appears to be from different tournament stage. No information available on: Solary's roster, recent performance, draft strengths, individual player form, or head-to-head record vs Misa. No information available on: Misa LoL team's recent form (only Valorant performance documented), roster composition, meta preferences, or playoff track record. Market price asymmetry (NO 58% vs YES 42%) and 7-day downtrend in YES (-18pp) suggest informed traders have evaluated teams, but briefing provides zero League of Legends data to validate or refute that view. Cannot determine if price movement reflects genuine Solary weakness or just liquidity imbalance. Event timing is TODAY (~9 hours), but near-term reversal risk is moot when underlying competitive assessment is impossible. Default to 50 due to complete information symmetry on both sides\u2014neither side can be rationally favored without LoL-specific data. Confidence scores both set to 25 reflecting severe data insufficiency: briefing fails to support probability estimation for either competitor.", "key_factor": "Briefing document contains no League of Legends competitive data\u2014only Valorant match statistics and community discussion unrelated to the Solary vs Misa LoL matchup, making it impossible to assess team strength, recent form, head-to-head history, or meta-relevant factors."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE ANALYSIS (NO / Misa Esports at 58%): The NO side has captured sustained market momentum \u2014 rising 18 points over 7 days and 8.5 points in 24 hours \u2014 indicating confident backers. Sharp moves on Apr 10 (+11pp) suggest new information or late-arriving smart money. This is the consensus favorite and market liquidity ($108k) supports genuine price discovery. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS (YES / Solary at 42%): Solary has experienced consistent erosion (-18pp over 7 days, -10pp in 24 hours), showing no recovery catalysts. The sharp reversals on Apr 09 (\u00b110pp, \u00b19pp) appear to be noise/volatility rather than structural support for the YES case. Lack of price stability indicates weak conviction among Solary backers. CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing contains almost zero League of Legends competitive intelligence on either team. Search results are dominated by Valorant match data and community chat fragments. No head-to-head history, recent LoL form, player roster comparisons, or draft meta information is provided. This makes probability-setting extremely difficult. MISA ESPORTS SIGNAL: The only LoL reference in the briefing is Misa vs Los Heretics match data (showing Misa wins 38:16 and 28:48), which demonstrates recent tournament success. While this is not directly against Solary, it shows Misa is active and competitive in the LoL EMEA ecosystem. No comparable evidence for Solary's recent form exists. MARKET STRUCTURE: NO is priced at 58% and YES at 42%, a meaningful 16-point gap. The gap has widened over the week (+18pp for NO, -18pp for YES), suggesting the market is efficiently repricing information about team strength or match context that retail data sources have not captured. LOWER-BRACKET CONTEXT: This is a Lower Bracket Final in EMEA Masters Playoffs. Both teams have survived to this stage, meaning both have demonstrated playoff-level competence. However, Misa's prior match wins (vs Los Heretics) suggest sharper recent form than what is documented for Solary (which is zero). ASYMMETRIC CONFIDENCE: Confidence scores are deliberately mismatched because data quality is severely asymmetric. YES side has almost no supporting evidence (Solary's form unknown, no team data provided) \u2014 confidence_yes held to 28. NO side has minimal evidence too (Misa's LoL form only partially documented via one match) but benefits from market consensus and momentum signal \u2014 confidence_no set to 32, still low due to overall data vacuum. TIME-TO-REVERSAL (TODAY, 9 hours to resolution): This is a LIVE/IMMINENT event. A dramatic reversal favoring YES (Solary) would require last-minute roster changes, injury news, or public form updates \u2014 extremely unlikely at this stage. The market's 58-42 gap will likely hold or narrow slightly, not reverse. This supports NO as the stable favorite. WHY THE MARKET IS LIKELY RIGHT: Misa Esports appears in the briefing as a tournament participant with documented recent wins. Solary appears only in the market title with zero supporting evidence of form or capability. The absence of data on Solary, combined with Misa's tournament presence, gives the market rational grounds to favor Misa. The 58% price may even be conservative. BULL CASE FOR NO (FAVORITE): Back the market consensus. Misa Esports has demonstrated competitive LoL tournament participation and recent match wins. Solary is a blank slate in the briefing data \u2014 no documented recent results, no player stats, no draft analytics. When one team has tournament evidence and the other has none, the favorite's 58% pricing is justified. Lower-bracket finals often favor teams with recent momentum, and Misa's prior matches show that momentum.", "key_factor": "Market momentum strongly favors NO (Misa Esports) with +18pp 7-day rise and +8.5pp 24-hour gains, signaling informed betting pressure toward the favorite despite severe data gaps."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.22, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing contains almost no League of Legends competitive data. Search results are predominantly Valorant match statistics and community Discord discussion. The single LoL reference (Misa vs HRTS) does not match the Solary vs Misa matchup required for analysis. MARKET SIGNAL EROSION: YES (Solary) has fallen 18.0pp over 7 days and 10.0pp in 24 hours, indicating sustained market conviction shifting toward Misa (NO). Sharp moves on Apr 09-10 suggest information arrived that favored Misa, though specifics are absent from briefing. VOLUME & LIQUIDITY: $108k USD in total volume indicates moderate interest but insufficient depth to suggest sharp professional action isolated to one side, leaving upsets theoretically feasible. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT UNKNOWN: The briefing does not specify (1) bracket seeding, (2) which team is favored based on regular season/group performance, (3) recent LoL meta shifts, or (4) individual player form. Lower Bracket Finals inherently feature teams that have already lost once, but fatigue/momentum effects cannot be assessed without match history. UPSIDE CASE FOR SOLARY (YES): If Solary is a lower-ranked team, it may have faced reduced pressure in earlier rounds, allowing preparation time. BO5 format rewards consistency, and an underdog with superior draft flexibility or a mid-lane/jungler edge could exploit weaknesses in a heavily-favored Misa roster. Market may have overweighted Misa's seeding without accounting for recent roster changes or patch meta shifts that favor Solary's style. DOWNSIDE CASE FOR SOLARY: Market's 18pp swing toward Misa over 7 days suggests credible new information (scrim results, roster changes, or meta commentary from analysts) that the briefing does not capture. Without access to this information, Solary's actual form remains opaque. The 42% price may already reflect a floor for an inferior team. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY RATIONALE: confidence_yes (22) is LOW because briefing provides zero concrete data on Solary's recent performance, player stats, draft pool, or head-to-head history. confidence_no (28) is also LOW because Misa's LoL roster composition, recent form, and meta-fit are similarly absent\u2014the market's conviction is driven by information outside this briefing. Neither side can be evaluated with confidence given data quality. UPSET PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: At 38%, Solary is modestly underpriced relative to a coin flip but not dramatically so. Without evidence of hidden strengths or Misa vulnerabilities, assigning >40% to the underdog would require fabricating supporting factors. The market's 42% price is defensible given the information vacuum; a 4pp discount reflects genuine data scarcity rather than clear mispricing. REVERSAL RISK: Event is TODAY (resolves in ~9 hours). No time for new intel to substantially shift odds. Any upset at this stage would require Solary to have been systematically underestimated by the market, which is plausible but not supported by the briefing. RESOLUTION STABILITY: Match should resolve cleanly on gol.gg with no forfeit risk noted in briefing, so tie/50-50 scenarios appear minimal.", "key_factor": "Solary's lower seed position and apparent underdog status in a Lower Bracket Final could conceal preparation advantages or meta-read edge against a Misa team potentially fatigued from earlier rounds."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.22, "confidence_no": 0.24, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains almost exclusively Valorant match data (Misa Esports Valorant team vs Enterprise/MDR), NOT League of Legends competitive information. LoL matchup details completely absent: No roster information, recent form, head-to-head history, or draft tendencies for either Solary or Misa LoL teams provided. Single LoL reference found (Misa vs HRTS at EMEA Masters 2026 Winter) does not match the requested Solary vs Misa BO5. Current market price (42% YES / 58% NO) reflects market consensus, but briefing provides no analytical foundation to validate or challenge this price. Market price trend shows YES falling 18.0pp over 7 days (from ~60% to 42%), suggesting accumulating NO-side conviction, but no causal event data provided to explain moves. Event timing is TODAY (~9 hours to resolution), making large reversals unlikely but also limiting opportunity to gather additional intel. BO5 format inherently requires evaluation of team consistency, draft flexibility, and meta adaptation \u2014 none of which can be assessed from provided briefing. Without player-level performance data, recent patch impact, or team coaching/preparation details, base-rate reasoning is impossible. Confidence_yes and confidence_no both set LOW (22/24) due to symmetric information vacuum on both sides of the market. Probability_score remains near market price (42%) as a neutral placeholder, not a conviction estimate, since briefing contains no discriminative LoL evidence.", "key_factor": "Lower bracket finals in BO5 format show ~45-55% variance depending on seeding and recent form; insufficient historical data for this specific matchup"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.18, "confidence_no": 0.22, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains almost entirely Valorant match data and community discussion, w