{"run_id": "f7d6b715-7743-4ec3-b8d8-6e87586028fe", "timestamp": "2026-04-14T11:41:58.390524+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1978409", "question": "Counter-Strike: Misa Esports vs Aurora Young Blood (BO1) - ESEA Advanced Europe Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike match between Misa Esports and Aurora Young Blood in the ESEA Advanced Europe Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 14 at 11:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Misa Esports\" if Misa Esports win the match against Aurora Young Blood.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Aurora Young Blood\" if Aurora Young Blood win the match against Misa Esports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T21:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-14T15:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.415, "volume_usd": 1.265819, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["29509081582541011289666474423176067185590538718849465856965253025125868989794", "103715795702268750290425319374051232432629873897751189827780617175908317961157"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.65, "rationale": "Resolution condition is clear: YES resolves if Misa Esports wins the BO1 match; NO if Aurora Young Blood wins. No ambiguity in criteria text. Market currently prices Misa at 42% (YES), Aurora at 58% (NO), indicating slight favorite to Aurora. Prices have been stable over 7 days. Data provided is from ESEA S56 Europe Finals (Mar 27-29), showing Aurora Young Blood ranked #178 vs Misa #232, giving Aurora a 54-point ranking advantage. Aurora Young Blood shows stronger map pool: Dust2 75%, Overpass 75%, Ancient 86% (4-map streak). Misa has weak Anubis (0%) and Mirage (44%) rates. BO1 format significantly increases variance\u2014upsets are more common than in BO3/BO5 series, reducing the predictive value of ranking differential. Misa shows recent improvement trajectory (+110 points, +57 ranking positions) in finals data, but this momentum must be evaluated ~2 weeks later on April 14. Critical data gap: No April form data provided. Teams may have undergone roster changes, had different scrim results, or shifted meta understanding between late March and mid-April. Aurora Young Blood's 5-6th finals placement vs Misa's 1-2nd suggests Misa may have been stronger in the finals bracket, but regular season on April 14 is a different context. Market price of 42% YES appears roughly calibrated to the available ranking/form data, with slight undervaluation of Misa's improvement trajectory and BO1 variance. Confidence in YES is moderate (42): Misa's improvement arc supports it, but stale data (2 weeks old) and Aurora's ranking advantage create meaningful uncertainty. Confidence in NO is higher (65): Aurora's ranking, map pool strength, and bookmaker consensus are supported by March data, but BO1 variance and missing April form data prevent higher confidence.", "key_factor": "Briefing data is from March 2026 finals results; no current April 14 regular season form data provided, creating significant uncertainty about team trajectory and roster status between March 29 and April 14."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "NO SIDE (FAVORED) STRENGTHS: Aurora Young Blood holds a decisive ranking advantage (#178 vs #232 for Misa), reflecting more sustained competitive performance across the broader ESEA landscape. This gap is substantial and not noise. Aurora Young Blood demonstrates dominance on critical map pools: Dust2 (75% win rate), Overpass (75%), and Ancient (86% over 4-map streak). In BO1 formats, map-specific expertise is decisive since only one map is played. Recent HLTV metrics and statistics favor Aurora Young Blood with 'better recent form according to HLTV metrics and more consistent performance data' per the briefing. This suggests the underdog has been more reliable lately. Market consensus at 58% NO reflects professional oddsmakers' aggregated assessment of the matchup. The 16-percentage-point spread is meaningful and suggests clear data supporting Aurora's position. YES SIDE (UNDERDOG) WEAKNESSES: While Misa showed +110 points and +57 ranking gains during the S56 Finals period (late March), this improvement trajectory has NOT yet translated to surpassing Aurora's absolute ranking. The improvement is relative, not yet superior in absolute terms. Misa's historical map performance is weaker: Anubis (0% win rate) and Mirage (44%) create liabilities. If the randomly-selected BO1 map hits one of these weak spots, Misa's chances collapse significantly. The briefing notes 'limited direct head-to-head match history available,' which prevents contrarians from claiming Misa has beaten Aurora recently. Without direct evidence, relying on abstract 'momentum' is speculative. BO1 format increases variance, but it does NOT eliminate fundamentals. Superior map pools and ranking positions still predict outcomes with better-than-coin-flip accuracy. Aurora's map dominance (75%+ on multiple key maps) is concrete, not speculative. Aurora Young Blood's 5-6th finals finish vs Misa's 1-2nd positioning appears to be snapshot from a specific tournament bracket, not a reliable long-term signal. Current HLTV rankings (#178 vs #232) are more predictive than tournament bracket seeding. VERDICT FOR FAVORITE: Aurora Young Blood's ranking advantage, superior map pool statistics, and consistent recent form justify the 58% market pricing. Misa's recent improvement (+110 points) is noted but has not yet closed the fundamental gap. In a single-map format with 9 hours until play, sudden reversals are unlikely without major roster news, which is absent from the briefing.", "key_factor": "Aurora Young Blood's superior current ranking (#178 vs #232), stronger map pool performance (Dust2 75%, Overpass 75%, Ancient 86%), and consistent competitive positioning support the market favorite."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "UNDERDOG STRENGTH \u2014 Misa's Improvement Arc: The briefing shows Misa gained +110 points and +57 ranking positions during ESEA S56 Europe Finals period (Mar 27-29), demonstrating clear upward momentum. This is the most concrete positive signal for Misa and suggests the team is peaking into this regular season match. UNDERDOG STRENGTH \u2014 BO1 Variance Factor: Best-of-one matches are inherently high-variance. A single map eliminates consistency advantages and increases upset probability. The briefing explicitly flags BO1 'increasing variance and reducing predictability,' which benefits the underdog Misa. UNDERDOG STRENGTH \u2014 Aurora's Specific Map Weaknesses: Aurora Young Blood shows critical vulnerability on Anubis (0% win rate) and Mirage (44% win rate). If Misa selects or forces either of these maps, the matchup probability shifts materially in Misa's favor. This concrete weakness is underutilized in the market pricing. FAVORITE VULNERABILITY \u2014 Aurora's Ranking Inflated by Outdated Data: Aurora's #178 ranking appears to be based on pre-finals data, while Misa's +110 point surge reflects post-finals form. The briefing shows Aurora finished 5-6th in finals while Misa had 1-2nd positioning, yet ranking still favors Aurora. Rankings may not reflect current momentum. FAVORITE STRENGTH \u2014 Aurora's Overall Map Dominance: Aurora demonstrates strong win rates on Dust2 (75%), Overpass (75%), and Ancient (86% with 4-map win streak). These are meta-relevant maps in competitive play. This is robust evidence of Aurora's solidity on the most-played maps. FAVORITE STRENGTH \u2014 Aurora's Better HLTV Metrics: The briefing explicitly states 'Aurora Young Blood shows better map win percentages in recent matches' and 'better recent form according to HLTV metrics and more consistent performance data.' This is direct, current evidence favoring Aurora. CRITICAL DATA GAP \u2014 No Direct H2H or Recent Match Records: The briefing acknowledges 'Limited direct head-to-head match history available.' Without recent direct matchups, we cannot calibrate how these two teams specifically play each other. This gap reduces confidence in predicting the exact outcome. CRITICAL DATA GAP \u2014 Roster/Form Context Unclear: The briefing notes 'Aurora Young Blood finished 5-6th in finals bracket while Misa was in 1-2nd positioning suggests recent roster/form changes.' This is vague. Are these changes positive or negative for each team? Current roster status is unknown, creating material uncertainty. MARKET SIGNAL \u2014 Stable Pricing Over 7 Days: YES (Misa) has held steady at 42% with only -1.0pp change over 7 days and -1.0pp in 24 hours. This stability suggests the market has digested available information and priced in Aurora's fundamentals. A reversal would require new information or sudden form shift. TIMING CONSIDERATION \u2014 Match is TODAY (~9 hours): This is LIVE/IMMINENT. There is minimal time for new information to emerge that could justify a significant repricing toward Misa. The 42% price likely reflects equilibrium given available data. VERDICT ON UPSET CASE: Misa is legitimately underpriced on BO1 variance alone, and the +110 point improvement is a real positive signal. However, Aurora's superior current HLTV metrics, better map performance on meta maps, and stronger ranking position represent substantive fundamental advantages. The market has priced this appropriately at ~40% for the underdog. Confidence in an upset is moderate at best\u2014Misa has a genuine 35-40% chance, but Aurora is the clearer favorite with 60-65% win probability based on available evidence.", "key_factor": "Misa's documented +110 point improvement trajectory and upward momentum into the finals period, combined with BO1 variance that favors underdogs in single-map formats."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "Aurora Young Blood holds a significant ranking advantage (#178 vs #232 for Misa), which aligns with the market's 58% NO pricing and bookmaker consensus. Aurora Young Blood demonstrates superior map-specific performance: Dust2 (75%), Overpass (75%), Ancient (86%) vs Misa's weak Anubis (0%) and modest Mirage (44%). BO1 format inherently reduces predictability by 15-20pp relative to BO3; single-map outcomes are more variance-prone and less reflective of true team strength than series play. Misa's recent +110 point and +57 ranking improvement is noted, but absolute ranking position (#232) remains substantially below Aurora (#178), limiting the significance of trajectory alone. Market price of 42% YES / 58% NO appears reasonably calibrated to the ranking differential and map-win data; no obvious mispricing detected. Head-to-head history is unavailable in briefing; cannot adjust base rate for specific team matchup dynamics or recent roster changes. Event timing is TODAY (resolves in ~9 hours); limited time for significant form-shifting news or roster disruptions. Confidence in NO (Aurora victory) is moderately high due to ranking advantage and map data; confidence in YES is lower due to uncertainty around Misa's actual current form relative to improvement trajectory claims.", "key_factor": "In BO1 Counter-Strike matches between mid-tier EU teams, the higher-ranked team wins approximately 60-65% of the time; however, BO1 format introduces 15-20pp variance due to map pool and day-form volatility."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "Aurora Young Blood holds structural advantage: ranked #178 vs Misa #232, with superior map pool (Dust2 75%, Overpass 75%, Ancient 86%) vs Misa's weak Anubis (0%) and Mirage (44%) BO1 format high-variance nature limits predictability, but Aurora's map dominance on pool-relevant maps reduces Misa's path to victory Misa's recent +110 points trajectory cited as bullish signal, but this improvement still leaves them ranked 54 positions below Aurora \u2014 insufficient to overcome structural gap Market price (42% YES / 58% NO) reasonably reflects Aurora's bookmaker-consensus favorite status and stronger HLTV metrics No evidence of crowd panic or irrational exuberance \u2014 prices appear calibrated to underlying team strength differential Data freshness concern: briefing dated 2026-04-14 11:41 UTC for same-day event (resolve 21:00 UTC), but no late-breaking lineup/roster changes reported Confidence in NO side elevated (72) due to multiple independent signals (ranking, map stats, bookmaker consensus) all pointing Aurora direction Confidence in YES side moderated (45) because Misa's improvement trajectory is real but magnitude insufficient to flip unfavorable matchup; BO1 variance cannot be quantified from briefing Market not mispriceable on available evidence \u2014 Aurora's 58% reflects appropriate risk premium for stronger competitor in high-variance format", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "Aurora Young Blood holds a 54-ranking-position advantage (#178 vs #232), reflecting sustained competitive tier positioning over Misa's recent trajectory. Map-specific performance data heavily favors Aurora: Dust2 75% (4/5), Overpass 75% (3/4), Ancient 86% (4/3 effective win streak)\u2014these are core competitive maps. Misa's +110 point gain in ESEA S56 Finals appears inflated; ranked opponent quality and finishing position (1-2nd in finals) vs Aurora's 5-6th suggests Misa may have faced weaker competition in point accumulation. Best-of-one format (BO1) introduces 15-25% outcome variance independent of ranking due to single-map elimination; however, this variance affects both teams equally and does not negate rating disparity. Aurora's consistency across multiple maps (4+ maps tracked with win rates >75%) demonstrates deeper map pool mastery than Misa's uneven performance profile (0% on Anubis, 44% on Mirage). Market pricing (58% NO) aligns with underlying competitive data; bookmaker consensus reflects professional oddsmaking that typically prices ESEA Advanced matches accurately. Head-to-head history absent; reliance on rating and map-pool analysis is standard for tier-2 esports but introduces ~10-15% confidence penalty due to team-specific tactical variance. Regular season timing (vs. finals context) may reduce preparation intensity for both teams, but Aurora's higher base rating provides structural advantage even in reduced-preparation scenarios. Misa's improvement trajectory is real but appears marginal relative to Aurora's absolute competitive positioning; recent form does not override ranking differential.", "key_factor": "Best-of-one matches in mid-tier European esports carry exceptionally high variance and map-pool dependency; Aurora's superior map-specific win rates (Dust2 75%, Ancient 86%, Overpass 75%) combined with higher ranking position (#178 vs #232) outweigh Misa's recent point gains, which may reflect lower-quality opponent defeats rather than tier-up performance."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "BRIEFING SILENCE ON ROSTER: No mention of current lineups, recent substitutions, or injury status for either team\u2014critical for same-day BO1 prediction. BO1 VARIANCE AMPLIFIER: Single-map format means tactical surprise (unexpected map pick, anti-strat preparation, or player substitution) can swing 10-15% win probability independent of overall ranking. MISA'S CONTRADICTORY SIGNALS: Finals data shows +110 points (+57 ranking positions) between two snapshots, yet current ranking (#232) remains significantly below Aurora (#178). This suggests either: (a) data staleness, or (b) recent collapse after finals momentum\u2014if latter, may trigger roster adjustment. AURORA'S WEAK MAP POOL EXPOSURE: 0% on Anubis, 44% on Mirage, suggests vulnerability on emerging/permaban maps. Misa's upward trajectory could correlate with specialization on maps Aurora avoids, not reflected in aggregate stats. FINALS VS. REGULAR SEASON CONTEXT: Aurora finished 5-6th in finals (lower seed) while Misa was 1-2nd (higher seed). Regular season match may see different motivation/preparation intensity; Misa may be more motivated to maintain seeding position. MISSING HEAD-TO-HEAD DATA: No direct match history provided; market price (58% NO) may reflect default ranking bias rather than competitive dynamics. LOW VOLUME / THIN MARKET: Only $1 USD volume suggests minimal sophisticated sharp money; price may not reflect true probability efficiently. TACTICAL META-SHIFT RISK: Counter-Strike patches and utility tweaks between Mar 29 finals and Apr 14 match could favor one team's core utility stack or default play structure; briefing contains no patch notes. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong data on Aurora's map win rates (Dust2 75%, Ancient 86%) supports NO confidence. Weak data on Misa's current roster, morale, and tactical preparation constrains YES confidence. TIME-TO-REVERSAL: Event is TODAY (~9 hours). Any major roster news, injury announcement, or map pool leak would drive immediate sharp action. Market stability (-1pp over 24h) suggests no such late-breaking information yet\u2014but absence of news does not guarantee absence of disruption.", "key_factor": "Misa deploys a substitute or roster change (injury, illness, or tactical swap) targeting a map pool that Aurora Young Blood has not recently faced, exploiting a meta-shift or tactical vulnerability not captured in aggregate win-rate stats."}], "final_score": 0.40422145328719716, "no_score": 0.5888984881209504, "edge": -0.010778546712802817, "no_edge": 0.003898488120950394, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 66% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1978409", "question": "Counter-Strike: Misa Esports vs Aurora Young Blood (BO1) - ESEA Advanced Europe Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike match between Misa Esports and Aurora Young Blood in the ESEA Advanced Europe Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 14 at 11:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Misa Esports\" if Misa Esports win the match against Aurora Young Blood.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Aurora Young Blood\" if Aurora Young Blood win the match against Misa Esports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T21:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-14T15:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.415, "volume_usd": 1.265819, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["295090815825410112896664744231760671855905387