D ABSENCE: Briefing explicitly states 'Previous head-to-head records between NAVI Junior and Formulation Gaming not found.' This eliminates direct historical edge assessment\u2014critical in lower-tier regional esports where meta/roster familiarity matters. BO3 FORMAT MITIGATION: Best of 3 reduces upset probability vs. single-map, but in Challengers-level play (lower MMR, less stable teams), variance is high. BO3 favors consistency, which academy teams may lack. MARKET EFFICIENCY TEST: Current 36% YES vs. historical EMA of 44% suggests market corrected downward based on late information. The sharp move at 11:43 UTC is not noise\u2014it's informed trading 17 minutes before/after scheduled start. RESOLUTION RISK: If match is delayed or incomplete, resolves 50-50 per criteria. If it began and one team forfeited, that team auto-wins (no 50-50). VCL Challengers matches occasionally experience technical delays but rarely forfeit at this stage. SPECIALIST ASSESSMENT: Without access to real-time Valorant competitive databases (VLR.gg API, live stream status, roster confirmations), I cannot independently verify outcome. The market's sharp move suggests it already knows. Setting probability at current market price with reduced confidence reflects information gap.", "key_factor": "The sharp 14.5pp drop in YES price at 11:43 UTC (17 minutes before scheduled 11:00 AM ET start) suggests real-time information asymmetry\u2014likely match result leakage, roster changes, or technical issue; market timing indicates event may already be live/resolved."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "SHARP MOVE SIGNAL: YES crashed -14.5pp in a single 11:43 UTC move on Apr 14 (match day), 3h 17m before scheduled 11:00 AM ET start\u2014suggests informed traders detected late-breaking roster/availability information unavailable in briefing. ACADEMY TEAM VOLATILITY: Junior/academy rosters are structurally fragile; parent org (Natus Vincere) may reassign players mid-tournament to senior squad if senior team needs coverage, leaving NAVI Junior undermanned or with substitutes. BRIEFING SILENCE ON ROSTERS: No player names, recent roster changes, injury status, or lineup confirmation provided for either team\u2014unusual omission for a same-day BO3; absence suggests potentially unstable or changing lineups. FORMULATION'S STAGE 1 PARITY: Briefing notes Formulation Gaming competed vs Team Liquid Academy (Tier 1 academy) and other established teams without documented losses\u2014suggests competitive caliber comparable to NAVI Junior, contradicting the organizational prestige gap argument. MOTIVATION ASYMMETRY: Group stage stakes are moderate (top 4 of 8); Formulation Gaming is likely fighting for playoff survival with full commitment; NAVI Junior may have split focus if parent org is rotating roster for senior team experimentation. NO HEAD-TO-HEAD DATA: Briefing explicitly states 'no recent confrontations'\u2014removing predictive anchor and making briefing-derived confidence artificially high; true form matchup unknown. TIMING PROXIMITY: Match resolves in ~9 hours with zero pre-match data updates in briefing\u2014high risk of last-minute changes (illness, technical issues, roster lockdown disputes) favoring underdog NO side by default uncertainty. MARKET LIQUIDITY COLLAPSE: $0 USD volume + 0.0pp/24h volatility post-crash indicates NO liquidity to absorb large bets, suggesting thin-market speculation rather than backed conviction; sharp move may reflect single large bet by informed trader with team-side intelligence.", "key_factor": "NAVI Junior roster instability or key player absence at match time due to parent organization prioritizing senior team commitments or mid-tournament personnel shifts."}], "final_score": 0.37754385964912285, "no_score": 0.6031914893617021, "edge": 0.012543859649122857, "no_edge": -0.03180851063829793, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 40% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1979224", "question": "Valorant: NAVI Junior vs Formulation Gaming (BO3) - VCL NORTH//EAST Group A", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between NAVI Junior and Formulation Gaming in the VCL NORTH//EAST Group A, initially scheduled for April 14 at 11:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"NAVI Junior\" if NAVI Junior win the match against Formulation Gaming.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Formulation Gaming\" if Formulation Gaming win the match against NAVI Junior.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-14T21:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-14T15:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.365, "volume_usd": 0.0, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["36429297867546116508562814938047600449237960078933522900335607688474967122758", "5170783045514401364831454210239263550224490750010454753856349272391078666278"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "key_facts": ["Group Stage: April 4<sup>th</sup> - 14<sup>th</sup>, 2026.", "Two groups of 8 teams; Single Round-Robin format; All matches are Bo3; Top 4 teams from each group advance to Playoffs", "Top Valorant esports teams rankings list and tiers in Europe.", "1638 1623 1609 1594 1580 1565 1551 1536 Matches Played Rating.", "Natus Vincere Junior roster, upcoming matches, results, rank, stats, and achievements.", "Stats, score, streams, and VODs from FRG vs.", "Formulation Gaming - Round 3 match of Challengers 2026: NORTH//EAST Stage 1 Valorant event.", "Stats, score, streams, and VODs from Enterprise Esports vs.", "Formulation Gaming - Round 5 match of Challengers 2026: NORTH//EAST Stage 2 Valorant event.", "Stats, score, streams, and VODs from Team Liquid Academy vs."], "news_summary": "NAVI Junior and Formulation Gaming are set to compete in the VCL NORTH//EAST Stage 2 Group Stage (April 4-14, 2026) in a Best of 3 match. NAVI Junior is a junior/academy team from the established Natus Vincere organization with documented participation in recent Challengers events. Formulation Gaming has also participated in previous Challengers stages, with match records available from Stage 1. Both teams are competing in a 8-team single round-robin group format where the top 4 advance to playoffs.", "side_yes_case": ["NAVI Junior represents an established organization with professional infrastructure and resources