ril 5 (9 days ago), establishing direct dominance. Market pricing at 30% YES reflects this baseline correctly. FORM DIVERGENCE: AKA HERO shows extreme volatility (2-1 win vs RIZON, then 0-2 losses to FOKUS and CGN). This inconsistency in a BO3 format favors the more stable opponent. DEFENSIVE BREAKDOWN: AKA HERO conceded 40+ kills from single opponents (Pa1ze vs FOKUS), exposing tactical vulnerabilities that ALTERNATE aTTaX exploited in their April 5 victory. RECENT MOMENTUM: Market fell -19.5pp over 7 days, with sharp -24.5pp drop on Apr 13 04:00 UTC. This suggests new intelligence (likely April 12 match updates confirming ALTERNATE aTTaX's continued competitive form) caused rational repricing downward for AKA HERO. NO COUNTER-SIGNAL: Briefing provides no evidence of AKA HERO recent coaching changes, roster alterations, or strategic innovation post-April 5 loss that would justify betting against ALTERNATE aTTaX's proven 2-0 dominance. MARKET EFFICIENCY: 30% YES price is NOT crowded or irrational\u2014it reflects documented underdog status with limited upside case. The -19.5pp 7-day decline shows market correctly incorporated new match data. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in NO (72%) due to direct precedent + form data. Confidence in YES only 35% because the case for AKA HERO rests on isolated RIZON win and MVP highlight, not sustained evidence of improvement vs the team that beat them 2-0. TIMING NOTE: Match resolves in ~7 hours (TODAY). Current price reflects pre-match information; no major news catalyst in last 24h to justify reversal. Market stable near 30%.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.68, "rationale": "Direct precedent is highly predictive: ALTERNATE aTTaX defeated AKA HERO 2-0 on April 5 (9 days ago), establishing skill/meta advantage in same tournament ecosystem; in Valorant, team compositions and agent pool strategies are relatively static across 2