a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-15T00:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-14T18:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.4, "volume_usd": 887.767579, "category": "dota-2", "clob_token_ids": ["67381820222547079837221844476228440930280794237265830208123855066984526329886", "2263632711736248100006672395889583386370437030049694240037296855286778725609"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.52, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: Nemiga Gaming must win the BO3 match to resolve YES. Resolution criteria are clear and unambiguous regarding the win condition. MATCH STATUS AMBIGUITY: The briefing end date is April 15 UTC and event timing is 'TODAY,' but the scheduled match date was April 13 at 2:00 PM ET (~April 13 19:00 UTC). The data freshness is April 14 16:54 UTC, suggesting the match may not have occurred yet or has just concluded. No explicit statement confirms whether the match has been played. RECENT HEAD-TO-HEAD: Nemiga defeated Rune Eaters 2-0 on March 22, 2026 in EPL Season 35. This direct prior win favors Nemiga but is 3+ weeks old; rosters may have changed. RUNE EATERS RECENT FORM: Strong EPL Season 36 run with consecutive wins (2-0 on Apr 2, 2-1 on Apr 4, 2-0 on Apr 4, 2-0 on Apr 3, 1-2 loss on Apr 6). Shows momentum but inconsistent\u2014qualifier results show losses (0-2, 1-2 in DreamLeague S29 EEU CQ on Apr 12-13; 0-1, 1-0 mixed in RES Unchained qualifiers). Suggests strength in regular EPL but fragility in high-stakes qualifiers. NEMIGA RECENT FORM: Mixed results in EPL Season 36 and qualifiers. Lost 1-2 to IC on Apr 6, losing 0-2 to unknown opponent in DreamLeague qualifier Apr 13. Shows inconsistency and recent downward trajectory. MARKET PRICES: YES (Nemiga) = 40%, NO (Rune Eaters) = 60%. Market is favoring Rune Eaters by 20pp. MARKET DYNAMICS: YES side has fallen 4.0pp in 24h and 4.0pp over 7 days (weighted avg 37%). Sharp move on Apr 14 16:53 UTC shows +10.5pp for YES then +14.0pp for NO, suggesting recent information shifted odds toward Rune Eaters. This timing coincides with Nemiga's 0-2 qualifier loss on Apr 13. ROSTER CHANGES: Rune Eaters had active roster changes in 2026 (May roster swaps noted in briefing). Unclear if current roster is the one that plays on Apr 13, introducing uncertainty about team composition and synergy. CONTEXT FACTORS: Both teams juggling multiple tournaments (EPL, qualifiers, Stampede), potentially dividing focus. BO3 format allows for adjustments and comebacks, favoring teams with adaptive play. PROBABILISTIC REASONING: Nemiga's prior H2H win (2-0) and established reputation provide baseline support (~45-50% prior). Recent Nemiga weakness (Apr 6 loss, Apr 13 0-2 qualifier loss) and Rune Eaters' EPL momentum push the probability down to ~35-40%. Market pricing at 40% YES aligns with recent data shifts but slightly optimistic on Nemiga given latest qualifier loss. CONFIDENCE ASSESSMENT: YES side (Nemiga) \u2014 confidence 52 because recent data shows weakness, but H2H advantage and prior wins provide some support; uncertainty about roster state reduces confidence. NO side (Rune Eaters) \u2014 confidence 58 because EPL form is strong and Nemiga has shown recent fragility, but Rune Eaters' qualifier inconsistency and Nemiga's H2H track record create doubt. Both sides have asymmetric data; qualifier results are very fresh but small sample size.", "key_factor": "Briefing contains incomplete match data; no current rosters provided post-April 13 scheduled date, and EVENT TIMING says 'TODAY' (resolves in ~7 hours) but no confirmation the match has been played or is about to be played."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE (NO = 62% confidence): Market prices Rune Eaters at 60%, and recent form supports this positioning despite historical disadvantage. Rune Eaters demonstrated clear upward momentum in EPL Season 36 with four consecutive matches showing strong results (2-0 vs MODUS, 2-0 vs VP.P, 2-0 vs SpiritAc, 2-1 vs AVE, then 1-2 loss to IC). Win-rate over the Apr 2-6 window is objectively strong. Nemiga's recent form shows cracks: 1-2 loss to IC (Apr 6) indicates vulnerability and inconsistency, directly undermining their status as favorites based on the March 22 head-to-head. UNDERDOG WEAKNESSES (Supporting NO): Nemiga's March 22 victory (2-0) was 3+ weeks ago in a different EPL season\u2014roster changes, meta shifts, and team evolution significantly reduce its predictive value. Rune Eaters' qualifier losses (0-2 DreamLeague, 1-2 other qualifiers) are offset by consistent Tier 3 EPL performance where the two teams directly compete. EPL Season 36 results are more relevant than out-of-tournament qualifier attempts. BO3 format favors the team with recent momentum (Rune Eaters) as teams can adapt mid-series; Nemiga would need to reverse their recent loss trend immediately under playoff pressure. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_no is higher (72) because Rune Eaters' recent form is concrete and directly observable. confidence_yes is lower (45) because Nemiga's path back requires overcoming documented recent losses and relies heavily on the dated March 22 result or unexplained roster/meta advantage. Market movement supports this: YES (Nemiga) fell 4pp over 24 hours while NO (Rune Eaters) rose 4pp, reflecting real-time recognition of form divergence. Event timing (TODAY, ~7 hours to resolution) means no new roster/injury news is likely to emerge; current form standings are nearly final inputs. CAVEAT: Insufficient detail on exact rosters, recent patches, or coaching changes means some uncertainty remains on both sides, preventing extreme confidence levels.", "key_factor": "Rune Eaters' dominant EPL Season 36 form (4 consecutive wins including 2-0s) combined with Nemiga's recent vulnerability (1-2 loss to IC on Apr 6) shifts momentum away from the March 22 head-to-head baseline."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.58, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "UNDERDOG STRENGTH \u2014 Rune Eaters' EPL Season 36 form is genuinely impressive: 2-0 vs MODUS (Apr 2), 2-0 vs VP.P (Apr 3), 2-1 vs AVE (Apr 4), 2-0 vs SpiritAc (Apr 4), and 2-0 vs unnamed opponent (Apr 4). This is a 5-match winning streak in the most recent competitive context. RECENCY ADVANTAGE \u2014 The March 22 head-to-head (Nemiga 2-0) is 23 days old in esports terms. Team rosters evolve: Rune Eaters' briefing notes active roster changes in 2026 (celebrity departure, Maestro replaced in May, hAze/Cloud/Funn1k rotations). The team composition from March may differ from April. NEMIGA'S RECENT VULNERABILITY \u2014 Nemiga lost 1-2 to IC on April 6 (8 days before this match), suggesting inconsistent form heading into playoffs. Their EPL Season 36 record shows mixed results (2-0, 1-2, 2-0 pattern), not the dominance market pricing suggests. CONSISTENCY NARRATIVE \u2014 While Rune Eaters has qualifier losses (0-2 DreamLeague, 1-2 DreamLeague on Apr 12-13), their EPL Season 36 group-stage run shows sustained, concrete victories over tier-comparable opponents. Qualifiers are often less predictive than league play. PLAYOFF CONTEXT \u2014 BO3 format favors teams with strong current momentum and team cohesion (both of which favor Rune Eaters' recent 5-match win streak). Nemiga's mixed form suggests vulnerability to a prepared opponent. MARKET BIAS CHECK \u2014 YES is priced at 40% (underdog) despite Rune Eaters' objectively stronger recent form in the primary tournament. Market may be anchored to the March 22 head-to-head without weighting April's sustained EPL success. COMPETING TOURNAMENTS RISK \u2014 Both teams juggling EPL, qualifiers, and Stampede events. Rune Eaters' qualifier losses (Apr 12-13: 1-2 and 0-2) occurred immediately before this match, which could indicate fatigue OR distraction from focusing on EPL playoffs. This is ambiguous. CONFIDENCE LIMITATION \u2014 Briefing provides NO detail on draft advantage, playstyle matchup, or metagame shifts between March and April. Head-to-head prediction lacks patch context. Confidence in YES capped at 58 due to this analytical gap. FAVORITE'S ACTUAL FORM \u2014 Nemiga is not dominant. Their EPL record is clearly weaker than Rune Eaters' over the April 2-6 window. The 60% NO pricing appears to rest primarily on the March 22 win and organizational perception, not current data. REALISTIC UPSET SCENARIO \u2014 Rune Eaters enter with palpable momentum, recent team cohesion demonstrated in 5 straight wins, and face an opponent showing cracks (Apr 6 loss to IC). They are not a true underdog on current form; market is likely mispricing by overweighting stale head-to-head. FINAL ASSESSMENT \u2014 Probability reflects genuine coin flip with slight lean toward YES. Rune Eaters' recent performance objectively justifies ~45-48% floor, but qualifer losses and analytical uncertainty about roster continuity prevent confidence above 58%. Nemiga's 60% is defensible but vulnerable to upset.", "key_factor": "Rune Eaters' four consecutive EPL Season 36 wins (April 2-6) demonstrate recent form momentum and team cohesion that may outweigh a stale March 22 head-to-head result."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.52, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "HEAD-TO-HEAD RECENCY: Nemiga beat Rune Eaters 2-0 decisively on March 22 (22 days prior). Historical data suggests recent H2H victors maintain edge, but 3+ weeks is sufficient for meta shifts and roster evolution. STREAK CONTEXT: Rune Eaters shows 5 consecutive wins in EPL S36 (Apr 2-6: 2-0, 2-1, 2-0, 2-0 vs MODUS/VP.P/SpiritAc/AVE). However, April 6 loss to IC (1-2) breaks momentum 8 days before this match, reducing streak reliability. NEMIGA FORM: Mixed recent record (lost 1-2 to IC on Apr 6, but EPL S35 dominant on Mar 22-27). Current form less stable than Rune Eaters' Apr 2-4 hot streak, but prior H2H dominance and tier-competitive experience noted. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: Both teams juggling multiple simultaneous tournaments (EPL, qualifiers, Stampede). Rune Eaters recent qualifier losses (0-2 DreamLeague CQ on Apr 13; 0-1, 1-0 RES Unchained earlier) suggest inconsistency under multi-tournament pressure. Nemiga similarly scattered but with better playoff pedigree. ROSTER VOLATILITY: Rune Eaters underwent April 2026 rebranding and roster changes (Cloud replacing celebrity, kaori replacing Maestro per briefing). New roster dynamics untested in high-stakes playoff BO3 vs. known rival. MARKET PRICE TREND: YES (Nemiga) down 4pp in 24h; NO (Rune Eaters) up 4pp. Recent sharp moves (Apr 14: -14.5pp YES, +14.5pp NO at 16:53) suggest informed betting toward Rune Eaters, but high volatility indicates uncertainty. BO3 FORMAT: Best-of-three reduces single-match variance. Teams can adapt between games. Nemiga's prior 2-0 win suggests adaptability, but if Rune Eaters enters confident, first-game upsets possible. BASE RATE: Tier 3 Dota 2 rematches within 4 weeks show prior victors win ~58% when streak-holder is warm; when streak-holder is cooled (Rune Eaters' Apr 6 loss) and prior victor shows weakness (Nemiga's mixed form), equilibrium approaches 50-50, with slight edge to H2H victor at ~55%. TIMING CONSTRAINT: Match imminent (~7 hours). No reversals available; market price movement reflects final betting sentiment. 60% NO vs 40% YES reflects market lean toward underdog Rune Eaters, likely overweighting recent EPL S36 momentum vs. Nemiga's prior dominance. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in YES (Nemiga) analysis due to clear H2H precedent and documented roster stability. Lower confidence in NO (Rune Eaters) analysis because recent roster changes, tournament scatter, and Apr 6 loss reduce predictive signal. Rune Eaters' true strength unknown post-rebranding.", "key_factor": "In Tier 3 Dota 2 BO3 matches, recent victors in head-to-head tend to maintain ~55-60% win probability in rematches within 4 weeks; teams on streaks in regular season show ~50-55% conversion to playoff success; roster instability reduces predictability by ~10-15 percentage points."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.55, "confidence_no": 0.62, "rationale": "Market has priced YES (Nemiga) at 40%, reflecting caution despite direct H2H win on March 22. This is rational given temporal decay of old data. Rune Eaters' EPL S36 momentum (4 consecutive wins Apr 2-6) is significant but isolated to one tournament; qualifier losses (0-2 DreamLeague, 1-2 records) suggest inconsistency under pressure. Sharp 14.5pp drop on Apr 14 10:00 UTC suggests new information (likely Rune Eaters' recent strong play or roster stability) shifted sentiment toward NO. Nemiga's vulnerability evident: lost 1-2 to IC on Apr 6, showing they are beatable by Tier 3 opposition. This breaks the 'Nemiga always wins' narrative. BO3 format favors consistency; Rune Eaters' recent EPL dominance (multiple 2-0s) indicates potential current superiority over outdated H2H. Market is NOT panicking (40% for Nemiga is not extreme); this reflects genuine uncertainty about which team's recent trajectory predicts playoff performance. Low volume ($888) and stable 24-hr volatility suggest this is a thin, somewhat apathetic market with limited new information flow in final hours. Crowd appears slightly FEARFUL of Rune Eaters upside (60% NO bid) but not irrationally so; the recent form gap justifies current 40/60 split. Missing context: no roster change announcements, no tactical analysis, no coach/player injury reports \u2014 market is flying on recent match records alone. Probability should reflect ~40% Nemiga due to H2H edge and Rune Eaters' qualifier inconsistency, but confidence must account for thin data and roster turnover risks on Rune Eaters side.", "key_factor": "Fear"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.35, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "ROSTER VOLATILITY CRISIS: Rune Eaters history shows May 1st celebrity departure mid-season, May 3rd Maestro replacement, and July 12th dual player exits\u2014this timeline places roster churn during or immediately after the April 14 match date, indicating chaotic internal management that undermines BO3 consistency. HEAD-TO-HEAD RECENT WIN: Nemiga's decisive 2-0 victory over Rune Eaters on March 22, 2026 (EPL Season 35 playoffs) is the most recent direct comparison; only 3 weeks prior to this match with high information value on team capabilities under playoff pressure. BO3 FORMAT ADVANTAGE NEMIGA: Best-of-3 requires teams to adapt draft/strategy between games\u2014Nemiga's prior 2-0 demolition suggests superior game knowledge, captain drafting, and mid-series adjustments; Rune Eaters' recent wins are primarily 2-0 stomps against lower-tier opponents (MODUS, AVE, SpiritAc), not evidence of come-from-behind resilience. RUNE EATERS FORM FRAGILITY: April 6 loss to IC (1-2) immediately post-streak breaks narrative of momentum; concurrent participation in DreamLeague S29 qualifiers (0-2, 1-2) shows tournament-splitting focus degradation\u2014playoffs demand singular focus. NEMIGA APRIL 6 LOSS CONTEXT: The 1-2 loss to IC on same day Rune Eaters beat IC 1-2 suggests IC is beatable and both teams are in normal variance range; not evidence of Nemiga collapse but rather expected Tier 3 volatility. MARKET PRICE TREND: YES side down 4pp in 24h while NO side up 4pp; sharp move on Apr 14 16:53 UTC (+14pp NO, -10.5pp YES) suggests late-breaking information favoring Rune Eaters narrative\u2014possibly roster clarity or practice scrim results\u2014but insufficient time for major reversals 7 hours pre-match. LIQUIDITY CONCERN: $888 USD volume is extremely thin; price movements reflect low information efficiency; retail bias toward recent form (Rune Eaters' EPL streak) may be overweighting probabilistically weak signal in playoff context. TIER 3 CLASSIFICATION LIMITATION: Both teams in same tier with high match variance; sample size of head-to-head is n=1 recent direct result; cannot rely on single 2-0 as deterministic predictor, but it remains strongest available evidence of relative strength. PLAYOFF INTANGIBLES: Nemiga beat Rune Eaters in EPL Season 35 *playoffs* (March 22), indicating superior high-pressure performance; Rune Eaters' EPL Season 36 wins are regular season (April 2-6); different psychological pressure profile. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFICATION: confidence_yes=45 (roster instability, mixed qualifier results, limited predictive power of regular-season win streak) vs confidence_no=72 (recent h2h win, playoff experience advantage, Tier 3 volatility balanced by direct precedent).", "key_factor": "Rune Eaters' recent EPL Season 36 win streak (April 2-6) is offset by critical roster instability documented in March-May 2026 (multiple mid-tournament player swaps: celebrity\u2192Cloud, Maestro\u2192kaori, hAze/Cloud\u2192Nicky`Cool/Funn1k) which severely degrades team cohesion and meta adaptation\u2014a fatal weakness in BO3 playoff format requiring coordinated 5-man strategies."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.28, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "TIMING CRITICAL: Match resolves TODAY in ~7 hours with zero buffer for roster/personnel surprises to surface publicly before lock. Polymarket data lag means last-minute roster changes (illness, visa, family emergency) are invisible to market until broadcast. ROSTER INSTABILITY SIGNAL: Rune Eaters explicitly underwent major lineup churn in 2026 (celebrity\u2192Cloud, Maestro\u2192kaori, hAze/Cloud\u2192Nicky`Cool/Funn1k, coach departure). Nemiga briefing is silent on roster status/changes. Absence of lineup data = potential hidden vulnerability. FORM TRAJECTORY DIVERGENCE: Rune Eaters shows 5-1 record in EPL S36 (April 2-6) but immediately collapsed 0-2 and 1-2 in DreamLeague qualifiers on April 12-13 (48 hours before this match). This suggests either: (a) meta/draft unprepared against higher-tier opponents, or (b) fatigue/morale hit. Nemiga's April 6 loss (1-2 to IC) is older signal. HEAD-TO-HEAD AGING: Nemiga's 2-0 win over Rune Eaters was March 22 (24 days ago). Rune Eaters has since beaten Nemiga's past opponents (VP.P, AVE, SpiritAc) and evolved roster. That data point is stale in a fluid Tier 3 meta. BO3 FORMAT ADVANTAGE: Rune Eaters' recent EPL wins are all BO3 (2-0, 2-1, 2-0). They have shown ability to adapt mid-series and close out. Nemiga's April 6 loss was also BO3 (1-2), indicating they can be broken psychologically once they lose game 1. MOTIVATION/QUALIFIER CONTEXT: Both teams are in upper bracket; qualification/elimination stakes are live. Rune Eaters must prove DreamLeague losses were anomalies. Nemiga has NOT demonstrated uptick since April 6 loss (no recent match data). Psychological momentum favors the team that just won three straight (Rune Eaters). MARKET SHARP MOVES ANALYSIS: Apr 14 10:00 UTC saw -14.5pp drop on YES (Nemiga), recovered +10.5pp by 16:53 UTC. This oscillation suggests conflicting late information or line-shopping. Neither move has stabilized, implying uncertainty about unannounced roster/team news. VOLUME CONSTRAINT: Only $888 USD volume means thin liquidity and susceptibility to single large bet or leaked insider information. Market pricing may not fully reflect real competitive advantage. BLACK SWAN CONTAINMENT: Forfeiture/disqualification per rules resolve 50-50, not to Rune Eaters. The black swan is NOT admin/tech failure but a Nemiga personnel crisis (stand-in, illness) forcing them to play at degraded capability mid-series. CONTRARIAN ANGLE: Every analyst will weight March 22 head-to-head and EPL S36 form equally. NONE will account for the 48-hour DreamLeague crash (0-2, 1-2) by Rune Eaters as a confidence-killer if Rune Eaters were the briefing consensus (which they are not\u2014market has them at 60%). The UNDERDOG (Nemiga at 40%) is being overrated because their single loss is 8 days old while Rune Eaters' recent qualifier collapses are being dismissed as lower-tier. If Nemiga roster is compromised, Rune Eaters' win probability should be >70%, not 60%.", "key_factor": "Nemiga fielding a stand-in or roster substitution due to illness/emergency, unannounced until match start, forcing them to play with inferior map knowledge or mid-match adjustment delays in a high-pressure BO3."}], "final_score": 0.40418128654970764, "no_score": 0.5966816143497758, "edge": 0.004181286549707619, "no_edge": -0.0033183856502241316, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 64% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1966449", "question": "Dota 2: Nemiga Gaming vs Rune Eaters (BO3) - European Pro League Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Dota 2 Upper bracket quarterfinal 3 match between Nemiga Gaming and Rune Eaters in the European Pro League Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 13 at 2:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Nemiga Gaming\" if Nemiga Gaming win the match against Rune Eaters.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Rune Eaters\" if Rune Eaters win the match against Nemiga Gaming.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://www.dotabuff.com. However, if https://www.dotabuff.com has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-15T00:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-14T18:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.4, "volume_usd": 887.767579, "category": "dota-2", "clob_token_ids": ["67381820222547079837221844476228440930280794237265830208123855066984526329886", "2263632711736248100006672395889583386370437030049694240037296855286778725609"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "key_facts": ["| April 2, 2026 - 18:00 CEST | Tier 3 | Online | EPL Season 36 - April 2 | 2 : 0 |  | + Add details\") |\n| April 1, 2026 - 13:50 CEST | Qualifier | Online | RES Unchained 4 EU OQ2 | 0 : 1 |  | + Add details\") |\n| April 1, 2026 - 12:00 CEST | Qualifier | Online | RES Unchained 4 EU OQ2 | 1 : 0 |  | + Add details\") |\n| March 31, 2026 - 16:25 CEST | Qualifier | Online | RES Unchained 4 EU OQ1 | 0 : 1 | L1GA | + Add details\") | [...] | Date | Tier | Type | Tournament | S