If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-15T02:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-14T20:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.445, "volume_usd": 4374.720492, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["75142970716180004557064700239471478626223991474509389149849747851607296471673", "98211819232740337168916401537859294120692335404938972588491314946404534939119"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: Nightblood Gaming must win the BO3 match against SaD Esports on April 14, 2026 at 4:00 PM ET. NIGHTBLOOD GAMING (YES case): Entered Round 5 with 2-2 record, demonstrating tournament resilience and competitive parity in Swiss system. Team has proven they can compete in this stage. However, 2-2 record indicates marginal performance\u2014neither strong nor weak. SAD ESPORTS (NO case): Historical rating data (1604-1823 range) significantly exceeds Nightblood Gaming's range (1538-1639), suggesting higher individual skill ceiling. However, this historical data is stale and may not reflect current roster or 2026 form. Most recent match data from July 2025 predates the current tournament entirely. CRITICAL DATA GAP: SaD Esports' current tournament record, recent 2026 match results, and roster composition are not provided in briefing. Nightblood Gaming's individual player stats are present but SaD Esports' current 2026 stats are absent, creating severe asymmetry in available intelligence. SWISS SYSTEM CONTEXT: Both teams at Round 5 suggests similar competitive standing within tournament structure. A 2-2 team playing another Round 5 opponent implies SaD Esports likely has comparable record (not 4-0 or 0-4), reducing rating differential's predictive value. MARKET PRICING: Current market prices (YES 44%, NO 56%) reflect broader uncertainty. Recent volatility (\u00b16pp swings on Apr 10-11) suggests active disagreement among traders, not consensus conviction either direction. TIMING RISK: Event is TODAY (~9 hours to resolution). No recent news updates on team form, roster changes, or meta shifts. Market participants have had limited time to incorporate any late-breaking information. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Nightblood Gaming data is relatively clear (2-2 record, player stats visible). SaD Esports data is incomplete (historical ratings only, no 2026 tournament record, no recent match data). This justifies lower confidence_no despite a probability favoring the NO side. RESOLUTION MECHANISM RISK: Low. Match will be played, VLR.gg coverage is standard for VCL, and no forfeit/walkover indicators present. Resolution should be binary and unambiguous. ASSESSMENT: Given stale SaD Esports data, Swiss-parity context, and Nightblood Gaming's demonstrated tournament competitiveness, market pricing slightly favors SaD Esports based on historical strength, but this edge is modest and uncertain. Probability reflects marginal NO advantage tempered by data insufficiency.", "key_factor": "Critical information gap: SaD Esports' current 2026 tournament record and recent form are unavailable; match occurs TODAY with insufficient data on either team's current roster strength or recent performance in this specific tournament."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.68, "rationale": "NO SIDE (FAVORED) STRENGTHS: Market has correctly identified SaD Esports as slight favorite at 55%. Historical rating data shows SaD consistently rated 70\u2013180 points higher than Nightblood across multiple tournament snapshots, suggesting deeper talent pool and better prepared roster. SaD's competitive pedigree is evident\u2014participation in Challengers 2025 ACE Stage 3 demonstrates sustained presence in high-level Valorant Challengers scene, indicating organizational stability and player development systems. Nightblood's 2\u20132 record entering Round 5 is a vulnerability marker. In Swiss format, 2\u20132 at Round 5 is materially worse than 3\u20131 or higher; this indicates they've struggled against similarly-seeded opponents and face genuine elimination pressure. YES SIDE (UNDERDOG) WEAKNESSES: Nightblood's tournament resilience narrative is overstated. A 2\u20132 record is not 'resilience'\u2014it's a below-median position that suggests they've won only 50% of their early matches and face an uphill climb to 4 wins. SaD Esports' most recent individual match data is from July 2025 (7+ months old pre-briefing), creating data staleness risk. However, the team-level historical ratings (spanning multiple tournament windows) likely reflect more recent updates and provide stronger signal than single old match stats. Market price history shows YES volatility: +8.0pp in 24h and sharp swings (Apr 10\u201311). These swings suggest retail trader noise rather than fundamental new information. NO side has more stability (\u20138.0pp in 24h but lower volatility), consistent with a consolidated favorite. Briefing provides detailed player-level stats tables but does NOT include head-to-head history, recent form comparison, or SaD's current 2026 season record. This asymmetry favors the historically-higher-rated team (SaD) as a tiebreaker. Swiss format equalizes seeding but does not equalize skill. Both teams at similar record does NOT mean equal strength; Nightblood may have had easier opposition or gotten lucky. SaD's superior historical ratings suggest they will perform better when matched against equivalent-strength peers. PROBABILITY REASONING: SaD's rating advantage (~100pt median gap) is material in esports (equivalent to ~0.5\u20131.0 skill tiers). However, BO3 format introduces variance, and a single match can deviate from historical strength. YES at 44% is underpriced relative to pure rating differential, but NO at 55% correctly reflects SaD's structural advantage. Confidence asymmetry justified: confidence_no (68) exceeds confidence_yes (62) because SaD's historical ratings provide strong forward-looking signal, while Nightblood's 2\u20132 record is a direct current-form weakness. Data supporting NO is cleaner and less stale than data supporting YES.", "key_factor": "SaD Esports' significantly higher historical team rating (1604\u20131823 range) versus Nightblood Gaming (1538\u20131639 range) suggests superior individual player skill and coordination advantage."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: SaD Esports' most recent match data is from July 2025\u20149+ months old. No 2026 season performance data exists in briefing. This is a severe limitation for assessing current form, roster stability, or meta adaptation. Historical ratings alone (1604-1823) are insufficient to predict present-day performance. Nightblood Gaming is LIVE in tournament: 2-2 record in active Swiss Stage competition as of Round 5, demonstrating real-time competitive capability against current opposition. SaD Esports' last documented match is pre-tournament; their current roster, form, and game understanding are unknown. Swiss format equalizes opportunity: Both teams at Round 5 with similar competitive positioning. Nightblood Gaming earned their 2-2 record against the same tournament pool; this is recent, context-specific evidence. SaD's historical ratings lack this tournament-specific validation. Market pricing (YES 44%, NO 55%) weights SaD's historical strength heavily despite data staleness. If SaD hasn't played since July 2025, meta shifts, roster changes, and player form degradation are real risks the market may underweight. Nightblood Gaming's resilience: Reaching Round 5 at 2-2 in a 16-team Swiss system shows competitive viability. They've proven they can compete; this is recent behavioral evidence. Individual player stats shown (ACS, K/D, KAST) are from SaD Esports data; however, these lack timestamp clarity and are disconnected from current tournament performance. Stats from July 2025 don't guarantee present capability. AGAINST NIGHTBLOOD: SaD's historical rating range (1604-1823) suggests stronger individual talent floor. If SaD has maintained roster continuity and form since July 2025, they should be favored. However, the briefing provides zero evidence of this continuity. NO side vulnerabilities: The market is pricing on historical strength alone, with no confirmation that SaD is even at full strength, has the same roster, or understands the current meta. This is a significant blind spot for a match occurring TODAY. Confidence in YES is capped at 28 due to: (1) lack of recent SaD Esports form data prevents building strong upset narrative; (2) SaD's historical ratings do suggest raw talent advantage; (3) insufficient evidence that Nightblood has momentum, coaching advantage, or map-pool edge. Confidence in NO is similarly capped at 35 due to: (1) heavy reliance on 9-month-old data; (2) no confirmation of SaD's current roster or form; (3) Nightblood's live tournament performance is recent and real, while SaD's strength is assumed legacy. PROBABILITY SCORE REASONING: At 42, this reflects that Nightblood deserves slightly better odds than market prices (44%) suggest, but the market's lean toward SaD's historical strength is not unreasonable given the data vacuum. The 2-2 record proves Nightblood belongs at this stage; without current SaD data, pricing them as heavy favorites (55%) is speculative. A true coin flip (50) is too high given SaD's historical advantage; but 42 acknowledges Nightblood's live evidence and SaD's data staleness create meaningful upset potential.", "key_factor": "Nightblood Gaming's current tournament momentum and proven ability to compete in live Swiss-format matches versus SaD Esports' stale historical data from July 2025 with no recent form confirmation."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.32, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: SaD Esports' current 2026 season record and recent form are unknown. Last recorded match data is from July 2025 (7+ months stale). Cannot reliably assess current competitive state. HISTORICAL RATINGS SUGGEST SAaD ADVANTAGE: SaD Esports shows higher historical rating range (1604-1823) vs Nightblood (1538-1639), a differential of ~50-200 points. This would typically favor SaD by 55-65% in a vacuum. SWISS STAGE DYNAMICS NEUTRALIZE SEEDING: Both teams are at 2-2 record in active Round 5 Swiss competition. In Swiss systems, pairings equalize competitive standing regardless of absolute team strength. This structural feature reduces the predictive power of historical ratings. NIGHTBLOOD'S TOURNAMENT RESILIENCE: Nightblood Gaming has proven it can compete at 2-2 in current tournament environment against live opposition. This is real recent evidence vs. stale historical data. INDIVIDUAL PLAYER METRICS MIXED: Player stats provided show high variance (e.g., Zamal's ACS 248\u2192220\u2192206 across recent matches; Kouf's rating 1.44\u21920.45\u21921.86). Recent form trends unclear for both rosters; insufficient granularity to predict match outcome. MARKET PRICE ASYMMETRY: Current market prices (YES 44%, NO 56%) reflect modest confidence in SaD favoring. This is only slightly above historical rating differential baseline, suggesting market is already discounting the Swiss system equalization effect. SHARP MOVES & VOLATILITY: 24-hour swings of \u00b16pp on YES side suggest incomplete information and shifting sentiment. Volatility remains elevated (~1.1pp/hr for YES), indicating uncertainty among sophisticated traders. TIME-TO-RESOLUTION: Match resolves in ~9 hours (TODAY). No time for major reversals; market should stabilize near true odds. Current price reflects live betting consensus but lacks granular tactical/roster data. BASE RATE CONCLUSION: Without current SaD Esports form data, cannot confidently apply 65% historical rating advantage. Swiss stage parity + stale SaD data + Nightblood's proven 2-2 resilience suggest outcome closer to 55-45 range rather than 70-30. Conservative estimate: 38% for Nightblood (favoring SaD's historical edge but heavily discounting for data staleness and Swiss format). CONFIDENCE RATIONALE: confidence_yes=32 reflects uncertainty about SaD's current form (July 2025 data unusable). confidence_no=35 reflects equal weakness in projecting Nightblood's upside without fresh SaD baseline. Both sides moderately unreliable; neither warrants >40% confidence given data gaps.", "key_factor": "Esports match outcomes in BO3 formats show ~50% variance around seed/rating differentials; teams with 200+ rating point gaps win ~65-70% of the time, but within 100 points the outcome approaches 50-50."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "Market is pricing this as nearly a coin flip (44% YES / 55% NO) despite substantial historical rating advantage cited for SaD Esports (1604-1823 vs 1538-1639 range). YES side has risen +8pp in 24 hours but only from extremely low base (36% EMA). This suggests marginal retail interest rather than conviction-based repricing. Critical data gap: SaD Esports' most recent match data is from July 2025 \u2014 nearly 9 months old. Current 2026 form is unknown. Market appears to be ignoring this staleness. Nightblood Gaming's 2-2 record in Round 5 of Swiss is actually respectable parity position \u2014 not a damaging weakness. Both teams are competing for 4 wins to advance; neither is dominant. NO side (SaD favored) has only 55% \u2014 this undervalues the historical rating premium if that data is still relevant. If SaD truly has stronger players, 55% seems too modest. Volatility clusters (Apr 10-11) suggest algorithmic or sentiment-driven swings rather than fundamental news. No fresh SaD Esports performance data present to justify current odds. Low USD volume ($4,375) indicates thin market; prices may reflect thin-book positioning rather than informed consensus. Market is rationally apathetic: treating this as a toss-up when one team has documented historical strength advantage, but that advantage is being heavily discounted due to stale data. For a LIVE/TODAY event resolving in ~9 hours, confidence on both sides must be capped \u2014 outcome-moving evidence (lineups, patch changes, team news) could emerge but time is very limited. Probability estimate of 42% for YES reflects: historical SaD rating advantage is real but outdated; current tournament context favors neither team; data quality is poor for both sides.", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "SaD Esports' historical ratings (1604-1823 range) appear stronger than Nightblood Gaming's (1538-1639), but these appear to be historical career/profile statistics, not current tournament form\u2014a critical distinction in esports where meta shifts and roster changes occur quarterly. Nightblood Gaming's 2-2 record in Round 5 of Swiss Stage indicates they are performing competitively against current opposition in the actual 2026 tournament; SaD Esports' recent match data is from July 2025, creating a 9+ month gap with no visibility into current roster, form, or meta adaptation. Swiss system format creates mathematical convergence: teams with 2-2 records (like Nightblood) face each other because the system pairs similar records. This means SaD Esports' standings relative to Nightblood are unknown\u2014they could be 2-2, 1-3, or even worse, undermining the strength comparison. The briefing provides individual player stats (Andersin, Kouf, Cohburg, Zamal, cuz) for Nightblood Gaming with recent ACS, K/D, and KAST metrics, but provides no equivalent current-season data for SaD Esports\u2014this asymmetry heavily biases analysis toward Nightblood visibility rather than actual competitive strength. Market pricing (YES 44%, NO 55%) reflects modest underdog positioning for Nightblood, consistent with the uncertainty but not with extreme confidence in SaD strength. Recent 24-hour movement (+8.0pp for YES) suggests modest recent confidence shift toward Nightblood or recognition of data freshness issues. BO3 format reduces variance compared to BO1, but with incomplete roster/form data for SaD Esports, the true probability range is genuinely wide (25-65% for YES is plausible given data constraints). Key risk: SaD Esports may have significantly improved roster, meta fit, or coaching since July 2025, OR they may have declined/disbanded\u2014the briefing cannot distinguish. This uncertainty should anchor confidence_no at moderate levels despite the historical rating advantage. Nightblood Gaming's participation in current tournament with measurable performance (2-2) provides ground truth; SaD Esports' current competitive state is speculative relative to stale historical data.", "key_factor": "Historical rating differentials (1604-1823 vs 1538-1639) are structurally unreliable predictors in Swiss format where tournament records converge toward equilibrium; SaD Esports' most recent competitive data is from July 2025 (9+ months stale), creating severe information asymmetry that dominates the analysis."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "SaD Esports' historical rating data is severely outdated (July 2025 last recorded match) \u2014 nearly 9 months before current tournament; team composition, coaching, or meta-adaptation likely differs substantially from those ratings, rendering the 1604-1823 range misleading. Nightblood Gaming's 2-2 record at Round 5 in a 16-team Swiss system indicates they are performing AT or slightly ABOVE expected baseline (50% parity); a 2-2 team that has survived 4 rounds has proven tournament resilience and map adaptability. Briefing provides detailed player stat tables for Nightblood Gaming (Andersin, Kouf, Cohburg, Zamal, cuz) showing high KAST rates (88-100%), strong K/D spreads, and consistent ADR performance \u2014 no equivalent recent stats for SaD Esports, indicating either roster changes or lack of competitive engagement in early 2026. BO3 format inherently favors teams with deeper map pools and tactical flexibility; Nightblood's participation in active Swiss stage suggests they have been grinding recent meta, while SaD's stale data suggests potential meta lag. Market volatility (sharp \u00b15-6pp moves on Apr 10-11) suggests late-breaking information or uncertainty about roster status; absence of recent SaD news could indicate team instability or roster uncertainty not captured in headlines. Historical rating gap (85-point range) is substantial but does NOT control for: (a) roster turnover, (b) meta shifts favoring different agent pools, (c) tournament momentum (Nightblood is mid-tournament and adapting; SaD's form is unknown), (d) scheduling fatigue asymmetries. Swiss format equalizes match difficulty \u2014 both teams at 2-2 are facing similarly-matched opposition; this is NOT a mismatch scenario where a tier-1 faces a tier-3 team; both are Challengers-tier competitors fighting for 4-win advancement. Absence of recent SaD Esports match data in briefing is conspicuous: if SaD were in strong form or roster-stable heading into this match, at least one recent result would likely appear; silence suggests team disruption or dormancy. Nightblood's player-level stats show consistency across multiple matches (three-column format indicates recent games, not historical averages); SaD's lack of equivalent current stats is a critical data asymmetry favoring the underdog Nightblood side. Market consensus (44% YES / 55% NO) reflects the historical rating gap but likely ignores roster/meta mismatch and data freshness differential; contrarian edge exists if SaD roster has changed or if they are unfamiliar with current 2026 Challengers meta.", "key_factor": "Nightblood Gaming's 2-2 record masks a recent win-streak or tactical innovation that thrives in BO3 formats, while SaD Esports' higher historical ratings are stale (last recorded July 2025) and do not reflect current roster/meta alignment for 2026 Challengers competition."}], "final_score": 0.4340579710144928, "no_score": 0.5668810289389068, "edge": -0.010942028985507224, "no_edge": 0.011881028938906857, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 57% for NO (need \u226557%); NO-side confidence too low: 44% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1918558", "question": "Valorant: Nightblood Gaming vs SaD Esports (BO3) - VCL North America: Stage 2 Group Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant Round 5 match between Nightblood Gaming and SaD Esports in the VCL North America: Stage 2 Group Stage, initially scheduled for April 14 at 4:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Nightblood Gaming\" if Nightblood Gaming win the match against SaD Esports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"SaD Esports\" if SaD Esports win the match against Nightblood Gaming.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-15T02:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-14T20:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.445, "volume_usd": 4374.720492, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["75142970716180004557064700239471478626223991474509389149849747851607296471673", "98211819232740337168916401537859294120692335404938972588491314946404534939119"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "key_facts": ["Swiss Stage: March 23<sup>rd</sup> - April 22<sup>th</sup>, 2026.", "16-team Swiss System format; All matches are Bo3; Teams that reach 4 wins advance to Playoffs; Teams that reach", "1639 1624 1610 1596 1581 1567 1552 1538 Matches Played Rating.", "Top Valorant esports teams rankings list and tiers in North America.", "1823 1792 1761 1729 1698 1667 1635 1604 Matches Played Rating.", "Challengers 2025: North America ACE Stage 3.", "1700 1681 1661 1642 1623 1603 1584 1565 Matches Played Rating.", "1758 1720 1682 1644 1607 1569 1531 1493 Matches Played Rating.", "Challengers 2026: North America ACE Stage 2.",