{"run_id": "45460444-9150-412d-ab91-6cb65f65d080", "timestamp": "2026-04-15T13:51:12.806202+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1942729", "question": "Valorant: BBL Esports vs GIANTX (BO3) - VCT EMEA Group Omega", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between BBL Esports and GIANTX in the VCT EMEA Group Omega, initially scheduled for April 15 at 11:00AM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"BBL Esports\" if BBL Esports win the match against GIANTX.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"GIANTX\" if GIANTX win the match against BBL Esports.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-15T21:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-15T15:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.645, "volume_usd": 10779.344374000004, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["92748001937696945041743970979262078386777886960267604089624988851004135230000", "31218625657634872800559073162804271845309955686048374319436840960435082274650"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.64, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "CONDITION: BBL Esports wins the Bo3 match against GIANTX on April 15, 2026. Market price reflects 64% YES / 36% NO split, suggesting moderate confidence in BBL victory. BBL STRENGTHS: Won VCT 2026 EMEA Kickoff tournament (Jan-Feb 2026), demonstrating recent peak form and roster stability heading into Stage 1. BBL RECENCY CONCERN: Kickoff win was ~6-8 weeks before this match (Feb to mid-April); insufficient data on whether BBL sustained form through early Group Omega matches. GIANTX STRENGTHS: Defeated PACIFIC 2-1 with exceptional dual-duelist performances (ara and westside each 58 kills); shows firepower and ability to execute coordinated strategies in Bo3 format. GIANTX CONTEXT: Described as 'bouncing back' after 'slow kickoff start,' suggesting adaptation and resilience in Stage 1 group play. MISSING DATA: No head-to-head record provided; no current Group Omega standings; no post-Kickoff roster changes or performance metrics for either team; no coach/IGL adjustment impact quantified. FNATIC REFERENCE: Briefing mentions GIANTX lost to Fnatic (implied from scattered match data), but no context on when, score, or comparative strength of that loss. BO3 FORMAT: Best-of-three reduces variance; GIANTX's duelist-heavy composition can exploit map-specific weaknesses across multiple maps, not just one. MARKET VOLATILITY: YES side saw -5.5pp drop on Apr 12, suggesting possible information event (team news, roster concern, or community sentiment shift); currently stabilized near 64%. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong case for YES (recent major tournament win, established form). NO case relies on single recent win against PACIFIC and observed firepower without broader context on consistency or standing. RESOLUTION CRITERIA: Clear and unambiguous\u2014match winner determines outcome. No forfeit/withdrawal risk noted in briefing. PROBABILITY ASSESSMENT: 64% for BBL aligns with recent tournament victory and roster stability, but lack of current Group Omega data and GIANTX's demonstrated firepower prevents higher confidence in either direction.", "key_factor": "Briefing contains no recent head-to-head record, current Group Omega standings, or post-Kickoff roster/performance data for either team, limiting confidence in the NO case assessment."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.64, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "BBL KICKOFF DOMINANCE: BBL Esports won the VCT 2026 EMEA Kickoff tournament in Jan-Feb 2026, the most recent major EMEA competition. This is the strongest indicator of current form and team cohesion, occurring just ~6-8 weeks before this Stage 1 match. ROSTER STABILITY & TRACK RECORD: BBL has established roster stability and a proven competitive track record in the EMEA region, providing consistency that matters in BO3 formats where team synergy and map preparation are critical. GIANTX'S MIXED RESULTS: While GIANTX beat PACIFIC 2-1 with strong individual performances (ara/westside ~58 kills each), the briefing also notes GIANTX 'lost to Fnatic and other established teams,' indicating vulnerability against top-tier opposition. BO3 FORMAT REDUCES VARIANCE: Best-of-three maps favors the more complete, better-prepared team over upset-prone single-map scenarios. BBL's proven Stage 1 preparation advantage (Kickoff champion) is magnified in BO3. GIANTX KICKOFF PERFORMANCE GAP: The briefing does not mention GIANTX winning or excelling in the Kickoff tournament, suggesting BBL entered Stage 1 from a higher baseline of recent competitive success. TEAM COMPOSITION STABILITY: Community discussion notes roster/coaching adjustments across EMEA, but BBL's Kickoff victory suggests their changes (if any) were well-integrated, whereas GIANTX's trajectory is less clear. COUNTERPOINT - GIANTX DUELIST FIREPOWER: GIANTX's dual-Duelist composition (ara + westside) with individual performance data shows tactical versatility and map-specific strength that could exploit certain weaknesses in a BO3. COUNTERPOINT - GROUP STAGE MOMENTUM: GIANTX's 2-1 win over PACIFIC demonstrates they can execute at Group Omega level and generate momentum mid-tournament, reducing the recency gap from Kickoff. MARKET PRICE ALIGNMENT: 64% YES reflects BBL as clear favorite; market appears well-calibrated given Kickoff victory pedigree. Recent 24h volatility (-3.0pp on YES, +3.0pp on NO) suggests minor confidence erosion but not fundamental repricing. DATA GAPS - NO CONFIDENCE IMPACT: No head-to-head record, full Group Omega standings, or detailed map preferences provided limits precise calibration of GIANTX's specific weaknesses; confidence_no set to 55 to reflect uncertainty on underdog's full capability. TIMING: Match resolves TODAY in ~7 hours; sharp price moves on Apr 12-13 (\u00b19.5pp swings) suggest late-breaking intel or odds adjustment, but the 64/36 split currently holds. No catastrophic news evident in briefing.", "key_factor": "BBL Esports' recent EMEA Kickoff tournament victory (February 2026) demonstrates peak competitive form and roster stability heading into Stage 1 Group Omega play."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "YES SIDE STRENGTH: BBL won EMEA Kickoff (Feb 2026), demonstrating peak form ~6 weeks ago. Roster stability and EMEA pedigree support the 64% marke