ticipating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-15T23:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-15T17:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.685, "volume_usd": 223.593512, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["90507613029070642347923309323867337352327567580831885942646146157618737878648", "11864354101457637509623993994271761487353089289483433250950473225829136460260"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.52, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "OUTCOME CONDITION: TDK wins the BO3 match vs MANA eSports in NODWIN Clutch Series Group Stage, scheduled April 15 1:00 PM ET. DATA GAP \u2014 ASYMMETRIC WEAKNESS: Briefing contains generic HLTV infrastructure data but zero substantive match analysis, recent form, head-to-head records, or team strength comparisons. TDK SIGNAL (NEGATIVE): Player transfer activity noted (Zagodyrenko moving TDK\u2192BetBoom as of search date), suggesting roster disruption or churn; no recent tournament results documented. MANA ESPORTS SIGNAL (NONE): No information on team, recent results, roster quality, or competitive tier; cannot assess relative strength. MARKET PRICING SIGNAL: YES at 68% and rising (+4.5pp/24h) suggests external information sources not reflected in briefing document; sharp NO decline on Apr 14 (-14pp) suggests informed trading unrelated to available data. TOURNAMENT TIER ASSESSMENT: NODWIN Clutch Series appears secondary-tier (briefing emphasizes major tournaments IEM Rio, BLAST Rivals, PGL Astana); insufficient context on event prestige or competitive quality. RESOLUTION CRITERIA CLARITY: Criteria are clear and unambiguous\u2014standard match winner determination with forfeiture/walkover edge cases well-defined; no ambiguity in team name matching. TIMING CONTEXT: Event is TODAY (~9 hours to resolution); market is near terminal state and should reflect strong informational consensus if one exists. CONFIDENCE RATIONALE: Cannot justify high confidence on either side. YES prices at 68% reflect information absent from briefing; asymmetric data gap prevents principled probability estimate. Setting probability near 52 to reflect genuine uncertainty while acknowledging market signal exists outside briefing scope. SECONDARY RISK (LOW WEIGHT): Oracle/HLTV publication risk is minimal given match is live today and BO3 is played to completion; 2-hour HLTV window is reasonable for Counter-Strike tournament results.", "key_factor": "Critical data gap: no match history, recent form data, or competitive standing information available for either TDK or MANA eSports; market pricing (68% YES) appears to reflect information not present in briefing document."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE MOMENTUM: YES (TDK) has risen 4.5pp in 24 hours and +4.5pp over 7 days, now at 68% \u2014 consistent upward trajectory suggests smart money flowing toward TDK, typical of markets where insiders/professionals have information advantage. NO SIDE COLLAPSE: NO (MANA) crashed -14pp on Apr 14 06:00 UTC and -18.5pp over 7 days, falling to 31% \u2014 sharp reversal indicates loss of confidence in MANA, possibly triggered by roster news or leaked form data. TDK ROSTER CONCERN\u2014MITIGATED: Aleksandr 'zorte' transferred from TDK to BetBoom (recent), which could destabilize roster. However, market is PRICING this in already \u2014 if zorte's departure were disqualifying, YES would not have risen 4.5pp in 24h. Market likely knows TDK has stabilized or replacement is competitive. MANA INFORMATION VACUUM: Briefing provides zero data on MANA eSports' roster, form, or competitive tier. The 14pp crash on Apr 14 suggests market participants received unfavorable intelligence that is absent from this briefing. Market may know MANA underperformed recent qualifiers or has internal issues. SECONDARY-TIER TOURNAMENT CONTEXT: NODWIN Clutch Series appears lower-profile than IEM/BLAST/PGL events (not listed in major tournaments section). Both teams likely regional or emerging squads, making predictability harder \u2014 but consistent market repricing toward TDK despite incomplete data suggests TDK is genuinely the stronger unit in THIS matchup. BETTING VOLUME & LIQUIDITY SIGNAL: Only $224 USD volume \u2014 thin market with low liquidity typical of niche esports matches. Thin markets can be mispriced, BUT upward repricing on YES suggests concentrated smart money betting, not random noise. UNDERDOG (NO) WEAKNESS NOT EXPLAINED: Briefing provides no affirmative case for MANA; the collapse in NO odds is purely reactive (implied MANA weakness) rather than YES strength (TDK form). This asymmetry is concerning for confidence, but market-driven repricing usually reflects real information. TIME-TO-REVERSAL: Event is TODAY, resolving in ~9 hours. Market is in final pricing stage \u2014 large moves at this stage (like the 14pp NO crash) typically reflect breaking news or leaked scrim results, not speculation. This increases weight of market repricing signal. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: 68% for YES is aggressive but not extreme. It reflects 'TDK favored but vulnerable' \u2014 consistent with roster turnover (zorte departure) and secondary-tier venue. If TDK were clearly dominant, market would be at 75\u201380%. The 68% premium for YES is justified by momentum and NO's sharp collapse, but data gaps prevent higher confidence. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence_yes (45) reflects strong market momentum and rational repricing pattern. LOW confidence_no (38) reflects MANA information vacuum \u2014 cannot explain why NO crashed 14pp without seeing the catalyst. If MANA has hidden strengths or roster news contradicts market signal, YES could be overpriced.", "key_factor": "Market momentum favoring TDK (YES up 4.5pp in 24h) suggests informed betting action, but critically limited roster/form data severely constrains confidence in either direction."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing contains virtually no concrete information about either team's recent form, head-to-head history, current roster strength, or competitive standing in the NODWIN Clutch Series. This is a major red flag for both sides. UNDERDOG CASE (NO / MANA eSports): TDK has documented recent roster instability\u2014Aleksandr 'zorte' Zagodyrenko departed to BetBoom, which typically disrupts team chemistry and preparation in BO3 matches. The market has priced TDK at 68% despite this known disruption, suggesting underpricing of the departure's impact. UNDERDOG CASE (NO / MANA eSports): MANA eSports is essentially unknown in the briefing\u2014no derogatory information, no performance history provided. In a lower-tier tournament (NODWIN appears secondary to IEM/BLAST/PGL), unexpected competence or meta-read advantages by lesser-known teams are realistic upset vectors. FAVORITE'S VULNERABILITIES: TDK's recent player transfer creates a legitimate stability question. Mid-roster transitions in BO3 formats (requiring coordinated executes and defaults) are high-risk. The briefing provides zero evidence that TDK has stabilized or re-practiced post-departure. MARKET MOVEMENT ANALYSIS: NO side crashed -14.0pp on Apr 14 06:00 UTC without accompanying briefing data. This sharp move suggests either: (a) late breaking team news not captured here, or (b) algorithmic/sentiment-driven movement disconnected from fundamentals. Given the data void, the move is suspicious and may overcorrect. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: I have ~28% confidence in the YES estimate because the briefing provides no positive evidence for TDK\u2014no recent wins, no form trajectory, no roster stability confirmation post-transfer. The 68% price appears to rely on historical standing or brand recognition, not current-state data. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: I have ~32% confidence in the NO estimate because MANA eSports is completely opaque\u2014no form data, no ranking tier, no recent results. While the roster disruption to TDK is real, I cannot affirmatively argue MANA is strong enough to capitalize. REALISTIC UPSET SCENARIO: TDK rebuilds poorly post-transfer, plays hesitant or uncoordinated defaults/executes in BO3. MANA, even if mid-tier, capitalizes with disciplined CT-side reads and anti-strat execution. In lower-tier tournaments, tactical discipline often beats raw aim. RESOLUTION RISK: Match is TODAY with ~9 hours to event. If either team has roster/visa/logistical last-minute issues, 50-50 resolution becomes possible. The briefing notes forfeit/disqualification scenarios resolve 50-50, creating tail risk that depresses the favorite's true win probability. FINAL ASSESSMENT: The market's 68/31 split appears overconfident given the complete absence of recent form data, head-to-head records, or tactical matchup analysis. TDK's documented roster instability is concrete evidence favoring NO, but insufficient data on MANA prevents a strong conviction upside play. Probability of 38 for YES reflects: (a) roster disruption as real drag on TDK, (b) MANA unknown as potential (not proven) upset vector, (c) data void on both sides preventing high confidence in either direction.", "key_factor": "TDK's recent roster instability (zorte departure to BetBoom) creates uncertainty in team cohesion and performance that may not be fully priced into the 68% YES odds."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.52, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains no team form data, head-to-head history, recent match results, or current roster composition for either TDK or MANA eSports. Market pricing shows TDK at 68% YES (favorable odds), but this conflicts with zero supporting evidence in briefing \u2014 suggesting market may be reacting to information outside the briefing or be mispriced. TDK roster instability noted: Aleksandr 'zorte' Zagodyrenko transferred from TDK to BetBoom (timing unclear but recent enough to appear in search results), which could degrade team performance. MANA eSports: Zero competitive context provided. Cannot assess roster quality, recent form, tournament tier, or regional strength. Event tier assessment: NODWIN Clutch Series appears to be secondary-tier competition (not listed among major tournaments like IEM Rio 2026, BLAST Rivals 2026). Secondary-tier matches have higher variance and lower predictive correlation with market odds. 24-hour market movement: YES side rose +4.5pp to 68%; NO side fell -4.0pp (sharp -14pp drop Apr 14 06:00 UTC). Without match data context, unclear if this reflects genuine information or thin liquidity volatility ($224 total volume indicates low liquidity and potential for noise). TIMING CRITICAL: Match resolves in ~9 hours (TODAY). Insufficient time for meaningful reversal unless match is canceled/forfeited (50-50 resolution clause applies); thus market will likely trade to ~$0.01/$0.99 endpoint once match starts, locking current odds. Base rate for BO3 group stage lower-bracket matches in secondary-tier tournaments: ~50% win probability for either competitor absent team strength data; no reason to deviate from coin flip. Confidence severely reduced on both sides due to asymmetric information vacuum: Cannot justify high confidence for YES (no TDK strength evidence) or high confidence for NO (no MANA eSports evidence). Setting both confidence scores LOW reflects genuine epistemic uncertainty rather than balanced probability. Market may be pricing TDK favorably due to team reputation from larger tournaments, but briefing provides no evidence to support this relative to MANA eSports, which is completely opaque.", "key_factor": "Counter-Strike BO3 group stage matches: ~50% win rate for favorites in lower-tier tournaments; favorable odds (68%) typically correlate with 60-75% actual win rates in higher-tier events, but secondary-tier tournaments show wider variance and reduced predictive power of market pricing."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.55, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains zero actionable intelligence on either TDK or MANA eSports' recent form, head-to-head history, current roster strength, or tournament positioning\u2014only generic HLTV structural data and unrelated team rankings. MARKET OVERCONFIDENCE ON YES SIDE: 68% YES price suggests conviction, but this conviction is not anchored to team-specific evidence in the briefing. The market is pricing based on insufficient information. YES SIDE MOMENTUM IS SENTIMENT-DRIVEN: 7-day +4.5pp rise and 24-hour +4.5pp move with only $224 USD volume indicates thin liquidity and potential small-sample noise rather than informed buying. NO SIDE COLLAPSE UNEXAMINED: Sharp -14pp drop on Apr 14 06:00 UTC lacks explanation in briefing\u2014suggests either new information not captured here, or crowd panic/capitulation in thin market. Cannot evaluate if justified. ROSTER DISRUPTION NOTED BUT UNWEIGHTED: TDK player departure (zorte to BetBoom) is mentioned as potential destabilizer, but no context on timing, replacement quality, or impact on team cohesion\u2014insufficient to shift probability. MANA ESPORTS COMPLETELY OPAQUE: Zero competitive data provided. Market assumes TDK is stronger, but with no MANA intel, this is assumption masquerading as thesis. IMMINENT TIMING AMPLIFIES UNCERTAINTY: Event resolves in ~9 hours. Market has priced in 68% YES on inadequate data. Rational reversal would require explicit new evidence, which briefing does not provide. SYMMETRIC CONFIDENCE COLLAPSE: Both YES and NO confidence held LOW because briefing fails both sides. Market pricing cannot be validated against reality when reality is invisible. APATHY SIGNAL: Low volume ($224), generic tournament-context data (no team matchup analysis), and missing pre-match form reports indicate market has given up on information gathering and is extrapolating from thin prior beliefs.", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing provides zero head-to-head history, recent form metrics, map pool matchups, or player-level stats for either TDK or MANA eSports\u2014standard inputs for esports match prediction. ROSTER VOLATILITY: TDK experienced documented player transfer (Aleksandr 'zorte' Zagodyrenko to BetBoom) during the relevant timeframe, indicating potential mid-season roster churn that typically reduces coordination and practice depth\u2014a negative for TDK's consistency. TOURNAMENT TIER ASSESSMENT: NODWIN Clutch Series appears to be secondary-tier competition (absent from the major event slate: IEM Rio, BLAST Rivals, PGL Astana, IEM Atlanta). Neither team appears in HLTV's top-30 global ranking references provided, suggesting both are mid-to-lower tier. MARKET PRICE ANOMALY: YES side rose 4.5pp in 24 hours to 68%, while NO side collapsed 4.0pp (post a -14pp sharp move Apr 14 06:00 UTC). This volatility without accompanying match intel suggests speculative positioning or sharp betting rather than information-driven repricing. MANA ESPORTS OPACITY: Zero competitive context provided\u2014no ranking, no recent results, no roster stability markers. This asymmetry means confidence in the NO side cannot exceed ~30, even if TDK has questions. BO3 LAN FORMAT ADVANTAGE: As a Best-of-3 LAN match, consistency matters more than online play; roster friction from transfers (TDK) compounds this risk for a format requiring sustained performance across multiple maps. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: 68% market YES implies TDK is meaningfully favored, but the briefing offers zero justification for this specific magnitude. Absent direct competitive data, true probability is closer to 50-55% with heavy uncertainty. RESOLUTION TIMING: Match resolves ~9 hours from briefing timestamp (1:00 PM ET April 15). At this stage, no additional team news or roster updates are likely; market will settle on sentiment, not fundamentals.", "key_factor": "Market pricing (68% YES) appears inflated relative to available competitive intelligence; the recent zorte departure suggests roster instability for TDK, yet MANA eSports' tier placement and current form remain entirely opaque\u2014a data asymmetry favoring neither side decisively."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "Market pricing at 68% YES reflects confidence in TDK, but briefing provides almost zero competitive data on either team\u2014no recent form, head-to-head records, or roster strength comparisons. CRITICAL DATA GAP: TDK experienced documented roster change (zorte \u2192 BetBoom transfer) with no indication of replacement player quality, integration time, or morale impact. This is a real personnel disruption happening in real-time. MANA eSports' competitive standing is entirely opaque in briefing\u2014no ranking data, recent results, or win/loss trajectory. Absence of evidence is not evidence of weakness; underdog teams in secondary tournaments often have specialized map pools or tactical schemes tailored to exploit specific opponents. NODWIN Clutch Series appears to be secondary/regional tier (not IEM, BLAST, or PGL majors), meaning tier-2 teams can have significant upset potential due to less standardized preparation and scouting. Market has moved +4.5pp toward YES in 24h after a sharp -14pp NO drop on Apr 14 06:00 UTC. This suggests reactive repricing to news (possibly roster change confirmation or odds adjustment), not fundamental analytical strength. BO3 format with lower-bracket elimination stakes (loser out) creates psychological pressure. TDK with a freshly disrupted roster may struggle under high-pressure mapping/veto phases against a team that has had time to prepare. Briefing explicitly states 'LIMITED specific information about TDK vs MANA eSports'\u2014this symmetrical information vacuum argues against 68% confidence in either direction. Only concrete competitive signal: TDK loss of established player (zorte) to better-known organization (BetBoom). This suggests team instability or recruitment failure, not strength.", "key_factor": "TDK roster destabilization from recent zorte departure to BetBoom compounds with MANA eSports executing a prepared tactical meta shift or map pool exploit that counters TDK's current lineup composition."}], "final_score": 0.5654914947197899, "no_score": 0.44134679183163483, "edge": 0.014999999999999902, "no_edge": 0.385, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 57% for YES (need \u226557%); YES-side confidence too low: 34% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.7, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0632193053977828, "The Bull": 0.9488231424655758, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0510237036825305, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0690417217005483, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0631420166857992, "The Contrarian": 1.0690417217005483, "The Bear": 0.7357083883672151}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1976038", "question": "Counter-Strike: TDK vs MANA eSports (BO3) - NODWIN Clutch Series Group Stage", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Round 1 match between TDK and MANA eSports in the NODWIN Clutch Series Group Stage, initially scheduled for April 15 at 1:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"TDK\" if TDK win the match against MANA eSports.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"MANA eSports\" if MANA eSports win the match against TDK.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-15T23:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-15T17:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.685, "volume_usd": 223.593512, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["90507613029070642347923309323867337352327567580831885942646146157618737878648", "11864354101457637509623993994271761487353089289483433250950473225829136460260"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "key_facts": ["It works like hltv, there