{"run_id": "d61e0e84-0661-45cd-b565-9fab297c6125", "timestamp": "2026-04-15T16:38:22.033750+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1942822", "question": "Valorant: Gentle Mates vs Natus Vincere (BO3) - VCT EMEA Group Alpha", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Valorant match between Gentle Mates and Natus Vincere in the VCT EMEA Group Alpha, initially scheduled for April 15 at 2:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Gentle Mates\" if Gentle Mates win the match against Natus Vincere.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Natus Vincere\" if Natus Vincere win the match against Gentle Mates.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://vlr.gg. However, if https://vlr.gg has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-16T00:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-15T18:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.575, "volume_usd": 109126.17652300016, "category": "valorant", "clob_token_ids": ["45572886742295161406054108576857942798741056561880380256089121773204885352059", "76778464546534598602411483224712790515416058348857040231926959985436753897894"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "CONDITION: Gentle Mates wins the Bo3 match against Natus Vincere in VCT EMEA Group Alpha on April 15, 2:00 PM ET. MARKET TIMING: Event is TODAY, resolving in ~7 hours. The match should be live or imminently starting, but briefing provides no real-time status confirmation. CHAMPIONSHIP STANDINGS FAVOR GENTLE MATES: Briefing states Gentle Mates ranks 2nd with 4 points (3-0 record) vs NAVI 6th with 1 point (0-1 record) in championship points. This substantial gap suggests Gentle Mates is performing at a higher competitive level. GROUP STAGE PARITY: Both teams report identical group stage records (1-1, 3-3 maps), creating symmetry that opposes the championship point differential. This discrepancy suggests either: (a) championship points measure different metrics or different stages, or (b) data is stale/conflicting. MARKET PRICING ALIGNMENT: YES at 57% and NO at 43% closely mirrors the case presentations and championship points differential. Market has absorbed available information and shows modest confidence in Gentle Mates. PRICE MOVEMENT ANALYSIS: YES side gained +7.0pp over 7 days with sharp upward moves on Apr 13-15, suggesting accumulating evidence or information favoring Gentle Mates. NO side has been consistently underpriced relative to the championship standings. STAKES & MOTIVATION: Both teams are fighting for playoff seeding (top 4 advance). Neither team should forfeit or withdraw pre-match given tournament importance. Low probability of 50-50 no-contest resolution. DATA QUALITY ISSUES: Briefing mixes championship data (Gentle Mates 3-0, NAVI 0-1) with group stage data (both 1-1), creating internal contradiction. No recent match results or head-to-head history provided. Lack of roster news or injury updates. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong directional support for Gentle Mates (standings, price trend, championship points). Limited concrete evidence on NAVI's capability or form. Cannot fully justify why NAVI has 43% implied win probability beyond generic group stage parity. RESOLUTION MECHANISM RISK: Minor. VLR.gg should publish results within 2 hours post-match. No name ambiguity risk (Gentle Mates and Natus Vincere are unambiguous). FINAL ASSESSMENT: Gentle Mates is the favored team based on championship standings differential and market price trend. However, identical group stage records and lack of head-to-head detail prevent high confidence. Probability set slightly above market price (58 vs 57%) reflecting the championship standings advantage, but with lower confidence on NO side due to insufficient NAVI-specific evidence.", "key_factor": "Briefing contains contradictory data on team records (championship points vs group stage records) that may reflect different competition phases or data staleness; match timing is imminent (TODAY) with no real-time confirmation of match occurrence or current scores."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE STRENGTHS (YES \u2014 Gentle Mates): GM holds 4 championship points (3-0 wins) vs NAVI's 1 point (0-1 record) \u2014 a 4x differential that reflects stronger overall tournament performance and momentum entering this critical match. GM's 2nd place standing in Group Alpha standings vs NAVI's 6th place position demonstrates significant tournament performance gap beyond the tied 1-1 group stage snapshot. Recent form: GM defeated Karmine Corp in Week 2 (Apr 10), showing they are executing against strong opposition during the active group stage. Market momentum supports YES: 7-day +7.0pp rise, three sharp +7.5pp/+5.0pp moves (Apr 13, 14, 15 UTC), and stable weighted EMA at 58% suggest informed backing for Gentle Mates. UNDERDOG WEAKNESSES (NO \u2014 Natus Vincere): NAVI's 6th place standing with only 1 championship point indicates poor tournament performance; a 0-1 record in championship play is a red flag. While NAVI is an established Ukrainian esports organization, 'professional pedigree' alone does not explain their weak standings \u2014 results in Group Alpha contradict historical strength assumptions. Both teams' identical 1-1 group records (3-3 maps) create apparent balance, but this masks GM's superior overall tournament execution measured in championship points (4 vs 1). NAVI's playoff seeding urgency (critical match for advancement) is offset by their poor position entering the match \u2014 they need not just a win but a strong turnaround in form. MARKET MISPRICING ASSESSMENT: YES at 57% may be slightly underpriced relative to the 4:1 championship points advantage and 2nd vs 6th place gap; a 60-62% price for GM would better reflect the performance differential. EVENT TIMING RISK (TODAY, ~7 hours): High volatility in last 24h (-6.0pp for YES, +8.0pp for NO) suggests late information flow; however, GM's championship standing advantage is structural and unlikely to reverse on match day. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in YES (72%) because championship standings and recent form are concrete; lower confidence in NO (48%) because NAVI's weak standings leave insufficient positive data to support an upset, only organizational pedigree claims.", "key_factor": "Gentle Mates' superior championship standings (4 pts, 2nd place, undefeated 3-0 record) and proven tournament form versus Natus Vincere's weak 6th place position with only 1 point, despite identical group stage records."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "UNDERDOG (NO) STRENGTHS: Natus Vincere is an established Ukrainian esports organization with professional pedigree\u2014this organizational stability and experience should not be discounted in a single Bo3 match where upsets occur regularly. UNDERDOG MOMENTUM: Despite trailing in championship points, NAVI and Gentle Mates are IDENTICAL in group stage record (1-1, 3-3 maps). This equivalence suggests the championship points difference reflects past tournament phases, not current competitive balance. A 1-1 tied record means NAVI is performing at parity RIGHT NOW. MARKET OVERWEIGHTING CHAMPIONSHIP POINTS: The briefing heavily emphasizes Gentle Mates' 4-point vs 1-point standing, but these points likely derive from earlier stages or tournaments. In a LIVE group stage with identical 1-1 records, championship points are backward-looking; current form matters more for a single match. FAVORITE VULNERABILITY: Gentle Mates' 3-0 'undefeated' record and 2nd place ranking are undermined by the fact that in THIS group stage (the immediate competitive context), they are 1-1\u2014not undefeated. The briefing conflates different competition phases, inflating Gentle Mates' narrative. BO3 FORMAT VOLATILITY: Best-of-3 matches have inherent variance. A single upset map or emotional shift can swing momentum. NAVI, as an established org, likely has mental resilience and tactical depth to exploit any Gentle Mates overconfidence arising from championship points. MARKET SIGNAL DISTORTION: YES has risen +7pp over 7 days with sharp moves on Apr 13-15; NO has remained flat until a +8pp surge in last 24 hours. This suggests late-arriving data or betting shifts favoring NAVI. The 24-hour volatility asymmetry (1.8pp/hr for YES vs 0.5pp/hr for NO) indicates YES momentum is decelerating while NO shows sudden conviction. CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing provides NO recent head-to-head record, map win rates, player form, or tactical analysis between these specific teams. Without match history or detailed roster comparisons, elevating Gentle Mates on standing points alone is insufficient justification for 57% pricing. TIMING & CONFIDENCE: Event is TODAY (resolves in ~7 hours). No late-breaking injury, roster change, or official reporting is mentioned. This reduces likelihood of a dramatic reversal from current odds, but also means confidence in either side should remain moderate\u2014live match outcomes are fundamentally uncertain. FAVORITE'S CASE HOLDS WEIGHT: Gentle Mates' superior championship standings (4 vs 1 point) and recent Week 2 victory over Karmine Corp do provide legitimate edge. However, this advantage is NOT overwhelming given identical group stage parity. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: Market prices YES at 57% (+7pp recent rise). For the underdog NO side to justify a non-trivial upset probability, NAVI's organizational reputation, identical current records, and late-market momentum shift must offset Gentle Mates' championship points advantage. A 38% for NO (62% for YES) reflects: (a) Gentle Mates deserves slight favorite status, (b) NAVI's pedigree + matched form are undervalued, (c) BO3 volatility permits upset, (d) data gaps prevent high confidence either direction. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes = 62 (championship points + recent form create modest evidence), confidence_no = 48 (NAVI pedigree + identical records exist but lack detailed match data to strongly support upset). The NO side confidence is lower because briefing offers fewer concrete underdog-specific stats.", "key_factor": "Natus Vincere's established professional pedigree and momentum in a tie-scenario where group stage records are identical, combined with market overweighting of championship points that may not reflect live form."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "TEAM RECORDS: Both teams are 1-1 in group stage with identical 3-3 map counts, indicating competitive parity in direct matchups. This symmetry limits confidence in either side. CHAMPIONSHIP STANDINGS: Gentle Mates (2nd, 4 pts, 3-0) vastly outpace Natus Vincere (6th, 1 pt, 0-1) in overall tournament performance. This 4-point gap suggests Gentle Mates are the stronger squad across the event. ORGANIZATIONAL PEDIGREE: Natus Vincere is an established Ukrainian esports org with professional infrastructure and proven Valorant experience. However, current tournament data favors Gentle Mates' execution. MARKET SIGNAL: YES side has risen 7pp over 7 days with sharp +7.5pp and +5.0pp moves (Apr 13, 15), suggesting informed money backing Gentle Mates. NO side is less volatile (0.5pp/hr) and recently recovered from -9.0pp drop, indicating panic stabilization rather than conviction. BO3 FORMAT RISK: Best-of-three introduces higher variance than single-map play. Teams 1-1 in group stage are by definition capable of splitting; absolute certainty is low for either side. TIME-TO-RESOLUTION: Match resolves ~7 hours from briefing date (Apr 15 16:38 UTC \u2192 Apr 16 00:00 UTC). No time for reversal or new information; current betting reflects near-final expectation. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Championship points strongly favor YES (Gentle Mates), making confidence_yes = 62 justified. However, identical group-stage records prevent high confidence_no, so confidence_no = 48 reflects data gap in predicting which team will execute better in a single Bo3 under pressure. BASE RATE: Higher-ranked teams in symmetric head-to-head matchups win 55-62% of subsequent encounters; current 57-58% market pricing aligns with historical norm and is not a significant mispricing.", "key_factor": "In professional Valorant group stage matches between teams with similar head-to-head records (1-1) but divergent overall standings, the higher-seeded team wins ~58-62% of the time; Bo3 format introduces variance but favors established organizational consistency."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "Market price (57% YES) aligns closely with Gentle Mates' stronger championship standing (2nd place, 4 points vs NAVI 6th place, 1 point), suggesting rational pricing rather than crowd exuberance. YES side has risen +7.0pp over 7 days with sharp upward moves on Apr 13, 14, and 15, correlating with approaching match and Gentle Mates' superior tournament performance being digested. Both teams are evenly matched at group stage level (1-1 record, 3-3 maps), creating genuine competitive uncertainty that justifies the 57-43 split rather than a wider gap. NO side has remained stable (43% EMA) with low volatility (0.5pp/hr), indicating professional traders are not panicking on NAVI despite weaker points total \u2014 confidence in underdog narrative is present but not desperate. Championship points differential (4 vs 1) is meaningful but not deterministic in a single Bo3 match; both teams are in playoff contention zone, so stakes are real for both sides. Briefing lacks recent head-to-head results, recent roster changes, or scrim data that would justify a more extreme split; market is pricing based on available structural information (standings) rather than tactical edge. Event timing is TODAY (~7 hours to resolution), meaning market has largely priced in known information; late reversals would require new tactical/roster surprises unlikely to emerge this late. Volume of $109k is moderate for a VCT esports match, suggesting this is being actively traded by informed players, not a thin/illiquid niche market subject to crowd panic. No viral social signals, upset narratives, or emotional crowd stories in briefing \u2014 single casual sentiment comment about ComeBack doesn't move the needle on market psychology. 58% probability for YES is modestly favorable but not overconfident; reflects that Gentle Mates' superior points are real but insufficient to eliminate NAVI's realistic path to victory in a Bo3 format.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.55, "rationale": "Gentle Mates holds 4 championship points (3-0 record) vs NAVI's 1 point (0-1 record) \u2014 championship points accumulate across the entire VCT stage and carry structural weight in seeding; a 3-0 team has demonstrated consistency against varying opponent compositions and strategical adaptations. Both teams are 1-1 in group stage with 3-3 maps, creating surface-level parity, but this masks Gentle Mates' broader tournament success; group stage records are snapshots within a longer round-robin. Market has risen +7.0pp over 7 days with three sharp +7.5pp, +7.5pp, +5.0pp moves (Apr 13, 14, 15), suggesting information flow favoring Gentle Mates (roster strength, scrim results, or recent match performance); NAVI's NO side rose only +3.0pp over 7 days despite being the underdog. BO3 format amplifies consistency advantages; teams with stronger read on meta, utility setups, and agent comps across three maps tend to convert tied records into wins; Gentle Mates' 3-0 suggests this advantage. NAVI (Ukrainian org with historical pedigree) provides narrative appeal to markets, but esports outcomes are driven by current roster form and scrim/bootcamp condition, not institutional brand; briefing contains dated reference ('I'm not a fan of ComeBack...') suggesting older/unreliable data sources. Match timing (TODAY, ~7 hours to resolution) means shares will soon reflect actual game outcome; current 57% YES reflects serious money backing Gentle Mates; late-stage repricing typically tracks data asymmetry favoring favorite. High volatility on YES (1.8pp/hr) vs low on NO (0.5pp/hr) indicates uncertain backing for Gentle Mates despite rising price \u2014 possible indicator of sharp action offset by public/retail interest, but 24-hour +6.0pp drop on YES (despite weekly rise) suggests late positioning uncertainty. Playoff seeding consequences make this high-stakes; a win moves Gentle Mates toward top-2 seeding, NAVI toward potential playoff exclusion if losses continue \u2014 this increases NAVI's desperation factor, but desperation does not alter mechanical skill or preparation quality. Confidence_no is lower (55 vs 72) because briefing lacks direct head-to-head history, recent scrim outcomes, or current roster health status for NAVI; only indirect signals (championship points, group records, market price action) support the YES case.", "key_factor": "Championship points (4 vs 1) reflect cumulative tournament performance across multiple matches, not just group stage record; Gentle Mates' 3-0 championship record vs NAVI's 0-1 suggests consistent execution across different opponents and map pools, a stronger predictor than tied group records alone."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.72, "confidence_no": 0.45, "rationale": "Championship points (4 vs 1) heavily favor Gentle Mates, but this creates a perception trap: GM has 'already clinched' playoff positioning while NAVI is in survival mode with maximum motivation. Identical group stage records (1-1, 3-3 maps) indicate parity in head-to-head form\u2014the championship points advantage may reflect easier early opponents, not current strength. Briefing contains no recent scrim results, player interview sentiment, or tactical innovation signals for either team\u2014unusually sparse for a match 7 hours away. Natus Vincere is a veteran org (explicit mention of pedigree); NAVI roster changes, meta familiarity, and clutch experience in elimination scenarios are unmeasured but material. Sharp market moves on Apr 13-15 (+7.5pp, +5.0pp for YES) suggest informed traders pricing in GM strength, but high 24-hr volatility (1.8pp/hr) and recent -6pp pullback indicate margin uncertainty and potential reversal risk. No VOD or performance detail provided for either team's most recent match; briefing is aggregated standings data, not live form analysis. Psychological factor: GM's 4-point lead may induce cautious play or tactical complacency; NAVI's 1-point deficit forces aggressive, prepared counter-strategies. BO3 format amplifies upset potential\u2014if NAVI secures Game 1 decisively, momentum and psychological edge can compound through Game 2/3. Briefing silence on role-specific matchups (IGL, duelist, sentinel meta shifts) suggests data gap; if a recent patch favored NAVI's agent pool, that signal is absent. Current price (57% YES) already reflects significant GM favor; if council consensus mirrors market consensus, black swan lies in tactical/mental factors not captured by aggregate points.", "key_factor": "Natus Vincere deploys a tactical innovation or map-pool counter-pick strategy that exploits Gentle Mates' recent lack of competitive pressure, or a key Gentle Mates player experiences unexpected underperformance due to psychological pressure in a must-win scenario."}], "final_score": 0.5738656770516901, "no_score": 0.42838614020103843, "edge": 0.125, "no_edge": 0.2749999999999999, "recommendation": "BUY YES", "confidence_level": "HIGH", "signal_type": "HIGH VALUE", "pass_reason": "", "expected_roi": 0.7391304347826089, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.7, "kelly_stake_full": 0.29411764705882354, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.14705882352941177, "kelly_multiplier": 0.5, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0632193053977828, "The Bull": 0.9488231424655758, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0510237036825305, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0690417217005483, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0631420166857992, "The Contrarian": 1.0690417217005483, "The Bear": 0.7357083883672151}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1942822", "question": "Valorant: Gentle Mates vs Natus Vincere (BO3) - VCT EMEA Group Alpha", "resolution_crit