{"run_id": "bf728b47-e062-4864-98b9-7da773afe51c", "timestamp": "2026-04-15T16:40:59.254443+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1935295", "question": "LoL: UCAM Esports Club vs Team Heretics Academy (BO3) - LES Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between UCAM Esports Club and Team Heretics Academy in the LES Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 15 at 2:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"UCAM Esports Club\" if UCAM Esports Club win the match against Team Heretics Academy.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Heretics Academy\" if Team Heretics Academy win the match against UCAM Esports Club.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-16T00:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-15T18:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.41, "volume_usd": 10501.419681000005, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["64571365250686013982153175448290787294093482021999198637587494343339468400709", "73891594615992418583402383766245961335135242111626527225095864985291156438811"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.43, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: UCAM Esports Club must win the BO3 match vs Team Heretics Academy in LES Regular Season on April 15, 2:00 PM ET. CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing provides Kick-off Tournament standings (Heretics 60% WR, UCAM 57% WR) but market explicitly references LES Regular Season match\u2014these are different tournaments with potentially different rosters, meta, and team form. WIN RATE ANALYSIS: Heretics leads 60% (3-2) vs UCAM 57% (4-3) in Kick-off Tournament data. Marginal edge to Heretics, but small sample sizes (5 and 7 games) limit confidence in extrapolation. RECENT UCAM PERFORMANCE: UCAM lost 2-1 to top-seeded Movistar KOI Fenix, showing competitive ability but also vulnerability to prepared opponents. This suggests UCAM is mid-tier caliber, not dominant. HEAD-TO-HEAD DATA: No direct match record between teams provided. Cannot assess historical tendencies or playstyle matchups. MARKET PRICE SIGNAL: YES (UCAM) at 41%, NO (Heretics) at 59%. Market implies ~59% confidence in Heretics winning\u2014slightly favoring Heretics but treating it as competitive. Price movement shows YES rising +7pp over 7 days, suggesting late confidence shift toward UCAM, but NO side still dominant. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT MISMATCH: Data freshness is from Kick-off Tournament (late Feb-early Apr). Regular Season match may feature different preparation, roster adjustments, meta shifts, or team form changes not reflected in provided data. COMPARATIVE METRICS: Game duration (UCAM 32:30 vs Heretics 33:09) and GDM (UCAM +152 vs Heretics +120) are nearly identical\u2014no clear strength/weakness separation evident. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong data supporting Heretics' marginal statistical edge in Kick-off Tournament. Weak data for NO side because (a) sample is small, (b) tournament context differs from Regular Season, (c) no recent head-to-head, (d) meta may have shifted. Confidence in both YES and NO reduced due to tournament mismatch and small sample sizes. PROBABILITY ESTIMATE: Heretics' 60% vs UCAM's 57% win rate suggests ~51-52% Heretics edge, but market is priced at 59% Heretics. Market may be overweighting Heretics' standing or reacting to other information. Given marginal statistical edge to Heretics, modest uncertainty from data gaps, and market pricing, assign 43% to UCAM (57% implied to Heretics), slightly lower than market price to reflect Heretics' consistent statistical lead. TIMING: Event is TODAY (~7 hours to match). No time for significant reversals. Match will almost certainly be played and resolved cleanly.", "key_factor": "Briefing data is from Kick-off Tournament (late Feb-early Apr), but market references LES Regular Season match\u2014competitive context, roster, and meta may differ significantly, making historical win rates potentially unreliable."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.72, "rationale": "FAVORED SIDE (NO) STRENGTHS: Heretics Academy holds a 60% win rate vs UCAM's 57% in the Kick-off Tournament standings\u2014a meaningful edge in a tournament format where execution and team synergy are paramount. With a 3-2 record in only 5 matches, Heretics has demonstrated consistent performance with higher conversion efficiency. HERETICS' EXECUTION ADVANTAGE: Heretics' GDM (+120) and game duration (33:09) profile shows controlled, methodical gameplay\u2014suggesting the team wins through superior macro play and teamfighting discipline, not volatility. This is a structural advantage in BO3 best-of formats where adaptation matters. UCAM'S VULNERABILITY EXPOSED: While UCAM pushed Movistar KOI Fenix to game 3, they ultimately lost 2-1 to the tournament leader (80% win rate). This loss, despite competitive individual performances, suggests UCAM struggles against teams with superior preparation and mid-game execution\u2014precisely the scenario Heretics now presents. SMALL SAMPLE CAVEAT: Both teams have played only 5-7 matches total. However, in such small samples, win rate becomes MORE meaningful, not less\u2014each game is a higher percentage of the overall trend. Heretics' 60% is a stronger signal than UCAM's 57% given the limited data. UNDERDOG CASE (YES) WEAKNESSES: UCAM's case rests on 'competitive against KOI' and 'more total wins (4 vs 3),' but the 4-win advantage comes from a larger match volume (7 vs 5 games) and actually represents identical win rates (57% vs 60%). This is a framing error; UCAM is statistically weaker, not stronger. META & ROSTER UNKNOWNS: The briefing provides no direct head-to-head history, no recent roster changes, and no meta shifts between Kick-off Tournament data and today's Regular Season match. This creates real uncertainty, but it cuts both ways\u2014it does NOT favor the underdog by default. MARKET MOMENTUM MISREADS THE SITUATION: YES side rose +7pp over one week despite having worse tournament fundamentals. This appears to be retail/contrarian buying (UCAM as underdog narrative) rather than informed re-evaluation. The sharp volatility on Apr 11 (+5.5pp/-7.5pp swings) suggests emotional trading, not data-driven repricing. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Confidence in NO is HIGHER (72) because Heretics' win rate advantage, match discipline metrics, and tournament execution are all transparent and point toward NO. Confidence in YES is LOWER (45) because the case for UCAM rests on intangible 'competitiveness' against KOI and underdog narrative momentum, neither of which override the 3pp win-rate gap. PROBABILITY CALIBRATION: 38 for YES reflects that the favorite (NO at 59%) is modestly underpriced. Heretics should trade closer to 62-65%, with UCAM at 35-38%. The current 59/41 split shows smart money has not fully capitalized on the win-rate advantage; retail momentum has artificially boosted YES. This is a NO-side value play.", "key_factor": "Team Heretics Academy's superior win rate (60% vs 57%) and cleaner tournament execution in a limited-sample competition favors the consistency narrative, despite UCAM's competitive showing against top opposition."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.46, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "MARKET MISPRICING: YES priced at 41% despite UCAM holding 4 wins vs Heretics' 3 wins in the same tournament window \u2014 UCAM has MORE absolute victories yet lower implied probability, suggesting potential undervaluation. WIN RATE ADVANTAGE OVERSTATED: Heretics' 60% vs UCAM's 57% is a marginal 3pp difference across only 5 and 7 games respectively \u2014 statistically insignificant and well within noise margin for small samples. UCAM'S COMPETITIVE PEDIGREE: Lost 2-1 to league leader Movistar KOI Fenix (80% win rate) \u2014 this is NOT a weakness but evidence UCAM can hang with elite teams and push deep into series, suggesting meta-read capability. GAME QUALITY METRICS FAVOR UCAM SLIGHTLY: UCAM's GDM of +152 vs Heretics' +120 indicates superior gold management; similar game duration (32:30 vs 33:09) shows UCAM doesn't get snowowed and plays methodical, controllable games. HERETICS INCONSISTENCY: 3-2 record means Heretics has already lost 2 matches \u2014 they are NOT dominant, and their win rate reflects volatility, not steady excellence. UCAM's 4-3 shows they grind wins consistently. NO DIRECT HEAD-TO-HEAD DATA: Briefing explicitly states no direct record between these teams available \u2014 market may be anchoring on win rates without matchup-specific factors that could heavily favor UCAM's playstyle. SMALL SAMPLE SIZE CUTS BOTH WAYS: With only 5-7 games each, neither team has established true strength; BO3 format rewards adaptability and series preparation, not single-game win rate metrics. MARKET MOMENTUM SUPPORTS YES: YES side rose +7.0pp over 7 days and +3.5pp in 24 hours (despite being underdog), suggesting informed money may be recognizing UCAM value as match approaches. HERETICS' CASE WEAKER THAN APPEARS: Higher win rate on fewer wins is mathematically inflated; no narrative about Heretics' recent form, meta adaptation, or roster strength provided in briefing. CONFESSION OF DATA GAPS: Briefing notes match date/roster/meta information missing \u2014 this asymmetric ignorance means probability should be closer to 50-50 than current market implies; UCAM's concrete statistical strengths (absolute wins, competitive GDM) deserve weight.", "key_factor": "UCAM's demonstrated ability to compete against top-tier opposition (Movistar KOI Fenix) and superior absolute win count (4 vs 3) despite lower win rate suggests the market undervalues their consistency and adaptability in BO3 formats."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.45, "confidence_yes": 0.52, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "TEAM STRENGTH COMPARISON: Heretics Academy holds 60% win rate vs UCAM's 57% \u2014 a narrow 3pp margin. Historically, this small gap predicts Heretics as slight favorite but does not justify strong confidence. SMALL SAMPLE SIZES: Both teams have played only 5-7 matches in available tournament data. Low match count inflates noise in win-rate estimates and reduces reliability of standings-based prediction. RECENT PERFORMANCE SIGNAL: UCAM lost 1-2 to top-ranked Movistar KOI Fenix, showing competitive play but not winning the series. This neither strongly favors nor disfavors UCAM vs mid-tier Heretics. HEAD-TO-HEAD DATA GAP: No direct match history provided between UCAM and Heretics Academy. Without prior matchup data, must rely on tournament standings alone \u2014 a weak signal. COMPARABLE METRICS: UCAM's GDM (+152) vs Heretics (+120) and game duration averages (32:30 vs 33:09) show similar macro execution. No decisive advantage visible in raw stats. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT SHIFT: Briefing notes this is LES Regular Season match, while standings data is from LES 2026 Kick-off Tournament. Meta, roster, and form may have shifted. Introduces additional uncertainty. MARKET PRICE ANALYSIS: Current market prices YES 41% / NO 59% align closely with the 3pp win-rate gap. Market appears efficiently priced; no obvious mispricing detected. VOLATILITY OBSERVATION: YES side rose +7.0pp over 7 days (rising trend) and +3.5pp in 24h, suggesting recent sentiment shift toward UCAM or late money recognizing value. However, volatility is modest (2.2pp/hr) and sharp moves on Apr 11 suggest event-driven noise, not fundamental shift. BASE RATE FOR CLOSE MATCHUPS: When two mid-tier esports teams with win rates separated by 2-4pp compete in a BO3, the higher-seeded team wins 55-60% of such matches historically. This implies ~40-45% for the underdog. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Strong confidence in YES estimate (52) reflects the narrow competitive gap and recent rising market sentiment. Confidence in NO is slightly lower (48) because the data gap (no head-to-head, small sample, tournament context shift) prevents ruling out a UCAM upset. Both are moderate because the matchup is genuinely close.", "key_factor": "In BO3 esports matches between similarly-ranked teams (win rates within 3-5pp), the higher-ranked team wins approximately 55-60% of the time; upset probability ~40-45%"}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.44, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.58, "rationale": "Market price (41% YES / 59% NO) closely mirrors underlying fundamentals: Heretics Academy has a 60% win rate vs UCAM's 57%, a narrow 3pp gap reflected in the ~18pp spread. YES side has risen +7pp over 7 days and +3.5pp in 24 hours, suggesting gradual confidence building in UCAM \u2014 potentially driven by their competitive showing vs top-ranked Movistar KOI (pushing to game 3) and slightly higher absolute win count (4-3 vs 3-2). NO side remains anchored at 59% despite being statistically favored, indicating market is NOT panicking into Heretics despite their higher win rate \u2014 this is disciplined, not emotional. Sharp volatility on Apr 11 (\u00b17-8pp swings) suggests information absorption or speculation, but current stability indicates consensus has settled. Critical data gap: No direct head-to-head record exists; briefing emphasizes small sample sizes (UCAM 7 total, Heretics 5 total matches). This uncertainty argues against extreme confidence on either side. Heretics' 60% win rate appears margin of victory rather than dominant superiority \u2014 comparable game durations (33:09 vs 32:30) and similar GDM (+120 vs +152) indicate evenly matched teams. Market is NOT overweighting UCAM's recent competitive loss to MKF (2-1) \u2014 the 41% YES price already factors in vulnerability. NO side at 59% is reasonable but not excessive confidence. Event timing (TODAY, ~7 hours to resolution) means no material new information will emerge; price movement henceforth reflects final sentiment crystallization, not fundamental revision. Rational apathy assessment: Market is correctly pricing a coin-flip-adjacent matchup (57% vs 60% win rates) with a modest 18pp NO premium. Neither side appears mispriced by >5pp. Probability_score of 44 (vs market 41%) reflects marginal underweight on Heretics in context of small sample sizes and UCAM's competitive strength vs top teams \u2014 a mild contrarian lean, not a major misprice.", "key_factor": "Rational"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.44, "confidence_yes": 0.62, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "Win rate comparison is misleading due to severe sample size disparity: Heretics Academy has only 5 games (3-2) vs UCAM's 7 games (4-3), making Heretics' 60% rate less statistically robust. UCAM's 2-1 loss to Movistar KOI Fenix (80% leader) is more informative than raw standings\u2014it shows they compete in close series against superior teams, indicating strong draft flexibility and mechanics under pressure. Game duration metrics are nearly identical (UCAM 32:30 vs Heretics 33:09), suggesting both teams play at similar pace and game control\u2014no decisive macro advantage evident. GDM (Gold Differential at 15min) strongly favors UCAM (+152 vs +120): this metric indicates superior early game execution and wave state management, critical in BO3 where series momentum and drafting strategy compounds. Heretics Academy's 3-2 record includes no information on opponent quality; UCAM's losses include a top-tier team, making their 4-3 record against potentially tougher competition more meaningful. BO3 format amplifies draft adaptation: teams that lose game 1 can pivot strategy in games 2-3. UCAM's recent experience doing exactly this (against MKF) is an asymmetric advantage. Market price history shows YES side rising +7.0pp over 7 days and +3.5pp in 24 hours, suggesting informed traders believe UCAM chances are being underpriced at 41%; this contradicts pure win-rate narrative. No direct head-to-head record exists; this is a genuine coin-flip matchup with high variance outcomes typical of regional academy-tier LoL where individual player skill expression determines series winner. Resolution occurs TODAY (~7 hours) with BO3 format taking 2-3 hours: market reflects real-time information closer to game time than historical data; confidence in NO is lower due to lack of recent Heretics-specific intel. Academy-level LoL exhibits higher variance than professional tier due to less standardized macro execution; both teams' metrics suggest 45-55% range is accurate, making 41% YES price potentially undervaluing UCAM's recent form.", "key_factor": "UCAM's recent loss to top-seed MKF (2-1) demonstrates meta-reading and draft vulnerability against prepared opponents, while Heretics Academy's limited sample size (5 games) makes their 60% win rate statistically unreliable for prediction in BO3 format where adaptation matters."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.44, "confidence_yes": 0.52, "confidence_no": 0.48, "rationale": "UCAM just lost 2-1 to Movistar KOI Fenix (80% win rate team) \u2014 this high-stress loss against a dominant squad may have induced psychological fatigue or exposed draft weaknesses that Heretics can exploit with preparation time. Heretics Academy's 60% win rate is built on only 5 total games; UCAM's 57% on 7 games. Win-rate delta is marginal (3pp) and within noise \u2014 neither team has decisive sample size dominance. Briefing provides NO direct head-to-head record between UCAM and Heretics. Market price (59% NO) may be anchoring to seeding/standings alone without accounting for stylistic matchups or recent form trajectory. UCAM's GDM (+152) vs Heretics (+120) suggests UCAM scales better into late game, but if Heretics can win early/mid and close out before UCAM's scaling, the meta-mismatch flips the series. NO DATA on player injuries, roster changes, or meta patches between Kick-off Tournament (data source) and today's Regular Season match \u2014 academy teams often rotate squad depth, and a key starter benching on either side would dramatically shift odds. Heretics Academy's designation as 'academy' may mask competitive hunger; academy rosters sometimes outperform seeding when facing larger-org players (psychological underdog edge). Market has seen significant volatility (Apr 11: \u00b18pp swings), suggesting information asymmetry or late-breaking roster/tactical changes not reflected in the briefing's static standings. The 3.5pp YES rise in last 24 hours contradicts the NO consensus, hinting that live-action traders may have spotted a catalyst (coaching adjustment, scrim result, or meta read) invisible to the provided data. UCAM's recent loss to MKF included a 1-2 series (not a clean stomp), proving UCAM can win games against elite teams \u2014 Heretics is tier-2, not tier-1, making UCAM competitive here. Small match volume ($10.5k) means liquidity is thin; prices may be set by a handful of traders with asymmetric information rather than true consensus, creating mispricings on either side.", "key_factor": "Team Heretics Academy's academy-level roster exploitation of UCAM's recent high-stress losses against top competition, combined with a possible meta-shift favoring controlled, macro-heavy gameplay over mechanical execution."}], "final_score": 0.4348880114804434, "no_score": 0.5697854190199797, "edge": 0.29, "no_edge": 0.10999999999999988, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "MEDIUM", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 57% for NO (need \u226557%); NO-side confidence too low: 50% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.7, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0632193053977828, "The Bull": 0.9488231424655758, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0510237036825305, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0690417217005483, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0631420166857992, "The Contrarian": 1.0690417217005483, "The Bear": 0.7357083883672151}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1935295", "question": "LoL: UCAM Esports Club vs Team Heretics Academy (BO3) - LES Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between UCAM Esports Club and Team Heretics Academy in the LES Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 15 at 2:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"UCAM Esports Club\" if UCAM Esports Club win the match against Team Heretics Academy.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Team Heretics Academy\" if Team Heretics Academy win the match against UCAM Esports Club.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-16T00:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-15T18:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.41, "volume_usd": 10501.419681000005, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["64571365250686013982153175448290787294093482021999198637587494343339468