n the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-16T02:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-15T20:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.36, "volume_usd": 490.1210609999999, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["111020650431490990331980630874939833298519672504473954425422406027480449924150", "39668325464352330771334666735108863939224405215974936582604879210304236407947"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.36, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "CONDITION TO RESOLVE: Winthrop University wins a BO3 League of Legends match against Supernova in NAC Regular Season (scheduled April 15, 4:00 PM ET). CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains only fragmented collegiate esports data (Marvel Rivals, VALORANT, Rocket League, general NCAA structure) with no substantive information about the specific LoL matchup, either team's roster, or their competitive records in NAC. TEAM IDENTITY UNCERTAINTY: Search results reference 'Georgia Tech Gold vs Winthrop 3:2' but explicitly note this is a Marvel Rivals match, not LoL. No LoL-specific Winthrop data is provided. Supernova is not mentioned anywhere in the briefing. MARKET SIGNAL ANALYSIS: Current market pricing (YES 36% / NO 64%) suggests informed traders have assessed asymmetric conviction, but this briefing provides zero data to validate or contest that signal. VOLATILE PRICE HISTORY: Sharp swings (\u00b118pp on Apr 13, \u00b111.5pp on Apr 14) indicate trader uncertainty and possible information events unknown to this analysis. Recent +4pp rebound in YES over 24h suggests modest late confidence shift toward Winthrop, but source is opaque. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: Match timing (April 15, 4:00 PM ET \u2248 TODAY in briefing timeline) means outcome will be determined within hours. No ambiguity in resolution criteria if match completes normally. gol.gg is specified as primary source with 2-hour fallback to credible reporting\u2014both are standard and reliable. INABILITY TO ASSESS BOTH SIDES: No roster strength data, recent win-loss records, head-to-head history, or meta compatibility information for either Winthrop or Supernova in League of Legends. Cannot differentiate win probability between competitors. ASYMMETRIC CONFIDENCE: Market price (36/64) and volatile history suggest SOME traders have information. Absence of that data in this briefing means confidence in both YES and NO estimates must remain very low (\u226425). FINAL PROBABILITY: Aligning probability_score to current market midpoint (36%) acknowledges market consensus signal in absence of independent data validation. This is a passive calibration to market price, not a confident forecast.", "key_factor": "Briefing document contains no actionable intelligence on either team's LoL roster, recent form, head-to-head record, or competitive standing in NAC; team identities cannot be verified against official sources."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.64, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "MARKET STRUCTURE: NO is priced at 64% (favored) vs YES at 36% (underdog). As the Bull advocate for the favored side, I am arguing Supernova wins this BO3. MOMENTUM ANALYSIS: The 7-day trend shows NO rising +15pp (strongest directional signal in the briefing), while YES has fallen -15pp. This represents a consistent shift in belief toward Supernova over the past week. PRICE STABILITY: NO side shows higher recent volatility (1.4pp/hr vs 0.6pp/hr for YES) but the net 7-day movement is unidirectional upward, suggesting informed traders are moving toward Supernova despite daily noise. SHARP MOVES INTERPRETATION: Apr 13's -18pp move on YES (followed by +18pp on NO) and Apr 14's oscillations suggest event-driven repricing. The most recent net shift from Apr 13\u201314 left NO higher, indicating the correction favored Supernova. DATA GAPS ARE SYMMETRIC: The briefing contains NO specific roster, recent win-loss records, or head-to-head history for either team. This symmetry means the market price differential (64% vs 36%) cannot be explained by public information in the briefing alone. IMPLICATION OF SYMMETRIC DATA GAP: When data is absent for both sides equally, the market price becomes the primary signal. The 28pp spread strongly suggests professional bettors or early information moved the line toward Supernova. WINTHROP DATA CONTAMINATION: Available Winthrop data is from Marvel Rivals (Georgia Tech Gold vs Winthrop 3:2 at Alienware Clash 2026), not League of Legends. This confirms the briefing has no clean LoL form data for either team. TIMING PRESSURE: Event is TODAY (resolves in ~9 hours). With no new public information breaking in the briefing, the market had ~7 days to price in team quality. The consistent drift toward NO suggests embedded information or scout reports favored Supernova. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS FRAMING: Winthrop (YES) has experienced a 15pp erosion of support over 7 days with no counter-catalyst listed in the briefing. Absence of bullish news for an underdog reinforces the market move. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: confidence_yes = 28 and confidence_no = 32 both remain LOW because the briefing contains zero actionable team data (rosters, head-to-head, recent LoL results). Neither side can be evaluated on merit. However, NO's confidence is marginally higher because 7-day price momentum is an observable market signal that points to Supernova, even if the underlying reason is opaque. BULL CASE FOR NO: The market has voted with its feet over a full week. Professional liability suggests this 64% price reflects either superior team strength in Supernova, recent roster changes favoring them, or scout feedback. The consistency of the +15pp trend (despite volatility) is the strongest evidence in an information vacuum. WHY NOT HIGHER FOR NO: The 28pp spread is justified partly by data scarcity. A BO3 can flip on execution, map pool, and draft. Winthrop is not priced below 36%, meaning the market retains ~1-in-3 belief they can take the series. Without roster details, I cannot dismiss Winthrop entirely. MARKET EFFICIENCY CHECK: The 64-36 split with symmetric missing data suggests the line is stable and internalized by traders. No sharp moves in the last 4 hours (24-hour change: YES +4pp, NO -4pp) indicate the market has settled post-information-cascade.", "key_factor": "Market consensus and 7-day momentum favor NO (Supernova), with NO side rising +15pp over the week despite high volatility and insufficient team-level data."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing contains zero concrete League of Legends match results, roster information, or head-to-head records for either Winthrop or Supernova in the NAC. All available esports data references Marvel Rivals or different tournaments entirely. MARKET PRICING WITHOUT FOUNDATION: YES side has fallen 15pp over 7 days and NO has risen 15pp, yet the briefing provides NO evidentiary basis for this directional shift. This suggests the market is pricing based on speculation, hearsay, or off-chain consensus rather than published performance data. VOLATILE TRADING PATTERN: Sharp moves of \u00b118pp (Apr 13) and \u00b111.5pp (Apr 14) indicate high uncertainty and low conviction among traders. With $490 total volume and 9 hours to resolution, this is a thin, speculative market. WINTHROP'S HIDDEN CASE: Winthrop appears in esports results (Georgia Tech Gold match), indicating active competitive participation in collegiate circuit. If Winthrop has been competing in B-Tier and C-Tier tournaments recently with measurable results, there may be unpublished performance trends favoring them that market hasn't factored in. SUPERNOVA'S OPACITY: Supernova receives no mentions in the briefing data whatsoever. The absence of any results, roster info, or tournament history makes it impossible to assess their recent form, team stability, or competitive trajectory. Betting 64% on an entirely data-dark opponent is speculative. UNDERDOG VALUATION CHECK: At 36%, Winthrop is moderately underpriced if both teams are equally mysterious. A true coin-flip market with no predictive data would price at ~50%. The 14pp discount suggests market has real (off-chain) conviction toward Supernova, but that conviction is not substantiated in this briefing. BO3 FORMAT ADVANTAGE: Best-of-3 reduces variance compared to single-game formats. If Winthrop has any structural matchup advantage (draft, playstyle, regional meta), a 3-game series gives more opportunity to exploit it than a one-off match. RECENCY & MOMENTUM: 24-hour movement favored YES (+4pp) while 7-day trend favored NO (-15pp). This divergence suggests recent information may have supported Winthrop, but earlier information (stale or speculative) had favored Supernova. Weigh recent micro-signals carefully. RESOLUTION RISK MITIGATION: Match is TODAY (9 hours). Forfeit/cancellation resolves to 50-50, but no evidence in briefing suggests this risk is elevated. Assume match plays as scheduled. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: confidence_yes and confidence_no are both LOW (28 and 26 respectively) because the briefing contains insufficient data on either team. We cannot reliably assess Winthrop's actual competitive strength or Supernova's weaknesses. The probability_score of 38 reflects a modest lean toward YES (underdog) based on market repricing volatility and data scarcity favoring the discount side, but this is a genuine data-starved call. UNDERDOG THESIS: If the market has priced Winthrop down to 36% on speculative consensus alone, and both teams are equally opaque in published records, Winthrop may be underpriced by 8\u201312pp relative to a true 45\u201350% fair value. A modest YES lean is justified by data scarcity rather than fundamental strength.", "key_factor": "Severe data scarcity on both teams means market pricing may reflect speculative consensus rather than fundamental competitive analysis, creating potential for Winthrop to outperform a 36% underdog valuation."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.36, "confidence_yes": 0.22, "confidence_no": 0.21, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains no substantive information about either team's recent LoL performance, roster composition, or head-to-head record. The 'KEY FACTS' section contains garbled roster/region data unrelated to LoL (appears to be Valorant or other esports), making it unusable for analysis. Search results reference a Georgia Tech vs Winthrop match, but it was Marvel Rivals (not LoL), making it irrelevant to this market. No NAC (North American Challengers League) specific information was provided in the briefing. MARKET PRICE ANALYSIS: YES side currently at 36%, NO side at 64%. The spread suggests modest confidence in Supernova, but this is NOT anchored to fundamental team strength data. PRICE TREND: YES side fell 15.0pp over 7 days (strong downward pressure on Winthrop), with 24h volatility of 0.6pp/hr. NO side rose 15.0pp (consistent movement toward Supernova). This suggests market participants have information favoring Supernova, but without access to that information, cannot validate it. SHARP MOVES detected (\u00b118.0pp on Apr 13, \u00b111.5pp on Apr 14) suggest informed trading or news events, but no details provided in briefing. EVENT TIMING: TODAY (~9 hours to resolution). At this late stage, major reversals are unlikely without extraordinary events. Current market price likely reflects late-arriving information unavailable in this briefing. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Cannot independently assess either team's strength. The market's downward drift toward NO (Supernova) suggests information favoring Supernova exists but is not documented here. Confidence in both YES and NO must remain low due to data insufficiency. DUAL-PERSPECTIVE: Without team data, neither side can be strongly justified. Market participants appear to favor Supernova, but this confidence is not shared in the briefing, making it impossible to validate or refute. RESOLUTION: Setting probability_score to 36 (current market YES price) reflects market consensus in the absence of independent analytical foundation. Both confidence scores set to 22 due to complete lack of verifiable team performance data in briefing.", "key_factor": "Collegiate LoL match outcomes in NA Challengers League are unpredictable without team-specific performance data; base rate is ~50% for any given matchup when no comparative strength data exists."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.36, "confidence_yes": 0.22, "confidence_no": 0.23, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains NO actionable information about either Winthrop or Supernova's LoL capabilities, recent form, rosters, or head-to-head records. Search results conflate Marvel Rivals tournament data (Georgia Tech vs Winthrop) with League of Legends \u2014 irrelevant to this LoL market. Current market price of 36% YES / 64% NO reflects confidence in Supernova, but this confidence is UNSUPPORTED by any LoL-specific evidence in the briefing. Market shows extreme volatility (sharp -18pp and +11.5pp swings Apr 13-14) despite zero new information \u2014 suggests emotion-driven trading rather than skill-based assessment. 7-day trend (YES down 15pp, NO up 15pp) indicates sustained selling pressure on Winthrop, but briefing provides no rationale for this directional move. LOW VOLUME ($490 USD) and small data points (23 YES, 13 NO) suggest thin liquidity and high sensitivity to noise trades. Scheduled match time is TODAY at 4:00 PM ET (~9 hours from briefing timestamp 16:41 UTC on Apr 15) \u2014 no pre-match updates or expert analysis available. Both sides suffer equally from information vacuum: confidence_yes and confidence_no are both set to ~22 because neither team's actual strength can be evaluated. Market is pricing in a 64% Supernova win, but this appears to be CROWD CONSENSUS in absence of data rather than rational assessment. POSSIBLE SCENARIO: Market may be reflecting unobserved community knowledge (Reddit, Discord) about NAC standings, but this is not present in the briefing. RATIONAL APATHY DETECTION: If briefing had included roster comparisons, recent match results, or tournament standings, current price (36%) would be meaningfully defensible. Instead, price appears arbitrary. Probability_score remains at 36 (matching market price) because without data, any deviation would be pure speculation; however, confidence scores are deliberately LOW to signal that this probability is NOT evidence-based.", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.36, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "DATA INTEGRITY FAILURE: The briefing conflates multiple esports titles (Marvel Rivals, VALORANT, Rocket League, OW2) with LoL references; the only Winthrop data point is a Marvel Rivals 3:2 loss to Georgia Tech Gold, not LoL. ZERO MATCH INTELLIGENCE: No head-to-head records, recent LoL match results, roster compositions, or performance metrics for either Winthrop or Supernova in the NAC are provided. MARKET PRICE SIGNAL ASYMMETRY: The market has moved sharply (YES fell 15.0pp over 7 days, currently 36%) suggesting informed traders have conviction toward Supernova, but without data access to justifying information. VOLATILITY PATTERN: Sharp 18pp swings on Apr 13-14 indicate information events (likely match results or roster news) that are not documented in this briefing, creating an information gap. EVENT TIMING RISK: Match scheduled for April 15 4:00PM ET (~9 hours at briefing time); high-confidence predictions require team meta knowledge, draft tendencies, and recent scrim/boot camp data unavailable here. COLLEGIATE LoL CONTEXT ABSENCE: No tournament structure, seeding, or playoff implications provided; unclear if this is regular season play or playoff push, affecting team motivation and resource allocation. CONFIDENCE PENALTY: Both confidence scores held at 25 due to severe asymmetric data quality\u2014market pricing suggests informed NO conviction, but briefing contains no data to validate either side. BASELINE PROBABILITY: At 36% YES, market implies ~64% Supernova win probability; this aligns with NO-side trader conviction, but lacks evidentiary support in briefing for either outcome.", "key_factor": "The briefing document contains severely corrupted or mismatched data (Marvel Rivals results, VALORANT tournaments, Rocket League references, and collegiate athletic conference structures) with zero actionable League of Legends match intelligence for either team, rendering technical analysis of roster composition, patch-state meta alignment, or recent competitive form impossible."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.32, "confidence_yes": 0.22, "confidence_no": 0.24, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains zero LoL-specific information about either team\u2014no rosters, recent form, head-to-head records, or NAC standings. All references are to Marvel Rivals or other esports, creating information asymmetry that masks true competitive gap. MARKET SIGNAL CONTRADICTION: YES price has fallen 15pp over 7 days (sharp -18pp drop Apr 13) despite +4pp recovery in last 24h. This suggests informed traders have accumulated negative Winthrop intelligence post-initial pricing, but briefing provides no public justification\u2014possible hidden roster/coaching intel. TIMING PRESSURE: Event resolves TODAY in ~9 hours. A last-minute player absence (illness, emergency, or substitute requirement) is plausible for a collegiate match and could trigger immediate coordination collapse in a BO3 against an organized opponent. Such changes often break timing in champion select and early game macro. COLLEGIATE LoL FRAGILITY: University rosters are younger, less stable, and more vulnerable to external shocks than pro teams. Supernova (unknown history in briefing) may operate with more stable personnel or recent roster reinforcements not visible in search results. ABSENCE-OF-SIGNAL: Briefing's NEWS SUMMARY explicitly notes 'no direct information about team rosters, recent form, or head-to-head records.' This silence is itself a yellow flag\u2014if Winthrop were dominant, recent tournament wins would surface. Lack of positive coverage + falling odds = underdog weakness, not market mispricing. BO3 VARIANCE: Best-of-3 format amplifies early-game execution and champion pool depth. If Winthrop has narrow meta comfort or weak mid-lane/jungle synergy, Supernova can pivot draft strategy across three games\u2014variance favors the team with more adaptable playbook. ADMINISTRATIVE RISK (tertiary): Resolution criteria permit 50-50 tie if match delayed >7 days without winner. A server issue or schedule collision in Challengers League could push resolution beyond April 22, though low probability. CONTRARIAN PIVOT: Market consensus (64% NO) reflects informed traders' belief in Supernova, but with zero public data on either team, this is based on silent intelligence, not transparent performance metrics. The consensus is robust precisely because briefing is silent\u2014true black swan would require hidden Winthrop vulnerability (injury, internal conflict, meta mismatch) that emerges in draft/early game.", "key_factor": "Last-minute roster substitution or player illness at Winthrop creates coordination gaps that Supernova exploits in a high-pressure BO3 format, or administrative/technical delay pushes match beyond resolution window."}], "final_score": 0.40053120108496376, "no_score": 0.5950899465046217, "edge": 0.33999999999999997, "no_edge": 0.05999999999999994, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "NO-side confidence too low: 25% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.7, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0632193053977828, "The Bull": 0.9488231424655758, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0510237036825305, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0690417217005483, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0631420166857992, "The Contrarian": 1.0690417217005483, "The Bear": 0.7357083883672151}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1949736", "question": "LoL: Winthrop University vs Supernova (BO3) - North American Challengers League Regular Season", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL match between Winthrop University and Supernova in the North American Challengers League Regular Season, initially scheduled for April 15 at 4:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Winthrop University\" if Winthrop University win the match against Supernova.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Supernova\" if Supernova win the match against Winthrop University.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-16T02:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-15T20:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.36, "volume_usd": 490.1210609999999, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["111020650431490990331980630874939833298519672504473954425422406027480449924150", "39668325464352330771334666735108863939224405215974936582604879210304236407947"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "key_facts": ["Duelist (DPS)\")\nUnited States\nDuelist (DPS)\")\nUnited States\nVanguard (Tank)\")\nUnited States\nVanguard (Tank)\")\nUnited States\nStrategist (Support)\")\nUnited States\nStrategist (Support)\")\nUnited States\n\nDuelist (DPS)\")\nUnited States\nDuelist (DPS)\")\nUnited States\nVanguard (Tank)\")\nUnited States\nVanguard (Tank)\")\nUnited States\nStrategist (Support)\")\nUnited States\nStrategist (Support)\")\nUnited States\nUnited States\n\nDuelist (DPS)\")\nUnited States\nDuelist (DPS)\")\nUnited States\nVanguard (Tank)\")\nUnited States\nVanguard (Tank)\")\nUnited States\nStrategist (Support)\")\nUnited States\nStrategist (Support)\")\nUnited States\nUnited States [...] Duelist (DPS)\")\nUnited States\nDuelist (DPS)\")\nLebanon\nVanguard (Tank)\")\nSpain\nVanguard (Tank)\")\nUnited States\nStrategist (Support)\")\nIndonesia\nStrategist