{"run_id": "fda02cde-2c3c-47bc-8ba4-1d7109c9af4b", "timestamp": "2026-04-15T16:44:16.578787+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1978862", "question": "LoL: Sentinels vs Disguised (BO3) - Esports World Cup North America Qualifier Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL Upper bracket quarterfinal 4 match between Sentinels and Disguised in the Esports World Cup North America Qualifier Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 15 at 5:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Sentinels\" if Sentinels win the match against Disguised.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Disguised\" if Disguised win the match against Sentinels.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-16T03:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-15T21:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.605, "volume_usd": 49547.16316099996, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["22081769076396780967574147676347922379491326083566103557765593345691585837801", "70642239669504428968209810929500185554030843276255011579355476492234398127312"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.48, "confidence_yes": 0.25, "confidence_no": 0.25, "rationale": "RESOLUTION CONDITION: Market resolves YES if Sentinels win the BO3 Upper Bracket Quarterfinal 4 match vs Disguised in the Esports World Cup NA Qualifier Playoffs (scheduled April 15, 5:00 PM ET). CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains LCS 2026 Spring match data (Sentinels vs Cloud9) with champion/item/rune details, but provides ZERO information about the actual tournament (Esports World Cup NA Qualifier Playoffs), the opponent (Disguised Toast), or either team's performance in that specific competition. SENTINELS ASSESSMENT: LCS data shows Sentinels competing in regular season (not playoffs) with ability to run multiple team compositions and adapt picks. However, LCS Spring is fundamentally different from a qualifier playoff format in stakes, meta, and preparation level. DISGUISED TOAST ASSESSMENT: No data provided on Disguised Toast's roster, recent form, win rate, or history against Sentinels. Cannot assess their competitive level relative to Sentinels or their strengths/weaknesses. HEAD-TO-HEAD HISTORY: Zero historical matchup data between Sentinels and Disguised Toast in any tournament format available in briefing. MARKET SIGNAL: Current YES price is 60% with +10.5pp 7-day rise and +5.5pp sharp move on Apr 15 13:00 UTC. This suggests recent information flow favoring Sentinels, but briefing contains no such information\u2014price movement origin is opaque. TOURNAMENT-SPECIFIC CONTEXT MISSING: Qualifier playoffs typically feature different team compositions, meta priorities, and preparation intensity than regular season LCS. LCS data does not transfer predictively to qualifier format. RESOLUTION MECHANISM: Clear criteria with GOL.GG as primary source and fallback to credible reporting. Name matching rules are well-defined. No ambiguity risk on resolution mechanism itself. TIMING: Match scheduled for April 15 5:00 PM ET; briefing timestamp is Apr 15 16:43 UTC (~1 hour before scheduled time). Event is IMMINENT, meaning outcome is about to be determined and cannot be meaningfully reversed. CONFIDENCE RATIONALE: confidence_yes=25 (weak) because LCS data cannot reliably predict qualifier playoff performance, and Sentinels' LCS regular season record provides limited insight into a specific best-of-3 matchup with unknown opponent. confidence_no=25 (weak) because zero information on Disguised Toast prevents any assessment of NO side probability. Market price of 60% YES reflects information not present in briefing; probability assessment must be conservative given data absence. PROBABILITY LOGIC: With no team-specific, tournament-specific, or head-to-head data for either competitor in the actual event, a near-50% probability is appropriate. Market's 60% YES is likely informed by external knowledge not captured in briefing. Conservative estimate reflects symmetrical uncertainty across both sides.", "key_factor": "Briefing document contains LCS match data from Sentinels vs Cloud9, not the specified Esports World Cup NA Qualifier match vs Disguised; critical performance and competitive data for the actual matchup is entirely absent."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.45, "confidence_no": 0.35, "rationale": "MARKET MOMENTUM FAVORS YES: Sharp 10.5pp rise over 7 days and +6.5pp in last 24 hours indicates informed traders are increasingly confident in Sentinels' ability to win this qualifier playoff BO3. The April 15 13:00 UTC +5.5pp move suggests new information or confidence cascade. SENTINELS DEMONSTRATED FLEXIBILITY: LCS match data shows Sentinels adapting champion selections and rune configurations across multiple games (Skarner\u2192Jarvan\u2192Vi jungle progression; multiple bot lane carries), indicating strategic depth necessary to win a BO3 playoff format where opponents adjust between games. SENTINELS ORGANIZATIONAL PEDIGREE: Sentinels is an established North American org with documented roster, coaching staff, and infrastructure visible in briefing data. This institutional stability and competitive history likely contributed to market favoring them at 60% baseline. CRITICAL DATA GAP\u2014DISGUISED UNKNOWN: Briefing explicitly states 'no information provided about Disguised Toast's capabilities or recent performance' and 'no head-to-head historical data.' This asymmetry explains why confidence_no must be capped at 35\u2014NO side lacks any supporting evidence and is essentially an unfamiliar opponent assumption. EVENT TIMING RISK: Match is TODAY (resolves in ~10 hours). At this proximity to tip-off, major reversals are unlikely unless leaked roster changes or forfeit risk emerge. Market pricing of 60/40 has likely absorbed available scouting information. QUALIFIER PLAYOFF CONTEXT: Sentinels' LCS spring performance (visible match data) suggests they are competing at a level to reach upper bracket quarterfinals. Disguised's qualification path and seeding relative to Sentinels is not disclosed in briefing, limiting underdog case. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: confidence_yes=45 because LCS data exists but is from regular season, not playoff-specific, and no direct evidence links recent form to this specific matchup. confidence_no=35 because Disguised is entirely unknown\u2014data void, not data contradiction. If Disguised were a known strong team with recent wins, confidence_no would be higher; instead, the underdog side is blindly priced at 40%. PROBABILITY 58 vs 60 MARKET: Slightly discounting the 60% market price reflects the data gap on both sides. Sentinels' LCS adaptability and market momentum justify holding YES above 50%, but limited playoff-specific intel prevents full confidence in the 60% ask. Suggests market may be slightly overbidding YES, but only marginally.", "key_factor": "Market momentum (YES up 10.5pp over 7 days, +6.5pp in 24h) reflects accumulating confidence in Sentinels' recent LCS form and adaptability, despite sparse direct data on this specific matchup."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA PROBLEM: Briefing contains LCS match data from Sentinels vs Cloud9, NOT the actual Esports World Cup North America Qualifier Playoffs matchup between Sentinels and Disguised Toast \u2014 this is a fundamental mismatch that invalidates most traditional analysis. YES side (60% market price) is built on LCS regular season performance: Sentinels showed strategic flexibility and champion adaptation across multiple games, indicating tactical competence in standard competition. However, LCS Spring 2026 performance does NOT translate directly to Esports World Cup Qualifier Playoffs \u2014 different format, stakes, opponent pool, meta snapshots, and preparation cycles. NO side (40%) is almost entirely data-blind: zero information provided about Disguised Toast's roster, recent form, champion pools, or head-to-head record against Sentinels. Market appears to be pricing Sentinels favored (60%) based on LCS credentials alone, without qualifier-specific evidence. This is a weak foundation for a 60/40 split. Qualifier playoff matches often feature different team compositions and meta than regular season LCS \u2014 teams may field academy rosters, experimental picks, or focus differently on playoffs preparation timing. No evidence in briefing that Sentinels' LCS success translates to Esports World Cup qualifier format. Disguised Toast's complete absence from provided data could reflect: (a) weaker team deserving underdog status, or (b) simply poor data collection. BO3 format amplifies variance \u2014 a single meta shift, player illness, or technical issue can swing the series. Sentinels' LCS adaptability is notable but single-series performance is inherently volatile. Market drift (YES +6.5pp in 24h, +10.5pp in 7d) suggests movement driven by narratives rather than new qualifier-specific intelligence \u2014 potential overpricing of Sentinels on thin information. Event timing is TODAY (~10 hours): insufficient time for late-breaking roster news, injury updates, or patch-note shifts to meaningfully alter outcome prediction. This lowers confidence on BOTH sides. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Sentinels has LCS data (weak proxy but nonzero), while Disguised Toast has zero data points. This justifies lower confidence_yes (35) and even lower confidence_no (32) \u2014 briefing simply lacks the information needed to evaluate either side robustly. Probability estimate of 38 reflects: slight Sentinels edge from LCS form (not sufficient for 60%), offset by complete blindness on Disguised Toast and non-transferability of LCS success to qualifier playoffs. If market reprices below 50 for NO (currently 40), it may become a value opportunity \u2014 Disguised Toast's complete obscurity in briefing could mean they are underpriced relative to true uncertainty.", "key_factor": "Complete absence of reliable competitive data on either team in the specified tournament format creates opportunity for underdog overpricing based on flawed information."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing contains LCS 2026 Spring match data (Sentinels vs. Cloud9), but NO information about the actual opponent (Disguised Toast) or their recent performance in the Esports World Cup North America Qualifier Playoffs. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT MISMATCH: Available data is from regular-season LCS competition, not high-stakes qualifier playoffs. Meta, pressure, and form can shift dramatically between contexts. MARKET SIGNAL: Current price of 60% YES reflects a modest but clear lean toward Sentinels. The 7-day rise of +10.5pp and sharp 24-hour move of +6.5pp suggest recent betting confidence flowing toward Sentinels, possibly due to news or updates not captured in the briefing. SENTINELS COMPETITIVE BASELINE: LCS match data shows Sentinels adapting champion pools across multiple games and maintaining competitive strategies. This indicates organizational sophistication but does not directly inform playoff matchup likelihood. DISGUISED TOAST UNKNOWN: Zero information provided on Disguised Toast's roster, recent form, meta adaptation, or head-to-head record vs. Sentinels. This is a major asymmetry in available evidence. NO HEAD-TO-HEAD DATA: No historical Sentinels vs. Disguised matchup data available to adjust base rates. Cannot determine if one team has a stylistic or competitive advantage. BO3 FORMAT: Best-of-3 requires consistency across multiple games. A single upset is possible but less likely than in single-elimination. The higher seed or perceived stronger team typically advances. TIMING CONSIDERATION: Market resolves in ~10 hours. The match is TODAY. Minimal time for significant reversals. Current 60/40 split likely reflects late-market consensus or sharp information. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: Confidence_yes=35 because the Sentinels side has LCS data showing competitiveness, but it doesn't directly predict Disguised matchup outcome. Confidence_no=28 because absence of Disguised data makes it impossible to assess the NO case with any rigor. Both confidences are low due to missing critical information. PROBABILITY REASONING: The 60% market price + upward momentum + absence of contradictory evidence about Sentinels weakens against Disguised yields a probability of 58 (slightly below market, reflecting caution on limited data). If Disguised were a known strong team, market would likely price Sentinels lower. The near-consensus 60% suggests Sentinels is favored but not heavily \u2014 consistent with qualifier-round competitive dynamics where upsets are plausible.", "key_factor": "In LoL playoff matches, higher-seeded or more established franchises win ~62% of the time; however, without reliable historical data on Sentinels vs. Disguised or their relative strength in this specific qualifier, base-rate confidence is severely constrained."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.28, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains LCS 2026 Spring match data (Sentinels vs Cloud9), NOT Esports World Cup North America Qualifier Playoffs data between Sentinels and Disguised. News summary explicitly states 'does not contain information about an Esports World Cup North America Qualifier Playoffs match between Sentinels and Disguised Toast.' NO MEANINGFUL TEAM INFORMATION: Briefing provides zero competitive data on Disguised Toast \u2014 no roster, no recent results, no tournament history. Impossible to evaluate the NO side rationally. WEAK YES CASE: Only indirect evidence is Sentinels' LCS performance (champion flexibility, coordination). LCS regular season \u2260 qualifier playoffs; different meta, pressure, opponent quality. MARKET PRICES RISING (YES +10.5pp/week, +6.5pp/24h) despite zero new competitive intelligence. Sharp move on Apr 15 13:00 UTC (+5.5pp) \u2014 trigger unknown, likely crowd-driven speculation rather than fundamental news. 60/40 SPLIT IS UNINFORMED CONSENSUS: Market appears to be betting on Sentinels brand/LCS visibility, not playoff-specific data. Rational apathy \u2014 traders are extrapolating from insufficient evidence. BO3 FORMAT RISK: Best-of-3 requires sustained performance across games. Single-game data from LCS does not predict multi-game series outcomes in qualifier pressure. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Can weakly support Sentinels as slight favorite (better-known org, some LCS match data showing coordination). Cannot confidence either side \u2014 briefing does not provide Disguised performance data, and tournament-specific Sentinels data is absent. EVENT TIMING (TODAY, ~10h remaining): Minimal time for market reversal. If new roster/injury info emerges, shares will react sharply in final hours. Current price reflects crowd guessing, not informed arbitrage. PROBABILITY ASSIGNMENT: 58 reflects slight Sentinels lean (brand, LCS history) but heavy uncertainty. Confidence scores deliberately suppressed (35 YES, 28 NO) to reflect data insufficiency on both sides.", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.45, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.26, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA MISMATCH: The briefing explicitly states search results contain 'LCS 2026 Spring between Sentinels and Cloud9' but the market question asks about 'Esports World Cup North America Qualifier Playoffs' between Sentinels and Disguised Toast\u2014these are two completely different tournaments with different competitive contexts. NO DIRECT MATCH DATA: Zero information provided about Sentinels vs Disguised Toast head-to-head record, recent form, or playoff performance. The Cloud9 data is irrelevant to predicting outcomes against Disguised Toast. NO OPPONENT INTELLIGENCE: Disguised Toast (or Disguised as listed in market) competitive strength, roster composition, recent results, and playoff experience are entirely absent from the briefing. Cannot assess relative team strength without opponent data. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT UNKNOWN: Esports World Cup Qualifier Playoffs has different seeding, bracket positioning, and competitive pressure than LCS regular season. Sentinels' regular-season performance does not reliably predict playoff performance in a different tournament structure. MARKET PRICE MOMENTUM UNEXPLAINED: YES side has risen 10.5pp over 7 days with a sharp +5.5pp move on Apr 15. Without access to pre-match news, roster changes, or official announcements, cannot determine if this reflects genuine team strength or speculative/information-driven trading. TIMING CONSTRAINT: Event resolves in ~10 hours (TODAY). Match likely already played or actively in progress. Share prices approaching extremes ($0.59/$0.41 range) suggest outcome becoming clear, but briefing data cutoff is Apr 15 16:43 UTC\u2014only ~10 hours before resolution. BOOTSTRAP PROBABILITY FROM MARKET PRICES: Current market prices (YES 60% / NO 40%) reflect aggregate belief of traders with real-time access to streaming, team announcements, and live match observation. At this late stage, market prices are more reliable than speculative analysis from stale LCS data. ASYMMETRIC CONFIDENCE JUSTIFIED: Cannot confidently assess Disguised Toast's capabilities (confidence_no = 26) due to complete absence of opponent data. Similarly limited ability to project Sentinels' performance in qualifier format (confidence_yes = 28). Both confidence scores deflated due to data gap. LEAGUE OF LEGENDS TECHNICAL FACTOR: BO3 format requires adaptability across 3 separate games with potential meta shifts between games. Champion pool flexibility (visible in the Cloud9 data: Renekton, Gnar, Gwen top lane) matters, but without Disguised Toast's champion pool or playstyle, cannot predict draft advantage. RESOLUTION RISK: If match was canceled, forfeited, or delayed >7 days, market resolves 50-50. No indication in briefing of cancellation status, but timing sensitivity is critical.", "key_factor": "The briefing contains LCS Spring regular-season data (Sentinels vs Cloud9), not Esports World Cup Qualifier Playoffs data for Sentinels vs Disguised Toast, creating a critical data mismatch that undermines reliable probability assessment for the actual match in question."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.28, "confidence_no": 0.31, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing contains LCS Spring 2026 match stats (Sentinels vs Cloud9) but zero direct information about Disguised Toast, their recent form, roster composition, or head-to-head history vs Sentinels in qualifier format. MARKET SIGNAL MISMATCH: YES side has risen +10.5pp over 7 days and +6.5pp in 24h, suggesting late backing of Sentinels into a 60% price. Sharp move +5.5pp on Apr 15 13:00 UTC (2h before scheduled match) indicates last-minute information or sentiment swing, not fundamental analysis. DISGUISED TOAST BLIND SPOT: No recent competitive data available on Disguised Toast's macro play, mechanical skill level, or performance under playoff pressure. Market may be pricing them as presumed weaker without actual verification. BO3 VOLATILITY: Best-of-3 format requires consistent execution across 3 games. Single-game upsets are common in esports; Sentinels' aggregate LCS stats do not isolate clutch performance or vulnerability to specific compositions. ROSTER UNCERTAINTY: Briefing shows detailed LCS champion builds but does NOT confirm which players/roster Sentinels will field in qualifier vs Cloud9 (a peer-tier team). If a key player is fatigued, ill, or substituted, macro coordination collapses in high-stakes BO3. META FLUX: LCS patch/meta data stale relative to qualifier match today. Recent balance changes may favor Disguised Toast's champion pool or playstyle if they specialize in off-meta or counter-picks. TOURNAMENT CONTEXT ABSENT: No information on bracket seeding, momentum, or whether Sentinels/Disguised are coming off wins/losses. Morale and confidence state drive BO3 reversals. MARKET CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: 60/40 split is modest, not extreme. At $0.49k volume, this is moderately liquid but vulnerable to late sharp buying. Late 13:00 UTC +5.5pp spike suggests incomplete information or retail FOMO rather than professional consensus.", "key_factor": "Disguised Toast fields an unconventional roster substitution or tactical pivot that exploits Sentinels' predictable meta read, or a last-minute lineup change (illness, technical issue) degrades Sentinels' coordination in high-pressure game 2/3 scenarios."}], "final_score": 0.5080692931044422, "no_score": 0.49992326656116765, "edge": 0.09499999999999997, "no_edge": 0.30499999999999994, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 51% for YES (need \u226557%); YES-side confidence too low: 33% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.7, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0632193053977828, "The Bull": 0.9488231424655758, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0510237036825305, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0690417217005483, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0631420166857992, "The Contrarian": 1.0690417217005483, "The Bear": 0.7357083883672151}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1978862", "question": "LoL: Sentinels vs Disguised (BO3) - Esports World Cup North America Qualifier Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the LoL Upper bracket quarterfinal 4 match between Sentinels and Disguised in the Esports World Cup North America Qualifier Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 15 at 5:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Sentinels\" if Sentinels win the match against Disguised.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"Disguised\" if Disguised win the match against Sentinels.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://gol.gg/esports/home. However, if https://gol.gg/esports/home has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-16T03:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-15T21:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.605, "volume_usd": 49547.16316099996, "category": "league-of-legends", "clob_token_ids": ["22081769076396780967574147676347922379491326083566103557765593345691585837801", "70642239669504428968209810929500185554030843276255011579355476492234398127312"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "key_facts": ["Sentinels\nZaahen\nTop\nGrasp of the Undying\nInspiration\nFlash\nTeleport\nBramble Vest\nPlated Steelcaps\nDeath's Dance\nTrinity Force\nSundered Sky\nEmpty\nCS\nSkarner\nJungle\nGrasp of the Undying\nInspiration\nFlash\nSmite\nHeartsteel\nProtoplasm Harness\nThornmail\nRuby Crystal\nMercury's Treads\nEmpty\nCS\nRyze\nMi