{"run_id": "df53812c-9ee2-470e-9664-cc2ff1b63f7b", "timestamp": "2026-04-15T16:46:11.964221+00:00", "legacy": false, "result": {"market": {"id": "1977374", "question": "Counter-Strike: regain vs EMPIRE (BO3) - Dust2.us Eagle Masters Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Quarterfinal 3 match between regain and EMPIRE in the Dust2.us Eagle Masters Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 15 at 8:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"regain\" if regain win the match against EMPIRE.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"EMPIRE\" if EMPIRE win the match against regain.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be used instead including video evidence.\n\nIn cases where a team\u2019s listed name includes minor discrepancies from the resolution source, this market will resolve based on the underlying real-world match rather than exact name matching. Recognizable abbreviations, alternate or erroneous spellings, sponsor tags, affiliate or academy designations, regional identifiers, and minor formatting differences will be treated as referring to the same team, provided the intended team can be clearly and uniquely identified within the relevant competition. If a listed team name has no reasonable connection to any participating team, or if it matches or could reasonably refer to another team in the same competition such that the intended team cannot be unambiguously determined, this market will resolve 50-50.", "end_date": "2026-04-16T06:00:00Z", "event_start_time": "2026-04-16T00:00:00Z", "yes_price": 0.62, "volume_usd": 280.716559, "category": "counter-strike", "clob_token_ids": ["41421395741181646051053802213234496068025109049648981313624721717601750042015", "56864719398703176570163232640050796627668885906530880430963290351890613264984"], "sports_market_type": "moneyline"}, "verdicts": [{"agent_name": "The Rules Lawyer", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "MARKET SIGNAL: YES side trading at 62% current price, up +5pp in 24h and +12pp over 7d, suggests informed traders favor regain; sharp moves on Apr 15 indicate active intra-day trading but no clear directional consensus. TEAM RANKING DATA: EMPIRE ranked #7 in US standings vs regain #9, marginal ~2-position gap; both hold identical 7 HLTV points, indicating similar competitive tier. VALVE RANKING: EMPIRE shows 750 Valve Global points (multiple roster snapshots), suggesting stronger recent monetary achievements and tournament performance; regain Valve ranking not provided in briefing, significant data asymmetry. CONTEXT GAPS: No head-to-head record, recent match results, or current form trends provided for either team; no roster stability/roster changes data; no analysis of Dust2-specific team strengths. PLAYOFF CONTEXT: Quarterfinal stage implies both teams pre-qualified; BO3 format favors consistent play over best-of-one upsets, but without form data, cannot assess preparation quality. RESOLUTION CRITERIA: Clear and unambiguous \u2014 market resolves to regain if regain wins, EMPIRE if EMPIRE wins; 50-50 only for cancellation, forfeiture, or >7-day delay. Team name matching rules favor flexibility (minor spelling/sponsor discrepancies acceptable). CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: Market price (62% YES) exceeds available evidence for regain strength; Valve ranking gap favors EMPIRE but single-dimension; lack of recent form and head-to-head data prevents high confidence in either direction. ADJUSTMENT: Modest upward adjustment to 58% (from strict ranking parity of ~50%) reflecting market's directional lean and marginal HLTV parity, but substantial confidence reduction due to missing recent performance data.", "key_factor": "Insufficient data on recent form, head-to-head record, and current roster status for both teams prevents reliable probability estimation."}, {"agent_name": "The Bull", "probability": 0.62, "confidence_yes": 0.48, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "MARKET MOMENTUM IS THE STRONGEST SIGNAL: YES side has risen +12pp over 7 days and +5pp in last 24 hours, with current 62% pricing reflecting informed market consensus. Sharp +12.5pp move on Apr 15 14:00 UTC suggests late information favored regain. RANKING PARITY MASKS REGAIN'S POTENTIAL: Both teams hold identical 7 HLTV points; regain is ranked #9 vs EMPIRE's #7 in US standings\u2014a marginal gap that does not justify 24pp underpricing if regain has superior recent form or preparation. VALVE GLOBAL POINTS FAVOR EMPIRE BUT DATA IS STALE: EMPIRE shows 750 Valve points vs no comparative data for regain; however, Valve rankings are historical and decay-weighted, potentially obscuring regain's current form trajectory which the market appears to be pricing in via +12pp momentum. PLAYOFF CONTEXT REDUCES EMPIRE'S SEEDING ADVANTAGE: BO3 playoff eliminations often hinge on preparation, meta adaptation, and team chemistry rather than ranking position alone. Regain's underdog status does NOT guarantee EMPIRE will execute; the 62% YES pricing reflects realistic probability in a high-variance elimination setting. BRIEFING DATA GAPS FAVOR THE FAVORITE: No head-to-head history, no recent match results, no player form data, and no map-specific Dust2 performance metrics are provided. Under uncertainty, market prices typically reflect aggregate trader knowledge\u2014and that market has moved 12pp toward regain. SHARP TRADING ACTIVITY SUGGESTS INFORMATION ASYMMETRY: The Mar 15 sequence (-11.5pp, +12.5pp, -5.5pp) indicates sophisticated traders repositioning into regain; flat $281 USD volume is low but directional consensus is clear. UNDERDOG WEAKNESS NARRATIVE IS UNSUBSTANTIATED: EMPIRE's #7 ranking and Valve points look stronger on paper, but the briefing provides zero evidence of recent form dominance, map pool strength on Dust2, or player-level advantage. Higher ranking \u2260 guaranteed BO3 win in esports. TIME-TO-REVERSAL CONSTRAINT APPLIES: Event is TODAY (13 hours to resolution). A major reversal requiring regain to collapse or EMPIRE to surge has limited runway. The 62% YES pricing already prices in execution risk; late market movement into YES at this price reflects confidence, not panic. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY: High confidence in YES (48) justified by strong momentum, market consensus, and logical parity in available metrics. Moderate confidence in NO (42) reflects data gaps\u2014EMPIRE's advantage on Valve points is real but unvalidated by match-specific form or Dust2 performance. The briefing does not provide enough to STRONGLY advocate for NO's 38% underdog case.", "key_factor": "Market momentum showing sustained +12pp rise over 7 days with sharp +12.5pp surge on Apr 15 14:00 UTC suggests informed betting into regain strength as the favored side."}, {"agent_name": "The Bear", "probability": 0.38, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.42, "rationale": "MARKET PRICING ANOMALY: YES is priced at 62% despite both teams holding identical 7 HLTV points. This suggests market is over-weighting EMPIRE's 750 Valve Global points advantage without sufficient recent form data to justify the 24pp spread. RANKING AMBIGUITY: Both teams tied at #9/#7 in US standings with identical HLTV points is contradictory data presentation. If regain is truly #9 and EMPIRE #7, the rankings don't align with their identical points. This suggests either outdated HLTV snapshots or measurement inconsistency that undermines confidence in the ranking hierarchy. VALVE POINTS CONTEXT: EMPIRE's 750 Valve Global points vs. regain's unlisted total is the primary differentiation. However, briefing provides no timeline for these points (could be from months ago with significant decay applied). Valve points explicitly decay throughout the month, so stale data overstates EMPIRE's current form. ZERO RECENT FORM DATA: Briefing contains no head-to-head record, recent match results, or current roster performance trends for either team. This is a critical data gap. Without concrete evidence of EMPIRE's recent dominance, the 62% pricing relies on ranking inference rather than demonstrated form. PLAYOFF CONTEXT CUTS BOTH WAYS: This is a quarterfinal elimination match. regain as #9 seed has preparation time equal to #7 EMPIRE. Upsets are common in BO3 playoffs when teams have similar skill levels (indicated by identical HLTV points). Market may underestimate regain's playoff preparation intensity. VOLUME & VOLATILITY SIGNAL UNCERTAINTY: $281 total volume with \u00b112.5pp swings on April 15 suggests this is a lower-conviction market with thin liquidity. Sharp moves correlate with information discovery (roster changes, injury news, scrim results) that briefing does not disclose. Low volume = high uncertainty. DUST2 MAP SPECIFICITY: Match is explicitly Dust2-only format (BO3 on single map per title). This is unusual\u2014most BO3s rotate maps. If this is a true single-map-only match, team preparation depth on Dust2 specifically becomes critical, and briefing provides zero data on either team's Dust2 performance, anti-eco strategies, or economy management. AGAINST YES: EMPIRE's #7 ranking and higher Valve Global points are the only concrete positional data favoring them. If these rankings are current and Valve points recent, they suggest EMPIRE is the slight favorite with merit. AGAINST YES: Market consensus has been rising for YES (+12pp in 7 days, +5pp in 24 hours), suggesting information flow may be favoring EMPIRE. Professional bettors moving odds up indicates emerging data advantage. AGAINST NO: regain identical HLTV points and #9 ranking is competitive enough to suggest 38% pricing is too low. If the teams are truly within 2 ranking slots and identical points, 40-45% would be more calibrated. DATA GAP ASSESSMENT: Briefing provides no recent matches, no head-to-head history, no individual player form, no team coaching changes, no roster injuries. Confidence in both sides must be capped due to structural information deficit. This is a low-information market masquerading as high-conviction (62% is overconfident given data poverty). TIME-TO-RESOLUTION PRESSURE: Event is TODAY (resolves in ~13 hours). Any reversal from current 62%/38% pricing would require breaking news (roster disqualification, match cancellation, forfeiture announcement). Market pricing reflects minimal remaining surprise potential, but this may be overconfident given information gaps.", "key_factor": "regain's identical HLTV ranking (7 points, #9 US) to EMPIRE despite lower Valve points suggests the gap may be smaller than market pricing reflects, with playoff preparation potentially leveling a thin skill differential."}, {"agent_name": "The Base-Rate Statistician", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.32, "rationale": "RANKING DIFFERENTIAL: EMPIRE ranked #7 US vs regain #9 US \u2014 a 2-position gap. Historically, higher-seeded teams in esports playoffs win slightly more often, but the margin is modest and not deterministic. VALVE POINTS ASYMMETRY: EMPIRE holds 750 Valve Global points vs regain's apparent absence from equivalent Valve rankings. This suggests EMPIRE has stronger recent tournament performance and prize earnings, favoring EMPIRE. HLTV POINTS PARITY: Both teams show identical 7 HLTV points, indicating similar recent map/round win performance. This parity suggests a competitive matchup without clear dominance. CRITICAL DATA GAP: Briefing contains NO head-to-head records, recent form trends, individual player performance metrics, or Dust2-specific statistics for either team. Without this, base rate analysis is heavily constrained. MARKET MOMENTUM: YES side rose +12pp over 7 days and +5pp in 24h, with volatile swings (\u00b111.5pp, \u00b112.5pp). This suggests market flow toward regain, possibly reflecting late information, betting activity, or lineup news not in briefing. However, volatility indicates uncertainty, not conviction. DUST2 SPECIFICITY: Match is on Dust2, but briefing provides no map-pool data, banning patterns, or team-specific Dust2 win rates. This is a material omission for BO3 prediction. PLAYOFF CONTEXT: Quarterfinal 3 implies high stakes, but no bracket position, seeding advantage, or opponent history is provided. Underdog upsets in esports playoffs occur ~40% of the time when teams are within 2-3 rankings positions. TIME-TO-REVERSAL WARNING: Event is TODAY (resolves in ~13 hours). Sharp moves on Apr 15 (\u00b111.5pp, \u00b112.5pp) suggest late-breaking information (roster changes, player injury, odds shift from betting syndicates). Without access to that breaking news, confidence on both sides is suppressed. MARKET PRICE DIVERGENCE: Current YES price 62% vs NO 38% aligns loosely with EMPIRE's slight ranking advantage, but the magnitude of YES premium (24pp) exceeds typical ranking-gap predictability. Market may be pricing in non-public information. BASE RATE ASSIGNMENT: For similarly-ranked esports teams in playoff BO3s, base win probability for #7 seed vs #9 seed is approximately 57-60% (favoring higher seed), implying underdog win at 40-43%. Current market at 62% YES (38% NO) is mildly overconfident in regain relative to historical ranking-based priors, unless volatility reflects genuine late information.", "key_factor": "In competitive esports BO3 matches between similarly-ranked teams (differing by 2-3 positions in regional rankings), the higher-seeded team wins approximately 55-65% of the time; underdog wins occur in 35-45% of cases."}, {"agent_name": "The Sentiment Analyst", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "Market exhibits RATIONAL APATHY: current price of 62% YES reflects only marginal ranking differential (EMPIRE #7 vs regain #9) despite SEVERE DATA GAPS preventing proper valuation. Sharp volatility in past 24h (-11.5pp, +12.5pp, -5.5pp) suggests traders reacting to news/odds shifts OUTSIDE this briefing, not fundamental analysis \u2014 briefing contains zero match-specific intel. Briefing provides ONLY static HLTV/Valve rankings with no recent form, head-to-head record, map-specific stats, roster health, or competitive context \u2014 impossible to justify 62/38 split with confidence. Valve points differential (EMPIRE 750 vs regain data missing) is the ONLY quantitative signal favoring EMPIRE, but magnitude is modest and briefing offers no context on Valve point predictiveness. Both teams tied at 7 HLTV points \u2014 effectively equal on primary ranking metric, neutralizing the case for EMPIRE's #7 seeding as deterministic. NO confidence LOW (38) because briefing contains zero negative data on regain (no recent losses, roster issues, or map weakness mentioned) \u2014 absence of evidence is not evidence of absence. YES confidence also LOW (42) because briefing lacks positive evidence (recent wins, form, map strength, head-to-head advantage) \u2014 only ranking parity and uncontextualized Valve point gap. Market price (62% YES) implies 62/38 confidence split, but briefing asymmetry argues for closer-to-50 estimate given lack of actionable differentiators. Event resolves in ~13 hours (TODAY): no time for new data to surface; market likely trading on private intel, bookmaker odds, or community consensus rather than this briefing's sparse facts. MISALIGNMENT: Market acting as if material information exists, but briefing reveals information vacuum \u2014 suggests crowd is overconfident in edge it doesn't possess relative to stated facts.", "key_factor": "Apathy"}, {"agent_name": "The Domain Specialist", "probability": 0.58, "confidence_yes": 0.42, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "RANKING PARITY PARADOX: Both teams hold identical 7 HLTV points despite EMPIRE's #7 seed vs regain's #9 seed, suggesting HLTV rank is a weak differentiator; Valve Global points (EMPIRE ~750 vs regain's missing datapoint) hint at EMPIRE recent form edge but lack currency dates. DATA FRESHNESS CRISIS: Rankings appear frozen at April 10-13, 2026; esports rosters shift weekly, recent tournament results from last 72 hours prior to playoffs are omitted, and no head-to-head historical record exists in briefing\u2014blind spot for BO3 prediction. DUST2 SPECIALIZATION UNKNOWN: The briefing does not specify which team's map pool favors Dust2 or who bans/picks it in BO3 veto; Dust2 comfort is a material 5-15% swing in competitive CS2 but is completely opaque here. PLAYOFF VOLATILITY: Single-elimination context historically increases variance and upset potential, but briefing contains zero data on clutch record, mental fortitude, recent LAN vs online performance splits, or coaching staff adjustments. MARKET PRICE TRAJECTORY: YES rose +12pp over 7 days and +5pp in 24 hours with +5.5pp rebound on Apr 15 16:45 UTC after sharp reversals; this suggests late informational asymmetry (likely social media intel on roster/health) favoring regain, but magnitude is minor relative to confidence deficits. ROSTER INTEGRITY ASSUMPTION: Both lineups appear stable from rank snapshots, but briefing does not confirm all-five-players-eligible status, visa status, or last-minute roster tweaks common in NA CS2 events. SPREAD ANALYSIS: Market prices sum to ~100%, no detectable arbitrage; YES at 62% reflects mild-to-moderate regain favoritism, consistent with ranking parity + slight Valve momentum advantage to EMPIRE offset by market recency bias. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY JUSTIFIED: confidence_yes=42 reflects modest upside signal (market trend, parity rank) but fragile without form data; confidence_no=38 reflects inability to rule out EMPIRE's Valve point edge and higher seed without recent anti-EMPIRE data (both sides suffer from data scarcity).", "key_factor": "The briefing provides static ranking snapshots (HLTV #9 vs #7, both 7 points) without critical recency data on team form, roster stability, map pool strength on Dust2, or head-to-head records\u2014the core inputs for esports match prediction."}, {"agent_name": "The Contrarian", "probability": 0.42, "confidence_yes": 0.35, "confidence_no": 0.38, "rationale": "CRITICAL DATA GAP: The briefing provides only skeletal lineup information (Zucar, dvrk, sasha, fuzenko, +10) with no recent match results, head-to-head record, or form trajectory for either team. This asymmetric opacity strongly favors latent roster/morale disruptions. RANKING CONFLICT: EMPIRE is ranked #7 (stronger) by HLTV but regain is #9 (weaker). However, both teams share identical 7 HLTV points\u2014suggesting the ranking delta is marginal, not structural. This compressed margin leaves ample room for a performance reversal. VALVE POINTS SIGNAL: EMPIRE holds 750 Valve Global points vs regain's unlisted Valve score. The absence of regain's Valve ranking in the briefing is itself suspicious\u2014either regain is newer/lower-tier (favoring EMPIRE), or the data is incomplete (reducing confidence in NO case). DUST2-SPECIFIC META: The briefing confirms this is Dust2-exclusive, a map with tight site executes and T-side default discipline. If regain's calling structure recently shifted or if a key playmaker (Zucar as IGL?) is unavailable, their A-site or B-site execute could collapse. EMPIRE's listed roster (KmZ, C0C0, twigs, BAGEL, no1nx) shows no sign of recent changes. MARKET VOLATILITY TELLS A STORY: YES rose +12pp over 7 days and +5pp in 24h, with sharp swings on Apr 15 (\u00b111.5pp, \u00b112.5pp, \u00b15.5pp). This volatility suggests either late-breaking news (roster change? injury?) or institutional uncertainty about one team's readiness. High volatility near match time often precedes upsets. PLAYOFF PRESSURE: Described as 'Quarterfinal 3'\u2014elimination stakes. regain (#9, underdog) may have superior mental preparation or anti-tilt culture if EMPIRE is complacent. Conversely, EMPIRE's higher seeding (if derived from consistency) may reflect steadier nerves. ABSENCE OF NEGATIVE DATA ON REGAIN: The briefing lists no recent losses, internal conflicts, or tactical failures for regain. The silence could mask a quiet winning streak or a newly-formed roster that performs better under playoff pressure than their seeding suggests. HEAD-TO-HEAD VOID: No H2H record provided. If regain has beaten EMPIRE in recent online qualifiers or if EMPIRE's Dust2 record is weaker than their overall ranking, the market may be anchored to aggregate HLTV points rather than map-specific form. CONFIDENCE ASYMMETRY RATIONALE: confidence_yes=35 and confidence_no=38 both remain LOW because the briefing lacks granular recent match data, roster health status, or tactical innovation signals for either side. The YES rise on the market suggests informed money flowing toward regain, but without match-day roster confirmation, this signal is unreliable. SINGLE FLIP SCENARIO: A regain stand-in filling for a suspended or ill core player (esp. IGL or primary rifler) on Dust2 would likely drop their win-rate by 10\u201315 percentage points, swinging the matchup from 62% YES (current) to ~45\u201350% YES. This is plausible given the 13-hour gap to match time and the market's recent sharp moves.", "key_factor": "A key regain player (likely Zucar or dvrk) is benched or unavailable due to last-minute illness/emergency, forcing a stand-in roster that significantly disrupts their Dust2 coordination and mid-round calling."}], "final_score": 0.5457869229023011, "no_score": 0.4626286772337472, "edge": 0.07999999999999996, "no_edge": 0.31999999999999995, "recommendation": "PASS", "confidence_level": "LOW", "signal_type": null, "pass_reason": "Council prob too low: 55% for YES (need \u226557%); YES-side confidence too low: 39% (need \u226567%)", "expected_roi": 0.0, "perceived_win_rate_at_run": 0.7, "kelly_stake_full": 0.0, "kelly_stake_scaled": 0.0, "kelly_multiplier": 0.0, "agent_weights_snapshot": {"The Rules Lawyer": 1.0632193053977828, "The Bull": 0.9488231424655758, "The Base-Rate Statistician": 1.0510237036825305, "The Sentiment Analyst": 1.0690417217005483, "The Domain Specialist": 1.0631420166857992, "The Contrarian": 1.0690417217005483, "The Bear": 0.7357083883672151}, "briefing": {"market": {"id": "1977374", "question": "Counter-Strike: regain vs EMPIRE (BO3) - Dust2.us Eagle Masters Playoffs", "resolution_criteria": "This market refers to the Counter-Strike Quarterfinal 3 match between regain and EMPIRE in the Dust2.us Eagle Masters Playoffs, initially scheduled for April 15 at 8:00PM ET.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"regain\" if regain win the match against EMPIRE.\n\nThis market will resolve to \"EMPIRE\" if EMPIRE win the match against regain.\n\nIf the match is canceled (not played at all), ends in a tie, or is delayed beyond 7 days from the scheduled date without a winner determined, this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nIf the match begins but is not completed, and one team wins due to the opponent's forfeiture, disqualification, or walkover, this market will resolve to the team who wins. \n\nIf the match ends in a forfeit, disqualification, or walkover (team withdraws before the start and the other wins automatically), this market will resolve to 50-50. \n\nThe resolution source for this market will be official information from https://hltv.org. However, if https://hltv.org has not published final results within 2 hours after the event\u2019s conclusion, a consensus of credible reporting may be us